consider: goldbook:08057
consider: goldbook:08081

[Term]
id: goldbook:08017
name: critical value
def: "Measured quantity value for a quantity of a component in a material\, above which the component is declared to be present."
comment: "Another important concept in characterizing the capability of detection of measurement procedures is the limit of detection."
comment: "In some European legislations, the term "decision limit" (denoted as CCα) is used for the concept 'critical value'."
comment: "The critical value is chosen to give a probability α (usually 0.05) of a measured quantity value exceeding the critical value when the component is absent."
comment: "The critical value is usually considered to be a characteristic of a particular measurement procedure performed in a particular laboratory."
comment: "The detection decision is made by comparing a measured quantity value with the critical value."
comment: "The quantity measured is usually a mass fraction or a concentration but can also be, for example, a mass or an amount of substance."
synonym: "critical level" []
synonym: "decision level" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08028
consider: goldbook:08061

[Term]
id: goldbook:08018
name: determination
def: "Set of operations that are carried out on an object in order to provide qualitative or quantitative information about this object."
comment: ""Determination" is a superordinate concept of measurement and examination, and so, the term "determination" should not be used when "measurement" or "examination" applies."
comment: ""Determination" is a term in general usage and often implies a human decision."
comment: "ISO 9000 defines determination as "activity to find out one or more characteristics and their characteristic values"."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08049

[Term]
id: goldbook:08019
name: interferent
def: "Component of the matrix that embodies an influence quantity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08020
name: intermediate measurement precision
def: "Measurement precision under intermediate precision conditions of measurement."
comment: ""Intralaboratory precision" or "within-laboratory precision" is sometimes used as a synonym of intermediate measurement precision."
synonym: "intermediate precision" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08021
name: laboratory bias
def: "Contribution to measurement bias that is attributed to systematic effects on measurement results made in a laboratory."
comment: "Measurement bias in analytical chemistry may be considered to include run bias, laboratory bias, and measurement procedure bias."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
