consider: goldbook:08028
consider: goldbook:08040
consider: goldbook:08051
consider: goldbook:08073
consider: goldbook:08122

[Term]
id: goldbook:08023
name: linearity of a measuring system
def: "Ability of a measuring system to provide measured quantity values that are directly proportional to the quantity value of the measurand."
comment: "Linearity of a measuring system should not be confused with linearity of calibration."
comment: "The linearity of a measuring system is assessed during procedure validation."
comment: "The set of measured quantity values for which linearity of a measuring system applies is usually termed "linear interval" or "linear range"."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08024
consider: goldbook:08097

[Term]
id: goldbook:08024
name: linearity of calibration
def: "Closeness of agreement between indications obtained using calibrators in the first step of a calibration and indications predicted by the calibration function for the calibrators’ reference quantity values."
comment: "Calibration linearity should not be confused with linearity of a measuring system."
comment: "Linearity of calibration is assessed during procedure validation."
comment: "Linearity of calibration may be expressed by measures of agreement (for example, correlation coefficient) or deviation (for example, standard error of regression), obtained by regression of calibration data or assessed from a residual plot."
comment: "The concept applies to calibration functions of any mathematical form. The term "linearity" is historical and refers to a time when calibration graphs were constructed on paper and were invariably considered to be linear."
synonym: "calibration linearity" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08023
consider: goldbook:08097

[Term]
id: goldbook:08025
name: material homogeneity
def: "Uniform structure or composition of a material with respect to one or more specified properties."
comment: "A material is said to be homogeneous with respect to a specified quantity if the quantity values measured using aliquots of a specified size do not fall outside a specified interval. See minimum sample size."
comment: "Detailed guidance for the assessment of homogeneity of reference materials is given in ISO Guide 35."
comment: "In the homogeneity study of a candidate reference material, it is distinguished whether the analytical samples are taken from different supply units or from a single supply unit ("termed between-bottle homogeneity" or "within-bottle homogeneity", respectively)."
comment: "Inhomogeneity is a source of measurement uncertainty."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08034
consider: goldbook:08060

[Term]
id: goldbook:08026
name: material recovery
def: "Mass \(volume\, amount of substance\) of a specified component isolated from a system divided by the mass \(volume\, amount of substance\) of the system prior to isolation."
comment: "The measurement unit of material recovery is the measurement unit of the quantity related to the specified component divided by the unit of the quantity describing the system. When these units are the same, material recovery may be expressed as a percentage, and the quantity specified."
comment: "The term "recovery" is also used to describe a recovered quantity value ratio. Therefore, the term "recovery" should not be used without qualification unless the meaning is clear from the context."
synonym: "recovery" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08039

[Term]
id: goldbook:08027
name: material stability
def: "Constancy of a property of a material over time."
comment: "A material is said to be stable with respect to a specified property if its measured or examined property value does not fall outside a specified interval during storage under specified conditions over a specified period of time."
comment: "A reference material is assessed for the stability of an embodied property under conditions of transport ("short-term stability") and storage ("long-term stability")."
comment: "The term "stability" is also used for stability of a measuring instrument or process (see control limit)."
comment: "The variation of the property value over time adds a contribution to the uncertainty budget or the examination uncertainty, as applicable. Regarding the assessment of stability of the reference material, detailed guidance is given in ISO Guide 35."
synonym: "stability" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08069

[Term]
id: goldbook:08028
name: measurement procedure
def: "Detailed description of a measurement according to one or more measurement principles and to a given measurement method\, based on a measurement model and including any calculation to obtain a measurement result."
comment: "A measurement procedure can include a statement concerning a target measurement uncertainty."
comment: "A measurement procedure is usually documented in sufficient detail to enable an operator to perform a measurement."
comment: "An authorized measurement procedure is sometimes termed "standard operating procedure" (SOP) or "recommended operating procedure" (ROP)."
comment: "In ISO/IEC 17025, the term "method" is used for measurement procedure. "Examination procedure" is defined for medical laboratories."
comment: "Measurement procedures in chemistry can be structured according to ISO 78-2 or Annex A of the Eurachem Guide "The Fitness for Purpose of Analytical Methods"."
comment: "The historical term "assay" is now largely obsolete as a synonym for metrological terms such as measurement procedure but still used in composite terms, for example, immunoassay and bioassay."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08131
consider: goldbook:08133

[Term]
id: goldbook:08029
name: measurement procedure bias
def: "Contribution to measurement bias that is attributed to systematic effects on measurement results made according to a measurement procedure."
comment: "Contributions to measurement procedure bias are calculated during procedure validation."
comment: "Measurement bias in analytical chemistry may be considered to include run bias, laboratory bias, and measurement procedure bias."
comment: "Measurement procedure bias covers instrumental bias."
synonym: "measurement method bias" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
