[Term]
id: goldbook:08041
name: run bias
def: "Contribution to measurement bias that is attributed to systematic effects on measurement results made in a single analytical run."
comment: "Measurement bias in analytical chemistry may be considered to include run bias, laboratory bias, and measurement procedure bias."
