[Term]
id: goldbook:08051
name: working interval
def: "Set of quantity values over which a measuring instrument or measuring system provides measurement results with acceptable measurement uncertainty under defined conditions."
comment: "In some fields, the term is "measurement range". In entry 4.7 of VIM, a similar concept termed "measuring interval" is defined."
comment: "The lower limit of a working interval should not be confused with the detection limit."
comment: "The working interval is bounded by the lower and upper limit of quantification."
synonym: "working range" []
