[Term]
id: goldbook:08056
name: assessor
def: "Person\, assigned by an accreditation body\, with relevant professional expertise and experience who can determine the competence of a laboratory."
comment: "Depending on the role and responsibilities of an assessor, terms such as "lead assessor" and "technical assessor" are often used."
comment: "The assessor may work alone or as part of a team and be engaged in a voluntary or paid capacity."
comment: "The work of an assessor is often referred to as "assessment" and sometimes as "peer review"."
