[Term]
id: goldbook:08058
name: audit
def: "Systematic\, independent\, and documented process for obtaining objective evidence and evaluating it objectively to determine the extent to which the audit criteria are fulfilled."
comment: "An audit can be an internal audit (first party) or an external audit (second party or third party), and it can be a combined audit or a joint audit."
comment: "External audits include those generally termed second and third-party audits. Second-party audits are conducted by parties having an interest in the organization, such as customers, or by other persons on their behalf. Third-party audits are conducted by external, independent auditing organizations such as those providing certification/registration of conformity or governmental agencies."
comment: "Internal audits, sometimes termed first-party audits, are conducted by, or on behalf of, the organization itself for management review and other internal purposes and can form the basis for an organization's declaration of conformity. Independence can be demonstrated by the freedom from responsibility for the activity being audited."
comment: "The fundamental elements of an audit include the determination of the conformity of an object according to a procedure carried out by personnel not being responsible for the object audited."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
