[Term]
id: goldbook:08064
name: commutability of a reference material
def: "Property of a reference material\, demonstrated by the closeness of agreement between the relation among the measurement results for a stated quantity in this material\, obtained according to two given measurement procedures\, and the relation obtained among the measurement results for other specified materials."
comment: "Cases in which a reference material producer is required to conduct assessment of commutability are outlined in ISO 15194."
comment: "Guidance for assessment of commutability of reference material in laboratory medicine is provided by IFCC."
comment: "The material stability of commutable reference materials should be monitored regularly."
comment: "The measurement procedures referred to in the definition are the one preceding and the one following the reference material (calibrator) in question in a calibration hierarchy (see ISO 17511)."
comment: "The reference material in question is usually a calibrator and the other specified materials are usually routine samples."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
