id: goldbook:08084
name: laboratory information management system
def: "Information system which can provide services to one or more measuring systems."
comment: "In laboratory medicine, the term "Laboratory Information System" is common."
comment: "LIMS functionality can include sample registration and tracking (through barcodes, chips, etc.), electronic laboratory notebooks, report generation, quality control, and financial control."
comment: "Services include the control of automated analyses and collecting, processing, storing, and managing of data."
synonym: "laboratory information system" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08085
name: material characterization study
def: "Intralaboratory comparison or interlaboratory comparison with the aim of assigning a reference quantity value to a quantity with stated measurement uncertainty or value to a reference nominal property value with stated examination uncertainty."
comment: "A material characterization study often utilizes selected (routine or reference) laboratories to measure quantity values of a candidate reference material by measurement procedure(s) judged most likely to provide the smallest associated measurement uncertainty."
comment: "Although proficiency testing is not primarily intended as a material characterization study, reference materials are sometimes certified on the basis of results from a proficiency testing scheme after appropriate quality assurance procedures."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
