[Term]
id: goldbook:08086
name: matrix reference material
def: "Reference material that is characteristic of a real sample."
comment: "A chemical substance dissolved in a pure solvent is not a matrix reference material."
comment: "Matrix reference materials are intended to be used in conjunction with the chemical analysis of real samples of the same or a similar matrix."
comment: "Matrix reference materials may also be prepared by a spike of the component(s) of interest into an existing material."
comment: "Matrix reference materials may be obtained directly from biological, environmental, or industrial sources."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
