consider: goldbook:08138

[Term]
id: goldbook:08091
name: organization
def: "Person or group of people that has its own functions with responsibilities\, authorities\, and relationships to achieve its objectives."
comment: "In formal documents, the term "body" is often used to denote an organization, for example, "accreditation body", "certification body", "inspection body", "legislative body", and "regulatory body"."
comment: "The concept of "organization" includes, but is not limited to, sole-trader, company, corporation, firm, enterprise, authority, partnership, association, charity, or institution, or part or combination thereof, whether incorporated or not, public or private."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08092
name: out-of-control criteria
def: "Set of decision rules for identifying the presence of special causes."
comment: "Decision rules may include those relating to measured quantity values inside and outside of control limits in a control chart. They cover runs, trends, cycles, periodicity, concentration of points near the centre line or control limits, unusual spread of points within control limits (large or small dispersion), and relationships among values within subgroups."
comment: "Examples of decision rules and guidelines for the daily interpretation of a control chart are provided by Nordtest."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08068
consider: goldbook:08069

[Term]
id: goldbook:08093
name: participant in an interlaboratory comparison
def: "Laboratory\, organization\, or person that receives test items and submits results for review by the coordinator of an interlaboratory comparison."
synonym: "participant" []
