[Term]
id: goldbook:08094
name: performance characteristic of a measurement procedure
def: "Aspect of a measurement procedure that may be quantitatively investigated and assessed as part of procedure validation."
comment: "Measurement uncertainty is not a performance characteristic of a particular measurement procedure but a property of the measurement result obtained using that measurement procedure."
comment: "Performance characteristics that may be considered in procedure validation are analytical selectivity, sensitivity of a measuring system, working interval, ruggedness of a measurement procedure, linearity of a measuring system, linearity of calibration, critical value, limit of detection, limit of quantification, measurement trueness, and measurement precision."
synonym: "performance characteristic" []
synonym: "performance characteristic of a measurement method" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
