[Term]
id: goldbook:08095
name: performance score
def: "Statistic\, derived from a result reported by a participant in a proficiency testing scheme\, used in interpretation of participant performance and to allow comparison with defined objectives."
comment: "Names and defining equations of frequently used performance scores are listed in Table 1. Their definitions and interpretations are given in ISO/IEC 17043 and ISO 13528."
comment: "The purpose of a performance score is to express the deviation of the reported value from the assigned value in a proficiency testing scheme in a manner that allows comparison with performance criteria."
synonym: "performance statistic" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
