consider: goldbook:08104

[Term]
id: goldbook:08096
name: precision limit
def: "Quantity value\, less than or equal to what the absolute difference between two measured quantity values obtained under specified conditions of measurement is expected to be with a given probability."
comment: "ISO 3534-2 defines three kinds of precision limit: repeatability limit (\(r\)), intermediate precision limit, and reproducibility limit (\(R\)) obtained under repeatability conditions of measurement, intermediate precision conditions of measurement, and reproducibility conditions of measurement, respectively. The recommended probability is \(\pu{95\%}\)."
comment: "Precision limit at approximately \(\pu{95\%}\) is estimated by multiplying the standard deviation obtained under the specified conditions of measurement by \(2\sqrt{2}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08040

[Term]
id: goldbook:08097
name: procedure validation
def: "Process of defining an analytical requirement and confirming that the procedure under consideration has capabilities consistent with that requirement."
comment: "In ISO/IEC 17025, the term "method" is used as a synonym for measurement procedure."
comment: "Inherent in procedure validation is the need to evaluate performance characteristics of a measurement procedure."
comment: "Procedure validation is either done in a single laboratory or in the framework of an interlaboratory comparison."
comment: "The corresponding term in ISO 15189 is "validation of examination procedures"."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
