[Term]
id: goldbook:08106
name: quality
def: "Degree to which a set of inherent characteristics of an object fulfils requirements."
comment: ""Inherent", as opposed to "assigned", means existing in the object."
comment: "Measurement uncertainty provides a quantitative measure of the quality of a measurement result."
comment: "The term "quality" can be used with adjectives such as poor, good, or excellent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
