[Term]
id: goldbook:08110
name: quality management system
def: "Part of a set of interrelated or interacting elements of an organization to establish quality policies and quality objectives and processes to achieve those objectives."
comment: "A laboratory's structure, roles and responsibilities, planning, operation, practices, rules, and beliefs are also established within the quality management system."
comment: "Other common parts of a laboratory's management system are financial management and environmental management. These management systems should not be confused with a laboratory information management system."
