consider: goldbook:08112

[Term]
id: goldbook:08116
name: reference laboratory
def: "Laboratory that applies a reference measurement procedure\, a reference examination procedure\, or performs a calibration."
comment: "In laboratory medicine, a reference measurement laboratory is defined in ISO 15195."
comment: "The term "reference laboratory" may have other connotations in a national context."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08117
name: reference material certificate
def: "Document\, issued by a reference material producer\, containing the essential information for the use of a certified reference material and confirming that the necessary procedures have been carried out to ensure the validity and traceability of the stated property values."
comment: "A reference material certificate is usually valid for a stated period of time ("period of validity" or as described by its "expiry date"), which defines the shelf life of the certified reference material."
comment: "Documents containing the information described above may not, for legal or other (non-technical) reasons, be termed "certificate" (compare Note 1 to certified reference material)."
comment: "ISO Guide 31 is the guidance document to the required and recommended content of a reference material certificate."
comment: "In this definition, "traceability" covers both metrological traceability of a measurement result and examination traceability, but not object traceability."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08037
consider: goldbook:08046
consider: goldbook:08120

[Term]
id: goldbook:08118
name: reference material certification
def: "Process that formally establishes the certified property value\(s\) of a candidate certified reference material."
comment: "Properties of a material include qualitative properties such as identities of chemical substances and quantitative properties such as mass concentration."
comment: "Reference material certification is a "first-party attestation" in accordance with the definition of the term "declaration"."
comment: "The outcome of the process is a reference material certificate."
comment: "The process is the responsibility of the reference material producer."
synonym: "certification of a reference material" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
