[Term]
id: goldbook:08121
name: rejection interval
def: "Interval of non-permissible measured quantity values."
comment: "Non-permissible measured quantity values are associated with items that do not conform to specified requirements and lie outside the acceptance interval."
synonym: "rejection zone" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08052
consider: goldbook:08067
consider: goldbook:08129

[Term]
id: goldbook:08122
name: requirement
def: "Need or expectation that is stated\, generally implied or obligatory."
comment: ""Generally implied" means that it is custom or common practice for the organization and interested parties that the need or expectation under consideration is implied."
comment: "A specified requirement is one that is stated, for example, in documented information."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08091
consider: goldbook:08129

[Term]
id: goldbook:08123
name: ruggedness of a measurement procedure
def: "Ability of a measurement procedure to maintain acceptable performance under minor changes in operating conditions."
comment: "A measurement procedure, the performance of which remains unaffected by minor changes in operating conditions, is usually said to be "rugged" or "robust"."
comment: "Ruggedness is normally investigated as a part of procedure development and may be part of procedure validation."
comment: "The outcome of a ruggedness test provides objective evidence of the applicability of the measurement procedure during normal usage."
synonym: "robustness of a measurement procedure" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08028
consider: goldbook:08049
consider: goldbook:08097

[Term]
id: goldbook:08124
name: sensitivity of a measuring system
def: "Quotient of the change in an indication of a measuring system and the corresponding change in a quantity being measured."
comment: "Sensitivity of a measuring system can be obtained from the slope of the calibration curve."
comment: "Sensitivity of a measuring system can depend on the value of the quantity being measured."
comment: "Sensitivity of a measuring system should not be confused with diagnostic sensitivity in laboratory medicine."
comment: "Sensitivity of a measuring system should not be confused with limit of detection or limit of quantification."
comment: "The change considered in a value of a quantity being measured must be large compared with the resolution."
synonym: "analytical sensitivity" []
synonym: "sensitivity" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
