[Term]
id: goldbook:08125
name: Shewhart control chart
def: "Control chart with Shewhart control limits intended primarily to distinguish between the variation in the plotted measure due to random causes and that due to special causes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08068
consider: goldbook:08126

[Term]
id: goldbook:08126
name: Shewhart control limit
def: "Control limit determined statistically from the variation of the process due to random causes alone."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08069

[Term]
id: goldbook:08127
name: Shewhart means chart
def: "Shewhart control chart in which the means of measured quantity values are plotted against time. Figure 1\: Shewhart means chart of the means of duplicate analyses of a quality control material\, twice per day \(d\) over 20 days. Each point is the mean of the day’s four results \(\\\(n = 4\\\)\). Upper and lower warning limits \(UWL and LWL\) are at \\\(\\bar\{x\} \\pm 2s/\\sqrt\{n\}\\\)\, where \\\(\\bar\{x\}\\\) is the process mean\, \\\(s\\\) is the standard deviation under repeatability conditions of measurement\, and upper and lower action limits \(UAL and LAL\) are at \\\(\\bar\{x\} \\pm 3s/\\sqrt\{n\}\\\). A simulated measurement bias of one standard deviation is applied after day 10."
comment: "Nordtest terms a control chart with measured quantity values scaled by the mean or target value an "X-chart". ISO uses the term "X-control chart" for a control chart which plots single values."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08040
consider: goldbook:08107
consider: goldbook:08125

[Term]
id: goldbook:08128
name: Shewhart range chart
def: "Shewhart control chart in which the ranges of measured quantity values are plotted against time."
comment: "Nordtest advises that for Shewhart range charts, the best samples to be used are test samples selected from among the samples to be analysed in that analytical run."
comment: "The range is the greatest measured quantity value minus the least measured quantity value."
comment: "Warning and action limits are given in tables (for example) as a function of the number of measured quantity values (\(n\)) taken to obtain the range and of the expected average range."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
