[Term]
id: goldbook:08229
name: Cauchy function
def: "Function \\\(y = a/\(b^\{2\} + x^\{2\}\)\\\) where \\\(a\\\) and \\\(b\\\) are constants."
comment: "If \(x\) is replaced by \(\tilde{\nu} - \tilde \nu_{0}\) this function yields a Lorentzian band centered at \(\tilde{\nu}_{0}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08230
name: charge coupled device
def: "Device that stores information in the form of charge packets in an array of closely spaced capacitors."
comment: "In spectroscopy, the charge packets are created by interaction with electromagnetic radiation and the devices are extremely sensitive detectors for near infrared and visible radiation."
comment: "The packets can be transferred from one capacitor to the next sequentially by electronic manipulation, so that the information contained in the array can be sequentially read electronically."
synonym: "CCD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242
consider: goldbook:08642

[Term]
id: goldbook:08231
name: circular birefringence
def: "Difference between the refractive indices of an optically active medium for left\, \\\(n^\{\\rm\{L\}\}\\\)\, and right\, \\\(n^\{\\rm\{R\}\}\\\)\, circularly polarized radiation \(\\\(n^\{\\rm\{L\}\}-n^\{\\rm\{R\}\}\\\)\)."
comment: ""Circular birefringence" is also used to describe the phenomenon of having different refractive indices for left and right circularly polarized radiation."
comment: "Like the refractive indices (\(n^{\rm{L}}\), \(n^{\rm{R}}\)), circular birefringence changes with wavenumber."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242
consider: goldbook:08301

[Term]
id: goldbook:08232
name: dephasing
def: "Loss of coherence between the upper and lower states of a transition."
comment: "Dephasing leads to either homogeneous broadening or inhomogeneous broadening depending on the system. The continually changing intermolecular interactions cause a shift of the frequency of the intramolecular vibration. If these interactions change much more slowly than the amplitude of this shift, heterogeneous broadening results and causes a Gaussian band. If these interactions change much faster than the amplitude of this shift, homogeneous broadening occurs and the observed spectral band is a notionally narrowed Lorentzian band. In the general case, the broadening due to dephasing is neither homogeneous nor heterogeneous and the line shape is neither Gaussian nor Lorentzian."
comment: "The term 'dephasing' arises from the density matrix formalism that is used in a phenomenological approach to simplify the description of the relaxation dynamics of a molecule coupled to its surroundings."
synonym: "phase relaxation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08252
consider: goldbook:08285
consider: goldbook:08611
consider: goldbook:08619

[Term]
id: goldbook:08233
name: detector gate width
def: "Time for signal integration after start of detection."
comment: "Optimization of gate width allows detection of species with different decay rates."
synonym: "detector integration time" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08234
name: difference spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of spectroscopy in which spectral subtraction is used to help the study and identification of individual species in a mixture."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08290

[Term]
id: goldbook:08235
name: diffuse reflectance
def: "Diffuse reflected \(remitted\) radiant power \(\\\(P_\{\\rm\{rem\}\}\\\)\) divided by incident radiant power \(\\\(P_\{0\}\\\)\). \\\(R = P_\{\\rm\{rem\}\}/P_\{0\}\\\)."
comment: "Some authors distinguish between remittance and diffuse reflectance by excluding specular reflection in the latter."
comment: "The sum of remittance, transmittance, and absorptance equals one."
synonym: "remission fraction" []
synonym: "remittance" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08292

[Term]
id: goldbook:08236
name: diffuse reflection
def: "Reflection in which electromagnetic radiation incident on a scattering surface at a certain angle is reflected \(remitted\) over all angles."
comment: "Diffuse reflection is a complicated process and involves transmission, reflection, and scattering."
synonym: "remission" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08235
consider: goldbook:08242
consider: goldbook:08281

[Term]
id: goldbook:08237
name: diffuse transmission
def: "Process in which radiation is transmitted by a scattering sample and leaves the sample in directions other than that required by Snell’s law of refraction. The process is complicated and involves transmission\, reflection\, and scattering."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08238
name: dipole coupling
def: "Coupling of different motions through dipole-dipole forces."
comment: "In vibrational spectroscopy of crystals, intermolecular vibrational coupling through interaction of resonant transition dipoles throughout the whole crystal."
synonym: "transition-dipole transition dipole coupling" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
