[Term]
id: goldbook:08246
name: energy level
def: "Set of one or more stationary quantum states of a free atom\, ion\, or molecule having a particular internal energy."
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{J}\). Common unit: electron volt, symbol \(\pu{eV}\), where \(\pu{1 eV} = \pu{1.602176634E-19 J}\). Energy levels are also expressed as \(\pu{kJ mol-1}\)."
synonym: "energy state" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08247
name: experimental absorbance
def: "Decadic absorbance as measured with no corrections for other processes."
comment: "Internal absorbance is used to term absorbance corrected for other processes."
comment: "The term emphasizes that radiation might be lost from the beam by reflection, luminescence, scattering, and possibly vignetting (e.g., spectral shifts introduced from changing a radiation beam diameter or shape), and not solely by absorption."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
