consider: goldbook:08281

[Term]
id: goldbook:08248
name: folding
def: "The appearance of peaks at incorrect frequencies in a mathematically-processed spectrum due to insufficient density of datapoints in the time-domain spectrum or from peaks outside of the sampled frequency range.This process can be simulated by folding a spectrum that shows the correct wavenumbers back onto itself at \\\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{\\rm\{M\}\}\\\) and its multiples."
comment: "Folding is a consequence of undersampling in spectroscopy."
comment: "In vibrational spectroscopy, when a spectrum is sampled correctly only up to a wavenumber \(\tilde{\nu}_{\rm{M}}\), radiation of wavenumber \(\tilde{\nu} \gt \tilde{\nu}_{\rm{M}}\) appears to have a wavenumber between 0 and \(\tilde{\nu}_{\rm{M}}\), per the table below:"
synonym: "aliasing" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08275
consider: goldbook:08297
consider: goldbook:08301
consider: goldbook:08708

[Term]
id: goldbook:08249
name: free induction decay
def: "Indication from a pulsed spectroscopy experiment that takes the form of damped sine waves arising from the excited system returning to equilibrium."
comment: "In nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy, the FID consists of sine waves oscillating at the Larmor angular frequency (\(\omega\)) and dampened by net dephasing time relaxation (\(T_{2}^{*}\)), \(\sin (\omega t) \exp(-t/T_{2}^{*})\)."
synonym: "FID" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
