[Term]
id: goldbook:08256
name: Hilbert transforms
def: "Functions that interrelate the real part\, \\\(f'\\\)\, and imaginary part\, \\\(f''\\\)\, of the refractive index\, \\\(\\boldsymbol\{\\hat\{n\}\} = n + \{\\rm\{i\}\}k\\\)\, or relative permittivity\, \\\(\\boldsymbol\{\\hat\{\\epsilon\}\} = \\epsilon' + \\rm\{i\}\\epsilon''\\\)\, through \\\[f'\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\) - f_\{\\infty\}' = \\frac\{1\}\{\\pi\} P \\int_\{-\\infty\}^\{\\infty\} \\frac\{f''\(\\tilde\{ u\}\)\}\{\\tilde\{ u\} - \\tilde\{ u\}_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\}\\rm\{d\}\\tilde\{ u\}\\\] \\\[f''\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\) - f_\{\\infty\}' = \\frac\{-1\}\{\\pi\} P \\int_\{-\\infty\}^\{\\infty\} \\frac\{f'\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\) - f_\{\\infty\}'\}\{\\tilde\{ u\} - \\tilde\{ u\}_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\}\\rm\{d\}\\tilde\{ u\}\\\] where \\\(P\\\) means that the principal part of the integral is taken at the singularity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08257
name: instrument line shape
def: "Idealized form of a feature in a spectrometer corresponding to a transition."
comment: "For Fourier-transform spectra, ILS varies with the apodization function used."
comment: "Ideal line shapes include Lorentzian, Gaussian, and Voigt functions, whose parameters are the line position, maximum height, and half-width."
synonym: "ILS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
