consider: goldbook:08252
consider: goldbook:08254
consider: goldbook:08298

[Term]
id: goldbook:08258
name: integrated intensity
def: "Area under a spectral band in an absorption spectrum where the absorption is linearly proportional to the amount of absorber in unit area."
comment: "The absorption quantity is usually a Beer-Lambert absorption coefficient, but recently \(\tilde{\nu} \alpha_{\rm{m}}''(\tilde{\nu})\), the wavenumber times the imaginary part of local molar polarizability, has been used for neat liquids to correct for dielectric effects."
comment: "The area under a band in a transmittance spectrum is not linearly proportional to the amount of absorber."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08285
consider: goldbook:08301
consider: goldbook:08617

[Term]
id: goldbook:08259
name: integration range
def: "Frequency or wavenumber range over which the integrated intensity of an absorption band is measured by numerical integration of the area under the band."
comment: "For Gaussian bands, integration over one full width half maximum to each side of the band centre yields \(\pu{98\%}\) of the area under the band."
comment: "Lorentzian bands integration over \(\pu{3.1}\) or \(\pu{15.9}\) full width half maximum to each side yields \(\pu{90\%}\) and \(\pu{98\%}\) of the band area."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08251
consider: goldbook:08252
consider: goldbook:08258
consider: goldbook:08285
