[Term]
id: goldbook:08291
name: spectrum
def: "Graph of a quantity derived from the radiant power at each wavelength \(frequency or wavenumber\) as ordinate plotted against the wavelength \(frequency or wavenumber\) of electromagnetic radiation as abscissa."
comment: "In mid-infrared and Raman spectroscopy, wavenumber is mostly used today, while it is more commonly replaced by wavelength in near infrared spectroscopy."
comment: "Quantities plotted include absorbance, absorption coefficient, transmittance, reflectance, luminescence."
