[Term]
id: goldbook:08296
name: two-dimensional correlation spectrum
def: "Three-dimensional surface in which two of the dimensions show frequency axes \(\\\( u_\{1\}\\\)\, \\\( u_\{2\}\\\)\) and the third axis shows a correlation function of the spectral intensities observed at \\\( u_\{1\}\\\) and \\\( u_\{2\}\\\)."
comment: "The shape of the surface shows whether the bands at the two wavenumbers are or are not correlated, and hence allows deductions to be made about the extent to which the different parts of the molecule are linked in their response to the applied external perturbation."
synonym: "2-D correlation spectrum" []
