[Term]
id: goldbook:08299
name: wavelength in medium
def: "Distance travelled by a wave of electromagnetic radiation in one cycle in a non-absorbing medium of real refractive index \\\(n\\\). \\\(\\lambda = \\lambda_\{0\}/n\\\)."
comment: "In spectroscopy, the unqualified term 'wavelength' frequently means the vacuum wavelength, and symbol \(\lambda\) frequently means \(\lambda_{0}\)."
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{m}\). Common unit: \(\pu{nm}\) or \(\pu{\upmu m}\)."
