[Term]
id: goldbook:08301
name: wavenumber in medium
def: "Reciprocal of wavelength of electromagnetic radiation. \\\(\\sigma = 1/\\lambda\\\)."
comment: "In spectroscopy, the unqualified term 'wavenumber' (sometimes referred to as "reciprocal centimetre" \(\pu{cm-1}\)) often means vacuum wavenumber, and symbol \(\sigma\) often means \(\tilde{\nu}\)."
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{m-1}\). Common unit: \(\pu{cm-1}\)."
synonym: "wavenumber" []
