[Term]
id: goldbook:08302
name: wavenumber in vacuum
def: "Reciprocal of the vacuum wavelength of electromagnetic radiation. \\\(\\tilde\{ u\} = 1/\\lambda_\{0\}\\\)."
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{m-1}\). Common unit: \(\pu{cm-1}\)."
comment: "The symbol \(\nu\) is often used instead of \(\tilde{\nu}\); this usage should be discouraged."
comment: "Wavenumber is related to the energy change, \(\Delta E\), induced when the radiation is absorbed by \(\Delta E = hc_{0}\tilde{\nu}\), where \(h\) is the Planck constant and \(c_{0}\) the speed of the radiation."
comment: "Wavenumber should only be used when no confusion with frequency is possible."
synonym: "vacuum wavenumber" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
