[Term]
id: goldbook:08311
name: 90° pulse
def: "Pulsed radiofrequency signal that rotates the bulk magnetization vector \(\\\(\\boldsymbol\{M\}_\{0\}\\\)\) of a nuclear spin to its orthogonal plane."
comment: "In a simple 1D NMR experiment, this is from the \(z\) axis to the \(xy\) plane."
