[Term]
id: goldbook:08321
name: combined rotation and multiple pulse spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy for obtaining high-resolution solid-state nuclear magnetic resonance spectra on nuclei with high gyromagnetic ratio such as \\\(\\ce\{^\{1\}H\}\\\) and \\\(\\ce\{^\{19\}F\}\\\)."
comment: "CRAMPS is based on coherent-averaging theory, which attempts to describe the time evolution of a system in terms of an average Hamiltonian derived from the density matrix formalism of quantum mechanics."
synonym: "CRAMPS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
