[Term]
id: goldbook:08327
name: cross polarization
def: "Technique in solid-state nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy that enables polarization from abundant spins such as \\\(\\ce\{^\{1\}H\}\\\) or \\\(\\ce\{^\{19\}F\}\\\) to be transferred to dilute spins such as \\\(\\ce\{^\{13\}C\}\\\) or \\\(\\ce\{^\{15\}N\}\\\) to enhance signal-to-noise ratio."
comment: "Cross polarization requires that nuclei are dipolar coupled to one another."
