[Term]
id: goldbook:08339
name: Ernst angle
def: "When signal averaging in a single-pulse nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy experiment\, flip angle giving the best signal-to-noise ratio for a given combination of spin-lattice relaxation time and repetition rate."
comment: "Named after Richard Ernst. It is employed to allow the maximum signal to noise to be generated in a fixed amount of time, \(\cos (\theta_{\rm{E}}) = e^{-(t_{\rm{d}} + t_{\rm{a}})/T_{1}}\), where \(t_{\rm{d}}\) is the interpulse delay, \(t_{\rm{a}}\) is the acquisition time, and \(T_{1}\) is longitudinal relaxation time."
