[Term]
id: goldbook:08351
name: heteronuclear decoupling
def: "Spin decoupling in nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy between two different nuclei \(e.g.\, \\\(\\ce\{^\{13\}C\}\\\) and \\\(\\ce\{^\{1\}H\}\\\)\) by appropriate excitation of the decoupled nucleus."
comment: "Heteronuclear decoupling is normally performed to simplify spectra or to enhance signal-to-noise ratio by combining individual components of the NMR signal."
comment: "Notation: \(\ce{^{13}C\{^{1}H}\}\) denotes observation of \(\ce{^{13}C}\) nucleus with simultaneous decoupling of \(\ce{^{1}H}\) nuclei."
