[Term]
id: goldbook:08381
name: non-uniform sampling
def: "Technique employed within a high dimensionality nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy experiment that acquires only a subset of the data points traditionally acquired linearly thus enabling a reduction in experiment time or an increased resolution in the resultant spectra."
comment: "NUS uses reconstruction methods to allow the extraction of complete sets of chemical shift information."
synonym: "NUS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
