[Term]
id: goldbook:08385
name: nuclear Overhauser effect
def: "Change of intensity of one resonance when the spin transitions of another are somehow perturbed from their equilibrium populations."
comment: "The nuclear Overhauser effect at nucleus \(i\) for perturbation of spin \(S\) is expressed as a relative intensity change between the equilibrium intensity (\(I\)) and that in the presence of the nOe (\(I_{\rm{o}}\)). \(\eta_{i}({\rm{S}}) = (I - I_{o})/I_{o}\). The effect may be given as a percentage \(\eta \times \pu{100 \%}\)."
comment: "\(\eta\) can be positive or negative depending on the motional properties of the molecule and the signs of the gyromagnetic ratios."
comment: "nOe allows a measure of through space rather than through bond interactions between nuclei and is proportional to the inverse \(6^{\rm{th}}\) power of the internuclear distance."
synonym: "nOe" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "nuclear Overhauser enhancement" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08386
name: nuclear Overhauser effect difference spectroscopy
def: "One dimensional nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy that yields\, through subtraction of spectra generated with and without selective excitation of a specific resonance\, the nuclear Overhauser enhancement of nuclei spatially close to a selectively excited nucleus."
synonym: "nOe difference spectroscopy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08384
consider: goldbook:08385

[Term]
id: goldbook:08387
name: nuclear Overhauser effect spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy based on the nuclear Overhauser effect to observe nuclei that are close to each other in space."
comment: "A NOESY spectrum yields through space correlations via dipolar cross-relaxation."
comment: "For small molecules, NOE may be observed between protons that are up to \(\pu{0.4 nm}\) apart, while the upper limit for large molecules is about \(\pu{0.5 nm}\)."
comment: "NOESY also detects chemical and conformational exchange, when it is termed exchange spectroscopy (EXSY)."
comment: "NOESY is typically run as a homonuclear \(\ce{^{1}H}\) experiment."
synonym: "NOESY" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
synonym: "nuclear Overhauser enhancement spectroscopy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
