id: goldbook:08391
name: phase correction
def: "Linear combination of the real and imaginary parts of a 1-D nuclear magnetic resonance spectrum to produce peaks with pure absorption mode line shape."
comment: "The phase correction is normally described by the automatic or manual setting of a fixed zero order and a frequency dependent first order phase constant."
