id: goldbook:08397
name: pulsed-field gradient
def: "Short\, timed pulse in nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy that momentarily destroys the magnetic field homogeneity within the sample through a spatial-dependent field intensity."
comment: "A PFG is characterized by its power, shape, duration and axis."
comment: "PFG techniques are used in magnetic resonance imaging, spatially-selective NMR, and diffusion ordered NMR spectroscopy (DOSY)."
comment: "The net result of the pulse is that spins are dispersed in the transverse plane (defocussed) and produce zero net magnetization."
