[Term]
id: goldbook:08402
name: radiation damping
def: "Line-broadening effect on intense signals in high field nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy."
comment: "Radiation damping can also produce other effects including changes to amplitude and phase of adjacent peaks."
comment: "Radiation damping occurs when the rotating transverse magnetization of the sample is intense enough to induce large enough electromotive force in the radiofrequency coil strong enough that it feeds back to the sample. This causes a rotation of magnetization back to the \(+z\) axis and results in line-broadening of the intense peak."
