def: "In nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy\, one of two equally sized blocks of frequency data \\\(\\pu\{90\\!^\{\\circ\}\}\\\) out of phase to each other produced by Fourier transformation of the time domain signal."
comment: "Usually only the real frequency data is displayed and in simple 1D spectra equates to the NMR signals being absorption mode (in-phase)."
