[Term]
id: goldbook:08418
name: spin
def: "Intrinsic angular momentum of a nucleus \(or other sub-atomic particle\)."
comment: "In nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy, only nuclei with spin \(I \gt 0\) are observable."
comment: "Nuclei with a spin of \(½\) generate the simplest nuclear magnetic resonance spectra and are thus the most commonly studied."
comment: "The magnitude of nuclear spin is \((h/2\pi)\sqrt{I(I + 1)}\) where \(I\) is the spin quantum number and \(h\) is the Planck constant."
comment: "The spin of a nucleus is dependent on the numbers and alignments of the spins of its individual protons and neutrons."
