[Term]
id: goldbook:08432
name: three-dimensional nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy in which data are collected in three time domains."
comment: "A 3-D NMR experiment may be constructed from a 2-D NMR experiment by inserting an additional indirect evolution time and a second mixing period between the first mixing period and the direct data acquisition."
synonym: "3-D NMR" []
