[Term]
id: goldbook:08435
name: total correlation spectroscopy
def: "Two-dimensional nuclear magnetic resonance homonuclear correlation experiment\, which creates correlations between all protons within a given spin system\, not just between geminal or vicinal protons as in COSY."
comment: "TOCSY uses a spin lock to allow propagation of magnetization through scalar couplings."
synonym: "TOCSY" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "homonuclear Hartmann-Hahn spectroscopy (HOHAHA)" []
