[Term]
id: goldbook:08438
name: triple-resonance nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy using three NMR-active nuclei."
comment: "For proteins the three nuclei are usually \(\ce{^{1}H}\) hydrogen, \(\ce{^{13}C}\) carbon, and \(\ce{^{15}N}\) nitrogen, which requires suitable labelling of the sample."
synonym: "triple-resonance NMR" []
