[Term]
id: goldbook:08457
name: axial viewing mode
def: "Inductively-coupled plasma optical emission spectrometer configuration in which the entrance slit is aligned with the main plasma axis."
comment: "Matrix interferences, which originate in the cooler plasma tail, can degrade precision and accuracy."
comment: "The large amount of light captured in this method, includes information from the sample of interest plus background, which can be considerable."
