[Term]
id: goldbook:08458
name: background continuum emission
def: "Intense continuous background usually observed in laser-induced breakdown spectra."
comment: "The continuum emission originates from Bremsstrahlung radiation, which predominates the first part of the plasma life time and decreases with further plasma evolution."
