id: goldbook:08478
name: gate delay
def: "Time between the application of a laser pulse and the start of detection in laser-induced breakdown spectroscopy."
comment: "The gate delay varies from some hundreds of nanoseconds to several microseconds."
comment: "Use of a suitable gate delay allows the high intensity background continuum emission present in the early stages of plasma formation to be removed."
