name: inductively-coupled plasma spectrometry
def: "Measurement method of atomic spectroscopy that uses an inductively-coupled plasma to excite and ionize atoms."
comment: "ICP methods are described by their method of detection of ions in the plasma and include inductively-coupled plasma optical emission spectroscopy, and inductively-coupled plasma mass spectrometry."
synonym: "ICP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "inductively-coupled plasma spectroscopy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
