consider: goldbook:08488

[Term]
id: goldbook:08491
name: inductively-coupled plasma optical emission spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of atomic spectroscopy that uses an inductively-coupled plasma to excite and ionize atoms with measurement of the number and kind of ions in the plasma from their emission of electromagnetic radiation \(see optical emission spectroscopy\)."
synonym: "ICP-OES" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08216
consider: goldbook:08242
consider: goldbook:08488
consider: goldbook:08513

[Term]
id: goldbook:08492
name: inductively-coupled plasma robustness
def: "Ability of an inductively-coupled plasma to withstand slight modification in the operating conditions and/or matrix composition with no significant changes in its fundamental characteristics \(i.e.\, temperatures\, electron number density\) or the analytical figures of merit \(i.e.\, sensitivity\, detection limits or signal-to-noise ratio\)"
synonym: "plasma robustness" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08282
consider: goldbook:08488

[Term]
id: goldbook:08493
name: inductively-coupled plasma thermal pinch
def: "Decrease in the inductively-coupled plasma volume normally caused when an organic volatile solution is delivered to it. Organic vapours diffuse towards the outermost area of the plasma and its volume decreases."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08488

[Term]
id: goldbook:08494
name: inductively-coupled plasma torch
def: "Quartz component of an inductively-coupled plasma spectrometer where the plasma is generated and stabilized."
comment: "In ICP the torch is an open three concentric tubes assembly allowing the introduction of the three gas streams constituting the plasma. The inner tube of the torch can be made of a different material such as alumina and is usually called the injector."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08489

[Term]
id: goldbook:08495
name: initial plasma radiation zone
def: "Inductively-coupled plasma volume in inductively-coupled plasma optical emission spectroscopy where the analytically-relevant light emission begins to be observed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08488
consider: goldbook:08491

[Term]
id: goldbook:08496
name: interference curve
def: "Graph of absorbance or intensity plotted as a function of the concentration of an interfering element in an atomic spectroscopy experiment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08216

[Term]
id: goldbook:08497
name: inverse Bremsstrahlung
def: "Absorption of photon energy by free electrons."
comment: "Inverse Bremsstrahlung increases the kinetic energy of the electrons, which is important for heating the plasma."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08498
name: ionic cloud
def: "Gas phase containing free ions of analyte."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08499
name: laser ablation
def: "Removal of material as an aerosol from a surface on irradiation by a laser beam."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08500
name: laser induced breakdown spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of atomic spectroscopy that uses a focused laser beam to ablate\, atomize and excite atoms from a sample surface with subsequent measurement of the generated electromagnetic radiation."
synonym: "LIBS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08216
consider: goldbook:08242

[Term]
id: goldbook:08501
name: laser-induced breakdown spectrum
def: "Emission spectrum generated as a consequence of the decay of the excited states generated in a laser-induced plasma that consists of a continuous background and element-specific atomic or ionic lines and molecular bands."
comment: "LIBS spectra cover a wide wavelength range. Commonly, LIBS measurements are taken between the wavelengths of \(\pu{200 nm}\) and \(\pu{1000 nm}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08291
consider: goldbook:08300
consider: goldbook:08502

[Term]
id: goldbook:08502
name: laser-induced plasma
def: "Local plasma formed by the interaction between a laser beam and a solid sample and initiated by the production of primary electrons by multiphoton ionization and thermionic photoemission mechanisms."
comment: "As well as electrons, laser-induced plasma contains ions, and neutral atoms as well as excited species of the ablated matter. Decay of these excited species generates the light emission analysed in laser-induced breakdown spectroscopy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08500

[Term]
id: goldbook:08503
name: line-broadening
def: "Increase in the theoretical width of a spectral line owing to thermal motion of emitting atoms \(Doppler effect\)\, to electric field \(Stark effect\)\, to self-absorption and to pressure \(Lorentz effect\)."
comment: "Line-broadening increases the measurement uncertainty of a measurement."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08550

[Term]
id: goldbook:08504
name: line profile
def: "Graph of the variation of emitted radiation intensity as a function of wavelength \(emission line\) or the variation of the absorption factor as a function of wavelength \(absorption line\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242
consider: goldbook:08300

[Term]
id: goldbook:08505
name: low sample consumption system
def: "Liquid-sample introduction system to an inductively-coupled plasma spectrometer adapted to work at sample flow rates below \\\(\\pu\{100 \\upmu L min-1\}\\\)."
comment: "The system is normally composed of a micro-nebulizer and a low inner volume spray chamber."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08489
consider: goldbook:08510

[Term]
id: goldbook:08506
name: measurement efficiency
def: "Number of detector events per atom in the sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08507
name: microwave cavity
def: "Resonant cavity that permits focusing a microwave field inside a discharge tube thus giving rise to a standing wave."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08508
name: microwave-induced plasma
def: "Plasma generated in a microwave cavity."
comment: "The plasma results as a consequence of ionization of a given gas in presence of electrons and a microwave field."
synonym: "microwave plasma" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08507

[Term]
id: goldbook:08509
name: nebulization
def: "Conversion of a liquid into an aerosol consisting of droplets suspended in a gas stream."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08510
name: nebulizer
def: "Device for producing nebulization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08509

[Term]
id: goldbook:08511
name: non-specific emission or attenuation
def: "Electromagnetic radiation\, within the bandpass filter used\, emitted by\, or absorption caused by\, atoms\, molecules and radicals that are subject to the atomizer by all components\, apart from the analyte\, that are present there during measurement."
comment: "These effects include scattering or absorption effects by solid particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242

[Term]
id: goldbook:08512
name: normal plasma analytical zone
def: "Inductively-coupled plasma volume mainly responsible for emission of analytically-useful light because processes leading to excited species\, such as droplet desolvation\, element vaporization\, atomization \(or ionization\) and excitation have been completed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08488

[Term]
id: goldbook:08513
name: optical emission spectroscopy
def: "Measurement principle of atomic emission spectroscopy in which the emitted electromagnetic radiation is in the range of frequencies from the infrared\, through visible\, to the ultra-violet region."
comment: "OES is used as the detector in inductively-coupled plasma optical emission spectroscopy, and glow-discharge optical emission spectroscopy."
synonym: "OES" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
