consider: goldbook:08483
consider: goldbook:08491

[Term]
id: goldbook:08514
name: overall efficiency of atomization
def: "In atomic spectroscopy\, mass of analyte converted into free atoms in the atomizer divided by mass of analyte entering the dispersion device."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08216

[Term]
id: goldbook:08515
name: Penning excitation
def: "Collisional excitation and ionization mechanism of inductively-coupled plasma spectrometry involving analyte atoms and metastable argon atoms."
synonym: "Penning ionization" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08489

[Term]
id: goldbook:08516
name: percentage transmission
def: "In atomic spectroscopy\, flux of mass of sample divided by the flux of mass of solvent blank\, measured under the same conditions\, expressed as a percentage."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08216

[Term]
id: goldbook:08517
name: permanent modifier
def: "Substance added together with the sample or standards in electrothermal atomic absorption spectroscopy that is refractory\, or forms a refractory species \(e.g.\, a carbide\)\, and thus does not need to be renewed for several atomization cycles."
comment: "This is a particular type of chemical modifier for electrothermal AAS."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08471

[Term]
id: goldbook:08518
name: plasma arc
def: "Plasma formed by an arc-discharge."
comment: "The discharge is blown through a suitable orifice to form a plasma jet. The high-temperature, electric field-free gaseous region is designed as the region of observation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08469

[Term]
id: goldbook:08519
name: plasma excitation temperature
def: "Temperature governing the number density of atomic species in their ground state and excited states following a Boltzmann distribution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08520
name: plasma gases
def: "Gas streams used to maintain and stabilize the inductively-coupled plasma. The external stream is the main constituent of the plasma and confines the plasma avoiding melting of the torch walls; the intermediate gas stream keeps the plasma at a given height above the top of the torch and\, the central stream carries the aerosol and promotes its injection in the plasma central channel."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08488

[Term]
id: goldbook:08521
name: plasma induction zone
def: "Inductively-coupled plasma volume where there is a maximum interaction between the electromagnetic field and the plasma gas \(mostly argon\). This is the plasma’s hottest area and has a toroidal configuration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08488

[Term]
id: goldbook:08522
name: plasma ionization temperature
def: "Temperature associated with the energy level of plasma ions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08246

[Term]
id: goldbook:08523
name: plasma local thermodynamic equilibrium
def: "Condition for which the temperatures estimated from different particles \(atoms\, molecules\, ions\, electrons\) constituting a plasma are locally coincident."
synonym: "LTE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08524
name: plasma shielding
def: "Prevention of laser pulse energy from reaching a sample surface as a result of the presence of a laser-induced plasma."
comment: "The main process leading to plasma shielding is the absorption of the laser energy by electrons (inverse Bremsstrahlung) and multiphoton ionization (mainly relevant for shorter laser wavelengths)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08497
consider: goldbook:08502

[Term]
id: goldbook:08525
name: plasma termination
def: "Extinction of the plasma after a laser pulse as a consequence of self-absorption \(quenching\) and recombination of electrons and ions."
comment: "The time elapsed between initiation and extinction of the plasma ranges from tenths of microseconds to a few milliseconds."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08526
name: platform atomization
def: "Sample support made of graphite that is inserted into the atomizer tube in electrothermal atomic absorption spectroscopy. The sample\, a liquid or a solid\, is deposited onto this platform\, from which it undergoes all the transformations leading to atomization. The use of a platform delays atomization\, until a more stabilized temperature in the gas phase is reached."
synonym: "L’vov platform" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08471

[Term]
id: goldbook:08527
name: pneumatic nebulizers
def: "Nebulizers for which the aerosol generation principle is based on the exposure of the liquid sample to a high velocity gas stream."
comment: "Most common designs include cross flow, concentric, parallel path, entrained and Babington and V Groove."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08510

[Term]
id: goldbook:08528
name: preheating inductively-coupled plasma zone
def: "Inductively-coupled plasma volume where tertiary aerosols suffer from complete solvent evaporation\, element salt vaporization and dissociation into atoms."
synonym: "preheating plasma zone" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08488

[Term]
id: goldbook:08529
name: primary aerosol
def: "Aerosol generated by a nebulizer."
comment: "Usually, primary aerosols contain coarse droplets, they are polydisperse in terms of drop diameters and they are turbulent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08510

[Term]
id: goldbook:08531
name: pulse energy
def: "Total optical energy content of a laser pulse. Integral of optical power over pulse duration."
comment: "Pulse energies range from microjoules to millijoules for Q-switched lasers, whereas mode-locked lasers achieve much lower pulse energies (picojoules, nanojoules or sometimes several microjoules)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08530

[Term]
id: goldbook:08532
name: pulsed laser
def: "Laser system that emits electromagnetic radiation in the form of pulses of a defined and constant duration."
comment: "A pulsed laser produces no continuous optical wave."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242

[Term]
id: goldbook:08533
name: pyrolysis curve
def: "Graph of absorbance against pyrolysis temperature in electrothermal atomic absorption spectroscopy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08471

[Term]
id: goldbook:08534
name: quartz atomizer
def: "Atomizer that is used to atomize those elements that form volatile species \(e.g.\, hydrides\) at relatively low temperatures \(e.g.\, \\\(\\pu\{1000^\{\\circ\}C\}\\\) or below\)."
comment: "These can be heated externally or positioned in a flame (see flame in flame atomic spectroscopy)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08476

[Term]
id: goldbook:08535
name: radial viewing mode
def: "Inductively-coupled plasma optical emission spectrometer configuration in which the plasma and the entrance slit are perpendicular and from which the signal is taken perpendicularly to the main plasma axis."
comment: "This configuration yields lower sensitivities than the axial viewing mode."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08457
consider: goldbook:08491

[Term]
id: goldbook:08536
name: radiofrequency generator
def: "Component of an inductively-coupled plasma spectrometer responsible for the generation of alternating current in the radiofrequency portion of the electromagnetic spectrum \(see table\)."
synonym: "RF generator" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08279
consider: goldbook:08489

[Term]
id: goldbook:08537
name: radiofrequency glow discharge optical emission spectroscopy
def: "Optical emission spectroscopy in which a radiofrequency-powered glow discharge is operated with frequencies in the low megahertz range."
comment: "The use of these frequencies establishes a negative direct current (DC)-bias voltage on the sample surface. The DC-bias is the result of an alternating current waveform that is centered about negative potential; as such it more or less represents the average potential residing on the sample surface. Radio-frequency has ability to appear to flow through insulators (non-conductive materials)."
synonym: "RF-GD-OES" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08481
consider: goldbook:08513

[Term]
id: goldbook:08538
name: reference flux density
def: "Intensity transmitted by the reference medium in a double-beam spectrometer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08241

[Term]
id: goldbook:08539
name: reflected power
def: "Incident power that is not absorbed by the plasma."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08487

[Term]
id: goldbook:08540
name: repetition rate
def: "Number of laser pulses emitted by a pulsed laser system per unit time."
comment: "For laser systems with pulse duration in the nanosecond regime repetition rates range from \(\pu{1 Hz}\) to \(\pu{20 Hz}\), whereas for femtosecond laser systems increased repetition rates up to \(\pu{1000 Hz}\) are possible."
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{Hz}\)."
synonym: "pulse frequency" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08530
consider: goldbook:08532

[Term]
id: goldbook:08541
name: resonant inelastic X-ray scattering
def: "Measurement method of inelastic X-ray spectroscopy that uses a hard or soft X-ray beam to excite transitions of core-level electrons into empty energy levels. The subsequent transition of an electron into the core state is accompanied by X-ray emission with characteristic momentum and energy."
comment: "The incident photon energy is selected for resonance with an X-ray absorption edge of the system, such that the observed shifts in momentum and energy provide element-specific chemical sensitivity, with the capacity to distinguish the same element located at inequivalent sites."
synonym: "RIXS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "resonant X-ray Raman" []
synonym: "resonant X-ray emission" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08246

[Term]
id: goldbook:08542
name: Saha’s ionization equation
def: "Equation that relates the ionization state of an element present in a gas in thermal equilibrium to the temperature and the pressure of the medium."
comment: "For a gas composed of a single atomic species, the Saha equation is written: \[(n_{i+1}/n_{i}) n_{\rm{e}} = 2\lambda^{-3}(g_{i+1}/g_{i}) \exp[-(\epsilon_{i + 1} - \epsilon_{i})/kT]\] where \(n_{i}\) is the number density of atoms with \(i\) electrons removed, \(g_{i}\) is the degeneracy of the \(i^{\rm{th}}\) state, \(\epsilon_{i}\) is the ionization energy of the \(i^{\rm{th}}\) state, \(n_{\rm{e}}\) is the number density of electrons, \(\lambda\) is the thermal de Broglie wavelength of an electron, \(k\) is the Boltzmann constant, and \(T\) is the thermodynamic temperature of the gas."
comment: "The thermal de Broglie wavelength is given by: \[\lambda = \sqrt{\frac{h^{2}}{2\uppi m_{\rm{e}} kT}}\] where \(h\) is the Planck constant, \(k\) the Boltzmann constant, \(T\) temperature, and \(m_{\rm{e}}\) the mass of an electron."
synonym: "Saha–Langmuir equation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08543
name: sample flux density
def: "Intensity transmitted by the atomizer when the latter is supplied with the sample solution or a reference solution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08538

[Term]
id: goldbook:08544
name: saturator
def: "Buffer containing interfering element\(s\) in sufficient quantity to reach the limit of enhancement or dispersion \(i.e.\, saturation\) of the interference curve."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08545
name: sequential detection
def: "Sequential spectrometers use a dispersive element \(grating\) in combination with entrance and exit slits for selection of specific wavelengths. Geometric arrangements include the Czerny-Turner and the Ebert-geometry\, both offering high resolution measurements. However\, they do not permit simultaneous recording of different spectral lines\, even for single emission line intensity\, and adjacent spectral background has also to be measured sequentially."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08549
consider: goldbook:08550

[Term]
id: goldbook:08546
name: solvent blank flux density
def: "Intensity transmitted by the atomizer when the latter is supplied with the solvent blank."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08547
name: solvent nucleation
def: "Solvent condensation on solid particles or droplets contained in an aerosol."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08548
name: solvent transport rate
def: "Mass of solvent\, both in liquid and vapour forms\, reaching an inductively-coupled plasma per unit of time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08488

[Term]
id: goldbook:08549
name: spectral background
def: "Electromagnetic radiation\, within the bandpass used\, emitted by\, and/or in the case of atomic absorption spectroscopy\, absorbed in\, the atomizer when nothing is supplied to the atomizer but the gases involved in its operation."
comment: "In the case of flame atomic spectroscopy, the term "flame background" is used."
synonym: "flame background" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242
consider: goldbook:08451
consider: goldbook:08475

[Term]
id: goldbook:08550
name: spectral line
def: "In atomic spectroscopy\, a very narrow band of frequencies of electromagnetic radiation emitted or absorbed by atoms\, which undergo a single electronic transition."
comment: "A distinction is made between lines corresponding to transition of neutral atoms (e.g., \(\ce{Ba I}\ \pu{553.548 nm}\) and \(\pu{577.762 nm}\)) and ions (e.g., \(\ce{Ba II}\ \pu{455.403 nm}\))."
comment: "The radiation is centred on a peak whose wavelength characterizes the line and which corresponds to the emission or absorption maximum."
synonym: "line" []
synonym: "spectral line" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
