[Term]
id: goldbook:08572
name: atomic polar tensor
def: "3 × 3 tensor that gives the change in the components of the molecular dipole moment when the atom is displaced in three-dimensional space."
comment: "APTs have been widely used in the analysis of infrared absorption intensities."
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{C}\). Common unit: \(\pu{D Å-1 \approx 3.33564E-30 C}\)."
comment: "The rows correspond to different components of the dipole moment and the columns to \(x\), \(y\ (\rm{g})\) and \(z\) displacements."
