[Term]
id: goldbook:08577
name: Christiansen effect
def: "Collections of solid particles that are transparent to electromagnetic radiation of a particular wavelength and are slightly larger than the wavelength of the radiation transmit poorly due to reflection and scattering from the interfaces. The transmission increases markedly at wavenumbers at which the refractive index of the particles is close to that of the surrounding medium."
comment: "The Christiansen effect frequently causes strong absorption bands from coarsely ground particles to be distorted due to the change in refractive index associated with the anomalous dispersion of the refractive index through the absorption region."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242
consider: goldbook:08281
consider: goldbook:08300

[Term]
id: goldbook:08578
name: Christiansen filter
def: "Optical filter based on the Christiansen effect."
comment: "Such filters have been made from quartz particles in air, immersed in \(\ce{CCl4}\), or immersed in mixtures of \(\ce{CCl4}\) and \(\ce{CS2}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08577

[Term]
id: goldbook:08579
name: coherent anti-Stokes Raman spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of Raman spectroscopy that uses third-order susceptibility and is one of several four-wave mixing spectroscopies. The excitation is through lasers of wavenumber \\\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{1\}\\\) and \\\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{2\}\\\)\, which coincide spatially and temporally in the sample and produce an output laser of wavenumber \\\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{3\} = 2\\tilde\{ u\}_\{1\} - \\tilde\{ u\}_\{2\}\\\)."
comment: "Experimentally, \(\tilde{\nu}_{1}\) is kept constant and \(\tilde{\nu}_{2}\) is scanned. A laser beam output is observed at the wavenumber for anti-Stokes Raman scattering \(\tilde{\nu}_{1} + \tilde{\nu}_{\rm{M}}\) when \(\tilde{\nu}_{1} - \tilde{\nu}_{2} = \tilde{\nu}_{\rm{M}}\), where \(\tilde{\nu}_{\rm{M}}\) is the wavenumber of an active vibration in the sample."
comment: "The Raman scattered radiation emerges as a laser beam instead of being scattered into three dimensions, thus greatly enhancing the sensitivity over that in normal Raman scattering."
synonym: "CARS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08302
consider: goldbook:08570
consider: goldbook:08667
consider: goldbook:08669

[Term]
id: goldbook:08580
name: combination transition
def: "Transition in which more than one vibration changes its degree of excitation; i.e.\, in which more than one vibrational quantum number changes."
comment: "Combination band results from a combination transition."
comment: "Combination transitions are either sum or difference transitions, although some authors restrict them to sum transitions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08581
name: continuous scan interferometer
def: "Interferometer in which the optical path difference is continually changed."
comment: "Continuous scan interferometer is typically used for Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy."
comment: "In rapid-scan interferometers, the rate of change of optical path difference is above \(\pu{0.05 cm s-1}\), high enough that no additional modulation is needed."
comment: "In slow scan interferometers, the rate of change of optical path difference is less than \(\pu{0.05 cm s-1}\) and a mechanical chopper or some other ancillary modulation is frequently used to provide an adequate modulation frequency."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08605
consider: goldbook:08653
consider: goldbook:08681

[Term]
id: goldbook:08582
name: Coriolis coupling
def: "Coupling between rotational and vibrational molecular motion caused by Coriolis forces."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08583

[Term]
id: goldbook:08583
name: Coriolis force
def: "In vibrational theory\, the motion of a polyatomic molecule is usually initially regarded as the independent superposition of a rotation and a vibration\, with the vibration considered in a coordinate system that rotates with the molecule. This initial treatment must be corrected for centrifugal forces and for Coriolis forces. The Coriolis force on an atom is given by \\\(F_\{\\rm\{Coriolis\}\} = 2m v_\{\\rm\{a\}\} \\omega \\sin \\varphi\\\)\, where \\\(m\\\) is the mass of the atom\, \\\(v_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\) is its apparent velocity in the rotating coordinate system\, \\\(\\omega\\\) is the angular velocity of the coordinate system\, and \\\(\\varphi\\\) is the angle between the velocity vector and the axis of rotation."
comment: "SI unit: \(\ce{N}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08584
name: critical angle
def: "Smallest angle of incidence at which total internal reflection occurs."
comment: "If \(n_{2}\) and \(n_{1}\) are the refractive indices, and \(n_{2} > n_{1}\), at the boundary, \(\sin \theta_{\rm{c}} = n_1/n_2\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08585
name: deformation vibration
def: "Vibration in which the dominant change from equilibrium is in one or more valence angles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08586
name: depolarization ratio
def: "Raman intensity with the electric vector of the scattered electromagnetic radiation perpendicular to that of the incident radiation divided by the Raman intensity with electric vectors parallel."
comment: "In normal Raman scattering with linearly polarized exciting radiation, \(\rho \le 0.75\) for totally symmetric vibrations and \(\rho = 0.75\) for all other vibrations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
