[Term]
id: goldbook:08589
name: divided spinning cell
def: "Measuring instrument for Raman spectroscopy incorporating a dish-shaped cell that is divided by a vertical partition through its middle to allow different liquids in its two halves. It is rotated about a vertical axis through its centre and the Raman scattered radiation from each half is measured alternately. With a standard liquid in one half and a sample in the other it is used to determine Raman scattering intensities relative to the standard."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
