[Term]
id: goldbook:08592
name: electrical harmonicity
def: "Influence of the linear term\, \\\(\\Sigma_\{k\} \(\\partial \\boldsymbol\{\\mu\}/\\partial Q_\{k\}\) Q_\{k\}\\\)\, in the expansion of the electric dipole moment. \\\(Q\\\) is the normal coordinate."
comment: "Electrical harmonicity should not be confused with mechanical harmonicity."
