[Term]
id: goldbook:08593
name: electron energy loss spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of vibrational spectroscopy in which a constant-energy beam of electrons passes through or is reflected from a sample and the energy distribution in the transmitted or reflected beam is analysed to give a spectrum of number of electrons against electron energy loss."
comment: "EELS is used for the study of electronic states and has an energy resolution of \(\pu{0.25 eV}\) or better (corresponding to an approximate wavenumber of \(\pu{2000 cm-1}\))."
synonym: "EELS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
