consider: goldbook:08503

[Term]
id: goldbook:08620
name: interference fringes
def: "Sinusoidal intensity variation due to interference of electromagnetic radiation that undergoes multiple reflection between two flat and parallel surfaces."
comment: "A spectrum of interference fringes is termed a channel spectrum."
comment: "Interference fringes are frequently observed in the transmission spectrum of a cell with flat windows and in non-scattering polymer films."
synonym: "channel fringes" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
