[Term]
id: goldbook:08625
name: inverse Raman scattering
def: "Raman scattering showing absorption when Stokes Raman scattering exceeds anti-Stokes Raman scattering\, in an experiment in which a sample is simultaneously illuminated by coincident beams from a continuum source and a pulse laser at \\\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{0\}\\\). Energy is absorbed from the continuum at \\\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{0\} + \\tilde\{ u\}_\{\\rm\{s\}\}\\\) where \\\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{\\rm\{s\}\}\\\) is the wavenumber of a Raman-active vibration in the sample that is excited by this process\, and this energy is emitted at \\\(\\tilde\{ u\}_\{0\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
