[Term]
id: goldbook:08655
name: ordinary wave
def: "In a uniaxial crystal electromagnetic radiation with electric vector perpendicular to the optic axis and which obeys the normal laws of refraction."
comment: "In uniaxial crystals the optic axis coincides with the symmetry axis. The refractive index of the crystal is the same in all directions perpendicular to the optic axis but is different along the optic axis. Consequently, electromagnetic rays or waves that do not travel along the optic axis experience different refractive indices in different directions perpendicular to their direction of propagation. Two waves result, one has its electric vector perpendicular to the optic axis and forms the ordinary wave. The other is the extraordinary wave."
synonym: "ordinary ray" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242
consider: goldbook:08600

[Term]
id: goldbook:08656
name: overtone transition
def: "Transition between the ground state and a state in which a single mode of vibration is multiply excited."
comment: "An overtone band results from an overtone transition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08637

[Term]
id: goldbook:08657
name: pATR spectrum
def: "\\\(-\\log_\{10\}\\\) of the spectrum obtained in attenuated total reflection spectroscopy."
comment: "The term is used to avoid the confusing, but common and incorrect, practice of calling it the absorbance spectrum."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08291
consider: goldbook:08573

[Term]
id: goldbook:08658
name: photoacoustic saturation
def: "Condition in photoacoustic spectroscopy in which all bands with greater than a certain absorption intensity appear to have the same intensity."
comment: "Photoacoustic saturation arises when the sample is optically opaque and thermally thin, i.e., when the thermal diffusion depth, \(L\), is greater than the optical absorption depth, \(\mu_{\beta}\), and less than the sample thickness. The condition may be relieved by increasing the modulation frequency sufficiently that \(L\) becomes less than \(\mu_{\beta}\), i.e., that the sample becomes thermally thick."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08650
consider: goldbook:08696

[Term]
id: goldbook:08659
name: photothermal spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of spectroscopy in which the absorption of electromagnetic radiation by a sample is detected as a result of the heat generated by the absorption."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242

[Term]
id: goldbook:08660
name: polarized Raman band
def: "Raman band with depolarization ratio \\\(\\rho \\le 0.75\\\) for linear polarized incident radiation in normal Raman spectroscopy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08586
consider: goldbook:08587
consider: goldbook:08665
consider: goldbook:08669

[Term]
id: goldbook:08661
name: potential coupling
def: "Coupling of vibrational displacements through terms in the vibrational potential energy. The second-order \(quadratic\) terms cause harmonic potential coupling while the cubic and higher terms cause anharmonic potential coupling."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08635
consider: goldbook:08636
consider: goldbook:08707

[Term]
id: goldbook:08662
name: p-polarization
def: "Polarization when electromagnetic radiation is incident upon a surface with its electric vector in the plane of incidence and\, therefore\, inclined to the reflecting surface unless the incidence is normal."
synonym: "TM polarization" []
synonym: "transverse magnetic polarization" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242

[Term]
id: goldbook:08663
name: pressure broadening
def: "Increase in the line width of a spectral line of a gas due to molecular collisions and other intermolecular interactions that reduce the lifetime of an excited state."
comment: "At pressures sufficiently low that the line width is far smaller than the line wavelength, the line width increases linearly with pressure, the broadening is homogeneous and the line shape is Lorentzian."
synonym: "collision broadening" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08300
consider: goldbook:08550

[Term]
id: goldbook:08664
name: quantum cascade laser
def: "Laser that emits mid-infrared radiation."
comment: "A QCL can be used as a source for infrared spectroscopy."
synonym: "QCL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08617
consider: goldbook:08618

[Term]
id: goldbook:08665
name: Raman band
def: "Spectral band in Raman spectroscopy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08285
consider: goldbook:08669

[Term]
id: goldbook:08666
name: Raman optical activity
def: "Phenomenon that vibrations in chiral molecules and materials Raman scattering right circularly polarized incident radiation to a different extent than left circularly polarized incident radiation."
comment: "In practice, the circular polarization of the exciting beam, or of the scattered beam, or of both beams simultaneously, may be selected. Raman optical activity is usually specified as 'right minus left' circular polarizations, in unfortunate contrast to the 'left minus right' specification that is universal in vibrational circular polarization and other forms of optical activity."
synonym: "ROA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08667
name: Raman scattering
def: "Inelastic scattering of electromagnetic radiation by molecules that are excited to higher energy levels."
comment: "Normal Raman scattering occurs through changes in polarizability of a molecule during a vibration, not the hyper-polarizabilities, and is excited by radiation that is not in resonance with electronic transitions in the sample."
comment: "The energy of the scattered photon can be lesser (Stokes Raman scattering) or greater (anti-Stokes Raman scattering) than that of the incident photon."
synonym: "normal Raman scattering" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08242
consider: goldbook:08245
consider: goldbook:08246
consider: goldbook:08570
consider: goldbook:08683

[Term]
id: goldbook:08668
name: Raman shift
def: "Difference in wavenumber between the incident and scattered electromagnetic radiation in Raman spectroscopy."
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{m-1}\). Common unit: \(\pu{cm-1}\)."
synonym: "Raman wavenumber shift" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
