[Term]
id: goldbook:08692
name: symmetric
def: "Term used in at least two senses in vibrational spectroscopy. In general usage\, a symmetric molecule is a molecule with high symmetry. In more specific usage\, a property is symmetric with respect to a symmetry element if it remains unchanged by the action of the corresponding symmetry operation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
