[Term]
id: goldbook:08702
name: transflection
def: "Reflection absorption at near-normal incidence when the thickness of the absorbing medium is large enough to yield an interpretable spectrum. The substrate is usually a mirror for mid-infrared measurements and a ceramic disk for near-infrared measurements. The angle of incidence is typically between \\\(\\pu\{0\\!^\{\\circ\}\}\\\) and \\\(\\pu\{45\\!^\{\\circ\}\}\\\)."
comment: "Transflection is widely used in IR microscopy and is particularly convenient for measuring transmission-like spectra in a near-infrared instrument configured for diffuse reflection measurements by mounting the sample on a non-absorbing diffusely reflecting substrate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08222
consider: goldbook:08236
consider: goldbook:08291
consider: goldbook:08647

[Term]
id: goldbook:08703
name: transmission Raman spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of Raman spectroscopy in which the sample is illuminated on one side and the Raman signal is collected from the opposite side."
comment: "text"
synonym: "TRS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08669

[Term]
id: goldbook:08704
name: vibrational circular dichroism
def: "Circular dichroism\, \\\(k^\{\\rm\{L\}\} – k^\{\\rm\{R\}\}\\\)\, for vibrational transitions."
comment: "Vibrations in chiral molecules and materials absorb left circularly polarized radiation to a different extent than right circularly polarized radiation."
synonym: "VCD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
