name: drift current
def: "Electric current caused by electric drift."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08777
consider: goldbook:08797

[Term]
id: goldbook:08794
name: drift velocity
def: "Average velocity that a charge carrier attains due to an applied electric field."
comment: "If an electric field is absent, charge carriers move randomly. An applied electric field induces drift (net movement) of charge carriers in a preferred direction. Average net velocity of this movement is called the drift velocity \(v_{\rm{d}}\)."
comment: "The drift velocity of a charge carrier is directly proportional to the applied electric field strength \(E\):  \[v_{\rm{d}} = \mu E\]  where constant \(\mu\) is the charge carrier mobility in the given material."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08775
consider: goldbook:08780

[Term]
id: goldbook:08795
name: electret
def: "Dielectric material with a permanent or quasi-permanent electric dipole."
comment: "A real-charge electret is obtained by the charge carrier injection onto the surface or into a parent dielectric material. It may contain either positive or negative excess charges or both, which must be trapped so that a good insulating parent dielectric material such as a fluoropolymer must be used."
comment: "An oriented-dipole electret is obtained by poling a parent dielectric material with dipolar groups at a temperature above the glass transition temperature \(T_{\rm{g}}\), and eventual next stabilization of the structure by cooling the electret down below \(T_{\rm{g}}\) or by crosslinking."
comment: "Electrets are electric equivalents of magnets; electric magnets. Some oriented-dipole electrets are ferroelectric polymers and piezoelectric polymers. Quartz is an example of the natural electret."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08775
consider: goldbook:08790
consider: goldbook:08857

