[Term]
id: goldbook:08806
name: electron tunneling
def: "Quantum mechanical effect of passing an electron through a potential energy barrier separating two energy equivalent regions."
comment: "The electron tunneling effect is exploited, e.g., in scanning tunneling microscopes, pressure sensors based on quantum tunneling polymer composites and in touchable panels of electronic devices."
synonym: "electron quantum tunneling" []
