[Term]
id: goldbook:08809
name: electrorheological effect
def: "Reversible change in the apparent viscosity of a liquid system such as suspension of polar or good polarizable microparticles in an oil\, upon exposure of an electric field."
comment: "Interaction of electric dipoles induced on suspended particles produces strands of particles spanning between electrodes, which results in a giant increase in the viscosity of the suspension (up to five orders of magnitude) during its exposure to an electric field."
