[Term]
id: goldbook:08822
name: fill factor
def: "Ratio of the real maximum output power\, \\\(P_\{\\rm\{max\}\}\\\)\, that can be obtained with an actual solar cell to the product of the open-circuit potential\, \\\(V_\{\\rm\{oc\}\}\\\)\, and short-circuit photocurrent\, \\\(I_\{\\rm\{sc\}\}\\\)\: \\\[f_\{\\rm\{FF\}\} = P_\{\\rm\{max\}\}/V_\{\\rm\{oc\}\}I_\{\\rm\{sc\}\}\\\]"
comment: "The \(P_{\rm{max}}\) value is obtained from the cell volt-ampere characteristic as the maximum of the product \(V\!\cdot\!I = P\). Note that the product \(V_{\rm{oc}}\!\cdot\!I_{\rm{sc}}\) is not a theoretical maximum output power of the cell, since the product is zero at both these values as \(I = 0\) for the open circuit and \(V = 0\) for short circuit."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
