[Term]
id: goldbook:08824
name: head-tail isomerism
def: "Constitutional isomerism of polymeric \(oligomeric\) chains composed of identical non symmetric repeating units consisting in different orientations of the units."
comment: "In the repeating unit of a vinyl polymer: \(\ce{-CHR-CH2\bond{-}}\), the substituent-bearing group \(\ce{CHR}\) is denoted 'head' (H) while the other one 'tail' (T). There exist three modes how two such units can be linked in a chain: head-to-tail (HT), head-to-head (HH) and tail-to-tail (TT). "
comment: "The uniformity/non-uniformity of repeating units’ orientation determines the regularity/irregularity of macromolecules."
synonym: "HT-isomerism" []
synonym: "regioisomerism" []
