[Term]
id: goldbook:08870
name: Schottky barrier
def: "Potential energy barrier at a semiconductor-metal junction with the current rectifying characteristics."
comment: "The diode based on the Schottky barrier is a Schottky diode or a hot carrier diode. Schottky diodes show switching times down to below \(\pu{1 ns}\) and a low applied potential drop (\(\pu{0.15}\) to \(\pu{0.45 V}\))."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08871
name: second harmonic generation
def: "Transformation of the input monochromatic radiation beam into a double frequency \(half wavelength\) beam."
comment: "Frequency doubling is a nonlinear optic effect typical of non-centrosymmetric crystals with a high second-order electric susceptibility. It is utilized in the laser and radio-communication techniques to obtain higher frequency signals, e.g., that of the wavelength \(\pu{533 nm}\) from the signal of \(\pu{1066 nm}\)."
synonym: "frequency doubling" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08872
name: sensor
def: "Transducer-type device that responds to a specific property of its surroundings or to a coming stimulus by a visually readable change in its state or by generation of a signal that can be read by an observer or instrument."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08873
name: short circuit photocurrent
