[Term]
id: goldbook:08876
name: stimulated radiative charge carrier recombination
def: "Radiative charge carrier recombination induced by incident photons of appropriate wavelength\, which synchronize emission of other photons as to their wavelength\, phase\, polarization and direction of travel."
comment: "If this process takes place in a system with a high population of excited states, it leads to stimulated emission, the principle of the function of lasers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
