[Term]
id: goldbook:08886
name: polyarylenevinylenes
def: "Polymers composed of macromolecules containing exclusively alternating arenediyl or heteroarenediyl \(formerly arylene or heteroarylene\, respectively\) and ethene-1\,2-diyl \(formerly vinylene\) or substituted vinylene constitutional repeating units in the backbone\:  where Ar is a divalent arenediyl or heteroarenediyl group and \\\(\\ce\{R^\{1\}\}\\\) and \\\(\\ce\{R^\{2\}\}\\\) are each hydrogen\, or an alkyl\, aryl or heteroaryl group \(structure-based polymer class name\)."
comment: "Polyarylenevinylenes are a subclass of conjugated polymers."
comment: "Polyarylenevinylenes are of interest mainly due to their electroluminescent properties."
