[Term]
id: goldbook:08887
name: polyazomethines
def: "Polymers composed of macromolecules containing azomethine \(azanylylidenemethanylylidene\) linkages in the backbone\: \\\[\\ce\{-N=CR-\}\\\] where \\\(\\ce\{R\}\\\) is hydrogen\, or an alkyl or aryl group \(structure-based polymer class name\)."
comment: "A polymer with only pendant azomethine groups is excluded."
comment: "The name azomethine is derived from the traditional names 'azo' for azanylylidene group \(\ce{-N=}\) and methine' for the methanylylidene group \(\ce{-CH=}\)."
comment: "The original distinction between polyazomethines and poly(Schiff base)s, which is that a group \(\ce{R}\) in \(\ce{-N=CR-}\) linkage cannot be hydrogen in a polyazomethine but can be hydrogen in a poly(Schiff base), making polyazomethines a subclass of poly(Schiff base)s, has nearly completely disappeared."
synonym: "poly (Schiff bases)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

