[Term]
id: goldbook:08902
name: polythiazoles
def: "Polymers composed of macromolecules containing thiazole rings in the backbone\:  where R is hydrogen\, alkyl\, aryl\, heteroaryl\, substituted alkyl\, substituted aryl or substituted heteroaryl \(structure-based polymer class name\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:08903
name: polythiophenes
def: "Polymers composed of macromolecules containing exclusively thiophene rings in the backbone \(structure-based polymer class name\)."
comment: "Poly(thiophene-2,5-diyl), often written as poly(thiophene), is the generic polythiophene."
comment: "Polythiophenes are a subclass of conjugated polymers. The highest practical applications has found poly[3,4-(ethylenedioxy)thiophene] (PEDOT). Regioregular poly(3-alkylthiophenes) are studied as materials for organic solar cells. They become conducting upon oxidative doping."
comment: "Regular polymers of a monosubstituted thiophene are prepared by catalytic coupling polymerization of the corresponding thiophene derivative or its defined dimers (dimers mostly provide regular but regioirregular polymers, see the chart below). Oxidative polymerization of an asymmetric thiophene monomer gives an irregular polythiophene with considerably worse functional properties. "
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08785
consider: goldbook:08866
consider: goldbook:08875

[Term]
id: goldbook:08904
name: polyvinylcarbazoles
def: "Polymers prepared from a vinylcarbazole or a substituted vinylcarbazole or both in admixture \(source-based polymer class name\)."
comment: "A typical polyvinylcarbazole is poly(N-vinylcarbazole) that is usually prepared by a radical or a coordination chain polymerization of N-vinylcarbazole."
comment: "Polyvinylcarbazoles are photoconducting polymers that transport charge carriers via carbazolyl pendant groups. They found wide applications, for example, in xerographic photocopying."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08850

[Term]
id: goldbook:08905
name: polyvinylenes
def: "Polymers composed of macromolecules containing exclusively ethene-1\,2-diyl \(formerly vinylene\) or substituted ethene-1\,2-diyl constitutional repeating units in the backbone\: \\\[\\ce\{-CR^\{1\}=CR^\{2\}-\}\\\] where \\\(\\ce\{R^\{1\}\}\\\) and \\\(\\ce\{R^\{2\}\}\\\) are each hydrogen or an alkyl\, aryl\, or heteroaryl group \(structure-based polymer class name\)."
comment: "Delocalization of electrons in conjugated chains gives to main-chain single bonds a partial character of double bonds, which restrict free rotations around these bonds which, therefore, show the cis-trans like isomerism. Four basic stereoregular polyvinylene chains can be derived: "
comment: "Polyvinylenes are almost exclusively prepared by polymerization of acetylene derivatives. Therefore, based on the source, they are mostly polyacetylenes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0501
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08789
consider: goldbook:08882

[Term]
id: goldbook:08906
name: polyzwitterions
def: "Polymers composed of macromolecules consisting of zwitterionic repeating units \(structure-based polymer class name\)."
comment: "From the chemical structure point of view, a zwitterionic polymer is an ampholytic polymer containing ionic groups of opposite sign, commonly in the same pendant group."
comment: "Polybetaines are a subclass of polyzwitterions."
comment: "Polyzwitterions are mostly polyelectrolytes, since their zwitterionic groups are usually located in pendant groups (not in main-chain groups)."
comment: "Unlike polyampholytes, polyzwitterions have anions and cations in the same monomeric unit."
synonym: "poly(inner salts)" []
synonym: "polyamphions" []
synonym: "zwitterionic polymers" []
