[Term]
id: goldbook:08908
name: controlled polymerization
def: "Term indicating control of a certain kinetic feature of a polymerization or structural aspect of the polymer molecules formed\, or both."
comment: "Generally, the adjective 'controlled' should not be used without specifying the particular kinetic or structural feature that is subject to control."
comment: "The expression 'controlled polymerization' is sometimes used to describe a radical or ionic polymerization in which reversible deactivation of the chain carriers is an essential component of the mechanism, interrupting the propagation to secure control of one or more kinetic features of the polymerization or one or more structural aspects of the macromolecules formed, or both."
comment: "The expression controlled radical polymerization is sometimes used to describe a radical polymerization conducted in the presence of reagents that lead to, e.g., atom-transfer radical polymerization (ATRP), aminoxyl-mediated radical polymerization (AMRP), or reversible-addition-fragmentation chain transfer (RAFT) polymerization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
