[Term]
id: goldbook:08914
name: living radical polymerization
def: "Radical polymerization in which chain termination and irreversible chain transfer are absent."
comment: "Radical polymerizations, controlled radical polymerizations and reversible-deactivation radical polymerizations are not living radical polymerizations as there is a non-zero probability of chain termination."
comment: "The term living radical polymerization can be used to refer to a hypothetical radical polymerization that occurs without chain termination."
comment: "Use of the adjectives pseudo-living, quasi-living, 'living' (within quotation marks) or other terms that containing the word living to describe a radical polymerization with only some living characteristics is deprecated."
