consider: goldbook:08959

[Term]
id: goldbook:08927
name: outer-sphere electron transfer ATRP
def: "Atom-transfer radical polymerization where the activation step involves consecutive single electron transfer and atom or group transfer."
comment: "OSET-ATRP may be referred to as ATRP."
comment: "Terms containing the phrase 'living radical polymerization' are deprecated."
comment: "The terms SET-RDRP (single-electron-transfer reversible-deactivation radical polymerization), SET-LRP (single-electron-transfer living radical polymerization), and zero-valent metal-mediated polymerization (e.g., \(\ce{Cu^{0}}\)-mediated radical polymerization) are sometimes used to describe a process where the polymerization commences with the activator in the form of a zero-valent metal, e.g., \(\ce{Cu^{0}}\). The use of terms that might imply an outer sphere electron-transfer mechanism without evidence that the reaction proceeds by OSET-ATRP is deprecated."
synonym: "OSET-ATRP" []
synonym: "single-electron-transfer RDRP (SET-RDRP)" []
