[Term]
id: goldbook:08940
name: catalytic chain termination
def: "Chain termination process involving transfer of a group to a reagent \(the catalyst\) that in turn transfers that group to a propagating species to terminate a chain and regenerate the original reagent."
comment: "Catalytic chain termination may be observed as a side reaction in certain reversible-deactivation radical polymerizations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
