[Term]
id: goldbook:08941
name: chain activation
def: "Unimolecular dissociation of a dormant species to form a mediating agent and a propagating species."
comment: "Chain deactivation (in SRMP) is the reverse of chain activation (in SRMP)."
comment: "In aminoxyl-mediated radical polymerization [nitroxide-mediated polymerization (NMP)], the dormant species is an alkoxyamine and the mediating agent is an aminoxyl radical."
comment: "In organometallic-mediated radical polymerization (OMRP), the domant species and the mediating agent are organometallic species."
comment: "In reversible addition-fragmentation radical polymerization (RAFRP), the dormant species is a stable radical and the mediating agent is a non-propagating olefin, e.g., 1,1-diphenylethylene."
synonym: "activation (in SRMP)" []
synonym: "unimolecular activation" []
synonym: "unimolecular chain activation" []
