[Term]
id: goldbook:08942
name: chain activation
def: "Reaction of an activator with a dormant species to form a deactivator and a propagating species."
comment: "Chain deactivation (in ATRP) is the reverse of chain activation (in ATRP)."
comment: "The activation and deactivation process may form part of a catalytic cycle. However, in general, the activator should not be called a catalyst."
synonym: "activation (in ATRP)" []
synonym: "bimolecular activation" []
synonym: "bimolecular chain activation" []
