[Term]
id: goldbook:08946
name: chain termination
def: "Chemical reaction in which a chain carrier is converted irreversibly into a non-propagating species without the formation of a new chain carrier."
comment: "The recommended symbol for the rate coefficient for chain termination in a polymerization is \(k_{\rm{t}}\)."
comment: "The term 'chain deactivation' is often used to stress that, in contrast to chain termination, the formation of non-propagating species may be reversible; see chain deactivation."
synonym: "irreversible chain deactivation" []
synonym: "termination" []
