[Term]
id: goldbook:08991
name: living ring-opening metathesis polymerization
def: "Ring-opening metathesis polymerization in which chain termination and irreversible chain transfer are absent."
comment: "Ring-opening metathesis polymerizations should not be described as living if there is a non-zero probability of chain termination (e.g., due to side reactions consuming some part of the catalyst) or irreversible chain transfer (e.g., due to backbiting)."
