[Term]
id: goldbook:08992
name: metathesis polymerization
def: "Polymerization in which unsaturated monomers are transformed into unsaturated polymers by a process of bond redistribution."
comment: "Metathesis polymerization is most often metal-catalyzed and the kinetic-chain carriers alternate between metal-carbene complexes and metallacyclobutanes or between metal-carbyne complexes and metallacyclobutenes."
comment: "The two most common forms of metathesis polymerization are ring-opening metathesis polymerization (ROMP) and acyclic diene metathesis polymerization (ADMET). ADMET is not a chain polymerization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08933

[Term]
id: goldbook:08993
name: ring-opening metathesis polymerization
def: "Metathesis polymerization in which an unsaturated cyclic monomer is converted into an unsaturated monomeric unit that is either acyclic or contains fewer rings than the cyclic monomer."
comment: "In general, ring-opening metathesis polymerizations that show some living characteristics should not be called living ring-opening metathesis polymerization when there are side reactions leading to loss of catalyst or irreversible chain transfer."
synonym: "ROMP" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08991
consider: goldbook:08992

[Term]
id: goldbook:08994
name: electron-transfer ring-opening metathesis polymerization
def: "Ring-opening metathesis polymerization \(ROMP\) proceeding through one-electron redox processes in the absence of a metal carbene initiator."
comment: "ET-ROMP may be initiated by single electron-transfer to a vinyl ether from a photoredox catalyst or by electrochemical processes to create a radical cation as the kinetic-chain carrier."
synonym: "ET-ROMP" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08933

[Term]
id: goldbook:08995
name: coordination polymerization
def: "Chain polymerization that involves the preliminary coordination of a monomer molecule with a chain carrier."
comment: "Coordination polymerization often occurs by pseudo-ionic polymerization."
comment: "The term 'metal-catalyzed polymerization' without explanation to designate coordination polymerization is deprecated."
