[Term]
id: goldbook:09002
name: chain-walking polymerization
def: "Coordination polymerization in which the chain carrier migrates along the formed polymer chain through a series of \\\(\\ce\{\\upbeta\\mbox\{-\}hydrogen\}\\\) eliminations and reinsertions with inversion of stereochemistry."
comment: "CWP of \(\ce{\upbeta\mbox{-}olefins}\) generally leads to less branched polymers than those formed by classical coordination polymerization."
comment: "In contrast to classical coordination polymerizations, which provide linear polyethylene, CWP of ethylene leads to a branched polymer."
synonym: "CWP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
