[Term]
id: goldbook:09003
name: coordinative chain-transfer polymerization
def: "Coordination polymerization in which a propagating chain is able to transfer reversibly between the catalyst and a chain-transfer agent\, thereby converting the active species into a dormant species."
comment: "Coordinative chain-transfer polymerization is a form of degenerative chain-transfer polymerization (DTP)."
synonym: "CCTP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
