id: goldbook:09007
name: pseudo-ionic polymerization
def: "Polymerization proceeding by insertion of a monomer into a polar bond without the generation of ions."
comment: "Most pseudo-ionic polymerizations involve concerted (e.g., four- or multi-centre) mechanisms of propagation."
comment: "The term pseudo-ionic polymerization has been most often used in connection with ring-opening polymerization."
