[Term]
id: goldbook:09014
name: locant
def: "Numeral or letter or a combination of both that identifies position\(s\) in a structure."
comment: "A locant appears in a name or general expression such as ‘2-substituted’."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09015
name: senior constitutional repeating unit
def: "More \(most\) senior CRU of a structure of a macromolecule or oligomer molecule containing two or more different types of CRUs."
comment: "If CRUs begin with an identical subunit, the choice depends on the seniority of the remaining subunits and the number and position of substituents."
comment: "The CRU beginning with the subunit of highest (higher) seniority is chosen as the S-CRU."
synonym: "S-CRU" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09016
name: preferred constitutional repeating unit
def: "Constitutional repeating unit \(CRU\) written with the subunits in a linear series from the highest \(higher\) seniority to the lowest \(lower\) or as close as possible by the shortest path."
comment: "The P-CRU is chosen with the lowest possible locant(s) for the substituents."
comment: "This definition is based on descriptions of methods to reach the P-CRU."
synonym: "P-CRU" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09017
name: subunit
def: "Largest main-chain \(backbone\) segment of the constitutional repeating unit \(CRU\) that can be named a single unit under organic nomenclature rules. This may be a ring or a ring system\, a heteroatom or a heteroatom chain\, or an acyclic carbon chain."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09018
name: dimensionless Henry’s law solubility constant
def: "Amount concentration \\\(c_\{\\rm\{l\}\}\\\) of a species in the liquid phase divided by the amount concentration \\\(c_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\\\) of that species in the gas phase under equilibrium conditions at infinite dilution\: \\\[H_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{cc\}\: = \\underset\{c_\{\\rm\{l\}\} \\to 0\}\{\\rm\{lim\}\}\\frac\{c_\{\\rm\{l\}\}\}\{c_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Instead of the amount concentrations \(c_{\rm{l}}\) and \(c_{\rm{g}}\), the mass concentrations \(\gamma_{\rm{l}}\) and \(\gamma_{\rm{g}}\) might be used here. This yields the same dimensionless Henry solubility because the molar mass \(M\) of the solute cancels out:\(\gamma_{\rm{l}}/\gamma_{\rm{g}} = (c_{\rm{l}}M)/(c_{\rm{g}}M) = c_{\rm{l}}/c_{\rm{g}}\)"
synonym: "dimensionless Henry solubility" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09021

[Term]
id: goldbook:09019
name: dimensionless Henry’s law volatility constant
def: "Amount concentration \\\(c_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\\\) of a species in the gas phase divided by the amount concentration \\\(c_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\\\) of that species in the liquid phase under equilibrium conditions at infinite dilution\: \\\[H_\{\\rm\{v\}\}^\{cc\}\: = \\underset\{c_\{\\rm\{l\}\} \\to 0\}\{\\rm\{lim\}\}\\frac\{c_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\}\{c_\{\\rm\{l\}\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Instead of the amount concentrations \(c_{\rm{g}}\) and \(c_{\rm{l}}\), the mass concentrations \(\gamma_{\rm{g}}\) and \(\gamma_{\rm{l}}\) can be used here. This yields the same dimensionless Henry volatility because the molar mass \(M\) of the solute cancels out: \(\gamma_{\rm{g}}/\gamma_{\rm{l}} = (c_{\rm{g}}M)/(c_{\rm{l}}M) = c_{\rm{g}}/c_{\rm{l}}\)."
synonym: "dimensionless Henry volatility" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09022

[Term]
id: goldbook:09020
name: Henry’s law constant
def: "Proportionality factor describing the equilibrium distribution of a chemical species between the gas phase and a liquid solution at infinite dilution of the solute according to Henry’s law. It is an umbrella term for the reciprocal quantities Henry’s law solubility constant and Henry’s law volatility constant. Because of its ambiguity\, it is strongly recommended to specify whether a solubility or volatility constant is intended."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09021
consider: goldbook:09022

[Term]
id: goldbook:09021
name: Henry’s law solubility constant
def: "Umbrella term for all variants of Henry’s law constants that are defined in such a way that the numerical value increases with increasing solubility of the solute. Variants include \\\(H_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{cp\}\\\)\, \\\(H_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{xp\}\\\)\, \\\(H_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{bp\}\\\)\, and \\\(H_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{cc\}\\\)\, as discussed elsewhere in this section."
synonym: "Henry solubility" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09022

[Term]
id: goldbook:09022
name: Henry’s law volatility constant
def: "Umbrella term for all variants of Henry’s law constants that are defined in such a way that the numerical value increases with increasing volatility of the solute. Variants include \\\(H_\{\\rm\{v\}\}^\{pc\}\\\)\, \\\(H_\{\\rm\{v\}\}^\{px\}\\\)\, \\\(H_\{\\rm\{v\}\}^\{pw\}\\\)\, and \\\(H_\{\\rm\{v\}\}^\{cc\}\\\)\, as discussed elsewhere in this section."
synonym: "Henry volatility" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09021

[Term]
id: goldbook:09023
name: Henry’s law volatility constant \(via p and c\)
def: "Partial pressure \\\(p\\\) of a species in the gas phase divided by the amount concentration \\\(c_\{\\rm\{l\}\}\\\) of that species in the liquid phase under equilibrium conditions at infinite dilution\: \\\[H_\{\\rm\{v\}\}^\{pc\}\: = \\underset\{c_\{\\rm\{l\}\} \\to 0\}\{\\rm\{lim\}\}\\frac\{p\}\{c_\{\\rm\{l\}\}\}\\\]"
comment: "The coherent SI unit for \(H_{\rm{v}}^{pc}\) is \(\pu{Pa m3 mol-1}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09022

[Term]
id: goldbook:09024
name: Henry’s law solubility constant \(via c and p\)
def: "Amount concentration \\\(c_\{\\rm\{l\}\}\\\) of a species in the liquid phase divided by the partial pressure \\\(p\\\) of that species in the gas phase under equilibrium conditions at infinite dilution\: \\\[H_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{cp\}\: = \\underset\{c_\{\\rm\{l\}\} \\to 0\}\{\\rm\{lim\}\}\\frac\{c_\{\\rm\{l\}\}\}\{p\}\\\]"
comment: "The coherent SI unit for \(H_{\rm{s}}^{cp}\) is \(\pu{mol m-3 Pa-1}\). Another commonly used unit is \(\pu{mol L-1 bar-1}\), equivalent to \(\pu{10E-2 mol m-3 Pa-1}\)."
synonym: "Henry solubility (defined via amount concentration and partial pressure)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09021

[Term]
id: goldbook:09025
name: Henry’s law solubility constant \(via x and p\)
def: "Amount fraction \\\(x\\\) of a species in the liquid phase divided by the partial pressure \\\(p\\\) of that species in the gas phase under equilibrium conditions at infinite dilution\: \\\[H_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{xp\}\: = \\underset\{x \\to 0\}\{\\rm\{lim\}\}\\frac\{x\}\{p\}\\\]"
comment: "The coherent SI unit for \(H_{\rm{s}}^{xp}\) is \(\pu{Pa-1}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09021

[Term]
id: goldbook:09026
name: Henry’s law solubility constant \(via b and p\)
def: "Molality \\\(b\\\) of a species divided by the partial pressure \\\(p\\\) of that species in the gas phase under equilibrium conditions at infinite dilution\: \\\[H_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{bp\}\: = \\underset\{b \\to 0\}\{\\rm\{lim\}\}\\frac\{b\}\{p\}\\\]"
comment: "Here, the symbol \(b\) is used for molality (instead of \(m\)) to avoid confusion with the symbol \(m\) for mass."
comment: "Molality refers to the mass of solvent and should not be confused with content which refers to the mass of solution."
comment: "The coherent SI unit for \(H_{\rm{s}}^{bp}\) is \(\pu{mol m-3 Pa-1}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09021

[Term]
id: goldbook:09027
name: Henry’s law volatility constant \(via p and x\)
def: "Partial pressure \\\(p\\\) of a species in the gas phase divided by the amount fraction \\\(x\\\) of that species in the liquid phase under equilibrium conditions at infinite dilution\: \\\[H_\{\\rm\{v\}\}^\{px\}\: = \\underset\{x \\to 0\}\{\\rm\{lim\}\}\\frac\{p\}\{x\}\\\]"
comment: "The coherent SI unit for \(H_{\rm{v}}^{px}\) is \(\pu{Pa}\)."
synonym: "Henry volatility (defined via partial pressure and liquid-phase amount fraction)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09022

[Term]
id: goldbook:09028
name: Henry’s law volatility constant \(via p and w\)
def: "Partial pressure \\\(p\\\) of a species in the gas phase divided by the mass fraction \\\(w\\\) of that species in the liquid phase under equilibrium conditions at infinite dilution\: \\\[H_\{\\rm\{v\}\}^\{pw\}\: = \\underset\{w \\to 0\}\{\\rm\{lim\}\}\\frac\{p\}\{w\}\\\]"
comment: "The coherent SI unit for \(H_{\rm{v}}^{pw}\) is \(\pu{Pa}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09022

[Term]
id: goldbook:09029
name: link
def: "Constitutive part of a conjugation that binds an active species to a substrate."
comment: "When release of the active species is desired, the link must be cleavable."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0502
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09030
name: prodrug conjugate
def: "Conjugate in which at least one conjugation includes a bioactive active species to be released by cleavage of the link where its action is desired."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0502
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09031
name: spacer arm
def: "Link used in a conjugation to distance the substrate from the active species that otherwise would have its activity affected by steric or other influences."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0502
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
