[Term]
id: goldbook:09032
name: materials chemistry
def: "Materials chemistry is the scientific discipline that designs\, synthesizes\, and characterizes materials with particular interest on both their processing and the understanding of useful or potentially useful properties displayed by the materials designed and synthesized for specific applications."
comment: "For a series of further details on both the structure-property relation and functionality by design, read the source."
comment: "The aspects of design, synthesis, and function (useful or potentially useful properties) are all needed for the topical item of material research/development/production to be part of materials chemistry."
comment: "The keywords "useful" and "properties" emphasize functionality as a major driving force of the practitioners of materials chemistry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09033
name: pnictogen bond
def: "Weak attractive interaction between an electrophilic region on a pnictogen atom in a molecular entity \(wherein the pnictogen is involved in other stronger bonds\) and a nucleophilic region in another\, or the same\, molecular entity."
comment: "A typical PnB is denoted by the three dots in \(\ce{R–Pn\bond{...}A}\), wherein \(\ce{R}\) is collectively representing the groups covalently bonded to the pnictogen atom Pn, Pn (the PnB donor atom) is any atom (possibly hypervalent) of Group 15 having at least one electrophilic (electron poor) region (the PnB donor region) involved in a bond with \(\ce{A}\), \(\ce{R–Pn}\) (the PnB donor) is a molecular entity containing the electrophilic pnictogen atom, and \(\ce{A}\) (the PnB acceptor) is a molecular entity having at least one nucleophilic (electron rich) region (the PnB acceptor region)."
comment: "An electrophilic region (typically associated with a \(\ce{\upsigma\mbox{-}}\) or \(\ce{\uppi\mbox{-}hole}\)) on a pnictogen atom in a molecular entity and a nucleophilic region in another or the same molecular entity can form bonds spanning a range of separations, energies, and other experimental or theoretical parameters; the use of the term PnB has to be limited to cases where separations, energies, and/or other experimental/theoretical parameters differ from those of corresponding covalent/ionic bonds."
comment: "Bonds wherein a pnictogen atom acts as the nucleophile and those wherein its electrophilic role cannot be identified must not be named PnBs."
comment: "Pnictogen atoms can concurrently form one or more than one PnB; the PnB donor and/or PnB acceptor can be charged molecular entities, thus forming charge-assisted PnBs."
comment: "The polar character of the pnictogen atom in the interaction (i.e., the electrophilic role in pnictogen bonded systems or its nucleophilic role in the other systems) is established by considering the physical and chemical properties of the starting molecular entities before the interaction formation and/or of the system assembled by the interaction (see onward)."
synonym: "PnB" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1002
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09034
name: alkalinity
def: "Measure of the capacity of aqueous media to react with hydrogen ions."
comment: "Alkalinity is often expressed as an equivalent mass concentration of calcium carbonate, for example "alkalinity equals \(\pu{3.2 mg L-1}\) as \(\ce{CaCO3}\).""
comment: "Alkalinity is used to assess the buffering capacity of natural waters and is measured by titration using methyl red (pH 4.5, total alkalinity) or phenolphthalein (pH 8.3, composite alkalinity)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09038

[Term]
id: goldbook:09035
name: back titration
def: "Titration of remaining reagent after addition of excess reagent to the titrand."
