[Term]
id: goldbook:09042
name: equivalence-point
def: "Stage of a titration at which the titrant has completely reacted with the titrand according to the stoichiometry of the reaction."
comment: "The term "equivalence-point" is also used for the quantity that expresses the volume or mass of titrant at the equivalence-point."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09051

[Term]
id: goldbook:09043
name: gravimetric analysis
def: "Measurement principle of quantitative chemical analysis based on measurement of mass."
comment: "The analyte of interest is separated from the sample in a form that allows measurement of mass (e.g., by precipitation), and its mass or amount of substance is calculated from the mass of the weighed compound whose stoichiometric composition must be exactly known."
synonym: "gravimetry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09044
name: gravimetric factor
def: "Mass fraction of analyte in a precipitate \(see precipitation\) obtained in a gravimetric analysis."
comment: "Gravimetric factor is calculated by \(g_{\rm{F}} = (M_{\rm{A}}v_{\rm{A}})/(M_{\rm{P}}v_{\rm{P}})\), where \(M_{\rm{A}}\), \(M_{\rm{P}}\) are molar masses of analyte and precipitate, respectively, and \(v_{\rm{A}}\) and \(v_{\rm{P}}\) are the stoichiometric numbers in the precipitation reaction."
comment: "Historically, the gravimetric factor is given the initialism GF, but to conform to the IUPAC convention that quantities should have a single symbol, it is recommended that \(g_{\rm{F}}\) is used in equations."
comment: "The gravimetric factor is used to calculate the mass fraction of an analyte in a sample (\(w\)) by \(w = m_{\rm{P}}/m_{\rm{sample}} \times g_{\rm{F}}\), where \(m_{\rm{P}}\) is the mass of precipitate and \(m_{\rm{sample}}\) the mass of sample."
synonym: "GF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09043

[Term]
id: goldbook:09045
name: homogeneous precipitation
def: "Precipitation in gravimetric analysis in which the precipitating agent is produced from a homogeneously dissolved precursor to minimise local excesses and supersaturation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09043

[Term]
id: goldbook:09046
name: indicator consumption error
def: "Systematic measurement error from the reaction of a visual indicator with a reactant in a titration."
comment: "A significant compensation of this error usually takes place because the standardization of the titrant is carried out in similar conditions to the analysis titration."
comment: "Indicator consumption error may be estimated by performing a blank titration."
comment: "Indicator consumption error may be expressed as a volume or mass of titrant."
comment: "The magnitude and sign of this error depends on the amount of substance of indicator used and the nature of the interaction between the indicator and the analyte."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09036

[Term]
id: goldbook:09047
