[Term]
id: goldbook:09050
name: stock solution
def: "Solution prepared by weighing an appropriate portion of a solid or by measuring out an appropriate volume of a liquid and dissolving it in the weighed mass of solvent or by adding solvent to a given volume."
comment: "A stock solution is usually of a greater concentration than is needed for the chemical purpose and is diluted to give the required concentration before use."
