[Term]
id: goldbook:09054
name: universal indicator
def: "Visual indicator composed of a solution of several pH indicators \(main components are thymol blue\, methyl red\, bromothymol blue and phenolphthalein\) that changes color through a range of pH values\, usually from 1 to 14."
comment: "Universal indicators are commercially available in the form of a solution or in paper strips accompanied by a color matching chart."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09055
name: volumetric titration
def: "Titration in which the titrant is added by volume."
comment: "Titrant is usually added from a calibrated burette."
synonym: "volumetry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09056
name: von Weimarn ratio
def: "Difference between the concentration of the supersaturated solution \(see supersaturation\) required for nucleation \(\\\(Q\\\)\) and its solubility \(\\\(S\\\)\)\, divided by the solubility\, \\\(\(Q − S\)/S\\\)."
comment: "The particle size of a precipitate increases as its relative supersaturation decreases, so \(Q\) should be kept low and \(S\) should be high during gravimetric analysis by precipitation."
comment: "The units of the quantities \(Q\) and \(S\) must be the same."
synonym: "relative supersaturation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
