[Term]
id: goldbook:09077
name: open circuit potential
def: "Electrode potential of working electrode relative to the reference electrode when no potential or electric current is being applied to the electrochemical cell."
comment: "In the case of a reversible electrode system, the OCP is also referred to as the equilibrium electrode potential. Otherwise, it is called the rest potential, or the corrosion potential, depending on the system being studied."
synonym: "OCP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
