[Term]
id: goldbook:09078
name: polarizable electrode
def: "Electrode whose potential changes with an applied potential."
comment: "A non-polarizable electrode is an electrode that holds its potential essentially constant by efficiently allowing electric current to pass. This is a desirable characteristic for a reference electrode."
