def: "Electrode with smallest dimension of less than 25 micrometre."
comment: "Electrode dimensions of micrometres are now routine and the distinction between ‘ultramicro’ and ‘micro’ electrodes is not usually made."
comment: "Electrodes are described by their smallest dimension. Thus, an electrode of \(\pu{1 \upmu m \times 1 mm}\) is termed a ‘microelectrode’."
