[Term]
id: goldbook:09087
name: quasi-reference electrode
def: "Electrode that maintains a constant\, but not generally well-defined\, potential in an electrochemical cell."
comment: "Examples are platinum or silver wires used in non-aqueous electrolytes or ionic liquids. Quasi-reference electrodes are calibrated against a reference electrode or by using a redox couple of known standard electrode potential."
synonym: "QRE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-0109
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
