consider: goldbook:09074
consider: goldbook:09124
consider: goldbook:09138

[Term]
id: goldbook:09141
name: linear-scan voltammetry
def: "Voltammetry in which the electric current is recorded as the electrode potential is varied linearly with time. See figure.Linear scan voltammogram of current against applied potential for a reversible redox couple."
comment: "LSV corresponds to the first half cycle of cyclic voltammetry."
comment: "The peak current is expressed by the Randles–Ševčík equation."
comment: "The scan is usually started at a potential where no electrode reaction occurs."
synonym: "LSV" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "linear-sweep voltammetry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-0109
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
