[Term]
id: goldbook:09172
name: Auger spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of electron emission spectroscopy that utilizes Auger electrons emitted from the target following excitation with an electron beam or X-ray beam."
comment: "An electron beam in the energy range \(\pu{2 keV}\) to \(\pu{30 keV}\) is often used for excitation of the Auger electrons. Auger electrons can also be excited with X-rays, ions, and other sources, but the term Auger electron spectroscopy, without additional qualifiers, is usually reserved for electron-beam-induced excitation. Where an X-ray source is used, the Auger electron energies are referenced to the Fermi level, but, where an electron beam is used, the reference may either be the Fermi level or the vacuum level. Conventionally, spectra may be presented in the direct or differential forms."
comment: "Chemical species are identified from the energies of the emitted Auger electrons and the typically low energies of the emitted electrons and resulting escape depth mean the technique is particularly sensitive for surface species analysis."
comment: "Most AES is performed under high vacuum or ultra-high vacuum."
synonym: "AES" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Auger electron spectroscopy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09173
name: Auger photoelectron coincidence spectroscopy
def: "Detection of an Auger electron and a core-level photoelectron\, emitted from a solid irradiated by mono-energetic X-rays\, within a sufficiently short time that the Auger electron shall arise from the decay of the particular core-hole associated with the photoelectron."
synonym: "APECS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09174
name: elastic peak electron spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method in which an electron spectrometer is used to measure the energy\, intensity\, and/or energy broadening distribution of quasi-elastically scattered electrons from a solid or liquid surface."
comment: "An electron beam in the energy range \(\pu{100 keV}\) to \(\pu{3 keV}\) is often used for this kind of spectroscopy."
comment: "EPES is often an auxiliary method of Auger electron spectroscopy and reflection electron energy loss spectroscopy (REELS), providing information on the composition of the surface layer. EPES is suitable for the experimental determination of the electron inelastic mean free path, the electron differential elastic scattering cross section, and the surface excitation parameter."
comment: "In general, electron sources with energy spreads that are less than \(\pu{1 keV}\) are required to provide adequate information."
synonym: "EPES" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09172
consider: goldbook:09246
consider: goldbook:09327
consider: goldbook:09329

[Term]
id: goldbook:09175
name: direct recoil spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method to elucidate composition and structure of the outermost atomic layers of a solid material\, in which principally monoenergetic neutral atoms or singly charged probe ions are used to sputter atoms or ions out of the solid surface\, their energy being recorded at one or more angle of scattering."
comment: "In the analysis, it is assumed that the recoiled atom or ion is from a single binary elastic scattering event. The energy is the complement of the primary ion scattered ion energy."
comment: "The scattered primary ions can be removed from the spectrum by a suitable choice of angle of scattering."
comment: "This method is often combined with rutherford backscattering spectrometry, as they share many concepts and instrumental items."
synonym: "elastic recoil detection" []
synonym: "elastic recoil detection analysis" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09178
consider: goldbook:09378

[Term]
id: goldbook:09176
name: low-energy ion scattering spectrometry
def: "Measurement method to elucidate the composition and structure of the very outermost atomic layers of a solid material\, in which principally monoenergetic\, singly-charged probe ions scattered from the surface are detected and recorded as a function of their energy\, angle of scattering\, or both."
comment: "LEIS(S) is a form of ion beam analysis in which the probe ions, typically \(\ce{He+}\) or \(\ce{Ne+}\), have energies in the range \(\pu{0.1 keV}\) to \(\pu{10 keV}\)."
comment: "The acronym usually has only one “S”."
synonym: "LEIS, LEISS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09378

[Term]
id: goldbook:09177
name: medium-energy ion scattering spectrometry
def: "Measurement method to elucidate the composition and structure of the outermost atomic layers of a solid material\, in which principally monoenergetic\, singly-charged probe ions scattered from the surface are detected and recorded as a function of their energy\, angle of scattering\, or both."
comment: "By using channelling and aligning the incident-ion beam along a crystal axis, the scattering from the substrate can be suppressed, enhancing the signal quality and visibility obtained for amorphous overlayers. By further aligning the detector along a second crystal axis, the double-alignment mode, the scattering from the substrate can be further suppressed, improving the signal quality and visibility for amorphous overlayers to a high level."
comment: "In some cases, an angle-sensitive detector is used that allows extensive structure and depth profile (see depth profiling) information to be obtained."
comment: "MEIS is a form of ion beam analysis in which the probe ions, typically protons, have energies in the range \(\pu{100 keV}\) to \(\pu{200 keV}\)."
comment: "The acronym usually has only one “S”."
synonym: "MEIS, MEISS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09244
consider: goldbook:09378

[Term]
id: goldbook:09178
name: Rutherford backscattering spectrometry
def: "Measurement method to elucidate composition and structure of layers at the surface of a solid material\, in which principally monoenergetic\, singly charged probe ions scattered from the surface with a Rutherford cross section are detected and recorded as a function of their energy or angle of scattering\, or both."
comment: "By using channelling and aligning the incident-ion beam along a crystal axis, the scattering from the substrate can be suppressed so that enhanced signal quality and visibility are obtained for amorphous overlayers."
comment: "RBS is a form of ion beam analysis in which the probe ions, typically \(\ce{He+}\) but sometimes \(\ce{H+}\), have energies in the range \(\pu{1 MeV}\) to \(\pu{2 MeV}\). In its traditional form, a solid-state energy-dispersive detector is used. In the form of high-resolution RBS, the energy can be reduced to \(\pu{300 keV}\) and a high-resolution (ion optical) spectrometer can be used."
synonym: "RBS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09378
consider: goldbook:09381

[Term]
id: goldbook:09179
name: desorption atmospheric pressure chemical ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge and the abundance of ionized entities emitted from a sample in air as a result of a nearby corona discharge in a humid carrier gas."
comment: "Both positive and negative ions are observed with the mechanisms involving protonation through water molecules and ionization through the Penning process."
comment: "The carrier gas is usually nitrogen."
synonym: "DAPCI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09182
consider: goldbook:09190

[Term]
id: goldbook:09180
name: desorption atmospheric pressure photoionization mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge and the abundance of ionized entities emitted from a sample in air as a result of desorption by a jet of hot solvent vapour and ionization by ultraviolet light."
comment: "Both positive and negative ions are observed."
comment: "The desorption mechanism is thermal."
synonym: "DAPPI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09181
consider: goldbook:09184
consider: goldbook:09185
consider: goldbook:09188

[Term]
id: goldbook:09181
name: desorption electrospray ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge and the abundance of ionized entities emitted from a sample in air as a result of the bombardment by ionized solvent droplets generated by pneumatically assisted electrospray ionization."
comment: "DESI is one of the few surface analysis methods designed to analyse materials without exposure to vacuum. It is used for complex molecules, organic molecules, and biomolecules. In vivo analysis is claimed to be possible."
comment: "Water and methanol are often used as the solvents to create the droplets. Acids and alkalis are added to control the solution pH."
synonym: "DESI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09182
name: direct analysis in real time
def: "Measurement method in which a mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge and the abundance of ionized entities emitted from a sample in air as a result of the interaction with a beam containing metastable\, excited atoms heated to about \\\(\\pu\{500^\{\\circ\}C\}\\\)."
comment: "Both positive and negative ions are observed, although the mechanism for positive ions can be through protonation involving water molecules and the process for negative ions through Penning ionization."
comment: "DART is the registered trademark of JEOL, USA, Inc."
comment: "The beam atoms usually used are helium, nitrogen, or neon."
synonym: "DART" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09190

[Term]
id: goldbook:09183
name: dynamic secondary-ion mass spectrometry
def: "Secondary-ion mass spectrometry analysis with primary ion current density sufficiently high for use in the analysis of sample surface layers in the depth direction."
comment: "Dynamic SIMS is often simply termed SIMS."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192

[Term]
id: goldbook:09184
name: electrospray laser desorption ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge quotient and the abundance of ionized entities emitted from a sample in air via ablation by a focused pulsed laser while simultaneously directing an electrospray jet through the desorbed plume to enhance sample ionization."
comment: "Both positive and negative ions are observed."
comment: "The desorption mechanism is thermal."
comment: "With the addition of a matrix on the sample, this is termed matrix-assisted laser desorption electrospray ionization (MALDESI)."
comment: "With the use of an infrared laser for ablation, this has sometimes been termed laser ablation electrospray ionization (LAESI)."
synonym: "ELDIMS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09180
consider: goldbook:09181
consider: goldbook:09185

[Term]
id: goldbook:09185
name: extractive electrospray ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge and the abundance of ionized entities emitted from a sample in air as a result of an inert gas being passed over the sample to pick up the molecules\, which are subsequently ionized by ionized solvent droplets generated by pneumatically assisted electrospray ionization."
comment: "Both positive and negative ions are observed."
synonym: "EESI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09180
