[Term]
id: goldbook:09186
name: G-SIMS
def: "Variant of static secondary-ion mass spectrometry in which the intensities for each mass in two spectra from the same area\, recorded with different beam energies or different bombarding ions\, are ratioed to each other and the result is used to scale one of the spectra to generate a new spectrum."
comment: "As with static SIMS, the ion areic dose during measurement is restricted to less than \(\pu{E16}\) ions per \(\pu{m2}\) to an extent that depends on both the material of the sample and the size of the molecular fragments being analysed."
comment: "The G-SIMS spectrum enables the mass of whole molecules on the surface to be determined more readily than in static SIMS."
comment: "The “G” in G-SIMS originally indicated the gentleness of the process generated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09193
consider: goldbook:09223

[Term]
id: goldbook:09187
name: laser ablation electrospray ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge and the abundance of ionized entities emitted from a sample in air as a result of laser ablation and electrospray ionization."
comment: "Both positive and negative ions are observed with the mechanisms involving protonation through water molecules and ionization through the Penning process."
comment: "The laser wavelength is usually in the infrared region."
synonym: "LAESI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
