[Term]
id: goldbook:09188
name: matrix-assisted laser desorption electrospray ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge and the abundance of ionized entities from a sample that has been mixed with a matrix whose role is enhancing the ion yield produced by laser ablation and electrospray ionization."
comment: "Both positive and negative ions are observed."
comment: "The matrix, e.g. glycerol, allows efficient absorption of the laser energy and assists the desorption of the analyte molecules in the ejected charged droplets."
synonym: "MALDESI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09180
consider: goldbook:09181
