[Term]
id: goldbook:09189
name: matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a time-of-flight mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge and the abundance of ions emitted\, as a result of a short pulse of laser illumination\, from a sample whose analyte is contained in a matrix that assists the formation of ions."
comment: "MALDI is used to analyse non-volatile polar biological and organic macromolecules, as well as polymers, to masses of over \(\pu{3000 ku}\)."
comment: "The matrix used for assisting the ion emission needs a strong absorbance at the laser wavelength and a low enough mass to sublime. Examples of matrices for \(\pu{337 nm}\) wavelength laser light are 2,5-dihydroxybenzoic acid (DHB), 3,5-dimethoxy-4-hydroxycinnamic acid (sinapinic acid), and α-cyano-4-hydroxycinnamic acid (CHCA)."
synonym: "MALDI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09190
name: plasma assisted desorption ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a mass spectrometer is used to measure the ratio of mass to charge and the abundance of ionized entities emitted from a sample in air as a result of the bombardment by a focused plasma."
comment: "Both positive and negative ions are observed, although the mechanism for positive ions can be through protonation involving water molecules and the process for negative ions through Penning ionization."
comment: "The beam atoms usually used are helium, nitrogen, air, or argon."
comment: "The energy of the plasma ions is very low."
synonym: "PADI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09182

[Term]
id: goldbook:09191
name: reactive desorption electrospray ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Mode of desorption electrospray ionization mass spectrometry with reactive chemicals within the spray solution to enhance the analytical specificity."
comment: "The method has been used to detect chemical warefare agents, as well as natural products in marine alga."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09181

[Term]
id: goldbook:09192
name: secondary-ion mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement method in which a focused beam of primary ions produces secondary ions by sputtering from a solid surface. The secondary ions are analysed by mass spectrometry."
comment: "SIMS is, by convention, generally classified as either dynamic, in which the material surface layers are continually removed as they are being measured, or static, in which the ion areic dose during measurement is restricted to less than \(\pu{E16}\) ions \(\pu{m2}\) in order to retain the surface in an essentially undamaged state."
synonym: "SIMS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09183
consider: goldbook:09193

[Term]
id: goldbook:09193
name: static secondary-ion mass spectrometry
def: "Method of secondary-ion mass spectrometry using low current densities for analysis of sample surface components\, in contrast with dynamic secondary-ion mass spectrometry\, which is used for analysis of components in the depth direction."
comment: "Ions are usually detected by a time of flight mass spectrometer (TOF-SIMS)."
comment: "The ion areic dose during measurement is restricted to less than \(\pu{E16}\) ions per \(\pu{m2}\) to an extent that depends on both the material of the sample and the size of the molecular fragments being analysed."
comment: "When the sample is an organic molecule in solid form, the term is often changed to organic SIMS or molecular SIMS."
synonym: "SSIMS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09183
consider: goldbook:09192
consider: goldbook:09223

[Term]
id: goldbook:09194
name: surface-assisted laser desorption/ionization mass spectrometry
def: "Matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization mass spectrometry using a combined liquid and particulate matrix."
comment: "The first particulate matrix to be used was graphite. More recently, nano particle matrices have been used. Ethane-1,2-diol (ethylene glycol) is a typical liquid."
synonym: "SALDI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09189

[Term]
id: goldbook:09195
name: attenuated total reflection infrared spectroscopy
def: "Attenuated total reflection spectroscopy in which the infrared absorption spectrum of a sample in contact with a prism is measured."
comment: "ATRIRS has particular application in the surface chemical analysis of solid particle films immersed in aqueous solution."
comment: "Most ATRIR work is carried out with an angle of incidence of \(\pu{45\!^{\circ}}\) inside a \(\ce{ZnSe}\) or diamond prism, both with a refractive index of 2.4. With such optical conditions, total internal reflection is achieved with an effective sample refractive index less than about 1.7 for almost all powdered samples."
synonym: "ATRIRS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09196
name: diffuse reflection-absorption infrared spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method in which the infrared absorption spectrum of light reflected and transmitted from powdered samples is measured."
comment: "Used for the analysis of weakly-reflective surfaces in gas phase or vacuum."
synonym: "diffuse reflectance infrared Fourier transform spectroscopy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09197
name: ellipsometry
def: "Measurement method for the thickness of transparent surface films and layers and for the refractive index of a reflecting material."
comment: "Ellipsometry may utilise monochromatic light, while spectroscopic ellipsometry employs a range of frequencies."
comment: "Radiation that is linearly polarized oblique to the surface becomes elliptically polarized after reflection at non-normal incidence. The ellipticity is obtained from measurements of the intensity and polarization of the incident and the reflected radiation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09198
name: extended X-ray absorption fine structure spectroscopy
def: "X-ray absorption fine structure spectroscopy in the energy region from the core-level edge to an energy several hundred $\\pu\{eV\}$ greater."
comment: "EXAFS has been used as an alternate term for the superordinate concept of XAFS."
comment: "Extended X-ray absorption fine structure results mainly from the single scattering of the photoelectron from surrounding atoms and is exhibited as oscillations in the absorption cross section with increasing photon energy. Analysis of the oscillations provides information, through bond lengths, on the local chemical environment of the emitting atom."
synonym: "EXAFS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09212

[Term]
id: goldbook:09199
name: grazing-incidence small-angle X-ray scattering analysis
def: "Measurement method in which the elastically scattered intensity of X-rays from a reflecting surface is measured for small-angle deflections at grazing incidence."
comment: "GISAXS provides structural information for the surface or for particles on the surface, with lengths scales between several nm and several hundred nm."
comment: "The grazing incidence angle depends on photon energy and material and is typically less than \(\pu{2\!^{\circ}}\)."
synonym: "GISAXS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09200
name: off-specular X-ray reflectometry
def: "X-ray reflectometry in which significant scattered intensity arises from imperfections in the specimen\, the scattered intensity falling outside the specular condition \(see specular X-ray reflectometry\)."
comment: "Imperfections generating diffuse XRR include surface and interface roughnesses, film defects, and inhomogeneities. Quantitative estimates of these can be made by modelling."
synonym: "diffuse X-ray reflectometry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09204
consider: goldbook:09214

[Term]
id: goldbook:09201
name: reflection-absorption infrared spectroscopy
def: "Spectroscopy based on reflection-absorption."
comment: "RAIRS allows improved discrimination between species at the surface and those in the bulk."
comment: "RAIRS is most sensitive at metal surfaces with grazing incidence."
comment: "RAIRS is usually employed with the sample in a vacuum or gas."
comment: "RAIRS may be employed with polarization modulation to minimize background absorption."
synonym: "infrared reflection-absorption spectroscopy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09202
name: scanning near-field optical microscopy
def: "Measurement method in microscopy in which spectroscopic data may be collected with the detector closer to the sample than the optical wavelength employed."
comment: "Includes near-field infrared, Raman, and fluorescence spectroscopies."
synonym: "SNOM" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
synonym: "near-field optical microscopy" []
synonym: "near-field scanning optical microscopy (NSOM)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09203
name: small-angle X-ray scattering
def: "Measurement method in which the elastically scattered intensity of X-rays is measured for small-angle deflections."
comment: "Angular scattering is usually measured within the range \(\pu{0.1\!^{\circ}}\) to \(\pu{10\!^{\circ}}\). This provides structural information on macromolecules, as well as periodicity on length scales typically larger than \(\pu{5 nm}\) and less than \(\pu{200 nm}\) for ordered or partially ordered systems."
comment: "The X-ray source can be a synchrotron, in which case the term synchrotron radiation small-angle X-ray scattering (SRXAS) is occasionally encountered."
comment: "Wide-angle X-ray scattering (WAXS) is an analogous technique, similar to X-ray crystallography, in which scattering at larger angles, which is sensitive to periodicity on smaller length scales, is measured."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09204
name: specular X-ray reflectrometry
def: "Mode of X-ray reflectrometry in which the angle between the detected beam and the sample surface is equal to that of the incident beam and the sample surface."
comment: "In this case, the angle scattering \(2 \theta\) is twice the incidence angle, \(\omega\). The detected, scattered X-ray intensity is measured as a function of either \(\omega\) or \(2 \theta\) or the scattering vector, \(q_{\rm{z}}\). The intensity data are usually presented as a function of \(q_{\rm{z}}\) or \(\omega\)."
comment: "Specular XRR is the plainary mode for XRR and is often meant when the term XRR is used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09200
consider: goldbook:09214

[Term]
id: goldbook:09205
name: sum frequency generation spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method from non-linear optics in which a structurally-ordered sample at an interface between two phases is irradiated by single frequency visible and variable frequency infrared pulses of light to generate a sum frequency vibrational spectrum of the interfacial species without any bulk phase contribution."
comment: "Closely related to second harmonic generation."
synonym: "SFGS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "vibrational sum frequency spectroscopy (VSFS)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09206
name: surface extended X-ray absorption fine structure spectroscopy
def: "Extended X-ray absorption fine structure spectroscopy in which\, instead of measuring X-ray absorption\, electron emission arising from that absorption is measured."
comment: "Emitted electrons include Auger electrons and secondary electrons."
comment: "The detection of emitted electrons provides greater surface sensitivity than is generally found with extended X-ray absorption fine structure measurements."
synonym: "SEXAFS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09198

[Term]
id: goldbook:09207
name: surface-enhanced infrared spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method giving enhanced infrared absorption in the measured infrared spectrum of a sample adsorbed on a roughened thin metal substrate. The metal substrate is deposited onto a prism and data is collected by total internal reflection."
comment: "SEIRAS enhancements can be \(\pu{E2}\) or greater."
synonym: "SEIRAS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09209
name: surface-enhanced resonant Raman spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of surface-enhanced Raman spectroscopy \(SERS\) by which the Raman spectrum is significantly enhanced under the conditions that\, whilst undergoing SERS\, the molecules are excited by radiation that is in resonance with electronic transitions in the sample."
comment: "Enhancements of up to and greater than \(\pu{E10}\) have been measured."
comment: "The acronym SERRS is used for both surface-enhanced resonant Raman scattering and spectroscopy."
synonym: "SERRS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09208

[Term]
id: goldbook:09210
name: tip enhanced raman spectroscopy
def: "Measurement method of Raman spectroscopy combining surface-enhanced Raman spectroscopy and scanning using an atomic force microscope or scanning tunnelling microscope to produce maps of a surface."
comment: "TERS is one of several near-field optical spectroscopic techniques."
synonym: "TERS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
