[Term]
id: goldbook:09239
name: compositional depth profile
def: "Chemical composition measured as a function of distance normal to the surface."
synonym: "CDP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09240
name: crater depth
def: "Average depth of the region of a crater from which the measured signal is derived."
comment: "The crater depth can be modified by the formation of a reacted layer (e.g. an oxide) following any exposure to the atmosphere or other environments necessary when conducting the crater depth measurement."
comment: "The crater is generally formed by ion bombardment in sputter depth profiling and, in this case, can be different from the thickness of sample material removed by sputtering due to dilation of the altered layer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09244

[Term]
id: goldbook:09241
name: cross-sectioning
def: "Sample preparation in which the sample is cleaved\, cut\, or polished in a plane perpendicular to the interface under study\, so that associated compositional differences or gradients can be observed in that plane."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09242
name: damage limit
def: "Particle fluence above which significant changes in the spectrum or in a stated peak\, arising from damage processes\, are observed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
