[Term]
id: goldbook:09243
name: delta layer
def: "Layer of discrete composition\, one atom thick\, formed during the growth of material on a substrate."
comment: "These films are often formed during epitaxial growth on single-crystal substrates."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09244
name: depth profiling
def: "Monitoring of signal intensity as a function of a variable that can be related to distance normal to the surface."
comment: "Signal intensity is usually measured as a function of the sputtering time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09239

[Term]
id: goldbook:09245
name: depth resolution parameter
def: "Parameter that can be used as a coefficient in an analytic fit to a measured compositional depth profile or as a qualitative way of describing that profile."
comment: "Depth resolution parameters usually give no indication of distinguishability, but are useful in instrumental evaluation and profile deconvolution."
comment: "Parameter definitions should be used consistently."
comment: "Standard deviations can be used for any bell-shaped curve. If parameters are measured for a step change in composition, care must be taken that the depth range for the measurements is large enough to ensure that the signal becomes constant with depth on either side of the step."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09443

[Term]
id: goldbook:09246
