[Term]
id: goldbook:09249
name: erosion rate
def: "Change in the position of the surface as a result of particle or photon irradiation divided by time of irradiation."
comment: "Erosion rate can be deduced from surface profilometer measurements of a crater after analysis. In this case, the effects of the altered layer and post-profile oxidation need to be considered."
comment: "The rate can be measured as a velocity."
comment: "Where the erosion is caused by sputtering, initially the erosion rate can be less than the sputtering rate as a result of the retention of sputtering particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09286

[Term]
id: goldbook:09250
name: field-induced migration
def: "Effect occurring in insulators or semi-conductors where internal electric fields cause the migration of sample atoms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09251
name: flux of a beam of particles
def: "\\\(\\mathit\{\\Phi\} = \{\\rm\{d\}\}N/\{\\rm\{d\}\}t\\\)\, where \\\(N\\\) is number of particles of a specified type and \\\(t\\\) is time."
comment: "For a parallel beam, fluence rate and flux density are equivalent measures."
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{s^{-1}}\). For a beam of charged particles (ions) the flux is expressed in ampere, i.e. \(F \times ze\), where \(z\) is the charge on a particle and \(e\) the elementary charge (\(\pu{1.602176634E-19 C}\))."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09252
name: focused ion beam system
def: "Ion beam system used for machining small regions with sub-micron precision."
comment: "FIB-machined surfaces can have an ion-damaged surface that needs to be removed."
comment: "In general, FIBs use a liquid metal ion source to generate a finely focused ion beam with diameters typically in the range \(\pu{7 nm}\) to \(\pu{300 nm}\) and of sufficient flux, typically \(\pu{4 pA}\) to \(\pu{20 pA}\), to machine small items for study by Auger electron spectroscopy, secondary-ion mass spectrometry, or transmission electron microscopy in an economic time. They are also used to manufacture scanning probe microscopy tips, those for atom force microscopy having radii down to \(\pu{2 nm}\)."
synonym: "FIB" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
