[Term]
id: goldbook:09254
name: image depth profile
def: "Three-dimensional representation of the spatial distribution of a particular elemental or molecular species\, as indicated by emitted secondary ions or electrons\, as a function of depth or material removed by sputtering."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09422

[Term]
id: goldbook:09255
name: impact energy
def: "Kinetic energy of particles on impact with a sample surface."
comment: "For primary-ion beams in secondary-ion mass spectrometry (SIMS), the ion impact energy is given by the difference in electric potential between the ion source and the sample surface multiplied by the charge on the ion. In some SIMS systems, the beam energy is given for the source potential with respect to ground, but the sample potential need not be at ground. The impact energy takes account of any sample potential."
comment: "Use of the qualifier “impact” indicates that this is the energy of the particles striking the surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192

[Term]
id: goldbook:09256
name: implanted areic dose
def: "Number\, \\\(N_\{\\rm\{imp\}\}\\\)\, of energetic particles of a specified type incident on a solid within a surface area \\\(A\\\) and stopped within the solid divided by \\\(A\\\). \\\(D_\{\\rm\{imp\}\} = N_\{\\rm\{imp\}\}/A\\\)."
comment: "Particles that are not stopped within the solid are either backscattered or transmitted."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09257
name: information depth
def: "Maximum depth\, normal to the surface\, from which useful information is obtained."
