[Term]
id: goldbook:09267
name: photoionization cross section
def: "Total ionization cross section for an incident photon of a given energy interacting with a material to produce one or more photoelectrons from all sub-shells that are energetically accessible."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09357

[Term]
id: goldbook:09268
name: plasmon
def: "Excitation of valence-band electrons in a solid in which collective oscillations are generated."
comment: "Plasmon excitations are often observed as characteristic energy loss peaks associated with other peaks in the spectrum, such as those of any elastically scattered primary electrons, photoelectron peaks, Auger electron peaks, and ionization edges."
comment: "Plasmons are prominent in some materials and not others."
comment: "Two types of plasmon are commonly observed: bulk plasmons, associated with material remote from the surface, and surface plasmons, associated with material at the surface. When the term plasmon is used without a qualifier, the term refers to the bulk plasmon. Occasionally, interface plasmons can be observed that are associated with interfaces. Bulk plasmon energies depend on the electronic structure of the material and are roughly proportional to the square root of valence-band density. Surface plasmon energies are typically between \(\pu{50\%}\) and \(\pu{90\%}\) of bulk plasmon energies."
synonym: "bulk plasmon" []
synonym: "volume plasmon" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09315

[Term]
id: goldbook:09269
name: preferential sputtering
def: "Change in equilibrium surface composition of the sample\, which can occur when sputtering multicomponent samples."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09270
name: primary beam
def: "Directed flux of beam particles or photons incident on a sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09251

[Term]
id: goldbook:09271
name: projected range
def: "Distance from the surface at which an energetic ion or atom comes to rest in the sample\, projected along the direction of the beam."
comment: "Calculations usually deal with the mean or average projected range for a large number of ions or atoms of the same species and the same energy."
comment: "Used in energetic-ion analysis, Rutherford backscattering spectrometry, and secondary-ion mass spectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
