[Term]
id: goldbook:09274
name: raster
def: "Two-dimensional pattern generated by the deflection of a primary beam."
comment: "Commonly used rasters cover square or rectangular areas."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09275
name: redeposition
def: "Deposition of sputtered sample material back onto the sample surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09276
name: relative instrument spectral response function
def: "In Auger electron spectroscopy \(AES\)\, secondary-ion mass spectrometry\, and X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy\, the spectrometer response function divided by the response function of a reference instrument\, or the average for several such instruments\, as a function of energy \(AES\, XPS\, etc.\) or mass \(SIMS\)."
comment: "The RISR can be used to relate spectra from one instrument to spectra from another when using similar excitation sources and geometries."
synonym: "RISR" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09172
consider: goldbook:09192
consider: goldbook:09283

[Term]
id: goldbook:09277
name: relative resolution
def: "Resolution of a spectrometer at a given energy\, mass\, or wavelength divided by that energy\, mass\, or wavelength."
comment: "Designs of spectrometer generally maintain the resolution either to be constant throughout the spectrum or to be proportional to the energy, mass, or wavelength being scanned. For the former, the term resolution is useful, whereas, for the latter, the relative resolution or resolving power is more useful."
comment: "In practice, the relative resolution of a spectrometer can be deduced using a source with an emission line of known width, usually chosen to be as narrow as possible."
comment: "It can be convenient to specify the relative energy resolution of an electron spectrometer, the relative mass resolution of a mass spectrometer, or the relative wavelength resolution of an optical spectrometer."
comment: "The relative resolution is often expressed as a percentage."
comment: "The relative resolution of a spectrometer is the reciprocal of the resolving power of a spectrometer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09329

[Term]
id: goldbook:09278
name: relative sputtering rate
def: "Sputtering rate of a sample divided by the sputtering rate of a reference sample sputtered under the same conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09286

[Term]
id: goldbook:09279
name: sample bias
def: "Electric potential applied to the whole or part of the sample\, referenced to the electric potential of the sample holder."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
