[Term]
id: goldbook:09280
name: sample charging
def: "Change in the electrical potential in the sample or on the sample surface caused by particle or photon bombardment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09281
name: sample voltage
def: "Electric potential difference of the sample referenced to ground."
comment: "For insulators, the sample voltage is assumed to be the same as that of the sample holder if an effective charge neutralizing device is used."
comment: "The sample voltage can be pulsed or constant, depending on the type of instrument."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09279

[Term]
id: goldbook:09282
name: solid angle of analyser
def: "Solid angle allowing particles or photons to be transmitted from a point on the sample to the detector."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09283
name: spectrometer response function
def: "Number of particles detected with a spectrometer divided by the number of such particles per solid angle and per interval of the dispersing parameter available for measurement as a function of the dispersing parameter."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09284

[Term]
id: goldbook:09284
name: spectrometer transmission function
def: "Number of particles transmitted by the analyser divided by the number of such particles per solid angle and per interval of the dispersing parameter \(e.g. energy\, mass\, or wavelength\) available for measurement as a function of the dispersing parameter."
synonym: "analyser transmission function" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09283

[Term]
id: goldbook:09285
name: sputter depth profile
def: "Compositional depth profile obtained when the surface composition is measured while material is removed by sputtering."
comment: "In some analytical methods, such as secondary ion mass spectrometry, the sputtering is often accomplished by the ion beam used for analysis, but in other methods an ion beam might need to be added."
synonym: "SDP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
