[Term]
id: goldbook:09337
name: initial energy state
def: "Core-hole excited state of an atom prior to Auger transition or to X-ray emission."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09340

[Term]
id: goldbook:09338
name: initial energy state
def: "Ground state of an atom prior to photoelectron emission."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09339
name: initial-state Auger parameter
def: "\\\(\\beta = 3E_\{\\rm\{B\}\} + E_\{\\rm\{K\}\}\\\)\, where \\\(E_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) and \\\(E_\{\\rm\{K\}\}\\\) are\, respectively\, the binding energy of a photoelectron peak and the Fermi level referenced \(see Fermi level referencing\) kinetic energy of an Auger electron peak\, each involving the same initial core level of the same element."
comment: "The initial-state Auger parameter is useful for evaluating the change in the atomic core potential contribution to changes in binding energy between two environments, provided the Auger transition is between core levels that have similar binding energy shifts."
comment: "This parameter has no relation to the asymmetry parameter, which is also given the symbol \(\beta\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09306
consider: goldbook:09308
consider: goldbook:09332
consider: goldbook:09343

[Term]
id: goldbook:09340
name: interatomic Auger process
def: "Auger transition in which at least one of the final electron vacancies is localized in valence levels or molecular orbitals of atoms adjacent to the atom in which the initial vacancy occurred."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09341
name: interface core-level shift
def: "Energy shift observed in core-level photoelectron spectroscopy arising from the changed bonding and/or from the displacements of atoms from their bulk positions near an interface between two materials."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09358

[Term]
id: goldbook:09342
name: intrinsic plasmon
def: "Plasmon excited at the same time as the excitation of a core-level photoelectron or an Auger electron associated with the same locality as the excitation of the photoelectron or Auger electron."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09268
consider: goldbook:09331

[Term]
id: goldbook:09343
name: modified Auger parameter
def: "Sum of the Fermi level referenced \(see Fermi level referencing\) kinetic energy of a narrow Auger electron peak in the spectrum and the binding energy of the most intense photoelectron peak from the same element."
comment: "The modified Auger parameter is the sum of the Auger parameter and the energy of the X-rays responsible for the measured photoelectron peak. Unlike the Auger parameter, it does not depend on the energy of the X-rays."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09308
consider: goldbook:09332
consider: goldbook:09339

[Term]
id: goldbook:09344
name: pass energy
def: "Mean kinetic energy of detected particles in the energy-dispersive portion of an electron energy analyser."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09325

[Term]
id: goldbook:09345
name: photoelectric work function
def: "Minimum photon energy required to liberate an electron from the surface of a conducting solid by absorption of that photon."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09297

[Term]
id: goldbook:09346
name: photoelectron X-ray satellite peaks
def: "Photoelectron peaks in a spectrum resulting from photoemission induced by characteristic minor X-ray lines associated with the X-ray spectrum of the anode material."
synonym: "satellite peaks" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09348

[Term]
id: goldbook:09347
name: photoelectron X-ray satellite subtraction
def: "Removal of photoelectron X-ray satellite peaks from a spectrum."
comment: "For unmonochromated \(\ce{Al}\) and \(\ce{Mg}\) X-rays, the satellites usually removed are \(\ce{K}\upalpha_{3,4}\) and \(\ce{K}\upalpha_{5,6}\). More sophisticated subtraction methods also remove the \(\ce{K}\upalpha_{2}\), \(\ce{K}\upalpha^{\prime}\), and \(\ce{K}\upbeta\) satellites."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09346

[Term]
id: goldbook:09348
name: photoemission
def: "Emission of electrons from atoms or molecules caused by the photoelectric effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09349
name: pure-element relative sensitivity factor
def: "In electron spectroscopy\, coefficient\, proportional to the intensity measured for a pure sample of an element\, by which the measured intensity for that element is divided in calculations to yield the atomic concentration or atomic fraction of the element present in the sample."
comment: "Sensitivity factors depend on parameters of the excitation source, the spectrometer, and the orientation of the sample to these parts of the instrument. The numerical values of the sensitivity factors can also depend on the method used to measure the peak intensities."
comment: "The choice of atomic concentration or atomic fraction should be made clear."
comment: "The source of sensitivity factors should be given to ensure that the correct matrix factors or other parameters are used. Matrix factors are significant and should be used with pure-element relative sensitivity factors."
comment: "The type of sensitivity factor utilized should be appropriate for the formulae used in the quantification process and for the type of sample analysed, for example homogeneous samples or segregated layers."
synonym: "PERSF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09263
consider: goldbook:09310

[Term]
id: goldbook:09350
name: relaxation energy
def: "Energy associated with intra-atomic or extra-atomic electronic readjustment to the removal of an atomic electron\, so as to minimize the energy of the final state of the system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09333

[Term]
id: goldbook:09352
name: selected-area aperture
def: "Aperture in the electron or ion optical system restricting the detected signal to a small area of the sample surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09353
name: shakeoff
def: "Multi-electron process in which two or more electrons are emitted\, partitioning between them the excess kinetic energy."
comment: "Shakeoff leads to a continuum background intensity at kinetic energies below that of the parent peak in the electron spectrum. This is in contrast to shakeup, which leads to peak structure, also at kinetic energies below that of a parent peak."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09354

[Term]
id: goldbook:09354
name: shakeup
def: "Multi-electron process in which an atom is left in an excited state following a photoionization or Auger electron process\, so that the outgoing electron has a characteristic kinetic energy slightly less than that of the parent photoelectron."
comment: "Shakeup peaks are usually observed within \(\pu{10 eV}\) of the parent peak. However, for gases where the background is low, shakeup peaks have been identified at kinetic energies up to \(\pu{100 eV}\) less than that of the parent peak."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09353

[Term]
id: goldbook:09355
name: Shirley background
def: "In Auger electron spectroscopy and X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy\, background calculated to fit the measured spectrum at points at greater and lesser kinetic energy than the peak or peaks of interest\, such that the background contribution at a given kinetic energy is in a fixed proportion to the total peak area above that background for greater kinetic energies."
comment: "Fitting to the background can be made by averaging over a given number of energy channels."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09172
consider: goldbook:09360

[Term]
id: goldbook:09356
name: spectator hole
def: "Electronic configuration of an atom containing an electronic vacancy that can be present during processes\, such as Auger electron and X-ray photoelectron emission\, but is not created or destroyed in the process."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09348

[Term]
id: goldbook:09357
name: sub-shell photoionization cross section
def: "Cross section for an incident photon interacting with a material to produce one or more photoelectrons from a given sub-shell."
comment: "Photoionization from one sub-shell can lead to shake-up or shakeoff of electrons from other shells."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09267
consider: goldbook:09353
consider: goldbook:09354

[Term]
id: goldbook:09358
name: surface core-level shift
def: "Energy shift observed in core-level photoelectron spectroscopy arising from the reduced coordination of the surface or near-surface atoms compared to bulk atoms."
comment: "Surface core level shifts are often observed for single crystals and nanoparticles and depend on the crystal surface exposed. Shifts can be to lower or higher binding energy, depending on the band structure of the bulk solid. For the outermost atom layer, the shift can be as high as \(\pu{0.4 eV}\). In X-ray photoelectron emission, the sampling depth is generally many atom layers when photoelectrons are detected with emission angles at, or close to, the surface normal. The shift for the outermost atom layer is thus seen most clearly at near-grazing emission angles. Separate energy shifts can be detected for the second and third atom layers from the surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09348

[Term]
id: goldbook:09359
name: total secondary-electron yield
def: "Total number of electrons emitted from a sample divided by the total number of electrons incident at a given energy and angle of incidence. \\\(\\sigma = \\delta + \\eta\\\)\, where \\\(\\delta\\\) is the secondary-electron yield and \\\(\\eta\\\) is the backscattering coefficient."
comment: "The total secondary-electron yield is often simply called the secondary-electron yield. This leads to confusion with the term of that name, which is restricted to secondary electrons with energies less than or equal to \(\pu{50 eV}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09314
consider: goldbook:09423

[Term]
id: goldbook:09360
name: Tougaard background
def: "In Auger electron spectroscopy and X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy\, intensity distribution of the background due to inelastic scattering obtained from the differential inelastic scattering cross section with respect to energy loss and the three-dimensional distribution of the emitting atoms in the surface region."
comment: "A number of classes of atomic distributions can be used together with different differential inelastic scattering cross sections. The atomic distribution and the inelastic scattering cross section should be specified."
comment: "The Tougaard background is usually calculated to match the measured spectrum over a wide energy range that excludes the peak region and the spectral region extending to approximately \(\pu{50 eV}\) less kinetic energy than the peaks of interest. The measured spectrum should be corrected for the spectrometer response function of the measuring instrument before the calculation of the Tougaard background."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09172
consider: goldbook:09283
consider: goldbook:09336
consider: goldbook:09355

[Term]
id: goldbook:09361
name: vacuum level referencing
def: "Method of establishing the kinetic energy scale in which the zero point corresponds to an electron at rest at the vacuum level."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09300
consider: goldbook:09332

[Term]
id: goldbook:09362
name: valence-band spectrum
def: "X-ray photoelectron energy distribution arising from the excitation of electrons from the valence band of the sample material."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09363
name: aligned incidence spectrum
def: "Backscattering spectrum recorded with the analysing beam aligned with crystallographic axes or planes of the sample that produce channelling."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09364

[Term]
id: goldbook:09364
name: backscattering spectrum
def: "Plot of backscattering yield versus backscattering energy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09365
name: beam chopper
def: "Electrostatic or electromagnetic device used to generate pulses of ions from a continuous ion beam."
comment: "The beam chopper can be used to define the pulse length and hence the mass resolution in a time-of-flight mass spectrometer and it can also be used to select particular ions in a beam that contains more than one species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09260
consider: goldbook:09393

[Term]
id: goldbook:09366
name: binary elastic scattering peak
def: "In ion-scattering spectrometry\, increase in the spectrometer detection system response above the background signal\, which can be attributed to the binary elastic scattering of an incident ion by a surface atom of a particular mass."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09230

[Term]
id: goldbook:09367
name: blocking geometry
def: "Experimental arrangement wherein the atom rows or planes of a single-crystal target are aligned parallel to a vector from the sample to the detector."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09368
name: electronic stopping cross section
def: "Stopping cross section arising from energy transfer to the electrons of the sample."
comment: "The maximum of the nuclear stopping cross section occurs at energies of the order of \(\pu{1 keV}\) per nucleon, whereas that of the electronic stopping cross section occurs at above \(\pu{100 keV}\) per nucleon. The absolute value of the electronic stopping cross section maximum is significantly greater than that for the nuclear stopping cross section."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09387

[Term]
id: goldbook:09369
name: energy edge
def: "Values of the backscattering energy for an element\, or for an isotope\, that is located at the surface of a sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09228

[Term]
id: goldbook:09370
name: surface approximation energy
def: "Simplification of calculations involving the energy of an ion passing through a solid sample\, where the energy of the ion at the surface is used in place of a properly averaged energy."
comment: "This approximation is used to determine the energy at which scattering cross sections (see elastic scattering cross section, inelastic scattering cross section) or stopping cross sections, or both, are evaluated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09246
consider: goldbook:09336
consider: goldbook:09387

[Term]
id: goldbook:09371
name: enhanced elastic cross section
def: "Cross section of an atom for elastic scattering that is greater than the Rutherford cross section due to partial penetration of a nucleus in the sample by the incident particle."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09381

[Term]
id: goldbook:09372
name: experimental scattered-ion intensity
def: "Measured response of the energy filtering and detection system as a consequence of bombarding the sample material with an ion beam\, usually presented as the ordinate of an ion-scattering spectrum."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09260
consider: goldbook:09373

[Term]
id: goldbook:09373
name: ion-scattering spectrum
def: "Plot of the intensities of ions\, scattered from a sample\, as a function of the scattered-ion energy divided by the incident-ion energy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09382
consider: goldbook:09390

[Term]
id: goldbook:09374
name: kinematic factor
def: "Particle energy after an elastic collision divided by the energy before the collision\, in the laboratory frame of reference."
comment: "The symbol \(K\) is often used for the kinematic factor and might have a subscript added in ion-scattering spectrometry or Rutherford backscattering spectrometry measurements, denoting the target atom as either, say, \(K_{\ce{Si}}\) or \(K_{28}\). The subscript for atomic mass is preferred, since the isotope is correctly identified."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09178

[Term]
id: goldbook:09375
name: nuclear reaction cross section
def: "Cross section at a given beam energy and emission direction of the detected product for a particular nuclear reaction per atom."
comment: "SI unit \(\pu{m2}\). Commonly used unit barn, \(\pu{1 barn} = \pu{E-28 m2}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09376
name: nuclear stopping cross section
def: "Stopping cross section arising from energy transfer to atomic nuclei of the sample."
comment: "The maximum of the nuclear stopping cross section occurs at energies of the order of \(\pu{1 keV}\) per nucleon, whereas that of the electronic stopping cross section occurs at above \(\pu{100 keV}\) per nucleon. The absolute value of the electronic stopping cross section maximum is significantly greater than that of the nuclear stopping cross section."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09387

[Term]
id: goldbook:09377
name: pileup
def: "Counts in a backscattering spectrum arising from two or more separate events that occur so closely in time that the signals are not resolved by the detection system and cause counts to be recorded in erroneous channels."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09364

[Term]
id: goldbook:09378
name: probe ion
def: "Ion intentionally produced by an ion source and directed onto the sample surface at a known angle of incidence and a known energy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09379
name: random incidence spectrum
def: "Backscattering spectrum recorded with the analysing beam incident on the sample in a direction such as to produce no channelling."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09364

[Term]
id: goldbook:09380
name: resonance reaction
def: "Nuclear reaction that has a narrow peak in the nuclear reaction cross section as a function of energy\, the nuclear reaction cross section at the peak being so much larger than the nuclear reaction cross sections at adjacent energies on either side of the peak that essentially all the particles detected from the reaction are due to the peak."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09375

[Term]
id: goldbook:09381
name: Rutherford cross section
def: "Elastic scattering cross section calculated using classical mechanics and a Coulomb potential."
comment: "The resulting cross section formula was first derived by Rutherford."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09178
consider: goldbook:09246
consider: goldbook:09371

[Term]
id: goldbook:09382
name: scattered-ion energy
def: "Kinetic energy of a primary ion after a collision."
comment: "Following binary elastic scattering, the kinetic energy of the primary or probe ions, \(E_{\rm{s}}\), is given by \(E_{\rm{s}} = E_{0}[M_{0}/(M_{0} + M_{1})]^{2} \{\cos\theta + [(M_{0}/M_{1})^{2} - \sin^{2}\theta]^{½}\}^{2}\) where \(E_{0}\) is the kinetic energy of the incident probe ion prior to scattering; \(M_{0}\) is the mass of the probe ion; \(M_{1}\) is the mass of the target atom; \(\theta\) is the angle between the initial and final velocity vectors for the probe ion, as determined from a common origin in the laboratory coordinate system, expressed as a value between \(\pu{0\!^{\circ}}\) and \(\pu{180\!^{\circ}}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09378
consider: goldbook:09414

[Term]
id: goldbook:09383
name: scattered-ion energy ratio
def: "Scattered-ion energy divided by energy of the incident probe ion prior to a collision."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09378
consider: goldbook:09382

[Term]
id: goldbook:09384
name: screening
def: "Response arising from electrons in an atom causing an apparent reduction in the coulomb potential of the nucleus."
comment: "In ion-beam analysis, when the incident ion is far from the target nucleus, the atom in which the nucleus sits looks neutral to the ion as a result of screening. The screening reduces the scattering cross section slightly from the Rutherford cross section (about \(\pu{1\%}\) per 50 increase in the target atomic number for \(\pu{2 MeV}\) \(\ce{He}\)). The effect becomes more pronounced and increasingly uncertain as the energy decreases and, for low-energy ion scattering spectrometry, the cross section is no longer really well-known."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09176
consider: goldbook:09381

[Term]
id: goldbook:09385
name: screening function
def: "Factor by which the Rutherford cross section is reduced as a result of screening in a given experiment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09381
consider: goldbook:09384

[Term]
id: goldbook:09386
name: stopping cross section factor
def: "Energy loss of a particle scattered at a given depth in the sample\, and detected at a given angle\, by the product of the atomic density of the sample atoms and the depth of scattering."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09387
name: stopping cross section
def: "Rate of energy loss of a particle with distance along its trajectory in a sample divided by the atomic density of sample atoms for a sample of infinitesimal thickness."
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{J m2}\) or \(\pu{J m2 kg^{-1}}\). Common unit \(\pu{eV m2}\) or \(\pu{eV m2 kg^{-1}}\)."
comment: "The atomic density is usually taken as the number density, \(N\), but sometimes as the mass density, \(\rho\). The stopping cross section is thus given either by \(S(E)\equiv (1/N){\rm{d}}E/{\rm{d}}x\) or by \(S(E)\equiv (1/\rho){\rm{d}}E/{\rm{d}}x\), where \({\rm{d}}E/{\rm{d}}x\) is the rate of loss of energy \(E\) with distance \(x\) along the particle trajectory. Note that \({\rm{d}}E/{\rm{d}}x\) is often called the stopping power, although it is not in units of power. This inconsistency for the term stopping power leads to its deprecation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09388
name: swift ion
def: "Ion moving with a velocity exceeding the Bohr speed of \\\(c/137\\\)\, where \\\(c\\\) is the velocity of light."
comment: "For argon and gold, this criterion requires energies greater than \(\pu{1 MeV}\) and \(\pu{5 MeV}\), respectively."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09389
name: system resolution
def: "Energy resolution or depth resolution measured in a backscattering spectrum for a monoenergetic incident-ion beam."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09245
consider: goldbook:09364

[Term]
id: goldbook:09390
name: theoretical scattered-ion intensity
def: "Calculated intensity for probe ions scattered into a specified solid angle at a given direction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09378

[Term]
id: goldbook:09391
name: thin target
def: "In energetic-ion analysis and Rutherford backscattering spectrometry\, sample whose thickness is sufficiently small that the variation in energy of particles backscattered from atoms of each constitutive element is small with respect to the system resolution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09178
consider: goldbook:09389

[Term]
id: goldbook:09392
name: analyser blanking
def: "Action to prevent secondary ions from travelling through the mass spectrometer and being detected."
comment: "This action is usually made by pulsing one of the relevant electrode potentials in time-of-flight mass spectrometers to deflect ions of a selected mass range in which intense peaks occur, so that those masses are not detected and thus do not cause unwanted detector saturation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09422

[Term]
id: goldbook:09393
name: beam bunching
def: "Reduction in the spread of arrival times of an ion pulse by reduction in the speed of the leading ions or acceleration of those at the trailing edge of the pulse."
comment: "This procedure can degrade the optimum focus of the ion beam, since different ions experience different fields."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09260

[Term]
id: goldbook:09394
name: buncher
def: "Device to shorten the time length of a pulse of ions so that they arrive at a point over a reduced time interval."
comment: "The point is usually the sample surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09395
name: dilute limit
def: "Atomic fraction or concentration of impurity species in a homogeneous matrix below which the secondary-ion mass spectrometry can safely be assumed to be linear with composition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192

[Term]
id: goldbook:09396
name: disappearance cross section
def: "Cross section for the loss of intensity of an ion signal observed as a result of the bombardment by primary ions."
comment: "Generally, the larger the molecule, the larger the disappearance cross section."
comment: "It is often assumed that the material being studied is present as a monolayer; however, this is an experimentally measured parameter and a value can be obtained irrespective of the precise form of the material under study. The disappearance cross section has practical significance and might or might not be simply related to the damage cross section."
comment: "The ion signal used is usually that for a large or characteristic fragment of the molecule, such as a cationized ion, protonated ion, or deprotonated ion from the molecule, at a surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09414

[Term]
id: goldbook:09397
name: dual-beam profiling
def: "In secondary-ion mass spectrometry\, sputter depth profiling involving two ion guns."
comment: "In time-of-flight mass spectrometers, one beam is used with a short on-time for the secondary ion mass spectrometry analysis, while a second is used during the period when the first is off and the mass analysis has been completed in each cycle. The second gun provides the ions for sputter removal of the sample to form the depth profile. This combination allows practical sputtering rates to be achieved and the profiling to be optimized separately from the optimization for the SIMS analysis."
comment: "Two similar ion guns can be used in opposite azimuths of the sample to reduce the development of topography."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192
consider: goldbook:09244
consider: goldbook:09286

[Term]
id: goldbook:09398
name: extraction field
def: "In secondary-ion mass spectrometry\, electric field above a sample\, operational during ion emission from the sample."
comment: "The extraction field can be pulsed or constant, depending on the type of instrument."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192

[Term]
id: goldbook:09399
name: extractor voltage
def: "Electric potential\, referenced to the sample\, of the electrode defining the field above the sample and used to facilitate introduction of emitted ions into the mass spectrometer."
comment: "In pulsed-extraction mode, the extractor voltage will be pulsed to the high value required to extract ions emitted from the sample by the primary-ion pulse for at least the time period necessary for the heaviest ion to pass through the extractor electrode and will then be reduced to the extraction bias voltage until the next pulse is required."
comment: "This voltage, together with the separation distance between the sample and the extractor electrode, defines the extraction field."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09398
consider: goldbook:09414

[Term]
id: goldbook:09400
name: fast-atom bombardment secondary ion mass spectrometry
def: "Secondary ion mass spectrometry in which the primary-ion beam is replaced by a fast-atom beam."
synonym: "FAB-SIMS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192
consider: goldbook:09414

[Term]
id: goldbook:09401
name: fractional ion yield
def: "Number of ions of a particular species sputtered from a sample divided by number of particles of that species sputtered from that sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09253
consider: goldbook:09265
consider: goldbook:09299

[Term]
id: goldbook:09402
name: g index
def: "Power for the ratio of mass intensities in two mass spectra measured for two different primary ion conditions\, used to generate the G-SIMS spectrum."
comment: "A value of 13 has been found to be effective for the g index in generating G-SIMS spectra and a continuous variation between 0 and 40 for analysis."
comment: "The different primary ion conditions can be two, well-separated, energies for the same primary ion or two different primary ions, usually at the same beam energy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09186
consider: goldbook:09414

[Term]
id: goldbook:09403
name: G-SIMS with fragmentation pathway mapping
def: "Development of G-SIMS in which the g index is varied in order to deduce the linkages between product ions and precursor ion."
synonym: "G-SIMS-FPM" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09186
consider: goldbook:09402

[Term]
id: goldbook:09404
name: ion beam ratio
def: "Intensity of analyte ion divided by intensity of matrix ion\, both corrected for isotopic abundance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09405
name: liquid-metal ion gun
def: "Ion gun utilizing a liquid-metal Taylor cone as the source of the primary ions."
comment: "The Taylor cone generates ion sources of very high brightness. This design enables the gun to provide beam diameters in the range \(\pu{50 nm}\) to \(\pu{1 \upmu m}\) for ion beam energies in the range \(\pu{5 keV}\) to \(\pu{30 keV}\), the smallest diameters generally being at the higher energies."
synonym: "LMIG" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09414

[Term]
id: goldbook:09406
name: mass accuracy
def: "Measured mass minus reference value for that mass."
comment: "In practice, mass accuracy is expressed as a fractional error."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09420

[Term]
id: goldbook:09407
name: metastable background
def: "Intensity in a mass spectrum arising from ions that spontaneously fragment between emission and detection."
comment: "In reflectron time-of-flight mass spectrometers, the decay of metastable ions leads to broad peaks at a mass dependent on the drift energy and reflector voltage. Good design minimizes these background signals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
