property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09427
name: shots per pixel
def: "Number of ion pulses incident at each pixel in an image for one raster frame in secondary ion mass spectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192
consider: goldbook:09274

[Term]
id: goldbook:09428
name: SIMS ion image
def: "Two-dimensional surface map of the spatial distribution of the amount of a particular secondary ion emitted from within a specific area of the sample in secondary ion mass spectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192
consider: goldbook:09293
consider: goldbook:09422

[Term]
id: goldbook:09429
name: static limit
def: "Ion fluence above which any significant changes in the spectrum\, arising from beam damage\, are observed in secondary ion mass spectrometry."
comment: "Classically, a limit of \(\pu{E12}\) ions per \(\pu{cm2}\), or \(\pu{E16}\) ions per \(\pu{m2}\) is taken as the limit not to be exceeded in static secondary ion mass spectrometry. This limit is based on one incident ion for each \(\pu{1000}\) surface atoms."
comment: "For imaging, the total molecular signal can be used, and here the limit can be greater and reach \(\pu{100}\) times the limit given in Note 1."
comment: "For large molecules, the damage cross section and disappearance cross section are both generally larger than for small molecules, leading to a static limit less than \(\pu{E12}\) ions per \(\pu{cm2}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192

[Term]
id: goldbook:09430
name: stop event
def: "Registration of a particle by a time-to-digital converter in secondary ion mass spectrometry."
comment: "The arrival time for each ion providing a pulse at the detector is registered by the time-to-digital converter (TDC). This is a stop event. TDCs might only record a fixed number of stop events during the time following each primary-ion pulse, for example 512 or 1024, other events being lost."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192
consider: goldbook:09414

[Term]
id: goldbook:09431
name: transformation probability
def: "Probability of a defined charged or neutral species being produced\, by consumption of a defined parent atomic or molecular configuration at a surface\, as a result of sputtering in secondary ion mass spectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192

[Term]
id: goldbook:09432
name: ultra-shallow depth profile
def: "Depth profile in secondary-ion mass spectrometry where the depth over which significant changes occur is less than \\\(\\pu\{10 nm\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192

[Term]
id: goldbook:09433
name: useful ion yield
def: "In secondary ion mass spectrometry\, number of ions of a particular isotope detected divided by the number of atoms of the same element sputtered from the sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192

[Term]
id: goldbook:09434
name: useful spatial resolution
def: "Image resolution in secondary ion mass spectrometry obtained in practice."
comment: "The image resolution is poorer than the primary-ion beam diameter as a result of either the need to maintain the damage level below a limit set by the integrity of the data or the need to record sufficient signal when the sample is being consumed during analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09192

[Term]
id: goldbook:09435
name: absorption length
def: "Distance over which the transmitted X-ray intensity falls by \\\(1/e\\\)\, where \\\(e\\\) is the base of the natural logarithm."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09436
name: beam footprint
def: "Area on the specimen irradiated by X-rays in X-ray reflectrometry."
comment: "In typical commercial equipment, the beam width is \(\pu{200 \upmu m}\), so at \(\pu{0.3\!^{\circ}}\) incident angle, the beam footprint is \(\pu{38 mm}\) long; at \(\pu{1\!^{\circ}}\), it is \(\pu{11.5 mm}\) and at zero incidence angle it is infinite. For \(\pu{100 \upmu m}\) incident beam width, these values are halved."
comment: "The beam footprint along the beam direction can be reduced by the use of a suitable knife-edge diaphragm mounted in a plane that is normal to the sample surface and whose normal, in turn, aligns with the beam azimuth. The knife-edge is parallel to, and adjusted to be close to, the surface at the point where the X-ray beam centre strikes the sample surface. This closeness limits the footprint size but also reduces the measured signal intensity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09214

[Term]
id: goldbook:09437
name: beam spill-off
def: "Fraction of the incident X-ray beam in X-ray reflectrometry missing the specimen."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09214

[Term]
id: goldbook:09438
name: delayed onset
def: "X-ray energy at which there is a significant increase of absorption and for which the increased absorption occurs at a greater energy than a core-level binding energy."
comment: "For many elements, there is a significant increase of absorption when the X-ray energy is equal to the electron-binding energy for a sub-shell. A delayed onset occurs for some elements and sub-shells when the corresponding increase of absorption occurs, instead, at an energy larger than the sub-shell binding energy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09439
name: dispersion plane
def: "Plane containing the source\, detector\, incident\, and specularly reflected X–ray beams in X-ray reflectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09214

[Term]
id: goldbook:09440
name: total reflection of X-rays
def: "Condition where the glancing angle for the incident X-rays is at or less than the critical angle and the X-rays are either reflected or absorbed in a region very close to the surface."
comment: "The reflected intensity is close to \(\pu{100\%}\) of the incident intensity and the transmitted intensity is zero."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09441
name: wave vector
def: "Vector in reciprocal space describing the direction of propagation of X-rays and equal in magnitude to \\\(2\\uppi/\\lambda\\\)\, where \\\(\\lambda\\\) is the wavelength of the X-rays."
comment: "In different fields of study, the wave vector is taken as \(2\uppi/\lambda\) or as \(1/\lambda\). In X-ray reflectometry the former is usually used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09442
name: X-ray jump ratio
def: "X-ray absorption coefficient at an energy just above an absorption edge divided by that at an energy just below the edge."
comment: "X-ray absorption spectra can have complex shapes for X-ray energies in the vicinity of photoionization thresholds, and a well-defined edge is not always observed at the threshold."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09443
name: observed interface width
def: "In secondary-ion mass spectrometry\, Auger electron spectroscopy\, and X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy\, distance over which a change in signal intensity from \\\(\\pu\{16\\%\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{84\\%\}\\\)\, or from \\\(\\pu\{84\\%\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{16\\%\}\\\)\, is measured at the junction of two dissimilar matrices\, the thicknesses of which are more than six times that distance"
comment: "The change in signal intensity should be quoted with the observed interface width."
synonym: "depth resolution" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09172
consider: goldbook:09192
consider: goldbook:09245

[Term]
id: goldbook:09444
name: surface plasmon resonance
def: "Resonant interaction between the natural frequency of a surface plasmon and incident light of the same frequency."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09294

[Term]
id: goldbook:09445
name: adhesion promoter
def: "Interfacial agent comprised of molecules possessing two or more functional groups\, each of which exhibits preferential interactions with the various types of phase domains in a composite."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09446
name: aerial image
def: "Image of a mask pattern that is projected onto the photoresist coated wafer by an optical system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09495
consider: goldbook:09523

[Term]
id: goldbook:09447
name: annealing
def: "Thermal treatment of a solid polymer material at a fixed or changing temperature that leads to desired changes in its physical structure and properties without involving complete melting or dissolution."
comment: "Annealing may be carried out by exposure of a crystalline polymer to a poor solvent or to its vapors."
comment: "Annealing of a crystalline polymer is usually carried out by keeping the polymer at temperatures just below its melting point."
comment: "In a crystalline polymer, the process of annealing leads to reorganization and involves an increase of order in existing crystallites, an increase in degree of crystallinity, and changes to more stable polymorphs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09448
name: solvent vapor annealing
def: "Annealing via the exposure of a substrate to solvent vapor."
comment: "Solvent vapor annealing is most commonly used in lithography to process block copolymer (BCP) thin films, often leading to a more equilibrated structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09449
name: thermal annealing
def: "Annealing in which a heating step is used to activate chemical processes in a resist that depend on diffusion."
comment: "Thermal annealing is frequently employed in photolithography and in block copolymer lithography."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09454
consider: goldbook:09517
consider: goldbook:09564

[Term]
id: goldbook:09450
name: anti-reflective coating
def: "Material used in lithography or in other technologies that is applied to a surface in order to reduce reflection."
synonym: "ARC" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
