consider: goldbook:09564

[Term]
id: goldbook:09459
name: contact hole
def: "Hole in a layer of a semiconductor device enabling contact with an underlying semiconductor layer."
comment: "Contact holes are usually of a diameter less than \(\pu{100 nm}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09460
name: contrast
def: "Maximum of the absolute value of the gradient of a contrast curve taken as a measure of the ability of a resist to differentiate the regions that have been exposed to radiation from those that have not."
comment: "For ease of determination, for positive- and negative-tone resists respectively, contrasts are usually calculated as \[\gamma =\frac{1}{2\log_{10} (D_{\rm{n}}^{0.5}/D_{\rm{n}}^{0})} \quad {\rm{and}} \quad \gamma =\frac{1}{2\log_{10} (D_{\rm{p}}^1 /D_{\rm{p}}^{0.5})}\] in which \(D_{\rm{n}}^{0}\), \(D_{\rm{n,p}}^{0.5}\), and \(D_{\rm{p}}^{1}\) are the incident exposure doses to light or radiation required for incipient gel formation in a negative-tone system, the dose at \(\pu{50\%}\) of the original resist thickness remaining after development for either system, and the clearance dose for a positive-tone system, respectively."
synonym: "contrast ratio" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09461
consider: goldbook:09468
consider: goldbook:09477
consider: goldbook:09564

[Term]
id: goldbook:09461
name: contrast curve
def: "Plot of the fraction of the original thickness that remains after the development of a uniformly irradiated resist versus the logarithm of the incident exposure dose."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09468
consider: goldbook:09477
consider: goldbook:09564

[Term]
id: goldbook:09462
name: critical dimension
def: "Length of the smallest geometrical features that can be formed in a lithographic process."
comment: "The critical dimension uniformity (CDU), which is a statistical measurement of the variation in length of the smallest geometrical feature, is often as low as \(3\:\upsigma\) of \(\pu{10\%}\) of the CD."
comment: "The final device CD is often notably smaller than the smallest geometrical features that can be formed in a lithographic process, achieved, for example, by etch or slimming processes."
synonym: "CD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09463
name: dark loss
def: "Unwanted change in the solubility of a resist that takes place in the absence of exposure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
