def: "Empirical observation by Gordon E. Moore\, co-founder of Intel\, that\, over the history of computing hardware\, the number of transistors on integrated circuits doubles approximately every two years."
comment: "Moore’s law applies more fundamentally to advances in lithographic processing, particularly achievable resolution, since the inception of printed circuit boards."
