[Term]
id: goldbook:09573
name: silylation
def: "Introduction of a substituted silyl group \(\\\(\\ce\{R3Si\}\\\)\) to an alcohol\, carboxylic acid\, amine\, thiol\, or phosphate\, commonly as a protecting group."
comment: "Trimethylsilylation used to protect reactive functional groups, such as hydroxy or amino groups, from their reaction with growing anionic species in anionic polymerization."
synonym: "silation" []
