[Term]
id: goldbook:09574
name: soft bake
def: "Short\, low temperature annealing step following the coating of a wafer with a photoresist."
comment: "The purpose of the soft bake is to (1) drive out remaining coating solvent from the resist layer; (2) improve the adhesion of the resist to the substrate; and (3) anneal the shear stresses introduced during spin-coating."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
