[Term]
id: goldbook:09575
name: stamp
def: "Three-dimensional template comprising the negative pattern used to leave an impression on the surface of a malleable material."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09576
name: supramolecular assembly
def: "Molecular system comprising two or more self-assembled molecular\, or molecular and ionic\, entities held together by means of non-covalent intermolecular binding interactions."
comment: "The dimensions of supramolecular assemblies can range from nanometers to micrometers."
comment: "The use of the term supramolecular polymer is discouraged."
comment: "While a supramolecular assembly may comprise only two molecular or molecular/ionic entities, for example a DNA double helix or a host-guest complex, the term is more commonly used to denote larger constructs, typically with rod-like, sheet-like, or spherical structures."
synonym: "supramolecular species" []
synonym: "supramolecular structure" []
synonym: "supramolecule" []
