[Term]
id: goldbook:09581
name: top-surface imaging
def: "Lithographic process in which the exposed region of resist is silylated and the image then formed through reactive oxygen etch."
comment: "Oxygen plasma is used to convert any silicon to \(\ce{SiO2}\)."
comment: "Usually a chemically amplified photoresist is used."
synonym: "TSI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
