[Term]
id: goldbook:09614
name: generation
def: "Set of constitutional repeating units separated from the free valence of a dendron by the same number of constitutional repeating units."
comment: "Generations are numbered consecutively starting from the constitutional repeating unit bearing the free valence. Example of a four-generation dendron, highlighting constitutional repeating units of generations 1 to 4 and the end-groups. The preferred constitutional repeating unit is chosen such that the branch points are at its end in the dendron direction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1217
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
