[Term]
id: goldbook:09625
name: number of pseudo-generations
def: "Number of generations of the hypothetical dendrimer molecule that would present the same ratio of constitutional repeating units to core unit."
comment: "In hyperbranched polymers obtained by the \({\rm{AB}}_{x}\mbox{-}\rm{type}\) monomer + \({\rm{B}}_{y}\mbox{-}\rm{type}\) monomer polycondensation approach, where \(\rm{A}\) and \(\rm{B}\) represent mutually reactive groups, the number of pseudo-generations \(n\) can be calculated by solving the equation: \[r = y(x^n - 1)/(x - 1)\], where \(r\) is the mole ratio of \({\rm{AB}}_{x}\mbox{-}\rm{type}\) monomer to \({\rm{B}}_{y}\mbox{-}\rm{type}\) monomer in the initial monomer mixture. See the figure for an example of \({\rm{AB}}_2\) and \({\rm{B}}_{3}\mbox{-}\rm{type}\) monomers (\(x = 2\) and \(y = 3\)). Idealized representation of an aliphatic hyperbranched polyester macromolecule obtained by one-step bulk polyesterification of 3-hydroxy-2-(hydroxymethyl)-2-methylpropanoic acid (\({\rm{AB}}_{2}\mbox{-}\rm{type}\) monomer) and 2-ethyl-2-(hydroxymethyl)propane-1,3-diol (\({\rm{B}}_{3}\mbox{-}\rm{type}\) molecule). "
comment: "The number of pseudo-generations can be a decimal number, while the number of generations of a dendrimer molecule is an integer."
comment: "The use of the terms generation and number of generations for a hyperbranched polymer is not acceptable."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1217
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
