id: goldbook:09639
name: blood group
def: "Red cell phenotypes classified by their antigenic structural characteristics\, which are under the control of various allelic genes."
comment: "The cell membrane properties that provide the specific antigenicity of the blood groups are called agglutinogens, as they agglutinate or clump in the presence of their specific antibody."
