[Term]
id: goldbook:09654
name: bioinformatics
def: "Discipline encompassing the development and utilisation of computational tools to store\, analyse\, and interpret biological data."
comment: "Among the most important bioinformatics tools are specialised databases with genetic and protein sequences accompanied by related data (biological function, cell localisation, etc.) and including search, alignment, and sorting algorithms or graphical modelling."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09655
name: biological recognition element
def: "Component of biological origin that translates information from the biochemical domain into a physical or chemical domain with a defined selectivity."
comment: "A biocatalytic recognition element is based on a biocatalytic reaction. Five types of biocatalyst are commonly used: (a) Enzyme (mono-or multi-enzyme): the most common and well-developed recognition system; (b) whole cells (micro-organisms, such as bacteria, fungi, eukaryotic cells or yeast) or cell organelles or particles (mitochondria, cell walls); and (c) tissue (plant or animal tissue slice). (d) Ribozymes, and (e) DNAzymes."
comment: "A biocomplexing or bioaffinity recognition element is based on the binding interaction of the analyte with macromolecules or organised molecular assemblies that have either been isolated from their original biological environment or engineered."
comment: "The main purpose of the biological recognition element is to provide a biosensor or other system with a high degree of selectivity for the kind of quantity to be measured."
comment: "Typical biological recognition elements include biocatalysts, immune receptors, nucleic acids, and others. Biologically-derived recognition elements, such as oligopeptides, oligosaccharides, and peptide nucleic acids are also of great interest."
synonym: "biochemical receptor" []
synonym: "biocomponent (at a biosensor)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09656
name: enzymatic decomposition
def: "Decomposition of organic materials \(e.g. starch\, sugars\, proteins\, lignin\, hemicelluloses\, etc.\) with specific enzymes or microbes in which the enzyme converts a high relative molecular mass compound into lower relative molecular mass species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09633

[Term]
id: goldbook:09658
name: lysis
def: "Breaking down of a cell."
comment: "A fluid containing the contents of lysed cells is called a "lysate"."
comment: "Lysis may be caused by physical, (bio)chemical, or biological means."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09659
name: microarray
def: "Two-dimensional arrangement of a device for analysis of sub-microlitre sample volume."
comment: "A collection of molecules spatially addressed on a surface within features that have micrometer dimensions. Planar device (flat plane) used for off-line determination and identification of biocompounds."
comment: "This screening format is a direct offshoot of genomic microarray technologies and makes use of ultra-low-volume miniaturization provided by nanodispensing technologies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09812
consider: goldbook:09832

[Term]
id: goldbook:09660
name: sample quality control
def: "Test of the purity of the sample that will be subjected to detailed biochemical analysis."
comment: "Microelectrophoresis belongs to methods used for sample quality testing."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09747

[Term]
id: goldbook:09661
name: affinity
def: "Strength of association between a single antibody and a single epitope of antigen."
comment: "Affinity of the immunochemical reaction: \[\ce{Antibody + Antigen -> Antibody{-}Antigen}\] is characterised by the affinity (binding, association) constant \[K_{\rm{A}} = [\ce{Antibody{-}Antigen}]/[\ce{Antibody}][\ce{Antigen}]\]"
comment: "The average binding constant reflects a population of antibody molecules (polyclonal antibody)."
synonym: "binding affinity" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09662
name: agglutination inhibition
def: "Type of agglutination in which particulate and soluble antigen compete for soluble antibody."
comment: "Typically, it is soluble antigen in the test medium which reacts first with the soluble antibody, inhibiting the agglutination of indicator particles. With viral hemagglutination inhibition assays, host antibodies resulting from a specific infection are the most common forms of agglutination inhibition assays. In this case, viral-specific antibodies block the sites on the virus that agglutinate erythrocytes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09663
name: antigenic determinant
def: "Part of the structure of an antigen molecule that is responsible for specific interaction with antibody molecules evoked by the same or a similar antigen."
synonym: "epitome" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09664
name: avidity
def: "Net affinity of all binding sites of all antibodies in the antiserum under specified physicochemical reaction conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09661

[Term]
id: goldbook:09665
name: binding capacity
def: "Amount of a ligand that binds to a receptor expressed in operational units."
comment: "Binding capacity is determined by saturating the receptor and then measuring the amount of complex forming ligand. Parameters like pH and ionic strength influence the capacity value, which will be changed depending on the experimental conditions."
comment: "Operational units are defined in contrast to the quantitative mass units of the affinity constant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09661

[Term]
id: goldbook:09666
name: blocking
def: "Coating of an immunospecific surface \(e.g. serum\, tissues\, cells\, biological macromolecules\, biosensor surface\) to form an active cover with selectivity or an inert layer."
comment: "Blocking is a pre-treatment method with blocking agents (e.g. monovalent Fab fragment, i.e. the antigen-binding fragment of an immunoglobulin molecule; mono or divalent antibodies; organic ligands; metals)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09634
consider: goldbook:09652

[Term]
id: goldbook:09667
name: bound/free ratio
def: "Amount of analyte bound by a label divided by amount of unbound \(free\) analyte"
synonym: "B/F" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09668
name: complement
def: "Array of serum proteins \(some of which are enzymes\) that become sequentially activated after the first member of the series is activated by either antigen-antibody complexes or microbial products."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09669
name: enzyme conjugate
def: "Conjugate that has an enzyme bound covalently."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09670
name: hemagglutination
def: "Agglutination reactions in which the particles used are erythrocytes."
comment: "Hemagglutination may be either direct, in which erythrocyte antigens are reactants, or indirect (passive) for coated antigen or, in the case of reverse (passive) assays, coated antibody. One of the most common uses of hemagglutination is to quantitate the number of hemagglutinating viruses (cf. influenza) or their soluble hemagglutinating surface subunits. It can also be used for blood typing."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09671
name: immunoblotting
def: "Technique that uses antibodies \(or other specific ligands in related techniques\) to identify target proteins among a number of unrelated protein species."
comment: "The techniques allow the detection of proteins from complex mixtures separated by gel chromatography and then transferred to a membrane. After incubation of the attached product from membrane with labelled antibody, the target proteins become visible."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09672
name: immunochemical specificity
def: "The extent to which the immunoassay responds only to \(all subsets of\) a specific analyte and not to other substances of similar structure that are present in the sample."
synonym: "specificity" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09673
name: immunocomplex
def: "Product of an antigen-antibody reaction that may also contain components of the complement."
comment: "Formation of the immunocomplex is characterised by the binding constant"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09661
consider: goldbook:09668

[Term]
id: goldbook:09674
name: immunoglobulin class
def: "Classification of immunoglobulins based on antigenic and structural differences of the heavy peptide chain."
comment: "Immunoglobulin subclass (isotype) represents the subdivision of an immunoglobulin class based on structural and antigenic differences in the heavy peptide chain. Four human \(\ce{IgG}\) subclasses and two \(\ce{IgA}\) subclasses have currently been recognised; \(\ce{IgM}\) subclasses have been postulated; \(\ce{IgD}\) and \(\ce{IgE}\) subclasses are unknown."
comment: "There are five classes: \(\ce{IgG}\), \(\ce{IgA}\), \(\ce{IgM}\), \(\ce{IgD}\), and \(\ce{IgE}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09675
name: immunoprecipitation
def: "Isolation and concentration of an antigen by forming a precipitate with an antibody."
comment: "Immunoprecipitation requires that the antibody be coupled to a solid substrate at some point in the procedure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09676
name: immunoreactivity
def: "Kinetic property of the immune response caused by an antigen."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09677
name: immunosensor
def: "Biosensor where one of the immunointeracting partners \(an antibody or an antigen as the analyte\) is immobilised on the surface of a physicochemical transducer."
comment: "The generated signal either directly reflects the amount of formed immunocomplex or corresponds to the amount of label."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09673

[Term]
id: goldbook:09678
name: indirect agglutination
def: "Agglutination in which antigen is first immobilised artificially onto the particulate surfaces\, either by physical adsorption or by chemical and/or immunochemical linkers."
comment: "Antigen-loaded particles can be used to detect the presence of the corresponding specific agglutinins in sample. Agglutination results by cross-linking of the antigen-bearing particles onto an extensive antigen-antibody lattice (i.e. in detectable agglutination of the particles)."
synonym: "passive agglutination" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09679
name: lateral flow test
def: "Migration of the sample zone driven by capillary forces in a porous carrier strip."
comment: "During migration the dissolved tracer becomes distributed between capture and control zones with immobilised antibodies."
comment: "The amount of the label compound in both zones depends on the concentration of the compound in the studied sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09680
name: monoclonal
def: "Arising from a single clone of cells."
comment: "In the case of immunoglobulin, "monoclonal" refers to its origin."
comment: "Usually, the monoclonal antibody is of a single immunoglobulin class containing only one light chain type of either the K or L variety. It also refers to all antibody molecules having identical physical-chemical characteristics and antibody specificity. Monoclonal antibodies have very restricted structural diversity and they are homogeneous compared with polyclonal antibodies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09681
name: monospecificity
def: "Immunoreactivity of an antiserum with its designated antigen."
comment: "In practice, true monospecificity to naturally occurring antigens does not occur in antisera produced by the immunization of the intact animal. An attempt is made to reduce the level of unwanted specificities below that which will interfere with the intended use of a particular immunochemical test."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09672
consider: goldbook:09676

[Term]
id: goldbook:09682
name: polyclonal
def: "Arising from multiple\, different clones."
comment: "Polyclonal antibodies (pAbs) are antibodies that are secreted by different B cell lineages within the body. They are a collection of immunoglobulin molecules that react against a specific antigen, each identifying a different epitope."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09683
name: reverse passive agglutination
def: "Modification of the indirect agglutination assay\, where the particles are coated with antibody."
comment: "These antibody-laden particles become probes for detecting specific antigens in the sample material. The presence of the relevant antigen will result in the agglutination of particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09684
name: sandwich immunoassay
def: "Immunoassay using chemical or immunochemical binding of analyte to a solid phase carrying antibody and the immunochemical binding of a second \(labelled\) reagent to the analyte."
comment: "This is one of the most common assays in clinical practice."
synonym: "two-site, noncompetitive immunoassay" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09685
name: amplification of deoxyribonucleic acid
def: "Process of producing multiple copies of a deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\) sequence by the repeated copying of a DNA segment."
synonym: "amplification of DNA" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09686
name: base pair
def: "Pair of two nucleobases\, consisting of one purine and one pyrimidine base\, held together by hydrogen bonds."
comment: "In deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA), guanine typically pairs with cytosine and adenine typically pairs with thymine. In ribonucleic acid (RNA), adenine typically pairs with uracil."
synonym: "bp" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
