[Term]
id: goldbook:09687
name: base sequence analysis
def: "Method for determining the nucleotide sequence."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09712

[Term]
id: goldbook:09688
name: basic local alignment search tool
def: "Computer algorithm that finds regions of local similarity between deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\) or protein sequences."
synonym: "BLAST" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09689
name: cloning
def: "Specialised deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\) technology for the production of multiple exact copies of a single gene or another segment of DNA."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09690
name: cloning vector
def: "Deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\) molecule into which another DNA fragment of appropriate size can be integrated without the loss of its capacity for self-replication."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09691
name: complementary sequence
def: "Nucleotide sequence that can form a double-stranded structure with another deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\) sequence by following base-pairing \(see base pair\) rules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09686
consider: goldbook:09712

[Term]
id: goldbook:09692
name: complete genome sequence
def: "High-quality\, low-error\, gap-free deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\) sequence of an entire genome of an organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09693
name: damage to deoxyribonucleic acid
def: "Alteration in the deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\) chemical structure resulting from interactions with physical or chemical agents occurring in the environment\, generated in the organisms as by-products of metabolism\, or used as therapeutics."
comment: "Terms "(product of) DNA damage" (lesion, adduct) and "mutation" should not be intermingled. Mutations refer to hereditable changes in DNA sequence—substitutions, deletions, or insertions of (one or more) standard base pair(s) and are not synonyms to "base mismatches". Importantly, DNA damage and its repair can promote the occurrence of mutations."
comment: "The main types of DNA damage include the interruption of the sugar-phosphate backbone (strand breaks) or the release of bases due to hydrolysis of N-glycosidic bonds (resulting in abasic sites), inter- and intra-strand crosslinks (such as pyrimidine dimers), and a variety of nucleobase lesions (adducts) resulting from reactions of DNA with a broad range of oxidants, alkylating compounds, and other agents."
synonym: "DNA damage" []
synonym: "damage to DNA" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09694
name: deletion
def: "Loss of a part \(one or more base pairs\) of deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09686

[Term]
id: goldbook:09695
name: deoxyribose
def: "Type of pentose sugar that is incorporated in the structure of deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09696
name: deoxyribonucleic acid fragmentation
def: "Breaking and/or separation of large deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\) molecules into smaller pieces \(fragments\)."
comment: "DNA fragmentation is also a consequence of damage to DNA."
comment: "DNA fragmentation is usually achieved via cleavage with restriction endonucleases at specific sites or non-specifically by, for example, sonication."
synonym: "DNA fragmentation" []
synonym: "fragmentation of DNA" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
