consider: goldbook:09703

[Term]
id: goldbook:09700
name: deoxyribonucleic acid profiling
def: "Identification of individuals by matching characteristics of their genome deoxyribonucleic acid \(DNA\) sequence."
comment: "Characteristics used include the frequency (or size) of tandem repeats in the genome."
comment: "DNA profiles are at a lower resolution than a full genome DNA sequence, but this is adequate for forensic purposes, such as in parental testing and criminal investigations."
synonym: "DNA profiling" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09701
