[Term]
id: goldbook:09720
name: real-time polymerase chain reaction
def: "Polymerase chain reaction where data are collected and monitored in real-time as the reaction proceeds."
comment: "Digital PCR is a new alternate method to conventional real-time PCR and quantitative PCR for absolute quantification and rare allele detection. Digital PCR works by partitioning a sample of deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA) or complementary DNA into many individual, parallel PCR reactions; some of these reactions contain the target molecule (complementary DNA, positive) while others do not (negative). A single molecule can be amplified a million-fold or more."
synonym: "real-time PCR" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
