property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09735
name: bottom-up proteomics
def: "Approach to identify proteins and characterise their amino acid sequences or post-translational modifications by sequential combination of proteolysis \(enzymatic proteolysis and chemical proteolysis\) prior to mass spectrometric analysis of the resulting proteolytic peptides."
comment: "In shotgun proteomics, the proteins in a mixture are digested, usually by a specific enzyme, and the resulting peptides are separated by liquid chromatography and identified by tandem mass spectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09726
consider: goldbook:09776
consider: goldbook:09786

[Term]
id: goldbook:09736
name: C-terminal analysis
def: "Chemical method for C-terminal sequencing of proteins and peptides starting at their C-terminus."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09737

[Term]
id: goldbook:09737
name: C-terminus
def: "End of an amino acid chain \(protein or polypeptide\)\, terminated by a carboxylic group."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09738
name: database searching
def: "Bioinformatics analysis of proteomic mass spectrometric data used in order to identify a protein or its post-translational modification. It results in a list of candidates presented mostly in order of the decreasing statistical significance of the hit."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09654

[Term]
id: goldbook:09739
name: difference gel electrophoresis
def: "Measurement method of two-dimensional gel electrophoresis used to study protein expression regulation by the differential staining of multiple gels representing different states of a proteome\, preferably with fluorescent dyes \(e.g. \\\(\\ce\{Cy\{3\}\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{Cy\{5\}\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{Cy\{2\}\}\\\)\)."
comment: "The resulting stained gels are analysed using 2D image analysis."
synonym: "DIGE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09788

[Term]
id: goldbook:09740
name: disulfide bond cleavage
def: "Chemical reduction of protein disulfide bonds."
comment: "Reductants, such as tributylphosphine (TBP), 2-sulfanylethan-1-ol (BME), or dithiothreitol (DTT) are used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09741
name: Edman degradation
def: "Method of N-terminal analysis in which the N-terminal amino acid residue is labelled and cleaved from the peptide without affecting other peptide bonds in the peptide chain."
comment: "The method is named after Pehr Victor Edman (1916–1977)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09753

[Term]
id: goldbook:09742
name: electron-transfer dissociation
def: "Ion fragmentation technique in mass spectrometry-driven proteomics based on the transfer of low energy electrons to the molecules selected for fragmentation."
comment: "ETD is particularly effective for analysis of post-translational modification."
synonym: "ETD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09780

[Term]
id: goldbook:09743
name: electron-transfer/higher-energy collision dissociation
def: "Ion fragmentation technique in mass spectrometry-driven proteomics that is a combination of electron-transfer dissociation \(ETD\) and higher-energy collision dissociation \(HCD\) in Kingdon trap instruments \(Orbitrap™\)."
comment: "The dual fragmentation allows generation of rich MS/MS spectra for peptide sequencing and post-translational modification (PTM) analysis."
synonym: "EthcD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09742
consider: goldbook:09748

[Term]
id: goldbook:09744
name: electrospray ionisation
def: "Soft ionisation technique in mass spectrometry-driven proteomics."
comment: "Electrospray ionisation is optimal for ionising liquid eluates from separation methods, as well as for the direct introduction of liquid samples to fragmentation in a mass spectrometer. Ionisation is made by positive or negative mode, depending on the ability of the molecules to form cations or anions. During the ionisation process, a biomacromolecule obtains a number of charges roughly proportional to its relative molecular mass. Also, non-covalent protein complexes may be ionised with ESI."
synonym: "ESI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09634
consider: goldbook:09780

[Term]
id: goldbook:09745
name: expression proteomics
def: "Field of study in proteomics that deals with the determination of changes in protein expression and regulation in response to different stimuli\, internal or external. It also includes the analysis of post-translational modifications \(e.g. phosphorylation\, glycosylation\, etc.\)\, their identification\, and their localisation."
synonym: "differential proteomics" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09746
name: functional proteomics
def: "Field of study in proteomics studying protein interactions on different levels\: protein-protein interactions \(interactomics\)\, the formation of protein complexes\, and the interaction of proteins with other biomolecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09633
consider: goldbook:09780
consider: goldbook:09872

[Term]
id: goldbook:09747
name: gel electrophoresis
def: "Separation technique used to separate or fractionate proteins and larger peptides according to their relative molecular mass using an electric field in polyacrylamide gel \(PAGE\)."
comment: "1D PAGE has two basic modes: a denaturing (or SDS) PAGE to estimate relative molecular masses and a native PAGE to separate proteins as their native structures."
synonym: "PAGE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09748
name: higher-energy collision dissociation
def: "Ion fragmentation technique in mass spectrometry-driven proteomics used mostly in Kingdon trap \(Orbitrap™\) instruments. It does not have low mass cut-off of collision-induced dissociation \(CID\) and therefore is used for the tandem mass tag of stable isotope labels."
synonym: "HCD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09780

[Term]
id: goldbook:09749
name: isoelectric focusing
def: "Separation technique used to separate or fractionate proteins and peptides in a gel \(or similar type of media\) according to their isoelectric point."
comment: "IEF is typically the first dimension of two-dimensional gel electrophoresis."
synonym: "IEF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09747

[Term]
id: goldbook:09750
name: mass fingerprinting
def: "Protein analysis where an unknown protein is chemically or enzymatically cleaved into peptide fragments whose masses are determined by mass spectrometry. The peptide masses are compared to peptide masses calculated for known proteins in a database and analysed statistically to determine the best match."
synonym: "mass mapping" []
synonym: "peptide mass fingerprinting" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09751
name: MS/MS data based identification
def: "Mass spectrometric method used for protein/peptide identification based on protein sequencing."
comment: "Using peptide ion fragments, the peptide sequence is read and a list of hit candidates is obtained in combination with database searching."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09738
consider: goldbook:11547

[Term]
id: goldbook:09752
name: multidimensional protein identification technology
def: "Non-gel step-wise multidimensional technique for separating and identifying individual components of complex protein and peptide mixtures. It combines fractionation of proteolytic peptides in steps on a strong cation exchanger \(SAX\) using ion exchange chromatography \(IEC\); each step uses higher elution force. Then\, each fraction is separated on reversed phase liquid chromatography and analysed using mass spectrometry."
synonym: "MudPIT" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09753
name: N-terminal analysis
def: "Chemical method for N-terminal sequencing of proteins and peptides starting at their N-terminus."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09741
consider: goldbook:09754

[Term]
id: goldbook:09754
name: N-terminus
def: "The end of an amino acid chain \(protein or polypeptide\)\, terminating in a free primary amine group."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09755
name: off-gel isoelectric focusing
def: "Separation technique used to fractionate proteins and peptides into discrete liquid fractions according to their isoelectric point."
synonym: "OFFGEL™" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09749

[Term]
id: goldbook:09756
name: off peptide product ions
def: "Protein/peptide sequencing approach using overlapping complementary information on a sequence acquired using proteolysis in bottom-up proteomic analysis by at least two different proteolytic approaches."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09735
consider: goldbook:11547

[Term]
id: goldbook:09757
name: peptide de novo sequencing
def: "Analytical process that derives an amino acid sequence of a peptide from its tandem mass spectrum without the assistance of a sequence database."
comment: "It is defined in contrast to protein/peptide identification using a database search. An advantage of de novo sequencing is its applicability to both known and novel peptides from organisms with unsequenced genome."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09758
name: peptide fragment ion
def: "Product ion which originates in a peptide precursor ion fragmentation process."
comment: "Peptide fragment ions are generated in pairs according to the kind of mechanism that dissociates the chemical bonds around the peptide bond."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09760

[Term]
id: goldbook:09759
name: peptide fragmentation technique
def: "Mass spectrometric technique that serves to generate peptide fragment ions through the fragmentation of peptide precursor ions via different physicochemical processes in an ion source."
comment: "This approach based on the top-down proteomics is an alternative to bottom-up proteomics. The main advantages include the potential for \(\pu{100\%}\) sequence coverage of the protein and improved detection of post-translational modifications."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09735
consider: goldbook:09758
consider: goldbook:09760
consider: goldbook:09786

[Term]
id: goldbook:09760
name: peptide precursor ion
def: "Peptide ion generated during the ionisation of peptides in an ion source or during tandem mass spectrometry of an intact protein in top-down proteomic analysis\, selected for further analysis by means of tandem mass spectrometry."
comment: "Once generated, a peptide fragment ion may become a precursor ion for tandem mass spectrometry of higher orders (\({\rm{MS}}^{n}\), \(n = 3\))."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09786

[Term]
id: goldbook:09761
name: peptidomics
def: "Study of the set of peptides in an organism\, its peptidome."
comment: "It uses similar approaches and methods as proteomics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09780

[Term]
id: goldbook:09762
name: protein complex
def: "Ensemble of two or more different associated proteins\, each with a specific function\, linked by non-covalent protein-protein interactions."
comment: "Protein complexes are required for most biological processes. Together they form molecular machines that perform biological functions."
comment: "Proteins with quaternary structure are not considered as protein complexes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09763
name: protein complex purification
def: "Set of methods serving to purify the intact protein complex for further analysis."
comment: "The methods used may employ single step affinity purification or tandem affinity purification (two affinity purification steps). These approaches include the direct application of an epitope on a bait protein for immunopurification or the genetic insertion of an affinity tag to bait protein, both used to co-purify the prey components of the protein complex."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09762

[Term]
id: goldbook:09764
name: protein database
def: "Collection of protein sequences from several sources\, including translations from annotated genetic coding regions\, as well as original protein and peptide sequences."
comment: "A protein database is fundamental for the determination of protein structure and function via bioinformatics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11547

[Term]
id: goldbook:09765
name: protein folding
def: "Physicochemical process by which a polypeptide folds into its characteristic and functional three-dimensional structure from a random coil."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09766
name: protein fractionation
def: "Methodical approach to simplify a complex mixture of proteomic sample."
comment: "Target compounds can either be separated into individual protein/peptides or fractionated into groups with similar physicochemical properties (polarity, charge, relative molecular mass, etc.). Different analytical separation methods are deployed to achieve this effect: liquid chromatography, gel electrophoresis, isoelectric focusing, affinity chromatography, etc."
synonym: "protein separation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09747
consider: goldbook:09749

[Term]
id: goldbook:09767
name: protein fragmentation
def: "Process which happens during tandem mass spectrometry of intact proteins."
comment: "This process is used in top-down proteomics. It generates specific peptide fragment ions from a selected protein precursor ion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09758
consider: goldbook:09786

[Term]
id: goldbook:09768
name: protein identification
def: "Analytical approach leading to the identity of a protein."
comment: "The identity of the protein is given in respect to the proteoform by its primary structure, post-translational modification, or tertiary structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09774
consider: goldbook:09785

[Term]
id: goldbook:09769
name: protein machine
def: "Supramolecular interacting system\, such as a metabolic circuit\, intracellular signal transduction\, or cell-to-cell communication."
comment: "These systems are operated under process control strategies involving integrated feedback control. The input and output of the circuits or modules are coordinated to assure the normal or adaptive function of the cell or organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09770
name: protein purification
def: "Series of processes conducted to isolate either the whole proteome or a subset from a biological sample."
comment: "Protein purification involves many different methods, such as chromatography, immunopurification, immunoprecipitation, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09675

[Term]
id: goldbook:09771
name: protein quantification
def: "Analytical methods and related techniques to measure the protein content."
comment: "Absolute quantification of proteins (AQUA) is performed via measurements on constituent proteolytic peptides using chemically synthesised isotope-labelled peptides as surrogate internal standards for mass spectrometry."
comment: "Protein quantification can be further divided into relative quantification and absolute quantification. Basic analytical methods used in proteomics to quantify protein content are immunoanalysis (see Western blotting), mass spectrometry or densitometry of differential staining. Especially mass spectrometry offers many techniques based either on stable isotope labelling or label-free approaches."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09789

[Term]
id: goldbook:09772
name: protein sequencer
def: "Equipment designed for the automatic determination of amino acid sequences of peptides using a method of N-terminal analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09741
consider: goldbook:09753

[Term]
id: goldbook:09773
name: protein staining
def: "Technique used to visualise proteins separated on electrophoretic slab gels."
comment: "Typically, three types of staining are commonly used: silver staining, which is highly sensitive and non-quantitative; Coommassie Brilliant Blue staining, which is less sensitive than silver staining and quantitative; and fluorescent dye staining, which is highly sensitive and quantitative."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09774
name: proteoform
def: "All of the different molecular forms in which the protein product of a single gene can be found\, including changes due to genetic variations\, alternatively spliced ribonucleic acid \(RNA\) transcripts\, and post-translational modifications."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09775
name: proteogenomics
def: "Field of biological research in-between proteomics and genomics using proteomic information \(mostly derived from mass spectrometry\) to improve gene annotations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09780

[Term]
id: goldbook:09776
name: proteolysis
def: "Protein cleavage to generate proteolytic peptides for bottom-up proteomic analysis\, either enzymatic or chemical."
comment: "Both enzymatic and chemical proteolysis may be sequence-specific or unspecific. Proteolysis is specific where cleavage appears at a few specific sequence motives (e.g. proteolysis by trypsin), or unspecific, being connected to wide range of sequence motives (e.g. proteolysis by chymotrypsin)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09735

[Term]
id: goldbook:09777
name: proteolytic digestion
def: "Exposure of a sample to proteolytic reactions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09776

[Term]
id: goldbook:09778
name: proteolytic enzyme
def: "Group of enzymes that cleave the polypeptide into shorter oligopeptides \(peptides\) and amino acids."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09779
name: proteolytic peptide
def: "Peptide generated via proteolysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09776

[Term]
id: goldbook:09780
name: proteomics
def: "Complex and comprehensive study of proteomes\, particularly proteins\, and the way they are expressed\, modified\, involved in metabolism\, as well as of their interactions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09781
name: relative quantification
def: "Type of protein/peptide quantification\, where the relative amounts of one protein in different samples is determined\, i.e. the ratio of the content of a protein/peptide in sample 1 to sample 2."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09782
name: stable isotope labelling
def: "Techniques which serve to quantify protein content by means of mass spectrometry. The principle lies in the introduction of a mass tag to an internal standard protein/peptide containing different stable isotopes than the protein/peptide in the sample. Mass resolved signals originating in the internal standard and the sample are read individually and evaluated."
comment: "In the case of a complex sample, the use of multiple reaction monitoring allows for the resolution of multiple overlapping signals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09783
name: structural proteomics
def: "Field in proteomics which focuses on higher orders of the protein structure\, mainly tertiary or quaternary."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09780
consider: goldbook:09785

[Term]
id: goldbook:09784
name: targeted proteomics
def: "Approach in proteomics focused on the selected proteins of a sample."
comment: "In a targeted analysis, the mass spectrometer is programmed to analyse a preselected group of proteins. This can be achieved using a technology called selected reaction monitoring (SRM; also referred to as multiple reaction monitoring, MRM), whereby assays are developed on a triple quadrupole instrument to detect fragment-ion signals arising from unique diagnostic peptides representing each of the targeted proteins."
comment: "Targeted proteomics achieves the highest sensitivity and throughput for hundreds or thousands of samples in regard to the intended aspect (namely target fragments)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09780

[Term]
id: goldbook:09785
name: tertiary structure of a protein
def: "Arrangement of all atoms of a protein molecule or a subunit of a protein molecule in space\, without regard to its relationship with neighbouring molecules or subunits."
comment: "The tertiary structure represents a three-dimensional fold/organisation of a polypeptide chain, one containing specific arrangements of secondary structures (see secondary structure of a protein)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09786
name: top-down proteomics
def: "Approach to identify proteins and characterise their amino acid sequences or post-translational modifications either by direct mass spectrometric analysis of an ionised protein molecule or by sequential combination of protein/peptide fragmentation in the ion source or mass analyser with ion trapping mass spectrometers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09735

[Term]
id: goldbook:09787
name: trypsin
def: "Serine protease with highly specific primary endoproteolytic activity that serves to generate proteolytic peptides in bottom-up proteomics analysis."
comment: "It may be modified by reductive methylation or glycosylation to increase its thermal stability."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09735

[Term]
id: goldbook:09788
name: two-dimensional gel electrophoresis
def: "Technique used to separate proteins using isoelectric focusing in a gel. The proteins are then further separated in the second dimension using denaturing PAGE."
comment: "2D PAGE greatly enhances the capacity of the separation and facilitates further analysis, such as the difference gel electrophoresis or the mass spectrometric analysis of gel separated proteins."
synonym: "2D PAGE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09747
consider: goldbook:09749

[Term]
id: goldbook:09789
name: Western blot
def: "Immunoanalytical technique for the identification of polypeptides separated using gel electrophoresis. The polypeptide is transferred by blotting to a membrane\, where it undergoes specific interaction with primary antibody that is specific to the protein of interest. The peptides are detected as complexes by a label and/or enzymatic reaction\, which may be conjugated to the primary antibody directly or via a separate \(secondary\) antibody."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09708
consider: goldbook:09728

[Term]
id: goldbook:09790
name: cultivation
def: "Sample pretreatment to degrade complex metabolites in the presence of oxygen; a method for amplifying the concentration of native metabolites in solution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09791
name: design of experiment
def: "Metabolomic workflow composed of sampling\, metabolism quenching\, metabolite extraction\, metabolite analyses\, data analysis\, and interpretation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09792
name: endometabolome
def: "Complete set of metabolites inside a cell \(intracellular metabolites\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09793
name: excretion
def: "Process removing compounds and their metabolites from the body\, usually through the kidneys \(via urine\) or in the feces. Unless excretion is complete\, the accumulation of foreign substances can adversely affect normal metabolism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09794
name: exometabolome
def: "Complete set of metabolites outside the cell \(extracellular environment\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09795
name: fingerprinting
def: "Qualitative analysis of the endometabolome."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09792

[Term]
id: goldbook:09796
name: fluxomics
def: "In vivo measurements of metabolic fluxes and integration of the results into stoichiometric network models."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09797
name: footprinting
def: "Qualitative analysis of the exometabolome."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09794

[Term]
id: goldbook:09798
