[Term]
id: goldbook:09802
name: metabolite profiling
def: "Strategy to identify and quantify a particular set of metabolites belonging to a specific metabolic pathway or class of compounds."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09803
name: metabolome
def: "Complete set \(from \\\(\\pu\{50\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{1000\}\\\) metabolites\) of organic or inorganic compounds of low relative molecular mass\, present in the cell or organism and which participate in the metabolic reactions required for growth\, maintenance\, and normal functioning."
comment: "The metabolome forms a large network of metabolic reactions where outputs from one enzymatic chemical reaction are inputs to other chemical reactions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09804
name: metabolomics
def: "Complex and comprehensive study of metabolome; identification and quantification of the small molecule metabolic products of a biological system \(cell\, tissue\, organ\, biological fluid\, or organism\) at a specific point in time."
comment: "An essential part of systems biology in addition to genomics, transcriptomics, proteomics, interactomics, and fluxomics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09780
consider: goldbook:09796
consider: goldbook:09803
consider: goldbook:09872

[Term]
id: goldbook:09805
name: metabonomics
def: "Measurement of the dynamic multiparametric metabolic response of a living system to pathophysiological stimuli or genetic modification."
comment: "This term is sometime misapplied to refer to the whole of "metabolomics"."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09804

[Term]
id: goldbook:09806
name: primary metabolite
def: "Metabolite directly involved in the normal life processes of each cell."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09807
name: activated nucleotide sugar
def: "Activated form of monosaccharide linked to a nucleotide to be available in a high-energy state for glycosyl transfer."
synonym: "nucleotide sugar" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
