[Term]
id: goldbook:09808
name: anomeric hydroxy group
def: "Hydroxy group that originates from the aldehydic or ketonic group of a monosaccharide after ring closure."
comment: "A functional group in one of two stereoisomers of a cyclic saccharide that differs only in its configuration at the hemiacetal or hemiketal carbon, which is also called the anomeric carbon. An anomer is a special type of epimer."
comment: "The group is sometimes called, incorrectly, "anomeric hydroxyl group"."
synonym: "glycosidic hydroxy group" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09829
consider: goldbook:09830

[Term]
id: goldbook:09809
name: carbohydrate
def: "Monosaccharide\, oligosaccharide and polysaccharide substances\, as well as substances derived from a monosaccharide by reduction of the carbonyl group \(alditol\)\, by oxidation\, including the oxidation of one or more terminal groups of a carboxylic acid\, or by replacement of one or more hydroxy groups by a hydrogen atom\, an amino group\, a thiol group\, or by similar heteroatomic groups. This term also includes derivatives of these of these compounds."
comment: "The term carbohydrate was applied originally to monosaccharides, in recognition of the fact that their empirical composition can be expressed as \(\ce{C_{m}(H2O)_{n}}\). However, the term is now used generically in a wider sense."
synonym: "glycan" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09810
name: comparative glycoproteomics
def: "Field of glycoproteomics that studies that the changes in the structures and expression levels of glycoproteins under different conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
