[Term]
id: goldbook:09815
name: glycoform
def: "Specific form of a glycoprotein containing a distinct glycan structure per glycosylation site."
comment: "Natural glycoprotein consists of a population of glycoforms resulting from variable glycan structure and/or glycan attachment site occupancy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09821

[Term]
id: goldbook:09816
name: glycogene
def: "Gene encoding an enzyme or other functional protein for glycan synthesis."
comment: "Proteins for glycan synthesis include glycosyltransferases, sugar-nucleotide synthases, sugar-nucleotide transporters, and sulfotransferases (see glycosylation, activated nucleotide sugars)."
comment: "The term should not be confused with glycogen (an energy-storage glucose polysacharide in animals and fungi)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09807
consider: goldbook:09827

[Term]
id: goldbook:09817
name: glycolipid
def: "Compound containing a glycan covalently linked to a lipid aglycon."
comment: "The term "lipid" comprises several types of compounds. Therefore, different classes of glycolipides are described. For example, typical glycolipids in higher organisms are glycosphingolipids."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09818
name: glycome
def: "Complete set of glycans and glycoconjugates produced by a species\, tissue\, or cell in a specified time\, space\, and environment."
comment: "Glycome is an analogue of the terms genome, proteome, and transcriptome."
comment: "The terms, as for example "sialome", are sometimes used for the specific subclasses of the glycome."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:09819
name: glycomics
def: "Complex and comprehensive study of the glycome."
comment: ""Glycomics" is an analogue of the terms genomics or proteomics. The terms, as for example "fucanomics" or "galactanomics", are sometimes used for the specialised fields of glycomics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09780
consider: goldbook:09818

[Term]
id: goldbook:09820
name: glycone
def: "Carbohydrate part of a glycoconjugate or a glycoside."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09809
