[Term]
id: goldbook:09979
name: nominal property
def: "Property of a phenomenon\, body\, or substance\, where the property has no size."
comment: ""Nominal property" is sometimes termed "nameable property", but not here."
comment: "The concept "nominal property" is defined as the opposite of "quantity", i.e. the former concept lacks the essential characteristic of "size" (or "magnitude"). In such cases, ISO 704:2009-6.5.4 allows a "negative definition"."
comment: "The term "attribute" has sometimes been used to designate "nominal property", but not here."
comment: "The term "qualitative property" is also used, but not here as it is ambiguous because "ordinal quantity" is often included under that term."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2011-0613
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
