[Term]
id: goldbook:09983
name: dedicated kind-of-nominal-property
def: "Kind-of-nominal-property with a sort of system and any pertinent sort\(s\) of component\(s\)."
comment: "A dedicated kind-of-nominal-property is not specified to any individual person, in contrast to an individual nominal property, and it cannot have a nominal property value."
comment: "In clinical laboratory report forms, dedicated kind-of-nominal-properties may be described according to an internationally recommended NPU syntax from IFCC-IUPAC. The syntax is System(specification)-Component(specification); kind-of-property(specification). The last "specification" might contain information on the examination procedure or the nominal property value set. The initial capital for System and for Component is mandatory.Examples of the NPU syntax:.Blood—Plasma; colour({milky, red, yellow});.Erythrocytes(Blood)—Erythrocyte antigen; blood group({A, B, AB, O}).For examples 1-4 above, individual nominal properties can be written as follows (omitting patient identity and time but including the nominal property value for clarity):Patient—Spinal fluid; colour(visual)=reddish;DNA(Leukocytes)—CYP2D6 gene; sequence variation(allele specific PCR)=*1/*3;Expectoration—Bacterium; taxon(Phadebact coagglutination test)=Mycobacterium tuberculosis;Monocytes(Blood)—Nuclei; shape=oval."
comment: "The dedicated kinds-of-nominal-property examples above correspond to examples 1-4 of kind-of-nominal-property."
comment: "The patient"s name (or other identifier), location, and date and time of obtaining the sample of the system under consideration shall always be given in the clinical laboratory report."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2011-0613
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09980
consider: goldbook:09982
consider: goldbook:09990
consider: goldbook:09996
consider: goldbook:09997

[Term]
id: goldbook:09984
name: examination
def: "Process of experimentally obtaining one or more nominal property values that can reasonably be attributed to a nominal property."
comment: "The activity of examination essentially consists in comparing the property considered, i.e. the examinand by way of an examining system, with the property of a "reference" of similar nature. Such a reference may be personal and subjective, such as a person"s memory of a colour, or the reference may be objective, such as a nominal reference material."
comment: "The outcome of an examination is an examination result."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2011-0613
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
