[Term]
id: goldbook:10007
name: examination precision
def: "Closeness of agreement between nominal indications on an examining system or examined values obtained by replicate examinations on the same or similar objects under specified examination conditions."
comment: ""Specified examination conditions" can, for example, be repeatability condition of examination, intermediate precision condition of examination, or reproducibility condition of examination."
comment: "A proportion distribution of a set of examined values describes proportions of data belonging to every possible nominal property value."
comment: "Examination precision can be expressed numerically by measures of dispersion of examined values such as Index of Qualitative Variation (IQV) and the Shannon"s entropy, under specified examination conditions. IQV varies between 0 (no dispersion, all examined values in a single class) and 1 (two or more classes with identical frequency). Shannon"s entropy varies between 0 (no dispersion, that is all examined values belong to a single category) and a maximum value equal to the logarithm (on basis 2) of the number of all categories. See Example."
comment: "Examination precision is a feature of an examining system used with a specified examination procedure."
comment: "Examination precision is used to define examination repeatability, intermediate examination precision, and examination reproducibility."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2011-0613
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09979
consider: goldbook:09984
consider: goldbook:09986
consider: goldbook:09991
consider: goldbook:09997
consider: goldbook:10000

