[Term]
id: goldbook:10047
name: data matrix
def: "Measurement results on a system arranged in a \\\(m \\times n\\\) matrix\, with \\\(m\\\) objects and \\\(n\\\) variables."
comment: "By convention a matrix is arranged with \(m\) rows and \(n\) columns."
comment: "For multi-way data the data is arranged in a hypercube of \(m \times n_{1} \times n_{2} \times\) …, where \(n_{1}\), \(n_{2}\) … are the kinds of explanatory variable."
comment: "Objects are also called "samples", but confusion with physical "test samples" in analytical chemistry should be avoided."
comment: "Variables are also called features, or explanatory variables."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10051
consider: goldbook:10056

[Term]
id: goldbook:10048
name: data pre-processing
def: "Manipulation of raw data prior to a specified data analysis treatment."
comment: "All data pre-processing methods imply some assumptions about the nature of the variability in the data set. It is important that these assumptions are understood and appropriate for the data set involved."
comment: "Aside from the three main categories of data pre-processing methods (mean centering, scaling and transformation), data pre-processing can refer to any other procedures carried out on the raw data, including mass binning and peak selection. In the case of multivariate images, this can also include region-of-interest selection and image filtering or binning."
comment: "More than one data pre-processing method can be applied to the same data set. The order of data pre-processing is important and can affect assumptions made on the nature of variance in the data set."
comment: "The term "pre-processing" is preferred to the term "pre-treatment" to reduce confusion with physical sample preparation or treatment prior to experimental analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10053
consider: goldbook:10058
consider: goldbook:10060

[Term]
id: goldbook:10049
name: dynamic time warping
def: "Process of synchronizing a data matrix so that it represents the same time shifts."
comment: "The method is used in chromatography to align peaks by their retention times."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10050
name: evaluation data
def: "Data used to validate a model."
comment: ""Test data" is also used for data from an unknown sample, and should not be used for "evaluation data"."
comment: "Evaluation data should be independent of the data used to calibrate or train a model."
synonym: "validation data" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
