id: goldbook:10064
name: variance scaling
def: "Scaling in which the scaling matrix is the standard deviation of each variable across the objects. \\\[a_\{i\,j\}^\{\\ast\} = \\frac\{a_\{i\,j\}\}\{s_\{j\}\}\\\]"
comment: "A variable occupies a column of the data matrix."
comment: "Variance scaling equalizes the importance of each variable in multivariate data."
comment: "When used with mean centering variance scaling is known as autoscaling."
