[Term]
id: goldbook:10080
name: Plackett−Burman design
def: "Incomplete experimental design to estimate main effects for which each combination of factor levels for any pair of factors appears the same number of times."
comment: "For \(4 \times N\) experiments, \(4 \times N − 1\) main effects and the mean are estimated."
comment: "If less than \(4 \times N − 1\) factors are being studied, dummy factors are inserted which allow estimation of the repeatability standard deviation of the measurement results."
comment: "Plackett–Burman designs are typically given for two levels, with a number of experiments that is a multiple of 4 but not a power of 2. (The latter case is a fractional-factorial design)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
