[Term]
id: goldbook:10081
name: resolution of a design
def: "One more than the smallest nth-order interaction effect that some main effect is aliased with."
comment: "Full-factorial designs have no effects that are aliased and therefore have infinite resolution."
comment: "Resolution is used to describe the extent to which fractional-factorial designs create aliased effects."
comment: "The resolution is written as a Roman numeral."
synonym: "resolution" []
