[Term]
id: goldbook:10082
name: response surface methodology
def: "Experimental design in which the response is modelled in terms of one or more factor levels."
comment: "Response surface methodology is usually associated with optimization. The model used is typically a quadratic function leading to a maximum or minimum response in the factor space."
comment: "The term "surface" implies two factors and a single response, when a plot of the modelled response as a function of values of the factors leads to a surface in the three-dimensional space. This can be generalized to any number of factors."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10042
consider: goldbook:10071
consider: goldbook:10072
