[Term]
id: goldbook:10083
name: alternating least squares regression
def: "Solution to the multivariate decomposition of a data matrix in which iteratively a solution of one output matrix is used to compute the second matrix\, after the application of constraints."
comment: "ALS is used to decompose multiple spectra (\(\boldsymbol{X}\)) into concentration (\(\boldsymbol{C}\)) and component spectra (\(\boldsymbol{S}\)). \(\boldsymbol{X} = \boldsymbol{C}\boldsymbol{S}^{\rm{T}}\). Because spectra and concentrations cannot be negative at each iteration negative values are set to zero."
synonym: "ALS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "alternating regression" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10055

[Term]
id: goldbook:10084
name: autoregression
def: "Stochastic process in which future values are estimated based on a weighted sum of past values."
comment: "A process called AR(1) is a first order process, meaning that the current value is based on the immediately preceding value. An AR(2) process has the current value based on the previous two values."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10085
name: biplot
def: "Combination plot of a scores plot as points and loadings plot as vectors for common factors."
comment: "Points in the scores plot (objects) that fall on a loadings vector are considered to be characterised by the variable associated with the vector."
comment: "The plots are scaled to facilitate interpretation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10096
consider: goldbook:10097
consider: goldbook:10113

[Term]
id: goldbook:10086
name: bootstrapping
def: "Estimation of parameters by multiple re-sampling from measured data to approximate its distribution."
comment: "Bootstrapping is an alternative to cross validation in model validation."
comment: "Multiple resamples of the original data allow calculation of the distribution of a parameter of interest, and therefore its standard error (see example)."
comment: "Random sampling with replacement is used when the data are assumed to be from an independent and identically-distributed population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10087
name: canonical variables
def: "Linear combinations of data with the greatest correlation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10088

[Term]
id: goldbook:10088
name: canonical variate analysis
def: "Multivariate technique which finds linear combinations of two sets of data that are most highly correlated."
comment: "The combinations with the greatest correlation, denoted U1 and V1 are known as the "first canonical variables". The next canonical functions, U2 and V2 are then restricted so that they are uncorrelated with U1 and V1. Everything is scaled so that the variance equals 1."
comment: "The relationship between the canonical variables is known as the canonical function."
synonym: "canonical analysis" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10089
name: common factor analysis
def: "Factor analysis in which latent variables are calculated that maximise the correlation with observed variables."
comment: "The common factors are not unique. Typically factors are rotated so that the factors are more easily interpreted in terms of the original variables."
synonym: "exploratory factor analysis" []
synonym: "factor analysis" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10093
consider: goldbook:10095

[Term]
id: goldbook:10090
name: core consistency diagnostic
def: "Method to assess the appropriateness of a PARAFAC model."
comment: "An appropriate PARAFAC model is a model where the components primarily reflect low-rank, trilinear variation in the data."
comment: "The principle of the method is to assess the degree of superdiagonality of the model."
synonym: "CONCORDIA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10103

[Term]
id: goldbook:10091
name: correspondence factor analysis
def: "Factor analysis applied to categorical data in which orthogonal factors are obtained from a contingency table."
synonym: "correspondence analysis" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10093

[Term]
id: goldbook:10092
name: evolving factor analysis
def: "Factor analysis that follows the change or evolution of the rank of the data matrix as a function of an ordered variable."
comment: "The changing rank is calculated by principal-component analysis on an increasing data matrix."
comment: "The ordering variable may be time."
synonym: "EFA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10093
consider: goldbook:10106

[Term]
id: goldbook:10093
name: factor analysis
def: "Matrix decomposition of a data matrix \(\\\(\\boldsymbol\{X\}\\\)\) into the product of a scores matrix \(\\\(\\boldsymbol\{T\}\\\)\) and the transpose of the loadings matrix \(\\\(\\boldsymbol\{P\}^\{\\rm\{T\}\}\\\)\)."
comment: "Factor analysis is equivalent to a rotation in data space where the factors form the new axes. This is not necessarily rotation that maintains orthogonality except in the case of PCA."
comment: "Factor analysis methods include common factor analysis (also called ‘factor analysis’), principal component analysis, and multivariate curve resolution."
comment: "Hence \(\boldsymbol{X} = \boldsymbol{TP}^{\rm{T}} + \boldsymbol{E}\), where \(\boldsymbol{E}\) is a residual matrix."
comment: "The number of factors selected in factor analysis is smaller than the rank of the data matrix."
comment: "The residual matrix contains data that are not described by the factor analysis model, and is usually assumed to contain noise."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10041
consider: goldbook:10047
consider: goldbook:10089
consider: goldbook:10096
consider: goldbook:10100
consider: goldbook:10106
consider: goldbook:10112

[Term]
id: goldbook:10094
name: <em>G</em>-fold cross validation
def: "Cross validation of a data set of \\\(N\\\) objects in which \\\(N/G\\\) objects are removed at each iteration of the procedure."
comment: "Because the perturbation of the model is larger than in leave-one-out cross validation, the prediction ability of the G-fold cross validation is less optimistic than obtained with leave-one-out cross validation."
comment: "Objects 1 to \(N/G\) are removed on the first iteration, then objects \(N/G + 1\) to \(2N/G\) after replacement of the first \(N/G\) objects, and so on."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10095
name: latent variable
def: "Variable that is inferred through a mathematical model from other variables that are observed."
comment: "A distinction can be made between ‘hidden variable’, which is considered to be an actual variable that is buried in the effects of other variables and noise, and a ‘latent variable’ that is entirely hypothetical."
comment: "The factors obtain from common factor analysis are termed latent variables."
synonym: "hidden variable" []
synonym: "latent construct" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10041
consider: goldbook:10089

[Term]
id: goldbook:10096
name: loadings
def: "Projection of a factor onto the variables."
comment: ""Loadings" (plural) refers to a column in the loadings matrix that relates to a particular factor. "loading" (singular) is the particular contribution of a variable in the original space to the factor."
comment: "In multivariate curve resolution the term "pure component spectrum" is interchangeable with the term "loading" and is therefore deprecated. The term, in spectroscopy, may be confused with the spectrum for a pure material."
comment: "In principal component analysis the loadings are also the cosine angles between the variables and a particular factor."
comment: "The loadings on a factor reflect the relationships between the variables on that factor."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10100
consider: goldbook:10106
consider: goldbook:10112

[Term]
id: goldbook:10097
name: loadings plot
def: "Plot of one loading against variable number\, or two or three loadings against each other."
comment: "Usually the loadings associated with the early factors (1, 2, 3) are plotted to reveal relationships among the variables."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10085
consider: goldbook:10096

[Term]
id: goldbook:10098
name: maximum likelihood principal component analysis
def: "Principal-component analysis that incorporates information about measurement uncertainty to develop models that are optimal in a maximum likelihood sense."
synonym: "MLPCA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10106

[Term]
id: goldbook:10099
name: mean squared error of prediction
def: "In multivariate calibration the average of the squared deviation of estimated values from the values of evaluation data. For \\\(N\\\) evaluation data where \\\(c_\{i\}\\\) is an observed value and \\\(\\hat c_\{i\}\\\) is the predicted value. \\\[E_\{\\rm\{MSEP\}\} = \\frac\{\\sum\\limits_\{i\\\,=\\\,1\}^\{i\\\,=\\\,N\} \(\\hat c_\{i\}\\\,-\\\, c_\{i\}\)^2\}\{N\}\\\]"
comment: "Mean squared error of prediction is the square of root mean squared error of prediction."
synonym: "mean squared error of estimation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10050
consider: goldbook:10110
consider: goldbook:10153

[Term]
id: goldbook:10100
name: multivariate curve resolution
def: "Factor analysis for the decomposition of multicomponent data into a linear sum of chemically-meaningful components when little or no prior information about the composition is available."
comment: "MCR factors are extracted by the iterative minimization of the residual matrix using an alternating least squares approach, while applying suitable constraints, such as non-negativity, to the loadings and scores. MCR can be performed on the data matrix with or without data pre-processing."
comment: "MCR factors are not unique but are dependent on initial estimates, the number of factors to be resolved, constraints applied and convergence criteria. MCR factors are not required to be orthogonal."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10048
consider: goldbook:10083
consider: goldbook:10093

[Term]
id: goldbook:10101
name: non-linear iterative partial least squares
def: "Iterative decomposition of a data matrix to give principal components."
comment: "The algorithm is very fast if only a few principal components are required, because the covariance matrix is not computed."
comment: "Writing the model as \(\boldsymbol{X} = \boldsymbol{T}\boldsymbol{P}^{\rm{T}} + \boldsymbol{E}\), the first principal component is computed from a data matrix. The data explained by this PC are then subtracted from \(\boldsymbol{X}\) and the algorithm applied again to residual data. The procedure is repeated until sufficient principal components are obtained."
synonym: "NIPALS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10047
consider: goldbook:10107

[Term]
id: goldbook:10102
name: nonlinear mapping
def: "Projection of objects defined in a multivariate space onto two- or three-dimensional space so that the distances between objects are preserved as well as possible."
comment: "An often applied criterion for the mapping error (\(E\)) is the relative squared error between the true distance \(d_{ij}\) and mapped distance \(\delta_{ij}\)."
comment: "Several iterative optimization procedures can be applied to minimize \(E\), such as steepest descent."
synonym: "NLM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10103
name: parallel factors analysis
def: "Decomposition of a three-way data matrix into the sum of sets of two-way loadings matrices."
comment: "A representation of PARAFAC is \(x_{ijk} = \sum\limits_{r\,=\,1}^R a_{ir}b_{jr}c_{kr} + e_{ijk}\), where \(x_{ijk}\) is \(i\),\(j\),\(k\)-th element of the data matrix, and \(a_{ir}\), \(b_{jr}\), \(c_{kr}\) are the components of the loadings matrices. \(e_{ijk}\) is the \(i\),\(j\),\(k\)-th element of residual matrix."
comment: "A schematic representation of the PARAFAC model is "
comment: "PARAFAC is a special case of the Tucker3 model (see Tucker tri-linear analysis) where the core matrix is the identity matrix, and \(r = s = t = R\) ."
comment: "The PARAFAC model is also known as Canonical Decomposition (CANDECOMP)."
synonym: "canonical decomposition" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10096
consider: goldbook:10116

[Term]
id: goldbook:10104
name: prediction error sum of squares
def: "In multivariate calibration for a prediction set of \\\(N\\\) data where \\\(c_\{i\}\\\) is an observed value and \\\(\\hat c_\{i\}\\\) is the predicted value. \\\[E_\{\\rm\{PRESS\}\} = \\sum\\limits_\{i\\\,=\\\,1\}^\{i\\\,=\\\,N\} \(\\hat c_\{i\} - c_\{i\}\)^2\\\]"
synonym: "residual sum of squares" []
synonym: "sum of squared errors of prediction" []
synonym: "sum of squared residuals" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10110
consider: goldbook:10153

[Term]
id: goldbook:10105
name: principal component-discriminant analysis
def: "Discriminant analysis on a multivariate data set that has been subject to principal-component analysis."
comment: "This procedure removes collinearity from the multivariate data and ensures that the new predictor variables, which are PCA scores, are distributed normally."
synonym: "PC-DA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10055
consider: goldbook:10106

[Term]
id: goldbook:10106
name: principal-component analysis
def: "Factor analysis in which factors are calculated that successively capture the greatest variance in the data set."
comment: "The factorization is written \(\boldsymbol{X} = \boldsymbol{T}\boldsymbol{P}^{\rm{T}} + \boldsymbol{E}\), where \(\boldsymbol{T}\) is the scores matrix, \(\boldsymbol{P}\) is the loadings matrix and \(\boldsymbol{E}\) is a residual matrix."
comment: "The factors are orthogonal and are known as principal-component factors."
comment: "The term "principal-component analysis" is preferred to the plural "principal-components analysis"."
synonym: "PCA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10093
consider: goldbook:10096
consider: goldbook:10101
consider: goldbook:10107
consider: goldbook:10112

[Term]
id: goldbook:10107
name: principal-component factor
def: "Orthogonal factors obtained in a principal-component analysis."
comment: "ISO 18115 recommends the use of the term "PCA factor"."
comment: "The successive factors explain reducing fractions of the variance of the data set, and are written PC1, PC2 …"
synonym: "PC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "principal component" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10106

[Term]
id: goldbook:10108
name: Procrustes analysis
def: "Comparison of shapes of multi-dimensional objects by a series of geometrical transformations to minimise the sum of squared distances between the transformed and target structures while maintaining the internal structure of the objects."
comment: "For two objects defined by \(\boldsymbol{X}\) and \(\boldsymbol{Y}\) the manipulation orthogonal rotation/reflection matrix \(\boldsymbol{R}\) Procrustes analysis minimises: \(\parallel\! \boldsymbol{Y} - \boldsymbol{X}\boldsymbol{R}\parallel^{2}\) subject to \(\boldsymbol{R}^{\rm{T}} \boldsymbol{R} = \boldsymbol{R} \boldsymbol{R}^{\rm{T}} = 1\)."
comment: "Ordinary, or classical, Procrustes analysis is when an object is compared to one other object, which may be a reference shape. Generalized Procrustes analysis compares three or more shapes to an optimally-determined mean shape."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10109
name: root mean square error of cross validation
def: "Root mean square error of prediction when the predicted data is obtained by cross validation."
synonym: "RMSECV" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
