[Term]
id: goldbook:10110
name: root mean squared error of prediction
def: "In multivariate calibration or classification for \\\(N\\\) evaluation data where \\\(c_\{i\}\\\) is an observed value and \\\(\\hat c_\{i\}\\\) is the predicted value \\\[E_\{\\rm\{RMSEP\}\} = \\sqrt \{\\frac\{\\sum\\limits_\{i\\\,=\\\,1\}^\{i\\\,=\\\,N\} \(\\hat c_\{i\}\\\,-\\\,c_\{i\}\)^2\}\{N\}\}\\\]"
comment: "For completely independent, normally distributed evaluation data, RMSEP is a measure of the bias of the calibration."
comment: "RMSEP is related to the prediction error sum of squares (PRESS) by \(E_{\rm{RMSEP}} = \sqrt \frac{E_{\rm{PRESS}}}{N}\) ."
comment: "When prediction is by cross validation RMSEP may be termed root mean square error of cross validation."
synonym: "root mean squared error of estimation" []
synonym: "standard error of estimation" []
synonym: "standard error of prediction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10050
consider: goldbook:10153

[Term]
id: goldbook:10111
name: simple-to-use interactive self-modelling mixture analysis
def: "Interactive method to obtain concentrations and pure spectra from spectra of mixtures using directly-measured variables."
comment: "A data matrix \(\boldsymbol{D} = \boldsymbol{C} \times \boldsymbol{P}^{\rm{T}} + \boldsymbol{E}\) where \(\boldsymbol{C}\) is a concentration matrix, \(\boldsymbol{P}\) pure spectra of mixture components and \(\boldsymbol{E}\) an error matrix. Pure spectra are estimated \(\boldsymbol{\hat Y}\) which allows projection of a concentration matrix \(\boldsymbol{C^{\ast}}\) from which the data matrix can be reconstructed and compared with the measured spectra. \[\left\{ {\matrix{ {\boldsymbol{\hat P} = \boldsymbol{D}^{\rm{T}} \boldsymbol{C}(\boldsymbol{C}^{\rm{T}}\boldsymbol{C})}^{-1} \cr {\boldsymbol{C^{*}} = \boldsymbol{C}\boldsymbol{\hat P}(\boldsymbol{\hat P}^{\rm{T}}\boldsymbol{\hat P})}^{-1} \cr}} \right. {\rm{then}}\;{\boldsymbol{D}_{{\rm{recon}}}} = \boldsymbol{C^{*}} \times \boldsymbol{\hat P}^{\rm{T}}\]"
comment: "Second derivatives of spectra can be used for modelling."
comment: "The directly-measured variables are called "pure variables" in the method."
synonym: "SIMPLISMA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10047

[Term]
id: goldbook:10112
name: score
def: "Factor analysis projection of an object onto a factor."
comment: "In principal-component analysis, the factors are orthogonal and the scores are an orthogonal projection of the objects onto a factor."
comment: "The scores on a factor reflect the relationships between objects for that factor."
comment: "The term scores (plural) refers to a whole column in the scores matrix that relates to a particular factor. The term score (singular) is the projection of a particular object onto the factor."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10093
consider: goldbook:10096
consider: goldbook:10106

[Term]
id: goldbook:10113
name: scores plot
def: "Plot of one score against object number\, or two or three scores against each other."
comment: "Usually the scores associated with the early factors (1, 2, 3) are plotted to reveal relationships among the objects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
