consider: goldbook:10097
consider: goldbook:10112

[Term]
id: goldbook:10114
name: simulated annealing
def: "Generic probabilistic meta-heuristic to locate a good approximation to the global optimum of a given function in a large search space\, in which there is a slow decrease in the probability of accepting worse solutions as the solution space is explored."
comment: "The function \(E(\rm{s})\) to be minimized is analogous to the internal energy of the system in that state. The goal is to bring the system, from an arbitrary initial state, to a state with the minimum possible energy. At each step, the heuristic considers some neighbouring state \(s^{\prime}\) of the current state \(s\), and probabilistically decides between moving the system to state \(s^{\prime}\) or staying in state \(s\). These probabilities ultimately lead the system to move to states of lower energy. Typically this step is repeated until the system reaches a state that is good enough for the application, or until a given computation budget has been exhausted."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10115
name: singular value decomposition
def: "A factorization of an \\\(m \\times n\\\) matrix \(\\\(\\boldsymbol\{M\}\\\)\) such that \\\(\\boldsymbol\{M\} = \\boldsymbol\{U\}\\boldsymbol\{\\Sigma\} \\boldsymbol\{V\}^\{T\}\\\)\, where \\\(\\boldsymbol\{U\}\\\) is an \\\(m \\times m\\\) matrix\, \\\(\\boldsymbol\{\\Sigma\}\\\) is a \\\(m \\times n\\\) matrix and \\\(\\boldsymbol\{V\}^\{\\rm\{T\}\}\\\) is a \\\(n \\times n\\\) matrix."
comment: "If \(\boldsymbol{M}\) is a data matrix with \(m\) objects and \(n\) variables, the matrix \(\boldsymbol{U}\) is the scores matrix, the diagonal of \(\boldsymbol{\Sigma}\) contain the square roots of the eigenvalues and \(\boldsymbol{V}\) is the loadings matrix."
synonym: "SVD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10047
consider: goldbook:10096
consider: goldbook:10112

[Term]
id: goldbook:10116
name: Tucker tri-linear analysis
def: "Decomposition of a three-way data matrix into a three-way core matrix\, and three\, two-way loadings matrices."
comment: "A graphical representation of the Tucker3 model is "
comment: "A representation of the Tucker3 model is \[x_{ijk} = \sum\limits_{r\,=\,1}^R \sum\limits_{s\,=\,1}^S \sum\limits_{t\,=\,1}^T a_{ir}b_{js}{c_{kt}z_{rst} + e_{ijk}}\] where \(x_{ijk}\) is the data matrix, \(a_{ir}\), \(b_{js}\), \(c_{kt}\) are the loadings matrices, and \(z_{rst}\) is the core matrix. \(e_{ijk}\) is the residual matrix."
synonym: "Tucker3 model" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
