[Term]
id: goldbook:10123
name: disjoint principal component analysis
def: "Principal-component analysis \(PCA\) independently performed on each class as a step in classification."
comment: "Soft independent modelling of class analogy is an example of the use of disjoint principal component analysis."
comment: "When a PCA model is obtained using all classes, it is known as conjoint PCA."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
