[Term]
id: goldbook:10124
name: Euclidean distance
def: "Distance \(\\\(d_\{i\,j\}\\\)\) between two objects \(\\\(i\\\) and \\\(j\\\)\) calculated as the square root of the sum of the squared differences between \\\(k\\\) variables \(\\\(x\\\)\) that describe the objects. \\\[d_\{i\,j\} = \\sqrt \{\\sum\\limits_\{k\\\,=\\\,1\}^\{k\\\,=\\\,N\} \(x_\{i\,k\} - x_\{j\,k\}\)^2\}\\\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
