[Term]
id: goldbook:10125
name: forward chaining
def: "Inference method from data to hypothesis."
comment: "In logic, forward chaining is the application of modus ponens (if \(\rm{P}\) implies \(\rm{Q}\), given \(\rm{P}\) then \(\rm{Q}\))."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10126
name: forward stepwise linear discriminant analysis
def: "Linear discriminant analysis in which variables to build the discriminant functions are introduced one at a time to maximise the discrimination\, until there is no significant improvement."
comment: "Interrelationships between variables that have not yet been selected are ignored, and variables already added, which may become largely redundant through subsequent additions, cannot be removed."
comment: "Significant improvement is usually tested by an F-test"
