[Term]
id: goldbook:10127
name: fuzzy clustering
def: "Classification in which membership of an object in each possible class is given a weight between zero and one."
comment: "In so-called hard cluster algorithms membership of a group can only take values 0 or 1, but in fuzzy clustering any value between 0 and 1 is allowed subject to the sum of all memberships of an object being 1."
