[Term]
id: goldbook:10131
name: <em>k</em>-nearest neighbour
def: "Non-parametric supervised classification method for objects based on the closest training examples in the variable space."
comment: "An object is classified by a majority vote of its \(k\)-nearest neighbours, with the object being assigned to the class most common."
comment: "When \(k = 1\) the method is known as "nearest neighbour"."
comment: "\(k\) is a small positive integer."
