[Term]
id: goldbook:10140
name: regularized discriminant analysis
def: "Discriminant analysis in which the criterion function is based on a combination of pooled covariance matrix and the individual within-group covariance matrix."
comment: "The covariance matrix (\(\sum_{k}(\lambda)\)) is related to the class covariance matrix (\(\sum_{k}\)) and the pooled covariance matrix (\(\sum_{\rm{pooled}}\)) by \(\sum_{k}(\lambda) = (1 - \lambda)\sum_{k} + \lambda\sum_{\rm{pooled}}\)"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10141
name: similarity index
def: "Quantity that describes the equivalence of two objects characterised by multivariate data."
comment: "A similarity index may be in the interval, where 0 is complete dissimilarity and 1 is complete equivalence."
comment: "When the term "distance" is used the quantity is some function of the differences of coordinates in the multivariate data space."
synonym: "similarity distance" []
