[Term]
id: goldbook:10144
name: supervised classification
def: "Classification in which\, in a first step\, a model is built using data from objects of known classes\, and in a second step\, the model is applied to new data to assign a class to unknown objects."
comment: "Algorithms for supervised classification include discriminant analysis, support vector machine, artificial neural network, Bayesian classifier."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10077

[Term]
id: goldbook:10145
name: Tanimoto similarity index
def: "Fraction of variables that are considered to agree between two objects."
comment: "The Tanimoto index is essentially similar to the Jaccard index. (See https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaccard_index)."
comment: "The Tanimoto index is used in drug discovery and QSAR for comparison of structures in large data bases in an efficient way."
comment: "The rules for agreement must be defined. For example in an elemental analysis, element concentrations equivalent within \(\pu{20\%}\)."
synonym: "Tanimoto index" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10146
name: unsupervised classification
def: "Classification in which no prior information about membership of groups is known."
comment: "Algorithms for unsupervised classification include k-means cluster analysis, hierarchical cluster analysis."
comment: "The number of groups may be specified."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
