[Term]
id: goldbook:10150
name: errors-in-variables regression
def: "Least squares regression in which both the response variable and predictor variable have measurement error."
comment: "The model for EIV regression is \[\left\{\matrix{c_{i} = \alpha + \beta x_{i}^{*} + \varepsilon_{i} \cr x_{i} = x_{i}^{*} + \eta_{i} \cr}\right.\] where \(x^{*}\) is the true value of the predictor variable, \(c_{i}\) concentration and \(\varepsilon\) and \(\eta\) are errors."
comment: "Total least squares regression is performed by singular value decomposition."
comment: "When the errors \(\varepsilon\) and \(\eta\) have the same variance the method is called orthogonal regression and minimises the perpendicular distance of a point to the regression line."
synonym: "total least squares regression" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10115

[Term]
id: goldbook:10151
name: mean squared error of calibration
def: "In calibration for \\\(N\\\) calibration data where \\\(c_\{i\}\\\) is an observed value and \\\(\\hat c_\{i\}\\\) is the value predicted by the calibration function. \\\[E_\{\\rm\{MSEC\}\} = \\frac\{\\sum\\limits_\{i\\\,=\\\,1\}^\{i\\\,=\\\,N\} \(\\hat c_\{i\} - c_\{i\}\)^2\}\{N\}\\\]"
comment: "Mean squared error of calibration is the square of the root mean squared error of calibration."
synonym: "mean residual sum of squares" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10157

[Term]
id: goldbook:10152
name: multilinear least squares regression
def: "Multivariate calibration in which the coefficients of the regression are calculated directly from the indications and values of standards."
comment: "If \(\boldsymbol{X}^{\rm{T}} \boldsymbol{X}\) has full rank only because of noise, the solution can become unstable."
comment: "In \(\boldsymbol{X} \boldsymbol{b} = \boldsymbol{c} + \boldsymbol{e}\) (where \(\boldsymbol{X}\) is a vector of indications, \(\boldsymbol{b}\) are coefficients of the model, \(\boldsymbol{c}\) is a vector of values of the quantity of interest and \(\boldsymbol{e}\) a vector of errors), \(\boldsymbol{b} = \boldsymbol{X^{+}} \boldsymbol{c}\), where \(\boldsymbol{X^{+}}\) is the pseudo-inverse of \(\boldsymbol{X}\), calculated as \(\boldsymbol{X^{+}} = (\boldsymbol{X}^{\rm{T}} \boldsymbol{X})^{-1} \boldsymbol{X}^{\rm{T}}\)"
comment: "It is assumed that \(\boldsymbol{X}^{\rm{T}} \boldsymbol{X}\) has full rank, i.e. there are more objects than variables, and the variables are independent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10041
consider: goldbook:10153

[Term]
id: goldbook:10153
name: multivariate calibration
def: "Calibration in which the indications are multivariate data."
comment: "In multivariate regression and calibration the problem is usually posed as a relation between the indications \(\boldsymbol{X}\) (which are multivariate) and the property to be measured \(\boldsymbol{y}\). Note that this is a reversal of the traditional form, \(x\) (concentration)/\(y\ (\rm{g})\) (indication) of linear calibration. \(\boldsymbol{X}\) is a vector of observations (indications), and \(\boldsymbol{c}\) a vector of concentrations. In matrix form: \(\boldsymbol{X} \boldsymbol{b} = \boldsymbol{c} + \boldsymbol{e}\) where \(\boldsymbol{b}\) are the coefficients of the model and \(\boldsymbol{e}\) is a vector of errors."
comment: "Regression establishes the coefficients \(\boldsymbol{b}\) (\(\boldsymbol{X} \boldsymbol{b} = \boldsymbol{c} + \boldsymbol{e}\)) from given indications \(\boldsymbol{X}\), or some factorization of \(\boldsymbol{X}\), and values \(\boldsymbol{c}\), or some factorization of \(\boldsymbol{c}\). Given indications \(\boldsymbol{X}_{\rm{u}}\) from an unknown sample, the quantity value \(c_{\rm{u}}\) can be calculated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10055

[Term]
id: goldbook:10154
name: ordinary least squares regression
def: "Least squares regression that minimizes the sum of squared differences between the known values of dependent variable and values predicted by a linear model."
comment: "Assumptions of the model are that error is only in the dependent variable, Normally-distributed, and homoscedastic."
comment: "OLSR is used for calibration and multivariate calibration."
synonym: "OLSR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "classical least squares regression" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10149
consider: goldbook:10153

[Term]
id: goldbook:10155
name: partial least squares regression
def: "Multivariate calibration which finds factors that maximise covariance between two blocks of data."
comment: "PLS finds factors (latent variables) in observed variables \(\boldsymbol{X}\) that explain the maximum variance in the variable(s) \(\boldsymbol{c}\), using the simultaneous decomposition of the two. It removes redundant information from the regression, i.e. factors describing large amounts of variance in the observed data that does not correlate with the predictions."
comment: "PLS may also be used in classification. See partial least squares discriminant analysis."
comment: "PLS1 refers to PLS for a single "c" variable. PLS2 is PLS that simultaneously obtains values for two or more "c" variables. Therefore in the equations of Note 2, PLS1 has vectors \(\boldsymbol{c}\) and \(\boldsymbol{q}\) and PLS2 has matrices \(\boldsymbol{C}\) and \(\boldsymbol{Q}\)."
comment: "The decompositions are \(\boldsymbol{X} = \boldsymbol{T}_{k}\boldsymbol{P}_{k}^{\rm{T}} + \boldsymbol{E}\) and \(\boldsymbol{C} = \boldsymbol{U}_{k}\boldsymbol{Q}_{k}^{\rm{T}} + \boldsymbol{F}\), and \(\boldsymbol{X^{+}} = \boldsymbol{W}_{k} (\boldsymbol{P}_{k}\boldsymbol{W}_{k})^{-1} (\boldsymbol{T}_{k}^{\rm{T}}\boldsymbol{T}_{k})^{-1} \boldsymbol{T}_{k}^{\rm{T}}\), where \(\boldsymbol{W}\) are weights that maintain orthogonal scores."
comment: "When used for multivariate calibration, evaluation data or cross validation may be used to choose the number of PLS factors and assess the accuracy of the prediction (although the same data must not be used to do both). This is important to guard against overfitting."
synonym: "PLS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "partial least squares" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10050
consider: goldbook:10112
consider: goldbook:10138
consider: goldbook:10153

[Term]
id: goldbook:10156
name: principal components regression
def: "Multivariate calibration in which a dependent variable is regressed against the scores of a chosen number of factors obtained from principal-component analysis of the predictor variable."
comment: "PCA decomposes the predictor variable data \(\boldsymbol{X}\) into \(k\) principal component factors \(\boldsymbol{\hat X}_{k} = \boldsymbol{T}_{k}\boldsymbol{P}_{k}^{\rm{T}}\), where \(k\) may be determined by cross validation. The dependent variable \(\boldsymbol{c}\) is then regressed against \(\boldsymbol{\hat X}_{k}\), \(\boldsymbol{c} = \boldsymbol{\hat X}_{k} \boldsymbol{\hat b}\)."
comment: "The factorization gives orthogonal factors, but no information about the predicted variable \(\boldsymbol{c}\) is used."
synonym: "PCR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10106
consider: goldbook:10107
consider: goldbook:10112
consider: goldbook:10152
consider: goldbook:10153
consider: goldbook:10155

[Term]
id: goldbook:10157
name: root mean squared error of calibration
def: "In calibration for \\\(N\\\) calibration data where \\\(c_\{i\}\\\) is an observed value and \\\(\\hat c_\{i\}\\\) is the value predicted by the calibration function. \\\[E_\{\\rm\{RMSEC\}\} = \\sqrt \\frac\{\\sum\\limits_\{i\\\,=\\\,1\}^\{i\,=\\\,N\} \(\\hat c_\{i\} - c_\{i\}\)^2\}\{N\}\\\]"
comment: "Overfitting results in a small RMSEC, but poor predictive ability."
synonym: "RMSEC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "standard error of calibration (SEC)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10158
name: underfitting of a calibration model
def: "Condition in which a model fails to describe the data adequately."
comment: "Underfitting generally occurs when a model is not sufficiently complex, such as having too few parameters."
synonym: "underfitting" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10159
name: weighted least squares regression
def: "Least squares regression in which a nonnegative constant is associated with each value of the dependent variable."
comment: "If the only source of dispersion in the dependent variable is normally distributed, the weights are the inverse of the variance of each value."
comment: "It is assumed the weights are known exactly."
comment: "The nonnegative constants are called weights."
synonym: "WLSR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0605
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10160
name: boundary layer thickness
def: "Distance from the interface beyond which mass transfer is determined by convection."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10161
name: breakthrough volume
def: "Sample volume at which a defined amount of an analyte pumped continuously through an extraction device will begin to be eluted. Typical breakthrough curve indicating the breakthrough volume \\\(V_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) and the sample volume corresponding to the saturation capacity of the sorbent \\\(V_\{\\rm\{C\}\}\\\) \(\\\(V_\{\\rm\{R\}\}\\\) corresponds to the chromatographic elution volume and \\\(\\upsigma_\{\\rm\{v\}\}\\\) the standard deviation of the derivative of the curve\).Typical breakthrough curve indicating the breakthrough volume \\\(V_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) and the sample volume corresponding to the saturation capacity of the sorbent \\\(V_\{\\rm\{C\}\}\\\) \(\\\(V_\{\\rm\{R\}\}\\\) corresponds to the chromatographic elution volume and \\\(\\upsigma_\{\\rm\{v\}\}\\\) the standard deviation of the derivative of the curve\)."
comment: "Defined amounts are usually given as a volume fraction of the sample volume (e.g. \(\pu{1\%}\), \(\pu{5\%}\) or \(\pu{10\%}\), etc.)."
comment: "The breakthrough volume, \(V_{\rm{B}}\), for a particular compound and sampling device is determined by its breakthrough curve (see figure)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10162
name: ion-pair extraction
def: "Transfer of ions from an aqueous phase to an immiscible liquid \(or solid\) phase by adding an ion of complementary charge to the aqueous phase."
comment: "Ion-pair extraction can also be done by adding the complementary-charge containing compound to the organic phase before extraction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10163
name: sorbent
def: "Condensed phase where extraction of analytes can occur at the surface and in the bulk."
comment: "If extraction occurs exclusively at the surface then adsorbent is the preferred term and if exclusively in the bulk then absorbent should be used."
comment: "Sorbent is typically used explicitly to describe a condensed phase where extraction occurs simultaneously by adsorption and absorption (termed sorption), or where the true mechanism has not been established and the use of adsorbent or absorbent would be inappropriate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10164
name: acceptor phase
def: "Component of a multi-phase system into which the target analytes are extracted."
comment: "In extractions employing a semipermeable membrane for phase separation the acceptor phase is the phase to which analytes are transferred from the donor phase."
comment: "When the acceptor phase is a liquid the term acceptor solution may be used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10171
consider: goldbook:10290

[Term]
id: goldbook:10165
name: active sampling
def: "Continuous extraction with movement of the sample matrix with respect to the extraction phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175

[Term]
id: goldbook:10166
name: batch extraction
def: "Extraction in which the extraction phase and the sample are confined in an extraction vessel and processed according to a defined procedure."
comment: "Term "batch" is also used in extraction to indicate a number of samples extracted sequentially or simultaneously by the same procedure (e.g. extraction of sample batch(es))."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10167
name: calibrant in extraction phase
def: "Internal standard that is incorporated in the extraction phase for calibration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175

[Term]
id: goldbook:10168
name: charcoal tube
def: "Tube filled with charcoal typically used to adsorb analytes from the gas or liquid phase."
comment: "Activated charcoal was used in early applications, but a wider selection of carbon materials are currently used, with properties tailored to each application."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10169
name: continuous extraction
def: "Extraction in which the sample is continuously introduced into the extraction device."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10170
name: countercurrent extraction
def: "Extraction in which both phases are continuously added \(or changed\) and flow \(or move\) in opposite directions as the extraction progresses."
comment: "The phases are either immiscible or separated by a membrane."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10171
name: donor phase
def: "In extraction\, the sample or sample solution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10172
name: dynamic extraction
def: "Extraction in which clean \(or recycled\) extraction phase is continuously passed through the sample."
comment: "The extraction phase can be a gas or a liquid."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175

[Term]
id: goldbook:10173
name: exhaustive extraction
def: "Type of extraction where the intent is a complete extraction of the analytes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10174
name: external calibration
def: "Calibration employing a simplified sample matrix spiked with target analyte embodying a reference value of the measurand."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10175
name: extraction phase
def: "Liquid\, solid\, or gas phase in contact with the sample for the purpose of removal of analytes from the sample matrix."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10176
name: extraction rate
def: "Rate at which analytes are transferred from the sample to the extraction phase."
synonym: "kinetics of extraction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175

[Term]
id: goldbook:10177
name: feed
def: "Solution or gas containing analyte introduced into an extraction."
comment: "If feed is used without qualification, the term may be taken to designate the initial liquid phase containing the main solute to be transferred or sample solution in a batch process."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10178
name: fluorous extraction
def: "Extraction in a biphasic system in which the main component of one phase is a highly fluorinated solvent \(liquid-liquid extraction\) or highly fluorinated sorbent \(solid-phase extraction\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10255

[Term]
id: goldbook:10179
name: leaching
def: "Dissolution of sample components from a solid with a liquid in which the solid phase is not wholly soluble."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10180
name: matrix-matched calibration
def: "Calibration employing external calibration in which standard solutions of target are prepared in a solution of analyte-free matrix."
comment: "Matrix-matched calibration is used to minimize the matrix effect on the measurement of target measurands."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10181
name: multiwell sample plate
def: "Plate with multiple wells for individual samples."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10182
name: optimisation of extraction
def: "Adjustment of extraction parameters to achieve a defined goal."
comment: "Many extractions are controlled by several parameters and their interactions. Optimum conditions are more efficiently identified by multivariate methods."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10183
name: passive sampling
def: "Extraction process driven by diffusion of analytes towards the extraction phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175

[Term]
id: goldbook:10184
name: salting in
def: "Addition of an electrolyte to an aqueous phase to decrease the distribution ratio of the analyte\(s\) or matrix."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10186
name: sequential extraction
def: "Extraction wherein extractants of increasing strength or different chemical character are used in order to extract analytes of interest."
comment: "The most commonly used approaches in elemental analysis are the BCR (now termed Standards, Measurement and Testing Program) and Tessier procedures."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10187
name: static extraction
def: "Batch extraction in which the extraction phase attains a constant composition before phase separation."
comment: "If the analytes are initially present as a solution in an immiscible liquid phase the process is synonymous with liquid-liquid extraction."
comment: "If the sample is a solid that is partially soluble in the extraction phase then leaching may be a more appropriate term."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10166
consider: goldbook:10175
consider: goldbook:10179

[Term]
id: goldbook:10188
name: steady state extraction
def: "State of a continuous process operating in such a way that the concentration of solutes in exit streams remains constant with respect to time for constant feed concentrations\, even though the two phases are not necessarily in thermodynamic equilibrium in any part of the process."
comment: "The term equilibrium should not be used to describe this situation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10177

[Term]
id: goldbook:10189
name: time-weighted average sampling
def: "A passive sampling or active sampling strategy over a relatively long time\, during which the amount of analyte\(s\) extracted is proportional to its average \(mean\) concentration over that time."
synonym: "TWA sampling" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10165
consider: goldbook:10183

[Term]
id: goldbook:10190
name: chemical hydride generation
def: "Type of chemical vapour generation wherein volatile hydrides are generated by reaction with \(usually\) borane complexes in aqueous solution."
synonym: "CHG" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10191
name: closed-loop extraction
def: "Extraction by a fixed volume of gas continuously recycled through the sample and a sorbent trap by a pump in a closed-circuit arrangement.Typical apparatus for closed-loop stripping analysis."
comment: "Closed-loop extraction was developed for trace analysis of volatile compounds (at mass concentrations of \(\pu{ng L-1}\)) in drinking water."
synonym: "closed-loop stripping analysis" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10201

[Term]
id: goldbook:10192
name: cryogenic trap
def: "Device used to concentrate volatile analytes from the gas phase by condensation on a cold surface."
comment: "Typically, cryogenic traps have a low thermal mass to respond rapidly to changes in temperature and are prepared from short lengths of capillary tubing. Sub-ambient temperatures are required for the efficient collection of analytes from a flowing gas stream and above ambient temperatures for evaporation into a flowing gas stream for analysis, usually by gas chromatography or atomic spectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10193
name: denuder
def: "Apparatus for the extraction of volatile analytes from a flowing gas stream by diffusion to the wall of a collection vessel\, where they are retained by chemisorption or strong physisorption by the wall coating."
comment: "Both liquid and solid sorbents are used for trapping."
comment: "There are many design variations."
synonym: "denuder device" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10194
name: dynamic headspace analysis
def: "Continuous removal of headspace above a sample by a flow of inert gas over or through the sample until all or a significant portion of the analytes have been removed from the sample. Sample vapours are typically transferred to a sorbent trap or cryogenic trap for collection.Typical apparatus for analysis by dynamic headspace \(purge and trap\). The gas flow \(sparging gas\) enters at the bottom of the sample container transporting volatile compounds through the headspace and purge head to the desorption tube for collection."
comment: "A typical apparatus for purge-and-trap is shown in the figure below."
comment: "Purge-and-trap is a version of dynamic headspace analysis in which volatile compounds are purged from solution by a continuous stream of gas bubbles (sparging gas) and transported through the headspace to a sorbent or cryogenic trap for collection."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10192
consider: goldbook:10198
consider: goldbook:10201

[Term]
id: goldbook:10195
name: extractive distillation
def: "Separation of close-boiling liquids by fractional distillation in the presence of a low-volatility solvent or salt that selectively interacts with one or more components of the mixture\, increasing the difference in vapour pressure of the sample components."
comment: "If the separation solvent forms an azeotrope with one or more sample components the process is called azeotropic distillation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10196
name: flash desorption
def: "Thermal desorption where the temperature of a packed tube or cryogenic trap is rapidly increased to transfer condensed or sorbed compounds to the gas phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10197
name: full-evaporation headspace analysis
def: "Small volume of sample in a headspace vessel maintained at a temperature sufficient to cause complete evaporation of analytes."
comment: "Equilibrium between the condensed and vapor phases no longer exists. As a consequence, the possibility of matrix interferences is reduced and the fraction extracted for low-volatility compounds is increased."
comment: "The full-evaporation technique is used with both static headspace analysis and dynamic headspace analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10198
name: headspace
def: "Volume of gas phase above a sample in a closed container."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10199
name: multiple headspace extraction
def: "Dynamic gas extraction carried out stepwise\, with sequential analysis of a number of headspace samples taken from the same vial."
comment: "At equilibrium the headspace is sampled and the remainder (or most of it) is exhausted and replaced by fresh gas phase. The process is repeated and the original sample concentration estimated from the peak areas for two consecutive extractions. \[A_{\rm{T}} = \frac{A_{1}^{2}}{A_{1} - A_{2}}\] where \(A_{\rm{T}}\) = estimated sum of all partial peak areas corresponding to exhaustive extraction, \(A_{1}\) the peak area obtained from the first headspace fraction, and \(A_{2}\) the peak area obtained in the second (consecutive) headspace fraction."
comment: "External calibration is required to convert peak areas into sample concentration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10174
consider: goldbook:10198

[Term]
id: goldbook:10200
name: simultaneous steam distillation-solvent extraction
def: "Extraction in which a sample dispersed in water and a water immiscible organic solvent \(extraction phase\) in separate flasks are heated simultaneously and their vapours co-condensed and separated into two streams in which water is returned to the sample flask and the extraction phase to the organic solvent flask.Apparatus for simultaneous steam distillation-solvent extraction with a lighter-than-water extraction phase. A = aqueous sample solution or slurry; B = immiscible organic solvent and receiving flask for extracted compounds; C = bowl for phase separation; D\, E\, F\, and G are solvent or vapour transfer arms; and H = entry port for additional solvent or alternative sample introduction position for continuous liquid–liquid extraction. Switching the position of flasks A and B allows extraction with a heavier-than-water extraction solvent."
comment: "A typical apparatus for simultaneous steam distillation-solvent extraction with a lighter-than-water extraction solvent is shown in the figure below."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175

[Term]
id: goldbook:10201
name: sorbent trap
def: "Tube filled with porous sorbent typically used to extract analytes from the gas phase."
comment: "The performance of a sorbent tube depends on the sorbent type, temperature, gas flow rate, and desorption time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10202
name: static headspace analysis
def: "Method of analysis\, in which a small aliquot of the gas phase in contact with the sample in a closed container is withdrawn for analysis."
comment: "At equilibrium, the analyte concentration in the gas phase is related to the sample concentration by a partition constant."
comment: "The sample vessel is thermostatted."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10203
name: thermal extraction
def: "Release of volatile compounds from a sample by heat."
comment: "The volatile compounds are typically transported by a gas stream to a sorbent tube or cryogenic trap for collection."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10192
consider: goldbook:10201

[Term]
id: goldbook:10204
name: thin-layer headspace analysis
def: "Dynamic headspace analysis of a flowing sample solution in the form of a thin film on the surface of a heated tube."
comment: "Volatile compounds in the sample solution pass into the gas phase and are continuously swept out of the tube for analysis or detection."
synonym: "TLHS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10194

[Term]
id: goldbook:10205
name: biphasic system
def: "Equilibrium system containing two or more solvents forming two phases with a single interface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10206
name: chelation solvent extraction
def: "Extraction method wherein charged analytes are extracted from an aqueous phase into an organic phase\, assisted by a chelating agent."
comment: "The analyte(s) are usually metal ions."
comment: "The chelating agent replaces water molecules in the coordination sphere of the metal ions. Consequently, the resultant metal chelates have a hydrophobic character which facilitates their transfer to the organic phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10207
name: cloud point extraction
def: "Coacervative extraction at a temperature above the cloud point temperature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10208

[Term]
id: goldbook:10208
name: coacervative extraction
def: "Extraction by a surfactant-rich\, water-immiscible phase formed by adding a dehydrating agent to a colloidal solution of the sample and a surfactant above its critical micelle concentration."
comment: "In cloud point extraction a small volume "surfactant-rich" phase enriched in sample components of moderate water solubility and a bulk aqueous phase with dissolved surfactant and highly water-soluble compounds are formed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10209
name: continuous liquid-liquid extraction
def: "Extraction in which a water-immiscible extraction solvent is continuously percolated through an aqueous solution and returned to the extraction solvent reservoir.Apparatus for continuous liquid–liquid extraction with a lighter-than-water extraction solvent \(left\) and a heavier-than-water extraction solvent \(right\). In each case the extraction solvent is contained in the round bottom flask and the aqueous sample in the vertical glass column."
comment: "Continuous liquid-liquid extraction techniques are used when the sample volume is large, the distribution constant is small, or the rate of extraction is slow."
comment: "Typical apparatuses are shown below."
comment: "Typically, a fixed volume of extraction solvent is recycled through the aqueous sample solution by distillation and condensation, and dripped into the sample solution. A siphon mechanism allows continuous recovery of the extraction solvent based on its relative density."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10210
name: Craig countercurrent distribution apparatus
def: "Apparatus for extraction based on a multistage countercurrent distribution."
comment: "The Craig CCD apparatus consists of a battery of glass vessels designed to allow the mixing, settling, and transfer of extracted phase (sample) and the addition of fresh solvent (extractant) in a repetitive fashion. Movement about the horizontal axis provides gentle mixing of the phases, settling, and decanting of the upper phase. The extraction process is slow but is fully automated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10217

[Term]
id: goldbook:10211
name: crosscurrent extraction
def: "Extraction comprising a cascading series of states where the raffinate is brought into a subsequent stage and contacted with fresh solvent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10212
name: differential contactor
def: "Type of continuous multistage extraction equipment in which there is only one interface at which phase separation by settling occurs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10213
name: dispersing solvent
def: "Solvent used to disperse the extraction solvent as fine droplets throughout the sample solution in dispersive liquid–liquid microextraction."
comment: "The dispersion solvent is typically a polar organic solvent miscible with water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10214

[Term]
id: goldbook:10214
name: dispersive liquid-liquid microextraction
def: "Extraction of analyte\(s\) from an aqueous solution by fine droplets of extraction phase dispersed throughout the solution."
comment: "The extraction phase can be formed by ion exchange when an ionic liquid is used as the extraction solvent."
comment: "The extraction phase is formed by a mixture of extraction and dispersion solvents injected into the sample solution."
comment: "The extraction phase is sedimented by centrifugation and collected for analysis."
synonym: "DLLME" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175

[Term]
id: goldbook:10215
name: liquid-ion exchange
def: "Liquid-liquid distribution process that involves the transfer of ionic species from the extractant to the aqueous phase in exchange for ions from the aqueous phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10216
name: liquid-phase microextraction
def: "Microextraction technique using a liquid as the extraction phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175
consider: goldbook:11552

[Term]
id: goldbook:10217
name: multistage countercurrent distribution
def: "Multistage countercurrent separation based on a discontinuous\, differential migration process employing stepwise extraction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10170

[Term]
id: goldbook:10218
name: single-drop microextraction
def: "Extraction of analytes from the gas phase or solution by a single drop of extraction solvent.Typical experimental arrangement for single-drop microextraction."
comment: "The extraction solvent with a volume typically \(\pu{\lt 50 \upmu L}\) is suspended as a drop from the tip of a microsyringe needle as shown in the figure below."
comment: "The sample is stirred or agitated during extraction. After extraction, the drop of acceptor phase is collected by withdrawing it into the syringe used to support the drop for the final analytical measurement."
comment: "Typically, the sample is aqueous and the acceptor phase is an organic solvent, resulting in a two-phase extraction system (\(\ce{aqueous\!->\!organic}\)). SDME can also be operated in three-phase mode (\(\ce{aqueous\!->\!organic\!->\!aqueous}\)), or in the headspace mode (\(\ce{aqueous\!->\!gas\!->\!organic or aqueous}\))."
synonym: "SDME" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10219
name: solidified floating organic drop
def: "Droplet of organic solvent recovered from the surface of the sample solution by solidification induced by cooling."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10220
name: solidified floating organic drop microextraction
def: "Microextraction employing a solidified floating organic drop."
comment: "The extraction solvent has a melting point near room temperature to facilitate collection after solidification induced by cooling. The solidified solvent is then melted and analysed."
synonym: "SFODME" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10219
consider: goldbook:11552

[Term]
id: goldbook:10221
name: stage
def: "Physically distinct part of an extraction process in which transfer of analyte\(s\) occurs\, followed by phase separation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10222
name: stagewise contactor
def: "Type of continuous multi-stage liquid-liquid distribution equipment in which each stage has a physically distinct cycle of interphase contact and separation."
comment: "There are the same number of phase separation interfaces as there are stages."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10223
name: two-phase aqueous partition
def: "Distribution in a biphasic system formed by two aqueous solutions containing structurally incompatible components \(two polymers or a polymer and a salt\) above a critical concentration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10224
name: matrix-solid phase dispersion
def: "Extraction in which samples are blended with an abrasive solid sorbent\, forming a free flowing powder from which target analytes are recovered by solvent elution.Typical work flow scheme for solid-phase matrix dispersion. \(i\) Sample is blended with an abrasive sorbent\, \(ii\) free flowing powder containing sample is packed in a short column\, and \(iii\) target analytes are recovered by elution."
comment: "A typical workflow scheme for matrix–solid-phase dispersion is shown in the figure below."
comment: "For additional sample clean-up the sorbent/sample mixture is deposited at the head of a solid-phase extraction cartridge containing a suitable sorbent to retard the elution of matrix components."
synonym: "MSPD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10225
name: microwave-assisted extraction
def: "Leaching using microwave energy to heat the solvent in contact with the sample or the sample directly."
comment: "Microwaves are electromagnetic radiation of \(\pu{300\!{–}\! 300,000 MHz}\). They heat the extraction solution by their interaction with dielectric compounds (solvent or sample). Microwave heating is more efficient and rapid than convection and conduction and enhances the migration rate of compounds into the extraction solvent. Microwave-assisted extraction may be performed in a closed vessel with control of temperature and pressure or in an open vessel at atmospheric pressure."
synonym: "MAE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10179

[Term]
id: goldbook:10226
name: pressurized hot-water extraction
def: "Extraction by water below its critical point \(\\\(\\pu\{374.15^\{\\circ\}C\}\\\) and \\\(\\pu\{22.064 MPa\}\\\)\)."
comment: "Instrument requirements are similar to pressurized-liquid extraction."
comment: "The solvation properties of water become closer to organic solvents at elevated temperatures."
synonym: "subcritical water extraction" []
synonym: "superheated water extraction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10227

[Term]
id: goldbook:10227
name: pressurized-liquid extraction
def: "Leaching performed at elevated temperature and pressure.Schematic diagram of a typical apparatus for pressurized-liquid extraction. Gas flow is used to displace the extraction solvent from the sample chamber."
comment: "A typical apparatus is shown in the figure below."
comment: "The sample, in the form of a fine powder or liquid supported on an inert solid, is packed into an extraction vessel and inserted in a flow-through system. The temperature, pressure, solvent type, and static and/or dynamic extraction time are varied to optimize the extraction performance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10179

[Term]
id: goldbook:10228
name: Soxhlet extraction
def: "Leaching with fresh solvent cycled multiple times through a fine solid sample contained in a porous thimble.Typical apparatus for classical Soxhlet extraction."
comment: "A typical apparatus for classical Soxhlet extraction is shown in the figure below."
comment: "The extraction solvent is cycled in a continuous-discrete process by distillation, condensation and siphoning. Extracted material accumulates in the distillation flask."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10179

[Term]
id: goldbook:10229
name: supercritical fluid extraction
def: "Use of a supercritical fluid to extract analytes from a solid or supported liquid sample."
comment: "The most common supercritical fluid for extraction is carbon dioxide (critical point = \(\pu{39.9^{\circ}C}\) and \(\pu{73.8 bar}\)). Its extraction properties are varied by changing its density (temperature and pressure) or by addition of polar organic solvents."
comment: "The powdered sample, or supported liquid, is packed into a vessel and extracted using static or dynamic extraction conditions. The extracted material is typically recovered by reducing the pressure of the extraction fluid, allowing it to evaporate."
synonym: "SFE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10230
name: QuEChERS \(quick\, easy\, cheap\, effective\, rugged and safe\) extraction
def: "Streamlined multiresidue method for extraction and clean-up of analytes in complex matrices."
comment: "Often used for samples containing pesticide residues."
comment: "The general procedure includes micro-scale extraction with acetonitrile, salt-assisted phase separation, and sample clean up using dispersive solid-phase extraction."
comment: "There are several procedural variations of the general method for application to particular compounds or sample matrices."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11552

[Term]
id: goldbook:10231
name: ultrasound-assisted extraction
def: "Extraction in which ultrasound energy is used to increase the extraction rate by enhancing the contact area between the sample and solvent and by promoting efficient agitation."
comment: "Ultrasound energy causes cavitation in solvents, which generates numerous tiny bubbles in liquids and mechanical erosion of solids, including particle rupture. It promotes digestion and slurry formation with solids and homogenization and emulsification with liquids."
comment: "Ultrasound energy is applied to samples in a vessel immersed in a water bath or applied more directly using devices, such as horns, probes, or sono-reactors."
synonym: "UAE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10176

[Term]
id: goldbook:10232
name: acid digestion
def: "Process in which the sample \(analyte and matrix\) is dissolved by an acid."
comment: "Acid digestion can also be used to remove a matrix constituent by selective volatilization, e.g. silicon by the use of hydrofluoric acid."
comment: "Acid digestion can be performed in closed or open vessels."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10233
name: closed-vessel acid digestion
def: "Type of acid digestion performed in a closed vessel at elevated pressure."
comment: "The increased rate of decomposition and retention of volatile trace elements is an advantage over open-vessel acid digestion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10232
consider: goldbook:10236

[Term]
id: goldbook:10234
name: digestion
def: "Sample dissolution with simultaneous matrix simplification."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10235
name: microwave acid digestion
def: "Type of bomb acid digestion with microwave radiation used for sample heating."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10236
name: open-vessel acid digestion
def: "Type of acid digestion performed at ambient pressure wherein the digestion temperature is limited by the boiling point of the acid."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10232
consider: goldbook:10233

[Term]
id: goldbook:10237
name: UV photochemical digestion
def: "Formation of free metal ions in aqueous solution by oxidation under the influence of UV light and possibly an oxidizing agent \(e.g. hydrogen peroxide or peroxodisulfate\) in order to break down dissolved organic matter and metal complexes."
comment: "Typical samples are sea water, waste water, drinking water, or fresh water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10238
name: cartridge
def: "Short disposable column containing a bed of porous particles immobilized between two porous frits."
comment: "The particles are sized to allow sample processing by gravity, gentle suction or low pressure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10239
name: conditioning solvent
def: "Small volume of solvent used to prepare the sorbent for efficient sample processing."
comment: "Principal roles include removal of contaminants from the sorbent bed to create the conditions for a stable flow of the sample solution during sampling and to facilitate wetting of hydrophobic sorbent surfaces before applying aqueous samples."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10240
name: elution solvent
def: "Small volume of strong solvent used to displace target analytes from the sorbent bed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10241
name: foamed polyurethane sorbent
def: "Sorbent consisting of spherical\, micron-sized\, agglomerated particles bound together in a rigid and highly porous structure used for the extraction of semi-volatile organic compounds from air in high-volume samplers."
comment: "Foamed polyurethane sorbents have a minor use for extracting compounds from water."
comment: "Their main attribute is their favourable aerodynamic properties, which permit sampling at high flow rates."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10242
name: immunosorbents
def: "Porous material with surface bound monoclonal or polyclonal antibodies capable of selective extraction of target analytes by formation of reversible antibody-antigen \(compound\) binding complexes."
comment: "A high level of selectivity is possible due to the specificity of antibody-antigen spatial fitting and interactions."
comment: "The porous support is chosen to minimize nonspecific matrix interactions to facilitate processing complex biological, environmental and food samples without additional clean up."
synonym: "immunoaffinity sorbents" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10243
name: inorganic oxide adsorbent
def: "Adsorbent with site-specific polar and ion exchange functional groups that extract analytes from a gas or liquid phase by their complementary interactions with the surface."
comment: "Compounds with hydrogen-bonding or ionic functional groups are extracted efficiently, while neutral dipolar compounds are extracted to a lesser extent and weakly polarizable compounds to a limited extent."
comment: "Typical inorganic oxide adsorbents include silica gel, alumina, magnesium silicate (Florisil), and zirconia."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10244
name: ion-exchange sorbent
def: "Porous sorbent material  containing fixed ionic sites with a complementary charge to that of the target analyte\(s\)."
comment: "Ion-exchange sorbents are usually classified as weak or strong depending on the identity of the ionic group and whether its charge is independent of the sample \(\rm{pH}\) (strong ion-exchanger) or can be varied by changing the sample \(\rm{pH}\) (weak ion-exchanger)."
comment: "Ionic or ionizable compounds are extracted almost exclusively from water by electrostatic interactions with ion-exchange sorbents."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10245
name: low-specificity sorbents
def: "Sorbent with a non-selective surface used almost exclusively to extract analytes from an aqueous solution. The sorbent has a largely passive role in the extraction\, with the driving force being the expulsion of the organic contaminants from waterto minimize disruption of the water structure."
comment: "From the gas phase compounds are extracted by non-polar and weakly polar interactions with high surface area sorbents."
comment: "Low-specificity sorbents have surfaces with a low concentration of polar functional groups and retain compounds mainly through non-selective dispersion interactions."
comment: "Typical low-specificity sorbents are chemically-bonded porous silica, hydrophobic macroporous polymers, and various forms of carbon."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10246
name: magnetic nanoparticle sorbent
def: "Sorbent consisting of nanometre-sized\, spherical particles with a magnetic or magnetisable core surrounded by a sorbent shell."
comment: "Magnetic nanoparticles have a high surface area-to-volume ratio and a low mass. They are easily dispersed in solution. A magnet facilitates recovery of the nanoparticles from the sample solution or suspension."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10247
name: mixed-mode sorbent
def: "Porous sorbent material with surface co-bonded ion exchange and alkyl functional groups."
comment: "The dual extraction mechanism allows fractionation of mixtures into a neutral and acidic fraction and a basic fraction by a stepwise change in \(\pu{pH}\) of the eluting solvent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10248
name: molecularly imprinted polymer sorbent
def: "Porous polymer sorbent with synthetic recognition sites with a high specificity for the sorption of a targeted compound or group of structurally-related compounds."
comment: "The imprint is obtained by the co-polymerization of functional and crosslinking monomers in the presence of a template molecule (the analyte) and a porogen. The resultant imprint possesses a steric (size and shape) and chemical (spatial arrangement of complementary functional groups) memory of the template molecule that enable the sorbent to selectively rebind the template molecule from a complex matrix."
synonym: "MIPS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10249
name: multiwell extraction plate
def: "Regular array of wells in a single moulded body with a short sorbent bed or disc embedded at the base of each well.Multiwell extraction plate."
comment: "Multiwell plates typically contain 24, 96, 256, or 384 wells with volumes varying from about \(\pu{100 \upmu L}\) to \(\pu{10 mL}\). They are used for parallel sample processing in high throughput applications."
comment: "The design of a typical multiwall extraction plate is shown in the figure below."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10250
name: needle trap
def: "Gas-tight syringe with a sorbent-filled needle."
comment: "Vertical movement of the plunger allows bidirectional flow of sample through the sorbent bed (active sampling). Alternatively, sampling can occur by diffusion of analytes into the syringe needle (passive sampling)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10165
consider: goldbook:10183

[Term]
id: goldbook:10251
name: particle-embedded glass fibre disc
def: "Suspension of micron-sized sorbent particles woven into a glass fibre matrix."
comment: "Small discs are self-supporting while larger discs require external support."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10252
name: particle-loaded membrane disc
def: "Suspension of micron-sized sorbent particles distributed throughout a web of poly\(tetrafluroethylene\) microfibrils formed into a thin disc of various diameters."
comment: "For general use the flexible discs are supported on a sintered glass disc in a filtration apparatus using suction to generate the desired flow through the membrane."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10253
name: restricted-access sorbent
def: "Porous material with a biocompatible outer surface and a retentive interior surface."
comment: "Access to the retentive interior surface is restricted for macromolecules by a physical or chemical diffusion barrier that facilitates elution of macromolecules and extraction of low-mass compounds."
comment: "The restricted access barrier can be accomplished by size exclusion, differential partitioning, or other phenomenon."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10254
name: rinse solvent
def: "Weak solvent used to displace matrix components from a sorbent without displacing the target analyte\(s\)."
comment: "An optional step, intermediate between sample application and elution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10255
name: solid-phase extraction
def: "Extraction of analytes from a gas\, liquid\, or fluid by transfer to a solid sorbent."
comment: "Typical uses of solid-phase extraction include isolation, concentration, solvent exchange, and matrix simplification."
synonym: "SPE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10256
name: solvent desorption
def: "Use of a solvent\, typically combined with agitation\, to remove target analytes from a sorbent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10257
name: sorbent-containing pipette tip
def: "Disposable pipette tip with a small packed bed\, disc\, or monolithic plug of sorbent at its narrow end.Sorbent containing pipette tips in an array for use with a multiwall sample plate."
comment: "A micropipettor is used to control sample processing steps. This arrangement facilitates the use of bidirectional flow (the cycling of sample and solvents across the sorbent bed in either direction) for sample processing."
comment: "A typical design of sorbent-containing pipette device for high throughput sample processing is shown in the figure below."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10258
name: sorptive-tape extraction
def: "Extraction from the surface of a solid by sorbent or polymer film in the form of a tape in direct contact with\, or in the headspace above\, the sample."
comment: "The tape is typically a suitably-sized sheet of poly(dimethylsiloxane) polymer, or a piece of particle-loaded membrane, with a large surface area-to-volume ratio."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10198

[Term]
id: goldbook:10259
name: stir bar sorptive extraction
def: "Extraction of compounds from solution by a sorbent coated magnetic stir bar by rapid stirring \(direct immersion\) or by exposure to the headspace above a sample \(headspace extraction\)."
comment: "Rapid stirring accelerates mass transfer overcoming some of the limitations of diffusion controlled mass transfer in sessile solutions."
comment: "Related devices for simultaneous stirring and sampling include rotating disc, stir rod, and stir membrane devices."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10198
consider: goldbook:10267

[Term]
id: goldbook:10260
name: surface-bound macrocyclic sorbent
def: "Porous sorbent with surface-bound macrocyclic ligands designed for the extraction of metal ions and some anions from aqueous solution."
comment: "Extracted ions are recovered by elution with a solution of complexing agent with a higher binding constant than the surface-bound macrocyclic ligand."
comment: "The selectivity of the extraction process depends on the stability of the host-guest complex, which can be optimized for individual ions by the choice of the macrocyclic cavity and the type of donor atoms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10261
name: surface-bound phenylboronic acid sorbent
def: "Porous sorbent with surface-bound phenylboronic acid groups for the selective extraction of bifunctional compounds by reversible formation of 5- or 6-membered covalent cyclic boronic acid complexes."
comment: "Extraction occurs at a basic \(\pu{pH}\) for compounds with hydrogen-donating functional groups on neighbouring carbon atoms (1,2- and 1,3-). The analytes are released by elution with an acidic aqueous-organic solvent solution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10262
name: biocompatible solid-phase microextraction
def: "Extraction by a matrix-compatible immersion solid-phase microextraction device where the extraction phase and support are chosen to eliminate matrix interferences."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10276

[Term]
id: goldbook:10263
name: blade format
def: "Solid-phase microextraction device where the extraction phase \(sorbent\) is dispersed in the form of a thin coating on the surface of a blade."
comment: "This technique is typically used as a 96-blade brush in conjunction with a multiwell sample plate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10181
consider: goldbook:10276

[Term]
id: goldbook:10264
name: coated-vessel format
def: "Sample vessel with sorbent-coated walls."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163

[Term]
id: goldbook:10265
name: cold fibre solid-phase microextraction
def: "Solid-phase microextraction in the fibre format with a sorbent temperature maintained below that of the sample matrix during extraction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
