[Term]
id: goldbook:10270
name: in-tube solid-phase microextraction
def: "Extraction utilizing a coated open tubular or packed capillary tube as the extraction phase in a flow system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10271
name: matrix-compatible solid-phase microextraction
def: "Immersion solid-phase microextraction where the extraction phase is designed to minimize sorption of particles or macromolecules present in the sample matrix."
comment: "Sorption of particles and macromolecules by the extraction phase is a potential source of interference in the extraction process or subsequent determination of analytes when sampling occurs by direct contact of the extraction phase with the sample. In some cases this can be addressed by incorporation of specific properties in the extraction phase that minimize matrix-extraction phase interactions for problem matrix components."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175
consider: goldbook:10268

[Term]
id: goldbook:10272
name: membrane-protected solid-phase microextraction
def: "Immersion solid-phase microextraction in which the extraction phase is surrounded by a permeable membrane that allows access of analytes to the extraction phase while shielding the extraction phase from matrix components with a potential to interfere in the extraction or subsequent analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175
consider: goldbook:10268

[Term]
id: goldbook:10273
name: particle sorbent
def: "Extraction phase in the form of sorbent particles."
comment: "Particles are typically of a nanometre size and applied in the dispersion mode of extraction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10175

[Term]
id: goldbook:10274
name: rotating disk sorptive extraction
def: "Sorbent-coated disc consisting of a polytetrafluoroethylene \(PTFE\) base with an integrated magnet and a sorbent film attached to one side."
comment: "Facilitates more rapid stirring than conventional sorbent-coated stir bars (see stir bar sorptive extraction) without deterioration of the sorbent coating, because it is not in contact with the vessel wall."
synonym: "RDSE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10259

[Term]
id: goldbook:10275
name: solid-phase dynamic extraction
def: "Solid-phase microextraction in which the extraction phase is coated on the internal surface of a needle."
synonym: "SPDE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10276

[Term]
id: goldbook:10276
name: solid-phase microextraction
def: "Microextraction where the extraction phase is a solid."
comment: "The extraction phase can also be a liquid physically coated on a fiber or wire support."
comment: "This term is often narrowly used to describe an extraction process employing a syringe-based sampling device with a short length of small gauge solid fiber or wire coated with sorbent attached to one end of the plunger of the syringe to facilitate bidirectional movement of the sorbent-coated fiber (wire) through the syringe needle for extraction, storage, and desorption of extractants. For extraction the sorbent is exposed to the headspace above the sample or immersed directly into the sample solution. Sample components diffuse into and/or onto the sorbent coating until equilibrium is reached. The extractants are subsequently recovered by thermal desorption into a gas stream (typically in the liner of an injection port of a gas chromatograph) or rinsed from the sorbent coating with solvent for determination by other methods."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10175
consider: goldbook:11552

[Term]
id: goldbook:10277
name: thin film format
def: "Solid-phase microextraction where the sorbent is in the form of a thin film on a support or self supported membrane."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10276

[Term]
id: goldbook:10278
name: electromembrane extraction
def: "Hollow-fibre liquid-phase microextraction in which the extraction is driven by an electrical potential sustained between the sample solution and the acceptor phase\, separated by a supported liquid membrane.Typical experimental arrangement for electromembrane extraction of cations \(anions extracted by reversing the polarity\). SLM\, supported liquid membrane in the form of a porous hollow fiber with solvent-filled pores."
comment: "A typical experimental arrangement is shown in the figure below."
comment: "Electromembrane extraction is typically performed in three-phase mode (\(\ce{aqueous\!->\!organic\!->\!aqueous}\))."
comment: "The sample is agitated or stirred during extraction."
synonym: "EME" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10164
consider: goldbook:10280
consider: goldbook:10293

[Term]
id: goldbook:10279
name: hollow fibre
def: "Narrow cylindrical tube prepared from a porous polymer."
comment: "The internal diameter of the tube is typically \(\pu{500 \upmu m}\) – \(\pu{1.5 mm}\) with walls \(\pu{100 \upmu m}\) to \(\pu{300 \upmu m}\) thick. Fibers are typically prepared from porous poly(propylene), although other materials can be used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10280
name: hollow-fibre liquid-phase microextraction
def: "Liquid-phase microextraction of analytes from a liquid \(or gaseous\) sample by a supported liquid membrane in the form of a porous hollow fibre with solvent-filled pores. The analytes are transferred to an acceptor phase contained in the cavity of the hollow fibre.Typical experimental arrangement for hollow-fiber supported liquid membrane \(SLM\) for liquid-phase microextraction."
comment: "A typical experimental arrangement is shown in the figure below."
comment: "The acceptor phase can be aqueous, which provides a three-phase extraction system (\(\ce{aqueous\!->\!organic\!->\!aqueous}\)), or an organic solvent, providing a two-phase extraction system (\(\ce{aqueous\!->\!organic}\))."
comment: "The sample is agitated or stirred during extraction."
comment: "The supported liquid membrane is generally an organic solvent immiscible with water and the sample an aqueous solution."
synonym: "HF-LPME" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10164
consider: goldbook:10216
consider: goldbook:10279
consider: goldbook:10293

[Term]
id: goldbook:10281
name: membrane extraction
def: "Extraction of analytes from a sample by permeation through a membrane."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:10282
name: membrane extraction with sorbent interface
def: "Membrane extraction with a sorbent trap for concentration of the permeate."
comment: "MESI is typically used in a system consisting of three components: (1) membrane extraction module; (2) sorbent interface; and (3) gas chromatograph. A flow of gas is used as the stripping phase to transfer permeate to the sorbent trap for concentration and thermal desorption into the gas chromatograph."
synonym: "MESI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10201
consider: goldbook:10281

[Term]
id: goldbook:10283
name: microdialysis
def: "Dialysis by a short length of hollow-fibre membrane used for sampling."
comment: "Microdialysis is performed mostly in a living biological system."
