[Term]
id: goldbook:10285
name: parallel artificial liquid membrane extraction
def: "Extraction of analytes from aqueous samples in a multiwell plate with a porous membrane at the base of each well by migration through the solvent-filled membrane pores into an acceptor phase located in each well."
comment: "PALME is usually performed in the three-phase mode (\(\ce{aqueous\!->\!organic\!->\!aqueous}\))."
comment: "The solvent-filled filter pores function as a supported liquid membrane typically based on an organic solvent immiscible with water."
synonym: "PALME" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
