[Term]
id: goldbook:10297
name: bead injection
def: "Fully renewable \(disposable\) packed sorbent bed for solid-phase extraction in a flow manifold or mesofluidic platform using programmable flow extraction.Bead-injection protocols for automated solid phase microextraction with sorbent renewal for each assay \[Reproduced from  https\://www.flowinjectiontutorial.com\].a\) Injection of a metered amount of particles or beads with reactive surfaces in the flow system followed by mechanical trapping or capture with the aid of external energy sources; b\) Injection of a metered volume of sample; c\) Interaction of analyte\(s\) with sorptive surfaces; d\) Preconcentration of analyte\(s\) followed by detection of native species or derivatization products; e\) Automatic removal of sorptive surfaces."
comment: "A typical workflow for bead injection in a flow manifold is shown in the figure below."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
