comment: "The most important occurrence is in farm animals pastured on plants containing phytoestrogens. The signs are those related to endometrial hyperplasia and vaginal tumefaction (swelling and puffiness), including long-term infertility and rectalprolapse, especially in pigs; uterine prolapse, especially in ewes; and feminization of males that have undergone castration."
