[Term]
id: goldbook:11094
name: pituitary
def: "Small endocrine gland sitting in a bony cavity \(the sella turcica\) at the base of the brain and connected to the hypothalamus."
comment: "The pituitary is structurally and functionally divided into anterior and posterior lobes. The anterior lobe secretes growth hormone (somatotropin), thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH), adrenocortocotropic hormone (ACTH), prolactin (PRL), luteinizing hormone (LH), and follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH). The posterior lobe develops from the hypothalamus and secretes oxytocin and antidiuretic hormone (ADH) (also called arginine vasopressin (AVP)). An intermediate lobe (indistinct in humans) secretes melanocyte-stimulating hormone (MSH)."
synonym: "hypophysis" []
