[Term]
id: goldbook:11435
name: density functional theory
def: "A quantum mechanical modeling method used to investigate the electronic structure of molecules using functionals that describe the spatially dependent electron density\, rather than the wavefunction as in ab initio and semi-empirical quantum chemical methods."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11436
name: descriptor
def: "A qualitative or quantitative property of a molecule or a part of a molecule."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11437
name: docking
def: "Computational methods that optimize the placement of a ligand in a macromolecular binding site of known or proposed 3D structure and provide a score as to the quality of the fit."
comment: "Docking programs differ as to whether conformational and chemical (tautomer, protomer) changes in the binding site are allowed and if only precalculated conformations of the ligand are used or if ligand flexibility is part of the docking."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
