[Term]
id: goldbook:11442
name: explicit solvent
def: "Individual solvent molecules that are included in a computation\, in contrast to those implied by a continuum approximation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11429

[Term]
id: goldbook:11443
name: extended connectivity fingerprints
def: "Hashed circular fingerprints that encode each atom according to its atomic symbol and hybridization for path length 2\, ECFP2; path length 4\, ECFP4; and path  length 6\, ECFP6."
synonym: "ECFP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "ECFP fingerprints" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11422

[Term]
id: goldbook:11444
name: false negative
def: "A model prediction of a negative result\, such as no biological activity\, when the true result is positive\, i.e. activity."
synonym: "FN" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11428

[Term]
id: goldbook:11445
name: false positive
def: "A model prediction of a positive result\, such as biological activity\, when the true result is negative\, i.e. inactivity."
synonym: "FP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11428

[Term]
id: goldbook:11446
name: force field
def: "A set of mathematical functions and their associated parameters used in a molecular mechanics or dynamics calculation of conformations\, flexibility\, and interactions of molecules."
comment: "Within the molecular mechanics approach, a set of potential functions defining bond stretch, bond angle (both valence and dihedral) distortion energy of a molecule as compared with its nonstrained conformation (that characterized by standard values of bond lengths and angles). A set of transferable empirical force constants is preassigned and the harmonic approximation is usually employed. Some force fields may contain terms for interactions between non-bonded atoms, electrostatic, hydrogen bond and other structural effects as well as account for anharmonicity effects. In vibrational spectroscopy, the inverse problem is solved of determining a set of force constants and other parameters of a chosen potential energy functions which would match with experimentally observed vibrational frequencies of a given series of congeneric molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11447
name: fragment keys
def: "Description of the structure of a molecule as the presence or absence of each of a pre-determined set of molecular substructures\, usually associated with a  particular location in a bit string."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11415
consider: goldbook:11457

[Term]
id: goldbook:11448
name: free energy perturbation
def: "A method that uses molecular dynamics or Metropolis Monte Carlo simulations to compute the relative free energy differences between two conditions\, typically the solution and bound states of a ligand-protein system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11449
name: functional class fingerprints
def: "Hashed circular fingerprints that encode each atom according to its property \(hydrophobic\, hydrogen bond donor\, hydrogen bond acceptor\, negatively charged\, or  positively charged\) for path length 2\, FCFP2; path length 4\, FCFP4; and path length 6\, FCFP6."
synonym: "FCFP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11422

[Term]
id: goldbook:11450
name: global model
def: "A computational model designed to cover all of chemistry space although it typically includes a measure of if the molecule for which the properties are to be  predicted is within or outside the applicability domain of the model."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11406

[Term]
id: goldbook:11451
name: graph-based method
def: "A computational method that converts the problem to be solved into a graph characterized by the character of the objects\, such the atoms of a molecule or molecules in a database\, and the distances between them."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11452
name: Hansch equation
def: "A QSAR equation that describes the relationship between the logarithm of the relative biological potency of a molecule \(\\\(\\log \(1/C_\{i\}\)\\\)\) and its electronic and hydrophobic properties\: \\\[\\log \(1/C_\{i\}\) = \\rho \\sigma_\{i\} + b\\\,\\log P_\{i\} - c\\\,\(\\log P_\{i\}\)^\{2\}\\\] in which fitting to the square term provides a parabola with an associated optimum log P."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11414
consider: goldbook:11469

[Term]
id: goldbook:11453
name: Hansch–Fujita π-constant
def: "A constant that describes the contribution of a substituent to the octan-1-ol-water log P of a compound.\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11469

[Term]
id: goldbook:11454
name: hashing
def: "An algorithm that maps data of variable length\, such as the raw descriptors of path or circular fingerprints or InChIs\, to a smaller fixed length vector."
comment: "Hashed InChIs are named InChIKeys."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11422
consider: goldbook:11455
consider: goldbook:11483

[Term]
id: goldbook:11455
name: InChIKey
def: "A fixed length \(character\) condensed digital representation of the InChI that is not human-understandable."
comment: "This is sometimes referred to as a hashed InChI."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11454
consider: goldbook:11456

[Term]
id: goldbook:11456
name: International Chemical Identifier
def: "A non-proprietary canonical identifier of chemical substances that can be used in printed and electronic data sources to enable easier linking of diverse data  compilations."
synonym: "InChI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11457
name: ISIS keys
def: "Predefined fragment keys that are used in 2D substructure and similarity searching with the ISIS software but are also generated by many other software  programs and used for 2D-QSAR or cluster analysis of molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11399
consider: goldbook:11447
consider: goldbook:11512
consider: goldbook:11521

[Term]
id: goldbook:11458
name: jackknifing
def: "A procedure to evaluate the accuracy of the statistics of a model\, such as the overall R2 or the contribution of particular properties\, by systematically recomputing the statistics generated from models developed by leaving out one or more observations at a time from the sample set."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11417
consider: goldbook:11499

[Term]
id: goldbook:11459
name: kappa shape descriptor
def: "A type of topological index."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11525

[Term]
id: goldbook:11460
name: kernel method
def: "Algorithms for pattern analysis that use functions such as Gaussians to enable them to operate in a high-dimensional descriptor space without ever computing  the coordinates of the data in that space."
comment: "The support vector machine (SVM) is the most widely used kernel method."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11405

[Term]
id: goldbook:11461
name: leave-some-out cross-validation
def: "A form of cross-validation in which more than one observation is left out at each run. Typically many runs with random samplings are performed."
synonym: "LSO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11462
name: leverage
def: "The influence of an observation on the coefficients of a fitted equation."
comment: "An observation with high leverage may be an outlier or in poorly explored property space."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11463
name: ligand efficiency
def: "Measure of the free energy of binding per heavy atom count \(i.e. non-hydrogen\) of a molecule."
comment: "An LE value of \(\pu{1.25 kJ mol-1}\) per non-hydrogen atom is the minimum requirement of a good lead or fragment."
comment: "It is used to rank the quality of molecules in drug discovery, particularly in fragment-based lead discovery."
synonym: "LE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11464
name: linear interaction energy
def: "A method that forecasts ligand binding free energies using force field estimations of the receptor-ligand interactions and thermal conformational sampling ."
synonym: "LIE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11446

[Term]
id: goldbook:11465
name: lipophilic ligand efficiency
def: "A measure of the efficiency of ligand binding that is corrected for binding driven by lipophilicity."
comment: "It is calculated as; \[LLE = \pu{p}K_{i} - \log P\] values of seven or greater are considered characteristic of a good clinical candidate."
synonym: "LLE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11466
name: loading of a property
def: "The contribution of the property to a principal component or partial least squares latent variable."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11467
name: local model
def: "A computational model that applies to only a subset of molecules\, typically a closely related series."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11450

[Term]
id: goldbook:11468
name: log <em>D</em>
def: "The logarithm of the ratio of the total concentration \(neutral and charged species\) of a compound in a nonpolar phase\, traditionally water-saturated octan-1-ol\, to that in water at a given \\\(\\pu\{pH\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11469
name: log <em>P</em>
def: "The logarithm of the ratio of the concentration of the uncharged form of a compound in a nonpolar phase\, traditionally water-saturated octan-1-ol\, to that in  water."
comment: "Common algorithms to calculate \(\log P\) are CLOGP and ALOGP."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11470
name: machine learning
def: "A computer algorithm that generates empirical models\, such as a model of biological potency as a function of the properties of the molecules\, that is derived  from the analysis of a training set for which all the necessary data are available."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11405
consider: goldbook:11503

[Term]
id: goldbook:11471
name: macromolecular crystallographic information file
def: "A file that describes in detail the features of a macromolecular structure and the X‑ray diffraction experiment that was used to derive that structure."
synonym: "mmCIF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11472
name: Markush structure
def: "A structure diagram that describes a set of related molecules with the structure of the common core and the structures of the substituents at each position."
comment: "Markush structures are commonly used in patent claims."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11520

[Term]
id: goldbook:11473
name: molecular diversity
def: "A measure of the spread of various properties or chemotypes within a set of compounds."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11474
name: molecular fingerprints
def: "Descriptions of the structure of a molecule calculated from the properties of each of its atoms and bonds that are then usually condensed into a fixed-length string by a hashing algorithm."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11405
consider: goldbook:11422
consider: goldbook:11432
consider: goldbook:11443
consider: goldbook:11449
consider: goldbook:11454
consider: goldbook:11483

[Term]
id: goldbook:11475
name: molecular similarity
def: "The degree to which two molecules resemble one another as calculated from their respective 2D or 3D properties\, molecular fingerprints\, fragment keys\, or superimposed 3D structures that usually ranges from 1 \(identical\) to 0 \(dissimilar\)."
comment: "Tanimoto or Tversky similarities for 2D structures and Carbo or Hodgkin for 3D structures."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11400
consider: goldbook:11402
consider: goldbook:11447
consider: goldbook:11474
consider: goldbook:11523
consider: goldbook:11529

[Term]
id: goldbook:11476
name: multidimensional scaling
def: "A visualization method that converts a dataset of distances between molecules in property space into coordinates in lower dimension space with emphasis on  preserving the relative distances between dissimilar molecules."
synonym: "MDS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11477
name: multiobjective optimization
def: "The search for those combinations of properties that produces the best compromise between the various objectives of the search\, for example properties of  compounds that are the best trade-off between potency\, bioavailability\, and selectivity."
synonym: "MOO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11480
consider: goldbook:11481

[Term]
id: goldbook:11478
name: orthogonal projections to latent structures
def: "A preprocessing method for partial least squares calculations that filters out variation that is not correlated to the property to be fit and so results in  improved interpretability of a PLS model while maintaining its predictivity."
synonym: "O-PLS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11479
name: overtraining
def: "Training a machine learning model for so long that the original input data is memorized with the result that model predictivity is degraded."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11480
name: Pareto front
def: "The various combinations of predictor properties that lead to optimum predicted compromises in multiple target properties."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11481
name: Pareto optimization
def: "The search for solutions to functions that provide a compromise between several desirable outcomes\, such as potency\, lack of toxicity\, and good absorption\, distribution\, metabolism\, and excretion \(ADME\) properties."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11482
name: partial atomic charges
def: "Charges assigned to atoms\, arising from the uneven distribution of electrons in bonds\, that are used to calculate intermolecular interaction energy or to  characterize the charge distribution of a molecule."
comment: "The charges can be derived from quantum chemical population analyses, fitted dipole moments or electrostatic potentials, spectroscopic data, or from partitioning electron density."
comment: "There is no firm theoretical basis for the assignment of partial atomic charges, hence there is no "correct" one."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11483
name: path fingerprints
def: "Vectors of Boolean arrays generated from the properties of the atoms and bonds in linear paths\, typically two to seven bonds long\, hashed into an integer of  fixed determined length."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11422
consider: goldbook:11432
consider: goldbook:11454
consider: goldbook:11519

[Term]
id: goldbook:11484
name: protein data bank file
def: "A text file that stores the atomic coordinates of a macromolecule\, usually a protein or nucleic acid with associated ligands\, solvent molecules and ions."
comment: "The documentation for the file format is at https://files.wwpdb.org/pub/pdb/doc/format_descriptions/Format_v33_Letter.pdf."
synonym: "PDB file" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11485
name: pharmacophore
def: "A proposal for the ensemble of steric and electronic features that define the optimal supermolecular intermolecular interaction of a ligand with a specific  biological target structure with the result that it triggers or blocks its biological response."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11486
name: pipelining programs
def: "Visual programming of the computational execution of sequential operations on a dataset\, with each node specifying an operation with options\, and the nodes processed sequentially."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11487
name: PLS latent variable
def: "One of the vectors of a linear combination of the input descriptors that a partial least squares calculation extracts from a dataset."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11488
name: PLS loading
def: "The contribution of a particular property to a PLS latent variable."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11487

[Term]
id: goldbook:11489
name: Poisson–Boltzmann equation
def: "A differential equation that uses a mean-field\, continuum model to describe the electrostatic interactions in ionic solutions where both ions and solvent are  treated implicitly\, resulting in less computational effort to describe biomolecules in ionic aqueous solutions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11429

[Term]
id: goldbook:11490
name: polar surface area
def: "Surface area over all polar atoms \(usually oxygen and nitrogen\)\, including any attached hydrogen atoms\, of a molecule."
comment: "Polar surface area is a commonly used metric (c.f. molecular descriptor) for the optimisation of cell permeability. Molecules with a PSA of greater than \(\pu{1.4 nm2}\) are usually poor at permeating cell membranes. For molecules to penetrate the blood-brain barrier, the polar surface area should normally be smaller than \(\pu{0.6 nm2}\), although values up to \(\pu{0.9 nm2}\) can be tolerated."
comment: "Sometimes sulfur atoms are included in the definition."
comment: "The value of PSA depends on the conformation of the molecule and also the algorithm and atomic radii used in the calculation."
synonym: "PSA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11436
consider: goldbook:11526

[Term]
id: goldbook:11491
name: pose diagram
def: "A 2D diagram that shows the interactions between a ligand and a protein in the 3D structure of the complex."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11492
name: posterior probability
def: "The conditional probability that is assigned to a quantity after relevant evidence is taken into account. The prior and posterior probabilities are linked by  the \(normalized\) likelihood function \(Bayes's theorem\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11412
consider: goldbook:11496

[Term]
id: goldbook:11493
name: prediction set
def: "Molecules that have been set aside from model development to test the reliability of the derived model."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11524

[Term]
id: goldbook:11494
name: principal component loading
def: "The contribution\, scaled between \\\(\\pu\{-1.0\}\\\) and \\\(\\pu\{1.0\}\\\)\, of an original variable to a particular principal component."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11495
name: principal component score
def: "A property of a molecule calculated from a principal components analysis of the original properties and the value of these properties for the molecule."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11496
name: prior probability
def: "The conditional probability that is assigned to a quantity before relevant evidence is taken into account\, for example\, the prior probability of an active  compound would be the fraction of the compounds in the dataset that are active."
comment: "The prior and posterior probabilities are linked by the (normalized) likelihood function (Bayes theorem)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11412
consider: goldbook:11492

[Term]
id: goldbook:11497
name: protein data bank
def: "An archive of freely available macromolecular structural data of proteins\, nucleic acids\, and complex assemblies."
comment: "The PDB is maintained by the Worldwide Protein Data Bank (wwPDB) with members RSCB PDB (USA), PDBe (Europe), PDBj (Japan), and BMRB (USA) that act as centers for deposition, data processing and distribution of PDB data."
comment: "The URL for the organization is https://www.wwpdb.org."
synonym: "PDB" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11498
name: q2
def: "The square of the leave-one-out cross-validation regression coefficient calculated from the variance of the observed versus predicted values of the target  property\, usually potency\, of each compound when eliminated during cross-validation."
comment: "This is related to r2, which is calculated as the fit of the observed to calculated for the whole dataset."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11499

[Term]
id: goldbook:11499
name: r2
def: "The ratio of the sum of squares explained by a regression model \(SSR\) to the 'total' sum of squares around the mean \(SST\)\, or\, because SST equals SSR plus the sum of squares of the error or residuals from the fit \(SSE\)\: \\\[R^\{2\} = \\frac\{\{\\rm\{SSR\}\}\}\{\{\\rm\{SST\}\}\} = 1 - \\frac\{\{\\rm\{SSE\}\}\}\{\{\\rm\{SST\}\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Except for the comparison of different models for the same dataset, \(R^{2}\) values are not a good indica- tion of fit of a model because the calculation depends on SST, which is larger if there is more spread in the observed values."
comment: "\(R_{2}\) values can range between \(\pu{0.0}\) and \(\pu{1.0}\)."
synonym: "$R^{2}$" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11500
name: random forest method
def: "A classification method that produces many recursive partitioning models\, each with a random selection of predictor properties\, and then combines the models  for predictions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11503

[Term]
id: goldbook:11501
name: recall
def: "The fraction of the total number of actives\, in the top-scoring docking hits\, such as the fraction of true actives that are retrieved in the top \\\(\\pu\{1\\%\}\\\) scoring molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11516

[Term]
id: goldbook:11502
name: receiver-operator characteristic curve
def: "A plot that shows the result of a test of the performance of a binary classifier by plotting the fraction of true positives identified versus the fraction of  false positives as the discrimination threshold is varied."
comment: "ROC curves are frequently used to compare different docking/scoring combinations or virtual screening protocols by the retrieval results from seeding a database of inactive molecules with known actives."
comment: "The area under the ROC curve (AUC) provides a measure of the superiority of the model over random predictions: If the value for the AUC for a ROC curve has the value of \(\pu{0.9\!-\! 1.0}\), the fit is considered excellent, whereas an AUC of \(\pu{0.5}\) suggests that the algorithm has no discriminatory power."
comment: "This is an example of using area under the curve as a measure of model performance."
synonym: "ROC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "ROC curve" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11407
consider: goldbook:11416
consider: goldbook:11445
consider: goldbook:11528

[Term]
id: goldbook:11503
name: recursive partitioning
def: "A classification method that uses predictor properties to successively divide the data set into subsets such that each resulting subset is enriched in  molecules that are in one class."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11504
name: regularization
def: "Introducing additional information in order to solve an ill-posed problem or to prevent overfitting\, usually taking the form of a penalty for complexity of the  model."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11505
name: response scrambling
def: "Evaluation of the robustness of a QSAR or classification model by repeatedly randomizing the target property of compounds\, developing models based on this  randomized property\, and comparing the statistics of fit of the scrambled models with those of the true model\, which should be superior."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11506
name: R-group decomposition
def: "The process whereby the molecules in a dataset are partitioned into the core \('scaffold'\)\, usually user-specified\, and the specific substituents \('R-groups'\)  found at each specific position."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11507
name: rule of five
def: "The rule of five states that molecules that violate two or more of the following rules are likely to have permeability problems; \(1\) CLOGP calculated octan-1-ol-water log P greater than 5.0; \(2\) molecular weight greater than 500; \(3\) more than five hydrogen bond donors; and \(4\) the sum of oxygen and nitrogen atoms is greater than 10."
comment: "Natural products, peptides and other substrates for biological transporters are exceptions."
comment: "The original authors also noted that one can calculate the octan-1-ol-water log P with the program MLOGP for which the cut-off is \(\pu{4.15}\). Users often use log P’s calculated with other programs or measured values."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11469

[Term]
id: goldbook:11508
name: scoring
def: "A mathematical formula that estimates the binding affinity of a ligand to a macromolecular target based on the structure of the complex."
comment: "Scoring is used to select poses and to rank compounds in docking."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11437

[Term]
id: goldbook:11509
name: structure-data format file
def: "A computer text file that follows a specified format in which each molecule is described by 2D or 3D coordinates\, atom type\, and connectivity to other atoms  and also specific user-definable fields that contain other information such as name and biological or chemical properties."
comment: "The format of the files is described in the following document: https://discover.3ds.com/sites/default/files/2020-08/biovia_ctfileformats_2020.pdf (link updated)."
synonym: "SDF file" []
synonym: "SDfile" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11510
name: sensitivity analysis
def: "Analysis\, often by finding approximate derivatives of the output with respect to each input\, that determines which of the descriptors in a model has the  greatest influence on the output."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11436

[Term]
id: goldbook:11511
name: similarity ensemble approach
def: "A method that predicts the probability that a molecule or set of molecules will be active against a particular target by considering its pairwise similarities  to all known ligands for that target."
synonym: "SEA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11512
name: similarity searching
def: "A virtual screening method that calculates the molecular similarity of an input 2D or 3D structure to each of the molecules in a database to identify a  requested number of most similar molecules or those above some similarity threshold."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11475
consider: goldbook:11523
consider: goldbook:11529
consider: goldbook:11533

[Term]
id: goldbook:11513
name: SMARTS
def: "An expansion of the SMILES language that describes a particular specific or generalized substructure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11514

[Term]
id: goldbook:11515
name: SMIRKS
def: "A derivative of the SMILES language that describes the transformation in a chemical reaction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11514

[Term]
id: goldbook:11516
name: specificity
def: "The ability of a two-class model to detect known inactive or non-toxic molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11501

[Term]
id: goldbook:11517
name: standard error of estimates
def: "The standard error of the errors or residuals\, observed minus calculated\, from a computational model\: \\\[\{\\rm\{SEE\}\} = \\sqrt \\frac\{\\sum \(Y_\{o\} - Y_\{c\}\)^\{2\}\}\{n\}\\\] in which \\\(Y_\{o\}\\\) is the observed value of \\\(Y\\\)\, \\\(Y_\{c\}\\\) is the calculated value of \\\(Y\\\)\, and \\\(n\\\) is the number of observations."
comment: "Sometimes also labeled root mean square deviation (RMSD)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11518

[Term]
id: goldbook:11518
name: standard error of prediction
def: "The standard deviation of the errors or residuals\, observed minus calculated\, from a computational model\: \\\[\{\\rm\{SEP\}\} = \\sqrt \\frac\{\\sum \(Y_\{o\} - Y_\{p\}\)^\{2\}\}\{n - k\}\\\] in which \\\(Y_\{o\}\\\) is the observed value of \\\(Y\\\)\, \\\(Y_\{p\}\\\) is the predicted value of \\\(Y\\\)\, \\\(n\\\) is the number of observations\, and \\\(k\\\) is the number of terms in the model."
comment: "Sometimes also labeled root mean square error of predication (RMSEP)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11517

[Term]
id: goldbook:11519
name: structural keys
def: "A pre-established set of substructures the presence or absence of which are used to describe a molecule and are used during substructure searching as a filter  to eliminate molecules that cannot match a query\, for clustering or similarity searching\, or for developing classification or regression models."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11474
consider: goldbook:11512
consider: goldbook:11521

[Term]
id: goldbook:11520
name: structure diagram
def: "A 2D drawing that shows the atoms of a molecular structure and the bonds that connect them."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11521
name: substructure searching
def: "A virtual screening method that uses a graph-based method to discover which molecules in a chemical structure database contain the substructure specified in  the query."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11451
consider: goldbook:11533

[Term]
id: goldbook:11522
name: supervised learning
def: "A machine learning method that aims to discover a relationship between the predictor and the response values\, such as exists in a QSAR or recursive  partitioning model."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11503

[Term]
id: goldbook:11523
name: Tanimoto similarity
def: "A scale that ranges from \\\(\\pu\{0.0\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{1.0\}\\\) when calculated as the ratio of the fingerprint bits or structural keys that both molecules have set divided by the number of bits or keys set in both molecules plus those set either molecule."
comment: "In set theory terms the Tanimoto similarity is equal to the ratio of the intersection set to the union set."
comment: "The Tanimoto similarity can also be calculated for molecules described by continuous variables. The similarities in this case range from \(\pu{-1\!{/}\! 3}\) to \(\pu{1.0}\)."
comment: "The value of a Tanimoto similarity of a pair of molecules depends on the molecular fingerprint or structural keys used in the calculation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11474
consider: goldbook:11529

[Term]
id: goldbook:11524
name: test set
def: "The set of molecules not used in any way to devise a computational model but instead are used to test its predictivity."
comment: "A test set differs from a prediction set in that the molecules and their associated activities may be derived from a source other than that from which the model was derived, for example, compounds tested after the model was developed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11493

[Term]
id: goldbook:11525
name: topological index
def: "A numerical value associated with chemical constitution for correlation of chemical structure with various physical properties\, chemical reactivity or biological activity. The numerical basis for topological indices is provided \(depending on how a molecular graph is converted into a numerical value\) by either the adjacency matrix or the topological distance matrix. In the latter the topological distance between two vertices is the number of edges in the shortest path between these."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11526
name: topological polar surface area
def: "An approximation to polar surface area that is calculated from the 2D structure."
synonym: "TPSA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11398
consider: goldbook:11490

[Term]
id: goldbook:11527
name: true negative
def: "A model prediction of a negative result\, such as no biological activity\, when the true result is also negative."
synonym: "TN" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11428

[Term]
id: goldbook:11528
name: true positive
def: "A model prediction of a positive result\, such as biological activity\, when the true result is also positive."
synonym: "TP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11428

[Term]
id: goldbook:11529
name: Tversky similarity
def: "An asymmetric measure in which a target structure is compared to a reference structure with user-selectable weighting of the relative importance of the fingerprint bits or structural keys that are present only in the reference versus the fingerprint bits or structural keys that are only in the target\, weightings for which the Tanimoto coefficient uses \\\(\\pu\{1.0\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11415
consider: goldbook:11474
consider: goldbook:11519
consider: goldbook:11523

[Term]
id: goldbook:11530
name: underdetermined system
def: "A system in which the number of descriptors is much larger than the number of observations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11531
name: validation set
def: "The molecules not used to devise a computational model but instead are used during model development to test for possible over-fitting as seen when additional  properties are added to a model but the predicted potencies of the validation set become less accurate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11532
name: virtual reaction
def: "The computer encoding of a possible chemical reaction between two explicit or Markush structures or substructures\, often with a mapping between the atoms in  the starting material and those in the product."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11472
consider: goldbook:11515

[Term]
id: goldbook:11533
name: virtual screening
def: "Computational methods that rank the molecules in a database by their forecast continuous or categorical biological or chemical properties."
comment: "Virtual screening is often used to predict the ability of molecules to bind to a macromolecular target of known 3D structure, to fit a ligand-based hypothesis of bioactivity, for their similarity to known actives, or to be mutagenic."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11534
name: workflow
def: "The sequence of steps used to perform a certain task."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-1204
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11535
name: apparent monomer
def: "Monomer which from the name of a polymer appears to have been used in the synthesis of the latter when it has actually been prepared from different precursor\(s\)."
comment: "The term replaces both of the formerly used terms "hypothetical monomer" and "implicit monomer", which are now deemed to be obsolete."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0702
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11536
name: block homopolymer
def: "Homopolymer that is composed of macromolecules comprising blocks that have at least one constitutional or configurational feature which is not present in the adjacent portions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0702
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11537
name: graft homopolymer
def: "Homopolymer composed of macromolecules with one or more species of block connected to the main chain as side chains\, these side chains having constitutional or configurational features that differ from those in the main chain."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0702
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11538
name: standardization
def: "Measurement of the concentration of a component of a solution with a reference measurement standard for the preparation of a secondary measurement standard"
comment: "Quantities that denote relative composition include mass concentration, number concentration, amount of substance concentration, molality, mass fraction, amount of substance fraction, and volume fraction."
comment: "Standardization is commonly performed by titration. It may be done by other means such as gravimetric analysis, e.g., standardize \(\ce{AgNO3}\) by precipitating \(\ce{AgCl}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2023-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09043

[Term]
id: goldbook:11539
name: controlled release
def: "Detection principle for a chemically modified electrode \(CME\) in which an analyte or reagent accumulated at a CME undergoes quantitative release \(egress\, stripping\, expulsion\, or microdosing\) to the test solution\, under electrochemical or chemical control."
comment: "Different mechanisms are involved in controlled release from the CME depending on the nature of the analyte or reagent and the method of accumulation. In the case of accumulation by covalent bonding, the anchoring bond is cleaved (ruptured) electrochemically. In the case of ion-exchange accumulation, an ionic (redox or acid-base) analyte or reagent is released by neutralizing its charge or the charge of the ion-exchanging redox polymer film or conducting polymer film."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-0109
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11540
name: all-solid-state ion-selective electrode
def: "Ion-selective electrode in which the ion-selective membrane contacts the electronic conductor without internal electrolyte solution."
comment: "Charge transfer is accomplished in the membrane by both ionic and electronic conductivities (mixed conductors)."
comment: "The inner reference electrode is replaced by an electronic conductor, e.g., a bromide sensor film of \(\ce{AgBr}\) is reversibly contacted with \(\ce{Ag}\), or an anion sensor based on cation radical salts is contacted with \(\ce{Pt}\)."
synonym: "metal contact ion-selective electrode" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-0109
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09119

[Term]
id: goldbook:11541
name: self-assembled monolayer
def: "Film\, one molecule thick\, in an ordered assembly on a surface."
synonym: "SAM" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11542
name: cationized molecule
def: "Ion formed by the association of a cation with a molecule \\\(\\ce\{M\}\\\)."
comment: "Cationization with, for instance, \(\ce{Ag}\), leads to high yields of some positive ion fragments or molecular ions. Each ion has a mass given by the sum of the mass of the parent molecule or fragment and the mass of the added metal atom or atoms. The \(\ce{Ag}\) can be used either as the substrate upon which the molecules are deposited or in the form of a sub-monolayer sputtered onto the molecules already on a surface."
comment: "\(\ce{NH4^{+}}\) can be used as well as metals to cationize molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11543
name: nominal mass
def: "Mass of a molecular ion or molecule calculated using the isotope mass of the most abundant constituent element isotope of each element rounded to the nearest integer value and multiplied by the number of atoms of each element."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11544
name: reflectron
def: "Component of a time-of-flight mass spectrometer that uses a static electric field to reverse the direction of travel of the ions and improves mass resolution by assuring that ions of the same m/z but different translational energy arrive at the detector at the same time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0404
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11545
name: adhesion
def: "Attachment of interfaces between phases or components that is maintained by intermolecular forces\, chain entanglements\, or both."
comment: "Adhesive strength (recommended symbol: \(F_{\rm{a}}\), unit: \(\pu{N m^{-2}}\)) is the force required to separate one condensed phase domain from another at the interface between the two phase domains divided by the area of the interface."
comment: "Interfacial adhesion is also referred to as tack."
comment: "Interfacial tension (recommended symbol: \(\upgamma\), unit: \(\pu{N m^{-1}}\), \(\pu{J m^{-2}}\)) is the change in Gibbs energy per unit change in interfacial area for substances in physical contact."
synonym: "tack" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1215
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11546
name: Michaelis–Menten equation
def: "The relationship between the initial rate \(velocity\) of an enzyme-catalysed reaction \\\(v_\{0\}\\\) and the initial substrate concentration \\\(\[\\ce\{S\}\]_\{0\}\\\) in the form \\\[v_\{0\} = V\[\\ce\{S\}\]_\{0\}/\(K_\{\\rm\{M\}\} + \[\\ce\{S\}\]_\{0\}\)\\\] where \\\(V\\\) \(the limiting rate\) and \\\(K_\{\\rm\{M\}\}\\\) \(the Michaelis constant\) are independent of the initial substrate concentration and constant at a given temperature and a given enzyme concentration. The reaction is then said to display Michaelis–Menten kinetics."
comment: "The symbol \(V_{\rm{max}}\) and the names "maximum rate" and "maximum velocity" are also in widespread use, although in general and under normal circumstances there is no finite substrate concentration at which \(v_{0} = V\). Hence, there is no maximum in the mathematical sense. The alternative name Michaelis concentration for \(K_{\rm{M}}\) may also be used and has the advantage of emphasizing that the quantity concerned has the dimension of a concentration and is not, in general, an equilibrium constant. The Michaelis constant is the substrate concentration at which \(v_{0} = V/2\)."
comment: "The term ‘hyperbolic kinetics’ is also sometimes used, because a plot of \(v_{0}\) against \([\ce{S}]_{0}\) has the form of a rectangular hyperbola through the origin with asymptotes \(v_{0} = V\) and \([\ce{S}]_{0} = -K_{\rm{M}}\). This term, and others that imply the use of particular kinds of plot, should be used with care to avoid ambiguity, as they can be misleading if used out of context."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11547
name: protein sequencing
def: "Determination of the primary structure of a protein."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2016-1120
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11548
name: zone pH
def: "pH of the solute zone in pH-zone-refining counter-current chromatography. \\\[\{\\rm\{pH\}\}_\{\\rm\{zone\}\} = \\pu\{p\}K_\{\\rm\{a\}\} + \\log\[\(K_\{\\rm\{DS\}\}/K_\{\\rm\{S\}\}\) - 1\]\\\]\, where \\\(K_\{\\rm\{DS\}\}\\\) is the partition ratio of solute $\\ce\{S\}$ \(an indicator for solute hydrophobicity\) and \\\(K_\{\\rm\{S\}\}\\\)\, the dissociation constant of the solute."
comment: "According to theoretical analysis two solutes that differ their zone \(\pu{pH}\) values by \(\pu{0.2}\) or greater can be resolved in \(\pu{pH}\)-zone-refining CCC."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09947

[Term]
id: goldbook:11549
name: intraparticle volume of the column
def: "Volume of the mobile phase within the pores of the particles in the stationary phase."
comment: "The retention time equivalent to \(V_{\rm{i}}\) is \(t_{\rm{i}}\) \[t_{\rm{i}} = \frac{V_{\rm{i}}}{F_{\rm{c}}}\]"
synonym: "intrastitial volume of the column" []
synonym: "stationary mobile-phase volume" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09963

[Term]
id: goldbook:11550
name: distribution constant \(exclusion\)
def: "Fraction of the intraparticle volume \(the volume of the pores\) available to the molecules of a particular sample component for diffusion\: \\\[K_\{0\} = \\frac\{V_\{\\rm\{R\}\} - V_0\}\{V_\{\\rm\{i\}\}\}\\\]"
comment: "In exclusion chromatography, \(K_{0}\) is related to the retention volume of a sample component and the inter- and intraparticle volumes of the column (\(V_{0}\) and \(V_{\rm{i}}\), respectively) in a manner analogous to the relationship in general liquid chromatography: \[V_{\rm{R}} = V_{0} + K_{0}V_{\rm{i}}\]"
comment: "The value of \(K_{0}\) varies between zero and unity. For an unretained compound, \(V_{\rm{R}} = V_{0}\) and thus, \(K_{0} = 0\). On the other hand, for a compound the molecules of which are smaller than the smallest pores, \(V_{\rm{R}} = V_{\rm{t}}\) and thus, \(K_{0} = 1\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09961
consider: goldbook:11549

[Term]
id: goldbook:11551
name: distribution constant calibration
def: "Calibration for extraction when close to equilibrium conditions\, using a known for the distribution constant for the analyte."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11552
name: microextraction \(methology\)
def: "Extraction method characterized by a low phase ratio\, so that at equilibrium the fraction extracted is low \(i.e. the extraction is not exhaustive\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11553
name: microextraction \(technique\)
def: "Extraction technique in which the volume \(mass\) of the extraction phase \(liquid or solid\) is substantially smaller than the sample volume \(mass\)."
comment: "The volume of extraction phase is typically \(\pu{\lt 100 \upmu L}\) or (mass \(\lt \pu{10 mg}\)) and the sample volume is \(\gt \pu{1 mL}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10175

[Term]
id: goldbook:11554
name: microextraction \(packed sorbent\)
def: "Solid-phase extraction using a syringe with a short sorbent bed located between the plunger and the needle."
comment: "The MEPS syringe facilitates low-dead volume sample processing by vertical movement of the plunger."
comment: "Typically based on a \(\pu{100 \upmu L}\) or \(\pu{250 \upmu L}\) volume syringe with a packed bed containing \(\pu{1\!{–}\! 2 mg}\) of sorbent."
synonym: "MEPS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0903
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:10163
consider: goldbook:10255

[Term]
id: goldbook:11556
name: acclimation
def: "Adjustment\, physiologically and \(or\) behaviorally\, of an organism to its environment or circumstances\, e.g.\, thermoregulation\, psychological adjustment."
comment: "In biology, acclimation refers to allowing this adjustment prior to initiating experimental observations, whereas the term acclimatization refers to adaptation or selection of an organism or population in its natural environment."
synonym: "acclimatization" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11557
name: acetylcholine
def: "Substance that functions as a neurotransmitter between nerve cells and between nerves and muscles."
synonym: "2-acetoxy-N,N,N-trimethylethanaminium" []
synonym: "ACh" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
