[Term]
id: goldbook:11558
name: acetylcholinesterase
def: "Enzyme that hydrolyzes acetylcholine."
synonym: "AChE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "acetylcholine hydrolase" []
synonym: "cholinesterase inhibitor" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11557

[Term]
id: goldbook:11559
name: acetylcholine receptor
def: "Integral membrane protein that allows the cell to respond to the binding of acetylcholine."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11557

[Term]
id: goldbook:11560
name: acoustic neuroma
def: "Non-malignant intracranial tumor of the eighth cranial nerve."
comment: "The eighth cranial (vestibulocochlear) nerve is involved in both hearing and balance."
comment: "This tumor arises from the Schwann cells."
synonym: "acoustic neurinoma" []
synonym: "vestibular Schwannoma" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11700
consider: goldbook:12064

[Term]
id: goldbook:11561
name: acroparesthesia
def: "Abnormal feeling of numbness\, tingling\, or burning of the skin\, typically in the extremities."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11562
name: action potential
def: "Brief\, spike-like depolarization associated with the passage of an impulse without decrement along the membrane of a muscle cell or nerve cell."
comment: "Action potentials also occur in many endocrine cells."
comment: "It is used for rapid signaling over a distance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11563
name: active avoidance test
def: "Fear-motivated associative avoidance test based on presentation of an adverse stimulus \(e.g.\, an electric current\) as a source of discomfort\, to create an environment from which the animal or subject would prefer to escape."
comment: "In this test, a mouse or rat learns to associate the occurrence of an aversive event with the presentation of a specific stimulus, and to avoid the event by actively moving to a different location. The number of avoidances (moving to the other location during the stimulus signal), number of non-responses or errors (failing to move to the other location during the trial), and response latency (time between signal onset and response), are used as an index of learning."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11626

[Term]
id: goldbook:11564
name: addiction
def: "Compulsive\, uncontrolled reward-seeking behavior\, especially referring to substance use."
comment: "An addiction may be psychological, referring to a craving or felt need for a behavior that produces a desired mental state without a known physiological basis, or it may be a physical (physiological) dependence in which discontinued use of a substance leads to symptoms of withdrawal."
synonym: "physical dependence" []
synonym: "psychological dependence" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11798
consider: goldbook:12181

[Term]
id: goldbook:11565
name: adenoma
