comment: "Domoic acid is produced by marine diatoms belonging to the genus Pseudo-nitzschia and the species Nitzschia navis-varingica. Domoic acid is passed on to humans by consumption of bivalve shellfish (mollusks) such as mussels, oysters, and clams that have accumulated it during filter feeding."
comment: "Often characterized by excitotoxicity and loss of hippocampal neurons."
