[Term]
id: goldbook:11770
name: fibrillation
def: "Rapid contractions or twitching of muscle fibrils\, but not of the muscle as a whole."
comment: "The term is commonly used for atrial fibrillation, where the muscles of the cardiac atrium show the phenomenon, leading to loss of normal rhythmic contraction, and also for loss of synchronized contraction of the ventricles, i.e., ventricular fibrillation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
