[Term]
id: goldbook:11772
name: flaccid
def: "Relaxed\, flabby\, or without tone."
comment: "Curare causes flaccid paralysis by binding to acetylcholine receptors and inhibiting their action."
comment: "Flaccid paralysis is a condition where one or more muscles are without tone. It is often caused by the lack of motor nerve impulses due to nerve trauma, disease or specific pharmaceuticals."
