[Term]
id: goldbook:11779
name: ganglion
def: "Cluster of nerve cell bodies located outside the brain and spinal cord\, i.e.\, in the peripheral nervous system.Note\: Ganglia interconnect to form a complex network known as a plexus and serve as relay stations where different neurons can modulate the signals of each other. Compare\: basal ganglion. Fibrous cyst usually attached to a tendon sheath."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:11780
name: ganglion cell
def: "Neuron located in a ganglion."
comment: "Included are cells in the ganglion cell layer of the retina, cells of the sympathetic nervous system in the adrenal medulla, cells in sympathetic and parasympathetic ganglia, and cells in the spiral (cochlear) ganglion involved in hearing."
