def: "Form of excitotoxicity where excess glutamate release in synapses \(glutamatergic storm\) leads to overstimulation\, followed by excess cellular calcium uptake\, cytotoxicity and apoptosis."
comment: "Excitotoxicity may occur after acute neuronalischemia and damage. It is believed to be a factor in chronic diseases of the nervous system, and in some withdrawal phenomena."
comment: "N-methyl-D-aspartic acid, kainic acid, and other ligands of the glutamate receptor induce this effect."
