comment: "Several theories have been advanced to explain the cause of multiple chemical sensitivity, including allergy, toxic effects, and neurobiological sensitization. There is insufficient scientific evidence to confirm a relationship between any of these possible causes and symptoms."
comment: "This syndrome is characterized by the patient’s belief that his or her symptoms are caused by very low-level exposure to environmental chemicals. The term "chemical" is used to refer broadly to many natural and man-made substances, some of which have several chemical constituents."
