[Term]
id: goldbook:12072
name: shellfish poisoning
def: "Illness associated with consumption of seafood contaminated with toxins."
comment: "Four syndromes with overlapping features are recognized. These are amnesic shellfish poisoning, diarrheal shellfish poisoning, neurotoxic shellfish poisoning, and paralytic shellfish poisoning."
comment: "These are primarily associated with consumption of bivalve molluscs such as mussels, clams, oysters and scallops that accumulate toxins produced by microscopic algae such as dinoflagellates and diatoms, and cyanobacteria."
