[Term]
id: goldbook:12087
name: startle reaction
def: "Rapid physiological and psychological response to a sudden\, unexpected stimulus that includes muscle contraction and avoidance posturing\, with an increase in heart rate\, respiration\, skin conductance\, and a negative affect."
comment: "In the startle response test, types and intensities of reactions (e.g., motor activity) are evaluated."
