[Term]
id: goldbook:12091
name: stereology
def: "Three dimensional interpretation of two dimensional cross sections of tissue and other materials."
comment: "Often used for estimating the number of neurons or neuronal cell bodies in a volume of tissue."
comment: "Stereology is different from tomography; the latter requires a complete set of planes to reconstruct the internal structure whereas stereology uses statistical methods to reconstruct the image from representative plane sections."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12092
name: unbiased stereology
def: "Stereological method that uses systematic analysis of defined spatial fractions of a sample to estimate numbers of neuronal nuclei independent of changes in size and shape that may occur during tissue processing."
