id: goldbook:12116
name: T-maze
def: "Simple type of test apparatus with three arms shaped like the letter 'T.' After placing a rodent in the middle\, it is recorded how often the animal enters each arm."
comment: "Rewards can be used for motivation, or the inborn trend for alternation can be tested."
comment: "The Y-maze is a variation of the T-maze where the apparatus is "Y"-shaped."
