id: goldbook:12119
name: tail immersion test
def: "Procedure in which the tail of a rodent is placed in a hot water bath \(typically between \\\(\\pu\{54^\{\\circ\}C\}\\\) and \\\(\\pu\{58^\{\\circ\}C\}\\\)\) and the time it takes the animal to remove the tail from the water is interpreted as a measurement of the relative degree of antinociception."
