[Term]
id: goldbook:12199
name: mean-square unperturbed end-to-end distance
def: "Mean-square end-to-end distance of a chain having unperturbed dimensions."
comment: "\(\lt\!r_{\rm{o}}^{2}\! \gt\) of a hypothetical, sufficiently long, linear chain of identical single skeletal bonds having rotational isomeric states that are independent of each other is given by the equation \[\lt\!r_{\rm{o}}^{2}\!\gt = nl^{2} \frac{(1 + \cos\theta)}{(1 - \cos \theta)} {\cdot} \frac{(1 + \lt\!\cos \phi\!\gt )}{(1 - \lt\!\cos \phi\!\gt)}\] where \(n\) is the number of skeletal bonds of length \(l\) and valence-angle supplement \(\theta\), and \(\lt\!\cos \phi\!\gt\) is the average of the cosine of the dihedral angles \(\phi\) defined over sequences of three contiguous skeletal bonds. This equation is useful for understanding the significance of characteristic ratio, steric factor, and effective bond-length."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12187
consider: goldbook:12202

[Term]
id: goldbook:12200
name: root-mean-square end-to-end distance of a freely rotating chain
def: "Root-mean-square end-to-end distance of a linear freely rotating chain."
comment: "If no ambiguity results, the term "freely rotating end-to-end distance" can be used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12201
name: mean-square end-to-end distance of a freely rotating chain
def: "Mean-square end-to-end distance of a linear freely rotating chain."
comment: "\(\lt\!r_{\rm{o,f}}^2\!\gt\) of a hypothetical, sufficiently long, linear freely rotating chain of identical single skeletal bonds is given by the equation \[\lt\!r_{\rm{o,f}}^{2}\!\gt = nl^{2}\frac{(1 + \cos \theta)}{(1 - \cos \theta)}\] where \(n\) is the number of skeletal bonds of length \(l\) and valence-angle supplement \(\theta\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12202
name: effective bond length
def: "Square root of the ratio of the unperturbed mean-square end-to-end distance of a linear chain to its number of skeletal bonds\, i.e.\, \\\[b = \(\\lt\\!r_\{\\rm\{o\}\}^\{2\}\\!\\gt\\!/n\)^\{1/2\}\\\]"
comment: "The effective bond length is a type of characteristic ratio relating to chain structure, cf., characteristic ratio."
comment: "\(b^{2}\) is the unperturbed mean-square end-to-end distance per skeletal bond. For a hypothetical, sufficiently long chain of identical single skeletal bonds having rotational isomeric states that are independent of each other, the equation in mean-square unperturbed end-to-end distance shows that the value of \(b\) depends on the values of \(l\), \(\cos \theta\) and \(\lt\!\cos \phi\!\gt\). In general, for actual chains, the value of \(b\) is still characteristic of the values of the lengths and valence angles of the skeletal bonds and of the dihedral bond-conformational angles, although it may be difficult to write an analytical expression for \(b\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12187
consider: goldbook:12199

[Term]
id: goldbook:12203
name: equivalent freely jointed chain
def: "Hypothetical freely jointed chain with the same mean-square end-to-end distance and contour length as an actual linear chain having unperturbed dimensions."
comment: "The number of links, \(m\), and their length, \(l^{\prime}\), are evaluated from the mean-square end-to-end distance, \(\lt\!r_{\rm{o}}^{2}\!\gt\), and contour length, \(r_{\rm{max}}\), of the actual chain using the equations in freely jointed chain and contour length, with \[m = \frac{r_{\max}^{2}}{\lt\!r_{\rm{o}}^{2}\!\gt} \quad {\rm{and}} \quad l^{\prime} = \frac{\lt\!r_{\rm{o}}^{2}\!\gt}{r_{\max}}\] For example, for polymethylene at room temperature, one freely jointed link is equivalent to about 10 actual \(\ce{C-C}\) skeletal bonds."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12197

[Term]
id: goldbook:12204
name: Kuhn segment
def: "Segment or link of an equivalent freely jointed chain."
synonym: "equivalent freely jointed link" []
synonym: "statistical segment" []
