[Term]
id: goldbook:12206
name: self-avoiding random-walk chain
def: "Freely jointed chain subject to the condition that the segments cannot intersect one another."
comment: "In the model of a self-avoiding chain, segments are considered to have a finite volume such that two or more cannot occupy the same volume simultaneously."
comment: "The self-avoiding random-walk chain model is used to represent a polymer chain with excluded volume."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12207
name: macromolecular coil
def: "Depiction of a macromolecule in which its segments are distributed about some point in space."
comment: "The point in space is usually chosen as the molecular centre of mass or a chain end."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12186

[Term]
id: goldbook:12209
name: chain stiffness
def: "Parameter describing the end-to-end distance of a linear\, single-strand macromolecular chain having unperturbed dimensions relative to that of a model macromolecular chain not subject to short-range interactions."
comment: "The steric factor, \(\sigma\), Kuhn segment length, \(l^{\prime}\), and persistence length, \(a\), are all measures of chain stiffness."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12205

[Term]
id: goldbook:12212
name: <i>g</i>-factor
def: "Ratio of the mean-square radius of gyration of a branched molecule\, \\\(\\lt\\!s_\{\\rm\{b\}\}^\{2\}\\!\\gt\\\)\, to that of an otherwise identical linear molecule\, \\\(\\lt\\!s_\{\\rm\{l\}\}^\{2\}\\!\\gt\\\)\, of the same relative molecular mass in the same solvent at the same temperature\, i.e.\, \\\(g = \\lt\\!s_\{\\rm\{b\}\}^\{2\}\\!\\gt\\!/\\!\\lt\\!s_\{\\rm\{l\}\}^\{2\}\\!\\gt\\\)."
comment: "The \(g\mbox{-}\rm{factor}\) is a quantity characterizing the effects of long-chain branches on the size of a branched molecule."
synonym: "contraction factor" []
synonym: "geometric contraction factor" []
synonym: "radius of gyration contraction factor" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12192
consider: goldbook:12211
consider: goldbook:12213

[Term]
id: goldbook:12213
name: <i>g</i>′-factor
def: "Ratio of the intrinsic viscosity of a branched molecule\, \\\(\[\\eta_\{\\rm\{b\}\}\]\\\)\, to that of an otherwise identical linear molecule\, \\\(\[\\eta_\{\\rm\{l\}\}\]\\\)\, of the same relative molecular mass in the same solvent at the same temperature\, i.e.\, \\\(g^\{\\prime\} = \[\\eta_\{\\rm\{b\}\}\]/\[\\eta_\{\\rm\{l\}\}\]\\\)."
comment: "The \(g^{\prime}\mbox{-}\rm{factor}\) is a quantity characterizing the effects of long-chain branches on the size of a branched molecule."
synonym: "hydrodynamic contraction factor" []
synonym: "viscosity contraction factor" []
