[Term]
id: goldbook:12214
name: molar mass
def: "Mass divided by amount of substance."
comment: "If the unit \(\pu{g mol-1}\) unit is used, the numerical values of molar mass, relative molecular mass and relative molar mass are equal."
comment: "In the present context, "amount of substance" is the number of molecules divided by the Avogadro constant, \(N_{\rm{A}} [= \pu{6.02214179(30)E23 mol-1}]\)."
comment: "The term "molar" may also be used for entities consisting of more than one molecule, such as complexes, aggregates, micelles, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12215
name: molar-mass average
def: "Any average of the molar mass\, molecular weight\, relative molar mass\, or relative molecular mass for a non-uniform polymer\, with the symbol \\\(\\rm\{k\}\\\) specifying the type of average."
comment: "An infinite number of molar-mass averages can in principle be defined, but only a few types of averages are directly accessible experimentally. The most important averages are defined in terms of simple moments of the distribution functions and are obtained by methods applied to systems in thermodynamic equilibrium, such as osmometry, static light scattering, and sedimentation equilibrium. Hydrodynamic methods, as a rule, yield more complex molar-mass averages."
comment: "Any molar-mass average can be defined in terms of mass fractions or mole fractions. In this document, the most important molar-mass averages are defined in terms of the mass fraction, \(w_{\rm{M}}\), of the species of molar mass \(M\). These definitions are most closely related to experimental determinations of molar-mass averages."
comment: "Quantities molecular-weight average, relative-molar-mass average, and relative-molecular-mass average (\(M_{\rm{r,k}}\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."
comment: "The various symbols that \(\rm{k}\) can be are given in the terms number-average molar mass, mass-average molar mass, z-average molar mass, (z+1)-average molar mass, and viscosity-average molar mass. For example, with \(\rm{k} \equiv n\), number-average quantities are defined."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12214
consider: goldbook:12216
consider: goldbook:12217
consider: goldbook:12218
consider: goldbook:12219
consider: goldbook:12220

[Term]
id: goldbook:12216
name: number-average molar mass
def: "The equation for number-average molar mass is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{n\}\} = \\frac\{1\}\{\\sum\\limits_\{M\} \(w_\{M\}/M\)\}\\\] The equation for number-average molecular weight  is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{r\,n\}\} = \\frac\{1\}\{\\sum\\limits_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\}\(w_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\}/M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\)\}\\\]"
comment: "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."
comment: "Quantities number-average molecular weight, number-average relative molar mass, and number-average relative molecular mass (\(M_{\rm{r,n}}\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12215

[Term]
id: goldbook:12217
name: mass-average molar mass
def: "The equation for mass-average molar mass is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{m\}\} \\equiv M_\{\\rm\{w\}\} = \\sum\\limits_\{M\} w_\{M\}M\\\] The equation for mass-average molecular weight  is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{r\,m\}\} \\equiv \{M_\{\\rm\{r\,w\}\}\} = \\sum\\limits_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\} w_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\} M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\\\]"
comment: "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."
comment: "Quantities mass-average molecular weight, mass-average relative molar mass, and mass-average relative molecular mass (\(M_{\rm{r,m}}\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12215

[Term]
id: goldbook:12218
name: z-average molar mass
def: "The equation for z-average molar mass is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{z\}\} = \\frac\{\\sum\\limits_\{M\} w_\{M\}M^\{2\}\}\{\\sum\\limits_\{M\} w_\{M\}M\}\\\] The equation for z-average molecular weight is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{r\,z\}\} = \\frac\{\\sum\\limits_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\} w_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\}M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}^\{2\}\}\{\\sum\\limits_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\} w_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\}M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\}\\\]"
comment: "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."
comment: "Quantities z-average molecular weight, z-average relative molar mass, and z-average relative molecular mass, (\(M_{\rm{r,z}}\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12215

[Term]
id: goldbook:12219
name: \(z + 1\)-average molar mass
def: "The equation for \(z + 1\)-average molar mass is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{z+1\}\} = \\frac\{\\sum\\limits_\{M\} w_\{M\}M^\{3\}\}\{\\sum\\limits_M w_\{M\}M^\{2\}\}\\\] The equation for \(z + 1\)-average molecular weight is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{r\,z+1\}\} = \\frac\{\\sum\\limits_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\} w_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\}M^\{3\}\}\{\\sum\\limits_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\} w_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\}M^\{2\}\}\\\]"
comment: "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."
comment: "Quantities (z + 1)-average molecular weight, (z + 1)-average relative molar mass, and (z + 1)-average relative molecular mass (\(M_{\rm{r,z+1}}\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12215

[Term]
id: goldbook:12220
name: viscosity-average molar mass
def: "The equation for viscosity-average molar mass is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{v\}\} = \\left\[\\sum\\limits_\{M\} w_\{M\}M^\{a\} \\right\]^\{1/a\}\\\] The equation for viscosity-average molecular weight is \\\[M_\{\\rm\{r\,v\}\} = \\left\[\\sum\\limits_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\} w_\{M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\}M_\{\\rm\{r\}\}^\{a\} \\right\]^\{1/a\}\\\] where \\\(a\\\) is the exponent in the Mark–Houwink equation\, \\\(\[\\eta\] = KM^\{a\}\\\)"
comment: "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."
comment: "Quantities viscosity-average molecular weight, viscosity-average relative molar mass, and viscosity-average relative molecular mass (\(M_{\rm{r,v}}\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."
comment: "The exponent \(a\) is different from the adjustable parameter of some of the distribution functions and from the persistence length."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12215

[Term]
id: goldbook:12221
name: apparent molar mass
def: "Molar mass\, molecular weight\, relative molar mass\, or relative molecular mass calculated from experimental data without the application of appropriate corrections."
comment: "Examples of corrections are those for finite polymer concentration, association, preferential sorption, compositional heterogeneity, constitutional heterogeneity, and also from experimental data obtained from an instrument (often an SEC instrument) calibrated using standard samples of known molar masses of a polymer constitutionally different from that being analysed."
comment: "Quantities apparent molecular weight, apparent relative molar mass, and apparent relative molecular mass (\(M_{\rm{r,app}}\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12214

[Term]
id: goldbook:12222
name: cumulative number-distribution function
def: "Cumulative distribution function in which the relative amount of a portion of a substance with values of the random variable or variables less than or equal to a given value or given values is expressed in terms of mole fraction."
synonym: "cumulative number distribution" []
synonym: "integral number distribution" []
synonym: "integral number-distribution function" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12223
name: cumulative mass-distribution function
def: "Cumulative distribution function in which the relative amount of a portion of a substance with values of the random variable or variables less than or equal to a given value or given values is expressed in terms of mass fraction."
comment: "It is the differential and cumulative mass-distribution functions that are usually determined experimentally."
synonym: "cumulative mass distribution" []
synonym: "integral mass distribution" []
synonym: "integral mass-distribution function" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12224
name: molar-mass dispersity
def: "Ratio of the mass-average molar mass\, \\\(M_\{\\rm\{m\}\}\\\)\, molecular weight\, relative molar mass\, or relative molecular mass\, \\\(M_\{\\rm\{r\,m\}\}\\\)\, to the number-average molar mass\, \\\(M_\{\\rm\{n\}\}\\\)\, molecular weight\, relative molar mass\, or relative molecular mass\, \\\(M_\{\\rm\{r\,n\}\}\\\). \\\[Ð\\!_\{\\rm\{M\}\} = M_\{\\rm\{m\}\}/M_\{\\rm\{n\}\} = M_\{\\rm\{r\,m\}\}/M_\{\\rm\{r\,n\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Use of the term "polydispersity index", or other terms involving the word "polydispersity", for \(M_{\rm{m}}/M_{\rm{n}}\), \(M_{\rm{r,m}}/M_{\rm{r,n}}\) is strongly discouraged."
synonym: "molecular-weight dispersity" []
synonym: "relative-molar-mass dispersity" []
synonym: "relative-molecular-mass dispersity" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12217

[Term]
id: goldbook:12225
name: degree-of-polymerisation dispersity
def: "Ratio of the mass-average degree of polymerisation\, \\\(X_\{\\rm\{m\}\}\\\)\, to the number-average degree of polymerisation\, \\\(X_\{\\rm\{n\}\}\\\). \\\[Ð\\!_\{\\rm\{X\}\} = X_\{\\rm\{m\}\}/X_\{\\rm\{n\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Use of the term "polydispersity index", or other terms involving the word "polydispersity", for \(X_{\rm{m}}/X_{\rm{n}}\) is strongly discouraged."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12226
name: dispersity
def: "Ratio of \\\(M_\{\\rm\{m\}\}\\\) to \\\(M_\{\\rm\{n\}\}\\\)\, or the ratio of \\\(X_\{\\rm\{m\}\}\\\) to \\\(X_\{\\rm\{n\}\}\\\) for a homopolymer or an alternating copolymer of sufficiently large molar mass\, such that the effects of the distinct structures of the end-groups of the constituent macromolecules can be neglected\, giving \\\(X_\{\\rm\{n\}\}\\\) directly proportional to \\\(M_\{\\rm\{n\}\}\\\)\, \\\(X_\{\\rm\{m\}\}\\\) directly proportional to \\\(M_\{\\rm\{m\}\}\\\) and \\\(Ð\\!_\{\\rm\{M\}\} = Ð\\!_\{\\rm\{X\}\} = Ð\\\)."
comment: "Dispersity is a measure of the dispersion (or spread) of a molar mass, molecular weight, relative molar mass, relative molecular mass, or degree-of-polymerisation distribution function. For a uniform polymer, \(Ð = 1\); for a polymer of sufficiently high \(X_{\rm{n}}\) having a Poisson distribution of molar masses, molecular weights, relative-molar-masses, or relative-molecular-masses, \(Ð \cong 1\); and for a polymer of sufficiently high \(X_{\rm{n}}\) having a most probable distribution of molar masses, molecular weights, relative-molar-masses, or relative-molecular-masses, \(Ð \cong 2\)."
comment: "For a copolymer that is not an alternating copolymer \(X_{\rm{n}}\) cannot be considered to be directly proportional to \(M_{\rm{n}}\), nor \(X_{\rm{w}}\) directly proportional to \(M_{\rm{w}}\). It is then necessary to state whether \(Ð\!_{\rm{M}}\) or \(Ð\!_{\rm{X}}\) is being used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12214

[Term]
id: goldbook:12228
name: semi-dilute solution
def: "Polymer solution in the concentration range at which the domains occupied by the dissolved macromolecules or entities start to overlap."
comment: "The semi-dilute solution behaviour sets in at concentrations larger than the overlap concentration, \(c^{\ast}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12229
name: concentrated solution
def: "Polymer solution in the concentration range at which the domains occupied by the dissolved macromolecules or entities overlap to such an extent that it is not possible to distinguish the individual domains from one another."
comment: "The limiting maximum mass concentration is the density of the bulk amorphous polymer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12230
name: entanglement
def: "Entanglement\, involving one or more macromolecular chains\, of duration at least equal to the period of observation."
comment: "A volume element, in which the chains of two or more macromolecules are entangled, acts as a temporary junction point of a transient polymer network, such as can occur in a semi-dilute solution or a concentrated solution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12228
consider: goldbook:12229

[Term]
id: goldbook:12231
name: mesh size
def: "Average distance between two adjacent entanglements on a given macromolecule in a semi-dilute solution\, a concentrated solution\, or bulk amorphous polymer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12228
consider: goldbook:12229

[Term]
id: goldbook:12232
name: blob
def: "Hypothetical spherical volume element occupied by a subchain of a macromolecule between two neighbouring entanglements on the same macromolecule."
comment: "It is assumed that the behaviours of portions of a macromolecule separated by more than the size of a blob are not correlated with each other."
comment: "The size of a blob is a scaling function of concentration and temperature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12233
name: scaling law
def: "Equation of the type \\\(y = k x^\{a\}\\\)\, relating two physical quantities\, \\\(x\\\) and \\\(y\\ \(\\rm\{g\}\)\\\)\, in which the value of the exponent \\\(a\\\) can be predicted by theory."
comment: "It has been shown that scaling laws are particularly useful in the description of semi-dilute polymer solutions."
comment: "The constant \(k\) cannot be predicted from theory and must be determined experimentally."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12234
name: free volume
def: "Difference between specific volume of an amorphous polymer and that of its perfect crystalline form."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12235
name: mean-field theory
def: "Theory reducing the difficult exact evaluation of interactions in a multi-body system to a simpler but approximate evaluation of an average effective interaction of one body with its surroundings."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12236
name: co-nonsolvency
def: "Decrease in solubility of a polymer in a solvent comprising more than one component\, each component of which by itself is a solvent for the polymer."
comment: "Poly(N-isopropylacrylamide) in water/methanol and poly(vinyl alcohol) in dimethylsulfoxide/water are examples of systems in which co-nonsolvency occurs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12237
name: osmometer
def: "Apparatus for measuring osmotic pressure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12238
name: osmometry
def: "Measurement of the osmotic pressure of a solution using an osmometer."
comment: "The osmometry of a dilute solution of polymer is an absolute method for determining the number-average molar mass of the polymer and the osmotic virial coefficients of the solution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12216
consider: goldbook:12227
consider: goldbook:12237
consider: goldbook:12239

[Term]
id: goldbook:12239
name: osmotic virial coefficient
def: "Coefficient in the expansion of the chemical potential of the solvent\, \\\(\\mu_\{\\rm\{s\}\}\\\)\, in powers of the mass concentration\, \\\(c\\\)\, of the solute\, i.e.\, \\\[\\mu_\{\\rm\{s\}\} - \\mu_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{\\circ\} = -\\mathit\{\\Pi\} V_\{s\}^\{\\prime\} = -RT V_\{s\}^\{\\prime\} \(A_\{1\}c + A_\{2\}c^\{2\} + A_\{3\}c^\{3\} + \\ldots\)\\\] where \\\(\\mu_\{\\rm\{s\}\}^\{\\circ\}\\\) is the chemical potential of the solvent in the reference state at the temperature of the system and ambient pressure\, \\\(\\mathit\{\\Pi\}\\\) is the osmotic pressure and \\\(V_\{s\}^\{\\prime\}\\\) is the partial molar volume of the solvent. In solvents comprising more than one component\, the definition applies to any solvent component."
comment: "The factor \(RT\) is sometimes included in the virial coefficients, to give \[\mu_{\rm{s}} - \mu_{\rm{s}}^{\circ} = -\mathit{\Pi}V_{s}^{\prime} = -V_{s}^{\prime}(A_{1}^{\prime}c + A_{2}^{\prime}c^{2} + A_{3}^{\prime}c^{3} + \dots),\quad {\rm{where}}\ A_{i}^{\prime} = RT A_{i}\]"
comment: "The first osmotic virial coefficient is the reciprocal number-average molar mass, i.e., \(A_{1} = 1/M_{\rm{n}}\). The values of the second and higher virial coefficients, \(A_{2}, A_{3}, \dots\), respectively, are characteristic of polymer-solvent and polymer-polymer interactions."
comment: "To evaluate \(M_{\rm{n}}\) and \(A_{2}\), \(\mathit{\Pi}/c\) is often plotted versus \(c\), so that \[\frac{\mathit{\Pi}}{c} = \left({\frac{\mathit{\Pi}}{c}} \right)_{\circ}(1 + \mathit{\Gamma}_{2}c + \mathit{\Gamma}_{3}c^{2} + \ldots),\ {\rm{where}}\ \left(\frac{\mathit{\Pi}}{c} \right)_{\circ} = \frac{RT}{M_{\rm{n}}}\ {\rm{and,}}\ \mathit{\Gamma}_{i} = M_{\rm{n}}A_{i}\]"
synonym: "virial coefficient of the chemical potential" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12216

[Term]
id: goldbook:12240
name: binodal
def: "Curve in the isobaric temperature-composition plane for a mixture defining the region of composition and temperature across which a transition occurs from miscibility of the components to conditions where single-phase mixtures are metastable or unstable."
comment: "Binodal compositions are defined by pairs of points on the curve defining the dependence of Gibbs energy of mixing on composition that have common tangents, corresponding to compositions of equal chemical potentials of each of the two components in two phases."
synonym: "binodal curve" []
synonym: "coexistence curve" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12241
name: cloud point
def: "Point in the isobaric temperature-composition plane of a binary or multicomponent mixture at which a decrease in transparency is observed due to the turbidity caused by phase separation."
comment: "A cloud point can be induced by varying temperature or composition."
comment: "A cloud point induced by varying temperature is heating-rate or cooling-rate dependent."
comment: "A cloud point is characterized by the first appearance of turbidity or cloudiness."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12242
name: cloud-point curve
def: "Curve of temperature vs. composition defined by the cloud points over range of compositions of two substances."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12241

[Term]
id: goldbook:12243
name: cloud-point temperature
def: "Temperature at a cloud point."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12241

[Term]
id: goldbook:12244
name: lower critical solution temperature
def: "Critical temperature below which a mixture is miscible at any composition."
comment: "An LCST exists for mixtures in which solubility decreases with temperature."
comment: "For a mixture containing or consisting of polymeric components, these may be different polymers or species of different molar mass of the same polymer."
comment: "The LCST depends upon pressure and the molar-mass distribution functions of the constituent polymer(s)."
comment: "The LCST occurs near the minimum on the cloud point curve."
comment: "The occurrence of an LSCT is less common than that of an upper critical solution temperature. It cannot be explained by simple polymer solution theories, such as the Flory–Huggins theory. However, it occurs for several polymer/solvent pairs and frequently for polymer blends."
synonym: "LCST" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
