consider: goldbook:12241

[Term]
id: goldbook:12245
name: translational diffusion
def: "Process by which the equilibrium statistical distribution of positions of molecules or entities in space is maintained or restored due to their translational Brownian motion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12246
name: translational frictional coefficient
def: "Frictional force\, \\\(F\\\)\, per unit velocity\, \\\(u\\\)\, experienced by an isolated spherical body moving unidirectionally in a viscous isotropic fluid\, i.e.\, \\\(F = fu\\\)."
comment: "More generally, \(\boldsymbol{f}\) is defined as the tensor that correlates the vectorial frictional force, \(\boldsymbol{F}\), on a body in a viscous fluid and the vectorial velocity, \(\boldsymbol{u}\) , with \(\boldsymbol{F} = \boldsymbol{f}\boldsymbol{u}\). However, the more general definition is not needed in polymer science as experimental determinations of the translational frictional coefficient all employ situations in which \(\boldsymbol{F}\) and \(\boldsymbol{u}\) are collinear and \(F = fu\)."
comment: "\(f\) is related to the translational diffusion coefficient, \(D\), of an isolated body by the Einstein equation \(D = kT/f\), where \(k\) is the Boltzmann constant and \(T\) the thermodynamic temperature."
synonym: "frictional coefficient (in polymer science)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12247

[Term]
id: goldbook:12247
name: translational diffusion coefficient
def: "Proportionality constant relating the flux per unit area\, \\\(J_\{n\}\\\)\, in unidirectional flow of amount\, \\\(n\\\)\, of entities \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\) to their concentration gradient in the direction \(\\\(x\\\)\) of flow\, \\\(\{\\rm\{d\}\}c_\{\\ce\{B\}\}/\{\\rm\{d\}\}x\\\)\, i.e.\, \\\(J_\{n\} = -D\{\\rm\{d\}\} c_\{\\ce\{B\}\}/\{\\rm\{d\}\}x\\\)."
comment: "More generally, \(D\) is defined using vectorial flow as the proportionality constant, relating the flux per unit area, \(\boldsymbol{J_{n}}\) , of amount, \(n\), of entities \(\ce{B}\) to their concentration gradient, \(\boldsymbol{\nabla} c_{\ce{B}}\), i.e., \(J_{n} = -D \boldsymbol{\nabla} c_{\ce{B}}\). However, the more general definition is not needed in polymer science as experimental determinations of the translational diffusion coefficient all employ unidirectional flow."
synonym: "diffusion coefficient (in polymer science)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12248
name: rotational frictional coefficient
def: "Torque\, \\\(T\\\)\, per unit angular velocity\, \\\(\\omega\\\)\, required for rotation of a body about a given axis in a viscous isotropic fluid\, i.e.\, \\\(T = \\zeta\\omega\\\)."
comment: "A body whose shape is described by principal axes, \(\rm{a}\), \(\rm{b}\), and \(\rm{c}\), of different lengths has three different rotational frictional coefficients denoted by \(\zeta_{\rm{a}}\), \(\zeta_{\rm{b}}\), and \(\zeta_{\rm{c}}\), relating to rotation about the axes \(\rm{a}\), \(\rm{b}\), and \(\rm{c}\), respectively, and three different rotational diffusion coefficients, \(\mathit{\Theta}_{\rm{a}}\), \(\mathit{\Theta}_{\rm{b}}\), and \(\mathit{\Theta}_{\rm{c}}\), where, for an isolated body in a viscous isotropic fluid, \(\mathit{\Theta}_{\rm{a}} = kT/\zeta_{\rm{a}}\), \(\mathit{\Theta}_{\rm{b}} = kT/\zeta_{\rm{b}}\), and \(\mathit{\Theta}_{\rm{c}} = kT/\zeta_{\rm{c}}\)."
comment: "\(\zeta\) is related to the rotational diffusion coefficient, \(\mathit{\Theta}\), of an isolated body in a viscous isotropic fluid by the equation \(\mathit{\Theta} = kT/\zeta\), where \(k\) is the Boltzmann constant and \(T\) the absolute temperature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12249
name: equilibrium sedimentation method
def: "Experimental method by which the distribution of the concentration of the solute or dispersed component in a dilute solution or dispersion along the centrifuge cell is measured at sedimentation equilibrium\, and the results are interpreted in terms of the molar masses of the solute species or their distribution functions\, or both."
synonym: "sedimentation-equilibrium method" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12214
consider: goldbook:12227

[Term]
id: goldbook:12250
name: equilibrium sedimentation in a density gradient
def: "Equilibrium sedimentation method using a multicomponent solvent forming a density gradient in a centrifugal field."
comment: "Equilibrium sedimentation in a density gradient can be used to determine the compositional heterogeneity of copolymers."
synonym: "sedimentation equilibrium in a density gradient" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12249

[Term]
id: goldbook:12251
name: Kraemer equation
def: "Equation describing the dependence of the inherent viscosity\, \\\(\\eta_\{\\rm\{inh\}\}\\\)\, of a dilute solution on the mass concentration of the solute\, \\\(c\\\)\, with \\\[\\eta_\{\\rm\{inh\}\} = \(\\ln \\eta_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\)/c = \[\\eta\] + k_\{\\rm\{K\}\}\[\\eta\]^\{2\} c\\\] where \\\(k_\{\\rm\{K\}\}\\\) is the Kraemer coefficient and \\\(\[\\eta\]\\\) is the intrinsic viscosity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12227

[Term]
id: goldbook:12252
name: Kraemer coefficient
def: "Parameter in the Kraemer equation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12251

[Term]
id: goldbook:12253
name: hydrodynamic interaction
def: "In a solution or dispersion\, the perturbation of the flow of the solvent continuum or dispersing medium continuum around a solute molecule\, a segment of a dissolved macromolecule or dispersed entity caused by the presence of the other solute molecules\, segments\, or dispersed entities."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12254
name: free-draining
def: "Adjective describing the undisturbed flow of solvent through the domain of a dissolved macromolecule."
comment: "Free-draining flow occurs in the limit of zero hydrodynamic interaction."
synonym: "freely draining" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12253

[Term]
id: goldbook:12255
name: impermeable
def: "Adjective describing the flow behaviour of a macromolecule in solution or a dispersed entity when\, due to hydrodynamic interaction\, the solvent or dispersion medium within the domain of the macromolecule or dispersed entity is essentially immobilised and moves with the dissolved macromolecule or dispersed entity."
synonym: "non-free-draining" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12253

[Term]
id: goldbook:12256
name: partial free-draining
def: "Adjective describing the flow behaviour of a macromolecule in solution or a dispersed entity when\, due to hydrodynamic interaction\, the solvent within the domain of the macromolecule or a dispersed entity becomes progressively more immobilised with respect to the macromolecule or a dispersed entity in the direction from its outer fringes inward."
comment: "Free-draining and impermeable behaviour are two extremes of the concept of partial free-draining behaviour."
synonym: "partially draining" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12253
consider: goldbook:12254
consider: goldbook:12255

[Term]
id: goldbook:12257
name: equivalent hydrodynamic volume
def: "Volume of the hydrodynamically equivalent sphere."
comment: "The molar equivalent hydrodynamic volume determined using measurements of intrinsic viscosity, \([\eta]\), is \(V_{\eta}\), where \(V_{\eta} = [\eta]M/N_{\rm{A}}\), with \(M\) the molar mass and \(N_{\rm{A}}\) the Avogadro constant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12258
name: equivalent hydrodynamic radius
def: "Radius of the hydrodynamically equivalent sphere."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12259
name: Stokes equation
def: "For an isolated dissolved molecule or dispersed entity\, an equation relating the translational frictional coefficient\, \\\(f\\\)\, to the equivalent hydrodynamic radius in translational diffusive flow\, \\\(r_\{D\}\\\)\, and to the viscosity of the solvent continuum or the dispersion medium continuum\, \\\(η_\{0\}\\\)\, with \\\[f = 6\\uppi \\eta_\{0\}r_\{D\}\\\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12246
consider: goldbook:12258

[Term]
id: goldbook:12260
name: Stokes–Einstein equation
def: "For an isolated dissolved molecule or dispersed entity\, an equation relating the translational diffusion coefficient\, \\\(D\\\)\, to the equivalent hydrodynamic radius in translational diffusive flow\, \\\(r_\{D\}\\\) \, and to the viscosity of the solvent continuum or the dispersion medium continuum\, \\\(\\eta_\{0\}\\\)\, with \\\[D = kT/\(6\\uppi \\eta_\{0\}r_\{D\}\)\\\] where \\\(k\\\) is the Boltzmann constant\, and \\\(T\\\) the thermodynamic temperature."
comment: "The Stokes–Einstein equation is derived by combining the Stokes equation with the Einstein equation \(D = kT/f\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12246
consider: goldbook:12247
consider: goldbook:12258

[Term]
id: goldbook:12261
name: Perrin equation
def: "For an isolated dissolved molecule or dispersed entity\, an equation relating the rotational diffusion coefficient\, \\\(\\mathit\{\\Theta\}\\\)\, to the equivalent hydrodynamic radius in rotational diffusive flow\, \\\(r_\{\\mathit\{\\Theta\}\}\\\)\, and to the viscosity of the solvent continuum or the dispersion medium continuum\, \\\(\\eta_\{0\}\\\)\, with \\\[D = kT/\(6\\pi \\eta_\{\\rm\{0\}\} r_\{\\mathit\{\\Theta\}\}^3\)\\\] where \\\(k\\\) is the Boltzmann constant and \\\(T\\\) the thermodynamic temperature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12258

[Term]
id: goldbook:12262
name: pearl-necklace model
def: "Model describing the flow behaviour of a dissolved chain macromolecule in terms of a freely jointed sequence of beads\, each of which offers hydrodynamic resistance to the flow of the surrounding solvent continuum and is connected to the next bead by a rigid rod that offers no hydrodynamic resistance."
synonym: "bead-rod model" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12263
name: Kirkwood–Riseman theory
def: "Theory\, based on the pearl-necklace model\, that describes the translational diffusive and viscous flows of an isolated linear macromolecule in solution in the theta state and accounts for the gradual change from free-draining behaviour at lower molecular weights to impermeable behaviour at higher molecular weights."
comment: "The Kirkwood–Riseman theory is usually applied in the impermeable limit when it essentially relates the equivalent hydrodynamic radius to the root-mean-square unperturbed radius of gyration, \(\lt\!s_{\circ}^{2}\!\gt\), with \[r_{D} = 0.675 \lt\!s_{\circ}^{2}\!\gt^{1/2}\] and \[r_{\eta} = 0.256 \lt\!s_{\circ}^{2}\!\gt^{1/2}\] where \(r_{D}\) and \(r_{\eta}\) are the equivalent hydrodynamic radii in translational diffusive flow and viscous flow."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12193
consider: goldbook:12254
consider: goldbook:12255
consider: goldbook:12258
consider: goldbook:12262

[Term]
id: goldbook:12264
name: Flory–Fox assumption
def: "Assumption that the Kirkwood–Riseman theory can be applied to linear isolated macromolecules in solution\, independent of whether they are in the theta state."
comment: "The Kirkwood–Riseman relationships between \(r_{D}\) and \(r_{\eta}\) and the root-mean-square radius of gyration, \(\lt\!s^{2}\!\gt\), are then \[r_{D} = 0.675 \lt\!s^{2}\!\gt^{1/2} = 0.675 \lt\!s_{\circ}^{2}\!\gt^{1/2} \alpha_{D}\] and \[r_{\eta} = 0.256 \lt\!s^{2}\!\gt^{1/2} = 0.256 \lt\!s_{\circ}^{2}\!\gt^{1/2} \alpha_{\eta}\] where \(r_{D}\) and \(r_{\eta}\) are the equivalent hydrodynamic radii in translational diffusive flow and viscous flow, and \(\alpha_{D}\) and \(\alpha_{\eta}\) are the corresponding expansion factors."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12191
consider: goldbook:12258
consider: goldbook:12263

[Term]
id: goldbook:12265
name: Flory–Fox equation
def: "Equation relating intrinsic viscosity\, \\\(\\eta\\\)\, and molar mass\, \\\(M\\\)\, to the mean-square radius of gyration\, with \\\[\[\\eta\]M = \\mathit\{\\Phi\}^\{\\prime\}\\!\\lt\\!s^\{2\}\\!\\gt^\{3/2\}\\\] where \\\(\\mathit\{\\Phi\}^\{\\prime\}\\\) is a parameter the value of which depends on the molar-mass distribution\, macromolecular constitution\, and chain expansion."
comment: "For a solution in the theta state, \(\mathit{\Phi}^{\prime}\) is denoted \(\mathit{\Phi}_{\uptheta}^{\prime}\) and its value is given by the Kirkwood–Riseman theory, with \(\mathit{\Phi}_{\uptheta}^{\prime} = \pu{4.22E22 mol-1}\)."
comment: "The Flory–Fox equation is sometimes written in terms of \(\lt\!r^{2}\!\gt\), the mean-square end-to-end distance, instead of \(\lt\!s^{2}\!\gt\), with \[[\eta]M = \mathit{\Phi} \lt\!r^{2}\!\gt^{3/2}\] where \(\mathit{\Phi} = \mathit{\Phi}^{\prime}/6^{3/2}\). The latter equality assumes that \(\lt\!r^{2}\!\gt = 6\!\lt\!s^{2}\!\gt\), which is only exactly true in the theta state. In this case, \[[\eta]M = \mathit{\Phi}_{\theta}\!\lt\!r^{2}\!\gt^{3/2}\] where \(\mathit{\Phi}_{\theta} = \mathit{\Phi}_{\theta}/6^{3/2} = \pu{2.87E21 mol-1}\)."
comment: "\([\eta]M/N_{\rm{A}}\), where \(N_{\rm{A}}\) is the Avogadro constant, is the equivalent hydrodynamic volume in viscous flow, \(V_{\eta}\), with \(V_{\eta} = 4\uppi r_{\eta}^{3}/3\), Hence, the Flory–Fox equation is consistent with the Kirkwood–Riseman theory and the Flory–Fox assumption. (See Notes to Kirkwood–Riseman theory and Flory–Fox assumption.)"
comment: "\(\mathit{\Phi}\) is known as the viscosity function or the Flory function."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12192
consider: goldbook:12197
consider: goldbook:12257
consider: goldbook:12263
consider: goldbook:12264

[Term]
id: goldbook:12266
name: Rouse theory
def: "Molecular theory for treating polymer chain dynamics based on the bead-spring model assuming the beads \(segments\) have zero excluded volume and there is no hydrodynamic interaction between the beads."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12253

[Term]
id: goldbook:12267
name: Rouse chain
def: "Hypothetical polymer chain satisfying the assumptions made in the Rouse theory."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12266

[Term]
id: goldbook:12268
name: reptation
def: "Snake-like movement of a polymer chain in a semi-dilute or concentrated solution or bulk amorphous polymer through the hypothetical tube created by neighbouring chains."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12228
consider: goldbook:12229

[Term]
id: goldbook:12269
name: tube model
def: "Model to describe the motion of a polymer chain confined in the hypothetical tube created by neighbouring chains."
comment: "In the tube model, the polymer chain moves along the hypothetical tube defined by the neighbouring polymer chains. The tube is continually undergoing tube renewal."
comment: "The tube model is an essential concept for reptation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12268
consider: goldbook:12270

[Term]
id: goldbook:12270
name: tube renewal
def: "Dynamic renewal of tubes by the disentanglement and re-entanglement of polymer chains."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12271
name: primitive chain
def: "Polymer chain allowed to undergo reptation along the tube created by neighbouring chains."
comment: "The chain can be depicted as a connected sequence of blobs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12232
consider: goldbook:12268

[Term]
id: goldbook:12272
name: uniform dispersion
def: "Dispersion of particles of identical size\, shape\, and constitution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12273
name: non-uniform dispersion
def: "Dispersion of particles not identical with respect to size\, shape\, or constitution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12274
name: static light scattering
def: "Experimental method based on the measurement of the time-averaged intensity of light scattered from a polymer solutions or a dispersion of particles at various angles with respect to the incident beam."
comment: "Measurement of the angular dependence of the time-averaged intensity of light scattered from a dilute solution of macromolecules or a dilute dispersion of particles that are not negligibly small with respect to the wavelength of the incident light can be used to evaluate an average radius of gyration of the solute macromolecules or dispersed particles."
comment: "Measurement of the concentration dependence of the intensity of light scattered from a dilute solution of macromolecules or a dilute dispersion of particles yields information on the thermodynamic interaction between the solute and solvent or dispersed particles and dispersion medium in terms of the second osmotic virial coefficient and, less frequently, higher virial coefficients."
comment: "SLS is an absolute method, i.e., one not requiring calibration, for the determination of the molar mass of a macromolecular substance or dispersion of particles."
synonym: "SLS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12214
consider: goldbook:12227
consider: goldbook:12239

[Term]
id: goldbook:12275
name: dynamic light scattering
def: "Experimental method based on the measurement of the time autocorrelation function of the intensity of light scattered from a polymer solution or a dispersion of particles."
comment: "The basic information that can be obtained from the time autocorrelation function of a polymer solution or a dispersion is: (i) for a uniform polymer or a uniform dispersion, the diffusion coefficient of the macromolecules or the dispersed particles; (ii) for a non-uniform polymer or a non-uniform dispersion, the distribution function of diffusion coefficients of the macromolecules or the dispersed particles."
synonym: "DLS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "photon-correlation spectroscopy (PCS)" []
synonym: "quasi-elastic light scattering (QELS)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12272
consider: goldbook:12273

[Term]
id: goldbook:12276
name: small molecule
def: "Molecule much smaller than the wavelength of the radiation in the solvent used."
comment: "For a molecule to be considered to be small, the lengths of all of its dimensions must be less than about one-twentieth of the wavelength employed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12277
name: large molecule
def: "Molecule of size similar to or larger than the wavelength of the radiation in the solvent used."
comment: "A molecule is treated as large if the length of its largest dimension exceeds about one-twentieth of the wavelength employed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12278
name: excess scattering
def: "Difference between the scattering intensity for a dilute solution or a dilute dispersion and that for the pure solvent or the dispersion medium at the same scattering angle."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12227

[Term]
id: goldbook:12279
name: static structure factor
def: "Function describing the dependence of relative scattering intensity on the magnitude of the scattering vector\, \\\(q\\\)\, for a polymer solution or a dispersion."
comment: "The static structure factor accounts for interference of the scattered radiation within individual macromolecules or individual dispersed particles, described by the form factor, as well as interference of the scattered radiation from different macromolecules or dispersed particles, reflecting the ordering of the positions of the scattering entities."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12280
name: dynamic structure factor
def: "Function describing the temporal dependence of relative scattering intensity on the magnitude of the scattering vector\, \\\(q\\\)."
comment: "The value of the dynamic structure factor is characteristic of the various modes of motions of the polymer molecules or the dispersed particles and their parts and is also characteristic of the time-dependent interference of scattering, reflecting ordering of the positions of the scattering entities in time. In dynamic light scattering, it can be derived from the time autocorrelation function."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12275

[Term]
id: goldbook:12281
name: elution time
def: "Time elapsed from the injection of the sample into a chromatography bed to the recording of a specified signal of the detector due to the sample having passed through the bed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12282
name: elution volume
def: "Volume of solvent that has passed through a chromatography bed from the injection of the sample to the recording of a specified signal of the detector due to the sample having passed through the bed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12283
name: transfer coefficient
def: "The anodic transfer coefficient \\\(\\alpha_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\) and the cathodic transfer coefficient \\\(\\alpha_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\\) are defined by the following equations\: \\\[\\alpha_\{\\rm\{a\}\} = \(RT/F\)\(\{\\rm\{d\}\}\\ln\\! j_\{\\rm\{a\}\}/\{\\rm\{d\}\}E\); \\quad \\alpha_\{\\rm\{c\}\} = -\(RT/F\)\(\{\\rm\{d\}\}\\ln\\!\\vert \{j_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\} \\vert /\{\\rm\{d\}\}E\)\\\] In these equations\, \\\(j_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\) and \\\(j_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\\) are the anodic and cathodic current densities\, respectively\, corrected for any changes in the reactant concentration at the electrode surface with respect to its bulk value; incidentally\, the symbols \\\(\\ln\\! j_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\) and \\\(\\ln\\!\\vert j_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\vert\\\) imply that the argument of the logarithm is of dimension one\, obtained by division with the corresponding unit\, e.g.\, \\\(\\ln\\! j_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\) meaning \\\(\\ln\(j_\{\\rm\{a\}\}/\\pu\{A m^\{-2\}\}\)\\\)\, and similarly for the other quantities \\\(\\vert j_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\vert\\\)\, \\\(k_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\) and \\\(k_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\\). \\\(E\\\) is the applied electric potential\, \\\(R\\\) is the gas constant\, \\\(T\\\) is the thermodynamic temperature\, and \\\(F\\\) is the Faraday constant. In practice\, \\\(\\alpha_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\) and \\\(\\alpha_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\\) are defined as the reciprocal of the corresponding Tafel slopes\, \\\(\{\\rm\{d\}\}E/\{\\rm\{d\}\}\\ln\\! j_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\) and \\\(-\{\\rm\{d\}\}E/\{\\rm\{d\}\} \\ln\\! \\vert j_\{\\rm\{c\}\} \\vert\\\)\, made dimensionless by the multiplying factor \\\(RT/F\\\). Both the transfer coefficient and the Tafel slope are determined at constant temperature and pressure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2014-5025
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12284
name: combined technique
def: "Application of two or more techniques to different samples at the same time. This can include thermal and nonthermal analytical techniques."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12306

[Term]
id: goldbook:12285
name: controlled-rate thermal analysis
def: "Sample-controlled method where the feedback used to control the heating is the rate of transformation."
synonym: "CRTA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12286
name: controlled temperature program
def: "Temperature history imposed on the sample during the course of the thermal analysis experiment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12287
name: cooling curve
def: "Experimental result of measuring the temperature of the sample as a function of time during cooling. Heating curves are obtained for temperature-time experiments during heating."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12288
name: derivative technique
def: "Pertaining to the \\\(1^\{\\rm\{st\}\}\\\) derivative \(mathematical\) of any curve with respect to temperature or time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12289
name: dielectric thermal analysis
def: "Technique where dielectric properties are measured."
synonym: "DEA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12290
name: differential technique
def: "Pertaining to a difference in measured or measurable quantities usually between a sample and a reference or standard material."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12291
name: heat-flow differential scanning calorimetry
def: "Technique where the difference between the heat-flow rates into a sample and a reference material is measured."
synonym: "DSC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "heat-flow DSC" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12292
name: power compensation differential scanning calorimetry
def: "Technique where the difference between the electrical powers into a sample and a reference material is measured."
synonym: "DSC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "power compensation DSC" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12293
name: dynamic technique
def: "Indicates\, especially in the mechanical analysis of materials\, that a parameter changes continuously during the experiment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12307

[Term]
id: goldbook:12294
name: dynamic mechanical analysis
def: "Technique where storage and loss viscoelastic moduli are determined with the help of a periodical stress."
synonym: "DMA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12295
name: gas flow
def: "Passage of gas from one part of the system to another. The gas may be either inert \(carrier gas\) or reactive\, either introduced into the system or evolving from the sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12296
name: isothermal technique
def: "Applied to a technique to indicate that the temperature is maintained constant throughout the experiment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12297
name: material
def: "The substance which is studied and from which the sample is taken."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12298
name: micro- technique
def: "Prefix used to denote that the technique measures small quantities\, either with respect to the amount of sample studied\, or with respect to the change in the properties measured."
comment: "Mathematically, micro = \(\upmu\) = \(\pu{E-6}\)."
comment: "The opposite prefix, macro-, is also occasionally used."
comment: "This prefix has been applied to many thermal methods, and the equipment associated with them, for example, microbalance, microreactor, microcalorimeter and also to the technique itself: microthermal, microscopic, and the property studied: microstructural."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12299
name: modulated technique
def: "Indicates that a parameter changes in a periodic manner during the experiment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12300
name: modulated temperature technique
def: "Applied to the technique name to indicate that a temperature modulation has been applied to the temperature program."
comment: "The prefix TM is occasionally used instead, but not recommended."
synonym: "MT" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12301
name: photo- technique
def: "Indicates that the experiment involves the illumination of the sample or measures the amount of light emitted from a sample. Where possible\, the wavelength range of the light should be specified."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12302
name: sample controlled technique
def: "Applied to the technique to indicate that a property of the sample is used either continuously or discontinuously to control the sample heating. Without this term\, it is assumed that the experiment is following a controlled-temperature program."
comment: "The generic term for all TA techniques making use of such feedback is sample-controlled TA (SCTA), whereas specific names will be of the form sample-controlled TGA (SC-TGA), etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12303
name: scan
def: "A term used to describe the data produced from a thermal analysis experiment. More correct usage is a thermal analysis curve\, or\, for a specific technique thermogravimetric curve\, etc."
comment: "This term is discouraged."
synonym: "thermal analysis curve" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12304
name: scanning technique
def: "Indicates that a specified experimental parameter\, if not temperature\, is changed in a controlled manner."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12305
name: scanning calorimetry
def: "Techniques where heat is measured as a function of temperature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12306
name: simultaneous technique
def: "Indicates the measurement of two or more properties of a single sample at the same time."
comment: "A hyphen is used to separate the abbreviations of the techniques; for example, simultaneous measurement of mass and heat flow rate (thermogravimetric analysis and differential scanning calorimetry) would be TGA-DSC."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12284

[Term]
id: goldbook:12307
name: static technique
def: "Indicates\, especially in the mechanical analysis of materials\, a constant parameter during the experiment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12293

[Term]
id: goldbook:12308
name: stepwise technique
def: "Indicates discrete\, discontinuous changes in an experimental parameter\, e.g.\, force\, temperature\, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12309
name: tan $\\delta$
def: "The dimensionless ratio of energy lost to energy returned during one cycle of a periodic process."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12294

[Term]
id: goldbook:12310
name: temperature-programmed desorption
def: "EGA using an inert atmosphere or vacuum\, in the absence of sample decomposition."
synonym: "TPD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12311
name: temperature-programmed oxidation
def: "Experiment using an oxidising atmosphere\, usually oxygen. Oxidation is monitored by any appropriate technique \(EGA\, TGA\, gas sorption\, etc.\)."
synonym: "TPO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12312
name: temperature-programmed reduction
def: "Experiment using a reducing atmosphere\, usually hydrogen. Reduction is monitored by any appropriate technique \(EGA\, TGA\, gas sorption\, etc.\)."
synonym: "TPR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12313
name: thermal curve
def: "Any graph of any combination of property\, time\, temperature derived from a thermal analysis technique."
comment: "Thermal curve is a loose abbreviation of the more correct term thermoanalytical curve."
comment: "This term is discouraged."
synonym: "thermoanalytical curve" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12314
name: thermally stimulated current
def: "Electrical current observed during heating and caused by the thermally initiated relaxation of the frozen-in electrical polarization of a sample."
comment: "By extension, the same name and abbreviation (TSC) are given to the thermal analysis technique based on the measurement of this current."
synonym: "TSC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12315

[Term]
id: goldbook:12315
name: thermally stimulated depolarisation
def: "Relaxation of frozen-in electrical polarization caused by a temperature increase."
comment: "The effect is measured through the thermally stimulated current."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12314

[Term]
id: goldbook:12316
name: thermo- technique
def: "Indicating the use of changing temperature during the experiment\, when in the name of a thermal analysis technique."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12317
name: thermoanalytical
def: "Of\, or pertaining to\, thermal analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12318
name: thermodiffractometry
def: "A technique where the X-ray diffraction of the sample is measured."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12319
name: thermogravimetric analysis
def: "A technique where the mass of the sample is measured\, also known as thermogravimetry."
synonym: "TGA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "thermogravimetry (TG)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12320
name: thermomanometry
def: "A technique where the gas pressure is measured."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12321
name: thermomechanical analysis
def: "A technique where the deformation of the sample is measured under constant load."
synonym: "TMA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12322
name: thermomicroscopy
def: "A technique where the optical properties of the sample are observed and measured through a microscope."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12323
name: thermospectrometry
def: "A group of techniques where a spectrum of the sample is measured."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12324
name: absolute quantitation of proteins
def: "Method for absolute quantitation of proteins via measurements on constituent proteolytic peptides using chemically synthesized isotope-labeled peptides as surrogate internal standards for mass spectrometry."
synonym: "AQUA" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12589

[Term]
id: goldbook:12325
name: accelerating potential
def: "Electrical potential difference used to impart translational energy to ions."
comment: "Accelerating voltage is often used as a synonym, but the terms are equivalent only in the case of a static accelerating potential."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12326
name: accurate mass
def: "Experimentally determined mass of an ion of known charge."
comment: "Accurate mass and exact mass are not synonymous. Accurate mass refers to a measured mass, and exact mass refers to a calculated mass."
comment: "Can be used to determine elemental composition to within limits defined by both the accuracy and precision of the measurement."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12407

[Term]
id: goldbook:12327
name: accurate mass tag
def: "Value of the mass of a peptide from a protein that has been chemically or enzymatically cleaved into fragments. The mass is recorded with sufficiently high accuracy and precision that it can be used in identification of the protein."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12522

[Term]
id: goldbook:12328
name: a-ion
def: "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\\(\\ce\{C-C\}\\\) bond."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12329
name: alkyl cation
def: "Even-electron positively charged saturated hydrocarbon ion containing no aromatic groups\, a special case of carbenium ions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12330
name: all-glass heated inlet system
def: "All-glass inlet system for ion sources operating under vacuum that can be heated to about \\\(\\pu\{500^\{\\circ\}C\}\\\) and allows low vapor pressure materials to be introduced into the mass spectrometer without breaking vacuum."
synonym: "AGHIS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12331
name: allyl cation
def: "Even-electron ion formulated as \\\(\\ce\{R^\{1\}R^\{2\}C=CR^\{3\}C+R^\{4\}R^\{5\}\}\\\) and its resonance forms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12332
name: ambient ionization
def: "Desorption of molecules and formation of ions outside the mass spectrometer directly from samples in their native environment with no or minimal sample preparation."
comment: ""Direct analysis in real time" is a proprietary term indicating the formation of ions from a solid or liquid sample at atmospheric pressure through the interaction of a gas stream containing internally excited atoms or molecules with the surface. The excited-state species are typically formed in a glow discharge in helium or nitrogen. The term should only be used to describe the commercial product."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12333
name: ambient mass spectrometry
def: "Mass spectrometry analysis performed using an ambient ionization technique."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12332

[Term]
id: goldbook:12334
name: angle resolved mass spectrometry
def: "Technique used to investigate details of the collisional excitation process by studying trends relating scattering angle of the precursor ion\, internal energy transferred\, and the masses of the ion and its collision partner."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12335
name: anionized molecule
def: "Ion formed by the association of an anion with a molecule\, \\\(\\ce\{M\}\\\)."
comment: "The terms quasi-molecular ion and pseudo-molecular ion are deprecated and should not be used in place of anionized molecule."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12336
name: atmospheric pressure chemical ionization
def: "Chemical ionization of a sample that is a gas or nebulized liquid\, using an atmospheric pressure corona discharge or beta emitter such as \\\(\\ce\{^\{63\}Ni\}\\\)."
synonym: "APCI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12373

[Term]
id: goldbook:12337
name: atmospheric pressure matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization
def: "Matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization in which the sample target is at atmospheric pressure."
synonym: "AP MALDI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12338
name: atmospheric pressure photoionization
def: "Direct ionization of molecules at atmospheric pressure by electron detachment induced by photons forming \\\(\\ce\{M^\{+.\}\}\\\)\, or atmospheric pressure chemical ionization in which the reactant ions are generated by photoionization of suitable dopant species and subsequent ion/molecule reactions of their molecular ions."
synonym: "APPI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12336

[Term]
id: goldbook:12339
name: autodetachment
def: "Process whereby a negative ion in a discrete state with energy greater than the detachment threshold loses an electron spontaneously without further interaction with an energy source."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12340
name: auxiliary gas
def: "Gas used in a spray ion source in addition to the nebulizing gas to aid in solvent removal."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12365

[Term]
id: goldbook:12341
name: average mass
def: "Mass of an ion or molecule weighted for its isotopic composition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12495

[Term]
id: goldbook:12342
name: axial ejection
def: "Ejection of an ion from an ion trap in a direction parallel to the longitudinal axis of the trap."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12447

[Term]
id: goldbook:12343
name: axialization
def: "Technique used in Fourier-transform ion cyclotron resonance mass spectrometers to limit the translational motion of the trapped ions so that they occupy a small volume near the trap center\, thus optimizing performance criteria including resolving power."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12344
name: base peak chromatogram
def: "Chromatogram obtained by plotting the signal of the ions represented by the base peak detected in each of a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of retention time."
comment: "This term should be used for samples introduced following a chromatographic separation."
synonym: "BPC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "base peak ion chromatogram" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12345
name: beam mass spectrometer
def: "Mass spectrometer in which an ion beam accelerated from the ion source is transmitted through a m/z analyzer\, or analyzers\, to the detector."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12346
name: benzyl ion
def: "Even-electron ion \\\(\\ce\{C7H7^\{+\}\}\\\) with the same carbon skeleton as toluene that has lost a hydrogen atom from the methyl side-chain that carries the positive charge."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12597

[Term]
id: goldbook:12347
name: b-ion
def: "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\\(\\ce\{C-N\}\\\) bond."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12348
name: blackbody infrared radiative dissociation
def: "Special case of infrared multiphoton dissociation wherein excitation of the reactant ion is caused by absorption of infrared photons radiating from heated blackbody surroundings\, which are usually the walls of a vacuum chamber."
synonym: "BIRD" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12433

[Term]
id: goldbook:12349
name: Brubaker lens
def: "Additional set of four short\, cylindrical electrodes\, mounted co-linearly with a transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer that is excited with some fraction of the AC potential but not the DC potential applied to the main quadrupole. The Brubaker lens thus acts as a high-pass filter for ion m/z\, but the resulting delay in application of the DC potential component also results in a reduction in defocusing by fringe fields and thus significantly improves overall ion transmission efficiency at a given mass resolution."
synonym: "Brubaker pre-filter" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12420
consider: goldbook:12601
consider: goldbook:12602

[Term]
id: goldbook:12350
name: buffer gas
def: "Inert gas used for collisional reduction of the internal or translational energy of ions\, such as in ion traps."
synonym: "bath gas" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12362
consider: goldbook:12447

[Term]
id: goldbook:12351
name: centroid acquisition
def: "Procedure of recording mass spectra in which an automated computer-based system detects peaks\, calculates the centroid based on the average m/z value weighted by the intensity\, and assigns m/z values based on a calibration file. Only the centroid m/z value and the peak magnitude are stored."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12536

[Term]
id: goldbook:12352
name: charged residue model
def: "Theoretical model for production of highly charged macromolecules by electrospray ionization in which the excess charges on electrosprayed droplets are transferred to and remain on molecules enclosed within the droplets after solvent evaporation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12438

[Term]
id: goldbook:12353
name: charge inversion reaction
def: "Reaction of an ion with a neutral\, surface\, or ion of opposite polarity\, in which the charge on the product ion is reversed in sign with respect to the reactant ion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12354
name: charge-mediated fragmentation
def: "Fragmentation of an ion in which the cleavage of one of its bonds is induced by the charge site. The cleaved bond is adjacent to the apparent charge site\, and its cleavage involves movement of the electron pair forming that bond to the original charge site and thus migration of the charge to the released fragment."
synonym: "heterolytic fragmentation; inductive cleavage" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12355

[Term]
id: goldbook:12355
name: charge remote fragmentation
def: "Fragmentation of an ion in which the cleaved bond is isolated from the apparent charge site by a distance of several bond lengths."
synonym: "CRF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12354

[Term]
id: goldbook:12356
name: charge site derivatization
def: "Chemical derivatization of molecules to introduce a fixed charge site\, thus improving ionization efficiency by electrospray ionization or matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization and directing subsequent ion fragmentation in a manner that facilitates structure identification."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12357
name: c-ion
def: "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\\(\\ce\{N-C\}\\\) bond."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12358
name: coaxial reflectron
def: "Reflectron that is arranged such that its main axis is coaxial with the ion source and first stage of the time-of-flight analyzer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12359
name: collector slit
def: "Slit installed in a magnetic sector mass spectrometer to allow only those m/z separated ions with a specific m/z into the detector system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12473

[Term]
id: goldbook:12360
name: collisional focusing
def: "Effect where collisions with a buffer gas in a radio-frequency ion trap or transmission quadrupole causes ions to lose translational energy and concentrate at the center of the trap or axis of the linear quadrupole. The effect increases with gas pressure up to a point where ion scattering becomes the dominant process."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12350
consider: goldbook:12447
consider: goldbook:12602

[Term]
id: goldbook:12361
name: collision cell
def: "Chamber in the ion path between m/z separation elements\, or between ion source acceleration region and the first analyzer\, in tandem mass spectrometry in space configurations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12364
consider: goldbook:12591

[Term]
id: goldbook:12362
name: collision gas
def: "Inert gas used for collisional excitation or a reactive gas used for ion/molecule reactions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12350

[Term]
id: goldbook:12363
name: collision quadrupole
def: "Transmission quadrupole to which an oscillating radio frequency potential is applied so as to focus a beam of ions through a collision gas or buffer gas with no m/z separation other than low m/z cut-off."
comment: "Higher-order multipoles can also be used in this manner."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12350
consider: goldbook:12362
consider: goldbook:12560
consider: goldbook:12602

[Term]
id: goldbook:12364
name: collision reaction cell
def: "Collision cell for removal of interfering ions by ion/neutral reactions in inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry."
synonym: "CRC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12361

[Term]
id: goldbook:12365
name: concentric nebulizer
def: "Pneumatic nebulizer in which the liquid flows through a central capillary and dispersion gas flows through a surrounding outer tube."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12366
name: consecutive reaction monitoring
def: "Multiple-stage mass spectrometry experiment with three or more stages of m/z separation in which products of sequential fragmentation or bimolecular reactions are selected for detection."
synonym: "CRM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12500
consider: goldbook:12501

[Term]
id: goldbook:12367
name: constant neutral mass gain spectrum
def: "Spectrum formed of all precursor ions that have undergone a selected m/z increase corresponding to the mass of a particular neutral species divided by the charge number of the precursor. The ions detected are the product ions produced by gain of a preselected neutral species mass following ion/molecule reactions of the precursor ions with a reactant gas in a collision cell."
synonym: "fixed neutral gain spectrum" []
synonym: "fixed neutral mass gain spectrum" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12361
consider: goldbook:12368

[Term]
id: goldbook:12368
name: constant neutral mass loss spectrum
def: "Spectrum of all precursor ions that have undergone a selected m/z decrement corresponding to the mass of a particular neutral divided by the charge number of the precursor. The ions detected are the product ions produced by loss of a preselected neutral mass following collision-induced dissociation of the precursor ions in a collision cell."
synonym: "fixed neutral loss spectrum" []
synonym: "fixed neutral mass loss spectrum" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12361
consider: goldbook:12367

[Term]
id: goldbook:12369
name: continuous dynode particle multiplier
def: "Ion-to-electron detector in which the ion strikes the inner surface of a continuous tube device and induces the production of secondary electrons that\, in turn\, impinge on the inner surfaces of the device to produce more secondary electrons. This avalanche effect produces an increase in the final measured current pulse."
synonym: "channel electron multiplier" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12395

[Term]
id: goldbook:12370
name: continuous-flow fast atom bombardment
def: "Variant of fast atom bombardment in which the mixture of analyte and liquid matrix is continuously supplied to the sample probe tip."
synonym: "CF-FAB" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12371
name: continuous-flow matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization
def: "Variant of matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization in which the analyte is dissolved in a liquid matrix that is continuously supplied to the sample probe tip."
synonym: "CF-MALDI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12372
name: conversion dynode
def: "Surface that is held at high potential so that ions striking the surface produce secondary charged particles that are subsequently detected."
comment: "For positive ions, the potential is negative and the secondary particles are electrons and negative ions. For negative ions, the potential is positive and the secondary particles are positive ions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12373
name: corona discharge
def: "Electric discharge generated in a gas\, usually at atmospheric pressure\, surrounding a conductor carrying a sufficiently high potential that the electric field around it ionizes the gas so as to form a plasma in the immediate vicinity of the conductor without causing complete electric breakdown or arcing."
comment: "A corona discharge can also be sustained in a liquid."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12422

[Term]
id: goldbook:12374
name: corona discharge ionization
def: "Formation of ions in a corona discharge."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12373

[Term]
id: goldbook:12375
name: counter-current gas
def: "Stream of inert gas\, often heated\, that is used in an electrospray or other spray ionization source to aid in the evaporation of solvent from the sprayed particles. The flow of the gas is in the direction opposite to that of the spray."
comment: "Curtain gas is a proprietary term used to indicate a flow of counter-current gas emanating from between two closely spaced plates each with a central orifice along the axis of a spray ionization source. The term should only be used to describe the commercial device."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12398
consider: goldbook:12579

[Term]
id: goldbook:12376
name: counter electrode
def: "Counter electrode in an electrospray ionization ion source is one of two electrodes between which the high electric potential is applied\, the other electrode being the electrospray needle."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12404

[Term]
id: goldbook:12377
name: cross-flow nebulizer
def: "Pneumatic nebulizer in which the dispersion gas flows at an angle\, usually \\\(\\pu\{90\\!^\{\\circ\}\}\\\)\, with respect to the column of liquid emerging from a capillary."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12378
name: curved field reflectron
def: "Reflectron designed to provide a decelerating field strength that varies with depth of ion penetration and thus with ion translational energy\, permitting energy focusing of ions with a range of translational energies such as those formed as product ions from post-source decay of metastable ions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12530

[Term]
id: goldbook:12379
name: cyclotron motion
def: "Circular motion of a charged particle moving perpendicularly to the direction of a magnetic field that results from the Lorentz force."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12380
name: Daly detector
def: "Detector consisting of an off-axis conversion dynode\, scintillator\, and photomultiplier. The dynode at high potential emits secondary electrons when ions impinge on the surface. The secondary electrons are accelerated onto the scintillator that produces light that is then detected by the photomultiplier detector\, which can be outside the vacuum system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12372
consider: goldbook:12446

[Term]
id: goldbook:12381
name: data-dependent acquisition
def: "Mode of data collection in tandem mass spectrometry in which a fixed number of precursor ions whose m/z values were recorded in a survey scan are selected using predetermined rules and are subjected to a second stage of mass selection in an MS/MS analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12485
consider: goldbook:12591

[Term]
id: goldbook:12382
name: deconvoluted mass spectrum
def: "Mass spectrum processed with an algorithm designed to extract a desired signal or signals from raw experimental data in which the desired signals have been complicated \(convolved\) by some interferences or in some other way."
comment: "Examples of deconvoluted mass spectra include mass spectra corrected for instrumental mass bias, or extraction of spectra for pure components from the spectrum of a mixture, or a mass (not m/z) spectrum of a biopolymer from an electrospray ionization spectrum containing peaks corresponding to several charge states."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12383
name: delayed extraction
def: "Application of the accelerating voltage pulse after a time delay in desorption ionization from a surface."
comment: "The extraction delay can produce energy focusing in a time-of-flight mass spectrometer."
synonym: "DE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12325
consider: goldbook:12386
consider: goldbook:12596

[Term]
id: goldbook:12384
name: deprotonated molecule
def: "Ion formed by the removal of a proton from a molecule \\\(\\ce\{M\}\\\) to produce an anion represented as \\\(\\ce\{\[M - H\]^\{-\}\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12385
name: desorption chemical ionization
def: "Formation of gas-phase ions by chemical ionization of gaseous molecules produced by the rapid heating and desorption of a solid or low vapour pressure liquid."
synonym: "DCI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12386
name: desorption ionization
def: "Formation of gas phase ions from a solid or liquid sample surface upon activation by heat\, strong electric field\, particles\, droplets\, or photon bombardment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12387
name: desorption ionization on silicon
def: "Soft ionization alternative to matrix-assisted desorption/ionization involving laser desorption ionization of a sample deposited on a porous silicon surface."
synonym: "DIOS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12463
consider: goldbook:12575

[Term]
id: goldbook:12388
name: diagnostic ion
def: "Product ion whose formation reveals structural or compositional information about its precursor ion."
comment: "For example, the phenyl cation in an electron ionization mass spectrum is a diagnostic ion for benzene and derivatives."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12389
name: dielectric barrier discharge ionization
def: "Atmospheric pressure chemical ionization in which the low-temperature plasma is not generated by a corona discharge but by a device consisting of two electrodes with at least one dielectric layer that separates the electrode from the plasma."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12336
consider: goldbook:12373

[Term]
id: goldbook:12390
name: d-ion
def: "High-energy fragment ion of a protonated peptide\, formally equivalent to a fragment ion formed by homolytic cleavage of a peptide \\\(\\ce\{C-N\}\\\) bond together with the part of the \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)-terminal side-chain starting at the \\\(\\ce\{\\upgamma\\mbox\{-\}carbon\}\\\) \(if any\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12391
name: direct exposure probe
def: "Device based on a modification of a direct insertion probe for exposing an involatile sample directly to the electron beam \(in an electron ionization source\) or to a chemical ionization plasma as in desorption chemical ionization."
comment: "The sample can be deposited on an inert surface or on a heater filament for rapid heating."
synonym: "DEP" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12385
consider: goldbook:12393

[Term]
id: goldbook:12392
name: direct infusion
def: "Method of liquid sample introduction in which the sample is continuously flowed into a mass spectrometer ion source."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12393
name: direct insertion probe
def: "Device for introducing a single sample of a solid or liquid\, usually contained in a quartz or other nonreactive sample holder\, into a mass spectrometer ion source."
synonym: "DIP" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12391

[Term]
id: goldbook:12394
name: direct liquid introduction
def: "Direct delivery of a liquid sample at a low solvent flow rate into the chemical ionization ion source of a mass spectrometer. The solvent vapour can act as the reagent gas."
synonym: "DLI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12546

[Term]
id: goldbook:12395
name: discrete dynode particle multiplier
def: "Ion-to-electron detector in which the ion strikes the surface of an electrode and induces the production of secondary electrons. In turn\, these impinge in sequence on dynodes at a more positive electric potential to produce more secondary electrons. This avalanche effect produces an amplification of several orders of magnitude in the final measured current pulse."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12369

[Term]
id: goldbook:12396
name: dissociative electron capture
def: "Ionization mechanism in which capture of a low-energy electron by a molecule leads directly to a dissociative state of the nascent anion\, an example of dissociative ionization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12397
name: drift tube
def: "Cylindrical chamber containing a buffer gas. Ions introduced at one end are caused to move to the other end by either a flow of the buffer gas or by a uniform longitudinal electric field."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12350

[Term]
id: goldbook:12398
name: drying gas
def: "Inert gas that is used to promote the removal of solvent from aerosol particles in spray ionization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12375
consider: goldbook:12579

[Term]
id: goldbook:12399
name: dynamic exclusion
def: "Software method used to minimize repeat selections of identical precursor ions for collision-induced dissociation in replicate chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry analyses of complex mixtures."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12381
consider: goldbook:12591

[Term]
id: goldbook:12400
name: einzel lens
def: "Three-element charged particle lens in which the first and third elements are maintained at the same electric potential. Such a lens produces focusing without changing the translational energy of the particle."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12401
name: electrohydrodynamic ionization
def: "Ionization process that produces charged droplets and gas-phase ions from a liquid under vacuum with the application of an electric field."
comment: "The process is formally equivalent to sub-ambient pressure electrospray ionization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12402
name: electron capture dissociation
def: "Process in which multiply protonated molecules interact with low-energy electrons followed by fragmentation. The capture of an electron by the even-electron cation \\\(\\ce\{\[M + nH\]^\{n+\}\}\\\) liberates energy and reduces its charge state\, thus producing the corresponding \\\(\\ce\{\[M + nH\]^\{\(n - 1\)+.\}\}\\\) odd-electron ion\, which readily fragments."
synonym: "ECD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12403
name: electron capture ionization
def: "Ionization of a gas-phase atom or molecule by attachment of a free electron to form molecular ions of the \\\(\\ce\{M^\{-.\}\}\\\) type."
synonym: "ECI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "electron capture negative ionization" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12404
name: electrospray needle
def: "Narrow bore tube from which highly charged droplets are emitted in electrospray ionization."
synonym: "electrospray emitter" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12405
name: electrostatic energy analyser
def: "Device consisting of pairs of parallel conducting plates\, concentric cylinders\, or concentric spheres that separate charged particles according to their ratio of translational energy to charge by means of a potential difference applied between the pair."
synonym: "ESA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "electric sector" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12406
name: even-electron rule
def: "Rule that states that even-electron ions tend to form even-electron fragment ions whereas odd-electron ions tend to dissociate to form either odd- or even-electron ions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12407
name: exact mass
def: "Calculated mass of an ion or molecule with specified isotopic composition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12326

[Term]
id: goldbook:12408
name: extracted ion chromatogram
def: "Chromatogram created by plotting the intensity of the signal observed at a chosen m/z value or set of values in a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of retention time."
synonym: "mass chromatogram" []
synonym: "reconstructed ion chromatogram" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12409
name: extracted ion electropherogram
def: "Electropherogram created by plotting the intensity of the signal observed at a chosen m/z value or set of values in a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of electrophoresis time."
synonym: "extracted ion electrophorogram" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12410
name: extracted ion profile
def: "Any plot of signal intensity observed at a chosen m/z value or set of values in a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of time\, including extracted ion chromatogram\, extracted ion electropherogram\, or from flow injection analysis or any other time-dependent sampling."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12408
consider: goldbook:12409
consider: goldbook:12600

[Term]
id: goldbook:12411
name: fast ion bombardment
def: "Ionization of any species by the interaction of a focused beam of ions\, with a translational energy of several thousand \\\(\\pu\{eV\}\\\)\, with a solid or liquid sample."
comment: "For a liquid sample, fast ion bombardment is the same as liquid secondary ionization."
synonym: "FIB" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12469

[Term]
id: goldbook:12412
name: field-free region
def: "Section of a mass spectrometer in which there are no electric or magnetic fields."
synonym: "FFR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12413
name: first stability region
def: "Stability region of a Mathieu stability diagram closest to the origin."
comment: "Ions within this region can traverse the full length of a transmission quadrupole or can be trapped in a Paul ion trap."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12486
consider: goldbook:12516
consider: goldbook:12602

[Term]
id: goldbook:12414
name: fixed precursor ion spectrum
def: "Spectrum obtained when data are acquired that determine the m/z values of product ions produced by the reaction of a selected precursor ion with a user-specified m/z value."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12415
name: flow injection mass spectrometry
def: "Method of flow injection analysis in which an aliquot of sample is injected\, without chromatographic separation\, into a liquid carrier stream for on-line mass spectrometry."
synonym: "flow injection analysis mass spectrometry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12416
name: focal plane detector
def: "Detector for m/z spatially dispersed ion beams in which all ions simultaneously impinge on the detector plane to produce spatially defined signals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12417
name: forward geometry
def: "Double-focusing mass spectrometer configuration in which the ion beam traverses the electric sector before the magnetic sector."
synonym: "normal geometry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12405
consider: goldbook:12473
consider: goldbook:12558

[Term]
id: goldbook:12418
name: forward library search
def: "Procedure of comparing a mass spectrum of an unknown compound with a mass spectral library so that the unknown spectrum is compared in turn with the library spectra\, considering only the m/z peaks that have intensities greater than a specific threshold in the unknown."
comment: "In a forward library search, a higher similarity index indicates the extent to which the library spectrum resembles the unknown spectrum."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12484
consider: goldbook:12559

[Term]
id: goldbook:12419
name: Fourier-transform mass spectrometry
def: "Mass spectrometry technique in which m/z values are represented by frequencies of ion motion and mass spectra are generated by Fourier transform mathematical operations from time domain transients produced by image current detection."
comment: "Fourier transform mass spectrometry is typically carried out using Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers or Kingdon traps."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12460

[Term]
id: goldbook:12420
name: fringe field
def: "Electric or magnetic field that extends from the edge of an electric sector\, magnetic sector\, lens\, or other ion optics element."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12405
consider: goldbook:12444
consider: goldbook:12473

[Term]
id: goldbook:12421
name: gas chromatography-mass spectrometry
def: "Technique by which a mixture is separated into individual components by gas chromatography\, followed by detection with a mass spectrometer."
comment: "Either a hyphen or slash can be used to indicate combined instruments."
comment: "The mass spectrum is typically obtained on a time scale that allows resolution of the component in a single chromatographic peak."
synonym: "GC-MS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "gas chromatography/mass spectrometry (GC/MS)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12466
consider: goldbook:12585
consider: goldbook:12595

[Term]
id: goldbook:12422
name: glow discharge ionization
def: "Formation of ions from gaseous atoms or molecules or from the vapor of a solid sample at the cathode by applying a potential difference between two electrodes immersed in a low-pressure inert gas environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12423
name: gridless reflectron
def: "Reflectron design in which the decelerating/accelerating field is produced without the use of wire-mesh grids."
comment: "This design improves ion transmission but at the cost of a less homogeneous field and thus reduced resolution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12424
name: hard ionization
def: "Formation of gas-phase ions accompanied by extensive fragmentation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12575

[Term]
id: goldbook:12425
name: high-field asymmetric waveform ion mobility spectrometry
def: "Separation of ions at atmospheric pressure between two electrodes due to simultaneous application of a high potential asymmetric waveform\, whereby ions migrate towards one of the two electrodes depending on the ratio of the high- to low-field mobility of the ion. A variable compensating DC potential is used to selectively transmit ions of interest."
synonym: "FAIMS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
synonym: "RF-DC ion mobility spectrometry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12426
name: hybrid mass spectrometer
def: "Mass spectrometer that combines m/z analyzers of different types to perform tandem mass spectrometry or higher-order \\\(\{\\rm\{MS\}\}^\{n\}\\\) experiment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12591

[Term]
id: goldbook:12427
name: hydrogen/deuterium exchange
def: "Exchange of hydrogen atoms with deuterium atoms in a chemical species in solution prior to introduction into a mass spectrometer\, or by ion/molecule reaction with a neutral gas inside a mass spectrometer."
synonym: "HDX" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12428
name: hydrogen shifts
def: "Sigmatropic reactions of ions in which the \\\(\\ce\{\\upsigma\\mbox\{-\}bonds\}\\\) broken and formed involve hydrogen atoms\, and are subject to the Woodward–Hofmann rules resulting from orbital symmetry considerations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12429
name: hyphenated mass spectrometry technique
def: "Analytical technique in which mass spectrometry is interfaced with a pretreatment step\, most often chromatographic separation but many other combinations are possible."
comment: "Despite the use of the term "hyphenated" in the name of the general category, a slash separator as in gas chromatography/mass spectrometry may also be used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12421

[Term]
id: goldbook:12430
name: image current detection
def: "Method of ion detection by measuring the current that results from the image charge induced by a coherent motion of ions passing near a conductor."
comment: "In Fourier transform mass spectrometers or Kingdon traps, the coherent orbital motion of ions between a pair of electrodes induces a radio frequency image charge in the electrodes and an alternating image current in the detection circuit connecting to the electrodes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12419
consider: goldbook:12460

[Term]
id: goldbook:12431
name: imaging mass spectrometry
def: "Procedure used to form chemically selective images of an object based on the mass spectrometric detection of ions desorbed from its surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12432
name: iminium ion
def: "Cation with the structure \\\(\\ce\{R2C=N^\{+\}R2\}\\\)."
comment: "The terms imonium ion and immonium ion are irregularly formed and should not be used."
synonym: "alkylideneaminylium ion" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12433
name: infrared multiphoton dissociation
def: "Dissociation of a reactant ion as a result of the absorption of multiple infrared photons."
synonym: "IRMPD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12348

[Term]
id: goldbook:12434
name: in-source collision-induced dissociation
def: "Dissociation of an ion as a result of collisional excitation during ion transfer from an atmospheric pressure ion source to the vacuum chamber of the mass spectrometer."
comment: "Terms such as cone voltage dissociation and capillary exit fragmentation are design specific versions of this term, and are deprecated."
comment: "This process is similar to ion desolvation but uses higher collision energy."
synonym: "in-source collisionally activated dissociation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12436

[Term]
id: goldbook:12435
name: internal fragment
def: "Fragment ion of a peptide ion precursor formed by a double backbone cleavage that contains neither the original \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)- or \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)-terminal residues. Typically a combination of b- and y-type cleavages or occasionally an a- and y-type combination."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12436
name: ion desolvation
def: "Removal of solvent molecules clustered around a gas-phase ion by means of heating and/or collisions with gas molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12437
name: ion enhancement
def: "Phenomenon in which the ionization efficiency of a compound is increased by the presence of another compound."
comment: "The effect is most significant in electrospray ionization but is also observed in atmospheric pressure chemical ionization and to a lesser extent in other ionization methods."
synonym: "ionization enhancement" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12336
consider: goldbook:12445

[Term]
id: goldbook:12438
name: ion evaporation model
def: "Mechanism for production of gas-phase ions from highly charged fine liquid droplets as in electrospray ionization that involves direct ejection of the ions from the droplet surface."
comment: "This mechanism is thought to be dominant for smaller molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12352

[Term]
id: goldbook:12439
name: ion funnel
def: "Series of stacked ring electrodes with progressively decreasing inner diameter to which a combined radio frequency and fixed potential is applied. The resulting field focuses ions travelling along the central axis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12440
name: ion gate
def: "Set of plates or grid of wires in an ion mobility spectrometer\, time-of-flight mass spectrometer\, or other mass spectrometer that is used to apply a pulsed electric field with the purpose of selectively deflecting charged particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12442
consider: goldbook:12480

[Term]
id: goldbook:12441
name: ion/ion reaction
def: "Reaction between two ions\, generally of opposite polarity."
comment: "The hyphenated term ion-ion reaction is superseded."
synonym: "ion-ion reaction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12442
name: ion mobility spectrometry
def: "Separation of ions according to their velocity through a buffer gas under the influence of an electric field."
synonym: "IMS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12350
consider: goldbook:12425

[Term]
id: goldbook:12443
name: ion/neutral complex
def: "Weakly bound species formed from an ion and neutral."
comment: "In the context of some unimolecular ion dissociations, these complexes are particular types of transition states or local energy minima that lie between precursor ions and product ions on the reaction coordinate."
comment: "The hyphenated formulation of this term, ion-neutral complex, is deprecated; the hyphen suggests a reaction of a species that is both an ion and a molecule and is not the intended meaning."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12444
name: ion optics
def: "Devices designed to control the formation\, focusing\, and deflection of charged particle beams in a vacuum under the influence of electric and magnetic fields."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12445
name: ion suppression
def: "Phenomenon in which the ionization efficiency of a species is lowered by the presence of a different species."
comment: "The effect is most significant in electrospray ionization but is also observed in atmospheric pressure chemical ionization and to a lesser extent in other ionization methods."
synonym: "ionization suppression" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12336
consider: goldbook:12437

[Term]
id: goldbook:12446
name: ion-to-photon detector
def: "Detector in which ions strike a conversion dynode to produce electrons that in turn strike a phosphor and the resulting photons are detected by a photomultiplier."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12372
consider: goldbook:12380

[Term]
id: goldbook:12447
name: ion trap
def: "Device for spatially confining ions using electric and magnetic fields alone or in combination."
synonym: "IT" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12448
name: isobaric tag for relative and absolute quantitation
def: "Chemical labeling reagents used for relative or absolute quantitation in proteomics\, based on covalent labeling of the \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)-terminus and side-chain amines of peptides from protein digestions with tags of varying mass."
synonym: "iTRAQ" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12449
name: isotope cluster
def: "Group of peaks representing ions of the same elemental composition\, but different isotopic compositions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12450
name: isotope coded affinity tag
def: "Chemical labeling reagents used for relative quantitation in proteomics\, consisting of a reactive group capable of labeling a defined amino acid side-chain\, an isotopically coded linker\, and a tag for the affinity isolation of labeled proteins and peptides."
synonym: "ICAT" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12451
name: isotope dilution mass spectrometry
def: "Quantitative mass spectrometry technique in which an isotopically enriched compound is used as a surrogate internal standard."
synonym: "IDMS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12589

[Term]
id: goldbook:12452
name: isotope ratio
def: "Ratio of the number of atoms of one isotope to the number of atoms of another isotope of the same chemical element in the same system."
comment: "Usually the minor, less abundant isotope to the major, most abundant isotope, for example, \(\ce{^{13}C}/\ce{^{12}C}\)."
synonym: "isotope–number ratio" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12453
name: isotope ratio mass spectrometry
def: "Measurement and study of the relative abundances of the different isotopes of an element in a material using a mass spectrometer."
synonym: "IRMS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "stable isotope mass spectrometry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12454
name: isotopolog ions
def: "Ions that differ only in the isotopic composition of one or more of the constituent atoms."
comment: "Isotopolog is an abbreviation of isotopic homolog."
synonym: "isotopic homolog ions" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12449

[Term]
id: goldbook:12455
name: isotopomeric ion
def: "Isomeric ions having the same numbers of each isotopic atom but differing in their positions within the ion."
comment: "Isotopomer is an abbreviation of isotopic isomer."
comment: "Isotopomeric ions can be either configurational isomers in which two atomic isotopes exchange positions or isotopic stereoisomers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12456
name: jet separator
def: "Gas chromatograph-to-mass spectrometer interface where the gas chromatography effluent expands into a lower-pressure region and then through a downstream orifice. The low mass carrier gas molecules diffuse from the jet axis\, leaving the sample stream enriched in the heavier analyte molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12493

[Term]
id: goldbook:12457
name: kinetic energy release
def: "Translational energy of fragments resulting from dissociation of a metastable ion measured relative to the center-of-mass."
comment: "In this context, kinetic energy is interpreted as translational, rather than vibrational or rotational, kinetic energy."
synonym: "KER" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12458

[Term]
id: goldbook:12458
name: kinetic energy release distribution
def: "Distribution of values of translational energies in the center-of-mass reference for an ensemble of metastable ions undergoing a specific dissociation reaction."
comment: "In this context, kinetic energy is interpreted as translational, rather than vibrational or rotational, kinetic energy."
synonym: "KERD" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12476

[Term]
id: goldbook:12459
name: kinetic shift
def: "Excess energy above the thermochemical threshold required to observe dissociation of a precursor ion within the timeframe of a particular mass spectrometry experiment."
comment: "Kinetic shifts are important when thermochemical quantities are deduced from appearance energy measurements."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12460
name: Kingdon trap
def: "Ion trapping device that consists of an outer barrel-like electrode and a coaxial inner spindle-like electrode that form an electrostatic field with a quadro-logarithmic potential distribution."
comment: "The frequency of harmonic oscillations of the orbitally trapped ions along the axis of the electrostatic field is independent of the ion velocity and is inversely proportional to the square root of m/z so that the trap can be operated as a mass analyzer using image current detection and Fourier transformation of the time domain signal."
comment: "The trademarked term "Orbitrap" has been used to describe a Kingdon trap used as a mass spectrometer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12430

[Term]
id: goldbook:12461
name: label-free quantitation
def: "Method for determining the concentration of proteins through a combination of protein digestion and liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry \(LC-MS\) without relying on stable isotope labeling. Protein quantification is achieved by measuring the signal intensity of peptide ions corresponding to a protein or by counting and comparing the number of fragment mass spectra identifying peptides of a given protein."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12466

[Term]
id: goldbook:12462
name: laser desorption
def: "Formation of gas-phase species from a solid or liquid sample surface upon activation using a short pulse of photons from a laser."
synonym: "LD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12463
name: laser desorption ionization
def: "Formation of gas-phase ions by the interaction of a laser with a solid or liquid material."
synonym: "LDI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12464
name: laser microprobe mass spectrometry
def: "Laser desorption ionization mass spectrometry\, particularly emphasizing spatially resolved composition information."
synonym: "LMMS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12463

[Term]
id: goldbook:12465
name: linear ion trap
def: "Two-dimensional Paul ion trap in which ions are confined in the axial dimension by means of a static electric potential."
synonym: "LIT" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12516

[Term]
id: goldbook:12466
name: liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry
def: "Technique by which a mixture of analytes is separated into individual components by liquid chromatography \(typically high-performance liquid chromatography\)\, followed by detection with a mass spectrometer."
comment: "Either a hyphen or slash can be used to indicate combined instruments."
synonym: "LC-MS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "liquid chromatography/mass spectrometry (LC/MS)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12467
name: liquid ion evaporation
def: "Spray ionization interface in which droplets are dispersed from a pneumatic nebulizer toward a high potential electrode that produces a static charge on the droplets leading to ion formation after solvent evaporation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12579

[Term]
id: goldbook:12468
name: liquid junction interface
def: "Means of coupling capillary electrophoresis to a mass spectrometer in which a liquid reservoir surrounds the separation capillary and transfer capillary to the mass spectrometer and provides electric contact for the capillary electrophoresis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12469
name: liquid secondary ionization
def: "Ionization of any species by the interaction of a focused beam of ions or atoms with a sample that is dissolved in a solvent matrix."
synonym: "LSI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12470
name: liquid sheath
def: "Flow of make-up liquid in a sheath flow interface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12570

[Term]
id: goldbook:12471
name: lock mass
def: "Mass of an ion of known m/z value\, derived from a suitable standard compound introduced into an ion source together with the sample to be analyzed\, which permits real-time recalibration by correction of m/z shifts arising from instrumental drift."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12472
name: low-energy collision-induced dissociation
def: "Collision-induced dissociation process wherein the precursor ion has laboratory-frame translational energy lower than a given value\, often taken to be \\\(\\pu\{1 keV\}\\\)."
comment: "This process can be carried out under single collision conditions but typically requires multiple collisions and the collisional excitation is cumulative."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12473
name: magnetic sector
def: "Device that produces a magnetic field perpendicular to a charged particle beam that deflects the beam to an extent that is proportional to the ratio of particle momentum and charge."
comment: "For a mono-energetic beam, the deflection is proportional to m/z."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12474
name: magnetron motion
def: "Slow rotation of the center of cyclotron motion around the central axis of a Penning ion trap that results from a drift of the cyclotron centre along the electric equipotential lines perpendicular to the magnetic field direction."
comment: "The characteristic frequency of this motion is called the magnetron frequency."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12379
consider: goldbook:12521

[Term]
id: goldbook:12475
name: make-up liquid
def: "Solvent that is mixed with the sample flow in a liquid introduction mass spectrometry interface in order to adjust the flow rate or solvent characteristics of the system\, for example\, to promote ionization efficiency."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12476
name: mass-analyzed ion kinetic energy spectrometry
def: "Procedure by which translational energy spectra are obtained from a sector mass spectrometer that incorporates at least one magnetic sector plus one electric sector in reverse geometry \(a magnetic sector followed by an electric sector\)."
comment: "In this context, kinetic energy is interpreted as translational rather than vibrational or rotational kinetic energy."
comment: "The accelerating potential, \(V\), and the magnetic flux density, \(B\), are set at fixed values to m/z select the precursor ions, which are then allowed to dissociate or to react in a field-free region between the two sectors. The translational energy-to-charge ratios of the various product ions are analyzed by scanning the electric sector field \(E\). The width of a product ion spectral peak is related to the kinetic energy release distribution for the dissociation process."
synonym: "MIKES" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12325
consider: goldbook:12405
consider: goldbook:12412
consider: goldbook:12458
consider: goldbook:12473
consider: goldbook:12558
consider: goldbook:12566

[Term]
id: goldbook:12477
name: mass calibration
def: "Means of determining m/z values of ions from experimentally detected signals using a theoretical or empirical relational equation."
comment: "Most commonly this is accomplished using a computer-based data system and a calibration file obtained from a mass spectrum of a compound that produces ions of known m/z values."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12478
name: mass defect
def: "Difference between the nominal mass and the monoisotopic mass of an atom\, molecule\, or ion."
comment: "Mass defect can be a positive or negative value dependent upon the elemental composition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12495

[Term]
id: goldbook:12479
name: mass discrimination
def: "Differences in overall detection sensitivities for ions of different m/z values in a mass spectrum\, caused by variations in ionization efficiency\, transmission efficiency through the interface between the ion source and the analyzer vacuum system\, analyzer\, and detector response."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12601

[Term]
id: goldbook:12480
name: mass gate
def: "Ion gate used to transmit ions in a given m/z range."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12440

[Term]
id: goldbook:12481
name: mass limit
def: "Value of m/z above or below which ions cannot be detected in a mass spectrometer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12482
name: mass selective axial ejection
def: "Use of mass selective instability to eject ions of selected m/z values from an ion trap along the trap axis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12447
consider: goldbook:12483

[Term]
id: goldbook:12483
name: mass selective instability
def: "Unstable trajectories in an ion trap for ions within a particular range of m/z values caused by an appropriate combination of oscillating electric fields."
synonym: "MSI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12482

[Term]
id: goldbook:12484
name: mass spectral library
def: "Collection of mass spectra of different compounds\, usually represented as arrays of signal intensity vs. the m/z values."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12485
name: mass spectrometry/mass spectrometry
def: "Acquisition and study of the spectra of the product ions or precursor ions of m/z selected ions\, or of precursor ions of a selected neutral mass loss."
comment: "MS/MS can be accomplished using instruments incorporating more than one analyzer (tandem mass spectrometry in space) or in trap instruments (tandem mass spectrometry in time)."
synonym: "MS/MS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "tandem mass spectrometry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12591
consider: goldbook:12592

[Term]
id: goldbook:12486
name: Mathieu stability diagram
def: "Graphical representation expressed in terms of dimensionless reduced coordinates that describes the stability or instability of charged particle motion in a transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer or Paul ion trap\, based on an appropriate form of the Mathieu differential equation."
synonym: "stability diagram" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12516
consider: goldbook:12602

[Term]
id: goldbook:12487
name: membrane introduction mass spectrometry
def: "Mass spectrometry measurement that uses a semi-permeable membrane separator that permits the passage of analytes directly from solutions or ambient air to the mass spectrometer ion source."
synonym: "MIMS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
synonym: "membrane inlet mass spectrometry" []
synonym: "membrane interface mass spectrometry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12488
name: membrane separator
def: "GC-MS interface with a polymer membrane that selectively passes analyte molecules in preference to the carrier gas thereby enriching the analyte in the gas stream."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12421

[Term]
id: goldbook:12489
name: microchannel plate
def: "Thin plate that contains a closely spaced array of channels each of which acts as a continuous dynode particle multiplier. A fast charged or neutral particle\, or a photon\, that strikes the plate causes a cascade of secondary electrons that ultimately exits the opposite side of the plate."
synonym: "MCP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "channel electron multiplier array" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12369

[Term]
id: goldbook:12490
name: microelectrospray
def: "Electrospray ionization at a low solvent flow rate\, typically several microliters per minute \(\\\(\\pu\{\\upmu L min-1\}\\\)\) or lower\, where a pump is used to provide the sample flow."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12502

[Term]
id: goldbook:12491
name: molecular beam mass spectrometry
def: "Mass spectrometry measurement in which the sample is introduced into the ion source of the mass spectrometer as a collimated beam of molecules with a narrow velocity distribution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12492
name: molecular effusion separator
def: "GC-MS interface that subjects the GC effluent to effusive flow through a porous glass tube. The lighter carrier gas passes out of the tube\, leaving the gas within the tube enriched in analyte."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12421

[Term]
id: goldbook:12493
name: momentum separator
def: "Mass spectrometer interface to inlets including chromatography and spray-based ion sources that enriches the sample by selecting the central part of the effluent or spray using an orifice or skimmer. Particles with a higher forward momentum diverge less from the spray axis for a given radial momentum."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12456

[Term]
id: goldbook:12494
name: monodisperse aerosol generating interface for chromatography
def: "Particle beam interface that incorporates a monodisperse aerosol generator."
synonym: "MAGIC" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12495
name: monoisotopic mass
def: "Exact mass of an ion or molecule calculated using the mass of the most abundant isotope of each element."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12326
consider: goldbook:12407

[Term]
id: goldbook:12496
name: moving belt interface
def: "Liquid sample mass spectrometer interface that uses two or more pulleys and a continuous loop of material. Samples are sprayed or deposited from solution onto the belt where they are transported into the vacuum system for vaporization or desorption and ionization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12497
name: MS/MS spectrum
def: "Mass spectrum obtained using tandem mass spectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12591

[Term]
id: goldbook:12498
name: MS<sup><i>n</i></sup>
def: "Symbol for multiple-stage mass spectrometry experiments designed to record product ion spectra where \\\(n\\\) is the number of product ion stages \(nth-generation product ions\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12501
consider: goldbook:12511
consider: goldbook:12535

[Term]
id: goldbook:12499
name: multicollector mass spectrometer
def: "Mass spectrograph based on a double-focusing magnetic analyzer that spatially disperses ions of different m/z values on to an array of Faraday cup detectors\, generally used with inductively coupled plasma ion sources for isotopic composition measurements."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12500
name: multiple reaction monitoring
def: "Application of selected reaction monitoring to multiple product ions from one or more precursor ions."
comment: "This term should not be confused with consecutive reaction monitoring, which involves the serial application of three or more stages of selected reaction monitoring."
synonym: "MRM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12366
consider: goldbook:12568

[Term]
id: goldbook:12501
name: multiple-stage mass spectrometry
def: "Multiple stages of precursor ion m/z selection followed by product ion detection for successive nth-generation product ions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12498
consider: goldbook:12511

[Term]
id: goldbook:12502
name: nanoelectrospray
def: "Electrospray ionization at a very low solvent flow rate\, typically hundreds of nanoliters per minute of sample solution or lower\, often without the use of an external solvent delivery system."
comment: "Nanospray should only be used to describe the commercial product."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12490

[Term]
id: goldbook:12503
name: negative ion chemical ionization
def: "Chemical ionization that results in the formation of negative ions."
synonym: "NICI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12504
name: neutralization-reionization mass spectrometry
def: "Procedure by which neutral species are formed from m/z selected ions by charge transfer to a collision gas or by dissociation. The neutral species are separated from the remaining ions and ionized through collisions with a second gas."
synonym: "NRMS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12505
name: neutral loss
def: "Loss of an uncharged species from an ion during dissociation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12506
name: neutral loss scan
def: "Scan used to generate a constant neutral loss spectrum."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12368

[Term]
id: goldbook:12507
name: nitrogen rule
def: "Rule stating that a neutral organic molecule containing one or more atoms of the elements \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{H\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{O\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{S\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{P\}\\\)\, or any halogen has an odd nominal mass if it contains an odd number of nitrogen atoms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12508
name: nozzle-skimmer dissociation
def: "Collisionally activated dissociation that is caused by collisions in the region between the nozzle and skimmer of an atmospheric pressure ionization source such as electrospray or atmospheric pressure chemical ionization."
comment: "The process can be induced by a higher than typical nozzle-skimmer voltage."
synonym: "in-source collision-induced dissociation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12336
consider: goldbook:12509

[Term]
id: goldbook:12509
name: nozzle-skimmer voltage
def: "Electric potential difference applied between the electrospray needle and the skimmer\, which is typically held at the same potential as the counter electrode."
synonym: "needle voltage" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12376
consider: goldbook:12404
consider: goldbook:12574

[Term]
id: goldbook:12510
name: <i>n</i><sup>th</sup>-generation product ion
def: "Serial product ions from dissociation or bimolecular reaction of selected precursor ions where \\\(n\\\) refers to the number of stages of dissociation or bimolecular reaction in a series of consecutive reactions that involve successive product ions."
comment: "Given the sequential fragmentation scheme: \[\ce{M1^{+} -> M2^{+} -> M3^{+} -> M4^{+} -> M5^{+}}\] \(\ce{M4^{+}}\) is the precursor ion of \(\ce{M5^{+}}\), a 1st-generation product ion of \(\ce{M3^{+}}\), a 2nd-generation product ion of \(\ce{M2^{+}}\), and a 3rd-generation product ion of \(\ce{M1^{+}}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12511

[Term]
id: goldbook:12511
name: <i>n</i><sup>th</sup>-generation product ion spectrum
def: "Mass spectrum recorded from any mass spectrometer in which the appropriate scan function can be set to record the appropriate generation product ion or ions of m/z selected precursor ions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12510

[Term]
id: goldbook:12512
name: orthogonal electrospray
def: "Configuration for electrospray ionization in which the axis of the spray is at a right angle to the axis of the sampling cone."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12563

[Term]
id: goldbook:12513
name: orthogonal extraction
def: "Pulsed acceleration of ions perpendicular to their original direction of travel into a mass spectrometer\, typically time-of-flight."
comment: "Ions may be extracted from a directional ion source, drift tube, or m/z separation stage."
synonym: "orthogonal acceleration" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12514
name: partial isotopic scrambling
def: "Partial random mixing of isotopes among specified atom positions in an ion or neutral species."
comment: "In mass spectrometry, this term usually refers to the partial random mixing of isotopes in isolated ions that were formed with a fixed isotopic composition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12515
name: particle beam interface
def: "Method for coupling liquid chromatography to mass spectrometry in which the effluent is passed through a heated capillary to form an expanding jet of vapour and aerosol particles. After passing through a skimmer that acts as a momentum separator\, the beam impinges on a heated surface to form ions through chemical ionization at the surface or ionization of the resulting vapour in a chemical ionization or electron ionization source."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12516
name: Paul ion trap
def: "Ion trapping device that depends on the application of radio frequency potentials between a ring electrode and two end-cap electrodes to confine the ion motion to a cyclic path described by an appropriate form of the Mathieu equation. The choice of these potentials determines the m/z value below which ions are not trapped."
synonym: "quadrupole ion storage trap" []
synonym: "quadrupole ion trap" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12517
name: peak matching
def: "Procedure for measuring the accurate mass of an ion using scanning mass spectrometers\, in which the peak corresponding to the unknown ion and that for a reference ion of known m/z are displayed alternately and caused to overlap by adjusting appropriate electric fields."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12326
consider: goldbook:12550

[Term]
id: goldbook:12518
name: peak parking
def: "Method used to extend the amount of time available for mass spectrometric analysis of the components in a narrow chromatographic peak. The eluent flow rate is reduced to an ultra-low level at the leading edge of the peak and held at this low flow rate for the duration of compound elution\, thus enabling collection of sufficient data for reliable statistical analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12519
name: peak stripping
def: "Data analysis technique used in elemental mass spectrometry to correct the intensity of an unresolved multiplet peak monitored for a specific element for contributions from a multi-isotopic contaminant. The correction is calculated from the measured intensity of a different isotopic peak of the contaminant and the known natural isotopic abundance ratio."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12520
name: Penning ionization
def: "Ionization via electron removal that occurs through the energy transfer from a neutral species \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\) internally excited to a metastable state \(such as a high Rydberg state\) to a neutral species \\\(\\ce\{M\}\\\) with lower ionization energy\, as represented by the following reaction\: \\\(\\ce\{N^\{\\ast\} + M -> N + M^\{+.\} + \\textit\{e\}^\{-\}\}\\\)."
comment: "Penning ionization differs from chemi-ionization in that no chemical change is involved."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12521
name: Penning ion trap
def: "Ion trapping device using a static magnetic field and a static electric potential well. The magnetic field confines the ion motion to circular orbits around the magnetic force line direction\, which aligns with the direction of the trap axis\, whereas the electric potential well confines the ion motion axially."
comment: "This device is used for the mass analyzer of Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12522
name: peptide mass fingerprinting
def: "Method for protein analysis where an unknown protein is chemically or enzymatically cleaved into peptide fragments whose masses are determined by mass spectrometry. The peptide masses are compared to peptide masses calculated for known proteins in a database and analyzed statistically to determine the best match."
synonym: "PMF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "mass mapping" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12327

[Term]
id: goldbook:12523
name: peptide sequence tag
def: "Sequence of peptide ion fragment masses that can be used to aid in the identification of the amino acid sequence."
comment: "Sequence tags are often obtained in tandem mass spectrometry analysis of peptides from an unknown protein that has been chemically or enzymatically cleaved into peptide fragments."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12591

[Term]
id: goldbook:12524
name: photodissociation
def: "Process wherein the reactant ion or molecule is dissociated as a result of absorption of one or more photons."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12525
name: photographic plate recording
def: "Recording of ion currents by allowing them to strike a photographic plate\, which is subsequently developed."
comment: "This technique is typically associated with ion-beams that have been spatially separated by m/z and focused across a focal plane as in a Mattauch–Herzog geometry magnetic sector instrument."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12473

[Term]
id: goldbook:12526
name: $\\boldsymbol\{\\pi\}$/n rad magnetic sector
def: "Arrangement in which an ion beam is deflected magnetically through \\\(\\pi/n\\ \\rm\{rad\}\\\)\, where \\\(n \\gt 1\\\)."
synonym: "180º/<em>n</em> magnetic sector" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12527
name: pneumatically assisted electrospray ionization
def: "Electrospray ionization in which the nebulization of the liquid stream is assisted by a concentric stream of gas."
comment: "Ionspray should only be used to describe the commercial product."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12528
name: point detector
def: "Detector in which the ion beam is focused onto a small area\, for example\, defined by a collector slit\, rather than dispersed by m/z spatially across a focal plane."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12359

[Term]
id: goldbook:12529
name: post-acceleration detector
def: "Detector in which a high potential is applied after m/z separation to accelerate the ions and produce an improved signal."
synonym: "PAD" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12372

[Term]
id: goldbook:12530
name: post-source decay
def: "Technique specific to reflectron time-of-flight mass spectrometers where product ions of metastable transitions or collision-induced dissociations generated in the flight tube prior to entering the reflectron are separated according to m/z to yield product ion spectra."
synonym: "PSD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12535

[Term]
id: goldbook:12531
name: precursor ion spectrum
def: "Mass spectrum in which the appropriate m/z separation function records the precursor ions of selected product ions or specified neutral loss."
comment: "The ion current recorded by the detector is that from the product ion but the m/z values corresponding to the peaks in the resulting spectrum are those of precursor ions that fragmented in the fashion specified by the m/z separation function of the tandem mass spectrometer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12535

[Term]
id: goldbook:12532
name: pre-ionization state
def: "Electronic state capable of undergoing autoionization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12533
name: probability-based matching
def: "Automated system for computer examination of the mass spectrum of an unknown mixture for the presence of a specific compound for which a standard spectrum is available in a library. The probability that the compound is present is given by a confidence index \\\(K\\\) such that \\\(2^\{K\}\\\) is the average number of randomly selected compounds whose mass spectra would have to be examined to find data which match the target spectrum to the same degree as does the unknown."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12534
name: product ion analysis
def: "Process whereby a precursor ion of a particular m/z is selected by m/z\, fragmentation is induced\, and the mass spectrum of the resulting product ions is recorded."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12535
name: product ion spectrum
def: "Mass spectrum in which the appropriate m/z separation analysis function is set to record the product ions of a selected precursor ion selected by m/z."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12531

[Term]
id: goldbook:12536
name: profile mode
def: "Method for acquiring a mass spectrum where each peak is displayed as a curve\, with the data points defining the curve corresponding to the signal intensities at each particular m/z value."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12351

[Term]
id: goldbook:12537
name: proton-bound dimer
def: "Dimeric ion consisting of two similar or dissimilar molecules bound together by hydrogen bonding with a shared proton."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12538
name: pyrolysis mass spectrometry
def: "Mass spectrometry technique in which the sample is heated to the point of decomposition and the gas-phase decomposition products are characterized by mass spectrometry."
synonym: "PYMS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12539
name: quadratic field reflectron
def: "Reflectron in which the electric field varies with the square of the distance from the entrance and compensates for kinetic energy spread to all orders."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12540
name: quadrupolar axialization
def: "Technique for axialization in Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers in which magnetron motion is converted into cyclotron motion by subjecting the trapped ions to a quadrupolar excitation field while they undergo collisions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12343
consider: goldbook:12379

[Term]
id: goldbook:12541
name: quadrupole time-of-flight
def: "Hybrid mass spectrometer consisting of a transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer coupled to an orthogonal acceleration time-of-flight mass spectrometer. A collision quadrupole is typically inserted between the two mass spectrometers."
synonym: "QTOF" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12363
consider: goldbook:12426
consider: goldbook:12513
consider: goldbook:12602

[Term]
id: goldbook:12542
name: quantitation by concatenated tryptic peptides
def: "Method for absolute quantitation of a protein or proteins in a multiplexed fashion using isotope-labeled peptides as surrogate internal standards. The labeled peptides are produced by synthesizing a gene coding for all desired peptides\, expressing this gene in E. coli culture containing appropriately labeled substrate\, and digesting with trypsin the expressed protein composed of the desired concatenated peptides."
synonym: "QCAT" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12589

[Term]
id: goldbook:12543
name: quasi-equilibrium theory
def: "Statistical theory of unimolecular reaction rates \(isomerization or fragmentation\) of molecular species that assumes that reaction occurs from the ground electronic state of the reactant regardless of its mode of formation\, at a rate determined by the free statistical redistribution of internal energy into those vibrational and rotational modes that must be activated sufficiently to reach the appropriate transition state for the specified reaction to occur."
comment: "The QET applies to isolated molecular species in the absence of collisions, as for ion fragmentations in a mass spectrometer. Early formulations assumed the reactant contained \(s\) identical harmonic oscillators of frequency \(\nu\), with a transition state corresponding to just one critical oscillator containing at least \(m\) quanta corresponding to the critical energy for reaction \(\varepsilon^{\ast} = m\nu\). A further assumption that \(m \gg s\) leads to an ultra-simple expression for the unimolecular rate constant at total internal energy \(\varepsilon\): \(k(\varepsilon) = \nu[(\varepsilon - \varepsilon^{\ast})/\varepsilon]^{(s-1)}\). Elimination of most of these simplifying assumptions followed development of the Rice–Ramsperger–Kassel–Marcus (RRKM) theory."
synonym: "QET" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12544
name: radial ejection
def: "Ejection of an ion from an ion trap in a direction perpendicular to the longitudinal axis of the trap."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12447

[Term]
id: goldbook:12545
name: Rayleigh limit
def: "Limiting droplet size at which self-fragmentation will occur for charged droplets generated in electrospray or other ionization processes. Self-fragmentation occurs when the electrostatic repulsion force generated by the excess charge exceeds the surface tension that maintains the integrity of the droplet."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12546
name: reagent gas
def: "Gas that reacts with ions to produce product ions through ion/molecule reactions; for example\, a gas such as methane\, ammonia\, or isobutane used in chemical ionization to create reagent ions or a gas used in ion traps or collision cells to perform gas-phase ion/molecule reactions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12361
consider: goldbook:12447
consider: goldbook:12547

[Term]
id: goldbook:12547
name: reagent ion
def: "Ion that reacts with a neutral to produce an ionized form of such species through an ion/molecule reaction\, for example\, as in chemical ionization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12548
name: recombination energy
def: "Energy released when an electron is added to an ionized molecule or atom."
comment: "This is the energy required for the reverse process of vertical ionization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12549
name: rectilinear ion trap
def: "Quadrupole ion trap whose electrodes form a rectilinear polygon\, the simplest form of which consists of two pairs of rectangular electrodes supplied with radio frequency \(RF\) potentials and a pair of electrodes to which a DC potential is applied. Slits or apertures in the electrodes allow injection and ejection of charged particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12516

[Term]
id: goldbook:12550
name: reference ion
def: "Stable ion whose structure or elemental formula is known with certainty. These ions are formed by direct ionization of a molecule of known structure or elemental formula\, and are used to verify by comparison the structure or thermochemistry of an unknown ion or to calibrate the m/z scale of the mass spectrometer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12551
name: relative isotope-ratio difference
def: "Measure of an isotope ratio in a sample of interest relative to a reference defined by the relation \\\[\\delta = \(R_\{\\rm\{sample\}\} - R_\{\\rm\{standard\}\}\)/R_\{\\rm\{standard\}\}\\\] where \\\(R\\\) is the isotope ratio of the element."
comment: "Relative isotope ratio differences are usually small and are therefore often expressed in units of parts per mil with symbol ‰."
comment: "The reference is often an international measurement standard."
comment: "The same relative differences are used to calculate delta values from the abundance of isotopomers and isotopologs, ion currents, frequencies, or optical extinctions."
comment: "Units of parts per thousand (\(\pu{ppt}\), \(\pu{E-3}\)) or parts per million (\(\pu{ppm}\), \(\pu{E-6}\)) are deprecated."
synonym: "delta notation" []
synonym: "isotope delta" []
synonym: "relative difference of isotope ratios" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12452
consider: goldbook:12454
consider: goldbook:12455

[Term]
id: goldbook:12552
name: residual gas analyser
def: "Mass spectrometer used to measure the composition and pressure of gases in an evacuated chamber and to test for leaks in pressurized systems."
synonym: "RGA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12553
name: resolution\: 10 per cent valley definition
def: "Value of \\\(\(m/z\)/\\Delta\(m/z\)\\\) measured for two peaks of equal height in a mass spectrum at m/z and \\\(m/z \\pm \\Delta\(m/z\)\\\) that are separated by a valley which at its lowest point is \\\(\\pu\{10\\%\}\\\) of the height of either peak. For peaks of similar height separated by a valley\, let the height of the valley at its lowest point be \\\(\\pu\{10\\%\}\\\) of the lower peak. Then the resolution \(\\\(\\pu\{10\\%\}\\\) valley definition\) is \\\(\(m/z\)/\\Delta\(m/z\)\\\) and should be given for a number of values of m/z."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12554

[Term]
id: goldbook:12554
name: resolution\: peak width definition
def: "For a single peak corresponding to singly charged ions at mass \\\(m\\\) in a mass spectrum\, the resolution may be expressed as \\\(\(m/z\)/\\Delta\(m/z\)\\\)\, where \\\(\\Delta\(m/z\)\\\) is the width of the peak at a height which is a specified fraction of the maximum peak height. It is recommended that one of three values 50\, 5\, or \\\(\\pu\{0.5\\%\}\\\) should always be used."
comment: "For an isolated symmetrical peak recorded with a system which is linear in the range between \(\pu{5\%}\) and \(\pu{10\%}\) levels of the peak, the \(\pu{5\%}\) peak width definition is equivalent to the \(\pu{10\%}\) valley definition. A common standard is the definition of resolution based upon \(\Delta m\) being full width of the peak at half its maximum (FWHM) height."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12553

[Term]
id: goldbook:12555
name: resonance-enhanced multiphoton ionization
def: "Multiphoton ionization in which the ionization cross section is significantly enhanced because the energy of the incident photons is resonant with an intermediate excited state of the neutral."
synonym: "REMPI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
synonym: "resonance ionization" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12556
name: resonance ion ejection
def: "Mode of ion ejection in an ion trap that relies on an auxiliary radio frequency potential that is applied to the end-cap or trapping electrodes. The potential is tuned to the classical oscillation frequency of a particular ion to eject it."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12447

[Term]
id: goldbook:12557
name: retro Diels–Alder reaction
def: "Ion fragmentation mechanism in which the molecular ion \\\(\\ce\{M^\{+.\}\}\\\) of a cyclic alkene fragments to form a neutral diene and an alkene radical cation or a diene radical cation and an alkene. The reaction is the reverse of the Diels–Alder reaction of organic synthesis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12558
name: reverse geometry
def: "Double-focusing mass spectrometer configuration in which the ion beam traverses the magnetic sector prior to the electric sector."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12405
consider: goldbook:12417
consider: goldbook:12473

[Term]
id: goldbook:12559
name: reverse library search
def: "Process of comparing a subset of the peaks in the mass spectrum of an unknown compound with peaks present in the library mass spectrum. Any peaks in the mass spectrum of the unknown compound that are not in the library spectrum are disregarded."
comment: "A reverse library search measures the extent to which the peaks in a reference spectrum are present in the unknown spectrum and is more effective than a forward library search when peaks arising from two or more components are present in the unknown spectrum"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12418

[Term]
id: goldbook:12560
name: RF-only quadrupole
def: "Transmission quadrupole device in which a sinusoidal radio frequency \(RF\) potential is applied between the connected pairs of opposite rod electrodes in a linear quadrupole\, providing a transmission device for all ions with m/z values above a cut-off value."
comment: "Higher-order multipoles can also be used in this manner."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12363
consider: goldbook:12602

[Term]
id: goldbook:12561
name: ring and double bond equivalent
def: "Conventional measure of the degree of unsaturation of an organic molecule given by \\\(X - Y/2 + Z/2 + 1\\\) where \\\(X\\\) is the number of carbon atoms\, \\\(Y\\\) is the number of hydrogen or halogen atoms and \\\(Z\\\) is the number of nitrogen and phosphorus atoms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12562
name: saddle field gun
def: "Compact ion and fast atom sources for use when small size and high beam intensity are required\, as in fast atom bombardment mass spectrometry. The discharge is produced by electrons oscillating between two cold cathodes in an electric field that possesses a single saddle point. To produce and intensify the plasma the electrons must have long path lengths\, achieved by allowing the electrons to have an oscillatory motion in the saddle-shaped electric field between the cathodes separated by the anode."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12411

[Term]
id: goldbook:12563
name: sampling cone
def: "Component of a spray ionization interface that consists of a cone with a small orifice through which the spray passes into a differentially pumped chamber"
comment: "A capillary can also be used in place of a cone."
comment: "In interfaces that have both a sampling cone and skimmer, the spray passes first through the sampling cone and then through the skimmer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12574
consider: goldbook:12579

[Term]
id: goldbook:12564
name: scan cycle time
def: "Time required to obtain a mass spectrum \(or other mass spectrometric data quantity\) such as in a separation coupled to mass spectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12565
name: secondary neutral mass spectrometry
def: "Mass spectrometry technique in which neutral species ejected from a sample surface as a result of bombardment by a primary beam of atoms or ions are ionized\, most often by photoionization\, prior to analysis."
synonym: "SNMS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12566
name: sector mass spectrometer
def: "Mass spectrometer consisting of one or more magnetic sectors for recording a mass spectrum of a monoenergetic beam of ions. Such instruments may also have one or more electric sectors for energy dispersion that can be arranged for velocity-focusing by compensating for dispersion by the magnetic sector if the beam is not truly monoenergetic. Such a combination provides double focusing of ions of the same m/z\, i.e.\, focusing with respect to both direction and speed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12405
consider: goldbook:12473

[Term]
id: goldbook:12567
name: selected ion flow tube
def: "Device in which m/z selected ions are entrained in an inert carrier gas and subsequently undergo ion/molecule reactions with molecules introduced into the gas flow."
synonym: "SIFT" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12397

[Term]
id: goldbook:12568
name: selected reaction monitoring
def: "Data acquired from one or more specific product ions corresponding to m/z selected precursor ions recorded via two or more stages of mass spectrometry."
comment: "Selected reaction monitoring applied to multiple product ions from one or more precursor ions is known as multiple reaction monitoring."
comment: "Selected reaction monitoring in multiple-stage mass spectrometry is known as consecutive reaction monitoring."
synonym: "SRM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12569
name: self-chemical ionization
def: "Chemical ionization of an analyte where the reagent ion is an ionized form of the analyte or one of its product ions."
synonym: "self-CI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12547

[Term]
id: goldbook:12570
name: sheath flow interface
def: "Capillary electrophoresis to electrospray ionization interface that uses a coaxial flow of make-up liquid that is introduced through a tube that is concentric with the separation capillary."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12475

[Term]
id: goldbook:12571
name: sheath gas
def: "Gas introduced through a tube that is coaxial with the electrospray emitter to pneumatically assist the formation of the sprayed droplets."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12572
name: sheath liquid
def: "Make-up liquid in a sheath flow interface"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12475
consider: goldbook:12570

[Term]
id: goldbook:12573
name: shotgun proteomics
def: "Protein identification using a combination of high-performance liquid chromatography and mass spectrometry in which the proteins in a mixture are digested\, usually by a specific enzyme\, and the resulting peptides are separated by liquid chromatography and identified by tandem mass spectrometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12591

[Term]
id: goldbook:12574
name: skimmer
def: "Cone with a central orifice that intercepts the center of a spray or jet expansion to sample the central portion of the expansion\, for example\, as in a momentum separator."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12493

[Term]
id: goldbook:12575
name: soft ionization
def: "Formation of gas-phase ions without extensive fragmentation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12424

[Term]
id: goldbook:12576
name: sonic spray ionization
def: "Process in which both anions and cations are produced at atmospheric pressure from an ionic solution due to a statistically unbalanced charge distribution in the minute droplets formed by the action of a sonic atomizer."
synonym: "SSI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12579

[Term]
id: goldbook:12577
name: space charge effect
def: "Result of mutual repulsion of particles of like charge \(ions\, electrons\, etc.\) that can limit the current in a charged-particle beam and can also cause some motion of ions in a beam or packet in addition to that caused by external fields."
comment: "Space charge effects on ion trajectories are most noticeable in ion trap instruments that confine large numbers of ions in a small volume."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12447

[Term]
id: goldbook:12578
name: spectral skewing
def: "Deviation of the peak intensities in a mass spectrum from their expected values that occurs when the relative concentration of the various analytes change during acquisition of the mass spectrum."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12579
name: spray ionization
def: "General term used to describe a range of ionization techniques for analytes in solution that involve dispersing the liquid into fine droplets as a component step."
comment: "Most of these techniques are examples of atmospheric pressure ionization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12580
name: stable isotope ratio analysis of amino acids in cell culture
def: "Proteomics technique that detects differences in protein abundance between cultured cell samples using stable isotopic labeling achieved with labeled amino acids in one cell culture and unlabeled ones in a separate culture."
synonym: "SILAC" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12581
name: stable isotope standards and capture by anti-peptide antibodies
def: "Method for absolute quantitation of a protein or proteins in a multiplexed fashion using isotope-labeled peptides as surrogate internal standards. The labeled peptides are produced by synthesizing a gene coding for each desired peptide\, cell-free transcription\, and translation of this gene in a medium containing \\\(\\ce\{^\{13\}C6\}\\\)-labeled lysine\, and digesting with trypsin the expressed protein composed of the desired concatenated peptides. For low-abundance proteins the sensitivity is increased by selective enrichment of the target peptides by antibody capture."
synonym: "SISCAPA" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12589

[Term]
id: goldbook:12582
name: static field
def: "Electric or magnetic field that does not change in time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12583
name: Stevenson’s rule
def: "Rule stating that in competing fragmentations the product ion formed from its neutral species counterpart with the lower ionization energy will usually be the more abundant."
comment: "The original version of this rule referred to reliability of determination of thermochemical data obtained for an ion produced by fragmentation of a single \(\ce{\upsigma\mbox{-}bond}\) in an odd-electron ion \(\ce{X{-}Y^{+.}}\), but was later extended to the version in more common use since then."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12584
name: stored waveform inverse fourier transform
def: "Technique to create excitation waveforms for ions in Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers or Paul ion traps. An excitation waveform in the time-domain is generated by taking the inverse Fourier transform of an appropriate frequency-domain programmed excitation spectrum\, in which the resonance frequencies of ions to be excited are included."
comment: "This procedure may be used for selection of precursor ions in MSn experiments."
synonym: "SWIFT" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12498
consider: goldbook:12516

[Term]
id: goldbook:12585
name: supercritical fluid chromatography-mass spectrometry
def: "Combined technique in which a mixture of analytes is separated into solutions of individual components by chromatography that uses a supercritical fluid as mobile phase\, followed by the ionization of the separation effluent in the ion source of a mass spectrometer."
synonym: "SFC-MS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "supercritical fluid chromatography/mass spectrometry (SFC/MS)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12586
name: surface-enhanced laser desorption/ionization
def: "Variant of matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization \(MALDI\) in which the matrix is replaced by a surface coating of a chromatographic stationary phase designed to selectively retain different subsets of proteins or peptides from a mixture depending on their physico-chemical properties or biochemical affinity characteristics."
comment: "Originally this technique was named surface-enhanced affinity capture (SEAC) to distinguish it from surface-enhanced neat desorption (SEND) where the surface coating is designed to increase the efficiency of laser desorption."
synonym: "SELDI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12462

[Term]
id: goldbook:12587
name: surface-induced dissociation
def: "Fragmentation that results from the collision of an ion with a surface."
synonym: "SID" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12588
name: surface-induced reaction
def: "Process wherein a reactant ion interacts with a surface to produce either chemically different species or a change in the internal energy of the reactant ion."
synonym: "SIR" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12589
name: surrogate internal standard
def: "Compound added in accurately known amounts to a sample to be analyzed for a specified analyte. The surrogate internal standard is chemically similar to the analyte so that losses in the analytical procedure are the same for both and thus the analyte concentration can be determined relative to that of the standard."
comment: "In quantitative mass spectrometry the preferred type is an isotope-labeled version of the analyte."
comment: "The abbreviated term "internal standard" is often used."
synonym: "internal standard" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12608

[Term]
id: goldbook:12590
name: sustained off-resonance irradiation
def: "Procedure associated with Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers to facilitate ion/neutral reactions such as low-energy collision-induced dissociation in which a radio-frequency electric field\, slightly off-resonance with respect to the cyclotron frequency of the reactant ion\, cyclically accelerates and decelerates the reactant ion that is confined in the Penning ion trap. As a consequence\, the orbit does not exceed the dimensions of the ion trap but maintains a high average translational energy for an extended time that activates an ion/neutral process."
synonym: "SORI" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12472
consider: goldbook:12521

[Term]
id: goldbook:12591
name: tandem mass spectrometry in space
def: "Tandem mass spectrometry procedure in which product ion spectra are recorded for ion beams in m/z analyzers separated in space. Specific m/z separation functions are designed so that in one section of the instrument ions are selected\, dissociated in an intermediate region\, and the product ions are then transmitted to another analyzer for m/z separation and data acquisition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12535

[Term]
id: goldbook:12592
name: tandem mass spectrometry in time
def: "Tandem mass spectrometry procedure in which product ion spectra are recorded in a single m/z analyzer \(such as a Paul ion trap\, linear ion trap\, or Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometer\) in discrete steps over time. Ions in a specific m/z range are selected\, dissociated\, and the product ions analyzed sequentially in time."
comment: "Mass spectrometers that can perform tandem mass spectrometry in time can also perform MSn."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12465
consider: goldbook:12498
consider: goldbook:12516
consider: goldbook:12535

[Term]
id: goldbook:12593
name: Taylor cone
def: "Conical shape of the liquid emanating from a capillary under high potential\, as in electrospray or other electrohydrodynamic spray processes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12594
name: thermospray ionization
def: "Spray ionization in which a liquid is flowed through a heated capillary to produce a spray of droplets and solvent vapor. Ions are formed due to the statistical imbalance of charges in the droplets or by a heated filament."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12579

[Term]
id: goldbook:12595
name: thin layer chromatography-mass spectrometry
def: "Technique by which a mixture of analytes is separated into individual components by liquid chromatography\, followed by the ionization of the separated species by an ion source of a mass spectrometer."
synonym: "TLC-MS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "thin layer chromatography/mass spectrometry (TLC/MS)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12596
name: time-lag focusing
def: "Energy focusing of ions formed in the gas phase in a time-of-flight mass spectrometer that is accomplished by introducing a time delay between the formation of the ions and the application of the accelerating potential pulse."
synonym: "TLF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
