consider: goldbook:12383

[Term]
id: goldbook:12597
name: tolyl ion
def: "Even-electron \\\(\\ce\{C7H7^\{+\}\}\\\) ion with the same carbon skeleton as toluene that has lost a hydrogen atom from one of the ring carbons that carries the positive charge."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12346

[Term]
id: goldbook:12598
name: toroidal ion trap
def: "Ion trapping device based on the three-dimensional structure formed by rotating the cross-section of a quadrupole ion trap about the edge perpendicular to the plane of the ring electrode. The resulting trapping region is toroidal."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12516

[Term]
id: goldbook:12599
name: total ion current electropherogram
def: "Plot of the total ion current in each of a series of mass spectra that are recorded as a function of electrophoresis time."
synonym: "total ion current electrophorogram" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12600
name: total ion current profile
def: "Any plot of total ion current in a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of time\, including total ion current chromatogram\, total ion current electropherogram\, flow injection mass spectrometry\, or any other time dependent sampling."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12410
consider: goldbook:12415
consider: goldbook:12599

[Term]
id: goldbook:12601
name: transmission efficiency
def: "Ratio of the number of ions leaving a region of a mass spectrometer to the number entering that region."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12602
name: transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer
def: "Mass spectrometer that consists of an array of four parallel rod electrodes whose centers form the corners of a square and whose opposing electrode pairs are connected. The electric potential applied between the connected pairs of rods is a superposition of a static potential and a sinusoidal radio frequency potential. The motion of an ion in the \\\(x\\mbox\{-\}y\\\) plane perpendicular to the length direction of the rod electrodes is described by the Mathieu equation whose solutions show that ions in a particular m/z range can be transmitted along the \\\(z\\mbox\{-\}\\rm\{axis\}\\\)."
synonym: "quadrupole mass analyzer" []
synonym: "quadrupole mass filter" []
synonym: "quadrupole mass spectrometer" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12603
name: transport region
def: "Region in a mass spectrometer in which an ion beam is transported from the ion source to the ion optics or from one ion optical element to the next."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12444

[Term]
id: goldbook:12604
name: triple quadrupole mass spectrometer
def: "Tandem mass spectrometer comprising two transmission quadrupole mass spectrometers in series\, with a \(non-selecting\) RF-only quadrupole \(or other multipole\) between them to act as a collision cell."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12361
consider: goldbook:12560
consider: goldbook:12602

[Term]
id: goldbook:12605
name: unimolecular dissociation
def: "Fragmentation reaction in which the molecularity of the reaction system is unity. The dissociation may arise from the extra energy acquired by a metastable ion produced in the ion source or that provided by collisional excitation of a stable ion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12606
name: unit mass resolution
def: "Mass resolution such that it is possible to clearly distinguish a peak corresponding to a singly charged ion from its neighbors \\\(\\pu\{1 u\}\\\) away\, usually with no more than \\\(\\pu\{5\\!-\\! 10\\%\}\\\) overlap."
comment: "This term is most frequently used to describe resolution obtained using a Paul ion trap or a transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12516
consider: goldbook:12602

[Term]
id: goldbook:12607
name: v-ion
def: "High-energy product ion of a protonated peptide formally equivalent to a y-ion with the ionizing proton on the \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)-terminus\, but with elimination of \\\(\\ce\{HR\}\\\) from the \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)-terminus where \\\(\\ce\{R\}\\\) is the side-chain on the \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)-atom of the \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)-terminal residue\, to give a \(\\\(\\ce\{H2N^\{+\}=CH-CO\\bond\{-\}\}\\\)\) structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12613

[Term]
id: goldbook:12608
name: volumetric internal standard
def: "Compound added in a fixed reproducible amount to a solution to be analyzed by gas chromatography to permit corrections for uncontrolled variations in injected volumes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12589

[Term]
id: goldbook:12609
name: Wahrhaftig diagram
def: "Diagram illustrating the relative contributions in unimolecular dissociation of an ion\, for example\, by homolytic cleavage of a single bond\, and fragmentation following rearrangement. The diagram is in two parts with a common horizontal axis representing the internal energy of the ion. The vertical axis in one part of the diagram shows the two types of rate constant on a logarithmic scale\, and that for the other portion of the diagram indicates the distribution function for internal energy of the ion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12605

[Term]
id: goldbook:12610
name: Wien filter
def: "Mass spectrometer in which m/z separation is achieved using crossed electric and magnetic fields."
comment: "It can also be operated as a charged particle energy analyzer or monochromator."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12611
name: w-ion
def: "High-energy product ion of a protonated peptide formally equivalent to a z-ion that has lost the part of the \\\(\\ce\{N\}\\\)-terminal side-chain starting at the \\\(\\ce\{\\upgamma\\mbox\{-\}carbon\}\\\) \(if any\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12614

[Term]
id: goldbook:12612
name: x-ion
def: "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\\(\\ce\{C-C\}\\\) bond."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12613
name: y-ion
def: "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\\(\\ce\{C-N\}\\\) bond."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12614
name: z-ion
def: "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\\(\\ce\{N-C\}\\\) bond."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12615
name: ADMET
def: "Acronym referring to the absorption\, distribution\, metabolism\, excretion\, and toxicity profile or processes for a xenobiotic upon its administration in vivo."
comment: "ADME is also used to delineate these selected parameters within the context of a xenobiotic’s pharmacokinetic profile. Because any of the five characteristics may become hurdles during drug development, ADMET behaviour is typically studied and optimized among efficacious analogues during the early drug discovery stage by using in vitro models that attempt to predict such behaviours in clinical studies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12646

[Term]
id: goldbook:12616
name: allosteric antagonist
def: "Compound that binds to a receptor at a site separate from\, but actively coupled to\, that of the endogenous agonist to reduce actively receptor signals."
comment: "The terms "allosteric antagonist" and "noncompetitive antagonist" are often synonymous but not necessarily so."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12694

[Term]
id: goldbook:12617
name: alpha-helix
def: "Secondary 3D structure of a protein or peptide containing a right-handed coiled or spiral conformation\, in which every backbone \\\(\\ce\{N-H\}\\\) group donates a hydrogen bond to the backbone \\\(\\ce\{C=O\}\\\) group of the amino acid four residues earlier."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12618
name: analogue
def: "Chemical compound having structural similarity to a reference compound."
comment: "Despite the structural similarity, an analogue may display different chemical and/or biological properties, as is often intentionally the case during design and synthesis to optimize either efficacy or ADMET properties within a given series."
synonym: "analog" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12615
consider: goldbook:12619
consider: goldbook:12658

[Term]
id: goldbook:12619
name: analogue-based drug discovery
def: "Strategy for drug discovery and/or optimization in which structural modification of an existing drug provides a new drug with improved chemical and/or biological properties."
comment: "Within the context of analogue-based drug discovery, three categories of drug analogues are recognized: Compounds possessing structural, chemical, and pharmacological similarities, termed "direct analogues" and sometimes referred to as "me-too" drugs; compounds possessing structural and often chemical but not pharmacological similarities, termed "structural analogues"; and structurally different compounds displaying similar pharmacological properties, termed "pharmacological analogues"."
synonym: "analog-based drug discovery" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12679
consider: goldbook:12681

[Term]
id: goldbook:12620
name: ATP binding cassette protein
def: "Large gene family of transporter proteins that bind ATP and use the energy to transport substrates \(e.g.\, sugars\, amino acids\, metal ions\, peptides\, proteins\, and a large number of hydrophobic compounds and metabolites\) across lipid membranes."
comment: "These proteins have an important role in limiting oral absorption and brain penetration of xenobiotics."
synonym: "ABC protein" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12653
consider: goldbook:12704

[Term]
id: goldbook:12621
name: attrition rate
def: "Rate of loss of drug candidates during progression through the optimisation and developmental stages while on route to the marketplace."
comment: "It has been estimated that for every \(\pu{10000}\) compounds examined during the early stages of biological testing just one reaches the market."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12622
name: autoinduction
def: "Capacity of a drug to induce enzymes that mediate its own metabolism."
comment: "This often results in lower, often sub-therapeutic, drug exposure on prolonged or multiple dosing."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12623
name: back-up compound
def: "Molecule selected as a replacement for the lead drug candidate should this subsequently fail during further preclinical evaluation or in clinical studies."
comment: "Ideally, a back-up should be pharmacologically equivalent to the lead drug but have significant structural differences. Possession of a distinct core scaffold is optimal."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12724

[Term]
id: goldbook:12624
name: best-in-class
def: "Drug acting on a specific molecular target that provides the best balance between efficacy and adverse effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12684

[Term]
id: goldbook:12625
name: beta-barrel
def: "Secondary 3D protein structure containing a large beta-sheet that twists and coils to form a closed structure in which the first-strand hydrogen bonds to the last."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12626

[Term]
id: goldbook:12626
name: beta-sheet
def: "Secondary 3D structure of a protein that takes on a flat\, pleated appearance."
comment: "Other common protein structural motifs are the alpha-helix and beta-barrel."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
