[Term]
id: goldbook:12647
name: druggability
def: "Capacity of a molecular target to be modulated in a favourable manner by a small-molecule drug."
comment: "It is estimated that only around \(\pu{10\%}\) of the human genome affords druggable targets."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12648
name: drug repurposing
def: "Strategy that seeks to discover new applications for an existing drug that were not previously referenced and not currently prescribed or investigated."
comment: "Various additional synonymous terms have been used to describe the process of drug repurposing. All appear to be used interchangeably."
synonym: "drug repositioning" []
synonym: "drug reprofiling" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12649
name: drug safety
def: "Assessment of the nontolerable biological effects of a drug."
comment: "Because the nontolerable effects of a drug are directly related to its concentration or dose, safety is generally ranked relative to the dose required to obtain the desirable effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
