property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12658
name: follow-on drug
def: "Drug having a similar mechanism of action to an existing drug."
comment: "Compounds may be of the same or different chemical class. A therapeutic advantage over first-in-class drugs must be demonstrated for regulatory approval."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12618
consider: goldbook:12619
consider: goldbook:12657

[Term]
id: goldbook:12659
name: fragment
def: "Low-molar-mass ligand \(typically smaller than \\\(\\pu\{200 Da\}\\\)\) that binds to a target with low affinity but high ligand efficiency."
comment: "Typically fragments have affinities in a concentration interval from \(\pu{0.1 mm}\) to \(\pu{1.0 mM}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12660
name: fragment-based lead discovery
def: "Screening libraries of low-molar-mass compounds \(typically \\\(\\pu\{120\\!\{-\}\\! 250 Da\}\\\)\) using sensitive biophysical techniques capable of detecting weakly binding lead compounds."
comment: "X-ray structures are frequently used to drive the optimisation of fragment hits to leads."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12659
consider: goldbook:12664
consider: goldbook:12677

[Term]
id: goldbook:12661
name: frequent hitter
def: "Structural feature that regularly results in a positive response in a variety of high-throughput or primary screens."
comment: "Such compounds often exert their actions through nonspecific mechanisms and are therefore unreliable leads."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12662
name: G protein
def: "Member of a family of membrane-associated proteins which on activation by cellular receptors lead to signal transduction."
synonym: "guanine binding protein" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12663
name: green chemistry
def: "Invention\, design\, and application of chemical products and processes to reduce or eliminate the use and generation of hazardous substances."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12664
name: hit
def: "Molecule that produces reproducible activity above a defined threshold in a biological assay and whose structural identity has been established."
comment: "Hits typically derive from high-throughput screening initiatives or other relatively extensive primary assays and do not become true hits until fully validated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12665
name: hit expansion
def: "Generation of additional compound sets that contain chemical motifs and scaffolds that have activity in the primary screen."
comment: "This methodology permits the identification of additional hits and new scaffolds and develops structure-activity relationships around existing hits."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12664
consider: goldbook:12724

[Term]
id: goldbook:12666
name: hit-to-lead chemistry
def: "Process by which a proven molecule or series derived from high-throughput screening or primary screens is chemically optimised to a viable lead or series."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12677

[Term]
id: goldbook:12667
name: homology model
def: "Computational representation of a protein built from the 3D structure of a similar protein or proteins using alignment techniques and homology arguments."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12668
name: hydrophobic fragmental constant
def: "Representation of the lipophilicity contribution of a constituent part of a structure to the total lipophilicity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12669
name: inhibitory concentration at 50%
def: "The concentration of an enzyme inhibitor or receptor antagonist that reduces the enzyme activity or agonist response by \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\)."
comment: "\(\rm{IC}_{50}\) values are influenced by experimental conditions (e.g., substrate or agonist concentration, which should be specified)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12670

[Term]
id: goldbook:12670
name: inhibition constant
def: "Equilibrium dissociation constant of an enzyme-inhibitor complex\: \\\(K_\{\\rm\{i\}\} = \[\\ce\{E\}\]\[\\ce\{I\}\]/\[\\ce\{EI\}\]\\\). The equilibrium dissociation constant of a receptor-ligand complex."
comment: "This value is usually obtained through competition binding experiments, where the \(K_{\rm{i}}\) is determined after the IC50 obtained in a competition assay performed in the presence of a known concentration of labeled reference ligand."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12669

[Term]
id: goldbook:12672
name: intrinsic solubility
def: "Equilibrium solubility of the uncharged form of an ionisable compound at a pH where it is fully unionised. \\\[\\ce\{HA\(s\)  HA\(aq\)\} \\quad \(1\)\\\] \\\[\\ce\{HA\(aq\)  H^\{+\}\(aq\) + A^\{-\}\(aq\)\} \\quad \(2\)\\\]"
comment: "The intrinsic solubility can be determined from the analytical composition at a \(\pu{pH}\) where \([\ce{HA}]\) is very much greater than \([\ce{A^{-}}]\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12654
consider: goldbook:12676
consider: goldbook:12730

[Term]
id: goldbook:12673
name: investigational new drug
def: "Drug not yet approved for general use by the national authority\, such as the Food and Drug Administration of the United States of America\, but undergoing clinical investigation to assess its safety and efficacy."
synonym: "IND" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12674
name: ionotropic receptor
def: "Transmembrane ion channel that opens or closes in response to the binding of a ligand."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12675
name: kinase
def: "Enzyme that transfers a phosphate group from high-energy donor molecules\, such as ATP\, to specific target molecules."
synonym: "phosphotransferase" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12676
name: kinetic solubility
def: "Composition of a solution with respect to a compound when its induced precipitate first appears."
synonym: "turbidimetric solubility" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12654
consider: goldbook:12672
consider: goldbook:12730

[Term]
id: goldbook:12677
name: lead
def: "Compound \(or compound series\) that satisfies predefined minimum criteria for further structure and activity optimization."
comment: "Typically, a lead will demonstrate appropriate activity, selectivity, tractable structure-activity relationship and have confirmed activity in a relevant cell-based assay."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12678

[Term]
id: goldbook:12678
name: lead validation
def: "Process by which a lead compound is authenticated by the confirmation of its expected pharmacological properties."
comment: "Usually, a cluster of structurally similar compounds showing discernable structure-activity relationships will support the validation process."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12677

[Term]
id: goldbook:12679
name: ligand-based drug design
def: "Method of drug discovery and/or optimization in which the pursuit of new structures and/or structural modifications is based upon one or more ligands known to interact with the molecular target of interest."
comment: "This approach is applicable even when no structural detail of the target is known. In such cases a series of analogues is usually prepared and tested to produce structure-activity relationship data that can be extrapolated to indirectly derive a topographical map of the biological surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12618
consider: goldbook:12619
consider: goldbook:12684

[Term]
id: goldbook:12680
name: metabotropic receptor
def: "Receptor that modulates electric potential-gated channels via G-proteins."
comment: "The interaction can occur entirely within the membrane or by the generation of diffusible second messengers. The involvement of G-proteins causes the activation of these receptors to last tens of seconds to minutes, in contrast with the brief effect of ionotropic receptors."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12662
consider: goldbook:12674

[Term]
id: goldbook:12681
name: me-too drug
def: "Term applied to drug analogues that offer no significant advantage over the prototype compound."
comment: "Continued use of this term is not recommended."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12618
consider: goldbook:12658

[Term]
id: goldbook:12682
name: microRNA
def: "Small single-stranded RNA molecules that play a significant role in the post-transcriptional regulation of gene expression."
comment: "MicroRNA usually comprises approximately 22 nucleotides."
synonym: "miRNA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12683
name: molecular descriptor
def: "Parameter that characterizes a specific structural or physicochemical aspect of a molecule."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12684
name: molecular target
def: "Protein \(e.g.\, receptor\, enzyme\, or ion channel\)\, RNA\, or DNA that is implicated in a clinical disorder or the propagation of any untoward event."
comment: "Usually, biochemical, pharmacological, or genomic information supporting the role of such a target in disease will be available."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12685
name: multidrug resistance
def: "Characteristic of cells that confers resistance to the effects of several different classes of drugs."
comment: "There are several forms of drug resistance. Each is determined by genes that govern how cells will respond to chemical agents. One type of multidrug resistance involves the ability to eject several drugs out of cells (e.g., efflux pumps such as P-glycoprotein)."
synonym: "MDR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12653
consider: goldbook:12704

[Term]
id: goldbook:12686
name: multiparameter optimisation
def: "Drug-likeness penetrability algorithm derived from CLOGP\, clogD\, molar mass\, topological polar surface area\, number of hydrogen-bond donors\, and \\\(\\pu\{p\}K_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\)."
comment: "The MPO desirability score is larger or equal to 4 on a scale of 0 to 6."
synonym: "MPO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12687
name: multitarget-directed ligand
def: "Ligand acting on more than one distinct molecular target. Targets may be of the same or different mechanistic classes."
synonym: "MTDL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "multitarget drug" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12684

[Term]
id: goldbook:12688
name: multitarget drug discovery
def: "Deliberate design of compounds that act on more than one molecular target."
synonym: "MTDD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12684

[Term]
id: goldbook:12689
name: Murcko assembly
def: "Core scaffold of a molecule that remains after all chain substituents that do not terminate in a ring are removed. Single atoms connected by a double bond are typically also retained."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12724

[Term]
id: goldbook:12690
name: neglected disease
def: "Term used to emphasise an imbalance between therapeutic needs and resource allocation."
comment: "Different groups define neglected diseases differently, but typically they include diseases such as schistosomiasis, Chagas disease, tuberculosis, and malaria, as well as other parasitic and vector-borne diseases."
comment: "The terms "tropical disease" and "neglected disease" are sometimes indistinguishable or used interchangeably."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12698

[Term]
id: goldbook:12691
name: neutral antagonist
def: "Ligand that blocks the responses of a receptor to both agonists and inverse agonists with the same intensity. It binds to the receptor without evoking any change of conformation or change to the ratio of activated to inactivated conformations."
comment: "Perfect neutral antagonism is difficult to achieve."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12692
name: new chemical entity
def: "Drug that contains no active moiety previously approved for use by the national authority\, such as the U.S. Food and Drug Administration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12693

[Term]
id: goldbook:12693
name: new molecular entity
def: "Active ingredient that has never before been approved in any form by the national authority\, such as the U.S. Food and Drug Administration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12692

[Term]
id: goldbook:12694
name: noncompetitive antagonist
def: "Functional antagonist that either binds irreversibly to a receptor or to a site distinct from that of the natural agonist."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12616

[Term]
id: goldbook:12695
name: nuclear hormone receptor
def: "Ligand-activated transcription factor that regulates gene expression by interacting with specific DNA sequences upstream of its target gene\(s\)."
synonym: "nuclear receptor" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12696
name: obviousness
def: "Term associated with intellectual property wherein the latter’s patentability is assessed relative to the combination of more than one item of 'prior art'."
comment: "To be patentable within the context of medicinal chemistry, a given compound must be: (i) novel, in that its specific arrangement of atoms has never been previously disclosed; (ii) non-obvious, in that its specific arrangement of atoms is not readily suggested to be of benefit by a person having ordinary skill in the art upon considering two or more other, previously disclosed structures; and, (iii) useful, in that it should have some benefit, the disclosure of the latter encompassing a valid "reduction to practice"."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12702

[Term]
id: goldbook:12697
name: off-target effect
def: "Pharmacological action induced by any molecule at molecular/biological sites distinct from that for which it was designed."
comment: "Such effects are dose-dependent and may be beneficial, adverse, or neutral."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12698
name: orphan disease
def: "Disease for which drug research\, development\, and marketing is economically unfavourable."
comment: "Sometimes the term "rare disease" is used synonymously with orphan disease, although there is a slight difference. For example, a rare disease is so uncommon that there is no drug development effort."
comment: "The poor commercial environment could be due to a lack of economic incentives or a lack of understanding of the diseases or a combination of both."
comment: "Which diseases are classified as orphan depends strongly on the country that classifies it. In the United States, for example, any disease affecting less than \(\pu{200000}\) people is considered an orphan or rare disease. Europe and countries such as Japan, Australia, and Singapore have a different definition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12690
consider: goldbook:12699

[Term]
id: goldbook:12699
name: orphan drug
def: "Pharmaceutical agent that has been approved specifically to treat a rare and commercially unfavourable medical condition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12698

[Term]
id: goldbook:12700
name: orphan receptor
def: "Receptor for which an endogenous ligand has yet to be identified."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12701
name: parallel synthesis
def: "Simultaneous preparation of sets of discrete compounds in arrays of physically separate reaction vessels or microcompartments without interchange of intermediates during the assembly process."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12702
name: patentability
def: "Set of criteria that must be satisfied in order to achieve commercial exclusivity for an invention."
comment: "These criteria are essentially the same in all major countries and include: suitability, novelty, inventiveness, utility, and the provision of an adequate description."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12696

[Term]
id: goldbook:12703
name: peptoid
def: "Peptide-like oligomer consisting of repeating \\\(N\\\)-substituted glycine units  where \\\(\\ce\{R1\}\\\) to \\\(\\ce\{R4\}\\\) are typically alkyl or aryl and may be the same or different."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12704
name: P-glycoprotein
def: "ATP-binding cassette transporter responsible for the efflux of small molecules from cells."
comment: "P-glycoproteins can play a major role in limiting brain penetration and restricting the intestinal absorption of drugs. Their over-expression in cancer cells becomes a common mechanism of multidrug resistance."
synonym: "Pgp" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12620
consider: goldbook:12653
consider: goldbook:12685

[Term]
id: goldbook:12705
name: pharmacogenetics
def: "Study of inherited differences \(variation\) in drug metabolism and response."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12706

[Term]
id: goldbook:12706
name: pharmacogenomics
def: "General study of all of the many different genes that determine drug behaviour."
comment: "The distinction between the terms pharmacogenetics and pharmacogenomics has blurred with time. and they are now frequently used interchangeably."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12705

[Term]
id: goldbook:12707
name: phase 0 clinical studies
def: "Exploratory first-in-human trials that involve microdosing of drug to allow the assessment of pharmacokinetic parameters with limited drug exposure."
comment: "These trials have no therapeutic or diagnostic intent but are designed to assist decision making by providing bioavailability, metabolism, and other limited data from a small number of patients."
synonym: "exploratory investigational new drug" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12708
consider: goldbook:12709
consider: goldbook:12710
consider: goldbook:12711

[Term]
id: goldbook:12708
name: phase I clinical studies
def: "Initial introduction of an investigational new drug into humans."
comment: "These studies are designed to determine the metabolic and pharmacologic actions of the drug in humans, the side-effects associated with increasing doses, and, if possible, to gain early evidence on effectiveness."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12673
consider: goldbook:12709
consider: goldbook:12710
consider: goldbook:12711

[Term]
id: goldbook:12709
name: phase II clinical studies
def: "Controlled clinical studies conducted in a limited number of individuals to obtain some preliminary data on the effectiveness of an investigational new drug for a particular indication or indications in patients with the disease or condition."
comment: "Phase II clinical trials have two subclasses, IIa and IIb. Phase IIa trials are essentially pilot clinical trials designed to evaluate efficacy (and safety) in selected populations of patients with the disease or condition to be treated, diagnosed, or prevented. Phase IIb trials extend those of Phase IIa to well-controlled trials that evaluate the same parameters in similar patient populations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12673
consider: goldbook:12707
consider: goldbook:12708
consider: goldbook:12710
consider: goldbook:12711

[Term]
id: goldbook:12710
name: phase III clinical studies
def: "Expanded controlled and uncontrolled trials in humans."
comment: "These trials are performed after preliminary evidence suggesting effectiveness of the drug has been obtained in phase II, and are intended to gather the additional information about effectiveness and safety that is needed to evaluate the overall benefit/risk relationship of the drug."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12707
consider: goldbook:12708
consider: goldbook:12709
consider: goldbook:12711

[Term]
id: goldbook:12711
name: phase IV clinical studies
def: "Extended post-marketing studies in humans."
comment: "These trials are designed to broaden information concerning treatment risks, benefits, and optimal drug use."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12707
consider: goldbook:12708
consider: goldbook:12709
consider: goldbook:12710

[Term]
id: goldbook:12712
name: phenotypic screening
def: "Evaluation of compounds \(small molecules\, peptides\, siRNA\, etc.\) in cells\, tissues\, or organisms for their ability to modify the system in a measurable manner."
comment: "Phenotypic screening differs from target-based screens in that it assesses the overall response of the compound under investigation rather than its specific response on a purified molecular target. Advances in molecular biology resulted in a marked shift away from phenotypic screening, although the latter is now regaining popularity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12727

[Term]
id: goldbook:12713
name: pipeline
def: "Discovery and development compound portfolio of a pharmaceutical company or research organization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12714
name: pivotal study
def: "Experiment that provides strong support for or against the drug or molecular target under investigation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12684
consider: goldbook:12718

[Term]
id: goldbook:12715
name: potential genotoxic impurity
def: "Confirmed or suspected presence of one or more known genotoxic materials in an active pharmaceutical ingredient."
comment: "Typically, such impurities arise from reactive intermediates involved in the synthetic pathway and have the potential to adversely affect subsequent genotoxicity tests."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12716
name: preclinical candidate
def: "Optimised lead compound successfully passing key screening\, selectivity\, and physicochemical criteria sufficient to warrant further detailed pharmacological and pharmacokinetic evaluation in animal models."
comment: "Critical studies usually include bioavailability, therapeutic efficacy in an appropriate disease model, and side-effect profiling."
synonym: "PCC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "safety assessment candidate" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12677

[Term]
id: goldbook:12717
name: privileged structure
def: "Substructural feature that confers desirable \(often drug-like\) properties on compounds containing that feature. They often consist of a semi-rigid scaffold that presents multiple hydrophobic residues without undergoing hydrophobic collapse."
comment: "For example, diazepam (below) in which the diphenylmethane moiety prevents association of the aromatic rings. "
comment: "Such structures are commonly found to confer activity against different targets belonging to the same receptor family."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12724

[Term]
id: goldbook:12718
name: proof of concept
def: "Procedure by which a specific therapeutic mechanism or treatment/diagnostic paradigm is shown to be beneficial."
comment: "Similar to, and often simultaneously associated with, that for a new drug candidate. This process usually involves an early supporting step prior to clinical testing and final validation within human studies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
