[Term]
id: goldbook:12727
name: small inhibitory double-stranded RNA
def: "Small RNA fragments that can combine with specific genes to silence their expression."
comment: "siRNAs are powerful tools that are often used for manipulating gene expression during molecular target validation."
synonym: "siRNA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "small interfering double-stranded RNA" []
