id: goldbook:12741
name: alpha relaxation peak
def: "Highest-temperature peak or lowest-frequency peak in the loss curve of a polymer."
comment: "Secondary relaxation peaks occurring successively at lower temperatures or higher frequencies are termed the beta (β-), gamma (γ-), relaxation or loss peaks."
synonym: "alpha loss peak" []
synonym: "α-loss peak" []
synonym: "α-relaxation peak" []
