[Term]
id: goldbook:12751
name: conformational melting
def: "Step-like increase in the conformational entropy of macromolecules\, or parts of macromolecules."
comment: "Conformational melting normally occurs along with crystalline melting in a partially crystalline polymer."
comment: "This melting can be caused by a temperature change or by interaction with a solvent."
