[Term]
id: goldbook:12752
name: conformational transition
def: "Transition between two conformational states."
comment: "Conformational melting is a type of conformational transition."
comment: "Conformational transitions are relevant in biopolymers, for example, nucleic acids and proteins or complex systems like lipid membranes, where a number of neighbouring local minima in the profile of the Gibbs energy are possible. A conformational transition can result in important biological action."
