def: "Enthalpy change observed near the glass transition when a sample is heated at a rate different from that at which it was cooled down\, or observed after annealing in the glassy state below the glass-transition temperature."
comment: "Enthalpy relaxation can be described by the Kohlrausch–Williams–Watts equation."
comment: "Enthalpy relaxation is caused by the transformation of a glassy material to a more stable glass."
comment: "Enthalpy relaxation reflects physical aging."
comment: "Moduli, stress–strain behaviour, and molecular motions are affected by enthalpy relaxation."
