[Term]
id: goldbook:12767
name: forced sinusoidal oscillation
def: "Deformation of a material by the application of a small sinusoidal strain \(\\\(\\gamma\\\)\) such that \\\[\\gamma = \\gamma_\{0\} \\cos \\omega t\\\] where \\\(\\gamma_\{0\}\\\) and \\\(\\omega\\\) are positive constants."
comment: "For linear viscoelastic behaviour, a sinusoidal stress (\(\sigma\)) results from the sinusoidal strain with \(\sigma = \sigma_{0} \cos (\omega t + \delta) = \sigma_{0} \cos \delta \cos \omega t - \sigma_{0} \sin \delta \sin \omega t\)."
comment: "\(\gamma\) may be in simple shear or uniaxial deformation."
comment: "\(\gamma_{0}\) is the strain amplitude."
comment: "\(\omega\) is the angular velocity of the circular motion equivalent to a sinusoidal frequency \(v\) with \(\omega = 2\uppi \nu\). The unit of \(\omega\) is \(\pu{rad s-1}\)."
synonym: "forced oscillation" []
synonym: "sinusoidal oscillation" []
