[Term]
id: goldbook:12769
name: fragility index
def: "Quantity characterising the fragility or the strength of a glass at a given temperature \\\[m = \\left \(\\frac\{\\rm\{d\} \\log_\{10\} \\tau\}\{\{\\rm\{d\}\} \(T_\{\\rm\{g\}\}/T\)\} \\right\)_\{T = T_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\}\\\] \\\(\\tau\\\) = relaxation time \[\\\(\\pu\{s\}\\\)\]; \\\(T_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\\\) = glass-transition temperature \[\\\(\\pu\{K\}\\\)\]; \\\(T\\\) = temperature \[\\\(\\pu\{K\}\\\)\]."
comment: "The value of the fragility index depends on the thermal history of the glass."
comment: "The values of \(m\) range from \(m \approx 16\) for a very strong glass to \(m \approx 250\) for a very fragile glass."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12768
consider: goldbook:12773
consider: goldbook:12804

[Term]
id: goldbook:12770
name: free oscillation
def: "Oscillatory deformation of a material specimen with the motion generated without the continuous application of an external force."
comment: "For any real sample of material, the resulting oscillatory deformation is one of decaying amplitudes."
synonym: "free sinusoidal oscillation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
