[Term]
id: goldbook:12772
name: gamma relaxation peak
def: "Third-highest-temperature or third-lowest-frequency peak in the loss curve of a polymer."
comment: "The \(\gamma\)-peak is typically related to localised motions involving side groups or a few atoms of a polymer chain."
synonym: "gamma loss peak" []
synonym: "γ-loss peak" []
synonym: "γ-relaxation peak" []
