[Term]
id: goldbook:12773
name: glass
def: "Amorphous matter in the glassy state\, i.e.\, below its glass-transition temperature."
comment: "A glass is usually described as a solid, as most physical properties vary in a manner similar to those in the crystalline state. However, considering the ongoing debate about the nature of the glass transition, and the ability of some glasses to flow, some authors prefer to consider glasses in the context of the liquid state."
comment: "The creep compliance of a glass is less than \(\pu{E-9 N-1 m2}\), and the dynamic viscosity larger than \(\pu{E4 Pa s}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12754
consider: goldbook:12774

[Term]
id: goldbook:12774
name: glassy state
def: "State of amorphous matter below its glass-transition temperature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12775
name: Hoffman–Weeks plot
def: "Plot of melting temperature\, \\\(T_\{\\rm\{m\}\}\\\)\, vs. crystallisation temperature\, \\\(T_\{\\rm\{cr\}\}\\\)."
comment: "A Hoffman–Weeks plot is used to determine the equilibrium melting temperature, \(T_{\rm{m}}^{0}\)."
comment: "\(T_{\rm{m}}^{0}\) is determined as the intersection of the straight line that describes \(T_{\rm{cr}} = T_{\rm{m}}\) with the extrapolated curve that is drawn through the experimental data points (\(T_{\rm{cr}}\), \(T_{\rm{m}}\))."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12766

[Term]
id: goldbook:12776
name: isotropisation temperature
def: "Temperature at which a transition from any anisotropic state to an isotropic liquid occurs."
comment: "In mesomorphic systems, the isotropisation temperature is usually called clearing temperature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12747

[Term]
id: goldbook:12777
name: Kauzmann temperature
def: "Temperature at which the extrapolation of the entropy of a super-cooled liquid is equal to the entropy of its crystalline state."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12778
name: Kohlrausch–Williams–Watts equation
def: "Equation describing the enthalpy relaxation\, \\\(\\Delta H\\\) which is observed during the annealing of polymers in the glassy state at a temperature\, \\\(T_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\)\, lower than \\\(T_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\\\) \\\[\\Delta H\(t_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\) = \\Delta c_\{p\}\(T_\{\\rm\{g\}\} - T_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\) \\exp\\!\\left\[- \\left \(\\frac\{t_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\}\{\\tau\} \\right\)^\{\\beta\} \\right\]\\\] \\\(\\Delta H\\\) = difference of the enthalpy in the initial\, glassy state\, and the enthalpy of the glassy state after annealing; \\\(t_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\) = time of annealing; \\\(\\Delta c_\{p\}\\\) = difference in heat capacity at the glass-transition temperature\, \\\(T_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\\\)\, and the starting temperature of the annealing process\, \\\(T_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\); \\\(\\tau\\\) = relaxation time at \\\(T_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\); \\\(\\beta\\\) = exponential factor."
comment: "Moduli, stress-strain behaviour, and molecular motions are affected by enthalpy relaxation, which reflects physical aging."
comment: "The exponential factor \(\beta\) has a value between 0 and 1, and characterises the asymmetry of the distribution of relaxation times."
synonym: "KWW Equation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12765
consider: goldbook:12774

[Term]
id: goldbook:12779
name: linear thermodilatometry
def: "Technique in which one dimension of a substance under negligible load is measured as a function of temperature while the substance is subjected to a controlled temperature program."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:12780
name: logarithmic decrement
def: "Natural logarithm of the ratio of the displacement of a damping curve separated by one period of the displacement."
comment: "If equals the \(n^{th}\) displacement of the damping curve and equals the \((n + 1)^{th}\) displacement (\(n = 1, 2, 3, \dots\)), then \(\mathit{\Lambda} = \ln(A_{n}/A_{n + 1})\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12756

[Term]
id: goldbook:12781
name: loss curve
def: "Plot of loss tangent \(\\\(\\tan \\delta\\\)\) vs. the temperature or the frequency of the forced sinusoidal oscillation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
