consider: goldbook:12783

[Term]
id: goldbook:12782
name: loss modulus
def: "Ratio of the amplitude of the stress \\\(\\pu\{90\\!^\{\\circ\}\}\\\) out of phase with the strain \(\\\(\\sigma_\{0\} \\sin \\delta\\\)\) to the amplitude of the strain \(\\\(\\gamma_\{0\}\\\)\) in the forced sinusoidal oscillation of a material. \\\[M^\{\\prime\\prime\} = \\frac\{\\sigma_\{0\} \\sin \\delta\}\{\\gamma_\{0\}\}\\\]"
comment: "For the definitions of the symbols used, see forced sinusoidal oscillation."
comment: "In a linear viscoelastic material, the strain \(\gamma = \gamma_{0} \cos \omega t\) produces a stress \(\sigma = \sigma_{0} \cos (\omega t + \delta) = \sigma_{0} \cos \delta \cos \omega t - \sigma_{0} \sin \delta \sin \omega t\)."
comment: "The loss modulus characterises the viscous response of a material."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12767

[Term]
id: goldbook:12783
name: loss tangent
def: "Tangent of the phase angle \(\\\(\\delta\\\)\) between stress and strain during a forced sinusoidal oscillation."
comment: "\(\tan \delta\) is also equal to the ratio of loss modulus to storage modulus."
synonym: "loss factor" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12767
consider: goldbook:12782
consider: goldbook:12802

[Term]
id: goldbook:12784
name: master curve
def: "Viscoelastic spectrum of a polymer or polymer material constructed using the time–temperature superposition \(TTS\) principle\, so that the spectrum covers a wide range of lengths of time or frequencies of measurement."
comment: "A master curve is usually constructed by superimposing a sequence of isothermal measurements of a viscoelastic property vs. time."
