[Term]
id: goldbook:12789
name: modulated heat flow
def: "Heat flow in a modulated-temperature DSC experiment."
synonym: "MHF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12790

[Term]
id: goldbook:12790
name: modulated-temperature DSC
def: "DSC experiment in which a small sinusoidal modulation overlays the change in temperature with time."
comment: "The resulting DSC data can be separated, by Fourier analysis, into components in-phase with the modulation (reversing heat flow) and out-of-phase with the modulation (nonreversing heat flow). \[\underbrace {{\left({\frac{{\partial H}}{{\partial t}}} \right)}_{p}}_{\rm{total\ heat\ flow}} = \frac{{\rm{d}}Q}{{\rm{d}}t} = \underbrace {C_{p}\frac{{\rm{d}}T}{{\rm{d}}t}}_{\rm{reversing\ heat\ flow}} + \underbrace {f\left({T,t}\right)}_{\rm{non\mbox{-}reversing\ heat\ flow}}\] The total heat flow is the average value calculated from the measured signals during the modulated heat flow (MHF). \(C_{p}\) is the heat capacity of the sample, \(\frac{{\rm{d}}T}{{\rm{d}}t}\) is the heating rate."
comment: "Use of the terms "oscillating DSC (ODSC)" and "modulated DSC (MDSC)" is discouraged."
synonym: "MTDSC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12789
consider: goldbook:12792
consider: goldbook:12797

[Term]
id: goldbook:12791
name: multiplexing
def: "Technique used in dynamic mechanical analysis in which a specimen is subjected to the superposition of a number of forced sinusoidal oscillations of different frequencies."
comment: "In one experiment, this technique delivers the frequency dependence of the mechanical properties at all the frequencies covered by the forced sinusoidal oscillations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12767

[Term]
id: goldbook:12792
name: non-reversing heat flow
def: "In modulated-temperature DSC\, the component of the total heat flow that is out-of-phase with the temperature modulation."
comment: "The out-of-phase component of the total heat flow relates to kinetic processes like crystallisation, melting, evaporation, or condensation."
comment: "The term "non-reversing" must not be confused with "irreversible"."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:12790

