[Term]
id: goldbook:12800
name: secondary relaxation temperature
def: "Temperature characterising a secondary relaxation peak identified as the temperature at which the loss modulus \(or loss tangent\)\, measured by DMA or DETA\, exhibits a maximum at the measurement frequency\, due to the occurrence of localised motions involving only short segments of the polymer chains\, or side groups of the polymer chains."
