[Term]
id: goldbook:12802
name: storage modulus
def: "Ratio of the amplitude of the stress in phase with the strain \(\\\(\\sigma_\{0\} \\cos \\delta\\\)\) to the amplitude of the strain \(\\\(\\gamma_\{0\}\\\)\) in the forced sinusoidal oscillation of a material. \\\[M^\{\\prime\} = \\frac\{\\sigma_\{0\} \\cos \\delta\}\{\\gamma_\{0\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Definition taken, with "forced sinusoidal oscillation" replacing "forced oscillation"."
comment: "For the definitions of the symbols used, see forced sinusoidal oscillation. In a linear viscoelastic material, the strain \(\gamma = \gamma_{0} \cos \omega t\) produces a stress. \[\sigma = \sigma_{0} \cos (\omega t + \delta) = \sigma_{0} \cos \delta \cos \omega t - \sigma_{0} \sin \delta \sin \omega t\]"
comment: "The storage modulus characterises the elastic response of a material."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
