[Term]
id: goldbook:12813
name: time–temperature superposition principle
def: "Principle stating that the value of a viscoelastic property measured at a given temperature\, after a given length of time or at a given frequency\, is equal to the value of the property at a different temperature after a length of time or at a frequency equal to the given length of time or given frequency multiplied by a shift factor\, \\\(a_\{T\}\\\) \, with the value of the shift factor being independent of length of the time or frequency."
comment: "The Williams–Landel–Ferry (WLF) equation provides a semi-empirical relation between the shift factor \(a_{T}\) and the temperature, at temperatures near the glass-transition temperature, \(T_{\rm{g}}\)."
synonym: "TTS Principle" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
