id: goldbook:12848
name: adhesion molecule
def: "Molecule belonging mainly to the immunoglobulins\, integrin superfamily \(e.g.\, LFA-1\, ICAM-1\) or selectins\, expressed on the cell membrane of various cells including those of the immune system. Interaction of adhesion molecules with each other as receptor and corresponding ligand facilitates cooperation \(cross-talk\) of cells\, signal transduction\, and information transfer between cells."
