[Term]
id: goldbook:12871
name: anaphylactic shock
def: "Immediate overreaction of the immune system to a drug or other agent in an individual who has previously encountered the agent and has produced antibodies to that agent."
comment: "The major manifestation of anaphylactic shock is angioedema, which leads to hypovalemia, obstruction of the airway, and bronchospasm; these in turn may lead to coma or death."
