[Term]
id: goldbook:12874
name: anaphylaxis
def: "Life-threatening type I hypersensitivity allergic reaction occurring in a person or animal exposed to an antigen or hapten to which they have previously been sensitized."
comment: "Consequences of the reaction may include angioedema, vascular collapse, shock, and respiratory distress."
