[Term]
id: goldbook:12880
name: antibody-forming cell assay
def: "Assay that measures the humoral immune response mediated by the concerted actions of antigen-presenting cells\, T lymphocytes\, and B lymphocytes\, generally by determination of murine primary IgM or IgG antibodies directed against the T-cell-dependent sheep red blood cell \(SRBC\) surface antigens after in vivo sensitization."
comment: "Due to involvement of multiple cell populations in mounting an antibody response, the AFC assay actually evaluates several immune parameters simultaneously. It is considered to be one of the most sensitive indicator systems for immunotoxicology studies."
synonym: "AFC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
