[Term]
id: goldbook:12881
name: antibody therapy
def: "Use of an antibody to target specific cells \(often tumor cells\) or signal transduction pathways \(often via chemokines/cytokines\) in the treatment of disease."
comment: "The main objectives are stimulation of the patient’s immune system to attack malignant tumor cells and the prevention of tumor growth by blockage of specific cell receptors."
