id: goldbook:12898
name: antinuclear antibody
def: "Antibody\, detectable in the blood\, that has the capability of binding to a substance\, e.g.\, DNA\, within the nucleus of the cells."
comment: "ANAs are found in patients whose immune system may be predisposed to cause inflammation against their own body tissues. ANAs indicate the possible presence of autoimmunity and are an indication of autoimmune disease, such as rheumatoid arthritis (RA), scleroderma, Sjögren syndrome, systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), and mixed connective tissue disease (MCTD)."
synonym: "ANA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
