id: goldbook:12975
name: CD5+ B lymphocyte
def: "Lymphocyte of type B-1a\, which is predominant in fetal lymphoid organs and in neonatal cord blood."
comment: "In adults, these cells range from \(\pu{2}\) to \(\pu{6\%}\) of total mononuclear cells in peripheral blood. They utilize an immunoglobulin (Ig) variable (V) gene repertoire different from that of CD5– B cells and they produce natural autoantibodies."
comment: "The expansion of autoreactive B1-a cells has been reported in peripheral blood of patients with autoimmune diseases [e.g., rheumatoid arthritis (RA), Sjögren syndrome, antiphospholipid syndrome (APS)]. In RA these cells can account for up to \(\pu{20\%}\) of circulating B cells and may produce rheumatoid factor."
