def: "Any of a large family of \\\(\\ce\{Ca^\{2+\}\}\\\)-dependent lectins; members of this family share primary structural homology in their carbohydrate-recognition domains and include many endocytic receptors\, many proteoglycans\, and all known collectins and selectins."
comment: "The C-type lectins are involved in many immune system functions, such as inflammation and immunity to tumor and virally infected cells, whereas the collectins are involved in innate immunity."
