[Term]
id: goldbook:13005
name: chronic allergic inflammation
def: "Disease of airways\, skin\, eyes and other organs\, resulting from repeated or continuous exposure to an allergen and involving immunoglobulin E \(IgE\) formation\, IgE-induced histamine-release from mast cells\, liberation of mediators such as cytokines and prostaglandins\, and local inflammation characterized by infiltrating leucocytes; it results in augmented susceptibility to the allergen."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
