[Term]
id: goldbook:13012
name: clonal anergy
def: "Form of self-tolerance developing as a consequence of negative selection during thymic selection processes. Clones of thymocytes whose antigen receptors \[T-cell receptors \(TCRs\)\] bind with high affinity to self-antigens in association with major histocompatibility complex \(MHC\) molecules are inactivated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
