[Term]
id: goldbook:13048
name: Coombs test
def: "Diagnostic test using anti-immunoglobulin \(Ig\) to agglutinate antibody-coated erythrocytes."
comment: "The direct Coombs test, or direct antiglobulin test (DAT) refers to agglutination of a blood sample due to antibodies present on the erythrocyte surface. In the indirect Coombs test, or indirect antiglobulin test (IAT) antibodies free in the subject’s serum are tested for their availability to agglutinate erythrocytes of known antigenicity."
synonym: "direct Coombs test" []
synonym: "direct antiglobulin test (DAT)" []
synonym: "indirect Coombs test" []
synonym: "indirect antiglobulin test (IAT)" []
