[Term]
id: goldbook:13050
name: corticosteroid
def: "Any of the family of steroid molecules that are produced in the adrenal cortex\, or their synthetic analogs."
comment: "Corticosteroids can induce apoptotic cell death in lymphocytes, especially developing thymocytes. Therefore, they are useful anti-inflammatory, anti-lymphoid tumor, and immunosuppressive agents."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
