[Term]
id: goldbook:13052
name: counter-regulation hypothesis
def: "Hypothesis that all types of infection early in childhood may protect against the development of atopy by driving the production of cytokines such as interleukin-10 \(IL-10\) and transforming growth factor $\\ce\{\\upbeta\\!\}$ \($\\ce\{TGF\\mbox\{-\}\\upbeta\\!\}$\)\, which downregulate both Th1 and Th2 responses."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
