[Term]
id: goldbook:13055
name: cross-presentation
def: "Activation of CD8+ lymphocytes by the presentation of exogenous antigens in association with major histocompatibility complex \(MHC\) class I molecules."
comment: "Cross-presentation can lead to different outcomes, tolerance or immunity."
comment: "The cells that cross-present antigens are the bone marrow-derived antigen-presenting cells (APCs). The form of antigen they monitor from tissues is predominantly cellular protein, acquired though phagocytosis and macropinocytosis and presented through two distinct pathways. In one pathway, antigen is transferred into the cytosol where it is degraded by proteasomes, and in the other, the antigen is hydrolyzed in the endocytic compartment"
comment: "This is in contrast to normal activation of these lymphocytes (direct-priming) that results from presentation of endogenous antigens."
synonym: "cross-priming" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
