[Term]
id: goldbook:13056
name: cross-reacting antibody
def: "Antibody that is able to react with an antigen that did not specifically stimulate its production."
comment: "Cross-reactions are usually weaker than the reaction of the antibody with the antigen that caused its production."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:13057
name: cross-reacting antigen
def: "Antigen that is able to react with an antibody induced by a different antigen. Note\: The two antigens may share the same antigenic determinants or carry determinants that are sufficiently alike stereochemically to enable the antibody to react with both. Antigen that has an identical structure in two strains of microorganism\, so that antibody raised against one strain will react with the other strain."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:13058
name: cross sensitivity
def: "State of immunological hypersensitivity to one substance that predisposes an individual to sensitivity to other substances that are related in chemical structure \(cross-reacting antigens\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:13057
consider: goldbook:13241

[Term]
id: goldbook:13059
name: cross-tolerance
def: "State of immunological tolerance to one substance produced by priming an animal with another substance that bears a cross-reacting antigen."
