[Term]
id: goldbook:13065
name: cytokine
def: "Any of a group of soluble small proteins released from a variety of cells\, typically of the immune system\, that affect cell behavior in an autocrine or paracrine fashion."
comment: "Cytokines produced by lymphocytes are known as lymphokines; those produced by monocytes are called monokines. Other types of cytokines include chemokines, growth factors, colony-stimulating factors (CSFs), transforming growth factors, interferons, interleukins, and tumor necrosis factors."
