id: goldbook:13082
name: decay-accelerating factor
def: "Cell-surface molecule that protects cells from lysis by complement."
comment: "The decay-accelerating factor binds to C3 convertases of both the alternative pathway and classical pathway of complement activation and, by displacing Bb and C2b respectively, prevents their action. Its absence causes the disease paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria."
synonym: "CD55" []
