[Term]
id: goldbook:13083
name: defensin
def: "Any member of a family of oligopeptides made within the body\, notably by neutrophils and macrophages\, and having potent antimicrobial properties."
comment: "Defensins play important roles against invading microbes. They act against bacteria, fungi, and viruses by binding to their membranes and increasing membrane permeability."
comment: "Human defensins are classified into the \(\ce{\upalpha\mbox{-}defensins}\) and \(\ce{\upbeta\mbox{-}defensins}\) on the basis of their sequence homology and their cysteine residues."
