[Term]
id: goldbook:13085
name: delayed-type hypersensitivity
def: "Form of T cell-mediated immunity in which the ultimate effector cell is the activated mononuclear phagocyte \(macrophage\); the response of DTH appears fully over \\\(\\pu\{24\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{48 h\}\\\). Previous exposure is required."
comment: "Examples include response to Mycobacterium tuberculosis (tuberculin test) and contact dermatitis."
synonym: "DTH" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Gell and Coombs Type IV reaction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
