[Term]
id: goldbook:13087
name: dendritic cell
def: "Ameboid cell that is major histocompatibility complex \(MHC\) class II-positive\, Fc receptor-negative\, and presents processed antigens to T cells in the T-cell areas of secondary lymphoid tissues."
comment: "Dendritic cells are potent stimulators of T-cell responses. Nonlymphoid tissues also contain dendritic cells, but these are not able to stimulate T-cell responses until they are activated."
comment: "Some authors also distinguish myeloid and lymphoid dendritic cells based on lineage."
comment: "Some confusion in the classification of dendritic cells may arise from systems based on function, morphology, or lineage, and possibly species differences."
comment: "There are three major subclasses of dendritic cells, conventional dendritic cells, Langerhans cells, and plasmacytoid dendritic cells."
comment: "This is a different cell type from the follicular dendritic cell, which is Fc receptor-positive."
synonym: "interdigitating dendritic cell" []
synonym: "interdigitating reticular cell" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
