[Term]
id: goldbook:13088
name: immune complex deposition
def: "Precipitation of immune complex in organs and tissues\, often causing local inflammation."
comment: "Immune complex deposition is a prominent feature of systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), cryoglobulinemia, rheumatoid arthritis (RA), scleroderma, and Sjögren syndrome."
