id: goldbook:13104
name: Draize test
def: "Context\: ocular; Test for potential to cause irritation to the eye in which the test substance is applied directly to the eye of restrained rabbits. Note\: Widely criticized as unethical. Now often replaced with an acute eye irritation test using cadaveric chicken eyes. Context\: skin; Test for the potential of a material to cause irritation or corrosion following local dermal application. Generally performed with rabbits."
