[Term]
id: goldbook:13114
name: enterotoxin
def: "Toxin affecting intestinal cells and thus causing food poisoning."
comment: "Enterotoxins stimulate many types of T cells by binding to major histocompatibility complex (MHC) class II molecules and the Vb domain of certain T-cell receptors (TCRs). Enterotoxins have thus been referred to as superantigens."
