[Term]
id: goldbook:13199
name: helper T lymphocyte
def: "Member of a subclass of T lymphocytes that provides help \(in the form of cytokines and/or cognate interactions\) necessary for the expression of effector function by other cells in the immune system."
comment: "Helper T cells recognize antigen in association with major histocompatibility complex (MHC) class II gene products. Depending on their capacity to produce various cytokines, one can functionally differentiate Th1 [interleukin-2- (IL-2-) and IFN-γ-producing] and Th2 (interleukins IL-3-, IL-4-, and IL-6-producing) cells."
synonym: "T helper cell" []
