[Term]
id: goldbook:13209
name: heterophile antibody
def: "Antibody raised against an antigen from one species\, which also reacts against antigens from other species."
comment: "Heterophile antibodies are usually of low affinity and are a common cause of problems with immunoassays."
comment: "Heterophile antibodies commonly arise from viral infection."
comment: "The existence of such antibodies explains observations of the presence of antibody against antigens from a variety of species without immunization."
