[Term]
id: goldbook:13226
name: host defense
def: "Ability of an individual to resist invasion by opportunistic agents and production of disease associated with exposure to microorganisms\, foreign tissue\, and particulates\, as well as certain types of neoplasia. Host defense may be either nonspecific \(innate or natural immunity\) or specific \(adaptive or acquired immunity\) in nature."
comment: "Immunological defense may involve chemotaxis, phagocytosis, reaction with immunoglobulins (Ig) and/or with complement, and T-cell cytotoxicity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
