[Term]
id: goldbook:13228
name: human immunodeficiency virus
def: "Causative agent of acquired immune deficiency syndrome \(AIDS\)."
comment: "HIV is a retrovirus of the lentivirus family that selectively infects macrophages and CD4+ T cells, leading to their slow depletion, eventually resulting in immunodeficiency."
comment: "There are two major strains of the virus, HIV-1 and HIV-2, of which HIV-1 causes most disease worldwide. HIV-2 is endemic to West Africa but is spreading."
synonym: "HIV" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
