[Term]
id: goldbook:13230
name: human leukocyte antigen
def: "Antigen coded by genes of the human major histocompatibility complex \(MHC\)."
comment: "Human HLA-A, -B and -C (resembling mouse H-2K, D and L) are MHC class I molecules, whereas HLA-DP, -DQ and -DR (resembling mouse I-A and I-E) are MHC class II molecules."
comment: "The genes for HLAs are situated on chromosome 6."
synonym: "HLA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
