[Term]
id: goldbook:13231
name: human leukocyte antigen polymorphism
def: "Discontinuous genetic variation in the major histocompatibility complex \(MHC\) that results in the occurrence of several different forms of MHC molecules among people."
comment: "Specific HLA polymorphisms are associated with a number of diseases, e.g., HLA-B27 is associated with ankylosing spondylitis, psoriatic arthritis, rheumatoid arthritis (RA), etc., and some chemical sensitivities."
synonym: "HLA Polymorphism" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
