[Term]
id: goldbook:13236
name: humoral immunity
def: "Specific immune response that is mediated primarily by humoral factors circulating in solution in the blood plasma and lymph \(i.e.\, antibodies and complement\)."
comment: "The induction of the humoral immune response generally requires the cooperation of cellular immune mechanisms."
synonym: "humorally mediated immunity (HMI)" []
