[Term]
id: goldbook:13241
name: hypersensitivity
def: "State in which an individual reacts with allergic effects following exposure to a certain substance \(allergen\) after having been exposed previously to the same substance. It is sometimes used loosely for any increased response."
comment: "Four types of hypersensitivity are recognized. Most common chemically induced allergies are type I [immunoglobulin E- (IgE-) mediated] and type IV (cell-mediated) hypersensitivity."
