[Term]
id: goldbook:13260
name: immune elimination
def: "Removal of pathogens or tumor cells by the immune system; the first step of immunoediting of tumors."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:13284

[Term]
id: goldbook:13261
name: immune enhancement
def: "Therapeutic stimulation of the immune response\, especially in tumor therapy."
synonym: "enhancement (in immunology)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:13262
name: immune equilibrium
def: "State in carcinogenesis where there is an equilibrium between elimination of tumor cells by the immune system and growth of non-immunogenic tumor cells; the second step in immunoediting."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:13271
consider: goldbook:13284

[Term]
id: goldbook:13263
name: immune escape
def: "Biological feature of an infectious agent or of a tumor cell that prevents its elimination by the immune system. Such a feature can be acquired by a selection process. Immune escape is the third step in immunoediting of tumors."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:13271
consider: goldbook:13284

[Term]
id: goldbook:13264
name: immune evasion
def: "Property of a pathogen that results in avoidance of attack by the immune system\, e.g.\, because of reduced phagocytosis\, lack of recognition by the innate immune system\, or suppression of the immune response."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
