[Term]
id: goldbook:13267
name: immune reserve hypothesis
def: "Hypothesis that the immune response involves multiple redundancies that are capable of compensating for acute reductions in certain immune functions."
comment: "Such a reserve might prevent a serious reduction in host resistance after temporary immunosuppression of selected parameters [e.g., natural killer (NK) cell function]."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
