[Term]
id: goldbook:13286
name: immunoglobulin A
def: "Class of immunoglobulin \(Ig\) characterized by $\\ce\{\\upalpha\\!\}$ heavy chains."
comment: "IgA antibodies are secreted mainly by mucosal lymphoid tissues, and in the dimeric form are present in mucosal secretions. IgA in the monomeric form is present in blood."
