[Term]
id: goldbook:13291
name: immunoglobulin E-mediated hypersensitivity
def: "State in which an individual reacts with allergic effects caused fundamentally by the reaction of antigen-specific immunoglobulin E \(IgE\) following exposure to a certain substance \(allergen\) after having been exposed previously to the same substance."
synonym: "IgE-Mediated Hypersensitivity" []
