[Term]
id: goldbook:13293
name: immunoglobulin M
def: "Class of immunoglobulin \(Ig\) characterized by \\\(\\upmu\\\) heavy chains."
comment: "It is the first immunoglobulin to appear on the surface of B cells and the first to be secreted."
comment: "Unlike other immunoglobulins that exist in the monomeric (IgA, IgD, IgE, and IgG) or dimeric (IgA) state, IgM is found in the blood as a pentamer."
synonym: "IgM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
