[Term]
id: goldbook:13295
name: immunoglobulin superfamily
def: "Large family of proteins characterized by possession of 'immunoglobulin-type' domains of approximately 110 amino acids folded into two \\\(\\ce\{\\upbeta\\mbox\{-\}pleated sheets\}\\\). Members include immunoglobulins \\\(A\\\)\, \\\(E\\\)\, \\\(G\\\)\, \\\(M\\\) \(IgA\, IgE\, IgG\, and IgM\)\, T-cell receptors \(TCRs\)\, and human leukocyte antigen \(HLA\) major histocompatibility complex \(MHC\) molecules."
