[Term]
id: goldbook:13362
name: killer cell immunoglobulin-like receptor
def: "Receptor expressed on natural killer \(NK\) cells that binds to major histocompatibility complex \(MHC\) class I molecules on target cells; binding MHC class I inhibits the signaling that would otherwise lead to target cell killing."
comment: "If immunoreceptor tyrosine-based inhibitory motif (ITIM) sequences are present in the KIR cytoplasmic domain, MHC class I molecule binding is inhibitory to the killer cell. KIRs lacking ITIMs can associate with immunoreceptor tyrosine-based activation motif (ITAM)-containing adaptor molecules, in which case binding of MHC class I molecules can activate the killer cell."
synonym: "KIR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
