[Term]
id: goldbook:13479
name: multipotent progenitor cell
def: "Undifferentiated stem cell\, obtained from adult bone marrow or other non-embryonic tissue sources\, that possesses the ability to differentiate into a variety of cell types\, especially into cells of a closely related family of cells that are expanded in vitro and deposited in master cell banks for 'off-the-shelf' use\, with potential hematopoiesis-inducing and immunomodulating activities."
comment: "Allogeneic multipotent adult progenitor cells (MAPCs) are non-immunogenic due to the lack of major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecule expression, and so elicit no immune response upon administration."
comment: "In vivo, bone marrow-derived adult stem cells are capable of maturing into a broad range of cell types and may help to restore the immune system by producing multiple therapeutic molecules in response to inflammation and tissue damage."
