[Term]
id: goldbook:13543
name: pattern recognition receptor
def: "Receptor found on many different cell types in the immune system that enables them to recognize pathogen-associated molecular patterns \(PAMPs\). Amongst the large number of different PRRs are the mannose receptor \(CD206\)\, macrophage scavenger receptor \(CD204\)\, and the toll-like receptors \(TLRs\)."
comment: "Many of the NOD-like receptors (NLRs) are thought to serve as PRRs."
synonym: "PRR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
