[Term]
id: goldbook:13557
name: pernicious anemia
def: "Disease in which the erythrocytes are abnormally formed\, due to an inability to absorb vitamin \\\(\{\\rm\{B\}\}_\{12\}\\\). True pernicious anemia refers specifically to a disorder of atrophied parietal cells leading to absent intrinsic factor\, resulting in an inability to absorb \\\(\{\\rm\{B\}\}_\{12\}\\\)."
comment: "This disease is associated with a variety of autoimmune endocrine diseases (e.g., Hashimoto thyroiditis, Addison disease, and autoimmune myasthenic syndromes)."
comment: "This is the end stage of \(\pu{10}\) to \(\pu{15\%}\) of autoimmune gastritis."
