[Term]
id: goldbook:13599
name: prick test
def: "Test carried out by placing a drop of a suspected allergenic extract on the skin of the forearm and gently pricking it into the upper layer of skin. Sensitivity to a substance is indicated if the spot swells slightly and becomes red within about \\\(\\pu\{15 min\}\\\)."
comment: "A positive result is far from conclusive and, at best, gives a vague indication of allergenicity. The prick test is inappropriate as a test for food allergens."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
