id: goldbook:13601
name: primary immune response
def: "Immune response to the first encounter with an antigen\, characterized by slow production of antibody molecules and the priming of lymphoid tissue in readiness for the production of a secondary immune response on subsequent challenge with the same antigen."
comment: "The primary response is generally weak, has a long induction phase or lag period, consists primarily of the release of immunoglobulin M (IgM) antibodies, and generates immunologic memory."
synonym: "primary response" []
