id: goldbook:13632
name: Raynaud phenomenon
def: "Intermittent bilateral attacks of vasospasm and ischemia of the fingers or toes and sometimes of the ears and nose\, marked by a severe pallor and often accompanied by paresthesia and pain."
comment: "It is brought on characteristically by cold or emotional stimuli and relieved by heat, and may be due to an underlying disease or anatomic abnormality."
comment: "The phenomenon is more common in women than men and occurs in most patients with progressive systemic sclerosis (SSc), mixed connective tissue disease (MCTD), and polymyositis/scleroderma overlap syndrome."
comment: "When the condition is idiopathic or primary, it is termed Raynaud disease."
