[Term]
id: goldbook:13829
name: honeycomb polymer film
def: "Hexagonal array of holes in a polymer film."
comment: "A method that utilizes the condensation of micrometer-size water droplets on the surface of solutions of block copolymers for the preparation of ordered micrometer-size honeycomb structures has led to the use of the extended term, honeycomb polymer from breath figures."
comment: "The cross-sectional dimensions of the holes of a hexagonal array are usually less than \(\pu{1 mm}\)."
synonym: "honeycomb polymer" []
