[Term]
id: goldbook:13835
name: layer-by-layer assembly
def: "Process whereby multilayered structures of molecules or particles of a substance are assembled on a solid substrate by sequential adsorption of monolayers held together by noncovalent interactions."
comment: "Layer-by-layer assembly is often used to alternately transfer polyelectrolytes that are positively and negatively charged."
comment: "The material at the liquid surface need not necessarily be present as a solid monolayer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-12
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:13837
name: mechanically interlocked molecular architecture
def: "Supramolecular structure in which molecules are linked only as a consequence of their topology."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-12
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:13838
name: metallomesogen
def: "Mesogen composed of molecules incorporating one or more metal atoms."
