[Term]
id: goldbook:13956
name: ecotoxicity
def: "Consequence of adverse effects caused by a substance on the environment and on organisms living in it."
comment: "If only living organisms (animals, plants, microorganisms) are concerned, the use of toxicity is recommended."
comment: "Using the term is recommended when adverse effects concern water, air, sediments, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-12-04
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:13957
name: environmentally degradable polymer
def: "Polymer that can be degraded by the action of the environment\, through\, for example\, air\, light\, heat\, or microorganisms."
comment: "When it is to be a source of material, such a polymer must be designed to degrade into products at a predictable rate compatible with the application. Such products are usually of lower molar mass than the original polymer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-12-04
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:13958
name: environmentally friendly
def: "Qualifiers for a substance\, device\, or process that has minimal deleterious impact on the environment\, which is air\, water\, minerals\, living systems\, etc."
comment: "Ecocompatible is introduced to complement biocompatible, whose meaning is limited to living systems."
comment: "The assignment of these qualifiers to a polymer must be based on a consistent life cycle assessment."
synonym: "ecocompatible" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-12-04
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
