[Term]
id: goldbook:13960
name: life cycle assessment
def: "Investigation and valuation of the environmental impacts of a given product or service caused or necessitated by its existence."
comment: "Also known as life cycle analysis, LCA, ecobalance, and cradle-to-grave analysis."
comment: "Assessing the life cycle of a polymer or a plastic must take into account all the factors that can be identified from the up-stage raw material to the waste management."
