[Term]
id: goldbook:13972
name: pseudorotaxane
def: "Rotaxane-like molecular assembly in which the threading component\(s\) has\(have\) ends small enough to permit threading or dethreading of the macrocyclic component\(s\)."
comment: "Pseudorotaxanes in which only one end of a threading component is capped with a stopper are sometimes called "semirotaxanes" or "half-capped pseudorotaxanes"."
comment: "The stability of a pseudorotaxane may arise not only from spatially hindered dethreading of its components, but also from interaction between threading and macrocyclic components, e.g., donor-acceptor or electrostatic or coordination (see recognition site)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-10-15
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
