[Term]
id: goldbook:13984
name: threadable ring
def: "Key part of a macrocyclic component\: molecular ring \(cycle\) large enough to be threaded onto a linear subchain of a threading component."
comment: "A threadable ring (cycle) should be distinguished from other smaller, non-threadable rings within a complex macrocyclic component, such as benzene, cyclooctane, or similar rings."
synonym: "threadable cycle" []
