[Term]
id: goldbook:14283
name: polymer network particle
def: "Particle having any shape and composed of a polymer network and possibly species of finite molar mass."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14284
name: artificial latex
def: "Latex obtained by emulsification of a polymer or oligomer solution in a liquid or by emulsification of a liquid polymer or liquid oligomer in a liquid."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14285
name: hybrid latex
def: "Latex comprising a polymer of relatively high molar mass and an oligomer or an alkyd resin\, in which there is usually chemical bonding between the two components\, formed either during latex synthesis or subsequently after formation of a film from the latex. Latex comprising multicomponent particles that contain both organic and inorganic material phases."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14286
name: inverse latex
def: "Nonaqueous latex in which the dispersed phase comprises hydrophilic polymer usually swollen with water."
comment: "An inverse latex is usually formed by inverse emulsion, inverse micro-emulsion, or inverse mini-emulsion polymerizations in which water-soluble monomer(s) dissolved in the dispersed phase is (are) polymerized."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307
consider: goldbook:14335

[Term]
id: goldbook:14287
name: latex particle
def: "Polymer particle that is present in a latex."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14288
name: natural latex
def: "Latex\, the dispersed phase of which is obtained from various plants."
comment: "Many plants when wounded produce a milky, sticky sap that is referred to as a latex."
comment: "The dispersed phase is often polyisoprene (2-methyl-1,3-butadiene).Example: Latex from the rubber tree, Hevea brasiliensis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307

[Term]
id: goldbook:14289
name: synthetic latex
def: "Latex obtained as a product of an emulsion\, mini-emulsion\, micro-emulsion\, or dispersion polymerization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14316
consider: goldbook:14317
consider: goldbook:14348

[Term]
id: goldbook:14290
name: equivalent particle diameter
def: "Diameter of a hypothetical spherical particle of the same composition that\, using a given particle-size determination method\, would give the same diameter as a substance composed of spherical or nonspherical particles at the same concentration."
comment: "Although the equivalent particle diameter is not a precisely defined quantity, as its value depends on the experimental method used for its determination, it is useful for particle characterization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14291
name: number-average particle diameter
def: "Calculated using the following equation\: \\\[\\left\\langle d_\{\\rm\{N\}\} \\right\\rangle = \\bar d_\{\\rm\{N\}\} = \\frac\{\\Sigma N_\{i\} d_\{i\}\}\{\\Sigma N_\{i\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Average diameters are defined and calculated by using relations or ratios between the main momentums of a representative statistical distribution that is the particle diameter distribution (e.g., \(z\mbox{-}\rm{average}\) diameter is the fifth momentum over the fourth one)."
comment: "Averages may be denoted by \(\left\langle ~ \right\rangle\) or by \(\bar{~}\)."
comment: "In principle, any method suitable for measuring the diameters of single particles (e.g., electron microscopy) could be used for the determination of all the averages given in the table. However, some experimental methods allow determination only of particular diameter averages."
comment: "In the formulae, \(N_{i}\) denotes the number of particles of diameter \(d_{i}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14292
name: surface-average particle diameter
def: "Calculated using the following equation\: \\\[\\left\\langle \{d_\{\\rm\{s\}\}\} \\right\\rangle = \\bar d_\{\\rm\{s\}\} = \\frac\{\\Sigma \{N_\{i\}\} \{d_\{i\}^\{3\}\}\}\{\\Sigma \{N_\{i\}\} \{d_\{i\}^\{2\}\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Average diameters are defined and calculated by using relations or ratios between the main momentums of a representative statistical distribution that is the particle diameter distribution (e.g., \(z\mbox{-}\rm{average}\) diameter is the fifth momentum over the fourth one)."
comment: "Averages may be denoted by \(\left\langle ~ \right\rangle\) or by \(\bar{~}\)."
comment: "In principle, any method suitable for measuring the diameters of single particles (e.g., electron microscopy) could be used for the determination of all the averages given in the table. However, some experimental methods allow determination only of particular diameter averages."
comment: "In the formulae, \(N_{i}\) denotes the number of particles of diameter \(d_{i}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14293
name: mass-average particle diameter
def: "Calculated using the following equation\: \\\[\\left\\langle d_\{\\rm\{m\}\} \\right\\rangle = \\bar d_\{\\rm\{m\}\} = \\frac\{\\Sigma \{N_\{i\}\} \{d_\{i\}^\{4\}\}\}\{\\Sigma \{N_\{i\}\} \{d_\{i\}^\{3\}\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Average diameters are defined and calculated by using relations or ratios between the main momentums of a representative statistical distribution that is the particle diameter distribution (e.g., \(z\mbox{-}\rm{average}\) diameter is the fifth momentum over the fourth one)."
comment: "Averages may be denoted by \(\left\langle ~ \right\rangle\) or by \(\bar{~}\)."
comment: "In principle, any method suitable for measuring the diameters of single particles (e.g., electron microscopy) could be used for the determination of all the averages given in the table. However, some experimental methods allow determination only of particular diameter averages."
comment: "In the formulae, \(N_{i}\) denotes the number of particles of diameter \(d_{i}\)."
comment: "The definition of mass-average diameter is meaningful only for latexes where the particles all have the same density."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14294
name: z-average particle diameter
def: "Calculated using the following equation\: \\\[\\left\\langle d_\{\\rm\{z\}\} \\right\\rangle = \\bar d_\{\\rm\{z\}\} = \\frac\{\\Sigma N_\{i\} d_\{i\}^\{5\}\}\{\\Sigma N_\{i\}d_\{i\}^\{4\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Average diameters are defined and calculated by using relations or ratios between the main momentums of a representative statistical distribution that is the particle diameter distribution (e.g., \(z\mbox{-}\rm{average}\) diameter is the fifth momentum over the fourth one)."
comment: "Averages may be denoted by \(\left\langle ~ \right\rangle\) or by \(\bar{~}\)."
comment: "In principle, any method suitable for measuring the diameters of single particles (e.g., electron microscopy) could be used for the determination of all the averages given in the table. However, some experimental methods allow determination only of particular diameter averages."
comment: "In the formulae, \(N_{i}\) denotes the number of particles of diameter \(d_{i}\)."
comment: "The definition of the \(z\mbox{-}\rm{average}\) diameter is meaningful only for latexes where the particles all have the same density and refractive index"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14295
name: volume-average particle diameter
def: "Calculated using the following equation\: \\\[\\left\\langle d_\{\\rm\{v\}\} \\right\\rangle = \\bar d_\{\\rm\{v\}\} = \\left\(\\frac\{\\Sigma N_\{i\} d_\{i\}^\{3\}\}\{\\Sigma N_\{i\}\}\\right\)^\{1/3\}\\\]"
comment: "Average diameters are defined and calculated by using relations or ratios between the main momentums of a representative statistical distribution that is the particle diameter distribution (e.g., \(z\mbox{-}\rm{average}\) diameter is the fifth momentum over the fourth one)."
comment: "Averages may be denoted by \(\left\langle ~ \right\rangle\) or by \(\bar{~}\)."
comment: "In principle, any method suitable for measuring the diameters of single particles (e.g., electron microscopy) could be used for the determination of all the averages given in the table. However, some experimental methods allow determination only of particular diameter averages."
comment: "In the formulae, \(N_{i}\) denotes the number of particles of diameter \(d_{i}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14296
name: particle-diameter dispersity
def: "Calculated using the following equation\: \\\[Ɖ_\{\\rm\{d\}\} = \\left\\langle d_\{\\rm\{m\}\} \\right\\rangle /\\!\\left\\langle d_\{\\rm\{N\}\} \\right\\rangle = \\bar d_\{\\rm\{m\}\}/\\bar d_\{\\rm\{N\}\} = \\frac\{\\Sigma N_\{i\}\\Sigma N_\{i\} d_\{i\}^\{4\}\}\{\\Sigma N_\{i\} d_\{i\} \\Sigma N_\{i\} d_\{i\}^\{3\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Averages may be denoted by \(\left\langle ~ \right\rangle\) or by \(\bar{~}\)."
comment: "For "particle-diameter dispersity", the term "diameter-polydispersity index" is not recommended as "polydispersity" is an undefined quantity. The term "non-uniformity factor" is also not recommended."
comment: "In principle, any method suitable for measuring the diameters of single particles (e.g., electron microscopy) could be used for the determination of all the averages given in the table. However, some experimental methods allow determination only of particular diameter averages."
comment: "In the formulae, \(N_{i}\) denotes the number of particles of diameter \(d_{i}\)."
comment: "The term "particle-diameter dispersity" and the symbol \(Ɖ_{\rm{d}}\) are an extension of the terms molar-mass dispersity (\(Ɖ_{\rm{m}}\)) and degree-of-polymerization dispersity (\(Ɖ_{\rm{X}}\)), where \(Ɖ_{\rm{m}} = \bar M_{\rm{m}}/\bar M_{\rm{n}}\) and \(Ɖ_{\rm{X}} = \bar X_{\rm{m}}/\bar X_{\rm{n}}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14297
name: homogeneous particle
def: "Particle that is spatially uniform with respect to chemical composition of the constituent polymer\(s\)."
comment: "A particle that is chemically homogeneous but has a radial distribution function of composition that is not step-like is not a homogeneous particle. Similarly, a block-copolymer micelle is not a homogeneous particle, although all constituent copolymer molecules can have identical compositions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14298
name: multicomponent particle
def: "Inhomogeneous particle consisting of two or more immiscible components.Examples of two-phase particle morphology."
comment: "Multicomponent particles are often obtained by sequential polymerizations of different monomers or monomer mixtures."
comment: "The components can be solid, liquid, or gaseous."
synonym: "composite particle" []
synonym: "structured particle" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14299
name: core-shell particle
def: "Polymer particle comprising at least two phase domains\, one of which \(the core\) lies within the other\(s\) that form the polymeric outer layer\(s\) \(the shell\(s\)\)."
comment: "Core-shell particles in which polymer synthesized in the second stage is located within one single domain, and the particles and polymer constituting the initial seed are located in the shell are usually called inverted core-shell particles."
comment: "Core-shell particles may be obtained by seeded emulsion polymerization in which the seed particles form the cores of the new particles, and polymer produced in the second stage and subsequent stages, if any, forms the shell."
comment: "Examples of core-shell particles are shown in multicomponent particle. A core may be composed of one single-phase domain of one type of polymer or copolymer block in a shell of a different type of polymer (or copolymer block)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14298
consider: goldbook:14300
consider: goldbook:14329
consider: goldbook:14376

[Term]
id: goldbook:14300
name: inverted core-shell particle
def: "Core-shell particle in which polymer synthesized in the second stage is located in the core of the particle and polymer constituting the initial seed is located in the shell."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14298

[Term]
id: goldbook:14301
name: multilayered particle
def: "Multicomponent particle made of at least two different polymers\, with an inner core of one polymer and with at least two layers of different polymers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14298

[Term]
id: goldbook:14302
name: occluded particle
def: "Multicomponent particle in which one polymer forms more than one phase domain within a matrix of another polymer."
comment: "The number and size of the domains can vary, and their spatial distribution within the particles is often not uniform."
comment: "This type of particle is also referred to as having microdomain morphology."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14298

[Term]
id: goldbook:14303
name: partially engulfed particle
def: "Multicomponent particle in which one or more polymer\(s\) cover\(s\) most\, but not all\, of the particle surface."
comment: "The degree of coverage may vary when neither polymer is preferentially covering the other one. The morphology is commonly referred to as a hemisphere."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14298

[Term]
id: goldbook:14304
name: macroporous particle
def: "Particle containing pores of diameters exceeding about \\\(\\pu\{50 nm\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14305
name: mesoporous particle
def: "Particle containing pores of diameters between approximately \\\(\\pu\{2 \\upmu m\}\\\) and \\\(\\pu\{50 \\upmu m\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14306
name: microporous particle
def: "Particle containing pores of diameters not exceeding \\\(\\pu\{2 nm\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14307
name: dispersed phase
def: "Phase constituted of particles of any size and of any nature dispersed in a continuous phase of a different composition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14308
name: continuous phase
def: "Phase not interrupted in space"
comment: "The continuous phase may be gaseous, liquid, or solid."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14309
name: dispersion medium
def: "Matrix for the dispersed phase."
comment: "If the continuous phase is a gas, the dispersion is called an aerosol."
comment: "The dispersion medium is the continuous phase of the dispersion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14310
name: nonaqueous dispersion
def: "Dispersion in which the continuous phase is nonaqueous."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14311
name: polymer dispersion
def: "Dispersion in which the dispersed phase consists of a polymer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307

[Term]
id: goldbook:14312
name: colloid stabiliser
def: "Compound increasing stability of a colloid."
comment: "A colloid stabilizer may be added to a colloid or synthesized during colloid preparation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14313
name: polymer colloid
def: "Colloidal dispersion in which at least one of the phases is a polymer\, either organic\, or inorganic or some combination of the two."
comment: "Particles of a liquid or a gas dispersed in a polymer, particles comprising "empty" shells made of polymers, and aerosols of polymer particles are all known examples."
comment: "The term "polymer colloid" is more general than latex. In a latex the dispersed phase is always a polymer, whereas in a polymer colloid this need not be so."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307

[Term]
id: goldbook:14314
name: polymer emulsion
def: "Emulsion in which the dispersed phase is a liquid polymer or a polymer solution."
comment: "The dispersing phase may be a low-molecular-weight liquid or a solution of another polymer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307

[Term]
id: goldbook:14315
name: macro-emulsion
def: "Emulsion in which the particles of the dispersed phase have diameters from approximately \\\(\\pu\{1 \\upmu m\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{100 \\upmu m\}\\\)."
comment: "Macro-emulsions comprise large droplets and thus are "unstable" in the sense that the droplets sediment or float, depending on the densities of the dispersed phase and dispersion medium. Separation of the dispersed and continuous phases usually occurs within time periods from a few seconds to a few hours, depending upon the viscosity of the fluid medium and the size and density of the droplets."
comment: "Macro-emulsions usually contain low-molecular-weight or polymeric surfactants that decrease the rates of coalescence of dispersed droplets. Droplets of the dispersed phase may be also stabilized by adsorption of solid particles onto their surface (so-called Pickering stabilization)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14316
name: mini-emulsion
def: "Emulsion in which the particles of the dispersed phase have diameters in the range from approximately \\\(\\pu\{50 nm\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{1 \\upmu m\}\\\)."
comment: "Mini-emulsions are usually stabilized against diffusion degradation (Ostwald ripening) by a compound insoluble in the continuous phase."
comment: "The dispersed phase contains mixed stabilizers, e.g., an ionic surfactant, such as sodium dodecyl sulfate (n-dodecyl sulfate sodium) and a short aliphatic chain alcohol ("co-surfactant") for colloidal stability, or a water-insoluble compound, such as a hydrocarbon ("co-stabilizer" frequently and improperly called a "co-surfactant") limiting diffusion degradation. Mini-emulsions are usually stable for at least several days."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14317
name: micro-emulsion
def: "Dispersion made of water\, oil\, and surfactant\(s\) that is an isotropic and thermodynamically stable system with dispersed domain diameter varying approximately from \\\(\\pu\{1 nm\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{100 nm\}\\\)\, usually \\\(\\pu\{10 nm\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{50 nm\}\\\)."
comment: "In a micro-emulsion the domains of the dispersed phase are either globular or interconnected (to give a bicontinuous micro-emulsion)."
comment: "The average diameter of droplets in macro-emulsion (usually referred to as an "emulsion") is close to one millimeter (i.e., \(\pu{E-3 m}\)). Therefore, since micro- means \(\pu{E-6 m}\) and emulsion implies that droplets of the dispersed phase have diameters close to \(\pu{E-3 m}\), the micro-emulsion denotes a system with the size range of the dispersed phase in the \(\pu{E-6} \times \pu{E-3 m} = \pu{E-9 m}\) range."
comment: "The term "micro-emulsion" has come to take on special meaning. Entities of the dispersed phase are usually stabilized by surfactant and/or surfactant-cosurfactant (e.g., aliphatic alcohol) systems."
comment: "The term "oil" refers to any water-insoluble liquid."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307

[Term]
id: goldbook:14318
name: hemi-micelle
def: "Type of micelle that exists in relatively small numbers below the critical micelle concentration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14319
name: ad-micelle
def: "Surfactant bilayer formed on a charged adsorbing surface."
comment: "Ad-micelles are usually formed on inorganic particles."
comment: "In the case of particles with charged surfaces the surfactant molecules are oriented with their charged head-groups toward the particle surfaces. In the case of further addition of surfactant, a surface bilayer may form, which is termed an ad-micelle (adsorbed micelle)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14320
name: micellar aggregation number
def: "Number of molecules constituting a micelle."
synonym: "micellar degree of association" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14321
name: micellar charge
def: "Combined charge of the surfactant ions and counterions tightly bound to a micelle."
comment: "Micelle with tightly bound ions behaves as a unit carrying the net charge."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14322
name: micellar relative molar mass
def: "Mass of a mole of micelles divided by the molar mass constant. The relative molar mass of micelles \(mic\) is thus \\\(M_\{\\rm\{r\,mic\}\} = M_\{\\rm\{mic\}\}/M_\{\\rm\{u\}\}\\\)."
comment: "1/12 of the molar mass of \(\ce{^{12}C}\) is termed "molar mass constant" with symbol \(M_{\rm{u}} = M(\ce{^{12}C})/12 = N_{\rm{A}} m_{\rm{u}}\) and unit \(\pu{g mol-1}\) where \(m_{\rm{u}}\) is the "atomic mass constant" with unit \(\pu{u}\) or \(\pu{Da}\), and \(N_{\rm{A}}\) is the Avogadro constant."
comment: "The micellar relative molar mass refers to a neutral micelle and thus includes the mass of counterions that compensate the charge of surfactant molecules in micelles."
synonym: "micellar molecular weight" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14323
name: particle number concentration
def: "Number of particles per volume of suspending medium."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14324
name: solids content
def: "Mass fraction of nonvolatile material in a polymer dispersion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14311

[Term]
id: goldbook:14325
name: polymer content
def: "Mass fraction of polymer in a polymer dispersion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14311

[Term]
id: goldbook:14326
name: dispersed-phase concentration
def: "Amount concentration of a species within the dispersed phase."
comment: "If the dispersed phase depends on quantities such as radius, \(r\), time, \(t\), etc., the recommended symbols are \([\ce{A}]_{\rm{p}}(r,t,\ldots)\) and \([\ce{M}]_{\rm{p}}(r,t,\ldots)\)."
synonym: "dispersed-phase amount concentration" []
synonym: "particle-phase amount concentration" []
synonym: "particle-phase concentration" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307

[Term]
id: goldbook:14327
name: continuous-phase concentration
def: "Concentration of species within the continuous phase of a dispersion."
comment: "If the continuous phase is water, the symbols \([\ce{A}]_{\rm{w}}\) and \([\ce{M}]_{\rm{w}}\) are usually used."
comment: "If the continuous-phase concentration depends on quantities such as time \(t\), etc., the recommended symbols are \([\ce{A}]_{\rm{cont}}(t,\ldots)\) and \([\ce{M}]_{\rm{cont}}(t,\ldots)\)."
synonym: "continuous-phase amount concentration" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14328
name: polymer mass fraction
def: "Mass fraction of polymer within the dispersed phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307

[Term]
id: goldbook:14329
name: emulsion polymerisation
def: "Polymerization whereby monomer\(s\)\, initiator\, dispersion medium\, and possibly colloid stabilizer constitute initially an inhomogeneous system resulting in particles of colloidal dimensions containing the formed polymer."
comment: "With the exception of mini-emulsion polymerization, the term "emulsion polymerization" does not mean that polymerization occurs in the droplets of a monomer emulsion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14345

[Term]
id: goldbook:14330
name: ab initio emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization in which no seed particles are added."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14331
name: batch emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization in which all the ingredients are placed in a reactor prior to reaction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14332
name: continuous emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization in which all the ingredients are added continuously and the product latex is removed continuously."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14333
name: emulsifier-free emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization carried out without the addition of a colloid stabilizer."
comment: "In an emulsifier-free emulsion polymerization, a colloid stabilizer is produced in situ (e.g., the polymerization of styrene initiated with potassium persulfate yields macromolecules with anionic end groups providing ionic stabilization of the colloidal polystyrene particles)."
comment: "Other names, such as emulsifier-less, soap-less, soap-free, surfactant-less, and surfactant-free emulsion polymerization, that are sometimes used, are not recommended."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14334
name: encapsulating emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization leading to the encapsulation of a solid within polymer particles or liquid polymer droplets."
comment: "An encapsulating emulsion polymerization is often performed inside ad-micelles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14319
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14335
name: inverse emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization in a nonaqueous medium in which the dispersed phase is usually an aqueous solution\, initially of monomer\(s\)\, and finally of polymer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14336
name: monomer-flooded emulsion polymerisation
def: "Semi-continuous emulsion polymerization in which the monomer\(s\) is\(are\) fed to the reactor at a rate that exceeds the rate of polymerization."
comment: "A monomer-flooded emulsion polymerization refers to a state where the monomer concentration in the polymer particles is at or greater than its equilibrium swelling value and therefore droplets may be formed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14340

[Term]
id: goldbook:14337
name: monomer-starved emulsion polymerisation
def: "Semi-continuous emulsion polymerization in which the polymerization rate is controlled by the feed rate\(s\) of monomer\(s\)\, in such a way that\, for most of the process\, the polymerization rate equals the monomer\(s\) feed rate\(s\)."
comment: "Usually a monomer-starved emulsion polymerization refers to a state where the monomer concentration in the polymer particles is less than its equilibrium swelling value."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14340

[Term]
id: goldbook:14338
name: power-feed emulsion polymerisation
def: "Semi-continuous emulsion copolymerization in which the instantaneous composition of the formed copolymer is the same as that of the added monomer mixture\(s\)."
comment: "A power-feed emulsion polymerization is normally achieved by feeding to the reactor monomer mixture(s) from one or more reservoirs under monomer-starved conditions. In the simplest case, reservoirs I and II are initially filled with monomers \(\ce{A}\) and \(\ce{B}\), respectively. During polymerization the contents of reservoir I are continuously pumped into the reactor and the contents of reservoir II are continuously pumped into reservoir I at definite rates."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14340

[Term]
id: goldbook:14339
name: seeded emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization with seed particles are formed in situ or added initially to the polymerizing mixture."
comment: "Under certain conditions the seed particles capture enough radical species from the aqueous phase so that no new particles are formed. In such polymerization, the number of growing particles is equal to the number of seed particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14329
consider: goldbook:14376

[Term]
id: goldbook:14340
name: semi-continuous emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization in which some of the ingredients are initially placed in a reactor and the remaining ingredients are added during the polymerization."
synonym: "semi-batch emulsion polymerization" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14341
name: vesicle polymerisation
def: "Polymerization inside the bilayer of a vesicle leading to formation of polymer inside the bilayer."
comment: "In the case of reactive copolymerizing surfactants (i.e., surfmers) hollow spherical entities can sometimes be obtained with a homogeneous distribution of polymer in the bilayer."
comment: "The bilayer may contain polymerizable and non-polymerizable molecules."
comment: "The morphology of such entities is called "parachute" morphology, owing to similarity of their shape to the shape of parachute canopy."
comment: "Usually phase separation occurs leading to entities with inhomogeneously distributed polymer (e.g., entities that contain a latex particle inside the vesicle’s bilayer)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14377

[Term]
id: goldbook:14342
name: micro-emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization in which the starting system is a micro-emulsion and the final latex comprises colloidal particles of polymer dispersed in an aqueous medium."
comment: "Diameters of polymer particles formed in the micro-emulsion polymerization usually are between \(\pu{10 nm}\) and \(\pu{50 nm}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14317
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14343
name: inverse micro-emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization in which the starting system is a micro-emulsion and the final system is composed of an organic continuous phase with an aqueous polymer solution as the dispersed phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307
consider: goldbook:14308
consider: goldbook:14317
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14344
name: micellar polymerisation
def: "Polymerization of a polymerizable surfactant in solution above its critical micelle concentration."
comment: "The initial micellar structure usually is not preserved during the polymerization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14345
name: mini-emulsion polymerisation
def: "Polymerization of a mini-emulsion of monomer in which all of the polymerization occurs within preexisting monomer particles without the formation of new particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14316

[Term]
id: goldbook:14346
name: inverse mini-emulsion polymerisation
def: "Emulsion polymerization in which the starting system is a mini-emulsion and the final system is composed of an organic continuous phase with an aqueous polymer solution as the dispersed phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307
consider: goldbook:14308
consider: goldbook:14316
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14347
name: precipitation polymerisation
def: "Polymerization in which monomer\(s\)\, initiator\(s\) and colloid stabilizer\(s\) are dissolved in a solvent and this continuous phase that is a nonsolvent for the formed polymer beyond a critical molecular weight."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14348
name: dispersion polymerisation
def: "Precipitation polymerization in which monomer\(s\)\, initiator\(s\)\, and colloid stabilizer\(s\) are dissolved in a solvent forming initially a homogeneous system that produces polymer and results in the formation of polymer particles."
comment: "The process usually results in polymer particles of colloidal dimensions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14347

[Term]
id: goldbook:14349
name: seeded dispersion polymerisation
def: "Dispersion polymerization in which seed particles are formed in situ or added prior to initiation of the polymerization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14348
consider: goldbook:14376

[Term]
id: goldbook:14350
name: precipitation polycondensation
def: "Precipitation polymerization proceeding by polycondensation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14347

[Term]
id: goldbook:14351
name: dispersion polycondensation
def: "Dispersion polymerization proceeding by polycondensation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14348

[Term]
id: goldbook:14352
name: precipitation polyaddition
def: "Precipitation polymerization proceeding by polyaddition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14347

[Term]
id: goldbook:14353
name: dispersion polyaddition
def: "Dispersion polymerization proceeding by polyaddition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14348

[Term]
id: goldbook:14354
name: suspension polymerisation
def: "Polymerization in which polymer is formed in monomer\, or monomer-solvent droplets in a continuous phase that is a nonsolvent for both the monomer and the formed polymer."
comment: "In suspension polymerization, the initiator is located mainly in the monomer phase."
comment: "Monomer or monomer-solvent droplets in suspension polymerization have diameters usually exceeding \(\pu{10 \upmu m}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14355
name: micro-suspension polymerisation
def: "Suspension polymerization in which the diameter of the monomer droplets is of the order of a few \\\(\\pu\{\\upmu m\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14354

[Term]
id: goldbook:14356
name: average number of radicals per particle
def: "Ratio of the total number of radicals in particles to the number of particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14357
name: critical oligomer degree of polymerisation for irreversible entry
def: "Lowest degree of polymerization of aqueous-phase oligomer-radicals needed for irreversible capture by colloidal particles\, micelles\, or both during a polymerization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14358
name: critical oligomer degree of polymerisation for precipitation
def: "Lowest degree of polymerization of oligomer-radicals that precipitate from the continuous phase during a polymerization."
comment: "\(j_{\rm{crit}}\) is usually equal to the degree of polymerization at which oligomer-radicals undergo a coil-to-globule transition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14359
name: intervals in emulsion polymerisations
def: "Periods in an emulsion polymerization defined by the formation of polymer particles\, and the presence or absence of monomer droplets in the polymerizing mixture."
comment: "In naming particular intervals, the word "interval" is always written with a capital I."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14360
name: interval 1 in emulsion polymerisation
def: "Period in a batch ab initio emulsion polymerization during which the formation of particles takes place."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14330
consider: goldbook:14331

[Term]
id: goldbook:14361
name: interval 2 in emulsion polymerisation
def: "Period in an emulsion polymerization during which no new particles are formed and monomer droplets are present."
comment: "This interval is associated with an approximately constant value of the average number of radicals per particle, an approximately constant value of monomer concentration in the particles, and, thus, an approximately constant rate of polymerization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14362
name: interval 3 in emulsion polymerisation
def: "Period in an emulsion polymerization during which no new particles are formed and no monomer droplets are present."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14329

[Term]
id: goldbook:14363
name: zero-one behaviour
def: "Limiting behaviour in an emulsion\, mini-emulsion\, or micro-emulsion polymerization during which the entry of a radical into a particle that contains a growing radical results in termination before significant propagation has occurred."
comment: "The value of the average number of radicals per particle (\(\bar N\)) for a zero-one system can never exceed \(\pu{0.5}\)."
comment: "This type of behaviour commonly occurs for small particles, the size of which depends on the type of monomer and on polymerization conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14316
consider: goldbook:14342
consider: goldbook:14356

[Term]
id: goldbook:14364
name: compartmentalisation behaviour
def: "Zero-one behaviour wherein radicals are isolated\, each being located within a different latex particle."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14363

[Term]
id: goldbook:14365
name: pseudo-bulk behaviour
def: "Behaviour in an emulsion\, mini-emulsion\, micro-emulsion\, suspension\, or dispersion polymerization wherein the kinetics are such that the rate equations are the same as those for polymerization in bulk."
comment: "Common extreme cases are (i) when the value of \(\bar N\) is so high that each particle effectively behaves as a micro-reactor, and (ii) when the value of \(\bar N\) is low, exit is very rapid and the exited radical re-enters another particle, may grow to a significant degree of polymerization, and so on before any termination event."
comment: "In a pseudo-bulk system, the average number of radicals per particle, \(\bar N\), can take any value."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14316
consider: goldbook:14317
consider: goldbook:14348
consider: goldbook:14356

[Term]
id: goldbook:14366
name: homogeneous micellisation nucleation
def: "Formation of primary particles as a result of micelle formation from surface-active oligomer radicals formed in a polymerization."
comment: "The surface-active oligomer radicals are usually formed by polymerization with initiators providing ionic end-groups."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14374

[Term]
id: goldbook:14367
name: micellar nucleation
def: "Formation of primary particles as a result of polymerization within monomer-swollen micelles initiated by the capture of primary radicals or oligomer-radicals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14374
consider: goldbook:14375

[Term]
id: goldbook:14368
name: coagulative nucleation
def: "A process combining nucleation by any mechanism with subsequent coagulation being a significant event in formation of colloidally stable particles."
comment: "The term "coagulative nucleation" does not mean that nucleation is caused by coagulation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14369
name: phase-transfer event in a dispersed system
def: "Transport of any species \(radical\, monomer\, chain-transfer agent\, etc.\) from the continuous to the discrete phase and vice-versa."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14370
name: radical entry
def: "Irreversible transport of a radical from the continuous to the dispersed phase."
comment: "This type of transport frequently involves a radical arising directly from initiator. An example is the sulfate radical anion \(\ce{SO4^{.-}}\), with the systematic name tetraoxidosulfate (\(•1-\)) (where the part in parentheses is pronounced "dot one minus"), propagating with monomer in the aqueous phase until the resulting oligomeric species enters a particle irreversibly."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14307

[Term]
id: goldbook:14371
name: radical entry frequency
def: "Average number of entry events per particle per unit interval of time."
comment: "The term "entry rate coefficient" is incorrect and is not recommended."
synonym: "entry frequency" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14372
name: radical exit
def: "Reversible or irreversible transport of a radical from the dispersed to the continuous phase."
comment: "This type of transport is frequently through transfer of the radical activity at the end of a macroradical within a particle to a smaller species which may then diffuse irreversibly out of the parent particle into the continuous phase."
synonym: "radical desorption" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14308

[Term]
id: goldbook:14373
name: radical exit frequency
def: "Average number of exit events per particle per unit interval of time per radical."
comment: "The term "exit rate coefficient" is incorrect and is not recommended."
synonym: "exit frequency" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14375
name: primary radical
def: "Radicals formed from an initiator molecule."
comment: ""Primary radical" describes the radical before it reacts with any molecule of monomer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14376
name: seed particle
def: "Particle in a polymer colloid that is the locus of subsequent polymerization."
comment: "A seed particle is either added to a polymerization mixture before the polymerization begins, or is formed in situ."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14313

[Term]
id: goldbook:14377
name: surfmer
def: "Monomer with the properties of a surfactant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14378
name: inisurf
def: "Initiator with the properties of a surfactant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14379
name: transurf
def: "Chain-transfer agent with the properties of a surfactant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14380
name: breaking of an emulsion
def: "Formation of a system with separate macrophases from an emulsion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14381
name: critical coagulation concentration
def: "Minimum concentration of electrolyte at and above which rapid coagulation occurs."
comment: "As the value of the \({\rm{c}}_{\rm{cc}}\) depends to some extent on the experimental circumstances (method of mixing, time between mixing and determining the state of coagulation, criterion for measuring degree of coagulation, etc.), these should be clearly stated."
comment: "Rapid coagulation occurs when the only forces between the particles are the attractive van der Waals forces, all other forces being negligible."
synonym: "critical coagulation amount concentration" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14384

[Term]
id: goldbook:14382
name: heterocoagulation
def: "Coagulation of particles of different kinds or sizes\, or both."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14383
name: homocoagulation
def: "Coagulation of colloidal particles of the same size and kind."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14384
name: fast coagulation rate
def: "Rate of coagulation in the absence of any repulsive barrier between particles."
comment: "The fast coagulation rate is usually measured by adding electrolyte at an increasing concentration, until the observed coagulation rate becomes independent of the electrolyte concentration."
synonym: "rapid coagulation rate" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14385
name: fast coagulation rate coefficient
def: "Rate coefficient for fast coagulation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14387
name: flocculation rate coefficient
def: "Rate coefficient for flocculation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14386

[Term]
id: goldbook:14388
name: micellisation
def: "Process in which surface-active molecules or ions aggregate into micelles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14389
name: orthokinetic coagulation
def: "Coagulation due to collisions of particles induced by hydrodynamic motion."
comment: "Orthokinetic coagulation occurs when shear-induced collisions dominate over collisions due to Brownian motion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14390
name: particle monolayer
def: "Monolayer of particles deposited at an interface."
comment: "A monolayer of regularly deposited particles is called a two-dimensional colloidal crystal."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14391
name: perikinetic coagulation
def: "Coagulation due to collisions of particles caused by their Brownian motion."
comment: "Perikinetic coagulation occurs in the absence of mixing or under conditions where shear-induced collisions are negligible compared to diffusion-induced collisions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14392
name: slow coagulation rate
def: "Rate of coagulation in presence of repulsive barriers between particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14393
name: slow coagulation rate coefficient
def: "Rate coefficient for slow coagulation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14394
name: stability ratio
def: "Ratio \\\(W = k_\{\\rm\{fast\}\}/k_\{\\rm\{slow\}\}\\\) or \\\(W = k_\{\\rm\{fast\}\}/k_\{\\rm\{floc\}\}\\\)\, for coagulation or flocculation\, respectively\, with \\\(k_\{\\rm\{fast\}\}\\\)\, \\\(k_\{\\rm\{slow\}\}\\\)\, and \\\(k_\{\\rm\{floc\}\}\\\) measured under the same mixing \(or hydrodynamic\) conditions."
comment: "When comparing \(W\) with theory, the fast coagulation rates are often approximated by the Smoluchowski rates of coagulation."
synonym: "Fuchs stability ratio" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14395
name: colloidally stable system
def: "System in which the particles essentially do not aggregate or sediment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14396
name: electrostatic stabilisation
def: "Stabilization of a colloid resulting from the mutual repulsion of the electrical double layers surrounding its particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14397
name: electrosteric stabilisation
def: "Stabilization of a colloid that has both steric and electrostatic stabilization characteristics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14396

[Term]
id: goldbook:14398
name: steric stabilisation
def: "Stabilization of a colloid resulting from covering particles with a layer of molecules solvated by the continuous medium."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-10-06-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14399
name: ecotoxicology
def: "Study of the toxic effects of chemical and physical agents on all living organisms\, especially on populations and communities within defined ecosystems; it includes transfer pathways of these agents and their interactions with the environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14400
name: mutagenicity
def: "Ability of a physical\, chemical\, or biological agent to induce \(or generate\) heritable changes \(mutations\) in the genotype in a cell as a consequence of alterations or loss of genes or chromosomes \(or parts thereof\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14401
name: ultrafine particle
def: "Particle in air of aerodynamic diameter \\\(\\pu\{\\lt 0.1 \\upmu m\}\\\)."
comment: "The fraction of the air particulates referred to as ultrafines is often referred to as the \(\pu{PM_{0.1}}\) fraction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14402
name: toxicogenetics
def: "Study of the influence of hereditary factors on the effects of potentially toxic substances on individual organisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14403
name: reproductive toxicity
def: "Ability of a physical\, chemical\, or biological agent to induce adverse effects in the reproductive system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14404
name: reproductive toxicology
def: "Study of the non-heritable adverse effects of substances on male and female reproductive function or capacity and on resultant progeny."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14405
name: risk assessment management process
def: "Global term for the whole process from hazard identification to risk management."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14406
name: risk management
def: "Decision-making process involving considerations of political\, social\, economic\, and engineering factors with relevant risk assessments relating to a potential hazard so as to develop\, analyze\, and compare regulatory options and to select the optimal regulatory response for safety from that hazard."
comment: "Essentially risk management is the combination of three steps: risk evaluation; emission and exposure control; risk monitoring."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14407
name: safety
def: "Reciprocal of risk\: practical certainty that injury will not result from a hazard under defined conditions."
comment: "Safety (toxicological): The high probability that injury will not result from exposure to a substance under defined conditions of quantity and manner of use, ideally controlled to minimize exposure."
comment: "Safety of a drug or other substance in the context of human health: the extent to which a substance may be used in the amount necessary for the intended therapeutic purpose with a minimum risk of adverse health effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14408
name: safety data sheet
def: "Single page giving toxicological and other safety advice\, usually associated with a particular preparation\, substance\, process\, use pattern\, or exposure scenario."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14409
name: immunotoxicity
def: "Ability of a physical\, chemical\, or biological agent to induce adverse effects in the immune system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-09-03-01
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14410
name: dormant polymer chain
def: "Temporarily deactivated chain carrier."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-04-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14411
name: reversible chain deactivation
def: "Deactivation of a chain carrier in a chain polymerisation\, reversibly converting the active center into an inactive one and then\, within the lifetime of a growing macromolecule\, regenerating an active center on the same original chain carrier."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-04-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14412
name: degenerate-transfer radical polymerisation
def: "Controlled reversible-deactivation radical polymerization in which the deactivation of the radicals involves degenerative transfer \(DT\) of a group \(or atom\)."
synonym: "DTRP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-04-03
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14413
name: absorbate
def: "Substance that enters and is retained inside a solid or semisolid matrix \(absorbent\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14414

[Term]
id: goldbook:14414
name: absorbent
def: "Solid or semisolid matrix that is able to accommodate and retain an absorbate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14413
consider: goldbook:15040

[Term]
id: goldbook:14415
name: abundance
def: "Total number of individual organisms in a population\, seen over a defined period of time in a certain place.Note\: For fish\, an estimate of total weight may replace number. Total number of organisms per unit of habitat space seen over a defined period. Amount of an element that exists in nature\, usually expressed in relative terms as a percentage of the total amount of all elements in a given medium \(e.g.\, the Earth’s crust\). Amount of an isotope of an element that exists in nature\, usually expressed in relative terms as a percentage of the total amount of all isotopes of the element."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14728
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14416
name: abundant element
def: "Element which is of common occurrence in the Earth’s crust."
comment: "Abundance may be defined in terms of occurrence in other regions, e.g., oceans, "freshwater"."
synonym: "abundant metal" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14415

[Term]
id: goldbook:14417
name: accessible
def: "Capable of being entered or reached; easy of access; such as one can go to\, come into the presence of\, reach\, or lay hold of; get-at-able."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14418
name: acclimatisation
def: "Processes\, including selection and adaptation\, by which a population of microorganisms develops the ability to degrade a substance\, or develops a tolerance to it. In experimental systems\, allowing an organism to adjust to its environment prior to undertaking a study. Modification of biological processes or structures in the maintenance of homeostasis in response to change in some environmental quality such as temperature\, salinity\, light\, radiation\, or toxicant concentration. Note\: It is an expression of phenotypic plasticity of individuals in response to a sublethal change in some environmental factor."
synonym: "acclimatation" []
synonym: "acclimation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14711
consider: goldbook:14744
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14419
name: acid precipitation
def: "Rain\, fog\, snow\, sleet\, or other particulate matter from the atmosphere with a _000078_ below \\\(\\pu\{5.6\}\\\) deposited from the air."
comment: "Rain under clean air conditions has a _000078_ slightly under \(\pu{6}\). This natural acidity is caused by dissolved carbon dioxide dissociating to form carbonate and hydrogencarbonate ions. "Acid rain" is caused by sulfur in fossil fuels, and nitrogen from the air combining with oxygen to form sulfur oxides and nitrogen oxides during combustion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14420
name: acid-volatile sulfide
def: "Soil- and sediment-associated solid-phase sulfides extractable with cold hydrochloric acid."
comment: "AVS may be chemically available by acid extraction without being bioavailable. Thus, AVS can reduce metal toxicity by binding metals in anoxic soils or sediments, thereby rendering them unavailable to most living organisms."
synonym: "AVS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14473
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14421
name: acute
def: "Of short duration\, in relation to exposure or effect; the effect usually shows a rapid onset. Note 1\: In regulatory toxicology\, 'acute' refers to studies where dosing is either single or limited to one day although the total study duration may extend to two weeks to permit appearance of toxicity in susceptible organ systems. Note 2\: In aquatic ecotoxicology\, exposure of the test organisms is typically continuous and of four days or less. In clinical medicine\, sudden and severe\, having a rapid onset."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14524

[Term]
id: goldbook:14422
name: acute-to-chronic toxicity ratio
def: "Numerical dimensionless quantity that is the ratio of an acute toxicity test result \(e.g.\, \\\(\\pu\{LC_\{50\}\}\\\)\) to a chronic toxicity test result \(e.g.\, maximum acceptable toxicant concentration\, MATC\) where both are expressed in the same units \(e.g.\, \\\(\\pu\{mg L-1\}\\\)\). Ideally\, the data are for the same chemical species."
comment: "It is in principle the inverse of an application factor and is used in a similar manner. The ACR is commonly used for estimating chronic toxicity of a chemical on the basis of its acute toxicity. The ACR should be greater than one because the ratio compares an acute to a chronic value."
synonym: "ACR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14421
consider: goldbook:14524
consider: goldbook:14832
consider: goldbook:15121

[Term]
id: goldbook:14423
name: additive effect
def: "Consequence that follows exposure to two or more physicochemical agents that act jointly but do not interact\: the total effect is the simple sum of the effects of separate exposures to the agents under the same conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14424
name: additive index
def: "Quantification of the joint action of toxicants in mixture by adding measures of their toxicity calculated in relation to the toxicity of a reference toxicant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14425
name: adenylate energy charge
def: "Index reflecting the balance of energy transfer between catabolic and anabolic processes\, calculated from the equation \\\[\\rm\{AEC\} = \(\[\\ce\{ATP\}\] + ½\[\\ce\{ADP\}\)/\(\[\\ce\{ATP\}\] + \[\\ce\{ADP\}\] + \[\\ce\{AMP\}\]\)\\\] where \\\(\\ce\{ATP\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{ADP\}\\\)\, and \\\(\\ce\{AMP\}\\\) are the amount concentrations of adenosine tri-\, di-\, and monophosphate\, respectively."
synonym: "AEC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14426
name: adsorption factor
def: "Ratio of the amount of substance adsorbed at the interface of a condensed layer and a liquid or gaseous phase to the total amount of the substance available for adsorption."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14427
name: age class
def: "Group of organisms of the same age within a population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14428
name: age composition
def: "Distribution of organisms among the various age classes present in the population. The sum of the number of individuals in all age classes equals the population size."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14429
name: age distribution
def: "Composition of a population in terms of how its abundance is distributed across age classes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14415
consider: goldbook:14427
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14430
name: age-specific death rate
def: "Mean number of deaths as tabulated for a life table interval or for a specific age class in a given year\, expressed per \\\(\\pu\{1000\}\\\) in that interval or age class."
synonym: "age-specific mortality" []
synonym: "age-specific number of individuals dying" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14427

[Term]
id: goldbook:14431
name: aggregation error
def: "Error in Bayesian probability analysis of model systems resulting from the use of a single set of parameters to represent a collection of distinct entities\, such as individuals\, in a population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14463
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14432
name: air pollution tolerance index
def: "Empirical index used to assess the tolerance of individual plants to contaminated air. The numerical value of \\\(T_\{\\rm\{I\}\}\\\) is obtained by combining various quantities according to the recipe \\\(\[A \(T + P\) + R\]/10\\\)\, where \\\(A\\\) is the mass of ascorbic acid divided by the dry mass of a leaf\, expressed as \\\(\\pu\{mg/g\}\\\)\, \\\(T\\\) is the total mass of chlorophyll divided by the fresh mass\, expressed as \\\(\\pu\{mg/g\}\\\)\, \\\(P\\\) is the pH of a leaf extract\, and \\\(R\\\) is the mass of water in the leaf divided by the wet mass\, expressed as percent."
comment: "In common usage, the equation is not formulated as a coherent equation, but requires the given units."
synonym: "APTI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14433
name: alga
def: "Any of various chiefly aquatic\, eukaryotic\, photosynthetic organisms\, ranging in size from single-celled forms to the giant kelp."
comment: "Algae of various species, often unicells, are used for toxicity testing in ecotoxicology. They are an important component of aquatic food webs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14434
name: algal bloom
def: "Rapid increase in the abundance of phytoplankton or benthic algae in a given area\, often as a result of an increased availability of nutrients or light\, or increase in temperature \(e.g.\, the spring bloom\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14468
consider: goldbook:14918

[Term]
id: goldbook:14435
name: algicide
def: "Substance intended to kill algae."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14436
name: algistatic
def: "Inhibiting algal population growth."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14435
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14437
name: allogenic succession
def: "Sequential appearance of species driven by external influences that alter local conditions; e.g.\, silt deposits changing a marshland to woodland."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15077

[Term]
id: goldbook:14438
name: ambient
def: "Surrounding \(applied to environmental media such as air\, water\, sediment\, or soil\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14439
name: ambient monitoring
def: "Continuous or repeated measurement of agents in the environment to evaluate ambient exposure and health risk by comparison with appropriate reference values based on knowledge of the probable relationship between exposure and resultant adverse health effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14438

[Term]
id: goldbook:14440
name: anadromous
def: "Showing anadromy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14441

[Term]
id: goldbook:14441
name: anadromy
def: "Life-history pattern that is characterized by egg incubation and early juvenile development in freshwater\, migration to seawater for adult development\, and a return to freshwater for spawning."
comment: "Obligatory anadromy is the term applied where migration to seawater is required for survival."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14516
consider: goldbook:14797

[Term]
id: goldbook:14442
name: analysis plan
def: "Scheme that defines the exact format and design of the assessment\, explicitly states the data needed\, and describes the methods and design for analyzing these data."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14443
name: anthropogenic
def: "Caused by or influenced by human activities. Describing a conversion factor used to calculate a dose or concentration affecting a human that has been derived from data obtained with another species\, e.g.\, the rat."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14444
name: antisymmetry
def: "Quality of a population of bilaterally symmetrical individuals in which the difference in measurement of a trait made from the right and left sides of individuals from that population produces a bimodal distribution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14696
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14445
name: arcsine square root transformation
def: "\\\(\\arcsin \\sqrt\{P\}\\\)\, where \\\(P\\\) is the value of a measured effect\, e.g.\, the proportion of exposed organisms in a population."
comment: "This transformation of effects data often fulfills an assumption of homogeneous variances for proportions of exposed individuals responding to a stimulus."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14446
name: artificial soil test
def: "Test with earthworms in which the toxicity of a substance by skin and gut uptake is determined by adding the earthworms to an artificial soil made of sand\, clay mineral\, and peat\, containing the substance of concern."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14447
name: artisol test
def: "Test with earthworms in which the toxicity of a substance by skin and gut uptake is determined by placing the worms in an artificial substrate consisting of silica\, water\, and glass balls\, containing the substance of concern."
comment: "In the artisol test, the earthworms ingest the silica paste as they do soil."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14448
name: aryl hydrocarbon hydroxylase
def: "Enzyme activity attributed to cytochrome P-450 monooxygenase isoforms and often measured in units of benzo\[a\]pyrene hydroxylation."
synonym: "AHH" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "unspecific mono-oxygenase" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14449
name: as low as reasonably achievable
def: "Describing the situation in which everything practicable is done to reduce risks to the minimum with the approval of the regulatory authorities."
synonym: "ALARA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14943

[Term]
id: goldbook:14450
name: assemblage
def: "Set of coexisting populations defined by phylogeny\, location\, or life style. Assemblages are intermediate between populations and communities."
comment: "An operational definition is "species located in the same place at the same time"."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14914
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14451
name: assessment endpoint
def: "Ecological property that is to be protected and the precise parameter to be measured for this property."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14836

[Term]
id: goldbook:14452
name: Association Française de Normalisation test
def: "Commercially available test kit\, certified by AFNOR as valid and equivalent to a standardized method."
synonym: "AFNOR test" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14453
name: asymptotic threshold concentration
def: "Concentration of a chemical at which some percentage of a population of test organisms is in a state of approximate homeostasis for a prolonged period of time \(\\\(\\pu\{48 h\}\\\) or more\)."
comment: "The asymptotic \(\pu{LC_{50}}\) is the concentration at which the \(\pu{LC_{50}}\) remains constant no matter how long exposure continues, i.e., there is no evidence of significantly increasing effects due to a longer exposure time."
comment: "This can be demonstrated as the concentration at which the toxicity curve is approximately asymptotic (parallel) to the time axis."
synonym: "ATCN" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14744
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14454
name: atmospheric deposition
def: "Process that transfers a chemical from the atmosphere to the Earth’s surface \(land\, water\, or vegetation\) by either dry impingement or by transport in rain or snow."
synonym: "deposition" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15135

[Term]
id: goldbook:14456
name: aufwuchs
def: "Floral and \(or\) or faunal communities attached to submerged surfaces in aquatic ecosystems."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14907

[Term]
id: goldbook:14457
name: autogenic succession
def: "Sequential appearance of species driven by processes operating within the community environment \(compare allogenic succession\)\, e.g.\, primary and secondary successions that occur on newly exposed land."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14437
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:15077

[Term]
id: goldbook:14458
name: autotroph
def: "Organism that is independent of outside sources for organic food materials and manufactures its own organic material from inorganic sources."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14459
name: autotrophic succession
def: "Sequential appearance of species in a location principally involving plants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15077

[Term]
id: goldbook:14460
name: axenic culture
def: "Growth of organisms of a single species in the absence of cells or living organisms of any other species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14461
name: baseline toxicity
def: "General\, nonspecific\, reversible mode of toxic action that can be produced in most living organisms by the presence of sufficient amounts of many organic chemicals."
comment: "Effects result from the general disruption of cellular activity. The mechanism producing disruption is unknown, with the main theories being binding to proteins in cell membranes and "swelling" of the lipid portion of cell membranes resulting from the presence of organic chemicals."
comment: "Hydrophobicity dominates the expression of baseline toxicity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14462
name: Bayesian
def: "Attributed to Thomas Bayes \(1702–1761\)\, English mathematician. The term is used to designate concepts relating to inverse probability\, especially Bayes’ theorem\, a theorem expressing the probability of one of a number of mutually exclusive events \\\(H_\{\\rm\{i\}\}\\\)\, given some other event \\\(E\\\)\, in terms of the probabilities of all the \\\(H_\{\\rm\{i\}\}\\\) independently of \\\(E\\\) and the probabilities of \\\(E\\\) given each \\\(H_\{\\rm\{i\}\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14463
name: Bayesian probability
def: "Subjective or objective concept of probability as a 'measure of the state of knowledge'."
comment: "Assessment of probability in Bayesian theory can be approached as, e.g., odds for one or the other result of a stochastic outcome. Modern machine learning methods are frequently based on Bayesian theory."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14464
name: behavioural teratology
def: "Study of behavioral abnormalities in otherwise apparently normal individuals after exposure in the embryonic state to a substance or physical agent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14465
name: behavioural toxicology
def: "Study of abnormal behavior produced by exposure to a substance or physical agent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14466
name: beneficial metal
def: "Non-essential metal which in some form \(chemical species\) at an appropriate dose can improve health of defined organisms\, commonly human beings."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14467
name: benefit
def: "Advantage to\, or improvement in condition of\, an individual\, a population\, a species\, an assemblage\, a community\, or an ecosystem."
comment: "For risk/benefit comparisons, the probability of benefit is the appropriate comparator."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14450
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14544
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14468
name: benthic
def: "Living on the bottom of an aquatic system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14469
name: bioaccessible
def: "Able to come in contact with a living organism and perhaps interact with it with the possibility of absorption into the organism."
comment: "Contact with a living organism may not result in any interaction of the substance with, and absorption by, the organism. In other words, bioaccessibility is a necessary precursor of bioavailability but not, on its own, sufficient for bioavailability to occur."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14470
name: bioaccumulation
def: "Progressive increase in the amount of a substance in an organism or part of an organism that occurs because the rate of intake from all contributing sources and by all possible routes exceeds the organism’s ability to eliminate the substance from its body."
comment: "Bioaccumulation of organic molecules usually correlates with lipophilicity. Bioaccumulation of metal ions tends to correlate with strong binding to biomolecules or incorporation into bone and teeth."
synonym: "accumulation in biology" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14476
consider: goldbook:14484

[Term]
id: goldbook:14471
name: bioaccumulation factor
def: "Ratio of tissue chemical residue to chemical concentration in an external environmental phase \(e.g.\, sediment\, water\, soil\, air\, or food\). BAF is measured at a steady state in situations where organisms are exposed to multiple sources \(e.g.\, water\, sediment\, food\)\, unless noted otherwise."
comment: "In relation to uptake from food, the concentration in the organism is typically expressed per unit body mass or per gram of lipid and the concentration in food is expressed per gram dry weight of food."
comment: "The compound may have entered the organism by any available route and from any component of the water or sediment."
comment: "The concentration in sediment may be expressed per gram dry weight of sediment or per gram of organic carbon and may be referred to as the biota-sediment accumulation factor (BSAF)."
comment: "The concentration in the organism is typically expressed per unit body mass or per gram of lipid (bioaccumulation factor, lipid-based)."
synonym: "accumulation factor" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14498
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14472
name: bioactivation
def: "Metabolic conversion of a xenobiotic to a more toxic derivative or to one that has more of an effect on living organisms."
synonym: "activation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15100

[Term]
id: goldbook:14473
name: bioavailable
def: "Able to be absorbed by living organisms."
synonym: "available" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14469

[Term]
id: goldbook:14474
name: biocenosis
def: "All the interacting organisms living together in a specified habitat."
comment: "The area occupied by a biocenosis is defined by a characteristic assembly of species."
synonym: "biocoenosis" []
synonym: "biological community" []
synonym: "biotic community" []
synonym: "ecological community" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14450
consider: goldbook:14728

[Term]
id: goldbook:14475
name: biocide
def: "Substance intended to kill living organisms. Nonagricultural pesticide used to control the severity and incidence of pests or diseases\, e.g.\, algicide\, slimicide\, or disinfectant for the control of algal\, fungal\, or bacterial growth."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14476
name: bioconcentration
def: "Process leading to a higher concentration of a substance in an organism than in environmental media to which it is exposed."
comment: "Usually applied to uptake by aquatic organisms directly from water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14470

[Term]
id: goldbook:14477
name: bioconcentration factor
def: "Measure of the tendency for a substance in water to accumulate in aquatic organisms defined as the ratio of the concentration of the substance of concern in the organism to the concentration in water at equilibrium."
comment: "The equilibrium concentration of a substance in an aquatic organism can be estimated by multiplying its concentration in the surrounding water by its BCF in that organism."
comment: "This parameter is an important determinant for human intake of contaminants from water by ingestion of aquatic food."
synonym: "BCF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549

[Term]
id: goldbook:14478
name: lipid-based bioconcentration factor
def: "Ratio of the concentration of the substance of concern in the lipid fraction of the test organism to the concentration in the ambient water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14438

[Term]
id: goldbook:14479
name: biodiversity
def: "Occurrence of a number of species within a given ecosystem or biome\, or the presence of a number of community types in a given area."
comment: "Biodiversity can be measured on many biological levels, but the term most commonly refers to the number of different species in a defined area (species richness) and is quantified by calculating a diversity index which takes into account the relative abundance of individuals of each species."
comment: "Biodiversity is often a measure of the health of biological systems."
comment: "In special cases, biodiversity may include a degree of genetic variation within a single species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14415
consider: goldbook:14489
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14599
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:15051

[Term]
id: goldbook:14480
name: biodiversity action plan
def: "Internationally recognized program designed to protect and restore biological systems containing threatened species and habitats."
comment: "The original impetus for these plans derives from the 1992 Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD)."
comment: "The principal elements of a BAP typically include: (a) preparing inventories of biological information for selected species or habitats; (b) assessing the conservation status of species within specified ecosystems; (c) creation of targets for conservation and restoration; and (d) establishing budgets, timelines, and institutional partnerships for implementing the BAP."
synonym: "BAP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14728

[Term]
id: goldbook:14481
name: biogeochemical cycle
def: "Movement of elements or molecules among organisms and nonliving compartments of the atmosphere\, lithosphere\, and hydrosphere."
comment: "Examples of biogeochemical cycles are the carbon, nitrogen, phosphorus, and sulfur cycles. These are defined as the global flow of \(\ce{C}\), \(\ce{N}\), \(\ce{P}\), and \(\ce{S}\) atoms, respectively, from plants through animals to the atmosphere, soil, water, and back to plants."
comment: "The water cycle refers to the global flow of water from surface and ground water sources to soil, plants, animals, and the atmosphere, and back to soil and surface water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14482
name: biological indicator
def: "Any biological species or group of species whose performance\, abundance\, or population status is used to determine the health of an environment or ecosystem by systematic monitoring of chemical\, physiological\, or behavioral changes."
comment: "Bioindicator is commonly misused as a synonym for the term biomarker. Such use is to be deprecated."
comment: "Deviation of bioindicator performance indicates some adverse effect. In a wider sense, the number and abundance of different indicator species (biodiversity, species richness) is used to calculate biotic indices."
synonym: "bioindicator" []
synonym: "indicator species" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14415
consider: goldbook:14479
consider: goldbook:14499
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14932
consider: goldbook:15051

[Term]
id: goldbook:14483
name: biological determinant
def: "Property of living organisms that affects human or environmental health."
comment: "Biological determinants may be either endogenous or exogenous. Endogenous biological determinants include genetic characteristics and physiological state. Exogenous biological determinants are other living organisms with which the organisms of concern interact, e.g., beneficial or harmful microorganisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14484
name: biomagnification
def: "Sequence of processes by which higher concentrations of a substance are attained in organisms at higher trophic levels. Result of these processes of bioconcentration and bioaccumulation by which tissue concentrations of bioaccumulated chemicals increase as the chemical passes up through two or more trophic levels. Note\: Biomagnification occurs in a food chain as a consequence of efficient transfer of a substance from food to consumer accompanied by the lack of\, or very slow\, excretion or degradation of the substance."
synonym: "bioamplification" []
synonym: "ecological magnification" []
synonym: "trophic enrichment" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15113

[Term]
id: goldbook:14485
name: biomagnification factor
def: "Ratio of concentrations of a compound at two consecutive trophic levels at steady state. It can also be expressed in terms of a rate constant-based bioaccumulation model \\\[B = C_\{n\}/C_\{n-1\} = \\alpha f/k_\{\\rm\{e\}\}\\\] where \\\(\\alpha\\\) is assimilation efficiency\, \\\(f\\\) is feeding rate\, and \\\(k_\{\\rm\{e\}\}\\\) is the first-order elimination constant. \\\(B\\\) can be calculated from field data on assumed trophic relations or from laboratory feeding experiments."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14484

[Term]
id: goldbook:14486
name: biomarker of effect
def: "Biomarker that\, depending upon the magnitude\, can be recognized as associated with an established or possible health impairment or disease."
synonym: "effect biomarker" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14487
name: biomarker of exposure
def: "Biomarker that relates exposure to a xenobiotic to the levels of the substance or its metabolite\, or of the product of an interaction between the substance and some target molecule or cell\, that can be measured in a compartment within an organism."
synonym: "exposure biomarker" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14537

[Term]
id: goldbook:14488
name: biomarker of susceptibility
def: "Biomarker of an inherent or acquired ability of an organism to respond to exposure to a specific substance."
synonym: "susceptibility biomarker" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14489
name: biome
def: "Set of plants and animals that occupy a certain geographic area."
comment: "The term is usually applied to large areas occupied by climax communities arising as a result of interactions between biotic and abiotic factors,"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14528

[Term]
id: goldbook:14490
name: biomodification
def: "Alteration of the chemical or physical properties of a substance by the action of living organisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14491
name: biomonitor
def: "n. Organism that provides quantitative information on the quality of the environment around it.Note\: The ideal substance biomonitor would indicate the presence of a specific pollutant and provide additional information about the amount present. v. To use organisms to monitor pollutants and to deduce possible effects on biota or routes of toxicant exposure to humans."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14492
name: biomonitoring type 1
def: "Determination of community changes along a gradient or among sites differing in levels of pollution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14493
name: biomonitoring type 2
def: "Determination of bioaccumulation in organisms among sites notionally varying in the level of contamination."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14470

[Term]
id: goldbook:14494
name: biomonitoring type 3
def: "Determination of effects on organisms using tools such as biochemical markers in sentinel species or some measure of diminished fitness or condition of individuals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14495
name: biomonitoring type 4
def: "Determination of genetically based resistance in populations of contaminated areas."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14496
name: biopesticide
def: "Biological agent with pesticidal activity\, e.g.\, the bacterium Bacillus thuringiensis when used to kill insects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14497
name: bioremediation
def: "Use of biological organisms such as plants or microbes to aid in removing hazardous substances from an area."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14498
name: biota-sediment accumulation factor
def: "Ratio of lipid-normalized tissue chemical residue to carbon-normalized sediment substance concentration \(units of mass lipid/mass organic carbon\)."
synonym: "BSAF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "accumulation factor (AF)" []
synonym: "bioavailability index (BI)" []
synonym: "biota-sediment factor (BSF)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14471

[Term]
id: goldbook:14499
name: biotic index
def: "One of several ranking systems calculated from the presence or abundance of sensitive species relative to tolerant species."
comment: "Biotic indices measure decreased environmental quality from effects on especially sensitive species and should not be compared to diversity indices, which measure community structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14536
consider: goldbook:14599

[Term]
id: goldbook:14500
name: biotic ligand
def: "Component of a living organism to which an ion or other substance in aqueous solution can bind\, usually with subsequent beneficial or harmful effect on the physiology of the organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14501
name: biotic ligand model
def: "Model that integrates the interactions of metals with ligands in water to calculate the speciation \(based on hardness\, salinity\, and presence of other metals\) and the concentration of ionic species producing toxicity. The BLM chemically and mathematically models the organism’s target site as ligand\(s\) competing with nonbiotic ligands\, based on the concept that toxicity occurs when a metal-\(biotic ligand\) complex reaches a critical concentration."
comment: "For fish, the biotic ligand for metal ions is either known or suspected to be the ion channel proteins in the gill surface that regulate the ionic composition of the blood. For other organisms, it is hypothesized that a biotic ligand exists and that mortality can be modeled in a similar way."
comment: "The BLM is a development of the free ion activity model (FIAM) for calculating free metal ions in relation to water-borne ligands and the Windermere humic aqueous model (WHAM) for calculating metal speciation in relation to organic species in water."
comment: "The model is a generalization of the FIAM. The difference between the BLM and the FIAM is the consideration of competitive binding at the biotic ligand, which models the protective effects of other metal cations, and the direct influence of \(\rm{pH}\)."
synonym: "BLM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14502
name: biotic score
def: "Weighted measurement of organisms present—the weighted part is determined by each group’s pollution tolerance or intolerance. As pollution increases in a stream\, the biotic score value tends to increase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14503
name: biotope
def: "Habitat shared by many species\, most often an area that is uniform in environmental conditions and in its distribution of animal and plant life."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14728

[Term]
id: goldbook:14504
name: bioturbation
def: "Group of processes whereby organisms affect the structure of sediment."
comment: "Bioturbation consists of two processes, particle mixing and irrigation, mainly executed by infaunal organisms but also by epifaunal organisms and bottom-feeding fish."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14505
name: biphasic dose–effect model
def: "Model of adverse effect vs. dose relationship that\, owing to hormesis\, dips down from the control level before increasing with the dose; individuals exposed to low\, but nontoxic concentrations are healthier than individuals not exposed to the chemical.Note\: Biphasic dose–effect curves occur for any nutrient. Hormesis is a phenomenon associated with compounds that have no nutrient properties. Model of adverse effect vs. dose relationship that changes slope owing to a change in the mechanism of toxic action.Note\: This may\, e.g.\, be due to saturation of a transport or metabolic system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14601
consider: goldbook:14745

[Term]
id: goldbook:14506
name: birth rate
def: "\(in demography\) Number of live births in a defined administrative jurisdiction in a calendar year divided by a midyear population of the jurisdiction\, with the customary multiplier of \\\(\\pu\{1000\}\\\) to produce a whole number rather than a decimal or a fraction. Note\: An alternative statistic is total fertility rate\, the average number of children born to each woman over the course of her life. In general\, the total fertility rate is a better indicator of fertility rates because\, unlike the crude birth rate\, it is not affected by the age distribution of the population. \(in ecology\) Number of births\, \\\(B\\\)\, in a population of a defined size\, \\\(N\\\)\, during a specified time interval \\\(\\Delta t\\\). The rate is calculated from the formula \\\[B = \\Delta N/\\Delta t\\\] where \\\(\\Delta N\\\) is the change in the number of births in a limited time period \\\(\\Delta t\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14904
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14507
name: boomerang effect
def: "Delayed damage from earlier environmental contamination."
comment: "Sometimes stated as "what you throw away can come back to hurt you"."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14508
name: borderline metal ions
def: "Metal ions intermediate in properties between class a and class b metal ions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14509
name: bottom-up ecotoxicological study
def: "Approach to investigating ecotoxicological effects that starts with a determination of the presence and nature of any adverse effects via responses at the suborganismal \(cellular and biochemical\) levels of organization rather than via the community and \(or\) ecosystem levels of organization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:15098

[Term]
id: goldbook:14510
name: Brillouin index
def: "Quantitative value for community species diversity calculated as \\\[H_\{\\rm\{B\}\} = \(\\ln N! - \\sum \\ln n_\{i\}!\)/N\\\] where \\\(N\\\) is the total number of individuals and \\\(n_\{i\}\\\) is the number of individuals in the \\\(i^\{\\rm\{th\}\}\\\) species."
comment: "Evenness for the Brillouin index is estimated as \(E = H_{\rm{B}}/H_{\rm{Bmax}}\) where \(H_{\rm{Bmax}}\) is the maximum possible Brillouin diversity which occurs when all species are equally abundant."
comment: "When a subsample is taken from a given area, the Brillouin index provides a better estimate of diversity than the Shannon–Wiener index for samples of the same size. It also corresponds to situations of sampling without replacement, whereas the Shannon–Wiener index is appropriate for sampling with replacement."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14599
consider: goldbook:15031

[Term]
id: goldbook:14511
name: broodstock
def: "Adult fish producing either eggs or sperm."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14512
name: calcinosis
def: "Any pathological condition characterized by the deposition of calcium salts in tissues."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14513
name: calcium sink
def: "Tissue such as arthropod cuticle\, bivalve shell\, or vertebrate bone that renders calcium or elements with similar biological behavior \(such as lead or cadmium\) less bioavailable during trophic interactions\, thus providing a mechanism for trophic dilution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14473

[Term]
id: goldbook:14514
name: carrying capacity
def: "Maximum population size expressed as total number of individuals\, biomass\, or population density that a given unit of habitat is capable of sustaining."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14728
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14515
name: catadromous
def: "Describing a species exhibiting catadromy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14516

[Term]
id: goldbook:14516
name: catadromy
def: "Life-history pattern that is characterized by egg incubation and early juvenile development in seawater\, migration to freshwater for adult development\, and return to seawater for spawning."
comment: "Obligatory catadromy is the term applied where migration to freshwater is required for survival."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14441

[Term]
id: goldbook:14517
name: catagenesis
def: "Long-term geochemical alteration to organic matter\, involving high temperatures and pressures deep below the surface of the Earth."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14518
name: cetaceans
def: "Whales\, dolphins\, and porpoises\, in the order Cetacea."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14519
name: Chapman mechanism
def: "Series of reactions by which ozone is formed in the stratosphere."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14520
name: chemical time bomb
def: "Substance or substances in a component of the environment which are not currently bioavailable but which may become bioavailable at an unknown time in the future with harmful consequences."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14473

[Term]
id: goldbook:14521
name: chloride cell
def: "Specialized cell with a role in ion regulation\, characterized by large numbers of mitochondria\, an extensive intracellular tubular network and a high concentration of \\\(\\ce\{Na+\}\\\)/\\\(\\ce\{K+\}\\\) ATPase. This cell is found in salt-secreting glands like the rectal gland of elasmobranchs\, the nasal gland of seabirds\, and the gills of both seawater and freshwater fish\, mainly on the primary lamellae but also on the secondary lamellae."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14522
name: chlorinity
def: "Proportion by mass of dissolved chloride ions in water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14523
name: chlorofluorocarbon
def: "Carbon-based chemical containing chlorine and fluorine\, responsible for ozone depletion in the stratosphere."
comment: "Formerly commonly used as aerosol propellants and refrigeration coolants, but now prohibited in many countries."
synonym: "CFC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14863

[Term]
id: goldbook:14524
name: chronic effect
def: "Consequence that develops slowly and \(or\) has a long-lasting course\: may be applied to an effect which develops rapidly and is long lasting."
synonym: "long-term effect" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14421

[Term]
id: goldbook:14525
name: chlorosis
def: "Loss of green color in plants owing to the lack of production or the destruction of chlorophyll."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14526
name: cladistics
def: "Systematic classification of groups of organisms on the basis of shared characteristics thought to derive from a common ancestor. Also\, the study of the branching of evolutionary lines of descent and the relationship between branches."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14527
name: cladogram
def: "Dendrogram illustrating the supposed evolutionary relationships between clades; a diagram showing cladistic relationships."
comment: "Cladograms are often based on such information as the number of differences in amino acids or nucleic acid bases in common proteins or genes, respectively. From estimated mutation rates, the evolutionary time can be estimated. Accordingly, cladograms have two components, branching order (showing group relationships) and branch length (showing extent of evolution)."
synonym: "evolutionary tree" []
synonym: "phylogenetic tree" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14528
name: climax community
def: "Community of plants and animals in a steady state due to ecological succession resulting in a composition of the community best adapted to average conditions in the area. The term is sometimes applied to soil development."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:15036
consider: goldbook:15077

[Term]
id: goldbook:14529
name: cold condensation theory
def: "Theory that pollutants with high vapor pressure\, e.g.\, mercury or persistent organic pollutants \(POPs\)\, in the air will condense onto soil\, water\, and biota at cool temperatures. Consequently\, the ratios for POP concentrations in the air and on condensed phases decrease as one moves from warmer to cooler climates."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14909
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14530
name: cometabolism
def: "Microbial transformation of a compound \(that is normally unable to support cell replication\) in the requisite presence of a transformable cosubstrate that supports cell replication."
comment: "The mechanisms of cometabolism considered likely in most cases involve an enzyme or enzymes that change the substrate to a product or products not further transformed by other enzymes (dead-end metabolites)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14552
consider: goldbook:14565
consider: goldbook:15022

[Term]
id: goldbook:14531
name: community
def: "Assembly of populations of different species of living organisms\, usually interdependent on and interacting with each other\, within a specified location in space and time."
synonym: "biocommunity" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14532
name: community conditioning hypothesis
def: "Hypothesis that ecological communities retain information about events in their history and will not return to their original state after perturbation."
comment: "This hypothesis was derived from the concept of nonequilibrium community ecology and was developed as a framework for understanding the persistence of dose-related responses in multispecies toxicity tests."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14533
name: community stability
def: "Tendency of a community to return to its original state after a disturbance \(competition\, temporarily changing environment\, etc.\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14534
name: community resilience
def: "Ability of a community to return to its former state after perturbation."
comment: "A community with high resilience will return to its original state faster than one with low resilience."
synonym: "ecological resilience" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14535
name: community resistance
def: "Ability of a community to avoid displacement from its present state by a disturbance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14536
name: community structure
def: "Species present in a community and their relative abundances."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14537
name: compartment
def: "Conceptualized part of the body \(organs\, tissues\, cells\, or fluids\) considered as an independent system for purposes of modeling and assessment of distribution and clearance of a substance. Part of an ecosystem considered as an independent system for purposes of assessment of uptake\, distribution\, and dissipation of a substance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:14538
name: competitive exclusion
def: "Outcompetition from a niche of one species by another that uses the available resources of the niche more efficiently\, eventually resulting in the exclusion of the outcompeted species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14877

[Term]
id: goldbook:14539
name: complimentary niches
def: "Niches where coexisting species occupy a similar position along one niche dimension\, e.g.\, altitude\, but differ along another\, e.g.\, diet."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14877

[Term]
id: goldbook:14540
name: concentration–response curve
def: "Graph of the relation between exposure concentration and the proportion of individuals in a population responding with a defined effect."
synonym: "exposure–response curve" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14541
name: conceptual model
def: "Linkage and interrelationship of assessment endpoint\(s\) and stressors."
comment: "Conceptual models include hypotheses of risk and a diagram of the conceptual model."
comment: "Establishing this includes evaluation of potential exposure pathways, effects, and ecological receptors."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14542
name: conceptual model diagram
def: "Figure showing pathways of exposure of organisms and illustrating areas of uncertainty or concern."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14543
name: conceptual site model
def: "Integration of information on contaminants of potential concern \(COPCs\)\, ecological resources\, evaluated exposure routes\, fate and transport mechanisms\, evaluated COPC toxicity\, identified assessment endpoints\, and risk questions and hypotheses\, into a description of all that is known and \(or\) expected about a contaminated site."
synonym: "CSM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14544
name: condition
def: "State of health determining potential for reproduction and growth."
comment: "Mainly used in fish, mussel, and oyster ecology."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14545
name: condition factor
def: "Parameter used to describe growth in fish. It reflects real growth and nutritional status better than simple measurement of body mass."
comment: "The condition factor, \(K\), is calculated from the following equation: \[K = m/l^{3}\] with mass, \(m\) and length \(l\) of the fish. The usual units are \(\pu{g cm-3}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14546
name: condition index
def: "Any quantitative measure of the condition in relation to a defined baseline."
comment: "In mussels, various shell indexes (volume/length, mass/length), glycogen concentration (w/bw), or relative organ mass are used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14544

[Term]
id: goldbook:14547
name: conservation biology
def: "Science applied to the conservation of genes\, populations\, species\, and ecosystems."
comment: "This science is concerned with the phenomena that affect the maintenance, loss, and restoration of biological diversity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14548
name: conservation ecology
def: "Science of analyzing and protecting the Earth’s biological diversity."
comment: "Conservation ecology is based on the biological, physical, and social sciences, economics, and the practice of natural-resource management. It concentrates on population dynamics issues associated with the small population sizes of rare species (e.g., minimum viable populations)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14859
consider: goldbook:14936

[Term]
id: goldbook:14549
name: contaminant
def: "Minor impurity present in a substance. Extraneous material inadvertently added to a sample prior to or during chemical or biological analysis. In some contexts\, as in relation to gas cleaning equipment\, used as a synonym for 'pollutant'\, especially on a small scale. Unintended component in food that may pose a hazard to the consumer. Any undesirable solid\, liquid\, or gaseous matter occurring\, as a result of human activities\, in a solid\, liquid\, or gaseous environmental medium\, even without adverse effects being observed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14928

[Term]
id: goldbook:14550
name: continuous effect
def: "Change that can be measured on a continuum from zero \(or even a negative value\) to positive values such as growth and reproduction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14965

[Term]
id: goldbook:14551
name: control
def: "Treatment in a toxicity test that duplicates all the conditions of the exposure treatments but contains no test material\, in order to determine the absence of toxicity under basic test conditions \(e.g.\, health of test organisms\, quality of dilution water\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14552
name: cooxidation
def: "Cometabolism whereby growing microorganisms oxidize a compound without using either carbon or energy derived from the oxidation of that compound."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14530

[Term]
id: goldbook:14553
name: copepod
def: "Minute marine or freshwater crustacean\, usually having six pairs of limbs on the thorax; some are abundant in plankton and others are parasitic on fish\, marine mammals\, and macro-invertebrates."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14554
name: corrosive
def: "n. Substance having the capability or tendency to cause slow destruction. adj. Gradually destructive; steadily harmful."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14555
name: cost–benefit analysis
def: "Procedure for determining the relationship of the expected benefits of a proposed action to the expected costs in order to decide whether the action provides the best option for the investment of limited resources."
synonym: "CBA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14556

[Term]
id: goldbook:14556
name: cost-effectiveness analysis
def: "Procedure for determining whether the expected beneficial effects of a defined course of action justify the cost when selecting among competing options for the use of limited resources."
comment: "Mainly used for comparing the relative value of various clinical strategies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14555

[Term]
id: goldbook:14557
name: cough
def: "Abrupt\, periodic reversal of water flow over the gills that dislodges and eliminates excess mucus from the gills’ surfaces."
synonym: "gill purge" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14558
name: critical body residue
def: "Whole-body concentration of a chemical that is associated with a given adverse biological response."
comment: "This assumes each organism is a single compartment, rather than multiple compartments as in reality. It has utility as a first approximation of dose."
synonym: "CBR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14559
name: critical life-stage testing
def: "Toxicity testing focused on the species life stage thought to be the most sensitive to the toxicant\, such as newly hatched individuals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14560
name: cross-resistance
def: "Condition in which enhanced tolerance to one toxicant also enhances tolerance to another."
synonym: "cotolerance" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14561
name: culture
def: "n. Stock of healthy cells\, tissue\, microorganisms\, or plants raised under well-defined and controlled conditions. v. To maintain a stock of healthy organisms under well-defined and controlled conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14562
name: cumulative dose
def: "Total dose resulting from repeated exposures or continuous exposure over a defined time to a substance or to radiation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14563
name: cumulative exposure
def: "Total exposure resulting from repeated and continuous exposure over a defined time to a substance or to radiation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14564
name: Daphnia
def: "Small\, mostly planktonic\, crustaceans\, between \\\(\\pu\{0.2 mm\}\\\) and \\\(\\pu\{5 mm\}\\\) in length."
comment: "Daphnia are members of the order Cladocera, and are one of the several small aquatic crustaceans commonly called water fleas because of their saltatory swimming style (although fleas are insects and thus only very distantly related). Daphnia spp. live in various aquatic environments ranging from acidic swamps to freshwater lakes, ponds, streams, and rivers."
comment: "Toxicity tests on Daphnia are required by most regulatory authorities. The results are often interpreted as applicable by extrapolation to the protection of all crustaceans."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14565
name: dead-end metabolite
def: "Substance formed by a microbe’s metabolism of a substrate \(most often during cometabolism\) that cannot be further metabolized by that organism."
comment: "Dead-end metabolites may be further metabolized by coexisting organisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14530

[Term]
id: goldbook:14566
name: death
def: "In assessing population ecology\, death of an individual is loss of the ability to reproduce."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14760

[Term]
id: goldbook:14567
name: death
def: "Irreversible cessation of all vital functions of an organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14568
name: death rate
def: "Number of deaths \\\(D\\\) in a closed population of size \\\(N\\\) during a specified time interval\, \\\(\\Delta t\\\). The rate is calculated from the formula \\\[D = -\\Delta N/\\Delta t\\\] where \\\(\\Delta N\\\) is the change in number of deaths over a specified time period."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14905
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14569
name: dechlorinated water
def: "Chlorinated water \(usually municipal drinking water\) that has been treated to remove chlorine and chlorinated compounds from solution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14570
name: decomposer
def: "Organism that breaks down dead matter or wastes of other organisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14571
name: defoliant
def: "Substance used for removal of leaves by its toxic action on living plants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15100

[Term]
id: goldbook:14572
name: demographic stochasticity
def: "Variability in population growth rates arising from random differences among individuals in survival and reproduction within a season."
comment: "Such variability is important only in populations that are fairly small."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14573
name: demography
def: "Study of populations\, especially their age structure and growth rates."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14574
name: density dependence
def: "Variation in characteristics of individuals or of a population produced by changes in the density of the population."
comment: "Density dependence may be seen in mortality rate, birth rate, fítness, sensitivity to environmental toxins, transmission of pathogens, and parasites, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14575
name: deposit feeder
def: "Animal that feeds on particles of matter in the soil or sediment\, usually the top soil or sediment where it is filled with organic matter. Feeding takes place either by ingesting soil or sediment or by trapping particles as they fall."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14576
name: depuration
def: "Loss of a substance from an organism owing to elimination and degradation."
comment: "The rate of depuration is expressed by its half life or the time needed to eliminate \(\pu{50\%}\) of the substance in a noncontaminated medium. This term is often referred to as the depuration time (\(\pu{DT_{50}}\))."
synonym: "depuration time" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14577
name: derived characteristic
def: "Predicted property of a substance that is dependent upon\, or is an approximation of\, a fundamental property and the prevailing environmental conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14578
name: deterministic
def: "Term applied to effects\, of which the extent varies with the dose and for which a threshold is believed to exist."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14579
name: deterministic analysis
def: "Detailed study in which all population and environmental parameters are assumed to be constant and accurately specified."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14580
name: deterministic model
def: "Mathematical model that is fully specified and does not include a stochastic component."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14581
name: detritus
def: "Organic debris from decomposing plants and animals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14582
name: detrivorous
def: "Describing an organism that survives by eating detritus."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14581

[Term]
id: goldbook:14583
name: developmental reference dose
def: "Reference dose determined for developmental consequences of a single\, maternal exposure during development."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14584
name: developmental stability
def: "Potential of an organism to develop into a consistent phenotype in an environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14585
name: diatom
def: "Member of a major group of eukaryotic algae\, among the most common types of phytoplankton. Unicellular\, some form chains or simple colonies. Diatom cells are encased in a frustule\, of widely diverse form\, made of silica \(hydrated silicon dioxide\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14586
name: diffuse source
def: "Release into the environment from multiple sources covering a wide area as opposed to point source."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14927

[Term]
id: goldbook:14587
name: dilution paradigm
def: "Belief that pollution is alleviated by dilution."
comment: "Sometimes stated as "The solution to pollution is dilution.""
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14588
name: dilution water
def: "Water used to dilute the test material in an aquatic toxicity test in order to prepare either different concentrations of a test chemical or different percentages of an effluent for the various test treatments."
comment: "The water (negative) control in a test is prepared with dilution water only."
synonym: "diluent" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14589
name: direct ecological effect
def: "Effect where a stressor acts immediately on an ecological component of interest and not through the consequences of effects on other components of the ecosystem."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14757

[Term]
id: goldbook:14590
name: directional asymmetry
def: "Deviation within a population from a mean of zero for the difference between a trait measured from the right and left sides of bilaterally symmetrical individuals from that population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14444
consider: goldbook:14696
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14591
name: direct toxicity
def: "Toxicity that results from\, and is readily attributable to\, substances acting at the sites of toxic action in and \(or\) on the exposed organisms that are exhibiting the adverse biological response in question."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14592
name: discharge
def: "Release of any waste into the environment from a point source."
comment: "Usually applied to release of liquid waste into water but may be applied to release to air."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14593
name: discrimination ratio
def: "Ratio measuring the degree of isotopic discrimination\, with a ratio of 1 indicating no discrimination."
comment: "In the context of discrimination between elements such as cesium and potassium in a trophic exchange, a discrimination factor or ratio is expressed as \([\ce{Cs}]_{\rm{food}}/[\ce{K}]_{\rm{food}}\) divided by \([\ce{Cs}]_{\rm{body}}/[\ce{K}]_{\rm{body}}\)."
synonym: "discrimination factor" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14777

[Term]
id: goldbook:14594
name: dispersant
def: "Substance used to disperse liquid spills\, e.g.\, oil spills in water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14595
name: dissolved organic carbon
def: "Amount concentration of carbon found dissolved in water samples from aquatic systems\, measured as total elemental carbon."
comment: "DOC is important in the transport and bioavailability of pollutants in aquatic systems."
comment: "Metals may form strong complexes with DOC, increasing metal solubility and concentration in water, while also reducing metal bioavailability."
comment: "The "dissolved" fraction of organic carbon is an operational classification. Operationally, DOC is defined as the organic matter that is able to pass through a defined filter (filters generally range in size between \(\pu{0.7 \upmu m}\) and \(\pu{0.22 \upmu m}\)). Conversely, particulate organic carbon (POC) in water is that carbon that is too large and is filtered out of a sample."
comment: "The DOC in marine and freshwater systems is part of the greatest cycled reservoir of organic matter on Earth and consists mostly of humic substances."
synonym: "DOC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14597
consider: goldbook:14928

[Term]
id: goldbook:14596
name: dissolved oxygen content
def: "Amount concentration of oxygen dissolved in water at a particular temperature and pressure."
comment: "This can be a limiting factor on the growth of aquatic populations."
synonym: "DOC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14597
name: dissolved organic matter
def: "Analogous to dissolved organic carbon\, but refers to the entire organic pool dissolved in water."
synonym: "DOM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14595

[Term]
id: goldbook:14598
name: disturbance
def: "Event that introduces\, removes\, or redistributes organisms\, changing the colonization potential of a given environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14599
name: diversity index
def: "Mathematical descriptor of species variation within a community."
comment: "All diversity indices are based on the relative abundance of a species, i.e., the sum of all individuals of that species divided by the sum of all individuals in the community of interest."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14510
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:15031
consider: goldbook:15034

[Term]
id: goldbook:14600
name: dose–effect
def: "Relation between dose and the magnitude of a measured biological change."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14601
name: dose–effect curve
def: "Graph of the relation between dose and the magnitude of the biological change produced measured in appropriate units."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14602
name: dose–effect relationship
def: "Association between dose and the resulting magnitude of a continuously graded change\, either in an individual or in a population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14603
name: dose–response curve
def: "Graph of the relation between dose and the proportion of individuals in a population responding with a defined biological effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14604
name: dose–response relationship
def: "Association between dose and the incidence of a defined biological effect in an exposed population usually expressed as percentage."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14605
name: drainage basin
def: "Area of land where water from rain or snow melt drains downhill into a body of water\, such as a river\, lake\, dam\, estuary\, wetland\, sea\, or ocean."
comment: "A drainage basin acts like a funnel, collecting all the water within the area covered by the basin and channeling it into a waterway. Each drainage basin is separated topographically from adjacent basins by a ridge, hill, or mountain, which is known as a water divide."
comment: "A drainage basin includes the streams and rivers that convey the water as well as the land surfaces from which water drains into those channels, separated from adjacent basins by a drainage divide."
synonym: "catchment" []
synonym: "catchment area" []
synonym: "catchment basin" []
synonym: "drainage area" []
synonym: "river basin" []
synonym: "water basin" []
synonym: "watershed" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14661
consider: goldbook:15136

[Term]
id: goldbook:14606
name: dynamic energy budget theory
def: "Theory that simple quantitative rules may be applied to define the organization of metabolism of individual organisms."
comment: ""Dynamic" refers to changes in energy budgets in relation to individual life cycle. The theory includes stoichiometric constraints and mass balance equations, allometric relationships, organizational uncoupling of metabolic modules, strong and weak homeostasis, and partionability of reserve kinetics."
comment: "In relation to ecotoxicology, effects of toxicants on energy allocation have been modeled by Kooijman and Bedaux."
synonym: "DEB" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "DEB theory" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14607
name: dynamically fragile community
def: "Community that is stable for only a very limited range of environmental characteristics\, e.g.\, a stable and predictable environment with respect to predator–prey ratios or disturbances caused by humans."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14608
name: dynamically robust community
def: "Community that is stable within a wide range of conditions\, e.g.\, in very variable and unpredictable environments."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14609
name: dynamic stability hypothesis
def: "Hypothesis that long food chains are less stable than short food chains."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14610
name: ecology
def: "Branch of biology that studies the interactions between living organisms and all factors \(including other organisms\) in their environment. Such interactions encompass environmental factors that determine the distributions of living organisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14611
name: ecological character
def: "Sum of biological\, physical\, and chemical components of an ecosystem and their interactions that maintain the ecosystem and its products\, functions\, and attributes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:14612
name: ecological energetics
def: "Study of the flow of energy within an ecological system from the time the energy enters the living system until it is irretrievably lost from the system as heat."
comment: "It is also referred to as production ecology, because ecologists use the word "production" to describe the process of energy input and storage in ecosystems."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:14613
name: ecological epidemiology
def: "Application of epidemiological methods to determine the cause\, incidence\, prevalence\, and distribution of adverse effects in nonhuman species inhabiting contaminated sites; it is frequently associated with retrospective ecological risk assessment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14995

[Term]
id: goldbook:14614
name: ecological imbalance
def: "Change in any biological\, physical\, or chemical components of an ecosystem\, or in their interactions\, which result in change in ecological character and its functions and attributes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:15050

[Term]
id: goldbook:14615
name: ecological mortality
def: "Toxicant-related diminution of fitness of an individual functioning within an ecosystem that is of a magnitude sufficient to be equivalent to somatic death."
comment: "This concept implies that an individual organism may be so incapacitated by an environmental change that, though still alive, its contribution to the ecosystem becomes negligible."
synonym: "ecological death" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:14616
name: ecological parameter
def: "Measurable variable whose value is a determinant of the characteristics of an ecosystem."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:14617
name: ecophysiology
def: "Study of physiology and tolerance limits of species that enhances understanding of their distribution in relation to abiotic conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14618
name: ecoregion
def: "Any of a number of regions into which a continent\, country\, etc.\, can be divided according to their distinct environmental conditions and habitat types. Large area of land or water with a characteristic\, geographically distinct assemblage of natural communities and species comprising a recurring pattern of ecosystems associated with characteristic combinations of soil and landform.Note\: The biodiversity of ecosystems in an ecoregion is often distinct from that of other ecoregions."
synonym: "bioregion" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14479
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14728
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14619
name: ecosystem
def: "Grouping of organisms \(microorganisms\, plants\, animals\) interacting together\, with and through their physical and chemical environments\, to form a functional entity within a defined environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14620
name: ecotone
def: "Area of gradual transition between two or more ecosystems."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14624

[Term]
id: goldbook:14621
name: ecotoxicologically relevant concentration
def: "Concentration of a pesticide \(active ingredient\, formulations\, and relevant metabolites\) that is likely to affect a determinable ecological characteristic of an exposed system."
synonym: "ERC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "environmentally relevant concentration" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14622
name: edaphic
def: "Pertaining to the soil."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14623
name: eddy motion
def: "Movement in a current of water or air\, that is contrary to the direction of the main current\, especially in a circular motion\, leading to irregularity in the motion of molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14624
name: edge effect
def: "Influence of the closeness of contrasting environments on an ecosystem\, seen at boundaries between natural habitats\, especially forests\, and disturbed or developed land."
comment: "Ecotones often have species assemblages with high species richness (\(S\)) and high abundance of individuals relative to those of the adjacent communities."
comment: "Edge effects lead to changes in species richness and population size at the boundary between two communities, most pronounced in small habitat fragments where they may extend throughout the patch."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14620
consider: goldbook:14728
consider: goldbook:14932
consider: goldbook:15051

[Term]
id: goldbook:14625
name: effect time
def: "Time taken for a substance to produce a precisely defined effect."
comment: "\(\pu{ET_{50}}\) is the median time it takes for a toxicant to produce a precisely defined effect in \(\pu{50\%}\) of a population."
synonym: "ET" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14626
name: effects assessment
def: "Component of risk assessment concerned with quantifying the manner in which the frequency and intensity of effects increase with increasing exposure to a contaminant or other source of stress \(also known as dose–response assessment or toxicity assessment\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14627
name: elasticity
def: "Ability of a community to return to its prestressed condition."
synonym: "community elasticity" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14628
name: elutriate
def: "Aqueous solution obtained after adding water to a solid substance \(e.g.\, sediment\, tailings\, drilling mud\, or dredging spoil\)\, shaking the mixture\, then centrifuging or filtering it or decanting the supernatant."
comment: "An operational definition is water collected from vigorous shaking (\(\pu{15 min}\) to \(\pu{30 min}\)) of one part sediment with four parts water. This mixture is allowed to settle, and the liquid phase is centrifuged and may be filtered."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14629
name: elutriate test
def: "Test in which a nonbenthic species\, such as Daphnia magna\, is exposed to an elutriate produced by mixing test sediment with water and then centrifuging the mixture."
comment: "The elutriate test was developed for evaluating the potential effects of disposing of dredged material in open water. Analyses of elutriate samples measure the water-soluble constituents potentially released from sediment to the water column during dredge disposal operations"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14630
name: emergent properties
def: "New properties emerging with upward steps in hierarchical systems\, such as ecological communities or ecosystems\, that cannot be predicted solely from our limited understanding of the system’s parts or components."
comment: "Such properties arise during the self-organization of complex systems and are the product of the evolution of these systems."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:14631
name: emission standard
def: "Quantitative limit on the emission or discharge of a substance from a source\, usually expressed in terms of a time-weighted average concentration or a ceiling value."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14632
name: endemic
def: "Pertaining to a species found in a discrete geographical unit\, such as an island\, habitat type\, or other defined area or zone."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14728

[Term]
id: goldbook:14633
name: endemism
def: "Ecological state of being unique to a place."
comment: "There are two subcategories of endemism-paleoendemism and neoendemism. Paleoendemism refers to a species that was formerly widespread but is now restricted to a smaller area. Neoendemism refers to a species that has recently arisen, e.g., by hybridization (see  and is now classified as a separate species. This is a common process in plants especially those that exhibit polyploidy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14634
name: endotherm
def: "'Warm-blooded organism' that regulates its body temperature to be \(almost\) constant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14635
name: endpoint
def: "Objective of measurement of a toxicity test."
comment: "Endpoints vary with the level of biological organization being examined and may include changes in biochemical markers or enzyme activities, mortality or survival, growth, reproduction, primary production, and changes in structure, abundance, and function in a community. Endpoints are used as criteria for toxicity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14636
