[Term]
id: goldbook:14639
name: environmental bioavailability
def: "Ratio of uptake clearance to the rate at which an organism encounters a given contaminant in an environmental medium \(e.g.\, soil\, sediment\, water\, food\) being processed by the organism."
comment: "This is a measure of an organism’s extraction efficiency, via respiratory, dietary, and surface absorption processes, from the environmentally available (bioaccessible) portion of a material."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
