[Term]
id: goldbook:14679
name: extrapolation
def: "Calculation\, based on quantitative observations in exposed test species or in vitro test systems\, of predicted dose–effect and dose–response relationships for a substance in the same species at other doses or in humans and other species at similar doses."
comment: "The term may also be used for qualitative information applied to species or conditions that are different from the ones in which the original investigations were carried out."
comment: "The term may be applied to predictions of such relationships in susceptible groups from knowledge of a group used for testing."
