def: "Passive diffusion down a gradient\, not requiring energy\, but occurring at a rate faster than expected by simple diffusion alone."
comment: "Facilitated diffusion may involve a membrane channel or a carrier molecule, often a protein. In the latter case, it may be referred to as facilitated transport. Both processes exhibit ligand specificity and saturation kinetics."
synonym: "facilitated transport" []
