[Term]
id: goldbook:14696
name: fluctuating asymmetry
def: "Deviation from perfect bilateral symmetry for a population of a bilaterally symmetrical species that is thought to reflect developmental instability."
comment: "A trait is measured from the right and left sides of each individual, and the variance in the difference (right–left) for the population is a measure of fluctuating asymmetry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14444
consider: goldbook:14590
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14697
name: fluid feeder
def: "Organism that feeds on the fluids of other animals or of plants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14698
name: food chain
def: "Hierarchical sequence of transfer of substances from prey organism to predator organism."
comment: "Interconnected food chains combine to form a food web in which most organisms consume or are consumed by more than one other type of organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14699
name: food-mass feeder
def: "Animal that feeds on the body parts of other animals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14700
name: fossil
def: "Mineralized or otherwise preserved remnant or trace \(such as a footprint\) of an animal\, plant\, and other organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14701
name: free ion activity model
def: "Model for acute metal toxicity to aquatic organisms based on the idea that toxicity occurs when the concentration of the free metal cation in solution reaches a certain level."
comment: "This model has been developed into the biotic ligand model."
synonym: "FIAM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14501

[Term]
id: goldbook:14702
name: Freundlich adsorption isotherm
def: "Empirical equation that describes the adsorption of a contaminant to soil. The equation is \\\[x/m = \(K_\{\\rm\{f\}\} C_\{\\rm\{e\}\}\) \\exp \(1/n\)\\\] where \\\(x/m\\\) is the mass ratio of concentrations of adsorbed substance at equilibrium divided by the concentration of the contaminant in soil\, \\\(C_\{\\rm\{e\}\}\\\) is the contaminant concentration in the aqueous phase at equilibrium\, \\\(K_\{\\rm\{f\}\}\\\) is the equilibrium constant \(the Freundlich adsorption constant\)\, and \\\(1/n\\\) is a contaminant specific exponent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14703
name: fulvic acid
def: "Humic substance that is soluble at all \\\(\\rm\{pH\}\\\)s."
comment: "Most of the humic substance in natural water is fulvic acid."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14746

[Term]
id: goldbook:14704
name: functional redundancy
def: "Apparently unaltered maintenance of community function despite changes in structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14705
name: functional response
def: "Change in some predator function\, such as prey consumption rate\, in response to changes in prey density."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14706
name: fundamental niche
def: "Environmental conditions under which a species can thrive."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14747
consider: goldbook:14877

[Term]
id: goldbook:14707
name: Gaia hypothesis
def: "Hypothesis proposed by James Lovelock that the Earth’s temperature\, albedo\, and surface chemistry are homeostatically regulated by the sum of all the biota of the Earth."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14708
name: gametic selection
def: "Natural selection resulting from differential success of gametes produced by heterozygotes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14709
name: gastrointestinal excretion
def: "Excretion through the intestinal mucosa by active or passive processes."
comment: "Some chemical species of metallic elements such as cadmium and mercury can experience significant levels of gastrointestinal excretion."
comment: "This may involve loss by normal cell sloughing of the intestine wall."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14710
name: general adaptation syndrome
def: "Specific syndrome associated with Selyean stress composed of three phases\: the alarm reaction\, adaptation or resistance\, and exhaustion; adaptation in all phases of the GAS results in restoration of homeostasis or reduced deviation from homeostasis."
synonym: "GAS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15025

[Term]
id: goldbook:14711
name: genetic adaptation
def: "Result of random genetic variation due to mutation and \(or\) to changes in allele frequencies\, causing variation in the survival and reproductive success of individuals and hence of groups of organisms\, with the consequence that those best adjusted to their environment flourish."
comment: "This process underlies the concept of natural selection leading to Darwinian evolution."
synonym: "adaptation" []
synonym: "evolutionary adaptation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14871

[Term]
id: goldbook:14712
name: genetic drift
def: "Evolutionary process of change in the allele frequencies in a population due to random changes in the frequency by which different alleles are transferred to the next generation."
comment: "In small populations, genetic drift may result in extinction of some alleles leading to evolutionary change over time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14713
name: genetic hitchhiking
def: "Situation in which a scored locus is acting only as a marker for a closely linked gene that is actually responsible for the difference in tolerance among genotypes. More generally\, it is the condition 'in which a given allele changes in frequency as a result of linkage or gametic phase disequilibrium with another selected locus'."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14714
name: genetic risk
def: "Risk to the progeny of an exposed individual of an adverse effect associated with heritable genetic damage\, e.g.\, damage to germ cells leading to a nonviable fetus or an offspring with a birth defect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14716
name: genus
def: "Low-level taxonomic rank used in the classification of living and fossil organisms."
comment: "Like almost all other taxonomic units, genera may sometimes be divided into subgenera, singular: subgenus. The largest main taxonomic unit below the genus is the species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14717
name: geographic information system
def: "Computerized system to handle spatial data at a reasonable cost; most allow one to archive\, organize\, integrate\, statistically analyze\, and display many kinds of spatial information using a common coordinate system."
synonym: "GIS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14718
name: global distillation
def: "Process by which persistent and relatively volatile organochlorine compounds are distilled from warmer regions of use to cooler regions of the globe."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14719
name: global fractionation
def: "Process by which some persistent organic pollutants \(POPs\) move more rapidly than others toward the polar regions. Because POPs differ in their individual rates of degradation\, vapor pressure\, and lipophilicity\, a fractionation occurs. The net result is a redistribution of the different POPs from the equator or site of origin toward the cold polar regions of the Earth."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14909

[Term]
id: goldbook:14720
name: global warming
def: "Heating up of the Earth’s climate thought to result from the increased atmospheric carbon dioxide \(\\\(\\ce\{CO2\}\\\)\) concentrations from fossil fuel burning\, release of other greenhouse gases\, and the worldwide destruction of forests."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14721
name: good laboratory practice principles
def: "Fundamental rules incorporated in Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development \(OECD\) guidelines and national regulations concerned with the process of effective organization and the conditions under which laboratory studies are properly planned\, performed\, monitored\, recorded\, and reported."
synonym: "GLP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "GLP principles" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14722
name: graded effect
def: "Consequence that can be measured on a graded scale of intensity or severity and its magnitude related directly to the dose or concentration of the substance producing it."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14965

[Term]
id: goldbook:14723
name: grasshopper effect
def: "Global distillation of persistent organic pollutants \(POPs\) involving seasonal cycling of temperatures such that movement toward the higher latitudes occurs in annual pulses."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14718
consider: goldbook:14909

[Term]
id: goldbook:14724
name: greenhouse gases
def: "Atmospheric gases that are relatively transparent to sunlight entering the atmosphere but absorb infrared radiation generated at the Earth’s surface. They include water vapor\, carbon dioxide \(\\\(\\ce\{CO2\}\\\)\)\, methane\, dinitrogen oxide \(nitrous oxide\)\, chlorofluorocarbons \(CFCs\)\, chloroethane \(methylchloroform\)\, carbon tetrachloride\, and the fire retardant\, halon. Ozone in the troposphere can also act as a greenhouse gas."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14725
name: growth
def: "Increase in size."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14672
consider: goldbook:14774
consider: goldbook:14811

[Term]
id: goldbook:14726
name: growth dilution
def: "Decrease in contaminant concentration in a growing organism because the amount of tissue in which the contaminant is distributed is increasing."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549

[Term]
id: goldbook:14727
name: guild
def: "Group of functionally similar species whose members interact strongly with one another but weakly with the remainder of the community."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14728
name: habitat
def: "Spatial area \(geographical area\) where a particular species population lives\, large enough to comprise a breeding population. Note\: A microhabitat or microenvironment is the immediate surroundings and other physical factors of an individual plant or animal within its habitat. Physical conditions that surround a species\, or species population\, or assemblage of species\, or community."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14729
name: hardness
def: "Concentration of all metallic cations\, except those of the alkali metals\, present in water."
comment: "In general, the concentration of calcium and magnesium ions in water, frequently expressed as \(\pu{mg L-1}\) calcium carbonate or equivalent, is used as a measure of hardness."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14730
name: hard water
def: "Water that contains mineral salts of divalent cations\, commonly calcium and magnesium and sometimes iron\(II\) \(ferrous\) ions\, principally as hydrogencarbonates\, chlorides\, and sulfates."
comment: "Hardness caused by calcium hydrogencarbonate is known as temporary, because boiling converts the hydrogencarbonate to calcium carbonate (\(\ce{CaCO3}\)), which has a very low solubility; hardness from the other salts is called permanent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14731
name: Hardy–Weinberg equilibrium
def: "State of a population if the frequencies of different alleles of all genes in the genome remain constant between generations."
comment: "The Hardy–Weinberg equilibrium is a very rare situation in natural populations. Deviation from the Hardy–Weinberg equilibrium is the basis for microevolution."
comment: "The Hardy–Weinberg equilibrium requires the following conditions: (1) the population is large ("infinite"), (2) mating is random, (3) there is no selection, (4) the net mutation rate is zero, and (5) there is no migration."
synonym: "genetic equilibrium" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14853
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14732
name: harm
def: "Adverse effect to an ecosystem\, community\, population\, species\, individual organism\, organ\, tissue\, or cell."
synonym: "damage" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14733
name: hazard assessment
def: "Determination of factors controlling the likely effects of a hazard such as the dose–effect and dose–response relationships\, variations in target susceptibility\, bioaccumulation potential\, persistence\, and mechanism of toxicity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14470
consider: goldbook:14600
consider: goldbook:14604
consider: goldbook:15085

[Term]
id: goldbook:14734
name: hazard evaluation
def: "Identification and assessment of the potential adverse effects that could result from manufacture\, use\, and disposal of a material in a specified quantity and manner."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14735
name: hazard identification
def: "Determination of substances of concern\, their adverse effects\, target populations\, and conditions of exposure\, taking into account toxicity data and knowledge of effects on human health\, other organisms\, and their environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14736
name: hazard index
def: "Sum of the hazard quotients for substances that affect the same target organ or organ system."
comment: "Ideally, hazard quotients should be combined for pollutants that cause adverse effects by the same mechanism. Aggregate exposures below an HI of \(\pu{1.0}\) are unlikely to result in adverse health effects over a lifetime of exposure. An HI greater than \(\pu{1.0}\) does not necessarily suggest a likelihood of adverse effects. The HI cannot be translated to a probability that adverse effects will occur, and is not likely to be proportional to risk."
synonym: "HI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14737

[Term]
id: goldbook:14737
name: hazard quotient
def: "Ratio of toxicant exposure \(estimated or measured\) to a reference value regarded as corresponding to a threshold of toxicity; often this is determined as the predicted environmental concentration \(PEC\) divided by the predicted no-effect concentration \(PNEC\)."
comment: "If the hazard quotient exceeds unity, the toxicant may produce an adverse effect, but normally this will require an HQ of several times unity; an HQ of less than one indicates that no adverse effects are likely over a lifetime of exposure."
synonym: "HQ" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14944
consider: goldbook:14945

[Term]
id: goldbook:14738
name: hazardous concentration
def: "Concentration of a substance producing a defined effect on \\\(\\pu\{\\textit\{p\} \\%\}\\\) \(usually \\\(\\pu\{5\\%\}\\\)\) of species of concern\, derived by means of a statistical extrapolation procedure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15052

[Term]
id: goldbook:14739
name: heavy metal
def: "Term used commonly but erroneously when referring to metal toxicity."
comment: "The term is deprecated as it has no generally agreed meaning and sometimes is even applied to nonmetals. It is a source of confusion to be avoided. The term "metal" is often adequate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14740
name: heterotherm
def: "Animal that partially regulates body temperature\, sometimes maintaining its body temperature at a certain level\, e.g.\, when active\, but at other times allowing it to fluctuate with the environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14741
name: heterotroph
def: "Organism obtaining organic food by eating other organisms or their excreta."
comment: "Animals, fungi, and most bacteria are heterotrophs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14742
name: heterotrophic succession
def: "Temporal sequential appearance of different heterotrophic species at a location\, most often decomposer organisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15077

[Term]
id: goldbook:14743
name: heterozygote advantage
def: "Greater Darwinian fitness \(reproductive output\) from heterozygous than from homozygous individuals of a species. This tends to preserve variation in the population gene pool."
synonym: "heterosis" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14744
name: homeostasis
def: "Totality of processes occurring in an open system or a closed system\, especially a living organism\, enabling it to regulate its internal environment to maintain stable\, constant conditions or the outcome of these processes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14745
name: hormesis
def: "Unexpected and unexplained but favorable biological response to low-level exposure to a substance or physical agent generally considered to be harmful."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14746
name: humic substances
def: "Nonvolatile organic anionic polyelectrolytes\, of biological origin\, in the molecular mass range \\\(\\pu\{500\\!\{-\}\\! 5000\}\\\)\, which have complex structures and are variable in composition."
comment: "Humic substances occur naturally as deposits on sediment and soil particles and constitute \(\pu{30\!{-}\! 50 \%}\) of the dissolved organic carbon (DOC) in natural waters. Humic substances are classified according to solubility and may contain humic acid, fulvic acid, and humin."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14595
consider: goldbook:14703
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14747
name: Hutchinsonian niche
def: "Intersection of ranges of tolerances for sets of resources utilized by organisms\, represented mathematically by a multidimensional hypervolume whose dimensions correspond to environmental variables. Any species is considered unimodally distributed\, i.e.\, confined to a habitat in the niche."
comment: "This niche concept is quantifiable and therefore particularly useful to ecologists. Hutchinson’s niche is the most accepted concept of the niche in use today. In practice, it is impossible to identify and quantify all the resources utilized by an organism. Thus, typically the limiting factors receive most attention."
comment: "Two aspects of the niche can be visualized: A realized niche for a species is the sum of niche dimensions unique to that particular species. A fundamental niche is the total sum of the species niche dimensions including parts shared with other species and parts unshared."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14706
consider: goldbook:14728
consider: goldbook:14877
consider: goldbook:14973

[Term]
id: goldbook:14748
name: hybrid
def: "Result of interbreeding between two animals or plants of different taxa.Note\: Hybrids between different species within the same genus are sometimes known as interspecific hybrids or crosses. Hybrids between different subspecies within a species are known as intra-specific hybrids. Hybrids between different genera are sometimes known as intergeneric hybrids. Cross-breed between populations\, breeds\, or cultivars within a single species.Note\: Hybridization is often used in plant and animal breeding to obtain desirable characteristics not found or inconsistently present in the parent individuals or populations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14716
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14749
name: hypoxemia
def: "Deficient oxygenation of the blood."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14750
name: hypoxic
def: "Dioxygen-deficient"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14751
name: incipient LC<sub>50</sub>
def: "Concentration of a chemical which is lethal to \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\) of the test organisms as a result of exposure for periods long enough for acute lethal action to cease; in other words\, the concentration below which \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\) of individuals will have a normal lifespan despite the previous exposure to a toxicant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14752
name: incremental unit risk estimate
def: "For an air pollutant\, the additional lifetime cancer risk occurring in a hypothetical population in which all individuals are exposed continuously from birth throughout their lifetimes to a concentration of \\\(\\pu\{1 \\upmu g m-3\}\\\) of the pollutant in the air they breathe."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14753
name: independent joint action
def: "Production of an effect by each toxicant in a given exposure that is independent of the others and occurs by a different mode of action."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14754
name: index of biological integrity
def: "Composite index combining 12 qualities of fish communities of warm-water\, low-gradient streams to determine the level of stream degradation."
comment: "This index has been modified and widely used in the United States."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14755
name: indicator species
def: "Species whose presence shows the occurrence of defined environmental conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14756
name: indigenous
def: "Native to a given region or ecosystem."
comment: ""Indigenous" is not synonymous with "endemic". In ecology, endemic means exclusively native to the biota of a specific place, whereas an indigenous species may occur in two or more different habitats."
comment: "The term is applied to a native species to distinguish it from species introduced as a result of human activity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14632
consider: goldbook:14728

[Term]
id: goldbook:14757
name: indirect ecological effect
def: "Effect resulting from imposed biotic or abiotic factors which alter ecosystem properties that in turn favor or disfavor an ecological component of importance \(e.g.\, a species\) and thus indirectly lead to improved or reduced fitness of that species. Result of imposed biotic or abiotic factors allowing indigenous or new species to dominate\, thereby affecting ecosystem composition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14756

[Term]
id: goldbook:14758
name: indirect photolysis
def: "Degradation of a contaminant through interaction with other molecules in solution that have absorbed light energy. This can occur through energy transfer or by chemical reaction with short-lived reactive species."
comment: "Dissolved humic and fulvic acids are good examples of photoactive compounds that can increase the degradation of contaminants through indirect photolysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549
consider: goldbook:14703

[Term]
id: goldbook:14759
name: indirect toxicity
def: "Adverse effects that result from agent\(s\) acting on and producing changes in the chemical\, physical\, and \(or\) biological environment external to the organisms under study \(e.g.\, decrease in food for predatory species due to direct toxicity from a chemical to prey may produce adverse effects in the predator species due to starvation rather than inducing any direct chemical toxicity in predator organisms\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14760
name: individual
def: "One whole organism."
comment: "Individuals have size, shape, and health or condition. They grow, reproduce, and die over time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14761
name: individual effective dose
def: "Concept forming the basis for most dose–response models\, which holds that there exists a smallest dose needed to kill any particular individual. The IED is a characteristic of an individual."
synonym: "IED" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14604

[Term]
id: goldbook:14762
name: industrial ecology
def: "Study of the flows of materials and energy in the industrial environment and the effects of these flows on natural systems."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14763
name: industrial melanism
def: "Gradual increase to predominance of melanic forms in populations from industrialized regions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14764
name: inertia
def: "Community’s ability to resist change."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14765
name: infauna
def: "Animals living in the sediment of aquatic systems but not on the surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14653

[Term]
id: goldbook:14766
name: initiating event
def: "Specific action that results in a risk being incurred."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14767
name: integrated risk information system
def: "USEPA database containing reference doses\, slope factors\, and drinking-water health advisories \(one-day\, ten-day\, longer-term\, and lifetime advisories\)\, and associated information."
synonym: "IRIS" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14768
name: interference competition
def: "Interspecies competition in which one species interferes with another\, as might occur with territoriality or aggressive behavior."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14769
name: interspecies competition
def: "Interference with or inhibition of one species by another."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14770
name: interspecific competition
def: "Competition by different species for the same \(limited\) resources."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14771
name: interspecific interaction
def: "Relations between different species in a community."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14772
name: interstitial water
def: "Water in sediment or soil that surrounds the solid particles. The amount of interstitial water is calculated and expressed as the percentage ratio of the mass of water in the sediment to the mass of the wet sediment."
synonym: "pore water" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14773
name: intraspecific competition
def: "Competition by individuals of the same species \(population\) for the same \(limited\) resources."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14774
name: intrinsic rate of growth
def: "\\\(r = \(\{\\rm\{natality\}\} + \{\\rm\{immigration\}\}\) - \(\{\\rm\{mortality\}\} + \{\\rm\{emigration\}\}\)\\\)"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14725

[Term]
id: goldbook:14775
name: intrinsic rate of increase
def: "Rate of increase in the size of a population growing under no constraints."
synonym: "Malthusian rate of increase" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14828
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14776
name: isobole approach
def: "Approach used to visualize or quantify joint action of chemical mixtures by plotting a graph \(isobologram\) of equally effective dose pairs \(isoboles\) for a single effect level. A particular effect level is selected\, such as \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\) of the maximum\, and doses of drugs \\\(\\ce\{A\}\\\) and \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\) \(each alone\) that give this effect are plotted as axial points in a Cartesian plot. The straight line connecting \\\(\\ce\{A\}\\\) and \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\) is the locus of points \(dose pairs\) that will produce this effect in a simply additive combination. This line of additivity allows a comparison with the actual dose pair that produces this effect level experimentally."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14777
name: isotopic discrimination
def: "The differential behavior of isotopes occurring if the rate or extent of participation in some biological or chemical process depends significantly on the mass of the isotope. Also called the isotope effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14778
name: iteroparous species
def: "Species that reproduces more than once."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14779
name: Kamofsky’s law
def: "Any agent will be teratogenic if it is present at concentrations or intensities producing cell toxicity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14780
name: keystone habitat
def: "High-quality habitat patch essential to maintaining the vitality of the metapopulation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14728
consider: goldbook:14850

[Term]
id: goldbook:14781
name: keystone species
def: "Species\, usually a top predator\, that influences the ecological community by its activity or role\, not its numerical dominance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14782
name: k-strategy
def: "Equilibrium strategy for species involving effective interactions with each other in the community\, allowing coexistence of many species. Equilibrium species are more effective competitors than opportunistic species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14783
name: larva
def: "Recently hatched insect\, fish\, or other organism that has different physical characteristics than those seen in the adult\, requiring metamorphosis to reach the adult body structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14784
name: law of frequence
def: "According to this 'law'\, there are comparatively many rare \(low abundance\) species\, and possibly comparatively many common \(high abundance\) species\, but relatively few in the middle \(of medium abundance\)."
comment: "Thus, if one collects data on species presence/absence in a set of quadrants, one tends to find a J-shaped pattern in the distribution of species frequencies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14785
name: leach
def: "With reference to a soluble chemical or mineral\, drain away from soil\, ash\, or similar material by the action of percolating liquid\, especially rainwater."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14786
name: leachate
def: "Water or waste-water that has percolated through a column of soil or solid waste in the environment\, carrying with it substances dissolved from the soil or waste."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14787
name: lentic
def: "Related to standing water riparian-wetland areas such as lakes\, ponds\, seeps\, bogs\, and meadows."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14997

[Term]
id: goldbook:14788
name: lentic water
def: "Nonflowing or still inland water; e.g.\, lakes\, ponds."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14789
name: Leslie matrix
def: "Square matrix used in population biology to predict population growth. The top row of the matrix is the fecundity for each age class of mothers\, and a subdiagonal is constructed from the number of individuals surviving from age class \\\(x\\\) to \\\(x + 1\\\). Multiplied by the population vector of the number of female offspring in each age class \\\(x\\\) at time \\\(t\\\)\, it predicts the age distribution of the population at the next time step \\\(t + 1\\\)\, corresponding to the age class interval \\\(x + 1\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14790
name: lethal
def: "Deadly; fatal; causing death."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14791
name: lethal body burden
def: "Total body uptake of a substance that is associated with mortality in short-term exposures."
synonym: "LBB" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14792
name: lethal time
def: "Time taken for a defined percentage\, usually \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\)\, of a test population to die."
comment: "The median lethal time (MLT) for \(\pu{50\%}\) of the test population is referred to as the \(\pu{MLT_{50}}\)."
synonym: "LT" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14625
consider: goldbook:14838
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14793
name: lethality
def: "Ability to cause death."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14794
name: Liebig's law of the minimum
def: "Observation that a population’s size \(number of individuals or biomass\) is limited by some essential factor in the environment that is scarce relative to the amount of other essential factors\, e.g.\, phosphorus-limited algal growth in a lake."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14795
name: life cycle
def: "Series of stages\, from a given point in one generation to the same point in next generation\, e.g.\, egglarva-adult-egg \(hyphenated when used as an adjective\, e.g.\, life-cycle strategy\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14796
consider: goldbook:14797

[Term]
id: goldbook:14796
name: life-cycle study
def: "Comprehensive study to determine the impact of a substance or mixture on the survival\, growth\, reproduction\, development\, or other important qualities at all stages of a species life cycle."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14797
name: life history
def: "Description of life-cycle events through which an organism passes\, with particular reference to those events that influence survival and reproduction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14795

[Term]
id: goldbook:14798
name: life table
def: "Statistical table that follows a hypothetical cohort of \\\(\\pu\{100000\}\\\) persons born at the same time as they progress through successive ages\, with the cohort reduced from one age to the next according to a set of death rates by age until all persons eventually die."
comment: "In ecology, fertility for each age class is normally included in the tables."
comment: "The life table is used mainly to indicate expectation of life at various ages. However, it also provides information on numbers of individuals who survive to various ages, median age at death, age-specific death rates, and the probability of dying at certain ages."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14430
consider: goldbook:14568
consider: goldbook:14610

[Term]
id: goldbook:14799
name: life-table response experiment
def: "Retrospective comparison of two or more populations in which the response variable is a life table or a complete set of stage-specific vital rates."
synonym: "LTRE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14800
name: limit value
def: "Limit concentration at or below which Member States of the European Community must set their environmental quality standard and emission standard for a particular substance according to Community Directives."
synonym: "LV" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14631
consider: goldbook:14645

[Term]
id: goldbook:14801
name: limited life-span paradigm
def: "Model based on the assumption that the maximum life span of an individual organism is an inherent\, genetically defined property of that organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14802
name: limnocorrals
def: "Artificial enclosures placed in the pelagic region of ponds\, lakes\, or marine environments. These systems vary in size from as little as \\\(\\pu\{2 L\}\\\) to over \\\(\\pu\{2.5E6 L\}\\\); however\, most of these systems have a volume between \\\(\\pu\{1000 L\}\\\) and \\\(\\pu\{E4 L\}\\\)."
comment: "These systems may or may not be in contact with the profundal region. Fish are generally excluded from these test systems."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14903

[Term]
id: goldbook:14803
name: limnology
def: "Study incorporating the study of all aspects of inland freshwater habitats including lakes\, ponds\, rivers\, streams\, swamps\, wetlands\, groundwaters\, and reservoirs that make up inland water systems"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14728

[Term]
id: goldbook:14804
name: linear free energy relationship
def: "An empirical relationship in which numerical parameters are associated with small perturbations in a parent molecule and are subsequently correlated with the change in the Gibbs energy of a certain reaction of the parent molecule vs. the perturbed molecules."
comment: "A classical example is the well-known Hammett equation, in which sigma (\(\upsigma\)) values are constructed for specific substituents on a benzoic acid parent molecule. The linear correlation is then between the (summed) sigma values for a set of compounds and the \(\pu{p}K_{\rm{a}}\) (free energy of acid dissociation) of those compounds."
synonym: "LFER" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14805
name: Litchfield method
def: "Simple\, semigraphical method for analyzing survival time data and estimating \\\(\\pu\{LT_\{50\}\}\\\) values."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14806
name: Litchfield–Wilcoxon method
def: "Semigraphical method for estimating a median lethal concentration \(\\\(\\pu\{LC_\{50\}\}\\\)\)\, median lethal dose \(\\\(\\pu\{LD_\{50\}\}\\\)\)\, or median effective concentration \(\\\(\\pu\{EC_\{50\}\}\\\)\). Although very easy to perform\, it is the most subjective method for such estimations because it involves fitting a line to data by eye."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14807
name: littoral
def: "Belonging to the shore of a lake\, river\, pond\, or especially the sea. Intertidal zone\, sometimes referring specifically to the shallow well-lit region along the shore."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14808
name: littoral enclosures
def: "Isolated shore regions of freshwater ponds separated from the main body of water by plastic dividers used for ecotoxicological testing. These test systems generally have a volume of \\\(\\pu\{1000 L\}\\\) to \\\(\\pu\{5E4 L\}\\\) and a maximum depth of \\\(\\pu\{2 m\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14809
name: loading
def: "Ratio of animal biomass to the volume of test solution in an exposure chamber."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14810
name: logistic curve
def: "Function\, often applied to growth curves\, fitting the general equation \\\[y = k/\(1 + e^\{a+bt\}\)\\\] where \\\(t\\\) represents time\, \\\(y\\\) the body weight or population size\, \\\(k\\\) the rate of growth\, and \\\(a\\\) and \\\(b \\gt 0\\\) are constants. In the logistic equation the percentage rate of increase decreases linearly as size increases. The resulting curve continually rises\, slowly at first\, more rapidly in the middle phase\, and slowly again near the end of growth."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14811
name: logistic growth
def: "Growth of a population under environmental constraints that set a maximum population size\, giving an S-shaped curve."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14514
consider: goldbook:14725
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14812
name: logit transformation
def: "In competitive binding assays\, the logit-log dose relationship\, in which the response is defined by \\\[R = \{\\rm\{logit\}\}\\\,\(y\) = \\ln \[y/\(1 - y\)\]\\\] where \\\(y = b/b_\{0\}\\\)\, \\\(b\\\) is fraction of tracer bound and \\\(b_\{0\}\\\) is the value of \\\(b\\\) with no unlabelled ligand in the system."
comment: "Logit-transformed assay data frequently yield straight-line dose-response data, amenable to statistical analysis. More generally in toxicology, the transformation is applied to dose-response data where \(b_{0}\) denotes the maximum response in the absence of a toxic substance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14813
name: log-normal transformation
def: "Transformation of data with a logarithmic function that results in a normal distribution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14814
name: Lorax incongruity
def: "Delusion of selfless motivation in environmental stewardship or advocacy."
comment: "The Lorax is a character in a popular children’s book by Dr. Seuss who "speaks for the trees, for the trees have no tongues"."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14815
name: loss of life expectancy
def: "Calculated estimate of loss in lifetime associated with a risk factor; it is estimated as the simple difference between life expectancy without the risk factor and life expectancy with the risk factor."
synonym: "LLE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14816
name: lotic
def: "Related to flowing continental waters\, such as rivers and streams."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14817
name: lotic mesocosms
def: "Streams of various sizes used to evaluate the effects of substances. Unlike lentic systems\, no standardized design has been developed for flowing-water test systems."
synonym: "lotic microcosms" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14787

[Term]
id: goldbook:14818
name: lotic water
def: "Flowing continental waters\, such as rivers and streams."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14819
name: lowest effective dose
def: "Lowest dose of a chemical inducing a specified effect in a specified fraction of exposed individuals."
synonym: "LED" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14820
name: lowest-observed-effect concentration
def: "Lowest concentration of a material used in an aquatic toxicity test that has a statistically significant adverse effect on the exposed population of test organisms compared with controls."
comment: "When derived from a life cycle or partial life cycle test, it is numerically the same as the upper limit of the maximum acceptable toxicant concentration (MATC). Also called lowest-observed-adverse-effect level (LOAEL)."
synonym: "LOEC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14832
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14821
name: l<i>x</i> life table or schedule
def: "Life table that summarizes mortality data for populations."
comment: ""\({\rm{l}}x\)" is the number of individuals in a cohort alive at age or stage class, \(x\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14822
name: l<i>x</i>m<i>x</i> life table
def: "Life table that summarizes both mortality and natality data for populations."
comment: ""\({\rm{l}}x\)" is the actual number or the proportion (as a decimal or percentage) of survivors at the beginning of age interval \(x\). Since several samples are often averaged together, the \({\rm{l}}x\) values may not always be whole numbers. "\({\rm{m}}x\)" is the number of female births to each age group of "mothers"; the number of eggs or young which are female (in a species with a 1:1 sex ratio, this is \({\rm{m}}x/2\) where \({\rm{m}}x\) is the total eggs or young produced per female at age \(x\)). Since, for most organisms, one male can fertilize a number of females, the size of the population is more dependent on the number of females present, and the calculations are usually done using only females."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14823
name: MacArthur–Wilson model
def: "Model of island colonization giving the mathematical relationship \\\[S\(t\) = S_\{\\rm\{EQ\}\}\(1 - e^\{-Gt\}\)\\\] where \\\(S\(t\)\\\) is the number of species present at time \\\(t\\\)\, \\\(S_\{\\rm\{EQ\}\}\\\) is the equilibrium number of species for the island\, and \\\(G\\\) is the rate constant for colonization of the island."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14824
name: macrocosm
def: "Large multi-species test system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14846
consider: goldbook:14852

[Term]
id: goldbook:14825
name: macronutrient
def: "Imprecise term referring to a nutrient required for survival\, or present in biological fluids or compartments at a level easily measured by existing analytical techniques."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14659

[Term]
id: goldbook:14826
name: macrophyte
def: "Aquatic plant large enough to be seen easily with the naked eye \(as distinct from phytoplankton and small algae\)."
comment: "The term "aquatic macrophyte" has no taxonomic significance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14827
name: male-mediated toxicity
def: "Disease or birth defects produced by a father’s exposure to a physical or chemical agent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14828
name: Malthusian theory
def: "Model\, developed by Thomas R. Malthus \(1766–1834\)\, implying that\, unchecked by environmental or social constraints\, human populations would double every 25 years\, regardless of the initial population size. Thus\, if \\\(X_\{i\}\\\) denotes the population size during time period \\\(i\\\) and \\\(r\\\) the population growth rate\, the Malthusian population model gives the relationship \\\[X\(I + 1\) = \(1 + r\)X_\{i\}\\\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14829
name: mass balance equation
def: "Equation that expresses the total mass of a chemical in terms of all the various forms and concentrations in different environmental compartments \(including biota\) in which it occurs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14830
name: maturity index
def: "Index for pollution based on the proportions of species in a soil nematode community that fall into various categories ranging from colonizers \(\\\(r\\mbox\{-\}\\rm\{strategists\}\\\)\) to persisters \(\\\(k\\mbox\{-\}\\rm\{strategists\}\\\)\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14782
consider: goldbook:15005
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14831
name: maulstick incongruity
def: "Assignment of ecological or biological significance of a contaminant’s effect based primarily on statements of statistical significance but contrary to biological probability."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14832
name: maximum acceptable toxicant concentration
def: "Geometric mean of the lowest exposure concentration that causes a statistically significant adverse effect \(lowest-observed-effect concentration\, LOEC\) and the highest exposure concentration where no effect is observed \(no-observed-effect concentration\, NOEC\) in a life-cycle \(full chronic\) or partial lifecycle \(partial chronic\) test."
comment: "Calculation of an MATC requires quantitative life-cycle toxicity data on the effects of a material on survival, growth, and reproduction."
synonym: "MATC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14820
consider: goldbook:14885

[Term]
id: goldbook:14833
name: maximum likelihood estimation
def: "Parametric method used to fit dose- or concentration-effect data to the log-normal\, log-logistic\, or other models."
comment: "Probit and logit approaches are most often applied with MLE methods."
synonym: "MLE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14953

[Term]
id: goldbook:14834
name: mean absorption time
def: "Mean time required for absorption of a drug or contaminant calculated as the difference in mean residence time \(MRT\) of the material introduced by the \(noninstantaneous\) route of interest and the MRT for the same material injected intravenously."
synonym: "MAT" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14835
name: mean generation time
def: "Average time interval required for a bacterial cell to divide or for the population to double under a defined set of conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14836
name: measurement endpoint
def: "Measurable response to a stressor \(e.g.\, fledglings produced per nest each year\) that is related to the valued qualities of the assessment endpoint \(e.g.\, reproductive success of bald eagles\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14837
name: median effective time
def: "For sublethal or ambiguously lethal effects\, the median time until \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\) of the exposed individuals respond."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14838
name: median inhibitory time
def: "Time required for a toxicant to inhibit a specified process in \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\) of a population under test conditions."
synonym: "inhibitory time (IT)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14625
consider: goldbook:14792
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14839
name: median time to death
def: "Median time resulting in death for \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\) of the exposed organisms."
synonym: "MTTD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14840
name: median tolerance limit
def: "Concentration of a substance in air\, water\, sediment\, or soil at which \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\) of the test organisms survive after a specified time of exposure. The \\\(\\pu\{TL_\{50\}\}\\\) \(equivalent to the \\\(\\pu\{TL_\{m\}\}\\\)\) is usually expressed as a time-dependent value \(e.g.\, \\\(\\pu\{24\\!\\mbox\{-\}h\}\\\) or \\\(\\pu\{96\\!\\mbox\{-\}h\}\\\) \\\(\\pu\{TL_\{50\}\}\\\); the estimated concentration at which \\\(\\pu\{50\\%\}\\\) of test organisms survive after \\\(\\pu\{24 h\}\\\) or \\\(\\pu\{96 h\}\\\) of exposure\)."
comment: "Unlike lethal concentration and lethal dose, the term "tolerance limit" is applicable in designating the level of any measurable lethal condition (e.g., extremes in \(\rm{pH}\), temperature, dissolved oxygen). \(\pu{TL_{m}}\) and \(\pu{TL_{50}}\) have been replaced by median lethal concentration (\(\pu{LC_{50}}\)) and median effective concentration (\(\pu{EC_{50}}\))."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14841
name: meiofauna
def: "Small benthic invertebrates living in interstices of soil or sediment or in aquatic systems."
comment: "The term loosely defines a group of organisms by their size, larger than microfauna but smaller than macrofauna. In practice, these are usually organisms that can pass through a \(\pu{1 mm}\) mesh but will be retained by a \(\pu{45 \upmu m}\) mesh, but the exact dimensions vary from researcher to researcher. Whether an organism will pass through a \(\pu{1\!\mbox{-}mm}\) mesh may depend upon whether it is alive or dead at the time of sorting."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14842
name: meiotic drive
def: "Any process that causes some alleles to be over-represented in the gametes which are formed during meiosis."
comment: "With normal Mendelian segregation at a genetic locus, on average half of an organism’s offspring inherit one of the alleles and the other half the other allele. This term refers to rare cases in which Mendel’s laws are broken, and one of the alleles is consistently found in more than half the offspring."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14843
name: melanic forms
def: "Individuals or subspecies with increased dark pigmentation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14844
name: melanism
def: "Increased black or nearly black pigmentation of skin\, feathers\, or hair of an organism\, resulting from \(increased\) synthesis of melanin."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14763

[Term]
id: goldbook:14845
name: Mendelism
def: "Fundamental principles of inheritance \(especially the laws of segregation and independent assortment and the existence of dominant and recessive characters\)\, propounded originally by Gregor Mendel \(1822–1884\) and forming the basis for the science of classical genetics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14846
name: mesocosm
def: "Enclosed and essentially self-sufficient \(but not necessarily isolated\) experimental environment or ecosystem that is on a larger scale than a laboratory microcosm."
comment: "A mesocosm is normally used outdoors or, in some manner, incorporated intimately with the ecosystem that it is designed to reflect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:14824
consider: goldbook:14852

[Term]
id: goldbook:14847
name: meta-analysis
def: "Process of using statistical methods to combine the results of different studies. In the biomedical sciences\, the systematic evaluation of a problem using information \(commonly in the form of statistical tables and other data\) from a number of independent studies."
comment: "A common application is the pooling of results from a number of small randomized controlled trials, none in itself large enough to demonstrate statistically significant differences, but capable of doing so in aggregate."
comment: "Meta-analysis has a qualitative component, i.e., application of predetermined quality criteria (e.g., completeness of data, absence of bias) and a quantitative component, i.e., integration of numerical information."
comment: "Meta-analysis includes overview and data pooling aspects, but implies more than either of these processes. Meta-analysis carries the risk of several biases reinforcing each other. Because of such problems inherent in the pooling of data from different studies, interpretation of the results of meta-analysis must be very cautious."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14848
name: metallothionein-like proteins
def: "Poorly characterized\, cysteine-rich metal-binding proteins or proteins not conforming precisely to the classic properties of metallothioneins."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14849
name: metameter
def: "Measurement or a transformation of a measurement used in the analysis of biological tests\, e.g.\, the probit metameter."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14850
name: metapopulation
def: "Set of local populations which interact via dispersing individuals among local populations; though not all local populations in a metapopulation need interact directly with every other local population."
comment: "A metapopulation is generally considered to consist of several distinct populations together with areas of suitable habitat which are currently unoccupied. Each population cycles in relative independence of the other populations and eventually goes extinct as a consequence of demographic stochasticity."
comment: "Individuals may immigrate to a small metapopulation and rescue that population from extinction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14572
consider: goldbook:14728
consider: goldbook:14932
consider: goldbook:14992

[Term]
id: goldbook:14851
name: method of multiple working hypotheses
def: "Method proposed to reduce precipitate explanation by considering all plausible hypotheses simultaneously in testing so that equal amounts of effort and attention are provided to each."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14852
name: microcosm
def: "Artificial multi-species test system that simulates major characteristics of the natural environment for the purposes of ecotoxicological effects and risk assessment; such systems are normally terrestrial or aquatic and may contain plants\, animals \(vertebrates and invertebrates\)\, and microorganisms."
comment: "The terms mesocosm and macrocosm are used to refer to larger and more complex systems than microcosms, but the distinction is often not clearly defined."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14824
consider: goldbook:14846

[Term]
id: goldbook:14853
name: microevolution
def: "Evolutionary change below the species level; a small change in the genetic make-up of a population from generation to generation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14854
name: microphyte
def: "Plant of microscopic size."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14855
name: Microtox® test
def: "Test involving luminescent marine bacteria of the Vibrio sp. \[e.g.\, V. \(Photobacterium\) phosphoreum\, V. fischeri\, V. harveyi\]. A decrease in bioluminescence is thought to reflect toxic action."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14856
name: mineral
def: "Naturally occurring substance\, usually crystalline\, which has a particular chemical composition and specific physical properties."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14857
name: minimum significant difference
def: "Difference between groups \(in tests with\, e.g.\, salmonid fish\, the difference in average weights or average mortality\) that would have to occur before it could be concluded that there was a significant difference between the groups."
comment: "The MSD is provided by Dunnett’s multiple range test."
synonym: "MSD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14858
name: minimal time to effect or response
def: "Minimum time required to get an effect or response. Regardless of the toxicant concentration\, the effect\, or response\, cannot occur any faster than this minimum time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14859
name: minimum viable population
def: "Smallest population size of a species allowing survival in the wild."
comment: "MVP is used in the fields of biology, ecology, and conservation biology/ecology."
comment: "More specifically, MVP is the smallest possible size at which a biological population can exist without facing extinction from natural disasters or demographic or environmental changes, or genetic drift."
synonym: "MVP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14860
name: mixing zone
def: "Area where an effluent discharge undergoes initial dilution and is extended to cover the secondary mixing in the ambient water body."
comment: "A mixing zone is an allocated impact zone where water quality criteria can be exceeded as long as acutely toxic conditions are prevented."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14861
name: model error
def: "Elements of uncertainty associated with the discrepancy between the model and the real world."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14862
name: monitoring test
def: "Test designed to be applied on a routine basis\, with some degree of control\, to ensure that the quality of an environmental compartment\, biological endpoint\, or effluent has not exceeded some prescribed criteria range. In a biomonitoring test\, organisms are used as 'sensors' to detect changes in the quality of water or effluent. A monitoring test implies generation of information\, on a continuous or other regular basis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14537

[Term]
id: goldbook:14863
name: Montreal protocol
def: "Officially the Protocol on Substances That Deplete the Ozone Layer\, a treaty signed on 16 September 1987\, in Montreal by 25 nations; there are now 168 subscribing nations. The protocol sets limits on the production of chlorofluorocarbons \(CFCs\)\, halons\, and related substances that release chlorine or bromine to the ozone layer of the atmosphere."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14523

[Term]
id: goldbook:14864
name: morphodynamics
def: "Study of the interaction and adjustment of the seafloor topography and fluid hydrodynamic processes\, seafloor morphologies\, and sequences of change dynamics involving the motion of sediment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14865
name: mortality
def: "Death rate\, the number of dead individuals per unit time."
comment: "Natality and mortality graphs together form a life table."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14514

[Term]
id: goldbook:14866
name: most-sensitive-species approach
def: "Ecotoxicological approach in which results for the most sensitive of all tested species are used as an indicator of the toxicant concentration below which the entire community is protected from adverse effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14867
name: moving average method
def: "Method of estimating \\\(\\pu\{LC_\{50\}\}\\\)\, \\\(\\pu\{EC_\{50\}\}\\\)\, or \\\(\\pu\{LD_\{50\}\}\\\). It can be implemented with straightforward equations if the toxicant concentrations are set in a geometric series and there are equal numbers of individuals exposed in each treatment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14868
name: multiple heterosis
def: "Higher fitness of an individual as a composite or summed effect of heterozygote superiority \(heterosis\) at each of a series of loci."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14869
name: mutualism
def: "Interaction between two or more species\, giving fitness benefit to all the involved species\, e.g.\, increased carrying capacity."
comment: "Similar interactions within one species are called cooperation."
comment: "Symbiosis is the form of mutualism leading to the closest spatial or physical association. The process may be obligate, meaning the involved species cannot survive alone. Examples include cleaner fish, pollination and seed dispersal, gut flora, and nitrogen fixation by fungi."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14514

[Term]
id: goldbook:14870
name: National Academy of Sciences paradigm of risk assessment
def: "Model for risk assessment with four components—hazard identification\, exposure assessment\, dose–response assessment\, and risk characterization."
comment: "This model is used for both human and ecological risk assessments."
synonym: "NAS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "NAS paradigm of risk assessment" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14673
consider: goldbook:14735

[Term]
id: goldbook:14871
name: natural selection
def: "Evolutionary theory\, originally proposed by Darwin\, of the preferential survival and reproduction of organisms better adapted to their environment as a result of genetic adaptation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14711

[Term]
id: goldbook:14872
name: natural radiation background
def: "Cosmic radiation emitted from stars and long-lived terrestrial radionuclides that are ubiquitously present in the Earth’s soils."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14873
name: nekton
def: "Aggregate of actively swimming animals in a body of water ranging from microscopic organisms to whales."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14874
name: neo-Darwinism
def: "Theory of biological evolution \(widely accepted since the 1920s\) based on Darwin’s theory of natural selection but incorporating the theories of later biologists regarding genes\, inheritance\, and mutation\, particularly those of Weismann and Mendel."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14845
consider: goldbook:15134

[Term]
id: goldbook:14875
name: neophyte
def: "Plant found newly in an area where it had not been recorded previously."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14876
name: net reproductive rate
def: "Expected number of females to be produced during the lifetime of a newborn female as estimated with a life table."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14877
name: niche
def: "Group of conditions and resources\, facilitating but limiting survival\, growth\, and reproduction of a defined group of organisms or species."
comment: "The abiotic or physical environment is part of the niche because it influences how populations affect, and are affected by, resources and enemies."
comment: "The niche influences how a population responds to the abundance of its resources and enemies."
comment: "The niche is influenced by its inhabiting populations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14539
consider: goldbook:14706
consider: goldbook:14747
consider: goldbook:14878
consider: goldbook:14932
consider: goldbook:14973

[Term]
id: goldbook:14878
name: niche preemption
def: "Rapid use and preemption of resources by a species that exploits them to the exclusion or severe disadvantage of another species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14877

[Term]
id: goldbook:14879
name: niche width
def: "Term referring to the area which a species could physically inhabit."
comment: "This area is defined by suitable climate and available food sources appropriate to that species as well as other factors such as temperature and air or water pressure levels. The niche width often differs from the realized niche."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14973

[Term]
id: goldbook:14880
name: not in my backyard principle
def: "Public acceptance of necessary provisions \(e.g.\, waste incinerators\) provided they do not affect the individual’s quality of life."
synonym: "NIMBY" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "NIMBY principle" []
