consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14894
name: oligotrophy
def: "State of being oligotrophic. Obligate or facultative capacity to live in low-nutrient habitats."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14666
consider: goldbook:14728

[Term]
id: goldbook:14895
name: optimal-foraging theory
def: "Theory that the ideal forager will obtain a maximum net rate of energy gain by optimally allocating its time and energy to the various components of foraging."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14896
name: optimal stress response
def: "Optimal stress response involves a shift in the balance in energy allocation between somatic growth rate and longevity \(survival\) to optimize Darwinian fitness under stressful conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14897
name: ozone layer
def: "Part of the Earth’s atmosphere\, mainly located in the lower portion of the stratosphere\, approximately \\\(\\pu\{15\\!-\\! 35 km\}\\\) above the Earth's surface\, containing relatively high concentrations \(a few micromoles per litre\) of ozone \(\\\(\\ce\{O3\}\\\)\) which is higher than concentrations in the lower atmosphere. The thickness varies seasonally and geographically."
synonym: "ozonosphere" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14898
name: palaeontology
def: "Branch of science that deals with extinct and fossil humans\, animals\, and plants\, or more generally with evidence of organic life during the geological past."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14899
name: paradigm
def: "Model or template. Body of concepts that\, in a particular branch of science\, has withstood rigorous testing\, and is generally accepted by scientists working in that field as offering true explanations of fact and observation.Note\: This usage is derived from the work of the philosopher T. S. Kuhn \(1922–1996\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14900
name: partial kill
def: "Treatment in a toxicity test in which some\, but not all\, exposed individuals are killed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14901
name: pathway
def: "Sequence of enzymatic or other reactions by which one biological material is converted to another."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14902
name: pedosphere
def: "Part of the Earth made up of soils and where important soil processes are occurring."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
