[Term]
id: goldbook:14914
name: phylogeny
def: "Pattern of historical relationships between species or other groups resulting from divergence during evolution."
comment: "Palaeontology is important for understanding phylogeny. Without the fossils of the many groups of organisms now extinct, it could not be understood how present life forms are interrelated."
comment: "Phylogenetic relationships are shown in diagrams (cladograms, phylogenetic trees, evolutionary trees)."
comment: "Phylogenetics, the science of phylogeny, is part of the larger field of systematics, also including taxonomy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
