[Term]
id: goldbook:14920
name: Pielou’s <i>J</i>
def: "Measure of species evenness for a sample from a community. It is calculated from the following equation\: \\\[\{\\rm\{Pielouߴs\}\}\\ J = \\frac\{H'\}\{\\log S\}\\\] where \\\(H'\\\) is the Shannon–Wiener diversity measure and \\\(S\\\) is the average species richness."
