[Term]
id: goldbook:14927
name: point source
def: "Single emission source in a defined location."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14928
name: pollutant
def: "Any undesirable solid\, liquid\, or gaseous matter occurring\, as a result of human activities\, in a solid\, liquid\, or gaseous environmental medium and causing adverse effects."
comment: ""Undesirability", like toxicity, is concentration-dependent, low concentrations of most substances being tolerable or even essential in many cases."
comment: "A primary pollutant is one emitted into the atmosphere, water, sediments, or soil from an identifiable source."
comment: "A secondary pollutant is a pollutant formed by chemical reaction in the atmosphere, water, sediments, or soil."
comment: "Pollutant should be distinguished from contaminant; the latter implies presence above background due to human activities; the former implies that the substance also is causing adverse effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14929
name: pollution-induced community tolerance
def: "Increase in tolerance to pollution resulting from species composition shifts in the community\, acclimatization of individuals\, and genetic changes in populations in the community."
synonym: "PICT" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14418
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14930
name: pollution tolerance index
def: "Means of measuring environmental quality\, usually water quality\, by determining the presence of indicator species\, classified into three groups—sensitive\, facultative\, and tolerant. Each group is assigned an index value 1\, 2\, and 3\, with the sensitive group having the highest index value. The number of species present from the list included in each group is identified in a representative environmental sample and the group index multiplied by the number of species in the group. The scores for each group are finally added to give the PTI for the environmental medium under consideration. The environmental quality is directly proportional to the value of the index."
synonym: "PTI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14931
name: polygenic control
def: "Control of a phenotypic trait by several genes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14932
name: population
def: "In ecology\, any group of interacting and interbreeding organisms of the same species occupying a given area at the same time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14933
name: population biomass
def: "Total mass or weight of organisms in a population\, given by the sum of the masses \(or weights\) of all the individual members of the population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
