[Term]
id: goldbook:14946
name: predictive risk assessment
def: "Risk assessment performed for a proposed future action\, such as the use of a new chemical or the release of a new effluent."
synonym: "prospective risk assessment" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14947
name: prevalence
def: "Number of instances of existing cases of a given disease or other condition in a given population at a designated time; sometimes used to mean prevalence rate."
comment: "When used without qualification, refers usually to the situation at a specified time (point prevalence)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932
consider: goldbook:14948

[Term]
id: goldbook:14948
name: prevalence rate
def: "Total number of individuals who have an attribute or disease at a particular time \(or during a particular period\) divided by the population at risk of having the attribute or disease at this point in time or midway through the period."
synonym: "prevalence ratio" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14949
name: primary lamellae
def: "Gill structures extending outward at right angles from the branchial arches."
synonym: "filaments" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14950
name: primary producer
def: "Organism capable of using the energy derived from light or a chemical substance in order to manufacture energy-rich organic compounds."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14951
name: primary succession
def: "Sequential colonization by species which begin to colonize the bare ground and modify the environmental conditions after a region is completely denuded; e.g.\, behind a retreating glacier\, early colonizing organisms provide the soils needed by succeeding organisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15036
consider: goldbook:15077

[Term]
id: goldbook:14952
name: principle of allocation
def: "Concept that there exists a cost or trade-off to every allocation of energy resources. Energy spent by an individual organism on one function\, process\, or structure cannot be spent on another. Optimal allocation of resources enhances Darwinian fitness."
synonym: "concept of strategy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14953
name: probit
def: "Probability unit obtained by adding 5 to the normal deviates of a standardized normal distribution of results from a dose-response study."
comment: "A plot of probit against the logarithm of dose or concentration gives a linear plot if the response follows a logarithmic normal distribution. Estimates of the \(\pu{LD_{50}}\) and \(\pu{ED_{50}}\)) (or \(\pu{LC_{50}}\) and \(\pu{EC_{50}}\)) can be obtained from this plot."
comment: "Addition of 5 removes the complication of handling negative values."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14954

[Term]
id: goldbook:14954
name: probit log transform
def: "Probability unit obtained from the standardized normal distribution plotted against the logarithm of the concentration or dose of a substance when a quantal or graded response has been measured. A linear plot provides evidence that the distribution is log-normal. Estimates of the \\\(\\pu\{L\(E\)C_\{50\}\}\\\) and \\\(\\pu\{L\(E\)D_\{50\}\}\\\)\, as well as the standard deviation for the distribution\, can then be made."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14722
consider: goldbook:14965

[Term]
id: goldbook:14955
name: problem formulation
def: "Planning and scoping phase that establishes the framework around which the risk assessment is done."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14956
name: product-limit method
def: "Nonparametric method for analyzing time-to-death or survival-time data that does not require a specific model for the survival curve."
synonym: "Kaplan–Meier method" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14957
name: proliferation
def: "Multiplication\, i.e.\, an increase by frequent and repeated reproduction or growth by cell division."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14958
name: propagule
def: "Portion of a plant\, fungus\, etc.\, that is capable\, when detached\, of giving rise to a new individual by asexual reproduction \(e.g.\, a cutting\, leaf bud\, bulbil\, seed\, or spore\). Less commonly\, any of the products of asexual reproduction in certain invertebrates."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14959
name: propagule rain
def: "Relative to metapopulation dynamics\, the presence of a seed bank or dormant stage for a species that continually introduces individuals to the patch regardless of the density of occupancy in the surrounding patches. This propagule rain increases the likelihood of population reappearance and decreases the likelihood of patch extinction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14850
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14960
name: Ptolemaic incongruity
def: "False assertion that any particular level of biological organization holds a more central or important role than any other in the science of ecotoxicology."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14961
name: pyrogenic
def: "Describing anything that causes fire. Describing products of fire; e.g.\, organic compounds produced by the high-temperature combustion of complex organic substances are pyrogenic compounds.Examples\: Polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons \(PAHs\) are examples of pyrogenic compounds. Describing a substance that produces fever."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14962
name: quality criteria
def: "Quality guidelines based on the evaluation of scientific data."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14963

[Term]
id: goldbook:14963
name: quality guidelines
def: "Numerical limits or text statements established to support and maintain designated uses of the environment or to protect human health."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14964
name: quality standards
def: "Fixed upper limits for exposure to certain chemicals recognized under law by one or more levels of government. Well-known examples include the air\, water\, and soil quality standards\, as well as threshold limit values for air pollutants in the workplace."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14928
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14965
name: quantal effect
def: "Condition that can be expressed only as 'occurring' or 'not occurring'\, such as death or occurrence of a tumor."
synonym: "all-or-none effect" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14722

[Term]
id: goldbook:14966
name: quantitative structure–metabolism relationship
def: "Quantitative association between the physicochemical and \(or\) the structural properties of a substance and its metabolic behavior."
synonym: "QSMR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14967
name: quotient method
def: "Calculation of the quotient of the measured or predicted environmental concentration \(PEC\) of a contaminant and the predicted no-effect level \(PNEC\)\, used as an expression of hazard or risk. Higher quotients constitute greater evidence of a hazard or a greater risk."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549
consider: goldbook:14737
consider: goldbook:14944
consider: goldbook:14945

[Term]
id: goldbook:14968
name: rain-out
def: "Removal of pollutants from air by incorporation into developing rain droplets of rain clouds."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14928

[Term]
id: goldbook:14969
name: rarefaction estimate of richness
def: "Estimate of species richness \(\\\(S\\\)\) expressed relative to that of a sample having a standard number of individuals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15051

[Term]
id: goldbook:14970
name: rate constant-based model
def: "Compartment model that employs rate constants to quantify the rate of change in concentration or amount of toxicant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14537

[Term]
id: goldbook:14971
name: rate-of-living theory of aging
def: "Theory that the total metabolic expenditure of a genotype is generally fixed\, and longevity depends on the rate of energy expenditure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14972
name: rate ratio
def: "Value obtained by dividing the rate in an exposed population by the rate in an unexposed population."
synonym: "RR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14973
name: realised niche
def: "Portion of a species’ fundamental niche that it actually occupies."
comment: "The realized niche is narrower than the fundamental niche due to pressure from, and interactions with, other organisms (e.g., superior competitors)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14747
consider: goldbook:14877

[Term]
id: goldbook:14974
name: reasonable worst case
def: "Semiquantitative term referring to the lower portion of the high end of the exposure\, dose\, or risk distribution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14975
name: reasonable maximum exposure
def: "Highest exposure that is reasonably expected to occur."
comment: "Typically, the \(\pu{95\%}\) upper confidence limit of the toxicant distribution is used: if only a few data points (\(\pu{6\!{-}\! 10}\)) are available, the maximum detected concentration is used."
synonym: "RME" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14976
name: receiving water
def: "Surface water \(e.g.\, in a stream\, river\, or lake\) that has received\, or is about to receive\, a discharged waste \(i.e.\, the surface water immediately around the discharge point\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14977
name: recommended limit
def: "Maximum concentration of a potentially toxic substance that is expected to be safe."
comment: "Such limits are rarely defined as legal limits to be enforced. They are analogous to guidelines, which have only advisory status."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14978
name: reconstituted water
def: "De-ionized or glass-distilled water to which reagent-grade chemicals have been added. The resultant synthetic freshwater is expected to be free from contaminants and have the desired \\\(\\rm\{pH\}\\\) and hardness characteristics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549

[Term]
id: goldbook:14979
name: redundancy hypothesis
def: "Hypothesis that many species are redundant\, and their loss will not influence the community function as long as crucial \(e.g.\, keystone and dominant\) species populations are maintained."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14980
name: reference environment
def: "Generalized description of the environment into which contaminants will be released and in which organisms will be exposed. Reference environments are used when there is no specific site at risk."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549

[Term]
id: goldbook:14981
name: reference sediment
def: "Whole sediment near an area of concern used to assess sediment conditions in the absence of substances of concern."
comment: "Such sediment is collected near a site of concern and should represent the background conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14982
name: reference site
def: "Relatively unpolluted site used for comparison with polluted sites in environmental monitoring studies\, often incorrectly referred to as a control site."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14983
name: reference toxicant
def: "Chemical used in an aquatic toxicity test as a positive control in contrast to the negative control provided by exposure water without the test chemical. Information collected is used to determine the general health and viability of the test organisms and assess consistency in testing protocol implementation."
comment: "In this definition, the term "positive control" is used to describe a procedure that is very similar to the actual experimental test and that is known from previous experience to give a positive result."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14984
name: reference toxicity test
def: "Test conducted in conjunction with sediment tests to determine possible changes in condition of the test species."
comment: "Deviations from an established normal range indicate a change in the condition of the test organism population. Reference toxicant tests are most often acute lethality tests performed in the absence of sediment."
comment: "Sediment spiked with a toxicant might also be included as a positive control for the sediment toxicity test."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14985
name: region
def: "Area of the Earth’s surface differentiated by its specific characteristics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14986
name: relative risk
def: "Ratio of the risk of disease or death among the exposed to the risk among the unexposed. Ratio of the cumulative incidence rate in the exposed to the cumulative incidence rate in the unexposed."
synonym: "RR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "risk ratio" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14987
name: remedial investigation
def: "Study that has three parts\: characterization or the type and degree of the contamination\, human risk assessment\, and ecological risk assessment."
synonym: "RI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14988
name: remedial investigation and feasibility study
def: "For an EPA Superfund site\, a study that has as its goal the implementation of 'remedies that reduce\, control\, or eliminate risks to human health and the environment' or\, more specifically\, the accumulation of 'information sufficient to support an informed risk management decision regarding which remedy appears to be most appropriate for a given site'."
synonym: "RI/FS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14989
name: remediation
def: "Giving a remedy. Removal of pollution or contaminants from environmental media such as soil\, groundwater\, sediment\, or surface water for the general protection of human health and the environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14990
name: remote sensing
def: "Technologies that allow the acquisition and analysis of data without requiring physical contact with the land or water surface being studied. Most determine qualities or characteristics of areas of interest based on measurements of visible light\, infrared radiation\, or radio energy coming from them."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14991
name: reproductive value
def: "Expected contribution of offspring during the life of an individual of an age class \\\(x\\\) in a life table."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14798

[Term]
id: goldbook:14992
name: rescue effect
def: "Increased probability of a vacated-patch reoccupation in a metapopulation as the number of nearby\, occupied patches increases."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14850

[Term]
id: goldbook:14993
name: resilience
def: "Ability of a community to maintain its structure and function in the face of disturbance\, and to reorganize following disturbance-driven change."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:14994
name: retention effect
def: "Observed effect of the properties of persistent organic pollutants \(POPs\) with high lipophilicity which causes them to be bound more firmly than less lipophilic POPs in solid phases such as soil and vegetation; consequently\, they spend less time in the atmosphere and are less available for transport in that medium."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14909
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:14995
name: retrospective risk assessment
def: "Risk assessment dealing with an existing condition."
synonym: "retroactive risk assessment" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14996
name: ring test
def: "Part of an external quality assurance program for assessment of an analytical method or test. A reference institute sends identical samples\, which have to be analyzed or tested for specified parameters\, to a number of different laboratories. The laboratory has a deadline before which to provide results. Statistical evaluation and interpretation of the results permits assessment of the reliability of the methods used and a comparison of the laboratories’ proficiency."
comment: "For accreditation of laboratories, regular participation in ring tests is obligatory, but accreditation is not essential for participation in the tests."
synonym: "round-robin test" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14997
name: riparian
def: "Interface between land and a flowing body of surface water."
comment: "Plant communities along river margins are called riparian vegetation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:14998
name: risk analysis
def: "Process for controlling situations where an organism\, system\, or subpopulation could be exposed to a hazard."
comment: "The risk analysis process consists of three components: risk assessment, risk management, and risk communication."
comment: "The term is misleading since "analysis" has the fundamental meaning "resolution or breaking up of anything complex into its various simple elements, the opposite process to synthesis; the exact determination of the elements or components of anything complex (with or without their physical separation)". The usage defined here originates with the WHO Joint Expert Committee on Food Additives and has been accepted in this context in spite of objections from terminologists."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:14999
name: risk characterisation
def: "Outcome of hazard identification and risk estimation applied to a specific use of a substance or occurrence of an environmental health hazard."
comment: "Risk characterization requires quantitative data on the exposure of organisms or people at risk in the specific situation. The end product is a quantitative statement about the proportion of organisms or people affected in a target population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14735
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15000
name: risk hypotheses
def: "Clear statements of postulated or predicted adverse effects of a toxicant on an assessment endpoint."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14451

[Term]
id: goldbook:15001
name: risk source
def: "Agent\, medium\, process\, procedure\, or site with the potential to cause an adverse effect or effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15002
name: risk quotient
def: "Ratio of predicted exposure concentration \(PEC\) to predicted no-effect concentration \(PNEC\)."
comment: "The higher this value is above one, the greater the risk. If the value is below one, there should be no risk as a result of the predicted exposure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14944
consider: goldbook:14945

[Term]
id: goldbook:15003
name: risk reduction
def: "Taking measures to protect humans or the environment against identified risks."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15004
name: rivet popper hypothesis
def: "Hypothesis that each species in a community contributes to its proper functioning."
comment: "Derived from the metaphor that the species can be compared to rivets that hold an airplane together, and the loss of each rivet weakens the structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:15005
name: r-strategy
def: "Opportunistic strategy favoring species that establish themselves quickly\, grow quickly to exploit as many resources as possible\, and produce many offspring."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15006
name: rules of practical causal inference
def: "Fox’s rules of practical causal inference that are used in ecotoxicology \(environmental epidemiology\) to infer causality for toxicant exposure/effect scenarios."
comment: "The rules apply the following criteria for objectively evaluating the relationship between a suspect cause and a chronic effect: (1) probability, (2) time order, (3) strength of association, (4) specificity, (5) consistency on replication, (6) predictive performance, and (7) coherence."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15007
name: run-off
def: "Portion of the wet precipitation on the land that ultimately reaches streams and\, eventually\, the sea."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15008
name: safe concentration
def: "Concentration of a substance to which prolonged exposure will cause no adverse effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15009
name: salinity
def: "Mass of dissolved salts in seawater\, brackish water\, brine\, or other saline solution divided by the mass of the solution."
comment: "Before 1978, the usual unit for \(S\) expressed as a mass fraction was permil (no longer recommended), now usually in units \(\pu{g kg-1}\) or expressed as \(\pu{g kg-1}\) without the units given explicitly."
comment: "In oceanography, where precise and reproducible determination of seawater density is of interest, practical salinity, \(S\), is defined in terms of the ratio \(k_{15}\) of the electrical conductivity of the seawater sample at \(\pu{15^{\circ}C}\) and \(\pu{1 atm}\) (\(\pu{1.01325 kPa}\)) to that of a potassium chloride (\(\ce{KCl}\)) solution, in which the mass fraction of \(\ce{KCl}\) is \(\pu{32.4536E-3}\) at the same temperature and pressure."
comment: "In practice, this quantity cannot be measured directly in seawater or other natural waters because of the difficulty of drying the salts from these waters. Salinity is usually calculated from another property (e.g., chlorinity, electrical conductivity) whose relationship to salinity is well known."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14522

[Term]
id: goldbook:15010
name: salt tolerance index
def: "Quotient calculated as total plant \(shoot + root\) dry mass at different salt concentrations compared to the total plant dry mass obtained for the controls\, as indicated below\: \\\[S_\{\\rm\{T\}\} = m_\{\\rm\{d\}\}\(\{\\rm\{x\}\}\)/m_\{\\rm\{d\}\}\(\{\\rm\{i\}\}\)\\\] where \\\(m_\{\\rm\{d\}\}\\\) is the total dry mass\, and \\\(x\\\)\, \\\(i\\\) refer to a control treatment and a defined salt treatment\, respectively."
synonym: "STI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15011
name: saprobic
def: "Living in or being an environment rich in organic matter but lacking oxygen."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15012
name: saprobic index
def: "Means of classifying the saprobic state of running waters\, covering the full range from unpolluted to extremely polluted waters."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15011

[Term]
id: goldbook:15013
name: saprobic water classification
def: "Biological classification of water quality according to five categories\: oligosaprobic\: clear\, with no or only slight pollution and high dissolved oxygen \(DO\) content; p-mesosaprobic\: moderately polluted with still high DO content; x-mesosaprobic\: polluted with not very high DO content; polysaprobic\: strongly polluted\, with negligible DO content; and antisaprobic\: so polluted that no living organism is capable of living in the water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15014
name: saprobien spectrum
def: "Characteristic change in community composition at different distances below the discharge of putrescible organic waste to a river or stream."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:15015
name: satellite groups
def: "Organisms or groups of organisms treated in a similar fashion to those in standard toxicity tests for the purpose of special additional studies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15016
name: scope for growth
def: "Index \(\\\(P\\\) = production\) calculated as the amount of energy taken into the organism in its food \(\\\(A\\\)\) minus the energy used for respiration \(\\\(R\\\)\) and excretion \(\\\(U\\\)\)\: \\\[P = A - R - U\\\]"
comment: "It is an indicator of the amount of energy available for growth or production of offspring."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15017
name: scope of activity
def: "Difference between the rates of oxygen consumption of an organism under maximal and minimal activity levels."
comment: "It reflects the respiratory capacity available for the diverse demands on and activities of an organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15018
name: screening level
def: "Decision limit or cut-off point at which a screening test is regarded as positive."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15019
name: screening test
def: "Test conducted to estimate the concentrations to be used for a definitive test. Acute test used early in a testing program to evaluate the potential of a substance to produce a given adverse effect \(e.g.\, mortality\)."
synonym: "preliminary test" []
synonym: "range-finding test" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14865

[Term]
id: goldbook:15020
name: secondary lamellae
def: "Parallel rows of projections on the dorsal and ventral sides of each primary lamella of the fish gill. They are the primary sites of gas exchange of the gills."
synonym: "respiratory lamellae" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15021
name: secondary poisoning
def: "Poisoning of a predator as a result of eating prey that has accumulated a toxicant as a result of biomagnification through its food chain."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14484

[Term]
id: goldbook:15022
name: secondary substrate metabolism
def: "Microbial growth on a nutrient substrate while transforming another substrate without gaining energetic benefit."
comment: "Although it must occur, secondary substance metabolism is very difficult to demonstrate in nature, but it can be demonstrated in pure cultures."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14530

[Term]
id: goldbook:15023
name: secondary succession
def: "Sequential appearance of species following major changes to an established ecosystem."
comment: "Catastrophic weather events, fire, or human activities all disturb the environment. After such an event on land, well-developed soil remains, giving pioneer species an easy foothold; similar changes occur in abandoned agricultural areas."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619
consider: goldbook:15036
consider: goldbook:15077

[Term]
id: goldbook:15024
name: selection components
def: "Components of the life cycle of an individual upon which natural selection can act. They are viability selection\, sexual selection\, meiotic drive\, gametic selection\, and fecundity selection."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14708
consider: goldbook:14842
consider: goldbook:15030
consider: goldbook:15124

[Term]
id: goldbook:15025
name: Selyean stress
def: "Syndrome named for Hans Selye \(1907–1982\) that consists of all the nonspecifically induced changes within a biological system following and during environmental stress."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15026
name: semelparous species
def: "Species that reproduces once."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15027
name: semi-continuous activated sludge test
def: "Test for inherent biodegradability of organic substances in activated sludge by measurement of the decrease in dissolved oxygen content \(DOC\) in the test system."
synonym: "SCAS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "SCAS test" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14596

[Term]
id: goldbook:15028
name: sentinel species
def: "Feral\, caged\, or endemic species used in measuring and indicating the level of contamination or effect during a biomonitoring exercise."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15029
name: seston
def: "Minute living organisms and particles of nonliving matter that float in water and contribute to turbidity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15030
name: sexual selection
def: "Natural selection involving differential mating success of individuals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15031
name: Shannon–Wiener diversity index
def: "Index based on the assumption that all species are represented in the sample studied and that the sample was obtained randomly\, giving the following mathematical relationship\: \\\[H = -\\sum \\limits_\{i=1\}^S p_\{i\} \\log p_\{i\}\\\] where \\\(p_\{i\}\\\) is the fraction of individuals belonging to the \\\(i\\\)-th species and \\\(S\\\) is the number of species."
comment: "The Shannon index is affected by both the number of species and their equitability, or evenness. Both a greater number of species and a more even distribution increase diversity as measured by \(H\)."
comment: "The most important source of error in this index is failure of sampling to include all species from the community of interest."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14599

[Term]
id: goldbook:15032
name: Shelford’s law of tolerance
def: "Species’ tolerance\(s\) along an environmental gradient \(or series of environmental gradients\) will determine its population distribution and size in the environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15033
name: silt
def: "Sediment particles with a grain size between \\\(\\pu\{0.004 mm\}\\\) and \\\(\\pu\{0.062 mm\}\\\)\, i.e.\, coarser than clay particles but finer than sand."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15034
name: Simpson’s diversity index
def: "Dominance index weighted toward the abundance of the most common species\, giving the probability of any two individuals drawn at random from an infinitely large community belonging to different species. The bias corrected mathematical form of Simpson’s index is \\\[D = \\sum \\limits_\{i=1\}^\{S\} p_\{i\}^\{2\}\\\] where \\\(p_\{i\}\\\) is the fraction of all organisms which belong to the \\\(i\\\)-th species and \\\(S\\\) is the number of species."
comment: "Since \(D\) and diversity are negatively related, Simpson’s index is usually expressed as either a reciprocal or a complementary form (\(1/D\) or \(1 - D\)) so that as the index goes up, so does measure of diversity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14599

[Term]
id: goldbook:15035
name: simulated field studies
def: "Experimental ecosystem that should be\: physically confined; self-maintaining; multitrophic; have a duration time exceeding the generation time of the penultimate trophic level present; and of size sufficient to enable pertinent sampling and measurements to be made without seriously influencing the structure and dynamics of the system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:15036
name: soil
def: "Naturally occurring\, unconsolidated mineral and \(or\) organic material at the surface of the Earth that is capable of supporting plant growth. It extends from the surface to \\\(\\pu\{15 cm\}\\\) below the depth at which properties produced by soil-forming processes can be detected."
comment: "Soil formation results from an interaction between climate, living organisms, and surface relief acting on soil parent material."
comment: "Unconsolidated material includes material cemented or compacted by soil-forming processes. Soil may have water covering its surface to a depth of \(\pu{60 cm}\) (or less in the driest part of the year)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15037
name: solvent drag
def: "Movement of a solute \(e.g.\, a contaminant\) along with the bulk movement of the solvent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549

[Term]
id: goldbook:15038
name: somatic death
def: "Death of an individual organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15039
name: somatic risk
def: "Risk of an adverse effect to the exposed individual associated with genetic damage to somatic cells\, e.g.\, damage leading to cancer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15040
name: sorbate
def: "Noncommittal term used instead of adsorbate or absorbate when the sorption process is undefined."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14413

[Term]
id: goldbook:15041
name: sorption constant
def: "Quantity describing the distribution of a substance between a solvent and a sorbent\, typically water and sediment\, at equilibrium\, e.g.\, \\\[K_\{\\rm\{d\}\} = \[\\pu\{C\(sediment\)\}\]/\[\\pu\{C\(water\)\}\]\\\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15042
name: source term
def: "Estimate of the total amount released\, or the temporal pattern of the rate of release\, of a pollutant from a source."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14928

[Term]
id: goldbook:15043
name: Spearman–Karber method
def: "Nonparametric method to estimate the \\\(\\pu\{LC_\{50\}\}\\\)\, \\\(\\pu\{EC_\{50\}\}\\\)\, or \\\(\\pu\{LD_\{50\}\}\\\) when it is difficult or unnecessary to assume a specific model for the dose- or concentration effect data."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15044
name: species–area relationship
def: "Common pattern in which the number of species on islands decreases as island area decreases."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15045
name: species assemblage
def: "Operationally defined subset of the entire community."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:15046
name: species–deletion stability
def: "Tendency in a model community for the remaining species to remain at locally stable equilibria after a species is made extinct."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:15047
name: species differences in sensitivity
def: "Quantitative or qualitative differences of response to the action\(s\) of a potentially toxic substance on various species of living organisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15100

[Term]
id: goldbook:15048
name: species diversity
def: "Heterogeneity of an ecological community\, considering both species richness \(\\\(S\\\)\) and species evenness."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:15049
consider: goldbook:15051

[Term]
id: goldbook:15049
name: species evenness
def: "Degree to which the individuals in the community are evenly or uniformly distributed among species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:15050
name: species imbalance
def: "Change in the species numbers or diversity in an ecosystem\, or in their interactions\, which results in change in ecological character and its functions and attributes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14614
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:15051
name: species richness
def: "Total number of species in an ecosystem."
comment: "This index makes no use of relative abundances."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14479

[Term]
id: goldbook:15052
name: species sensitivity distribution
def: "Statistical relationship between exposure concentration and a defined effect derived from a combination of single-species test data to predict concentrations affecting only a certain percentage of the total number of species in a defined community."
comment: "Single-species data [e.g., median lethal concentration (\(\pu{LC_{50}}\)) or no-observed-effect concentration (NOEC) values] for many species are fitted to a distribution relationship such as the log-normal or log-logistic curve. From this distribution of species sensitivities, a hazardous concentration (\(\pu{HC_{\textit{p}}}\)) is identified at which a certain percentage (\(p\)) of all species is likely to be affected. The most conservative form of this approach uses the lower \(\pu{95\%}\) tolerance limit of the estimated percentage to ensure that the specified level of protection is achieved"
synonym: "SSD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14738
consider: goldbook:14885

[Term]
id: goldbook:15053
name: species-specific sensitivity
def: "Quantitative and qualitative features of response to the action\(s\) of a potentially toxic substance that are characteristic for a particular species of living organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15100

[Term]
id: goldbook:15054
name: specific action concept
def: "Assumption made in radiotracer usage concerning specificity of action of a radionuclide used to trace or quantify the movement of a stable nuclide \(e.g.\, \\\(\\ce\{^\{14\}C\}\\\) for stable \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)\)\, implying that the radionuclide behaves identically in chemical and biological processes to its nonradioactive analog \(e.g.\, stable \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)\)."
comment: "Sometimes confusingly called the "specific activity concept"."
synonym: "specific activity concept" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15055
name: spiked bioassay approach
def: "Sediment toxicity test method to generate a concentration response model for effects to individuals placed in sediments spiked with different amounts of toxicant."
comment: "The method may also be used to test hypotheses regarding the mechanism of production of previously observed effects."
synonym: "SB" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "SB approach" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15056
name: spillover hypothesis
def: "Hypothesis that toxic effects of metals will begin to occur after the metal concentration exceeds the capacity of the amount of metallothionein present to bind the metal. The unbound metals then 'spill over' to interact at sites of adverse action. This is based on the assumption that binding by metallothionein sequesters toxic metals away from sites of action."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15100

[Term]
id: goldbook:15057
name: stable age distribution
def: "Abundance of relative age classes that a population approaches if it is allowed to grow exponentially."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14415
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15058
name: stable population
def: "Population with a constant distribution of individuals among the various age classes and a zero growth rate."
comment: "Stable populations do not change in size over time if environmental conditions do not change."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15059
name: standard
def: "That which is established as a measure or model to which others of a similar nature should conform."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14645

[Term]
id: goldbook:15060
name: standard
def: "Technical specification\, usually in the form of a document available to the public\, drawn up with the consensus or general approval of all interests affected by it\, based on the consolidated results of science\, technology\, and experience\, aimed at the promotion of optimum community benefits and approved by a body recognized on the national\, regional\, or international level."
synonym: "technical directive" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531

[Term]
id: goldbook:15061
name: static-renewal test
def: "Modified static aquatic toxicity test in which solutions are completely or partially replaced with new solutions at set periods during exposures or in which organisms are periodically transferred to new solutions."
synonym: "batch-replacement test" []
synonym: "renewal test" []
synonym: "renewed static test" []
synonym: "semi-static test" []
synonym: "static-replacement test" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15062
name: static-toxicity test
def: "Aquatic toxicity test in which the exposure water is not changed during the test."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15063
name: stratification
def: "Process by which materials form or are deposited in layers\, as in sedimentary rocks and some igneous rocks. The atmosphere and the ocean also exhibit stratification\, with the warmer air or water occupying the upper layers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15064
name: stratified sampling
def: "Sampling of individual subgroups \(strata\) of a population after its division into homogeneous strata."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15065
name: stress
def: "Any condition that results in reduced growth of an organism or that prevents an organism from realizing its 'genetic potential'."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15066
name: stressor
def: "Any physical\, chemical\, or biological factor causing an adverse response on any component of an ecosystem."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:15067
name: stress-protein fingerprinting
def: "Proposed use of the patterns of stress-protein induction seen in the field to suggest the particular toxicant inducing the response\, after patterns from organisms sampled in the field are compared with those obtained with single-candidate toxicants in the laboratory."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15068
name: stress proteins
def: "Several classes of proteins coded by genes transcriptionally activated by acute stresses\, generally serving a protective or adaptive function."
comment: "Stressors include physical agents such as heat and radiation, infection and inflammation, oxidative stress and hypoxia, desiccation and starvation, metals, xenobiotics, etc."
comment: "These proteins include chaperones such as the heat shock proteins, enzymes protective against oxidative stress, metallothioneins, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15069
name: stress theory of aging
def: "Theory that stress shortens longevity by accelerating energy expenditure. Selection takes place for resistance to stress\, and as an epiphenomenon\, individuals resistant to stress will predominate in extreme age classes of a population. The diminution of homeostasis under stress with age should be slowest in individuals with highest longevity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14744
consider: goldbook:14932
consider: goldbook:14971

[Term]
id: goldbook:15070
name: structural diversity
def: "Range of types of physical structure in a community that may provide habitats for species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14728

[Term]
id: goldbook:15071
name: structure–metabolism relationship
def: "Association between the physicochemical and \(or\) the structural properties of a substance and its metabolic behavior."
synonym: "SMR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15072
name: Sturm test
def: "Biodegradation test based on the measurement of \\\(\\ce\{CO2\}\\\) production."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15073
name: stygobiont
def: "Organism that lives only in groundwater."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15074
name: stygophile
def: "Organism that lives in groundwater and in surface water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15075
name: subcooled
def: "Term applied to a substance that is a liquid at a temperature lower than the saturation temperature for the existing pressure."
comment: "Sometimes such a substance is described as a "compressed" liquid since the existing pressure is greater than the saturation pressure for the given temperature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15076
name: subcooled liquid vapour pressure
def: "Vapor pressure of a subcooled liquid."
comment: "This physicochemical property is an important factor in determining the fate of chemicals in the environment and in allowing for the effects of environmental temperature variability."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15075

[Term]
id: goldbook:15077
name: succession
def: "Orderly sequential progression of changes in community composition that occurs during development of new populations in any area\, from initial colonization to the attainment of the climax typical of a particular geographic area."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
