[Term]
id: goldbook:15078
name: supercooled
def: "Term describing a substance that persists as a liquid at a temperature below its freezing point without solidification or crystallization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15079
name: surrogate organism
def: "Test organism\, or population that is cultured under laboratory conditions to serve as a substitute in toxicity testing for indigenous organisms\, communities\, or populations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15080
name: surrogate toxicant
def: "Relatively well-studied substance whose properties are assumed to apply to an entire chemically and toxicologically related class."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15081
name: surveillance
def: "Systematic ongoing collection\, collation\, and analysis of data and the timely dissemination of information to those who need to know in order that action can be taken to initiate investigative or control measures."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15082
name: survival time
def: "Time interval between initial exposure of an organism to a harmful substance and death."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15083
name: survivorship
def: "Proportion of animals surviving between two specified ages."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15084
name: survivorship curve
def: "Graph showing how survivorship from birth varies with age."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15085
name: susceptibility
def: "Condition of an organism or ecological system that makes it more vulnerable to a given exposure than the majority of the population or group of ecological systems to which it belongs."
comment: "Susceptibility is inversely proportional to the magnitude of the exposure required to cause a toxic effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15086
name: suspension feeder
def: "Animal that feeds by straining suspended matter and food particles from water\, typically by passing the water over a specialized structure\, such as the baleen of baleen whales."
comment: "Other types of feeder are deposit feeder, fluid feeder, and food-mass feeder."
comment: "Some animals that use this method of feeding are clams, barnacles, krill, mysids, sponges, whale sharks, and flamingoes."
synonym: "filter feeder" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14575
consider: goldbook:14697
consider: goldbook:14699

[Term]
id: goldbook:15087
name: syngenetic
def: "Describing mineral deposits formed at the same time as the enclosing rocks; characterized by or pertaining to a formation contemporaneous with the enclosing or surrounding rock."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15088
name: systematics
def: "Study of the diversity of past and present life forms and of relationships among them through time."
comment: "Relationships are visualized in cladograms (evolutionary trees, phylogenetic tree phylogenies). Systematics is used to understand the evolutionary history of life on Earth."
synonym: "taxonomy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14527
consider: goldbook:14667
consider: goldbook:14913

[Term]
id: goldbook:15089
name: taxocene
def: "Taxonomically defined subset of an entire community."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:15090

[Term]
id: goldbook:15090
name: taxonomy
def: "Science applied to the allocation of biological names and the rules of naming."
comment: "Classification (systematics) is the process of rank ordering of taxa according to presumptive evolutionary (phylogenetic) relationships."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14913
consider: goldbook:15088

[Term]
id: goldbook:15091
name: teratogenic
def: "Capable of causing nonheritable permanent structural malformations or defects in the offspring of an exposed parent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15092
name: terrestrial
def: "Relating to land\, as distinct from water or air."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15093
name: threshold-effect concentration
def: "Concentration calculated as the geometric mean of no-observed-effect concentration \(NOEC\) and lowest-observed-effect concentration \(LOEC\)."
comment: ""Chronic" or "subchronic" may be added as qualifiers dependent on the duration of exposure in the test."
comment: "The TEC is equivalent to the maximum acceptable toxicant concentration (MATC) used in some countries."
synonym: "TEC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14820
consider: goldbook:14832
consider: goldbook:14885

[Term]
id: goldbook:15094
name: threshold theory
def: "Theory that\, for a given substance\, no toxic effect can occur below a defined low dose."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15100

[Term]
id: goldbook:15095
name: tiered testing
def: "Structured approach to assessment of the fate and effects of substances\, where a tier of relatively simple tests is used initially to select substances of concern and to define their toxicity. If the information from these tests is inadequate for regulatory decisions\, further more complex tests \(higher tier tests\) may be required. For example\, under a tiered structure\, testing might progress from acute studies to chronic laboratory studies to field studies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15096
name: time-independent test
def: "Acute toxicity test with no predetermined temporal endpoint."
comment: "This type of test, sometimes referred to as a "threshold" or "incipient" lethality test, is allowed to continue until acute toxicity (mortality or a defined sublethal effect) has ceased or nearly ceased and the toxicity curve (median survival time vs. test material concentration) indicates a threshold or incipient concentration. With most test materials, this point is reached within \(\pu{7\!-\! 10 d}\), but it may not be reached within \(\pu{21 d}\). Practical or economic reasons may dictate that the test be stopped at this point and a test be designed for longer duration."
synonym: "TI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "TI test" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15097
name: tolerance index
def: "Quotient of an adequate parameter acquired under treated and control environments\, multiplied by \\\(\\pu\{100\}\\\)\, thus\: \\\[\\rm\{TI\} = \(\\rm\{parameter\\ treated\}/\\rm\{parameter\\ control\}\) \\times 100\\\]"
comment: "This index was originally defined in terms of root growth."
synonym: "TI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14432
consider: goldbook:14930
consider: goldbook:15010

[Term]
id: goldbook:15098
name: top-down ecotoxicological study
def: "Approach to investigating ecotoxicological effects that starts with a determination of the presence and nature of any adverse effects via responses at community and ecosystem levels of organization rather than the suborganismal levels of organization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14509
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:15099
name: total organic carbon
def: "Organic matter content of soil\, sediment\, or water determined by measurement of organic carbon as the ratio of mass of organic carbon/mass of solid or of water."
comment: "Most of the organic carbon in water is dissolved organic carbon (DOC), with the remainder referred to as particulate organic carbon. In natural waters, TOC is composed primarily of nonspecific humic materials."
comment: "TOC is determined by oxidation of the organic matter into carbon dioxide (\(\ce{CO2}\)) after removal of inorganic carbon such as carbonate or hydrogencarbonate. TOC includes all the carbon atoms covalently bonded in organic molecules."
synonym: "TOC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14595
consider: goldbook:14746
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:15100
name: toxic
def: "Able to cause injury to living organisms as a result of physicochemical interaction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15101
name: toxic unit
def: "Dose or concentration of a toxicant expressed in units of lethality such as units of \\\(\\pu\{LD_\{50\}\}\\\) or \\\(\\pu\{LC_\{50\}\}\\\)."
synonym: "TU" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "toxicity unit" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15102
name: toxicity curve
def: "Curve obtained by plotting the median survival times of a group of test organisms against the concentration of a substance on a logarithmic scale."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15103
name: toxicity equivalency factor
def: "Ratio of the toxicity of a chemical to that of another structurally related chemical \(or index compound\) chosen as a reference. In risk assessment\, ratio of the toxicity of a chemical to that of another structurally related chemical \(or index compound\) chosen as a reference. Factor used to estimate the toxicity of a complex mixture\, commonly a mixture of chlorinated dibenzo-p-dioxins \[oxanthrenes\]\, furans\, and biphenyls\: in this case\, TEF is based on relative toxicity to 2\,3\,7\,8-tetrachlorodibenzo-p-dioxin \[2\,3\,7\,8-tetrachlorooxanthrene\] for which the \\\(f = 1\\\)."
synonym: "TEF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15104
name: toxicity equivalent
def: "Contribution of a specified component \(or components\) to the toxicity of a mixture of related substances."
comment: "The amount-of-substance (or substance) concentration of total toxicity equivalent is the sum of that for the components \(\ce{B, C … N}\)."
comment: "Toxicity equivalent is most commonly used in relation to the reference toxicant 2,3,7,8-tetrachlorodibenzo-p-dioxin [2,3,7,8-tetrachlorooxanthrene] by means of the toxicity equivalency factor (TEF, \(f\)) that is 1 for the reference substance. Hence, where \(\pu{c}\) is the amount-of-substance concentration: \[T_{\rm{xe}} = \sum \limits_{i=B}^{N} f_{1} \pu{c}_{i}\]"
synonym: "TEQ" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15103

[Term]
id: goldbook:15105
name: toxicity identification and evaluation
def: "Systematic pretreatment \(e.g.\, \\\(\\rm\{pH\}\\\) change\, filtration\, or aeration\) of a sample to obtain defined fractions that are subsequently tested for their toxicity. This fractionation is designed to separate out defined substances and thus to identify the agent\(s\) primarily responsible for lethal or sublethal toxicity of a complex mixture."
synonym: "TIE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15106
name: toxicity value
def: "Factor used to estimate risk. It may be a reference dose or it may be calculated from the following equation\: \\\[T_\{\\rm\{x\}\} = m\\ C\\\] where \\\(m\\\) is the slope of a published dose-effect relationship and \\\(C\\\) is the toxicant concentration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14602

[Term]
id: goldbook:15107
name: trace nutrient
def: "Substance required in very small quantities by a defined organism to maintain health."
comment: "The quantities required for health and the species must be stated before application of this term has any meaning."
comment: "Use of the term is often misleading since it is meaningless unless accompanied by a statement of which organisms show a requirement for the nutrient and the amount required."
synonym: "micronutrient" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15108
name: trade-off
def: "Exchange of one advantageous character for another."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15109
name: trigger values
def: "Criteria applied to results from tests \(for fate or effects\) which prompt further studies\, e.g.\, moving to the next tier of tests\, which are generally more complex."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15095

[Term]
id: goldbook:15110
name: trophic
def: "Relating to nutrition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15111
name: trophic cascade
def: "Situation arising when predators in a food chain suppress the abundance of their prey\, thereby releasing the next lower trophic level from predation \(or herbivory if the intermediate trophic level is an herbivore\)."
comment: "For example, if the abundance of large piscivorous fish is increased in a lake, the abundance of their prey, zooplanktivorous fish, should decrease, large zooplankton abundance should increase, and phytoplankton biomass should decrease."
comment: "Trophic cascades may also be important for understanding the effects of removing top predators from food webs, as humans have done in many places through hunting and fishing activities."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14698
consider: goldbook:14918
consider: goldbook:14922
consider: goldbook:14923
consider: goldbook:15113
consider: goldbook:15139

[Term]
id: goldbook:15112
name: trophic dilution
def: "Decrease in contaminant concentration as trophic level increases; this results from a net balance of ingestion rate\, uptake from food\, internal transformation\, and elimination processes favoring loss of contaminant that enters the organism via food."
synonym: "biominification" []
synonym: "bioreduction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14549
consider: goldbook:15113

[Term]
id: goldbook:15113
name: trophic level
def: "Position in a food chain\, assessed by the number of energy-transfer steps to reach that level."
synonym: "trophic position" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14612
consider: goldbook:14698

[Term]
id: goldbook:15114
name: trophic structure
def: "Organization of an ecological community described in terms of energy flow through its various trophic levels."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14531
consider: goldbook:15113

[Term]
id: goldbook:15115
name: trophic transfer
def: "Transfer of a substance from one trophic level to another."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15113

[Term]
id: goldbook:15116
name: trophic transfer factor
def: "Ratio between the concentration of a compound in a predator and in its prey."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15117
name: turbidity of water
def: "Extent to which the clarity of water is reduced by the presence of suspended or other matter that causes light to be scattered and absorbed rather than transmitted \(in straight lines\) through the sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15118
name: twin-tracer technique
def: "Experimental method for evaluating assimilation that introduces simultaneously a radiotracer of the substance being assimilated and an inert tracer that will not be assimilated\, thus providing a basis for evaluating the assimilation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15119
name: type A organism
def: "Animal or plant living in contact with sediments but unable to ingest particulates."
comment: "The classification implies that such organisms take up substances from interstitial water but not from sediment-associated particulates; examples of such organisms are rooted macrophytes and benthic algae."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14433
consider: goldbook:14468
consider: goldbook:14772
consider: goldbook:14826
consider: goldbook:15120

[Term]
id: goldbook:15120
name: type B organism
def: "Animal or plant living in contact with sediments and capable of ingesting particulates."
comment: "The classification implies that such organisms take up substances from both interstitial water and from sediment-associated particulates."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14772
consider: goldbook:15119

[Term]
id: goldbook:15121
name: uncertainty factor
def: "In assay methodology\, confidence interval or fiducial limit used to assess the probable precision of an estimate. In toxicology\, value used in extrapolation from experimental animals to humans \(assuming that humans may be more sensitive\) or from selected individuals to the general population.Example\: A value applied to the no-observed-effect-level \(NOEL\) or no-observed-adverse-effect-level \(NOAEL\) to derive an acceptable daily intake \(ADI\) or tolerable daily intake \(TDI\).Note\: The NOEL or NOAEL is divided by the value to calculate the ADI or TDI."
synonym: "UF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "application factor (AF)" []
synonym: "assessment factor" []
synonym: "modifying factor (MF)" []
synonym: "safety factor" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15122
name: upstream water
def: "Water in a rivulet\, river\, or lake that is situated above a defined point\, in a direction opposite to that of the current flow."
comment: "Upstream water is not influenced by incoming effluent at or below the defined point because the effluent is carried away by the flow."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15123
name: uptake rate constant
def: "First-order one-compartment constant to describe the uptake of a substance by an organism from water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15124
name: viability selection
def: "Component of the life cycle of an individual in which natural selection can occur through the differential survival of individuals. It begins at the formation of the zygote and continues throughout the life of the individual."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14795

[Term]
id: goldbook:15125
name: vital rates
def: "Measures of how fast vital statistics change in a population \(usually expressed per \\\(\\pu\{1000\}\\\) individuals\)."
comment: "There are two categories within vital rates, crude rates referring to change in the whole population (e.g., overall change in births and deaths per \(\pu{1000}\)) and refined rates referring to change in a specific demographic such as age, sex, race, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15126
name: vulnerability
def: "Susceptibility to harm by toxicants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14732
consider: goldbook:15085

[Term]
id: goldbook:15127
name: Wahlund effect
def: "Net deficit of heterozygotes when two populations\, each in Hardy–Weinberg equilibrium but with different allele frequencies\, are mixed and the genotype frequencies quantified in a combined population sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14731
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15128
name: waldsterben
def: "Widespread and substantial decline in growth and the change in behavior of many softwood and hardwood forest ecosystems in central Europe."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14619

[Term]
id: goldbook:15129
name: waste-water
def: "General term describing effluents\, leachate\, and elutriates which enter the natural environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14628
consider: goldbook:14786

[Term]
id: goldbook:15130
name: weakest-link incongruity
def: "Questionable extension of the critical life-stage concept \(see critical life-stage testing\) that protection of the most sensitive life stage will ensure protection of all life stages; it assumes that exposure of field populations to concentrations identified in laboratory testing as causing significant mortality at a critical stage of life will result in significant impact on the field population"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14559
consider: goldbook:14932

[Term]
id: goldbook:15131
name: Weibull model
def: "Dose–response model of the form \\\[P\(d\) = \\gamma + \(1 - \\gamma\)\(1 - e^\{-\\beta d^\{\\alpha\}\}\)\\\] where \\\(P\(d\)\\\) is the probability of a tumor \(or other response\) from lifetime\, continuous exposure at dose \\\(d\\\) until age \\\(t\\\) \(when tumor is fatal\)\, \\\(\\alpha\\\) is a fitted dose parameter \(sometimes called the Weibull parameter\)\, \\\(\\beta\\\) is a fitted dose parameter\, and \\\(\\gamma\\\) is the background response rate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14604

[Term]
id: goldbook:15132
name: weight composition
def: "Distribution of organisms among the various weight classes present in a population."
comment: "The sum of individual weights over all weight classes equals the population biomass."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14932
consider: goldbook:14933

[Term]
id: goldbook:15133
name: weight of evidence
def: "\(in general\) Quantitative\, semiquantitative\, or qualitative estimate of the degree to which the evidence supports or undermines a given conclusion. \(in toxicology\) Estimate of the extent to which the available biomedical data support the hypothesis that a substance causes a defined toxic effect such as cancer in humans."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15100

[Term]
id: goldbook:15134
name: Weismannism
def: "Theory of evolution and heredity propounded by the German biologist\, August Weismann\, especially in regard to the continuity of the germ-plasm and the nontransmission of acquired characteristics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14667

[Term]
id: goldbook:15135
name: wet deposition
def: "Transfer of chemicals from the atmosphere to the Earth’s surface in atmospheric water precipitation \(atmospheric deposition\)\, e.g.\, rain\, snow\, or hail\, of pollutants that occur in the precipitation\, e.g.\, as a result of Brownian capture\, nucleation\, dissolution\, or impaction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14454
consider: goldbook:14928

[Term]
id: goldbook:15136
name: wetland
def: "Area of land consisting of soil that is saturated with moisture\, such as a swamp\, marsh\, or bog."
comment: "As defined in terms of physical geography, a wetland is an environment "at the interface between truly terrestrial ecosystems and aquatic systems making them inherently different from each other yet highly dependent on both"."
comment: "In many locations such as the United Kingdom and United States, wetlands are the subject of conservation efforts and biodiversity action plans (BAPs)."
comment: "Wetlands are ecotones. Wetlands often host considerable biodiversity and endemism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14479
consider: goldbook:14480
consider: goldbook:14547
consider: goldbook:14548
consider: goldbook:14620
consider: goldbook:14633
consider: goldbook:15036

[Term]
id: goldbook:15137
name: whole-effluent toxicity
def: "Total toxic effect of an effluent measured directly with aquatic organisms in a toxicity test."
synonym: "WET" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15100

[Term]
id: goldbook:15138
name: whole sediment
def: "Sediment and associated interstitial water that have had minimal manipulation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14772

[Term]
id: goldbook:15139
name: zooplankton
def: "Small floating or weakly swimming animals that drift with water currents and which\, with phytoplankton\, make up the planktonic food supply upon which almost all oceanic organisms ultimately depend."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:14918
consider: goldbook:14924

[Term]
id: goldbook:15140
name: normal equivalent deviation
def: "Proportion dying in a toxicity test expressed in terms of standard deviations from the mean of a normal curve."
synonym: "NED" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15141
name: absolute bioavailability
def: "Fraction of the administered dose of a drug from a dosage form absorbed intact into the systemic circulation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15175

[Term]
id: goldbook:15142
name: active transport of drugs
def: "Carriage of a solute across a biological membrane\, which requires a suitable carrier and the expenditure of energy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15143
name: administration
def: "Introduction of a substance to an organism by a defined route."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15144
name: administration of drugs ocular route
def: "Administration of drugs through the eye."
comment: "Drugs used to treat eye disorders can be administered as liquid or semi-solid dosage forms. Solid inserts, which release the drug in slow-release pattern, are also available."
comment: "Ocular drugs are almost always used for their local effects. Some drugs produce a local effect after they are absorbed through the cornea and conjunctiva. Some of these drugs then enter the bloodstream and may have unwanted or wanted systemic effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15175

[Term]
id: goldbook:15145
name: administration of drugs oral route
def: "Administration of drugs through the mouth to swallow."
comment: "It differs from intraoral administration."
comment: "Per-oral products can be powders, granules, uncoated or coated tablets, capsules, and liquids (solutions, emulsions, and suspensions). Liquids for oral use may contain antimicrobial preservatives and are supplied in multi- or single-dose containers."
comment: "This is the most convenient and popular administration route."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15159
consider: goldbook:15161
consider: goldbook:15193
consider: goldbook:15227

[Term]
id: goldbook:15146
name: administration of drugs parenteral route
def: "Method of introducing substances into an organism\, avoiding the gastrointestinal tract."
comment: "Parenteral administration includes some conventional (intravenous, intramuscular, subcutaneous) and some special (intradermal, intraventricular, etc.) routes."
comment: "Parenteral products can be solutions, suspensions, and emulsions. They are presented as sterile products. It is commonly used to imply administration by injection or infusion."
comment: "Parenteral routes may be employed whenever enteral routes are contraindicated or inadequate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15201

[Term]
id: goldbook:15147
name: administration of drugs rectal route
def: "Administration of drugs into the rectal cavity or through the rectum."
comment: "Products may be solid (suppositories) or liquid unit dosage preparations, or creams, ointments, and gels."
comment: "The rectal route has several drawbacks. These can be, in addition to psychological aversion, slow and incomplete absorption, and inadequacy where rapid absorption and high plasma levels are required."
comment: "This is an important way of administering a medicinal product that may not be tolerated orally, especially in pediatrics and geriatrics or when the patient has an infection of the gastrointestinal tract; or when the drug is less suited for oral administration because of side effects, bad taste, or enzymatic degradation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15184
consider: goldbook:15217
consider: goldbook:15238

[Term]
id: goldbook:15148
name: administration of drugs respiratory route
def: "Delivery to the lower respiratory tract in order to obtain a local or systemic effect."
comment: "Products usually deliver the active substance in the form of aerosol droplets or solid particles (powders)."
synonym: "introduction of drugs by inhalation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15200
consider: goldbook:15227

[Term]
id: goldbook:15149
name: administration of drugs topical route
def: "Administration of drugs on surfaces of the body."
comment: "Topical products usually produce pharmacological effects at or near the point of application, such as the skin, eyes, nose, throat, ears, and vagina, etc., but sometimes may also have systemic effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143

[Term]
id: goldbook:15150
name: administration of drugs transdermal route
def: "Introduction of products through unbroken skin by means of a specific drug delivery system \(such as a patch containing a semi-solid formulation of the drug\) for systemic and/or prolonged drug effect."
synonym: "diadermic administration" []
synonym: "percutaneous administration" []
synonym: "transcutaneous administration" []
synonym: "transdermic administration" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15177
consider: goldbook:15188

[Term]
id: goldbook:15151
name: administration of drugs vaginal route
def: "Introduction of products into the vagina normally for local effect."
comment: "Vaginal preparations may be liquid dispersions (solutions, foams), semi-solid (gels, creams, ointments), and solids (tablets, capsules, pessaries, tampons, sponges)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15159
consider: goldbook:15217
consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15152
name: angle of repose
def: "Characteristic angle of slope formed with the horizontal by the side of a static conical mound of powder."
comment: "A measure of cohesiveness in powders. The smaller the angle of repose the greater the ability of the powder to flow. A particle will begin to slide on a slope when the angle of inclination is sufficiently large to overcome the frictional forces, and conversely the particle will not move when the angle is below that required to overcome cohesion and adhesion."
comment: "Angle of repose is determined by a balance of gravitational force and the frictional forces caused by interparticulate interactions."
comment: "The angle of repose depends on the method of measurement."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15227

[Term]
id: goldbook:15153
name: appertisation
def: "Process by which food is rendered free from pathogenic\, toxigenic\, and spoilage organisms."
comment: "A term used in the food industry."
comment: "Appertization will not necessarily kill thermophilic spores, and thus products subjected to the process may not be sterile."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15154
name: bioequivalence
def: "Relationship between two preparations of the same drug in the same dosage form that have a similar bioavailability. Dosage forms containing the same drug are said to be bioequivalent if they do not differ significantly in the bioavailability \(e.g.\, AUC\, \\\(c_\{\\rm\{max\}\}\\\)\, \\\(t_\{\\rm\{max\}\}\\\)\) of the active constituent/ingredient\, when administered in the same dose under similar experimental conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15155
name: biological product
def: "Virus\, therapeutic serum\, toxin\, antitoxin\, or analogous product applicable to the prevention\, treatment\, or cure of diseases or injuries in humans and/or animals."
comment: "The term "analogous product" may include essentially all biotechnology-derived products and procedures including gene therapy, transgenics, and somatic cell therapy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15191

[Term]
id: goldbook:15156
name: biopharmaceutics
def: "Branch of pharmaceutical science that deals with the fate of drugs in the living system; particularly the release of the drug from its dosage form into a biological medium\, its passage across membranes into the systemic circulation\, metabolism\, and elimination\, and the application of this knowledge to obtain the desired therapeutic effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15175

[Term]
id: goldbook:15157
name: buccal tablet
def: "Usually a small\, flat\, and soft tablet\, which is designed to be placed inside the cheek to be directly absorbed through the mucosa for systemic effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15158
name: bulk density
def: "Characteristic of a powder rather than of individual particles given by the mass of powder occupying a known volume."
comment: "A powder can have only one true density, but it can have many different bulk densities, depending on how tightly the particles are packed."
comment: "Characteristics of importance in tablet production."
comment: "The bulk density is always lower than the true density of its component particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15227
consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15159
name: capsule
def: "Small edible package made usually from gelatin or other materials that can be filled with drugs \(solids or liquids\) to produce a unit dose\, mainly for oral use. Hard capsules consist of two pieces that fit one inside the other which are produced empty and filled in a separate operation\, and soft\, liquid-filled capsules\, which are manufactured and filled in one operation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15145

[Term]
id: goldbook:15160
name: carrier-mediated drug transport
def: "Transfer of a drug across a membrane by a transporter \(often a protein\) constituent of the cytosol membrane. Also known as active transport as opposed to passive diffusion/absorption."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15142
consider: goldbook:15171

[Term]
id: goldbook:15161
name: coating
def: "Technological process consisting of the application of a substance\, which forms a layer \(e.g.\, to protect the drug and/or the tablet\, to mask taste\, to control the rate of drug release \(e.g.\, film coating\, sugar coating\)."
comment: "Sugar coating is used to mask bad taste without altering release profile."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15162
name: compressed tablet
def: "A solid dosage form prepared to a desired shape\, usually in large-scale production\, by means of high pressure in a punch and die."
comment: "Most compressed tablets consist of the active ingredient and a diluent (filler), binder, disintegrator, and lubricant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15163
name: controlled-release dosage form
def: "Medication\, which due to its special technological construction provides for drug release having predefined kinetics \(zero order\, \\\(t^\{1/2\}\\\)\, first order\, etc.\) at a sufficient rate to maintain the desired therapeutic level over an extended period of time."
comment: "Also used to denote sustained-release products with zero-order release kinetics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15239

[Term]
id: goldbook:15164
name: critical moisture content
def: "A stage in the drying of solids\, above which the drying rate \(derived from the plot of the loss of moisture content against time\) is linear\, at which the drying rate ceases to be linear\, until it reaches the equilibrium moisture content."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15186

[Term]
id: goldbook:15165
name: crossover study
def: "Type of comparative bioavailability study designed in such a way as to take into account differences in bioavailability arising from differences between patients suffering from disease\, participating in the study."
comment: "The differences between the subjects may be in age, stage or severity of the disease, and prior drug treatment that some may have received. In such a crossover study, the patients are divided into two equal size groups, uniform with respect to age, body weight, sex, etc. The first group is given a specific dose of the product studied, while the second group is given a second product of proven clinical efficacy, containing the same active ingredient. After taking an appropriate number of blood samples from each individual and a washout period, the groups are reversed and the first group is given the product of proven clinical efficacy and the second is given the product being studied. This way each patient serves as his or her own control."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15166
name: crystalline
def: "Term that describes a solid of regular shape and the presence of three-dimensional order on the level of atomic dimensions\, for a given molecule."
comment: "Crystalline forms are often preferred, over amorphous forms, in pharmaceutical dosage forms, due to uniformity, reproducibility, and sometimes lack of hygroscopicity."
comment: "Crystallinity may be detected by diffraction techniques, heat-of-fusion measurements, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15175

[Term]
id: goldbook:15167
name: delayed-release dosage form
def: "Pharmaceutical preparation that releases the drug\(s\) at a time other than promptly after administration."
comment: "Typically, this is related to enteric coated tablets."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15185

[Term]
id: goldbook:15168
name: deliquescent
def: "Substance that absorbs sufficient moisture from the atmosphere to dissolve itself."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15169
name: depot
def: "Deposit of a drug in a body created by injection or by a similar mode of introduction to form a source of slow release."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15170
name: detergency
def: "Property\, which serves as basis for the process whereby surfactants are used for the removal of foreign matter from surfaces \(including dirt from clothes or body surfaces\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15233

[Term]
id: goldbook:15171
name: diffusion barrier
def: "Obstacle such as coating or embedding\, which acts as a factor controlling the rate of drug release."
comment: "Body fluids or membranes can also act as barriers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15161
consider: goldbook:15183

[Term]
id: goldbook:15172
name: disperse system
def: "Dosage form in which the active ingredient is insoluble in the carrier; includes aerosols \(solids or liquids in gas\)\, suspensions \(solids in liquids\)\, emulsions \(liquids in liquids\)\, and foams \(gas in liquid\)\, or ointments/creams \(solid in solid or in semi-solid\, or liquid in solid\)."
comment: "These systems are thermodynamically unstable and need to be stabilized by suspensifying or emulsifying agents."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15217

[Term]
id: goldbook:15173
name: divided granule
def: "Formulation in which individual doses of a granulated dosage form are separated \(e.g.\, gelatin capsules\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15159
consider: goldbook:15188
consider: goldbook:15194

[Term]
id: goldbook:15174
name: divided powder
def: "Powder formulation in which individual doses of a powdered dosage form are separately wrapped \(e.g.\, sachets\, envelopes\, or gelatin capsules\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15159
consider: goldbook:15175
consider: goldbook:15227

[Term]
id: goldbook:15175
name: dosage form
def: "Formulated preparation of molecules/drugs that are rarely if ever suitable for administration to patients without additives."
comment: "They can be designed for administration by all possible administration routes to achieve the desired therapeutic response."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15188
consider: goldbook:15238
consider: goldbook:15240
consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15176
name: dosage regimen
def: "Dose and dosing interval of a drug."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15177
name: drug delivery system
def: "Sophisticated dosage form\, which\, by its construction\, is able to modify/control the availability of the drug substance to the body by temporal or spatial considerations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
