consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15216
name: nanoencapsulation
def: "Formation of nanoparticles encapsulating a drug."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15217
name: ointment
def: "Greasy\, semi-solid preparation for external application\, often anhydrous\, containing dissolved or dispersed medicaments."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15172

[Term]
id: goldbook:15218
name: one-compartment model
def: "Kinetic model\, where the whole body is thought of as a single compartment in which a substance is distributed rapidly\, achieving an equilibrium between blood and tissue immediately."
comment: "In pharmacokinetics, the substance is a drug component which is assumed to be released from a dosage form and distributed instantly after absorption to reach an equilibrium between blood and tissues."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15175

[Term]
id: goldbook:15219
name: onset of drug action
def: "Time required to achieve the minimum effective plasma concentration following administration of the dosage form."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
