[Term]
id: goldbook:15222
name: pelletisation
def: "Process of agglomeration that converts fine powders or granules of bulk drugs and excipients into small\, free-flowing\, spherical\, or semi-spherical units\, referred to as pellets."
comment: "Pellets range typically between \(\pu{0.5 mm}\) and \(\pu{1.5 mm}\) in diameter."
comment: "The most widely used pelletization processes in the pharmaceutical industry are extrusion/spheronization, solution/suspension layering, and powder layering."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15193
consider: goldbook:15221
consider: goldbook:15227

[Term]
id: goldbook:15223
name: pharmaceutical equivalence
def: "To be pharmaceutically equivalent\, the generic and proprietary formulations must \(1\) contain the same amount of active ingredient; \(2\) contain the same active ingredient in the same dosage form; \(3\) be intended for the same route of administration; and \(4\) generally be labeled for the same conditions of use."
comment: "It is not usually required that the generic and the reference drug contain the same excipients, or that the mechanism by which the active drug substance is released from the formulation be the same. But, the regulation authority approves the generic equivalent on the basis of certain in vitro and in vivo data."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15154
consider: goldbook:15175
consider: goldbook:15188
consider: goldbook:15192

[Term]
id: goldbook:15224
name: pharmaceutics
def: "Science of preparation of drugs\, dosage forms\, and drug delivery systems taking into account the pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of the drug as well as its physical and chemical properties."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15175

[Term]
id: goldbook:15225
name: polymorph
def: "Solid material that exists at least in two different molecular arrangements\, i.e.\, distinctly different crystal species."
comment: "Solubility, melting point, density, crystal shape, crystal structure, and some other physical properties often differ from one polymorph to the other."
comment: "The differences between polymorphs disappear in solution or in the vapor phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15166

[Term]
id: goldbook:15226
name: powder grades
def: "Defined for powders used pharmaceutically\, according to particle sizes."
comment: "It is required that when the fineness of a powder is described by a number, all particles must pass through a sieve with aperture diameter in microns equal to that number."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15227

[Term]
id: goldbook:15227
name: powder
def: "Dry solid material consisting of many\, usually free flowing\, fine particles. Conventionally\, the title 'powder' should be restricted to powder mixes for internal use and alternative terms are used for other powdered formulations presented in this way\, e.g.\, dusting powders\, which are for external use."
comment: "The term "powder", when used to describe a dosage form, however, describes a formulation in which a drug powder has been mixed with other powdered excipients to produce the final product."
synonym: "powders" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15179
consider: goldbook:15188

[Term]
id: goldbook:15228
name: preformulation
def: "Exploratory activity that begins early in pharmaceutics\, involving studies designed to determine the compatibility of excipients with the active substance for a biopharmaceutical; physicochemical and bioanalytical investigation in support of promising experimental formulations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15156
consider: goldbook:15188
consider: goldbook:15224

[Term]
id: goldbook:15229
name: pseudopolymorph
def: "Different crystalline form\(s\) of a solvated compound that differ in the identity and/or the stoichiometry of the solvating molecule."
synonym: "pseudopolymorphs" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15166
consider: goldbook:15234

[Term]
id: goldbook:15230
name: repeat action dosage form
def: "Tablet or capsule distinguished from a sustained-release dosage form\, by the fact that it releases the medicinal agent\, or part of it\, at any time other than promptly after administration as opposed to a slow\, controlled manner."
comment: "A repeat action tablet contains usually two doses of the drug, the first being released immediately following per-oral administration. The second dose is released later, when the layer of enteric coating is dissolved."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15145
consider: goldbook:15159
consider: goldbook:15185
consider: goldbook:15239
consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15231
name: sieving
def: "Process that differentiates or separates solid particles according to their size using a meshed or perforated device."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15232
name: slugging
def: "Method by which powder particles are compressed into a large tablet\, called a slug\, which is subsequently dry-screened and compressed into a tablet."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15227
consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15233
name: solubilising agents
def: "Additives making a substance soluble or more soluble\, especially in water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15234
name: solvate
def: "Crystalline form of a compound in which one or more solvent molecules are part of the crystal structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15166
consider: goldbook:15195

[Term]
id: goldbook:15235
name: spheronisation
def: "Process of making dense\, spherical pellets by means of special spheronizing or pelletizing equipment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15221

[Term]
id: goldbook:15236
name: stent
def: "Scaffold placed into narrowed\, diseased vessels \(mainly coronary arteries\) or a device implanted in a vessel used to help keep it open."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15237
name: sublingual tablets
def: "Usually small\, flat\, and soft tablets\, which are designed to be placed under the tongue to allow direct absorption of the active ingredient through the mucosa for systemic effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15241

[Term]
id: goldbook:15238
name: suppositories
def: "Dosage form\, semi-solid\, used for the administration of drugs via the rectal route\, for systemic or local effect. When application is via other routes \(e.g.\, the vaginal route\)\, suppositories are termed differently\, inserts\, pessaries\, etc."
comment: "An important requirement for suppositories is a melting point (or disintegration/dissolution) at around \(\pu{{36}{-}{37} ^{\circ}C}\) so as to discharge the drug in the rectum."
comment: "The vehicles used in suppositories are of two types, i.e., fatty bases and water-soluble ones."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15143
consider: goldbook:15151
consider: goldbook:15175
consider: goldbook:15239

[Term]
id: goldbook:15239
name: sustained release
def: "Dosage form designed to release the drug contained therein at a continuous and controlled rate for a longer period of time that can normally be achieved with its conventional\, nonsustained counterpart."
comment: "Other terms used to describe the same concept include: "controlled release", "extended release", "long-acting", "gradual release", "modified release", "prolonged action", and "slow release"."
comment: "Per-oral administration of a single dose of a sustained-release product increases the duration of therapeutic action of the drug, beyond that achieved normally with a single dose of the corresponding non-sustained conventional counterpart."
comment: "Sustained-release injectables are also available."
synonym: "extended release" []
synonym: "gradual release" []
synonym: "long acting" []
synonym: "prolonged action" []
synonym: "slow release" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15175

[Term]
id: goldbook:15240
name: syrup
def: "Liquid preparation of high sugar concentration with or without medicinal and additional flavoring substances."
comment: "It is often required to add a cosolvent or water to the medicated syrup in order to dissolve the drug."
comment: "Syrup is a highly concentrated solution of sugar. Other polyols, such as glycerol or sorbitol, may be present to retard crystallization of sucrose or to increase the solubility of added ingredients."
comment: "When the syrup contains a medicinal substance, it is termed "medicated syrup"; and the syrup is diluted since USP syrup is close to a saturated solution. Although syrup tends (due to its very high [approximately \(\pu{85\%}\)] sucrose content) to resist mold or bacterial contamination, syrup may contain antimicrobial agents to prevent bacterial and mold growth."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15241
name: tablet
def: "Solid dosage form compressed into a specific shape containing medicinal substances with or without suitable diluents."
comment: "Tablets may vary in shape, size, color and weight, and may be classified according to the method of manufacture, as molded tablet and compressed tablet."
