[Term]
id: goldbook:15254
name: polyisocyanide
def: "Polymer prepared from an isocyanide."
comment: "Isocyanide monomers are also polymerized by cyclopolymerization to give polytriazines."
comment: "The class name polyisocyanide is preferably used for polymers in which every isocyanide monomeric unit contributes only one atom to a macromolecule backbone; the majority of these polymers are helical polymers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
