[Term]
id: goldbook:15261
name: styrene polymer
def: "Polymer prepared from styrene\, or a substituted styrene\, or both in admixture."
comment: "In common usage, "polystyrene" means a polymer prepared from pure styrene, frequently cross-linked with 1,4-divinylbenzene, rather than a styrene polymer."
comment: "Macromolecule of a regular styrene homopolymer is described by the constitutional repeating unit:  where \(\ce{R^{\upalpha}}\) and \(\ce{R^1}\) to \(\ce{R^5}\) are each \(\ce{H}\), alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl."
comment: "Styrene polymers are a subclass of vinyl polymers."
synonym: "polystyrene" []
