[Term]
id: goldbook:15262
name: vinyl polymer
def: "Polymer prepared from a monomer containing the vinyl group \\\(\\ce\{-CH=CH2\}\\\)."
comment: "Acrylic polymers, polyolefins, polyvinyl acetals, polyvinyl esters, polyvinyl ethers, polyvinyl halides, polyvinyl ketones, and styrene polymers, with \(\ce{R^{\upalpha} = \ce{H}}\) are subclasses of vinyl polymers."
comment: "Macromolecule of a regular vinyl homopolymer is described by the constitutional repeating unit: \(\ce{-CHR-CH2\bond{-}}\), where \(\ce{R}\) is alkyl, aryl, heteroaryl, halogen, or a heteroatom containing pendent group."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30
