[Term]
id: goldbook:15263
name: vinylidene polymer
def: "Polymer prepared from a monomer containing the ethene-1\,1-diyl group \\\(\\gt\\!\\ce\{C=CH2\}\\\)\, formerly called vinylidene."
comment: "A macromolecule of a regular vinylidene polymer is described by the constitutional repeating unit: \(\ce{-CR^1R^2\bond{-}CH2\bond{-}}\), where \(\ce{R^1}\) and \(\ce{R^2}\) are each alkyl, aryl, heteroaryl, or halogen, such as by the units: "
comment: "Vinylidene is correctly defined as ethenylidene only, meaning a divalent attachment to the same atom of a senior group, i.e., it is the correct name for the group \(\ce{=C=CH2}\) but not for the group \(\gt\!\ce{C=CH2}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15264
name: polyalkenylene
def: "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively alkene-α\,ω-diyl \(formerly alkenylene\) constitutional repeating units\: \\\[\\ce\{-\[-CH=CH-\[CH2\]_\{m\}\\bond\{-\}\]_\{n\}\\bond\{-\}\}\\\]"
comment: "Polyalkenylenes are sometimes referred to as polyalkenamers; use of this term is discouraged."
comment: "Polyvinylenes (\(m = 0\)) are excluded."
