id: goldbook:15265
name: polyalkylene
def: "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively alkane-α\,ω-diyl \(formerly alkylene\) constitutional repeating units\: \\\[\\ce\{-\[-CR^\{1\}R^\{2\}\\bond\{-\}\]_\{n\}\\bond\{-\}\}\\\] where \\\(\\ce\{R^1\}\\\) and \\\(\\ce\{R^2\}\\\) are each hydrogen\, alkyl\, or cycloalkyl."
comment: "Polyolefins are the most common polyalkylenes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30
