[Term]
id: goldbook:15267
name: polyamide
def: "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing carboxamide groups as linkages in the backbone\: \\\[\\ce\{-NR-CO\\bond\{-\}\}\\\] where \\\(\\ce\{R\}\\\) is hydrogen\, alkyl\, aryl\, or heteroaryl."
comment: "A polyamide containing pendent carboxy groups is a polyamide acid commonly referred to as a polyamic acid."
comment: "A polyamide containing, besides \(\ce{-NR-CO\bond{-}}\) linkages, exclusively aliphatic constitutional units is an aliphatic polyamide; examples are:  Trivial names of the type: polyamide \(m\) and polyamide \(m,n\) are only used for aliphatic polyamides. Polyamide \(m\) stands for a homopolymeric polyamide derived from an amino acid or a lactam comprising \(m\) carbon atoms; polyamide \(m,n\) stands for a copolymeric polyamide derived from an alkane-1,m-diamine containing \(m\) carbon atoms and an alkanedioic acid containing \(n\) carbon atoms (including those in \(\ce{CO}\) groups)."
comment: "A polyamide containing, besides \(\ce{-NR-CO\bond{-}}\) linkages, exclusively aromatic constitutional units is an aromatic polyamide commonly referred to as an aramide; example is: "
comment: "A polymer containing only pendent amide groups is excluded, e.g., polyacrylamide."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15268

[Term]
id: goldbook:15268
name: polyamide acid
def: "Polyamide containing pendent carboxy groups\:   where \\\(\\ce\{R\}\\\) is a constitutional unit with a connectivity three or higher."
comment: "A polyamide acid is mostly prepared as a processable precursor giving a polyimide upon thermal curing. The polyamide acid prepared from benzene-1,2:4,5-tetracarboxylic dianhydride (formerly pyromellitic anhydride) and hexane-1,6-diamine (formerly hexamethylenediamine) is an example of such a precursor: "
