def: "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing carbon-silicon linkages in the backbone\: \\\[\\ce\{-SiR^\{1\}R^\{2\}\\bond\{-\}CR^\{3\}R^\{4\}\\bond\{-\}\}\\\] where \\\(\\ce\{R^1\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{R^2\}\\\)\, \\\(\\ce\{R^3\}\\\)\, and \\\(\\ce\{R^4\}\\\) are each hydrogen\, alkyl\, aryl\, or heteroaryl."
comment: "A polycarbosilane containing, in addition to silanediyl groups, exclusively alkanediyl (formerly alkylene) or substituted alkanediyl constitutional repeating units is referred to as a polysilalkylene, whereas that involving exclusively arenediyl (formerly arylene) constitutional repeating units is referred to as a polysilarylene."
