[Term]
id: goldbook:15309
name: cardo polymer
def: "Polymer composed of macromolecules consisting of a single-strand main chain and many ring units\, each having one atom in common with the main chain."
comment: "A cardo polymer can also be defined as a polymer composed of macromolecules containing loop-like cyclic side groups, one ring atom of which is part of the backbone."
comment: "A cardo polymer can be represented graphically as follows: "
comment: "The adjective "cardo" is derived from the Latin word for heart because the cyclic unit, together with adjacent parts of the main chain, resembles the shape of a heart with arteries."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15310
name: catenane polymer
def: "Polymer composed of macromolecules consisting of physically catenated macrorings that have no atom in common and cannot be separated unless chemical bonds are broken."
comment: "A catenane polymer can be a linear, branched, or network polymer."
comment: "A catenane polymer can be graphically represented as follows: "
comment: "A catenane-polymer main chain resembles a jewelry or technical chain of physically interlocked rings."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15311
name: helical polymer
def: "Polymer composed of macromolecules that adopt partly or completely a helical conformation."
comment: "A helical structure is generated by regularly repeating rotations around the backbone bonds of a linear macromolecule."
comment: "Biopolymers such as nucleic acids, amylose, and some proteins are typical helical polymers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15312
name: activity coefficient at infinite dilution
def: "For a substance \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\)\, activity coefficient \\\(f_\{\\ce\{B\}\}\\\) extrapolated to infinite dilution\: \\\[\\ln \(f_\{\\ce\{B\}\}^\{\\infty\}\) = \\lim \\limits_\{x_\{\\ce\{B\}\} \\to 0\} \(\\frac\{\\mu_\{\\ce\{B\}\} - \\mu_\{\\ce\{B\}\}^\{\\ast\}\}\{RT\} - \\ln x_\{\\ce\{B\}\}\)\\\]"
comment: "The relation between the activity coefficient at infinite dilution and the standard chemical potentials is, for a solute \(\ce{B}\) in a solvent \(\ce{A}\), \[\ln f_{\ce{B}}^{\infty} = \frac{\mu_{m,\ce{B}}^{_{^⦵\!}} - \mu_{\ce{B}}^{\ast}}{RT} - \ln (M_{\ce{A}}m_{\ce{B}}^{_{^⦵\!}})\] where \(M_{\ce{A}}\) is the molar mass of the solvent."
comment: "Useful for dilute mixtures as an alternative to the standard chemical potential on a molality basis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15333
consider: goldbook:16270

[Term]
id: goldbook:15313
name: analytical method
def: "Class of experimental procedures for solubility determination in which a saturated solution is prepared and then analyzed to determine composition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15364

[Term]
id: goldbook:15314
name: aquamolality
def: "For a solute \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\) in a system containing solvent \\\(\\ce\{A\}\\\) and a reference solvent \\\(\\ce\{C\}\\\)\, \\\[m_\{\\ce\{B\}\}^\{\(\\ce\{C\}\)\} = m_\{\\ce\{B\}\} \\overline M/M_\{\\ce\{C\}\}\\\] where \\\(m_\{\\ce\{B\}\}\\\) is the molality of \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\)\, \\\(M_\{\\ce\{C\}\}\\\) is the molar mass of a reference component\, and \\\(\\overline\{M\}\\\) is the average molar mass of a mixed solvent\, defined for a system containing two solvents as \\\[\\overline M = x_\{ u\,\\ce\{A\}\} M_\{\\ce\{A\}\} + \(1 - x_\{ u\,\\ce\{A\}\}\) M_\{\\ce\{C\}\}\\\] the solvent amount fraction of solvent \\\(\\ce\{A\}\\\)."
comment: "Used most frequently in discussing comparative solubilities in water (\(\ce{C}\)) and heavy water (\(\ce{A}\)) and their mixtures, but applies to any reference component, where solvomolality is a more appropriate term."
synonym: "solvomolality" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15376

[Term]
id: goldbook:15315
