[Term]
id: goldbook:15320
name: coexistence curve
def: "Boundary of stable phase separation \(limits of solubility\) in a liquid or solid system of two or more components."
comment: "In a binary system, a plot of experimental variables such as temperature or pressure, or of theoretical variables such as Gibbs energy, against mole fraction displays the coexistence curve. In ternary or higher-order systems, coexistence curves are displayed on a plot of composition at constant temperature or pressure, usually on a ternary diagram."
comment: "The locus of the compositions of two co-existing phases on a phase diagram."
synonym: "binodal curve" []
synonym: "conodal curve" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
