[Term]
id: goldbook:15338
name: mass solubility
def: "Obsolete term for molality of a saturated solution of a gas."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15339
name: metatectic reaction
def: "Isothermal reversible reaction of a solid mixture phase \\\(\\upbeta\\\) which is transformed into a different solid phase \\\(\\upalpha\\\) plus a liquid phase \\\(\\ce\{l\}\\\) during cooling of a system. For a binary system\, \\\[\\ce\{\\upbeta  \\upalpha + 1\}\\\] where the forward arrow indicates the direction of cooling. The equilibrium transformation occurs along the metatectic line characterized by the metatectic temperature. The metatectic composition and temperature\, isobaric invariants of the system\, define the metatectic point\, which lies between the compositions of liquid \\\(\\ce\{l\}\\\) and solid phase \\\(\\upalpha\\\)."
comment: "From Greek μετα-, referring to position of melting relative to eutectectic and monotectic + -τηκτος, fusible."
comment: "Occasionally, a similar reaction takes place in the subsolidus region. Quite appropriately, it is called metatectoid reaction."
comment: "The alternate name catatectic reaction, from Greek κατα, down + -τηκτος, fusible has been suggested to emphasize the phenomenon of melting during cooling."
synonym: "catatectic reaction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15316
consider: goldbook:16270

[Term]
id: goldbook:15340
name: mole percent
def: "Deprecated term that includes both a quantity and a unit. Replace by mole fraction expressed as percent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15341
name: mole ratio
def: "Amount of one constituent divided by the amount of a second constituent in the same system. For constituents 1 and 2\, \\\[r_\{12\} = n_\{1\}/n_\{2\}\\\]"
synonym: "amount ratio" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
