[Term]
id: goldbook:15346
name: phase diagram
def: "Graphical representation\, by use of points\, lines\, and surfaces\, of the phases present at chemical equilibrium in unary\, binary\, ternary\, and higher-order systems containing two or more phases."
comment: "Phase diagrams may employ any pairs of the variables temperature, pressure, and compositions of various phases. Thus, temperature-composition and pressure-composition phase diagrams are possible, as well as diagrams showing only compositions under isothermal or isobaric conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
