[Term]
id: goldbook:15347
name: Poynting correction
def: "Factor used to convert experimentally determined Henry’s law constants at the saturation vapor pressure of the solvent \\\(\\ce\{A\}\\\)\, \\\(p_\{\\ce\{A\}\}^\{\\ast\}\\\)\, to a reference pressure \\\(p\\\) \\\[\\begin\{array\}\{c\} I_\{\\rm\{p\}\} = \\int_\{p_\{\\ce\{A\}\}^\{\\ast\}\}^p \\frac\{V_\{\\ce\{B\}\}^\{\\infty \{\\rm\{l\}\}\}\}\{RT\}\{\\rm\{d\}\}p \\\\ k_\{\\rm\{H\}\,\\ce\{B\}\}\(p\) = k_\{\\rm\{H\}\,\\ce\{B\}\}\(p^\{\\ast\}\) \\exp \\left\[I_\{\\rm\{p\}\}\(p\) \\right\]\\end\{array\}\\\] is the partial molar volume of liquid \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\) at infinite dilution in solvent \\\(\\ce\{A\}\\\). The second equation gives the relation between the two Henry’s law constants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15348
name: primary data
def: "Data reported in peer-reviewed scientific reports of original research which allow an assessment of data quality."
comment: "Primary data are distinguished from secondary data appearing in reviews, handbooks, compendia, etc. which hold the possibility of error and bias through transcription error, incomplete coverage of the primary literature, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15323

[Term]
id: goldbook:15349
name: Raoult’s law
def: "Fugacity \(\\\(\\tilde\{p\}_\{\\ce\{B\}\}\\\)\) of a gaseous component \(\\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\)\) in equilibrium with a liquid or solid mixture containing \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\) is directly proportional to the activity \(\\\(a_\{\\ce\{B\}\}\\\)\) of the component in the mixture \\\[\\tilde\{p\}_\{\\ce\{B\}\} = \\tilde\{p\}_\{\\ce\{B\}\}^\{\\ast\} f_\{\\ce\{B\}\} x_\{\\ce\{B\}\}\\\] where \\\(f_\{\\ce\{B\}\}\\\) is the activity coefficient of \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\) referenced to Raoult’s law at mole fraction \\\(x_\{\\ce\{B\}\}\\\) and \\\(\\tilde\{p\}_\{\\ce\{B\}\}\\\) is the fugacity of pure \\\(\\ce\{B\}\\\)."
comment: "An ideal mixture is defined by replacing fugacities with partial pressures and setting the activity coefficient equal to unity \[p_{\ce{B}} = p_{\ce{B}}^{\ast} x_{\ce{B}} = y_{\ce{B}}p\] The total pressure, \(p\), is then simply the sum of the partial pressures of all components."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16270

[Term]
id: goldbook:15350
name: reciprocal salt system
def: "System containing \\\(n\\\) ionic species with or without a single solvent. Because of electrical neutrality\, the system has \\\(n\\\) components in an aqueous system with a single solvent and \\\(n - 1\\\) components in a molten salt system."
comment: "Ternary aqueous systems containing a common ion can be considered as a limiting case of this class of system, where there is only one cation or one anion. For example, \[\ce{Na^{+},Zn^{2+} \Vert\ SO4^{2-} + H2O}\]"
comment: "There is a special notation for reciprocal salt systems that involves use of double vertical bars. All ionic species are specified. For example, \[\ce{K^{+},Na^{+} \Vert\ Cl^{-},NO3^{-} + H2O}\] denotes a four-component (quaternary) aqueous reciprocal salt system in which each cation can combine with each anion to produce anhydrous, hydrated, binary, or ternary solid components; i.e., the solution may become saturated with respect to any one of \(\ce{KCl}\), \(\ce{NaCl}\), \(\ce{KNO3}\), \(\ce{NaNO3}\), their hydrates, or anhydrous or hydrated binary compounds of the simple salts."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15351
name: reduced pressure
def: "Pressure divided by the critical pressure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15352
name: reduced temperature
def: "Temperature divided by the critical temperature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15353
name: reference data
def: "Data that are critically evaluated and verified\, obtained from an identified source\, and related to a property of a phenomenon\, body\, or substance\, or a system of components of known composition and structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020233
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
