[Term]
id: goldbook:15385
name: ceiling temperature
def: "Temperature above which\, in a given chain polymerization\, polymer of high molar mass is not formed."
comment: "A ceiling temperature is only observed for enthalpy-driven chain polymerizations in which \(\Delta H_{\rm{m}} \lt 0\) and \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}} \lt 0\), where \(\Delta H_{\rm{m}}\) and \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}}\) are respectively the enthalpy and entropy change per mole of monomer reacted."
comment: "Because \(\Delta G_{\rm{m}} = 0\) at the ceiling temperature, \(T_{\rm{c}} = \Delta H_{\rm{m}}/\Delta S_{\rm{m}}\). If \(\Delta H_{\rm{m}}^{\circ}\) and \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}}^{\circ}\) are the enthalpy and entropy changes in the standard state, and the monomer behaves ideally, then \[T_{\rm{c}} = \Delta H_{\rm{m}}^{\circ}/\{\Delta S_{\rm{m}}^{\circ} + R\ln ([{\rm{M}}]_{0}/c^{\circ})\}\] where \(c^{\circ} = \pu{1 mol dm-3}\) is the standard concentration and \([{\rm{M}}]_{0}\) is the initial monomer concentration. Thus, \(T_{\rm{c}}\) depends on the initial monomer concentration."
comment: "Below \(T_{\rm{c}}\), \(\Delta G_{\rm{m}} (= \Delta H_{\rm{m}} - T\Delta S_{\rm{m}}) \lt 0\); at \(T_{\rm{c}}\), \(\Delta G_{\rm{m}} = 0\); and above \(T_{\rm{c}}\), \(\Delta G_{\rm{m}} \gt 0\)."
comment: "For most chain polymerizations, \(\Delta H_{\rm{m}} \lt 0\) and \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}} \lt 0\)."
comment: "The symbol \(T_{\rm{c}}(c^{\circ})\) is used to denote the ceiling temperature when the initial monomer concentration, \([{\rm{M}}]_{0}\), is equal to \(c^{\circ}\)."
comment: "The symbol \(T_{\rm{c}}({\rm{bulk}})\) is used to denote the ceiling temperature when the initial monomer concentration is equal to its undiluted concentration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15401

[Term]
id: goldbook:15386
name: chain copolymerisation
def: "Chain polymerization in which a copolymer is formed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15387
name: chain depropagation
def: "Chemical reaction that results in the formation of a monomer molecule at an active center on the terminal unit of a chain carrier and decreases the degree of polymerization of the chain carrier by one."
comment: "Chain depropagation is the reverse of chain propagation."
synonym: "depropagation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15426

[Term]
id: goldbook:15388
name: chain-end reactivity ratio
def: "In a binary copolymerization\, the ratio of two rate constants defining the relative activity of an active center on a given type of terminal unit of a chain carrier toward one type of monomer\, in the two cases where the penultimate unit of the chain carrier is identical to and different from the terminal unit."
comment: "The chain-end reactivity ratios are expressed mathematically by the equations \[s_{1} = k_{211}/k_{111};\ s_{2} = k_{122}/k_{222}\]."
comment: "The monomer reactivity ratios, defined in accordance with the penultimate-unit effect, are \[r_{112} = k_{111}/k_{112};\ r_{212} = k_{211}/k_{212};\ r_{221} = k_{222}/k_{221};\ r_{121} = k_{122}/k_{121}\]. The symbols for the monomer reactivity ratios are often abbreviated to \(r_{1}\), \(r_{1}^{\prime}\), \(r_{2}\), \(r_{2}^{\prime}\), respectively (see monomer reactivity ratios for the definitions of \(r_{1}\) and \(r_{2}\) ignoring the penultimate-unit effect)."
comment: "The reactions involved are defined in accordance with the penultimate-unit effect, namely, \[\begin{array}{l} ...-{\rm{m}}_{11}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{1}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{111}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{11}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{21}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{1}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{211}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{11}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{11}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{2}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{112}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{12}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{21}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{2}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{212}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{12}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{12}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{1}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{121}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{21}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{22}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{1}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{221}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{21}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{12}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{2}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{122}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{22}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{22}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{2}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{222}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{22}^{\ast}, \end{array}\] where \({\rm{M}}_{1}\) and \({\rm{M}}_{2}\) are the two monomers involved in the binary copolymerization and \(-{\rm{m}}_{ij}^{\ast} (i,j = 1,2)\) denotes a chain carrier having an active site on its terminal monomer unit of type \({\rm{M}}_{j}\) and having the adjacent, penultimate monomer unit of type \({\rm{M}}_{i}\) (see chain carrier)."
synonym: "radical reactivity ratio" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15383
consider: goldbook:15410
consider: goldbook:15413

[Term]
id: goldbook:15389
name: chain-transfer constant
def: "In a homopolymerization\, rate constant for chain transfer\, \\\(k_\{\\rm\{tr\}\}\\\)\, divided by the rate constant for chain propagation\, \\\(k_\{\\rm\{p\}\}\\\)\, i.e.\, \\\(C_\{\\rm\{tr\}\} = k_\{\\rm\{tr\}\}/k_\{\\rm\{p\}\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15390
name: comonomer
def: "Monomer used in copolymerization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15391
name: copolymerisation composition equation
def: "Equation relating the instantaneous composition of a binary copolymer to the monomer reactivity ratios and the ratio of instantaneous monomer concentrations."
comment: "Integrated forms of the copolymer composition equation have been developed to relate polymer composition to monomer reactivity ratios and monomer conversions."
comment: "See also chain-end reactivity ratio, monomer reactivity ratios."
comment: "The copolymer composition equation is known also as the Mayo–Lewis equation."
comment: "The instantaneous composition of copolymer generally changes during the course of a copolymerization due to the changing composition of the monomer mixture (but see azeotropic polymerization)."
synonym: "Mayo–Lewis equation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15381
consider: goldbook:15388
consider: goldbook:15410

[Term]
id: goldbook:15392
name: coupling reaction
def: "Linking of two macromolecules through chemical reaction."
comment: "The coupling may proceed with or without interaction with an added coupling agent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15393
name: cross-propagation
def: "Propagation reaction in a copolymerization in which a chain carrier\, bearing at its active end a monomer unit of one kind\, reacts with a monomer molecule of another kind."
comment: "The recommended symbol for the rate constant of cross-propagation in a binary copolymerization is \(k_{ij}\) , in which \(i\) and \(j\) refer to (a) the type of terminal monomer unit of the chain carrier and (b) the reacting monomer molecule, respectively."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15383

[Term]
id: goldbook:15394
name: cross-termination
def: "Termination reaction in a copolymerization between two chain carriers with different chemical structures."
comment: "Cross-termination may occur by combination or disproportionation."
comment: "Usually only the chemical structures of the units at the active centers are considered."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15395
name: dead-end polymerisation
def: "Radical polymerization that stops\, as a consequence of the depletion of the initiator\, before the monomer has reacted fully."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15396
name: degradative chain transfer
def: "Chain transfer reaction that generates a new chain carrier of much lower reactivity than that of the original chain carrier."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15397
name: diffusion-controlled termination
def: "Chain termination in a chain polymerization in which the rate-determining step is a diffusion process."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15398
name: end-capping
def: "Reaction in which end-groups of a desired structure are intentionally formed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15399
name: enthalpy of polymerisation
def: "Change of enthalpy\, in a chain polymerization forming a homopolymer\, associated with the conversion of one mole of monomer into polymer under isobaric and isothermal conditions."
comment: "The subscripts in \(\Delta_{\rm{ab}} H_{\rm{m}}\) denote (a) the state of the monomer and (b) the state of polymer, as follows: g: gaseous state (hypothetical in the case of polymer);l: liquid state (must be specified in the case of a mesophase);s: in solution (solvent and mesophases, if any, must be specified);c: (condensed) amorphous, glassy states;c′: crystalline or partly crystalline state; e.g., \(\Delta_{\rm{lc}} H_{\rm{m}}\) means: from liquid state to amorphous or glassy state; \(\Delta_{\rm{ss}} H_{\rm{m}}\) means: from monomer in solvent to polymer in solvent."
comment: "The symbol \(\Delta H_{\rm{ab}}\), in common usage in polymer chemistry, is discouraged as the IUPAC-recommended symbol is \(\Delta_{\rm{ab}} H_{\rm{m}}\)."
comment: "Under defined standard conditions the enthalpy of polymerization is designated \(\Delta H_{\rm{m}}^{\circ}\)."
synonym: "molar enthalpy of polymerization" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15400
name: entropy of polymerisation
def: "Change of entropy\, in a chain polymerization forming a homopolymer\, associated with the conversion of one mole of monomer into polymer under isobaric and isothermal conditions."
comment: "The subscripts in \(\Delta_{\rm{ab}} S_{\rm{m}}\) denote the state of the monomer (a) and the state of polymer (b) (see enthalpy of polymerization (Note 2))."
comment: "Under defined standard conditions, the entropy of polymerization is designated \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}}^{\circ}\); thus, if the standard state refers to standard concentration, and the monomer behaves ideally, \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}} = \Delta S_{\rm{m}}^{\circ} + R\ln ([{\rm{M]}}_{0}/c^{\circ})\), where \([{\rm{M}}]_{0}\) denotes the starting monomer concentration and \(c^{\circ} = \pu{1 mol dm-3}\) is the standard concentration."
synonym: "molar entropy of polymerization" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15399

[Term]
id: goldbook:15401
name: floor temperature
def: "Temperature below which\, in a given chain polymerization\, polymer of high molar mass is not formed."
comment: "A floor temperature is only observed for entropy-driven chain polymerizations in which \(\Delta H_{\rm{m}} \gt 0\) and \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}} \gt 0\), where \(\Delta H_{\rm{m}}\) and \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}}\) are respectively the enthalpy and entropy change per mole of monomer reacted."
comment: "Above \(T_{\rm{f}}\), \(\Delta G_{\rm{m}} (= \Delta H_{\rm{m}} - T \Delta H_{\rm{m}}) \lt 0\); at \(T_{\rm{f}}\), \(\Delta G_{\rm{m}} = 0\); and below \(T_{\rm{f}}\), \(\Delta G_{\rm{m}} \gt 0\)."
comment: "Because \(\Delta G_{\rm{m}} = 0\) at the floor temperature, \(T_{\rm{f}} = \Delta H_{\rm{m}}/\Delta S_{\rm{m}}\). If \(\Delta H_{\rm{m}}^{\circ}\) and \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}}^{\circ}\) are the enthalpy and entropy changes in the standard state, and the monomer behaves ideally, then \[T_{\rm{f}} = \Delta H_{\rm{m}}^{\circ}/ \{\Delta S_{\rm{m}}^{\circ} + R\ln ([{\rm{M]}}_{0}/c^{\circ})\}\] where \(c^{\circ} = \pu{1 mol dm-3}\) is the standard concentration and \([{\rm{M}}]_{0}\) is the initial monomer concentration. Thus, \(T_{\rm{f}}\) depends on the initial monomer concentration."
comment: "Examples of chain polymerizations for which \(\Delta H_{\rm{m}} \gt 0\) and \(\Delta S_{\rm{m}} \gt 0\) are polymerizations of larger cyclic monomers, e.g., elemental sulfur (\(\ce{S8}\)) and octamethylcyclotetrasiloxane [2,2,4,4,6,6,8,8-octamethyl-1,3,5,7,2,4,6,8-tetraoxatetrasilocane], proceeding via ring-opening mechanisms."
comment: "The symbol \(T_{\rm{f}}(c^{\circ})\) is used to denote the floor temperature when the initial monomer concentration, \([{\rm{M}}]_{0}\), is equal to \(c^{\circ}\)."
comment: "The symbol \(T_{\rm{f}}({\rm{bulk}})\) is used to denote the floor temperature when the initial monomer concentration is equal to its undiluted concentration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15385

[Term]
id: goldbook:15402
name: free ion
def: "Ion whose behavior is independent of the influence of a counterion."
comment: "A free ion is a distinct kinetic entity, and its reactivity is usually different from that of an ion pair."
comment: "The behavior of a free ion may still be influenced by neighboring atoms or molecules."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15403
name: heat of polymerisation
def: "Heat absorbed or given off from the conversion of a specified amount of monomer into polymer."
comment: "The molar heat of polymerization is denoted by the symbol \(Q_{\rm{m}}\) and is the heat of polymerization of one mole of monomer. SI unit: \(\pu{J mol-1}\)."
comment: "The molar heat of polymerization is equal to the enthalpy of polymerization under isobaric and isothermal conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15399

[Term]
id: goldbook:15404
name: homopropagation
def: "Addition of a monomer to a chain carrier bearing a terminal group derived from the same monomer species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15405
name: ideal binary copolymerisation
def: "Binary copolymerization in which the relative rates of incorporation of the two types of monomer into the copolymer are independent of the nature of the monomer unit at the end of a propagating chain."
comment: "In an ideal binary copolymerization, \(k_{11}/k_{21} = k_{12}/k_{22}\) and \(r_{12} r_{21} = 1\). See monomer reactivity ratios."
comment: "In the special case of an ideal binary copolymerization in which \(r_{12} = r_{21} = 1\), the two monomers show equal reactivities toward both types of propagating species. Thus, \(k_{11} = k_{21}\) and \(k_{12} = k_{22}\). Hence, copolymerization of a mixture of two monomers with any ratio of monomer concentrations in the monomer feed gives rise to a copolymer in which the molar ratio of monomer units is identical to that in the monomer feed. (See also azeotropic copolymerization.)"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15381
consider: goldbook:15383
consider: goldbook:15410

[Term]
id: goldbook:15406
name: ideal copolymerisation
def: "Copolymerization in which all types of propagating species show the same relative reactivity toward the monomers present."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15407
name: interfacial polycondensation
def: "Polycondensation involving two monomers separately dissolved in immiscible solvents\, forming a twophase system\, with polycondensation taking place at \(or near\) an interface between the two phases."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15408
name: intermolecular chain transfer
def: "Chain transfer from an active center on a macromolecule to a different macromolecule."
comment: "An active center may be located anywhere along a macromolecular chain."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15382

[Term]
id: goldbook:15409
name: kinetic-chain length
def: "In a chain polymerization\, the rate of chain propagation divided by the sum of the rates of all of the chain-termination processes."
comment: "Chain-termination processes include termination by combination or disproportionation but do not include chain transfer."
comment: "In the absence of chain transfer, the kinetic-chain length will be equal to the degree of polymerization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15410
name: monomer reactivity ratios
def: "In binary copolymerization\, \(a\) the ratio \(\\\(r_\{12\}\\\)\) of the rate constant \(\\\(k_\{11\}\\\)\) for the homopropagation of monomer \\\(\\rm\{M\}_\{1\}\\\) to the rate constant \(\\\(k_\{12\}\\\)\) for the cross-propagation of the chain carrier \\\(\\ldots -\{\\rm\{m\}\}_\{1\}^\{\\ast\}\\\) with the monomer \\\(\\rm\{M\}_\{2\}\\\) and \(b\) the ratio \(\\\(r_\{21\}\\\)\) of the rate constant \(\\\(k_\{22\}\\\)\) for the homopropagation of monomer \\\(\\rm\{M\}_\{2\}\\\) to the rate constant for the cross-propagation \(\\\(k_\{21\}\\\)\) of the chain carrier \\\(\\ldots -\{\\rm\{m\}\}_\{2\}^\{\\ast\}\\\) with monomer \\\(\\rm\{M\}_\{1\}\\\). Thus\, \\\(r_\{12\} = k_\{11\}/k_\{12\}\, r_\{21\} = k_\{22\}/k_\{21\}\\\)."
comment: "The present definition ignores the penultimate-unit effect. For the definition of monomer reactivity ratios accounting for the penultimate-unit effect, see chain-end reactivity ratios (Note 3)."
comment: "The reactions involved are \[\begin{array}{l} ...-{\rm{m}}_{1}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{1}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{11}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{1}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{1}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{2}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{12}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{2}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{2}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{2}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{22}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{2}^{\ast} \\ ...-{\rm{m}}_{2}^{\ast} + {\rm{M}}_{1}\ce{->[\textit{k}_{21}]} ...-{\rm{m}}_{1}^{\ast} \\ \end{array}\] where \(\rm{M}_{1}\) and \(\rm{M}_{2}\) are the two monomers involved in the binary copolymerization and \(\ldots -{\rm{m}}_{i}^{\ast} (i = 1,2)\) denotes a chain carrier having an active site on its terminal monomer unit of type \({\rm{M}}_{i}\)."
comment: "The symbols \(r_{12}\) and \(r_{21}\) are often abbreviated to \(r_{1}\) and \(r_{2}\), respectively."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15383
consider: goldbook:15388
consider: goldbook:15393
consider: goldbook:15404
consider: goldbook:15413

[Term]
id: goldbook:15411
name: monomer reactivity scale
def: "Relative scale defined by the values of the rate constants for the addition of monomers to a reference active center."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
