[Term]
id: goldbook:15412
name: patterns of reactivity scheme
def: "Method for the prediction of monomer reactivity ratios in binary copolymerization\, based exclusively on experimentally determined parameters."
comment: "The parameters may be the monomer reactivity ratios for the separate copolymerizations of the monomers concerned, namely, 1 and 2, with a nonpolar monomer, e.g., styrene (\(\rm{S}\)), and a polar monomer, e.g., acrylonitrile (\(\rm{A}\)). The equations for the desired monomer reactivity ratios, \(r_{12}\) and \(r_{21}\), are then as follows: \[\ln r_{12} = \ln (r_{1\rm{S}} r_{\rm{S}2}) - [\ln\,(r_{\rm{AS}} r_{\rm{S}2}/r_{\rm{A}2)}][\ln\,(r_{\rm{SA}} r_{1\rm{S}}/r_{1\rm{A}})]/\ln\,(r_{\rm{AS}} r_{\rm{SA}})\] \[\ln r_{21} = \ln (r_{2\rm{S}} r_{\rm{S}1}) - [\ln\,(r_{\rm{AS}} r_{\rm{S}1}/r_{\rm{A}1)}][\ln\,(r_{\rm{SA}} r_{2\rm{S}}/r_{2\rm{A}})]/\ln\,(r_{\rm{AS}} r_{\rm{SA}})\]"
comment: "The patterns of reactivity scheme is known also as Jenkins’ scheme."
synonym: "Jenkins’ scheme" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15383

[Term]
id: goldbook:15413
name: penultimate-unit effect
def: "Phenomenon that the penultimate monomer unit preceding the active center on the terminal unit of an active polymer chain affects the reactivity of that active center."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15388

[Term]
id: goldbook:15414
name: primary-radical termination
def: "Termination reaction involving a radical chain carrier and a primary radical."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15415
name: pulsed-laser polymerisation
def: "Polymerization initiated by successive pulses of laser light."
comment: "In a radical polymerization, PLP allows determination of the propagation rate constants."
synonym: "PLP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15416
name: <i>Q-e</i> scheme
def: "Empirical equations expressing the monomer reactivity ratios in a binary radical copolymerization\, \\\(r_\{12\}\\\) and \\\(r_\{21\}\\\)\, in terms of the empirical parameters \\\(Q\\\) and \\\(e\\\) for the two monomers\, namely\, \\\(\\rm\{Q\}_\{1\}\\\)\, \\\(\\rm\{Q\}_\{2\}\\\)\, \\\(\\rm\{e\}_\{1\}\\\)\, and \\\(\\rm\{e\}_\{2\}\\\)\, with\\\(r_\{12\} = \(Q_\{1\}/Q_\{2\}\)\\exp \[-\{e_\{1\}\}\(e_\{1\} - e_\{2\}\)\]\\\) and \\\(r_\{21\} = \(Q_\{2\}/Q_\{1\}\) \\exp \[-\{e_\{2\}\}\(e_\{2\} - e_\{1\}\)\]\\\)"
comment: "Although the parameters are empirically derived, the parameter \(Q\) is considered to be a measure of the stabilization by conjugation of a monomer and the radical derived from it, while the parameter \(e\) is considered to be a measure of the polar effects of substituents on the monomer and the radical derived from it."
comment: "The Q-e scheme is known also as the Alfrey–Price scheme."
synonym: "Alfrey–Price scheme" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15383
consider: goldbook:15410

[Term]
id: goldbook:15417
name: radical reactivity scale
def: "Scale of the values of the rate constants for the reaction of radicals with a reference monomer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15418
name: rate of polymerisation
def: "Rate of consumption of monomers in a chain polymerization\, or the rate of consumption of the functional groups in the reaction mixture of a polycondensation or polyaddition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15419
name: secondary radical
def: "Radical formed by the rearrangement or fragmentation of a primary radical that is capable of initiating a polymerization."
comment: "The term "secondary radical" is also used to designate a radical centered on a secondary carbon atom, e.g., a 2-propyl radical."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15420
name: self-initiated polymerisation
def: "Polymerization in which initiating species are formed exclusively from the monomer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15421
name: solid-state polymerisation
def: "Polymerization of a crystalline monomer."
comment: "A solid-state polymerization may lead to a semi-crystalline polymer having a crystal structure different from that of the crystalline monomer, or alternatively it may proceed as a topochemical polymerization."
comment: "Depending on the initiation mode and the structure of the monomer, a solid-state polymerization may proceed by a radical or an ionic mechanism."
comment: "The initiating species can be formed by the action of heat, irradiation of the monomer with, e.g., ultraviolet light or γ-rays, or (less frequently) by chemical initiation."
comment: "Use of the term "bulk polymerization" to describe solid-state polymerization is discouraged."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15423

[Term]
id: goldbook:15422
name: spontaneous termination
def: "Chain termination proceeding as a unimolecular process."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15423
name: topochemical polymerisation
def: "Solid-state polymerization\, resulting in the formation of a polymer having essentially the same crystal structure as that of the monomer."
comment: "A topochemical polymerization does not involve significant atomic or molecular motions."
comment: "A topochemical polymerization is usually initiated by irradiation of the crystalline monomer with, e.g., ultraviolet light, γ-rays, or by chemical initiators."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15421

[Term]
id: goldbook:15424
name: transamidation
def: "Interchange reaction involving amide groups."
comment: "Transamidations commonly occur during polycondensations to form polyamides."
synonym: "amide interchange" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15425
name: transesterification
def: "Interchange reaction involving ester groups."
comment: "Transesterifications commonly occur during polycondensations to form polyesters."
synonym: "ester interchange" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15427
name: zwitterionic copolymerisation
def: "Copolymerization that is a zwitterionic polymerization."
comment: "A zwitterionic copolymerization usually involves a nucleophilic monomer and an electrophilic monomer, and it may produce an alternating copolymer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
