[Term]
id: goldbook:15428
name: zwitterionic polymerisation
def: "Chain polymerization in which a growing macromolecule bears two ionic chain carriers of opposite signs\, at one or both of its ends."
comment: "Chains in a zwitterionic polymerization may grow from one or both of their ends."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880102163
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15429
name: cyclic macromolecule
def: "Macromolecule in which the termini of the backbone are connected to form a ring."
comment: "Linear macromolecules comprising constitutional units that include small cyclic structures [e.g., the phenylene groups in poly(ethylene terephthalate)] are not cyclic macromolecules. However, a cyclic molecule comprising such constitutional (repeating) units is a cyclic macromolecule."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15430
name: main ring
def: "Macrocycle in a bridged polycyclic macromolecule or polycyclic macromolecular portion that contains the subunits of highest seniority."
comment: "In macrocyclic molecules with macrocyclic substituents, the ring that contains the subunits of highest seniority is called the parent macrocycle or macrocyclic system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15432

[Term]
id: goldbook:15431
name: path length
def: "Number of polymer main-chain \(backbone\) atoms between two subunits."
comment: "Where a ring or ring system constitutes all or part of a path between two subunits, the shortest continuous chain of atoms in the ring or ring system is selected."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15432
name: polycyclic macromolecule
def: "Molecule that includes more than one macrocycle\, all of which have at least one atom in common with another macrocycle."
comment: ""Multicyclic" or "pluricyclic" have been proposed as alternative terms for polycyclic. In accordance with nomenclature of organic chemistry, the term "polycyclic" is used here, since it does not lead to confusion with respect to "poly" in polymer. Therefore, the use of "multicyclic" or "pluricyclic" is discouraged as an alternative for "polycyclic"."
comment: "Molecules that have two rings without any common atom are not considered polycyclic, e.g., biphenyl. In general terminology, however, they are often regarded as polycyclic."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200880020201
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15433
name: abiotic degradation
def: "Process in which a substance is converted to simpler products by physical or chemical mechanisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15434
name: abortifacient
def: "Substance that causes pregnancy to end prematurely and causes an abortion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15435
name: abuse
def: "Improper use of drugs or other substances."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15436
name: acaricide
def: "Substance intended to kill mites\, ticks\, or other Acaridae."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15437
name: acceptable residue level
def: "Acceptable concentration of a residue that has been established for an antibiotic found in human or animal foods."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15438
name: acceptable risk
def: "Probability of suffering disease or injury that is considered to be sufficiently small to be 'negligible'."
comment: "Calculated risk of an increase of one case in a million people per year for cancer is usually considered to be negligible."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15439
name: accepted risk
def: "Probability of suffering disease or injury that is accepted by an individual."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15440
name: accidental exposure
def: "Unintended contact with a substance or change in the physical environment \(including\, e.g.\, radiation\) resulting from an accident."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15441
name: acid dissociation constant
def: "Equilibrium constant for the following reaction of an acid \\\(\\ce\{HB\}\\\)\: \\\[\\begin\{gathered\} \\ce\{HB\(aq\)  H^\{+\}\(aq\) + B^\{-\}\(aq\)\} \\\\ K_\{\\rm\{a\}\} = \[\\ce\{H^\{+\}\}\]\[\\ce\{B^\{-\}\}\]/\[\\ce\{HB\}\]c^\{\\rm\{o\}\} \\end\{gathered\}\\\] where \\\(c^\{\\rm\{o\}\} = \\pu\{1 mol L-1\}\\\) is the standard amount concentration and activity coefficients have been neglected."
comment: "Because this constant differs for each acid and varies over many degrees of magnitude, the acidity constant is often represented by the additive inverse of its common logarithm, represented by the symbol \(\pu{p}K_{\rm{a}}\) (using the same mathematical relationship as [\(\ce{H^{+}}\)] is to \(\rm{pH}\)), viz.: \[\pu{p}K_{\rm{a}} = -\log_{10}K_{\rm{a}}\] In general, a larger value of \(K_{\rm{a}}\) (or a smaller value of \(\pu{p}K_{\rm{a}}\)) indicates a stronger acid, since the extent of dissociation is larger at the same concentration."
comment: "This constant, because activity coefficients are neglected, is valid at a specified ionic strength. The thermodynamic dissociation constant is found by suitable extrapolation of the conditional constant to zero ionic strength. Note that it is defined as a dimensionless quantity, but sometimes it is given dimensions by omitting the standard amount concentration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15442
name: action level
def: "Concentration of a substance in air\, soil\, water\, or other defined medium at which specified emergency counter-measures\, such as the seizure and destruction of contaminated materials\, evacuation of the local population or closing down the sources of pollution\, are to be taken. Concentration of a pollutant in air\, soil\, water\, or other defined medium at which some kind of preventive action \(not necessarily of an emergency nature\) is to be taken."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15443
name: active ingredient
def: "Component of a mixture responsible for the biological effects of the mixture."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15815

[Term]
id: goldbook:15444
name: active metabolite
def: "Metabolite causing biological and \(or\) toxicological effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15445
name: acute toxicity test
def: "Study in which organisms are observed during only a short part of the life span and in which there is often only a single exposure to the test agent at the beginning of the study."
synonym: "short-term toxicity test" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15559

[Term]
id: goldbook:15446
name: adaptation
def: "Change in an organism\, in response to changing conditions of the environment \(specifically chemical\)\, which takes place without any irreversible disruptions of the given biological system and without exceeding normal \(homeostatic\) capacities of its response. Process by which an organism stabilizes its physiological condition after an environmental change.Note\: If this process exceeds the homeostatic range\, it becomes pathological and results in symptoms of disease \(adverse effects\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15447
name: added risk
def: "Difference between the incidence of an adverse effect in a treated group \(of organisms or a group of exposed humans\) and a control group \(of the same organisms or the spontaneous incidence in humans\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15695

[Term]
id: goldbook:15448
name: adverse event
def: "Occurrence that causes an adverse effect."
comment: "An adverse event in clinical studies is any untoward reaction in a human subject participating in a research project; such an adverse event, which may be a psychological reaction, must be reported to an institutional review board."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15449
name: aerodynamic diameter
def: "Diameter of a spherical particle with relative density equal to unity that has the same settling velocity in air as the particle in question."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15450
name: after-effect of a poison
def: "Ability of a poison to produce a change in an organism after cessation of contact."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15451
name: age sensitivity
def: "Quantitative and qualitative age dependence of an effect."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15452
name: air pollution control system
def: "Network of organizations that monitor air pollution. Group of measures or processes used to minimize or prevent air pollution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15453
name: albuminuria
def: "Presence of albumin\, derived from plasma\, in the urine."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15454
name: alkylating agent
def: "Substance that introduces an alkyl substituent into a compound."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15455
name: allometric growth
def: "Regular and systematic pattern of growth such that the mass or size of any organ or part of a body can be expressed in relation to the total mass or size of the entire organism according to the allometric equation\: \\\[Y = b\{x^\{\\alpha\}\}\\\] where \\\(Y\\\) = mass of the organ\, \\\(x\\\) = mass of the organism\, \\\(\\alpha\\\) = growth coefficient of the organ\, and \\\(b\\\) is a constant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15456
name: allometric scaling
def: "Adjustment of data to allow for change in proportion between an organ or organs and other body parts during the growth of an organism. Adjustment of data to allow for differences and make comparisons between species having dissimilar characteristics \(e.g.\, in size\, shape\, and metabolism\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15457
name: allometry
def: "Measurement of the rate of growth of a part or parts of an organism relative to the growth of the whole organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15458
name: allomone
def: "Semiochemical that is produced by an organism inducing a response in an organism of another species that is favorable to the emitter."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15841
consider: goldbook:16082
consider: goldbook:16124

[Term]
id: goldbook:15459
name: analytic study
def: "Study designed to examine associations\, commonly putative or hypothesized causal relationships."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15460
name: anaplasia
def: "Loss of normal cell differentiation\, a feature characteristic of most malignancies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15461
name: anthracosis
def: "Form of pneumoconiosis caused by accumulation of anthracite carbon deposits in the lungs due to inhalation of smoke or coal dust."
synonym: "coal miners’ pneumoconiosis" []
