property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15507
name: biochemical mechanism
def: "Reaction or series of reactions\, usually enzyme-catalyzed\, associated with a specific physiological event in a living organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15508
name: bioelimination
def: "Removal\, usually from the aqueous phase\, of a test substance in the presence of living organisms by biological processes supplemented by physicochemical reactions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15509
name: bioinactivation
def: "Metabolic conversion of a xenobiotic to a less toxic derivative."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15550

[Term]
id: goldbook:15510
name: biokinetics
def: "Science of the movements involved in the distribution of substances."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15511
name: biological cycle
def: "Complete circulatory process through which a substance passes in the biosphere. It may involve transport through the various media \(air\, water\, soil\)\, followed by environmental transformation\, and carriage through various ecosystems."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15512
name: biological preparation
def: "Compound derived from living organisms and their products for use in medicine or as a pesticide\, etc."
synonym: "biopreparation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15513
name: biological specimen
def: "Organ\, tissue \(including blood\)\, secretion\, or excretion product taken from an organism as a sample reflecting the state of the whole organism. Organism taken as a sample reflecting the state of a population or their environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15514
name: biological warfare
def: "Military operations using any organism \(bacteria\, virus\, or other disease-causing organism\) or toxin found in nature\, to kill\, injure\, or incapacitate human beings\, animals\, or plants."
synonym: "germ warfare" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15515
name: biopsy
def: "Excision of a small piece of living tissue for microscopic or biochemical examination; usually performed to establish a diagnosis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15516
name: biostatic
def: "Adjective applied to a substance that arrests the growth or multiplication of living organisms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15517
name: biota
def: "All living organisms as a totality."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15518
name: 2\,3-bis\(sulfanyl\)propan-1-ol
def: "Metal chelator that has been used in the treatment of arsenic\, antimony\, gold\, mercury\, and lead poisoning."
synonym: "2" []
synonym: "3-dimercaptopropan-1-ol" []
synonym: "British anti-Lewisite" []
synonym: "dimercaprol" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15519
name: bolus
def: "Single dose of a substance\, originally a large pill. Dose of a substance administered by a single rapid intravenous injection. Concentrated mass of food ready to be swallowed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15520
name: botanical pesticide
def: "Substance with activity against pests\, that is produced naturally within a plant and may act as a defense against predators."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15521
name: botulism
def: "Acute food poisoning caused by botulinum toxin produced in food by the bacterium Clostridium botulinum and characterized by muscle weakness and paralysis; disturbances of vision\, swallowing\, and speech; and a high mortality rate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15522
name: brady-
def: "Prefix meaning slow as in bradycardia or bradypnoea."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15523
consider: goldbook:16127

[Term]
id: goldbook:15523
name: bradypnoea
def: "Abnormally slow breathing."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16128

[Term]
id: goldbook:15524
name: breathing zone
def: "Space within a radius of \\\(\\pu\{0.5 m\}\\\) from a person’s face."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15525
name: bronchoconstriction
def: "Narrowing of the air passages through the bronchi of the lungs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15526

[Term]
id: goldbook:15526
name: bronchodilation
def: "Expansion of the air passages through the bronchi of the lungs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15525

[Term]
id: goldbook:15527
name: bronchospasm
def: "Intermittent violent contraction of the air passages of the lungs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15528
name: builder
def: "Material that enhances or maintains the cleaning efficiency of a surfactant\, in a detergent\, principally by inactivating water hardness; complex phosphates \(especially sodium tripolyphosphate\, i.e.\, pentasodium triphosphate\)\, sodium carbonate\, and sodium silicate are the builders most commonly used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15529
name: byssinosis
def: "Pneumoconiosis caused by inhalation of dust and associated microbial contaminants and observed in cotton\, flax\, and hemp workers."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15984

[Term]
id: goldbook:15530
name: bystander exposure
def: "Liability of members of the general public to come in contact with substances arising from operations or processes carried out by other individuals in their vicinity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15531
name: cacosmia
def: "Imagined perception of vile odors\, including coprosmia \(smelling feces\) and necrosmia \(the smell of death\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15532
name: calcification
def: "Form of mineralization in which organic tissue becomes hardened by deposition of calcium salts within its substance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15533
name: carbonylhemoglobin
def: "Compound that is formed between carbon monoxide and hemoglobin in the blood of animals and humans and is incapable of transporting oxygen."
synonym: "carboxyhemoglobin" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15534
name: carcinogenicity test
def: "Long-term \(chronic\) test designed to detect any possible carcinogenic effect of a test substance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15535
name: cardiotoxic
def: "Chemically harmful to the cells of the heart."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15536
name: carrier-linked prodrug
def: "Compound that contains a temporary linkage between a given active substance and a transient carrier group\, the latter producing improved physicochemical or pharmacokinetic properties and easily removable in vivo."
synonym: "carrier prodrug" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15537
name: carrier substance
def: "Substance that binds to another substance and transfers it from one site to another."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15538
name: case cohort study
def: "Variant of the case control study in which the controls are drawn from the same cohort as the cases but are identified before the cases develop; some of the controls may later become cases."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15539

[Term]
id: goldbook:15539
name: case control study
def: "Study that starts with the identification of persons with the disease \(or other outcome variable\) of interest\, and a suitable control \(comparison\, reference\) group of persons without the disease. The relationship of an attribute to the disease is examined by comparing the diseased and non-diseased with regard to how frequently the attribute is present or\, if quantitative\, the levels of the attribute\, in the two groups."
synonym: "case comparison study" []
synonym: "case compeer study" []
synonym: "case history study" []
synonym: "case referent study" []
synonym: "retrospective study" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15644

[Term]
id: goldbook:15540
name: catatonia
def: "Behavior marked by excessive and sometimes violent motor activity and excitement\, or by generalized inhibition or stupor\, that may occur in schizophrenia\, mood disorders\, or organic brain syndromes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15541
name: cell cycle
def: "Regulated biochemical steps that cells go through involving DNA replication and cell division\, usually depicted as a sequential cyclical series of events."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15542
name: cell-mediated hypersensitivity
def: "State in which an individual reacts with allergic effects caused by the reaction of antigen-specific T-lymphocytes following exposure to a certain substance \(allergen\) after having been exposed previously to the same substance or chemical group."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15695

[Term]
id: goldbook:15543
name: cell proliferation
def: "Rapid increase in cell number."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15544
name: cell strain
def: "Cells having specific properties or markers derived from a primary culture or cell line."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15545
name: censored data
def: "Sample observations for which the complete distribution is not known."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15546
name: certified reference material
def: "Reference material\, accompanied by documentation issued by an authoritative body and referring to valid procedures used to obtain a specified property value with uncertainty and traceability."
synonym: "CRM" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16177

[Term]
id: goldbook:15547
name: chain of custody
def: "Sequence of responsibility for a substance from the manufacturer to the distributor\, to the user\, or to the person\(s\) ultimately responsible for waste disposal. This term is also used in controlled transmission of samples from collection to analysis\, especially of samples of materials used for medico-legal or forensic purposes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15548
name: chelation therapy
def: "Treatment with a chelating agent to enhance the elimination or reduce the toxicity of a metal ion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15549
name: chemesthesis
def: "Sensations that arise when chemical compounds activate receptor mechanisms for other effectors\, such as light\, pain\, pressure\, and heat\, in the eye\, skin\, nose\, mouth\, and throat; for example\, the burning feeling from chili pepper\, the cooling from the menthol in mouthwash\, and the stinging feeling of carbonation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15550
name: chemical conversion
def: "Change from one chemical species to another."
synonym: "conversion" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15551
name: chemical safety
def: "Practical certainty that there will be no exposure of organisms to toxic amounts of any substance or group of substances\: This implies attaining an acceptably low risk of exposure to potentially toxic substances."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15552
name: chemical warfare
def: "Military operations using the toxic properties of chemical agents to kill\, injure\, or incapacitate human beings\, animals\, or plants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15553
name: chemophobia
def: "Irrational fear of chemicals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15554
name: chemosis
def: "Chemically induced swelling around the eye caused by edema of the conjunctiva."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15555
name: chemosteriliser
def: "Substance used to sterilize mites\, insects\, rodents\, or other animals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15556
name: cholinesterase inhibitor
def: "Substance that inhibits the action of acetylcholinesterase \(EC 3.1.1.7\) and related enzymes which catalyze the hydrolysis of choline esters\: Such a substance causes hyperactivity in parasympathetic nerves."
synonym: "anticholinesterase" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15961

[Term]
id: goldbook:15557
name: chromatin
def: "Stainable complex of DNA and proteins present in the nucleus of a eukaryotic cell."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15685

[Term]
id: goldbook:15558
name: chromosomal aberration
def: "Abnormality of chromosome number or structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15559
name: chronic toxicity test
def: "Study in which organisms are observed during the greater part of the life span and in which exposure to the test agent takes place over the whole observation time or a substantial part thereof."
synonym: "long-term toxicity test" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15445

[Term]
id: goldbook:15560
name: chronotoxicology
def: "Study of the influence of biological rhythms on the toxicity of substances or of the influence of a toxicant on biological rhythms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15561
name: ciguateratoxin poisoning
def: "Serious illness caused by eating carnivorous fish such as snappers and barracuda that have become contaminated by toxins produced by the microalga\, Gambierdiscus toxicus; gastrointestinal symptoms may accompany a wide variety of neurological symptoms\, including ataxia\, vertigo\, flaccid paralysis\, respiratory arrest\, and reversed perception of hot and cold; the neurological symptoms may persist for many years."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15562
name: circadian
def: "Relating to or exhibiting an approximately \\\(\\pu\{24\\!\\mbox\{-\}h\}\\\) periodicity."
synonym: "nychthemeral" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15563
name: circulation of substances
def: "Movement of xenobiotic substances in the environment with air flow\, river current\, sediment flow\, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15564
name: cirrhosis
def: "Liver disease defined by histological examination and characterized by increased fibrous tissue\, abnormal morphological and physiological changes such as loss of functional liver cells\, and increased resistance to blood flow through the liver \(portal hypertension\). Chronic interstitial inflammation and fibrosis of an organ."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15711
consider: goldbook:15796

[Term]
id: goldbook:15565
name: cirrhotic
def: "Describing an organ showing cirrhosis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15564

[Term]
id: goldbook:15566
name: clastogenesis
def: "Formation \(or generation\) of chromosomal breaks and \(or\) consequent gain\, loss\, or rearrangement of pieces of chromosomes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15567
name: clinical toxicology
def: "Scientific study involving research\, education\, prevention\, and treatment of diseases caused by substances such as drugs and toxins."
comment: "Often refers specifically to the application of toxicological principles to the treatment of human poisoning."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15568
name: clonic
def: "Pertaining to alternate muscular contraction and relaxation in rapid succession."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15569
name: cluster sampling
def: "A method of sampling in which the population is divided into aggregates \(or clusters\) of items bound together in a certain manner. A sample of these clusters is taken at random\, and all the items which constitute them are included in the sample. A sampling method in which each unit selected is a group of persons \(all persons in a city block\, a family\, etc.\) rather than an individual."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15570
name: cocarcinogen
def: "Chemical\, physical\, or biological factor that intensifies the effect of a carcinogen."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15571
name: Codex Alimentarius
def: "Collection of internationally adopted food standards drawn up by the Codex Alimentarius Commission\, the principal body implementing the joint FAO/WHO Food Standards Program."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15572
name: cohort
def: "Component of the population born during a particular period and identified by period of birth so that its characteristics \(such as causes of death and numbers still living\) can be ascertained as it enters successive time and age periods. The term 'cohort' has broadened to describe any designated group of persons followed or traced over a period of time\, as in the term cohort study \(prospective study\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15574

[Term]
id: goldbook:15573
name: cohort analysis
def: "Tabulation and analysis of morbidity or mortality rates in relationship to the ages of a specific group of people \(cohort\)\, identified by their birth period\, and followed as they pass through different ages during part or all of their life span. In certain circumstances such as studies of migrant populations\, cohort analysis may be performed according to duration of residence in a country rather than year of birth\, in order to relate health or mortality experience to duration of exposure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757
consider: goldbook:15893

[Term]
id: goldbook:15574
name: cohort study
def: "Analytic study in epidemiology in which subsets of a defined population can be identified who are\, have been\, or in the future may be exposed or not exposed\, or exposed in different degrees\, to a factor or factors hypothesized to influence the probability of occurrence of a given disease or other outcome. The main feature of the method is observation of a large population for a prolonged period \(years\)\, with comparison of incidence rates of the given disease in groups that differ in exposure levels."
synonym: "concurrent study" []
synonym: "follow-up study" []
synonym: "incidence study" []
synonym: "longitudinal study" []
synonym: "prospective study" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15459
consider: goldbook:15695
consider: goldbook:15809

[Term]
id: goldbook:15575
name: combined effect of poisons
def: "Simultaneous or successive effect of two or more poisons on the organism by the same route of exposure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15576
name: comet assay
def: "Means of measuring DNA damage\, particularly DNA strand breaks. A cell is embedded in agar and exposed to a DNA-damaging agent. The cell is then permeabilized with a detergent\, and an electric field is applied. If the cell’s genomic DNA has been broken into small fragments\, these fragments move out of the cell by electrophoresis and form a streak or 'tail' leading away from the cell which looks like a comet."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15577
name: comparative genomics
def: "Study of the relationship of genome structure and function across different biological species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15578
name: compartmentalise
def: "Separate into compartments."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15579
name: competent authority
def: "In the context of European Community Council Directive 79/831/EEC\, the Sixth Amendment to the European Community Council Directive 67/548/EEC relating to the Classification\, Packaging and Labeling of Dangerous Substances\, official government organization or group receiving and evaluating notifications of new substances."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15580
name: competent bacteria
def: "Culture of bacteria \(or yeast\) treated in such a way that their ability to take up DNA molecules without transduction or conjugation has been enhanced."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15581
name: complete mineralisation
def: "Complete breakdown of a complex organic compound to carbon dioxide\, water\, oxides\, and oxidative inorganic products such as nitrate or sulfate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15582
name: comprehensive effect of poisons
def: "Simultaneous or successive effect made on an organism by poisons entering from different media\, air\, water\, or food or through the skin."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15583
name: computational toxicology
def: "Application of mathematical and computer models to predict adverse effects and to better understand the mechanism\(s\) through which a given chemical causes harm."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15584
name: concentration–effect curve
def: "Graph of the relation between exposure concentration and the magnitude of the resultant biological change."
synonym: "exposure–effect curve" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15681

[Term]
id: goldbook:15585
name: concentration–effect relationship
def: "Association between exposure concentration and the resultant magnitude of the continuously graded change produced\, either in an individual or in a population."
synonym: "exposure–effect relationship" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15681

[Term]
id: goldbook:15586
name: concurrent validity
def: "Measurement and its criterion refer to the same point in time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15587
name: confounding
def: "Situation in which the effects of two processes are not distinguishable from one another\: The distortion of the apparent effect of an exposure on risk brought about by the association of other factors which can influence the outcome. Relationship between the effects of two or more causal factors as observed in a set of data\, such that it is not logically possible to separate the contribution which any single causal factor has made to an effect. Situation in which a measure of the effect of an exposure on risk is distorted because of the association of exposure with other factor\(s\) which influence the outcome under study."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15588
name: confounding variable
def: "Changing factor that can cause or prevent the outcome of interest\, is not an intermediate variable\, and is associated with the factor under investigation."
synonym: "confounder" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15589
name: conjunctiva
def: "Mucous membrane that covers the eyeball and lines the under-surface of the eyelid."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15590
name: conjunctivitis
def: "Inflammation of the conjunctiva."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15589

[Term]
id: goldbook:15591
name: conservative assessment of risk
def: "Assessment of risk that assumes the worst possible case scenario and therefore gives the highest possible value for risk\: Risk management decisions based on this value will maximize safety."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15592
name: construct validity
def: "Extent to which a measurement corresponds to theoretical concepts \(constructs\) concerning the phenomenon under study; for example\, if on theoretical grounds\, the phenomenon should change with age\, a measurement with construct validity would reflect such a change."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15593
name: contact poison
def: "Chemical that injures the target organism through physical contact and skin absorption rather than through ingestion or inhalation. Pesticide \(herbicide\) that causes injury to only the plant tissue to which it is applied or which is not appreciably translocated within plants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15774

[Term]
id: goldbook:15594
name: containment
def: "Process by which possible release\, discharge\, or spill of a toxic substance during normal use or after an accident is prevented by appropriate action."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15595
name: content validity
def: "Extent to which the measurement incorporates the domain of the phenomenon under study; for example\, a measurement of functional health status should embrace activities of daily living\, occupational\, family\, and social functioning\, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15596
name: contraindication
def: "Any condition that renders some particular line of treatment improper or undesirable."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15810

[Term]
id: goldbook:15597
name: control group
def: "Selected subjects of study\, identified as a rule before a study is done\, which comprises humans\, animals\, or other species who do not have the disease\, intervention\, procedure\, or whatever is being studied\, but in all other respects are as nearly identical to the test group as possible."
synonym: "comparison group" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15598
name: matched control
def: "Control \(individual or group or case\) selected to be similar to a study individual or group\, or case\, in specific characteristics\: some commonly used matching variables are age\, sex\, race\, and socioeconomic status."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15599
name: core grade
def: "Quality rating\, based on standard evaluation criteria established by the U.S. Office of Pesticide Programs regulatory agencies\, given to toxicological studies after submission by registrants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15600
name: count mean diameter
def: "Mean of the diameters of all particles in a population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15866

[Term]
id: goldbook:15601
name: count median diameter
def: "Calculated diameter in a population of particles in a gas or liquid phase above which there are as many particles with larger diameters as there are particles below it with smaller diameters."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15867

[Term]
id: goldbook:15602
name: crepitations
def: "Abnormal respiratory sounds heard on auscultation of the chest\, produced by passage of air through passages which contain secretion or exudate or which are constricted by spasm or a thickening of their walls."
comment: "Auscultation is the process of listening for sounds within the body by ear unassisted or using a stethoscope."
synonym: "crackles" []
synonym: "râles" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16058

[Term]
id: goldbook:15603
name: criterion
def: "Validated set of data used as a basis for judgment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15604
name: criterion validity
def: "Extent to which the measurement correlates with an external criterion of the phenomenon under study."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15605
name: critical concentration
def: "Concentration of a substance at and above which adverse functional changes\, reversible or irreversible\, occur in a cell or an organ."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15606
name: critical dose
def: "Dose of a substance at and above which adverse functional changes\, reversible or irreversible\, occur in a cell or an organ."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15607
name: critical effect
def: "For deterministic effects\, the first adverse effect that appears when the threshold \(critical\) concentration or dose is reached in the critical organ\: Adverse effects with no defined threshold concentration are regarded as critical."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15605
consider: goldbook:15610
consider: goldbook:16136

[Term]
id: goldbook:15608
name: critical end-point
def: "Toxic effect used by the USEPA as the basis for a reference dose."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15609
name: critical group
def: "Part of a target population most in need of protection because it is most susceptible to a given toxicant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16119

[Term]
id: goldbook:15610
name: critical organ
def: "Organ that first attains the critical concentration of a substance and exhibits the critical effect under specified circumstances of exposure and for a given population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15605
consider: goldbook:15607

[Term]
id: goldbook:15611
name: critical organ concentration
def: "Mean concentration of a substance in the critical organ at the time the substance reaches its critical concentration in the most sensitive type of cell in the organ."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15605
consider: goldbook:15610

[Term]
id: goldbook:15612
name: cross-sectional study
def: "Study that examines the relationship between diseases \(or other health-related characteristics\) and other variables of interest as they exist in a defined population at one particular time."
comment: "Disease prevalence rather than incidence is normally recorded in a cross-sectional study and the temporal sequence of cause and effect cannot necessarily be determined."
synonym: "disease frequency survey" []
synonym: "prevalence study" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15613
name: cumulative death rate
def: "Proportion of a defined group that dies within the specified time period \(e.g.\, month\, year\)."
comment: "It may refer to all deaths or to deaths from a specific cause or specific causes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16098

[Term]
id: goldbook:15614
name: cumulative effect
def: "Overall change that occurs after repeated doses of a substance or radiation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15615
name: cumulative incidence
def: "Number or proportion of individuals in a group who experience the onset of a health-related event during a specified time interval."
comment: "This interval is generally the same for all members of the group, but, as in lifetime incidence, it may vary from person to person without reference to age."
synonym: "incidence proportion" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15616
name: cumulative incidence rate
def: "Proportion of the cumulative incidence to the total population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15615

[Term]
id: goldbook:15617
name: cumulative incidence ratio
def: "Value obtained by dividing the cumulative incidence rate in the exposed population by the cumulative incidence rate in the unexposed population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15616
consider: goldbook:15695

[Term]
id: goldbook:15618
name: cumulative median lethal dose
def: "Estimate of the total administered amount of a substance that is associated with the death of half a population of animals when the substance is administered repeatedly in doses which are generally fractions of the median lethal dose."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15619
name: cumulative risk
def: "Probability of a common harmful effect associated with concurrent exposure by all relevant pathways and routes of exposure to a group of substances that share a common chemical mechanism of toxicity. Total probability of a harmful effect over time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15620
name: cyanotoxin
def: "Toxin produced by Cyanobacteria\, sometimes called blue–green algae."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15621
name: cyclooxygenase specific inhibitors
def: "Substances\, such as aspirin and ibuprofen\, that block the activity of cyclooxygenase \(COX\)\, an enzyme that is responsible for the formation of prostanoids \(including prostaglandins\, prostacyclin\, and thromboxane\); inhibition of COX can provide relief from inflammation and pain."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15622
name: cytochrome P420
def: "Inactive derivative of cytochrome P450 found in microsomal preparations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15623
name: cytochrome P448
def: "Obsolete term for cytochrome P450 I\, A1\, and A2\, one of the major families of the cytochromes P450 hemoproteins."
comment: "During the monooxygenation of certain substances, often a detoxification process, these iso-enzymes may produce intermediates which can initiate mutations, cancer, immunotoxic reactions, and adverse effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15624
name: cytoplasm
def: "Fundamental substance or matrix of the cell \(within the plasma membrane\) which surrounds the nucleus\, endoplasmic reticulum\, mitochondria\, and other organelles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15662
consider: goldbook:15890
consider: goldbook:15953

[Term]
id: goldbook:15625
name: decipol
def: "Unit of perceived air quality."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15626
name: decompensation
def: "Explicit pathophysiological changes following compensation for adverse effects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15627
name: decontamination
def: "Process of rendering harmless \(by neutralization\, elimination\, removal\, etc.\) a potentially toxic substance in the natural environment\, laboratory areas\, the workplace\, other indoor areas\, clothes\, food\, water\, sewage\, etc."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15628
name: dehydrogenase
def: "Enzyme that catalyzes oxidation of compounds by removing hydrogen."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15629
name: delayed effect
def: "Consequence occurring after a latent period following the end of exposure to a toxic substance or other harmful environmental factor."
synonym: "latent effect" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15630
name: dental fluorosis
def: "Tooth enamel malformations due to excessive fluoride exposure during dental development."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15631
name: deoxyribonucleic acid cloning
def: "Replication of DNA sequences ligated into a suitable vector in an appropriate host organism."
synonym: "DNA cloning" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15632
name: deoxyribonucleic acid repair
def: "Restoration of the molecular structure of DNA after it has been damaged by a chemical or physical agent\: This may involve direct DNA damage reversal\, base excision repair\, nucleotide excision repair\, mismatch repair\, or double-strand break repair"
synonym: "DNA repair" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15633
name: dependence
def: "A psychic craving for a drug or other substance that may or may not be accompanied by a physical dependency. Reliance on a drug or other substance to maintain health."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15634
name: depilatory
def: "Substance causing loss of hair."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15635
name: dermal
def: "Pertaining to the skin."
synonym: "cutaneous" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15636
name: dermal irritation
def: "Skin reaction resulting from a single or multiple exposure to a physical or chemical entity at the same site\, characterized by the presence of inflammation; it may result in cell death."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15637
name: descriptive epidemiology
def: "Study of the occurrence of disease or other health-related characteristics in populations\, including general observations concerning the relationship of disease to basic characteristics such as age\, sex\, race\, occupation\, and social class; it may also be concerned with geographic location. The major characteristics in descriptive epidemiology can be classified under the headings\: individuals\, time\, and place."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15638
name: desquamation
def: "Shedding of an outer layer of skin in scales or shreds."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15639
name: detriment
def: "Estimated measure of the expected harm or loss associated with an adverse event\, usually in a manner chosen to facilitate meaningful addition over different events. It is generally the integrated product of arbitrary values of risk and hazard and is often expressed in terms such as costs in U.S. dollars\, loss in expected years of life or loss in productivity\, and is needed for numerical exercises such as cost-benefit analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15448

[Term]
id: goldbook:15640
name: developmental toxicity
def: "Adverse effects on the developing organism \(including structural abnormality\, altered growth\, or functional deficiency or death\) resulting from exposure through conception\, gestation \(including organogenesis\)\, and postnatally up to the time of sexual maturation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15641
name: diaphoresis
def: "Profuse perspiration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15642
name: discharge standard
def: "Maximum amount of a pollutant released from a given source to a specified medium which is acceptable under specified circumstances."
synonym: "discharge release limit" []
synonym: "effluent standard" []
synonym: "emission standard" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15643
name: discordance
def: "Any difference in a character between individuals due to genetic differences such as may occur in dizygotic twins\, or between matched pairs in a case cohort study."
synonym: "genetic discordance" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15538

[Term]
id: goldbook:15644
name: disease
def: "Literally\, dis-ease\, lack of ease; pathological condition that presents a group of symptoms peculiar to it and which establishes the condition as an abnormal entity different from other normal or pathological body states."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15645
name: disposition
def: "Natural tendency shown by an individual or group of individuals\, including any tendency to acquisition of specific diseases\, often due to hereditary factors. Total of the processes of absorption of a chemical into the circulatory systems\, distribution throughout the body\, biotransformation\, and excretion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15646
name: dissipation
def: "Reduction in the amount of a pesticide or other compound that has been applied to plants\, soil\, etc. \(used when it is not clear whether this is by mineralization degradation\, binding\, or leaching\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15647
name: distribution volume
def: "Theoretical volume of a body compartment throughout which a substance is calculated to be distributed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15648
name: diuresis
def: "Excretion of urine\, especially in excess."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15649
name: diuretic
def: "Agent that increases urine production."
synonym: "micturitic" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15650
name: dominant half life
def: "Half life of a fraction of a substance in a specific organ or compartment if it defines approximately the overall clearance rate for that substance at a specific time point."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15651
name: dominant lethal mutation
def: "Genetic change occurring in a germ cell that does not cause dysfunction of the gamete but which is lethal to the fertilized egg or developing embryo which develops from it."
comment: "Induction of a dominant lethal event after exposure to a chemical substance (dominant lethal test) indicates that the substance has affected germinal tissue of the test species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15652
name: duplicate portion sampling method
def: "Study in which test persons consume their ordinary diet but\, for each meal\, they prepare for subsequent analysis a duplicate portion of all food as prepared\, served\, and consumed."
synonym: "duplicate diet study" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15653
name: duplicate samples
def: "Two samples taken under the same or comparable conditions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16045

[Term]
id: goldbook:15654
name: dysfunction
def: "Abnormal\, impaired\, or incomplete functioning of an organism\, organ\, tissue\, or cell."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15655
name: ectoparasiticide
def: "Substance intended to kill parasites living on the exterior of the host."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15656
name: elimination half life
def: "Period taken for the plasma concentration of a substance to decrease by half."
comment: "May also be applied to other body compartments such as blood, specific organs, or tissues."
synonym: "elimination half time" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15657
name: eliminator
def: "Substance that contributes to the elimination of a poison from an organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15658
name: embryotoxicity
def: "Production by a substance of toxic effects in progeny in the first period of pregnancy between conception and the fetal stage. Any toxic effect on the conceptus as a result of prenatal exposure during the embryonic stages of development\: These effects may include malformations and variations\, malfunctions\, altered growth\, prenatal death\, and altered postnatal function."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15659
name: embryotropic effect
def: "Change in the embryo and the regulation of its development."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15660
name: emission and exposure control
def: "Technical and administrative procedures and specifications applied for the monitoring\, reduction\, or elimination of emissions from a source or exposure to a target."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15661
name: endocon
def: "Portion of a conjugated metabolite that is derived from a natural product \(such as a sugar\, amino acid\, or other organic acid\) of the metabolizing organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15690

[Term]
id: goldbook:15662
name: endoplasmic reticulum
def: "Intracellular complex of membranes in which proteins and lipids\, as well as molecules for export\, are synthesized and in which the biotransformation reactions of the monooxygenase enzyme systems occur."
comment: "May be isolated as microsomes following cell fractionation procedures."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15663
name: endothelial
def: "Pertaining to the layer of flat cells lining the inner surface of blood and lymphatic vessels\, and the surface lining of serous and synovial membranes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15664
name: enteritis
def: "Intestinal inflammation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15665
name: enterohepatic circulation
def: "Cyclical process involving intestinal reabsorption of a substance that has been excreted through the bile\, followed by transfer back to the liver\, making it available for biliary excretion again."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15666
name: environment
def: "Aggregate\, at a given moment\, of all external conditions and influences to which a system under study is subjected."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15667
name: environmental damage
def: "Adverse effects to the natural environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15668
name: environmental exposure level
def: "Level \(concentration or amount or a time integral of either\) of a substance to which an organism or other component of the environment is exposed in its natural surroundings."
synonym: "EEL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15695

[Term]
id: goldbook:15669
name: environmental health
def: "Human welfare and its influence by the environment\, including technical and administrative measures for improving the human environment from a health point of view."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15670
name: environmental health impact assessment
def: "Estimate of the adverse effects to health or risks likely to follow from a proposed or expected environmental change or development."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15671
name: environmental health criteria documents
def: "Critical publications of IPCS containing reviews of methodologies and existing knowledge—expressed\, if possible\, in quantitative terms—of selected substances \(or groups of substances\) on identifiable\, immediate\, and long-term effects on human health and welfare."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15672
name: environmental hygiene
def: "Practical control measures used to improve the basic environmental conditions affecting human health\, for example\, clean water supply\, human and animal waste disposal\, protection of food from biological contamination\, and housing conditions\, all of which are concerned with the quality of the human environment."
synonym: "environmental sanitation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15673
name: environmental medicine
def: "Specialty devoted to the prevention and management of environmentally induced injury\, illness\, and disability\, and the promotion of the health of individuals\, families\, and communities by ensuring a healthy environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15674
name: environmental protection
def: "Actions taken to prevent or minimize adverse effects to the natural environment. Complex of measures including monitoring of environmental pollution\, development and practice of environmental protection principles \(legal\, technical\, and hygienic\)\, including risk assessment\, risk management\, and risk communication."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16061

[Term]
id: goldbook:15675
name: epigastric
def: "Pertaining to the upper-middle region of the abdomen."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15676
name: epileptiform
def: "Occurring in severe or sudden spasms\, as in convulsion or epilepsy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15677
name: epithelioma
def: "Any tumor derived from epithelium."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15678
name: eschar
def: "Slough or dry scab on an area of skin that has been burnt."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15679
name: estimated daily intake
def: "Prediction of the daily intake of a residue of a potentially harmful agent based on the most realistic estimation of the residue levels in food and the best available food consumption data for a specific population\: Residue levels are estimated taking into account known uses of the agent\, the range of contaminated commodities\, the proportion of a commodity treated\, and the quantity of home-grown or imported commodities."
comment: "The EDI is expressed in \(\pu{mg}\) residue per person."
synonym: "EDI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15820

[Term]
id: goldbook:15680
name: estimated environmental concentration
def: "Predicted concentration of a substance\, typically a pesticide\, within an environmental compartment based on estimates of quantities released\, discharge patterns\, and inherent disposition of the substance \(fate and distribution\) as well as the nature of the specific receiving ecosystems."
synonym: "EEC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "predicted exposure concentration (PEC)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15693

[Term]
id: goldbook:15681
name: estimated exposure concentration
def: "Measured or calculated amount or mass concentration of a substance to which an organism is likely to be exposed\, considering exposure by all sources and routes."
synonym: "EEC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15695

[Term]
id: goldbook:15682
name: estimated exposure dose
def: "Measured or calculated dose of a substance to which an organism is likely to be exposed\, considering exposure by all sources and routes."
synonym: "EED" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15695

[Term]
id: goldbook:15683
name: estimated maximum daily intake
def: "Prediction of the maximum daily intake of a residue of a potentially harmful agent based on assumptions of average food consumption per person and maximum residues in the edible portion of a commodity\, corrected for the reduction or increase in residues resulting from preparation\, cooking\, or commercial processing."
comment: "The EMDI is expressed in \(\pu{mg}\) residue per person."
synonym: "EMDI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15684
name: etiology
def: "Science dealing with the cause or origin of disease. In individuals\, the cause or origin of disease."
synonym: "aetiology" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15644

[Term]
id: goldbook:15685
name: eukaryote
def: "Cell or organism with the genetic material packed in a membrane-surrounded structurally discrete nucleus and with well-developed cell organelles."
comment: "The term includes all organisms except archaebacteria, eubacteria, and cyanobacteria (until recently classified as cyanophyta or blue–green algae)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16009

[Term]
id: goldbook:15686
name: European Inventory of Existing Chemical Substances
def: "List of all substances supplied either singly or as components in preparations to persons in a Member State of the European Community on any occasion between 1 January 1971 and 18 September 1981."
synonym: "EINECS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15687
name: excess lifetime risk
def: "Additional or excess risk incurred over the lifetime of an individual by exposure to a toxic substance."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15688
name: exchange transfusion
def: "Method of active artificial elimination of toxicity consisting in complete replacement of blood of the patient by donor blood."
synonym: "blood substitution" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15689
name: excretion rate
def: "Amount of substance and \(or\) its metabolites that is excreted divided by time of excretion."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15690
name: exocon
def: "Portion of a conjugated metabolite that is derived from the parent molecule."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15691
name: exogenous
def: "Resulting from causes or derived from materials external to an organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15692
name: exothelium
def: "Layer of flattened epithelial cells external to an organ or tissue."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15693
name: expected environmental concentration
def: "Calculated concentrations of a substance\, typically a pesticide\, in various environmental compartments based on calculations using maximum-exposure scenarios."
comment: "EEC models assume a maximum number of applications per growing season at the maximum rate of application according to the application methods stated on the product label."
synonym: "EEC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "expected exposure concentration (EEC)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15694
name: explant
def: "Living tissue removed from its normal environment and transferred to an artificial medium for growth."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15695
name: exposed
def: "Subject to a factor that is under study in the environment\, for instance\, an environmental hazard."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15696
name: exposed group
def: "People \(or other organisms\) who have been exposed to a supposed cause of a disease or health state of interest\, or possess a characteristic that is a determinant of the health outcome of interest."
synonym: "exposed" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15695
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15697
name: exposure limit
def: "General term defining an administrative substance concentration or intensity of exposure that should not be exceeded."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15698
name: exposure ratio
def: "In a case control study\, value obtained by dividing the rate at which persons in the case group are exposed to a risk factor \(or to a protective factor\) by the rate at which persons in the control group are exposed to the risk factor \(or to the protective factor\) of interest."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15539
consider: goldbook:15695

[Term]
id: goldbook:15699
name: exposure surface
def: "Surface on a target where a substance \(e.g.\, a pesticide\) is present."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15700
name: exposure test
def: "Determination of the level\, concentration\, or uptake of a potentially toxic compound and \(or\) its metabolite\(s\) in biological samples from an organism \(blood\, urine\, hair\, etc.\) and the interpretation of the results to estimate the absorbed dose or degree of environmental pollution; or the measuring of biochemical effects\, usually not direct adverse effects of the substance\, and relating them to the quantity of substance absorbed\, or to its concentration in the environment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15701
name: external validity
def: "Generalizability of the results of a particular study\, beyond the limits of the population actually studied."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15702
name: extracellular space
def: "Volume within a tissue\, outside cells\, and excluding vascular and lymphatic space."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15703
name: extracellular volume
def: "Volume of fluid outside the cells but within the outer surface of an organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15704
name: extraction ratio
def: "Amount of substance extracted from a source divided by the total contained within the source."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15705
name: extra risk
def: "Probability that an agent produces an observed response\, as distinguished from the probability that the response is caused by a spontaneous event unrelated to the agent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15706
name: extraneous residue limit
def: "Refers to a pesticide residue or contaminant arising from environmental sources \(including former agricultural uses\) other than the use of a pesticide or contaminant substance directly or indirectly on the commodity. It is the maximum concentration of a pesticide residue or contaminant that is recommended by the Codex Alimentarius Commission to be legally permitted or recognized as acceptable in or on food\, agricultural commodity\, or animal feed."
comment: "The mass content is expressed in milligrams of pesticide residue or contaminant per kilogram of commodity."
synonym: "ERL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15571

[Term]
id: goldbook:15707
name: extrapyramidal movement disorders
def: "Involuntary movement disorders mediated by signaling through neurons outside the pyramidal \(corticospinal\) tract\, often describing side effects of psychiatric medications."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15708
name: fertility
def: "Ability to conceive and to produce offspring\: For litter-bearing species\, the number of offspring per litter is used as a measure of fertility."
comment: "Reduced fertility is sometimes referred to as subfertility."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15709
name: fertility toxicant
def: "Produces abnormalities of male or female reproductive functions or impairs reproductive capacity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15710
name: fetotoxicity
def: "Toxicity to the fetus."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15711
name: fibrosis
def: "Abnormal formation of fibrous tissue."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15712
name: fiducial limit
def: "Form of confidence limit given as a stated probability\, for example\, \\\(P = \\pu\{0.95\}\\\)."
comment: "In toxicology, the terms "fiducial limits" and "confidence limits" are generally considered to be synonymous."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15713
name: first-order chemical reaction
def: "Chemical reaction where the initial rate is directly proportional to the concentration of one of the reactants. Any process in which a variable decreases with time at a constant fractional amount."
synonym: "first-order reaction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15714
name: fixed dose procedure
def: "Acute toxicity test in which a substance is tested initially at a small number \(3 or 4\) predefined doses to identify which produces evident toxicity without lethality\: The test may be repeated at one or more higher or lower defined discriminating doses to satisfy the criteria."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15715
name: fluorosis
def: "Adverse effects of fluoride\, as in dental or skeletal fluorosis."
synonym: "fluoridosis" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15716
name: foci
def: "Small groups of cells distinguishable\, in appearance or histochemically\, from the surrounding tissue\: indicative of an early stage of a lesion that may lead to the formation of a neoplastic nodule."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15717
name: food additive
def: "Any substance\, not normally consumed as a food by itself and not normally used as a typical ingredient of a given food\, whether or not it has nutritive value\, that is added intentionally to food for a technological \(including organoleptic\) purpose in the manufacture\, processing\, preparation\, treatment\, packing\, packaging\, transport\, or holding of the food. Addition results\, or may be reasonably expected to result \(directly or indirectly\)\, in the substance or its byproducts becoming a component of\, or otherwise affecting\, the characteristics of the food to which it is added."
comment: "The term does not include "contaminants" or substances added to food for maintaining or improving nutritional qualities."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15718
name: food allergy
def: "Hypersensitivity reaction to substances in the diet to which an individual has previously been sensitized."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15719
name: food intolerance
def: "Physiologically based reproducible\, unpleasant \(adverse\) reaction to a specific food or food ingredient that is not immunologically based."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15720
name: food web
def: "Network of food chains."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15721
name: forced diuresis
def: "Method of stimulating diuresis based on performing hydrational therapy\, sometimes with parallel introduction of diuretics\, with the aim of achieving increased clearance of a toxic substance in urine."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15722
name: founder effect
def: "Changes in allelic frequencies that occur when a small group is separated from a large population and establishes a colony in a new location."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15723
name: fumigant
def: "Substance that is vaporized in order to kill or repel pests."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15724
name: fungus preparation
def: "Substance obtained from fungi that has an insecticidal effect reflecting the pathogenicity of the fungi for insects."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15725
name: gametocide
def: "Substance intended to kill gametes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15726
name: gastroenteritis
def: "Inflammation of the stomach and intestine."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15727
name: gastrointestinal
def: "Pertaining to or communicating with the stomach and intestine."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15728
name: gavage
def: "Administration of materials directly into the stomach by esophageal intubation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15729
name: gene map
def: "Map showing the positions in the genome of genes or other genetic markers\, either relative to each other or as a physical map of absolute distances."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15730
name: generally regarded as safe
def: "Phrase used to describe the USFDA philosophy that justifies approval of food additives that may not meet the usual test criteria for safety but have been used extensively and have not demonstrated that they cause any harm to consumers."
synonym: "GRAS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15731
name: genetically modified organism
def: "Bacterium\, plant\, or animal whose DNA has been deliberately altered."
synonym: "GMO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15732
name: genetic polymorphism
def: "Existence of inter-individual differences in DNA sequences coding for one specific gene\, giving rise to different functional and \(or\) morphological traits."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15733
name: genetic susceptibility
def: "Predisposition to a particular disease or sensitivity to a substance due to the presence of a specific allele or combination of alleles in an individual’s genome."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15644

[Term]
id: goldbook:15734
name: genetic toxicology
def: "Study of chemically or physically induced changes to the structure of DNA\, including epigenetic phenomena or mutations that may or may not be heritable."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15735
name: germ-free animal
def: "Animal grown under sterile conditions in the period of postnatal development\: Such animals are usually obtained by Caesarean operation and kept in special sterile boxes in which there are no viable microorganisms \(sterile air\, food\, and water are supplied\)."
synonym: "axenic animal" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15736
name: germinal aplasia
def: "Complete failure of gonad development."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15737
name: glomerular
def: "Pertaining to a tuft or cluster\, as of a plexus of capillary blood vessels or nerve fibers\, especially referring to the capillaries of the glomerular of the kidney."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15738
name: glomerular filtration
def: "Formation of an ultrafiltrate of the blood occurring in the glomerulus of the kidney."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15739
name: glomerular filtration rate
def: "Volume of ultrafiltrate formed in the kidney tubules from the blood passing through the glomerular capillaries divided by time of filtration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15740
name: glue-sniffing
def: "Inhalation of solvent vapor from plastic cements or other adhesives in order to become intoxicated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
