[Term]
id: goldbook:15741
name: gnotobiota
def: "Specifically and entirely known microfauna and microflora of a specially reared laboratory animal."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15742
name: gnotobiote
def: "Specially reared laboratory animal whose microflora and microfauna are specifically known in their entirety."
synonym: "gnotobiont" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15743
name: goiter
def: "Noncancerous enlargement of the thyroid gland\, visible as a swelling at the front of the neck\, that is often associated with iodine deficiency."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15744
name: goitrogen
def: "Any substance \(such as thiouracil\) that induces the formation of a goiter."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15745
name: gonadotropic
def: "Pertaining to effects on sex glands and on the systems that regulate them."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15746
name: good agricultural practice
def: "Nationally authorized safe uses of pesticides under actual conditions necessary for effective and reliable pest control."
comment: "It encompasses a range of levels of pesticide applications up to the highest authorized use, applied in a manner that leaves a residue which is the smallest amount practicable. Authorized safe uses include nationally registered or recommended uses, that take into account public and occupational health and environmental safety considerations. Actual conditions include any stage in the production, storage, transport, distribution, and processing of food commodities and animal feed."
synonym: "GAP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15747
name: graminicide
def: "Pesticide \(herbicide\) used for the control of weedy grasses \(Gramineae\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15774

[Term]
id: goldbook:15748
name: ground treatment of plants
def: "Dusting or spraying of plants with pesticides by hand\, by special machines\, or by apparatus fixed to tractors or driven by them."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15749
name: guideline for exposure limits
def: "Scientifically judged quantitative value \(a concentration or number\) of an environmental constituent that ensures aesthetically pleasing air\, water\, or food and from which no adverse effect is expected concerning noncarcinogenic endpoints\, or that gives an acceptably low estimate of lifetime cancer risk from those substances which are proven human carcinogens or carcinogens with at least limited evidence of human carcinogenicity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15750
name: guideline value
def: "Quantitative measure \(a concentration or a number\) of a constituent of an environmental medium that ensures aesthetically pleasing air\, water\, or food and does not result in a significant risk to the user."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15751
name: guides to air quality
def: "Sets of atmospheric concentrations and exposure times that are associated with specific effects of varying degrees of pollution on humans\, animals\, vegetation\, and the environment in general."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15752
name: guides to environmental quality
def: "Sets of concentrations\, numbers and exposure times that are associated with the specific effects of factors in environmental media on humans\, animals\, vegetation\, and the environment in general."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15753
name: harmful occupational factor
def: "Component of the work environment\, the effect of which on a worker under certain conditions leads to ill health or reduction of working ability."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15754
name: harmful substance
def: "Substance that\, following contact with an organism\, can cause ill health or adverse effects either at the time of exposure or later in the life of the present and future generations."
synonym: "noxious substance" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15755
name: hazard communication standard
def: "U.S. OSHA standard requiring all employers to inform employees of the hazard of substances in the workplace and the steps necessary to avoid harm."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15756
name: hazardous production factor
def: "Production factor the effect of which on a worker under certain conditions results in injury or some impairment of health."
synonym: "hazard at work" []
synonym: "hazardous occupational factor" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15757
name: health
def: "State of complete physical\, mental\, and social well-being\, and not merely the absence of disease or infirmity. State of dynamic balance in which an individual’s or a group’s capacity to cope with the circumstances of living is at an optimal level. State characterized by anatomical\, physiological\, and psychological integrity; ability to perform personally valued family\, work\, and community roles; ability to deal with physical\, biological\, psychological\, and social stress; a feeling of well-being; and freedom from the risk of disease and untimely death. In ecology\, a sustainable steady state in which humans and other living organisms can coexist indefinitely."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15644

[Term]
id: goldbook:15758
name: health advisory level
def: "In the United States\, nonregulatory health-based reference level of chemical traces \(usually in ppm\, i.e.\, \\\(\\pu\{mg L-1\}\\\)\) in drinking water at which there are no adverse health risks when ingested over various periods of time."
comment: "Such levels are established for 1 day, 10 days, long-term and life-time exposure periods. They allow for a wide margin of safety."
synonym: "HAL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15759
name: health-based exposure limit
def: "Maximum concentration or intensity of exposure that can be tolerated without significant effect \(based on only scientific and not economic evidence concerning exposure levels and associated health effects\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15760
name: health hazard
def: "Any factor or exposure that may adversely affect health."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15761
name: healthy worker effect
def: "Epidemiological phenomenon observed initially in studies of occupational diseases\: Workers usually exhibit lower overall disease and death rates than the general population\, due to the fact that the old\, severely ill\, and disabled are ordinarily excluded from employment. Death rates in the general population may be inappropriate for comparison\, if this effect is not taken into account."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15644

[Term]
id: goldbook:15762
name: hematemesis
def: "Vomiting of blood."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15763
name: hematotoxicity
def: "Adverse changes in blood caused by exposure to chemicals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15764
name: hematuria
def: "Presence of blood in the urine."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15766
name: hemochromatosis
def: "Hereditary disorder affecting iron metabolism in which excessive amounts of iron accumulate in the body tissues."
comment: "The disorder is characterized by diabetes mellitus, liver dysfunction, and a bronze pigmentation of the skin."
