consider: goldbook:15796
consider: goldbook:16012

[Term]
id: goldbook:15915
name: nephropathy
def: "Any disease or abnormality of the kidney."
synonym: "renopathy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15644

[Term]
id: goldbook:15916
name: nephrosis
def: "Disease of the kidneys marked by degeneration of renal tubular epithelium."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15644

[Term]
id: goldbook:15917
name: nephrotoxic
def: "Chemically harmful to the cells of the kidney."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15918
name: nitrosative stress
def: "Adverse effects occurring when the generation of reactive nitrogen species in a system exceeds the system’s ability to neutralize and eliminate them; nitrosative stress may lead to nitrosylation reactions that can alter protein structure\, thus inhibiting normal function."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15919
name: no-acceptable-daily-intake-allocated
def: "This expression is applicable to a substance for which the available information is not sufficient to establish its safety\, or when the specifications for identity and purity are not adequate\, or when the available data show that the substance is hazardous and should not be used."
comment: "The basis for the use of the expression should be determined before action is taken; in the first two cases above, not being able to allocate an ADI does not mean that the substance is unsafe."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15920
name: nodule
def: "Small node or boss that is solid and can be detected by touch."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15921
name: no-effect dose
def: "Amount of a substance that has no effect on the organism."
comment: "It is lower than the threshold of harmful effect and is estimated while establishing the threshold of harmful effect."
synonym: "NED" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "subthreshold dose" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16136

[Term]
id: goldbook:15922
name: no-effect level
def: "Maximum dose \(of a substance\) that produces no detectable changes under defined conditions of exposure."
comment: "This term tends to be substituted by no-observed-adverse-effect level (NOAEL) or no-observed-effect level (NOEL)."
synonym: "NEL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15923
name: non-bioenvironmental transformation
def: "Change in the chemical or physical nature of a substance occurring as a result of physicochemical conditions and independent of any biological system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15924
name: nonionising radiation
def: "Electromagnetic radiation of low energy that is not capable of causing ionization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15925
name: nonoccupational exposure
def: "Environmental exposure outside the workplace to substances that are otherwise associated with particular work environments and \(or\) activities and processes that occur there."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15927
name: nosocomial
def: "Associated with a hospital or infirmary\, especially used of diseases that may result from treatment in such an institution."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15644

[Term]
id: goldbook:15928
name: nutritional table method
def: "Procedure for evaluating the dietary intake of a large number of people."
comment: "For each record of quantity of food consumed during a certain time period, the daily intake of the substance in question is calculated by multiplying the substance concentration in the food item (as obtained from the nutritional table) by the quantity of food consumed and dividing by the time of observation."
comment: "The accuracy of the method depends on the accuracy with which records of the food consumption can be established and the accuracy of the nutritional tables specifying the concentration of various nutrients, vitamins, essential, and non-essential substances including pesticide residues."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15929
name: nychthemeral
def: "Relating to or exhibiting a nychthemeron or \\\(\\pu\{24\\!\\mbox\{-\}h\}\\\) period."
synonym: "circadian" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15930
name: objective environment
def: "Actual physical\, chemical\, and social environment as described by objective measurements\, such as noise levels in decibels and concentrations of air pollutants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15931
name: occupational environment
def: "Surrounding conditions at a workplace."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15932
name: occupational exposure
def: "Experience of substances\, intensities of radiation\, etc.\, or other conditions while at work."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15933
name: occupational exposure limit
def: "Regulatory level of exposure to substances\, intensities of radiation\, etc.\, or other conditions\, specified appropriately in relevant government legislation or related codes of practice."
synonym: "OEL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15934
name: occupational exposure standard
def: "Level of exposure to substances\, intensities of radiation\, etc.\, or other conditions considered to represent specified good practice and a realistic criterion for the control of exposure by appropriate plant design\, engineering controls\, and\, if necessary\, the addition and use of personal protective clothing. In UK\, health-based exposure limit defined under COSHH Regulations as the concentration of any airborne substance\, averaged over a reference period\, at which\, according to current knowledge\, there is no evidence that it is likely to be injurious to employees\, if they are exposed by inhalation\, day after day\, to that concentration\, and set on the advice of the HSE Advisory Committee on Toxic Substances."
synonym: "OES" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15695
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15935
name: occupational hygiene
def: "Identification\, assessment\, and control of physicochemical and biological factors in the workplace that may affect the health or well-being of those at work and in the surrounding community."
synonym: "industrial hygiene" []
synonym: "occupational safety and health" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15936
name: occupational medicine
def: "Specialty devoted to the prevention and management of occupational injury\, illness\, and disability\, and the promotion of the health of workers\, their families\, and their communities."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
