[Term]
id: goldbook:15968
name: peritoneal dialysis
def: "Method of artificial detoxication in which a toxic substance from the body is transferred into liquid that is instilled into the peritoneum."
comment: "Effectively, this represents the employment of the peritoneum surrounding the abdominal cavity as a dialyzing membrane for the purpose of removing waste products or toxins accumulated as a result of renal failure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15969
name: permeability coefficient
def: "Quantity defining the permeability of molecules across a cell membrane and expressed as \\\[P = \\frac\{KD\}\{\\Delta x\}\\\] where \\\(K\\\) is the partition coefficient\, \\\(D\\\) is the diffusion coefficient\, and \\\(\\Delta x\\\) is the thickness of the cell membrane."
comment: "SI units \(\pu{m s-1}\); frequently used units \(\pu{cm s-1}\), with units \(\pu{cm2 s-1}\) for \(D\), and \(\pu{cm}\) for \(\Delta x\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15970
name: permeable
def: "Of a membrane\, allowing a given substance to pass through."
comment: "When applied to nonbiological membranes with no qualification, the term normally refers to water."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15971
name: permissible exposure limit
def: "Recommendation by U.S. OSHA for a time-weighted average concentration that must not be exceeded during any \\\(\\pu\{8\\!\\mbox\{-\}h\}\\\) work shift of a \\\(\\pu\{40\\!\\mbox\{-\}h\}\\\) working week."
synonym: "PEL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16143

[Term]
id: goldbook:15972
name: personal monitoring
def: "Type of environmental monitoring in which an individual’s exposure to a substance is measured and evaluated."
comment: "This is normally carried out using a personal sampler."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15974

[Term]
id: goldbook:15973
name: personal protective device
def: "Equipment \(clothing\, gloves\, hard hat\, respirator\, etc.\) worn by an individual to prevent exposure to a potentially toxic substance."
synonym: "PPD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "individual protective device (IPD)" []
synonym: "personal protective equipment (PPE)" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15974
name: personal sampler
def: "Compact\, portable instrument for individual air sampling\, measuring\, or both\, the content of a harmful substance in the respiration zone of a working person."
synonym: "individual monitor" []
synonym: "individual sampler" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15975
name: pest
def: "Organism that may harm public health\, attacks food and other materials essential to mankind\, or otherwise affects human beings adversely."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:15757

[Term]
id: goldbook:15976
name: phase III reaction
def: "Further metabolism of conjugated metabolites produced by phase II reactions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15977
name: phenome
def: "Complete phenotypic description of an organism \(by analogy with genome\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15978
name: photo-irritation
def: "Inflammation of the skin caused by exposure to light\, especially that due to metabolites formed in the skin by photolysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15979
name: phototoxicity
def: "Adverse effects produced by exposure to light energy\, especially those produced in the skin."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15980
name: physical map
def: "Map showing how much DNA\, measured in base pairs\, separates two genes."
comment: "Not to be confused with a genetic map which shows the position of genes in relation to each other, based on the frequency of crossing overs."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15981
name: piscicide
def: "Substance intended to kill fish."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15982
name: placentation
def: "Formation of a placenta in the uterus. Type or structure of a placenta. In botany\, arrangement of placentas within the plant ovary."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15983
name: plumbism
def: "Chronic poisoning caused by absorption of lead or lead salts."
synonym: "saturnism" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15984
name: pneumoconiosis
def: "Usually fibrosis of the lungs that develops owing to \(prolonged\) inhalation of inorganic or organic dusts."
comment: "Cause-specific types of pneumoconiosis are:anthracosis: from coal dustasbestosis: from asbestos dustbyssinosis: from cotton dustsiderosis: from iron dustsilicosis: from silica duststannosis: from tin dust"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15985
name: pneumonitis
def: "Inflammation of the lung."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15986
name: point mutation
def: "Change in a single base pair in DNA."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15987
name: poison-bearing
def: "Containing a poison."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15988
name: poisoning
def: "Morbid condition produced by a poison."
synonym: "intoxication" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15989
name: polyclonal antibody
def: "Antibody produced by a number of different cell types."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15990
name: polydipsia
def: "Chronic excessive thirst."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779071153
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:15991
name: polyuria
def: "Excessive production and discharge of urine."
