[Term]
id: goldbook:16231
name: chronic
def: "Long-term \(in relation to exposure or effect\)."
comment: "In clinical medicine, long-established or long-lasting."
comment: "In experimental toxicology, chronic refers to mammalian studies lasting considerably more than 90 days or to studies occupying a large part of the lifetime of an organism."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16232
name: chronic exposure
def: "Continued exposures occurring over an extended period of time\, or a significant fraction of the test species’ or of the group of individuals’\, or of the population’s lifetime."
synonym: "long-term exposure" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:16230

[Term]
id: goldbook:16233
name: benchmark concentration
def: "Statistical lower CL on the concentration that produces a defined response \(called the benchmark response or BMR\, usually \\\(\\pu\{5\\%\}\\\) or \\\(\\pu\{100\\%\}\\\)\) for an adverse effect compared to background\, defined as \\\(\\pu\{0\\%\}\\\).Dose–response curve showing BMC and BMCL \(BMC 10 % lower CL\)."
synonym: "BMC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16234
name: physiologically based pharmacokinetic modeling
def: "Mathematical modeling of kinetic behavior of a substance\, based on measured physiological parameters."
synonym: "PBPK" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "toxicologically based pharmacokinetic modeling" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16235
name: deterministic effect
def: "Phenomenon committed to a particular outcome determined by fundamental physical principles."
synonym: "deterministic process" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16236
name: stochastic
def: "Pertaining to or arising from chance and hence obeying the laws of probability."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16237
name: effect
def: "Change in biochemistry\, morphology\, physiology\, growth\, development\, or lifespan of an organism which results in impairment of functional capacity or impairment of capacity to compensate for additional stress or increase in susceptibility to other environmental influences."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16238
name: elimination rate
def: "Derivative with respect to time of the concentration or amount of a substance in the body\, or a part thereof\, resulting from elimination."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16239
name: local effect
def: "Change occurring at the site of contact between an organism and a toxicant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16240
name: toxicant
def: "This is the preferred term for a substance that is considered to be toxic under circumstances which are thought likely to happen."
comment: "This word comes from the Greek toxikos "of or for the bow" and was originally applied to the poison used to tip arrows. The term "poison" is nearly a synonym, but tends to be applied to substances that may be deliberately used for poisoning, such as pesticides, and often has overtones of criminal use."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16241
name: medicine
def: "Any drug or remedy."
comment: "This definition depends on usage. Any substance, e.g., herbs, willow bark, or honey, may be used as a drug or a remedy and, as always, the end effect will depend on the dose."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779091583
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16242
name: suspension of solid charged particles
def: "Dispersion of solid electrically charged particles\, commonly larger in size range than colloidal particles \(of approximate diameter range \\\(\\pu\{\{1\}\{-\}\{1000\} nm\}\\\)\) \(dispersed phase\)\, in water or an aqueous solution \(continuous\, liquid phase\)."
comment: "Suspension can be a uniform system, i.e., an optically equable (uniform) mixture of both phases, or a combined system in which a part of the liquid phase of the equilibrated suspension eqs is separated from the rest of the suspension. By sedimentation of particles, a concentrated phase (sediment) can be formed, in which particles are still surrounded by the intrinsic liquid phase, the eqs. Both parts remain in physical and electrical contact."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779010081
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16243
name: suspension potentiometric cell
def: "Galvanic cell containing\, as its essential component\, a uniform or combined suspension or one of its separated parts alone\, the eqs or sediment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779010081
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16244
name: anomalous liquid junction potential
def: "Electrochemical potential that arises at the reference electrode–measurement solution interface when\, during a potentiometric measurement\, the filling solution of the salt bridge of the reference electrode contacts the charged particles of a suspension."
comment: "The value of the anomalous liquid junction potential can exceed significantly the commonly occurring liquid junction potential, depending on the suspension species and the concentration of the filling solution. The contact between the electrolyte in the reference electrode (or its salt bridge) and the charged particles can change the ion arrangement around the particles and modify the approximate equality of the ion transport numbers in the electrolyte diffusion front (e.g., by ion exchange of \(\ce{H^{+}}\) or \(\ce{OH^{-}}\)); this ion exchange will diminish the suppression of the diffusion potential."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779010081
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16245
name: pIon
def: "General mathematical expression form of any ion X activity\: \\\[\\rm\{p\(ion\\ X\)\} = \{\\rm\{pX\}\} = -\\lg \{\\rm\{a_\{X\}\}\} = -\\lg \(\{\\rm\{m_\{X\}\} \\gamma_\{X\}/m^\{\\circ\}\}\)\\\]\, analogously to \\\[\\pu\{pH\} = -\\lg \{\\rm\{a_\{H\}\}\} = -\\lg \(\{\\rm\{m_\{H\}\} \\gamma_\{H\}/m^\{\\circ\}\}\)\\\]."
comment: "Practical pIon measurement with the proper reversible ISE can be carried out by means of a galvanic cell, composed correspondently to cell V. The accuracy and uncertainty of results obtained with ISEs depend analogously as in pH measurement for all on validity of standard solutions used, if the common guidelines for potentiometric measurement are taken in account."
comment: "The term "pIon" is used mainly in the literature, oriented to the practical routine work."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779010081
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16246
name: suspension pH
def: "Readings on a pH-meter scale obtained for a suspension of soil \(in water or electrolyte\) by any method for potentiometric pH measurement\, performed in a manner analogous to the pH measurement in solutions."
comment: "Most of the reported "suspension (soil) pH" values have no known quantitative connection with the hydrogen ion activity in suspensions; nevertheless, they are more or less repeatable characteristic values of the measured suspensions."
synonym: "soil suspension pH" []
synonym: "suspension soil pH" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779010081
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16247
name: bridgehead atom
def: "Atom that is part of two or more rings in a polycyclic molecule and that is separated from another bridgehead atom by bridges all of which contain at least one other atom."
synonym: "bridgehead" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1010
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16248
name: unimolecular
def: "Feature of a reaction in which only one molecular entity is involved."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1010
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16249
name: initialisation
def: "Process for converting a starting initiator or chain transfer agent into a macro-initiator or macro-chain-transfer agent during reversible-deactivation polymerization \(RDP\)."
comment: "In RAFT polymerization, initialization is sometimes known as the pre-equilibrium step."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08912
consider: goldbook:08935
consider: goldbook:08947
consider: goldbook:08962
consider: goldbook:08963

[Term]
id: goldbook:16250
name: conjugate
def: "Molecule or compound designed to support\, transport\, and/or deliver one or several active species in order to take advantage of their specificity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0502
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16251
name: scattering coefficient
def: "Negative Napierian logarithm of the ratio of the intensity of radiation scattered \(\\\(I_\{\\rm\{s\}\}\\\)\) by a non-absorbing sample to the incident intensity \(\\\(I_\{0\}\\\)\)\, divided by the path-length\, \\\(l\\\). \\\[s = -\\ln\(I_\{s\}/I_\{0\}\)/l\\\]"
comment: "SI unit: \(\pu{m-1}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08278

[Term]
id: goldbook:16252
name: numerical aperture
def: "For an optical fibre\, \\\(n_\{\\rm\{o\}\}\\\) sin \\\(\\theta_\{\\alpha\}\\\)\, where \\\(n_\{\\rm\{o\}\}\\\) is the refractive index of the exterior medium and \\\(\\theta_\{\\alpha\}\\\) is the maximum input half angle that can support propagation."
synonym: "NA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16253
name: molar activity \(material\)
def: "Activity of a specified radionuclide \(\\\(\\ce\{R\}\\\)\) in a material \(\\\(\\ce\{M\}\\\)\) divided by amount of substance of that material."
comment: "If the term 'molar activity' is used without qualification, it should be made clear whether it refers to a material or a radionuclide. See: molar activity of a radionuclide."
comment: "The SI unit of molar activity is \(\pu{Bq mol-1}\), but molar activity is often expressed in unit \(\pu{Ci mmol-1}\). (Curie, symbol \(\pu{Ci}\), is a former unit of activity equal to exactly \(\pu{3.7E10 Bq}\).)"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0302
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:08763

[Term]
id: goldbook:16254
name: Nernstian response
def: "Response of an ion-selective electrode according to a local thermodynamic equilibrium\, over a given range of activity \(or concentration\) that follows the Nernst equation."
comment: "For the Nernstian response, the potential difference of the ion-selective electrode cell is proportional to the decadic logarithm of the ionic activity of a given species (\(a_{\rm{A}}\)) with coefficient \((RT/z_{\rm{A}}F)/\log_{10}(\rm{e})\) (about \(0.0592/z_{\rm{A}}\,\pu{V}\) at \(\pu{298.15 K}\)), where \(R\) is the gas constant, \(T\) the thermodynamic temperature, \(F\) the Faraday constant, and \(z_{\rm{A}}\) the electron number of an electrochemical reaction of species \(\ce{A}\)."
comment: "Nernstian response implies ideal sensitivity, but not necessarily ideal selectivity, since interfering ions may also give a Nernstian response when they are present as the sole potential determining species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2018-0109
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09063
consider: goldbook:09068

[Term]
id: goldbook:16256
name: pre-column derivatisation
def: "Technique in chromatography in which the sample is chemically derivatized before entering the column."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:16257
name: phase volume ratio
def: "Volume of the mobile phase divided by volume of the stationary phase in a column in counter-current chromatography."
comment: "It is recommended that phase ratio in counter-current chromatography be given the subscript V (i.e. \(\beta_{\rm{V}} = V_{\rm{M}}/V_{\rm{S}}\)) to emphasize phase volume ratio."
comment: "The \(\beta\) in counter-current chromatography has been defined as the ratio of planetary radius (\(r\)) over main rotor radius (\(R\)), \(\beta = r/R\)."
comment: "The stationary phase volume retention ratio (\(S_{\rm{f}}\)) has been defined as the ratio of the volume of stationary phase (\(V_{\rm{s}}\)) to the total column/coil volume (\(V_{\rm{c}}\)), \(S_{\rm{f}} = V_{\rm{s}}/V_{\rm{c}}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09887

[Term]
id: goldbook:16258
name: total mobile-phase volume in column
def: "Sum of the interparticle volume of the column and intraparticle volume of the column\: \\\(V_\{\\rm\{t\}\} = V_\{0\} + V_\{\\rm\{i\}\}\\\)"
comment: "In the definition of \(V_{\rm{t}}\) the extra-column volume of the system (\(V_{\rm{ext}}\)) is neglected. If it is not negligible, it must also be added: \[V_{\rm{t}} = V_{0} + V_{\rm{i}} + V_{\rm{ext}}\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:11549

[Term]
id: goldbook:16259
name: retention time
def: "Retention time of a sample component\, the molecules of which are smaller than the largest pores of the particles of the stationary phase but larger than the smallest pores."
comment: "The retention time is related to the retention volume (in size-exclusion chromatography) (\(V_{\rm{R}}\)) and the flow rate (\(F_{\rm{c}}\)) by \(t_{\rm{R}} = V_{\rm{R}}/F_{\rm{c}}\) ."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:09963

[Term]
id: goldbook:16260
name: total mobile phase time
def: "Retention time of a sample component the molecules of which are smaller than the smallest pores of the particles of the stationary phase."
comment: "The total mobile phase time is related to the total mobile phase volume (in size-exclusion chromatography) (\(V_{\rm{t}}\)) and the flow rate (\(F_{\rm{c}}\)) by \(t_{\rm{t}} = V_{\rm{t}}/F_{\rm{c}}\) ."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111
