id: goldbook:A00129
name: acyl species
def: "Acyl intermediates include acyl anions\, acyl radicals and acyl cations \(synonym acylium ions\) which are formally derived from oxoacids $\\ce\{R_\{k\}E\(=O\)_\{l\}\(OH\)_\{m\}\}$ \($l  eq 0$\) by removal of a hydroxyl cation $\\ce\{HO^\{+\}\}$\, a hydroxyl radical $\\ce\{HO^\{.\}\}$ or a hydroxyl anion $\\ce\{HO^\{-\}\}$\, respectively\, and replacement analogues of such intermediates. Acyl anions\, radicals and cations can formally be represented by canonical forms having a negative charge\, an unpaired electron or a positive charge on the acid-generating element of the oxoacid.Acyl anions\, e.g. Acyl radicals\, e.g. Acyl cations\, e.g."
