[Term]
id: goldbook:A00137
name: additivity principle
def: "The hypothesis that each of several structural features of a molecular entity makes a separate and additive contribution to a property of the substance concerned. More specifically\, it is the hypothesis that each of the several substituent groups in a parent molecule makes a separate and additive contribution to the standard Gibbs energy change \(or Gibbs energy of activation\) corresponding to a particular equilibrium \(or rate of reaction\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
