[Term]
id: goldbook:A00176
name: aerosol
def: "Sol in which the dispersed phase is a solid\, a liquid or a mixture of both and the continuous phase is a gas \(usually air\)."
comment: "An aerosol can be characterized by its chemical composition, its radioactivity (if any), the particle size distribution, the electrical charge and the optical properties."
comment: "Modified from previous definition, within which particles with equivalent diameters usually between \(0.01\) and \(100\ \unicode[Times]{x3BC}\rm{m}\) are specified. This extends beyond the size range specified for a colloidal system. To avoid confusion the definition proposed here is recommended."
comment: "Owing to their size, the particles of the dispersed phase have a comparatively small settling velocity and hence exhibit some degree of stability in the earth's gravitational field."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779101801
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
