[Term]
id: goldbook:A00182
name: agglomeration
def: "Process of contact and adhesion whereby dispersed particles are held together by weak physical interactions ultimately leading to phase separation by the formation of precipitates of larger than colloidal size."
comment: "Agglomeration is a reversible process."
comment: "The definition proposed here is recommended for distinguishing agglomeration from aggregation."
synonym: "coagulation" []
synonym: "flocculation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779101801
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
