id: goldbook:A00228
name: alkyl groups
def: "Univalent groups derived from alkanes by removal of a hydrogen atom from any carbon atom $\\ce\{–C_\{n\}H_\{2n+1\}\}$. The groups derived by removal of a hydrogen atom from a terminal carbon atom of unbranched alkanes form a subclass of normal alkyl \($n$-alkyl\) groups $\\ce\{H\(CH2\)_\{n\}\}$. The groups $\\ce\{RCH2\}$\, $\\ce\{R2CH\}$ \($\\ce\{R  eq H\}$\)\, and $\\ce\{R3C\}$ \($\\ce\{R  eq H\}$\) are primary\, secondary and tertiary alkyl groups\, respectively."
