id: goldbook:A00268
name: amidium ions
def: "Cations formally derived by the addition of one hydron to the $\\ce\{N\}$ or $\\ce\{O\}$ atom of an amide and $N$-hydrocarbyl derivatives thereof. In organic chemistry an unspecified amidium ion is commonly a carboxamidium ion  or  The term does not imply knowledge concerning the position of the cationic centre\, e.g. $\\ce\{PhC\(=O\)N^\{+\}Me3\}$ N\,N\,N-trimethylbenzamidium."
