[Term]
id: goldbook:A00278
name: aminiumyl radical ions
def: "Radicals cations\, $\\ce\{R3N^\{.+\}\}$\, derivable from aminium ions\, $\\ce\{R3NH^\{+\}\}$\, by removal of a hydrogen atom. Aminiumyl radical ions are\, except for $\\ce\{H3N^\{.+\}\}$\, synonymous with the ammoniumyl radical ions. As the term ammonium is well known\, ammoniumyl radical ions is the more desirable class name."
