[Term]
id: goldbook:A00430
name: area of interface
def: "In all measurements it is desirable that quantities like the charge and the capacity be related to unit\, true\, surface area of the interface. While this is relatively simple for a liquid-liquid interface\, there are great difficulties when one phase is solid. In any report of these quantities it is essential to give a clear statement as to whether they refer to the true or the apparent \(geometric\) area and\, especially if the former is used\, precisely how it was measured."
