[Term]
id: goldbook:A00529
name: autophobicity
def: "If adsorption equilibrium and mutual saturation of the phases is not achieved instantly\, it is possible to distinguish the initial spreading tension\, \\\(\\sigma _\{\\rm\{i\}\}^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}\\\)\, from the final spreading tension\, \\\(\\sigma _\{\\rm\{i\}\}^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}\\\)\, when equilibrium has been reached. In the case in which \\\(\\sigma _\{\\rm\{i\}\}^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}\\\) is positive\, while \\\(\\sigma _\{\\rm\{i\}\}^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}\\\) is negative\, the system is said to exhibit autophobicity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:S05472

[Term]
id: goldbook:A00531
name: autoprotolysis
def: "A proton \(hydron\) transfer reaction between two identical molecules \(usually a solvent\)\, one acting as a Brønsted acid and the other as a Brønsted base. For example\:"
