[Term]
id: goldbook:A00543
name: Avogadro constant
def: "The Avogadro constant\, \\\(N_\{\\rm\{A\}\} = \\pu\{6.02214076E23 mol-1\}\\\)\, is a proportionality constant between the quantity amount of substance \(\\\(n\\\)\, with unit mole\) and the quantity for counting entities \(\\\(N\\\) with unit one\, symbol 1\)\, \\\(N = N_\{\\rm\{A\}\}\\ n\\\)."
comment: "In the revision of the International System of Units (SI) of 2019 the Avogadro constant became one of the seven defining constants with the exact value \(\pu{6.02214076E23 mol-1}\)."
comment: "The Avogadro number is the exact numerical value of the Avogadro constant, \(\pu{6.02214076E23}\)"
comment: "While the symbol \(N_{\rm{A}}\) is used to honour Amedeo Avogadro, the symbol \(L\) is used in honour of Josef Loschmidt."
