[Term]
id: goldbook:A04388
name: π-adduct
def: "An adduct formed by electron-pair donation from a $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}orbital\}$ into a $\\ce\{\\upsigma\\!\\mbox\{-\}orbital\}$\, or from a $\\ce\{\\upsigma\\!\\mbox\{-\}orbital\}$ into a $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}orbital\}$\, or from a $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}orbital\}$ into a $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}orbital\}$. For example\:  Such an adduct has commonly been known as a '$\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}complex\}$'\, but\, as the bonding is not necessarily weak\, it is better to avoid the term complex."
synonym: "π-complex" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
