[Term]
id: goldbook:B00591
name: baking
def: "The process in which the carbonaceous binder\, usually coal tar pitch or petroleum pitch\, as part of a shaped carbon mix is converted to carbon yielding a rigid carbon body by the slow application of heat. The process can take as little as \\\(14\\ \\rm\{days\}\\\) in coarse-grained\, electrothermic grades \(low binder level\) and as long as \\\(36\\ \\rm\{days\}\\\) in ultra-fine-grained\, specialty grades \(high binder level\). The final baking temperature can be in the range of \\\(1100\{-\}1500\\ \\rm\{K\}\\\)\, depending on the grade."
