id: goldbook:B00701
name: bond energy
def: "The average value of the gas-phase bond dissociation energies \(usually at a temperature of \\\(298\\ \\rm\{K\}\\\)\) for all bonds of the same type within the same chemical species. The mean bond energy for methane\, for example\, is one-fourth the enthalpy of reaction for\:  Tabulated bond energies are generally values of bond energies averaged over a number of selected typical chemical species containing that type of bond."
