[Term]
id: goldbook:BT06813
name: bioavailability
def: "Ratio of the systemic exposure from extravascular \(ev\) exposure to that following intravenous \(iv\) exposure as described by the equation\: \\\[F=\\frac\{A_\{\\rm\{ev\}\}\\ D_\{\\rm\{iv\}\}\}\{B_\{\\rm\{iv\}\}\\ D_\{\\rm\{ev\}\}\}\\\] where \\\(F\\\) is the bioavailabilty\, \\\(A\\\) and \\\(B\\\) are areas under the \(plasma\) concentration-time curve following extravascular and intravenous administration\, respectively\, and \\\(D_\{\\rm\{ev\}\}\\\) and \\\(D_\{\\rm\{iv\}\}\\\) are the administered extravascular and intravenous doses."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200476051033
