[Term]
id: goldbook:BT06997
name: back donation
def: "A description of the bonding of $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}conjugated\}$ ligands to a transition metal which involves a synergic process with donation of electrons from the filled $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}orbital\}$ or lone electron pair orbital of the ligand into an empty orbital of the metal \(donor–acceptor bond\)\, together with release \(back donation\) of electrons from an nd orbital of the metal \(which is of $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}symmetry\}$ with respect to the metal–ligand axis\) into the empty $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!^\{\\ast\}\\mbox\{-\}antibonding orbital\}$ $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}complex\}$ of the ligand."
synonym: "Chatt–Dewar–Duncanson model" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
