[Term]
id: goldbook:C00771
name: cage effect
def: "When in a condensed phase\, or in a dense gas\, reactant molecules come together\, or species are formed in proximity to one another\, and are caged in by surrounding molecules\, they may undergo a set of collisions known as an encounter; the term 'cage effect' is then applied.The cage effect is also known as the Franck–Rabinowitch effect."
