[Term]
id: goldbook:C00773
name: calcination
def: "Heating to high temperatures in air or oxygen."
comment: "In sol-gel processing the term applies to the heating of a polymer network containing metal compounds to convert it into an oxide network."
comment: "Modified from previous definition. The definition proposed here is more explicit about the elevated temperatures that are required."
comment: "The term is most likely to be applied to a step in the preparation of a catalyst."
