[Term]
id: goldbook:C00807
name: carbene analogues
def: "The electrically neutral mononuclear hydrides of group 14 having two non-bonding electrons\, the electrically neutral mononuclear hydrides of group 15 having four non-bonding electrons\, and also the compound $\\ce\{HB\{\:\}\}$ . The names of a number of these are shown below.  $\\ce\{RB\{\:\}\}$boranylidenes$\\ce\{RAs\{\:\}\}$arsanylidenes $\\ce\{RN\{\:\}\}$nitrenes$\\ce\{R2Sn\{\:\}\}$stannylidenes $\\ce\{R2Si\{\:\}\}$silylenes$\\ce\{RSb\{\:\}\}$stibanylidenes $\\ce\{RP\{\:\}\}$phosphanylidenes$\\ce\{R2Pb\{\:\}\}$plumbylidenes $\\ce\{R2Ge\{\:\}\}$germylidenes  Note that if $\\ce\{R\} = \\ce\{H\}$\, these compounds are parent hydrides; derivatives formed by substitution are named accordingly. However\, if the substituent's first atom\, bearing the free valence\, is of the same element as the atom of the carbene analogue\, other parent compounds may be required \(see carbenes\)\, e.g. $\\ce\{HN\{\:\}\}$ nitrene; $\\ce\{CH3N\{\:\}\}$ methylnitrene; $\\ce\{H2NN\{\:\}\}$ diazanylidene \(synonym isodiazene\, not aminonitrene\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567081307
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
