[Term]
id: goldbook:C00811
name: carbenium centre
def: "The three-coordinate carbon atom in a carbenium ion to which the excess positive charge of the ion \(other than that located on heteroatoms\) may be formally considered to be largely attributed\, i.e. which has one vacant p-orbital. \(N.B. It is not always possible to uniquely identify such an atom.\) This formal attribution of charge often does not express the real charge distribution."
