[Term]
id: goldbook:C00825
name: carbon–carbon composite
def: "A carbon fibre-reinforced carbon matrix material. The carbon matrix phase is typically formed by solid\, liquid or gaseous pyrolysis of an organic precursor material. The matrix is either a graphitizable carbon or non-graphitizable carbon\, and the carbonaceous reinforcement is fibrous in form. The composite may also contain other components in particulate or fibrous forms."
