[Term]
id: goldbook:C00986
name: charcoal
def: "A traditional term for a char obtained from wood\, peat\, coal or some related natural organic materials."
comment: "Charcoal has highly reactive inner surfaces and a low sulfur content. It has or has had, therefore, a variety of uses, e.g. in ferrous metallurgy and for gunpowder (minor uses: medical purposes and paint materials)."
