[Term]
id: goldbook:C00999
name: charge separation
def: "A process in which\, under the influence of a suitable driving force \(e.g. provided by photoexcitation\)\, electronic charge moves in a direction that increases the difference in local charges between donor and acceptor sites. electron transfer between neutral species is one of the most important examples."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
