[Term]
id: goldbook:C01000
name: charge shift
def: "A process in which under the influence of a suitable driving force \(e.g. provided by photoexcitation\) electronic charge moves without changing the difference in local charges between donor and acceptor sites. Electron transfer reversing the charges in a system composed of a neutral donor and a cationic acceptor or of a neutral acceptor and an anionic donor provide prominent examples."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
