[Term]
id: goldbook:C01004
name: charge-transfer device
def: "A charge-transfer device has a metal oxide semiconductor \(MOS\) structure that is composed of many independent pixels where charge is stored in such a way that the charge pattern corresponds to the irradiation pattern. These devices can be linear or two-dimensional. According to the method used to detect the charge pattern\, two types of charge-transfer devices can be distinguished\: charge-coupled devices \(CCDs\) and charge-injection devices \(CIDs\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567101745
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03255
consider: goldbook:S05591

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01005
name: charge-transfer reaction
def: "An ion/neutral species reaction wherein the total charge on the reactant ion is transferred initially to the reactant neutral species so that the reactant ion becomes a neutral entity. Considering some of the possible reactions of ions $\\ce\{M^\{2+\}\}$\, $\\ce\{M^\{+\}\}$ and $\\ce\{M^\{−\}\}$ with a neutral species $\\ce\{X\}$\, these would be further categorized as follows\:    All are ion/neutral species reactions and also charge permutation reactions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163101541
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01006
name: charge-transfer state
def: "A state related to the ground state by a charge-transfer transition."
synonym: "CT" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "CT state" []
