[Term]
id: goldbook:C01017
name: chemical activation
def: "When some of the energy required for a reaction is provided by a preceding exothermic chemical reaction there is said to be chemical activation. For example\, in the scheme\:   some or all of the energy required for X to decompose is provided by the first reaction."
