[Term]
id: goldbook:C01031
name: chemical oxygen demand
def: "A measure of the amount of oxygen\, divided by the volume of the system\, required to oxidize the organic \(and inorganic\) matter in wastewater using a chemically oxidizing agent. In practice\, it is usually expressed in milligrams $\\ce\{O2\}$ per litre."
synonym: "COD" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:L03594

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01032
name: chemical potential
def: "The chemical potential of a substance B in a mixture of substances B\, C ... is related to the Gibbs energy \\\(G\\\) of the mixture by\: \\\[\\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}=\(\\frac\{\\partial G\}\{\\partial n_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\}\)_\{T\,p\,n_\{\\rm\{C\} eq \\rm\{B\}\}\}\\\] where \\\(T\\\) is the thermodynamic temperature\, \\\(p\\\) is the pressure and \\\(n_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\)\, \\\(n_\{\\rm\{C\}\}\\\)\, ... are the amounts of substance of B\, C\, ... . For a pure substance B\, the chemical potential \\\(\\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}^\{*\}\\\) is given by\: \\\[\\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}^\{*\}=\\frac\{G^\{*\}\}\{n_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\}=G_\{\\rm\{m\}\}^\{*\}\\\] where \\\(G_\{\\rm\{m\}\}^\{*\}\\\) is the molar Gibbs energy\, and where the superscript * attached to a symbol denotes the property of the pure substance. The superscript \\\(^\{⦵\}\\\) or \\\(^\{\\circ\}\\\) attached to a symbol may be used to denote a standard thermodynamic quantity."
synonym: "partial molar Gibbs energy" []
