consider: goldbook:R05026

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01058
name: chirality
def: "The geometric property of a rigid object \(or spatial arrangement of points or atoms\) of being non-superposable on its mirror image; such an object has no symmetry elements of the second kind \(a mirror plane\, \\\(\\sigma =S_\{1\}\\\)\, a centre of inversion\, \\\(i=S_\{2\}\\\)\, a rotation-reflection axis\, \\\(S_\{2n\}\\\)\). If the object is superposable on its mirror image the object is described as being achiral."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00069
consider: goldbook:H02735
consider: goldbook:I03146
consider: goldbook:S06144

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01059
name: chirality axis
def: "An axis about which a set of ligands is held so that it results in a spatial arrangement which is not superposable on its mirror image. For example with an allene $\\ce\{abC=C=Ccd\}$ the chiral axis is defined by the $\\ce\{C=C=C\}$ bonds; and with an ortho-substituted biphenyl the atoms $\\ce\{C-1\}$\, $\\ce\{C-1'\}$\, $\\ce\{C-4\}$ and $\\ce\{C-4'\}$ lie on the chiral axis."
synonym: "axis of chirality" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01057
consider: goldbook:L03518

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01060
name: chirality centre
def: "An atom holding a set of ligands in a spatial arrangement which is not superposable on its mirror image. A chirality centre is thus a generalized extension of the concept of the asymmetric carbon atom to central atoms of any element\, for example $\\ce\{N^\{+\}abcd\}$\, $\\ce\{Pabc\}$ as well as $\\ce\{Cabcd\}$ ."
synonym: "asymmetric centre" []
synonym: "centre of chirality" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00479
consider: goldbook:C01058
consider: goldbook:L03518

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01061
name: chirality element
def: "General name for a chirality axis\, chirality centre or chirality plane. Also referred to as an element of chirality."
synonym: "element of chirality" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01059
consider: goldbook:C01060
consider: goldbook:C01062

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01062
name: chirality plane
def: "A planar unit connected to an adjacent part of the structure by a bond which results in restricted torsion so that the plane cannot lie in a symmetry plane. For example with \(E\)-cyclooctene the chiral plane includes the double bond carbon atoms and all four atoms attached to the double bond; with a monosubstituted paracyclophane the chiral plane includes the monosubstituted benzene ring with its three hydrogen atoms and the three other atoms linked to the ring \(i.e. from the substituent and the two chains linking the two benzene rings\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01057

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01063
name: chirality sense
def: "The property that distinguishes enantiomorphs. The specification of two enantiomorphic forms by reference to an oriented space e.g. of a screw\, a right threaded one or a left threaded one. The expression 'opposite chirality' is short for 'opposite chirality sense'."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01058

