[Term]
id: goldbook:C01120
name: coalification
def: "A geological process of formation of materials with increasing content of the element carbon from organic materials that occurs in a first\, biological stage into peats\, followed by a gradual transformation into coal by action of moderate temperature \(about \\\(500\\ \\rm\{K\}\\\)\) and high pressure in a geochemical stage."
comment: "Coalification is a dehydrogenation process with a reaction rate slower by many orders of magnitude than that of carbonization. Some specific reactions approach completion before others have started. The dehydrogenation remains incomplete. The degree of coalification reached by an organic material in the process of coalification increases progressively and can be defined by means of the measured C/H ratio and of the residual contents of oxygen, sulfur and nitrogen."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567030473
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C00840
consider: goldbook:T06446

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01121
name: coal tar pitch
def: "A residue produced by distillation or heat treatment of coal tar. It is a solid at room temperature\, consists of a complex mixture of numerous predominantly aromatic hydrocarbons and heterocyclics\, and exhibits a broad softening range instead of a defined melting temperature."
comment: "The hydrogen aromaticity in coal tar pitch (ratio of aromatic to total content of hydrogen atoms) varies from 0.7 to 0.9."
