[Term]
id: goldbook:C01128
name: cofactors
def: "Organic molecules \(cf. coenzymes\) or ions \(usually metal ions\) that are required by an enzyme of its activity. They may be attached either loosely or tightly prosthetic group\) to the enzyme. A cofactor binds with its associated protein \(apoenzymes\)\, which is functionally inactive\, to form the active enzyme \(holoenzyme\)."
