[Term]
id: goldbook:C01176
name: colloidally stable
def: "Particles which do not aggregate at a significant rate\: the precise connotation depends on the type of aggregation under consideration. For example\, a concentrated paint is called stable by some people because oil and pigment do not separate out at a measurable rate\, and unstable by others because the pigment particles aggregate into a continuous network."
