[Term]
id: goldbook:C01182
name: column chromatography
def: "A separation technique in which the stationary bed is within a tube. The particles of the solid stationary phase or support coated with a liquid stationary phase may fill the whole inside volume of the tube \(packed column\) or be concentrated on or along the inside tube wall leaving an open\, unrestricted path for the mobile phase in the middle part of the tube \(open-tubular column\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01183
name: column volume
def: "The geometric volume of the part of the tube that contains the packing\: \\\[V_\{\\rm\{c\}\} = A_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\ L\\\] where \\\(A_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\\) is the internal cross-sectional area of the tube and \\\(L\\\) the length of the packed part of the column. In the case of wall-coated open-tubular columns the column volume corresponds to the geometric volume of the whole tube having a liquid or a solid stationary phase on its wall."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01184
name: combination electrode
def: "An ion-selective electrode and an external reference electrode combined in a single unit\, thereby avoiding the need for a separate external reference electrode."
