[Term]
id: goldbook:C01229
name: concentration in experimental surface
def: "The amount of the material of interest divided by the total amount of substances in the volume of interest. Concentration may be defined in terms of numbers of atoms \(particles\) \(\\\(\\rm\{ppma\}\\\)\) or in terms of weight \(\\\(\\frac\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{g\}\}\{\\rm\{g\}\}\\\)\)."
