[Term]
id: goldbook:C01290
name: contact angle
def: "When a liquid does not spread on a substrate \(usually a solid\)\, a contact angle \\\(\\left\(\\theta\\right\) \\\) is formed which is defined as the angle between two of the interfaces at the three-phase line of contact. It must always be stated which interfaces are used to define \\\(\\theta\\\). It is often necessary to distinguish between the 'advancing contact angle' \\\(\(\\theta _\{\\rm\{a\}\}\) \\\)\, the 'receding contact angle' \\\(\(\\theta _\{\\rm\{r\}\}\) \\\) and the 'equilibrium contact angle' \\\(\(\\theta _\{\\rm\{e\}\}\) \\\). When \\\(\(\\theta _\{\\rm\{r\}\}\)  eq \(\\theta _\{\\rm\{a\}\}\) \\\) the system is said to exhibit contact angle hysteresis"
