[Term]
id: goldbook:C01301
name: continuous flow enthalpimetry
def: "A term used to describe methods wherein a reagent is continuously fed into a flowing analyte stream and the temperature difference is measured before and after a reactor \(mixing chamber\). Alternatively\, the temperature may be measured in a differential manner between a reference and a reactor chamber. The analyte concentration is directly proportional to the measured temperature difference. Synonymous with continuous flow enthalpimetric analysis."
