id: goldbook:C01324
name: cooperative transition
def: "A transition that involves a simultaneous\, collective displacement or change of state of the atoms and/or electrons in the entire system. Examples\: An order–disorder transition of atoms or electrons\, as in an alloy\, a ferromagnet or superconductor; a Jahn–Teller or ferroic transition; a martensitic transition."
