[Term]
id: goldbook:C01346
name: correlation analysis
def: "The use of empirical correlations relating one body of experimental data to another\, with the objective of finding quantitative estimates of the factors underlying the phenomena involved. Correlation analysis in organic chemistry often uses linear free-energy relations for rates or equilibria of reactions\, but the term also embraces similar analysis of physical \(most commonly spectroscopic\) properties and of biological activity."
synonym: "QSAR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:L03551
consider: goldbook:Q04981

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01347
name: correlation coefficient
def: "A measure of the degree of interrelationship which exists between two measured quantities\, \\\(x\\\) and \\\(y\\\); the correlation coefficient \(\\\(r\\\)\) is defined by the following relation\: \\\[r=\\frac\{\\sum _\{\\begin\{array\}\{c\} i=1 \\end\{array\}\}^\{n\}\(x_\{i\}- \\overline\{x\}\)\\ \(y_\{i\}- \\overline\{y\}\)\}\{\\sqrt\{\\sum _\{\\begin\{array\}\{c\} i=1 \\end\{array\}\}^\{n\}\(x_\{i\}- \\overline\{x\}\)^\{2\}\\ \\sum _\{\\begin\{array\}\{c\} i=1 \\end\{array\}\}^\{n\}\(y_\{i\}- \\overline\{y\}\)^\{2\}\}\}\\\] where \\\(x_\{i\}\\\) and \\\(y_\{i\}\\\) are the measured values in the \\\(i\\\)th experiment of \\\(n\\\) total experiments\, \\\(\\overline\{x\}\\\) and \\\(\\overline\{y\}\\\) are the arithmetic means of \\\(x_\{i\}\\\) and \\\(y_\{i\}\\\)\: \\\[\\overline\{x\}=\\frac\{\\sum _\{\\begin\{array\}\{c\} i=1 \\end\{array\}\}^\{n\}x_\{i\}\}\{n\}\\\] \(similar expression for \\\(\\overline\{y\}\\\)\). The linear correlation coefficient indicates the degree to which two quantities are linearly related. If \\\(x=a\\ y\\\) is followed then \\\(r=1\\\)\, and departures from this relationship decrease \\\(r\\\); if interpretations of data based on the linear correlation coefficient are to be made\, one should consult a book on statistics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01124

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01348
name: correlation diagram
def: "A diagram which shows the relative energies of orbitals\, configurations\, valence bond structures\, or states of reactants and products of a reaction\, as a function of the molecular geometry\, or another suitable parameter. An example involves the interpolation between the energies obtained for the united atoms and the values for the separated atoms limits."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:V06588

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01349
name: correlation energy
def: "The difference between the Hartree–Fock energy calculated for a system and the exact non-relativistic energy of that system. The correlation energy arises from the approximate representation of the electron-electron repulsions in the Hartree–Fock method."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
