[Term]
id: goldbook:C01358
name: corrosion rate
def: "The amount of substance transferred per unit time at a specified surface. Using Faraday's law\, the corrosion rate\, \\\( u_\{\\mathrm\{cor\}\}\\\)\, can be formally expressed as an electric current which at the corrosion potential is called the corrosion current\, \\\(I_\{\\mathrm\{cor\}\}\\\)\, e.g. for the anodic dissolution of one component of a material with \\\( u_\{\\mathrm\{cor\}\}\\\) in \\\(\\pu\{mol s-1\}\\\) and \\\(I_\{\\mathrm\{cor\}\}\\\) in \\\(\\mathrm\{A\}\\\) one obtains \\\(I_\{\\mathrm\{cor\}\}=n\\ F\\  u_\{\\mathrm\{cor\}\}\\\)\, \\\(n\\\) being the charge number of the electrode reaction and \\\(F\\\) the Faraday constant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198961010019
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
