[Term]
id: goldbook:C01394
name: critical excitation energy
def: "Minimum energy to excite a specific analytical signal. The term is most frequently used in connection with the generation of X-ray spectra\, designating the ionization \(binding\) energy of the orbital on which the transition ends."
