[Term]
id: goldbook:C01400
name: critical solution point
def: "The point\, with coordinates critical solution temperatures and critical composition\, on a temperature-composition phase diagram at which the distinction between co-existent phases vanishes. In solid-solid\, solid-liquid and liquid-liquid systems both upper and lower critical solution temperatures and corresponding 'critical solution compositions' can occur. Synonymous with consolute point."
synonym: "consolute point" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466030577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:C01402
name: critical temperature
def: "That temperature\, characteristic of each gas\, above which it is not possible to liquefy a given gas."
