[Term]
id: goldbook:CT06920
name: chiral stationary phase
def: "A stationary phase which incorporates a chiral selector. If not a constituent of the stationary phase as a whole\, the chiral selector can be chemically bonded to \(chiral bonded stationary phase \) or immobilised onto the surface of a solid support or column wall \(chiral coated stationary phase\)\, or simply dissolved in the liquid stationary phase."
