consider: goldbook:MT06971

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT06956
name: conformational analysis
def: "Conformational analysis consists of the exploration of energetically favourable spatial arrangements \(shapes\) of a molecule \(conformations\) using molecular mechanics\, molecular dynamics\, quantum chemical calculations or analysis of experimentally-determined structural data\, e.g\, NMR or crystal structures.Molecular mechanics and quantum chemical methods are employed to compute conformational energies\, whereas systematic and random searches\, Monte Carlo\, molecular dynamics\, and distance geometry are methods \(often combined with energy minimization procedures\) used to explore the conformational space."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199769051137
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01259
consider: goldbook:M03985

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07009
name: chemical bond
def: "When forces acting between two atoms or groups of atoms lead to the formation of a stable independent molecular entity\, a chemical bond is considered to exist between these atoms or groups. The principal characteristic of a bond in a molecule is the existence of a region between the nuclei of constant potential contours that allows the potential energy to improve substantially by atomic contraction at the expense of only a small increase in kinetic energy. Not only directed covalent bonds characteristic of organic compounds\, but also bonds such as those existing between sodium cations and chloride anions in a crystal of sodium chloride or the bonds binding aluminium to six molecules of water in its environment\, and even weak bonds that link two molecules of $\\ce\{O2\}$ into $\\ce\{O4\}$\, are to be attributed to chemical bonds."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:K03402
consider: goldbook:S05900

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07010
name: closed shell molecular systems
def: "Even-electron atomic or molecular systems whose electron configurations consist of doubly occupied orbitals."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07011
name: concerted reaction
def: "A single-step reaction through which reactants are directly transformed into products\, i.e.\, without involvement of any intermediates."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:S05691

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07012
name: conservation of orbital symmetry
def: "The orbital symmetry control of concerted reactions; this requires transformation of the molecular orbitals of reactants into those of products to proceed continuously by following a reaction path along which the symmetry of these orbitals remains unchanged. Reactions which adhere to this requirement are classified as symmetry-allowed reactions\, and those which do not as symmetry-forbidden reactions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:O04320
consider: goldbook:R05174
consider: goldbook:T06446

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07013
name: Coulomb repulsion
def: "The potential energy component corresponding to the electrostatic interaction between each pair of charged particles\: \\\[V=\\frac\{1\}\{4\\\: \\pi\\\: \\varepsilon_\{0\}\}\\ \\sum _\{i\}\\sum _\{j \\lt i\}e_\{i\}\\ e_\{j\}\\ \\Delta r_\{ij\}\\\] where \\\(\\varepsilon _\{0\}\\\) is the permittivity of a vacuum\, \\\(\\Delta r_\{ij\}\\\) is the distance between the two particles\, and \\\(e_\{i\}\\\) and \\\(e_\{j\}\\\) are the charges on particles \\\(i\\\) and \\\(j\\\). In molecular orbital theory\, the electrostatic repulsion between the two electrons occupying the orbitals \\\(\\Psi _\{i\}\\\) and \\\(\\Psi _\{j\}\\\). In the Hartree–Fock method\, the mean Coulomb repulsion is determined by the value of the coulomb integral \\\[J_\{ij\}=\\int \\int \\Psi _\{i\\rm\{*\}\}\\left\(\\mathbf\{r\}_\{1\}\\right\)\\ \\Psi _\{i\}\\left\(\\mathbf\{r\}_\{1\}\\right\)\\ \\left\(\\frac\{e^\{2\}\}\{r_\{12\}\}\\right\)\\ \\Psi _\{j\\rm\{*\}\}\\left\(\\mathbf\{r\}_\{2\}\\right\)\\ \\Psi _\{j\}\\left\(\\mathbf\{r\}_\{2\}\\right\)  \\ \\mathrm\{d\}\\mathbf\{r\}_\{1\} \\ \\mathrm\{d\}\\mathbf\{r\}_\{2\} = \\lt ij|ij \\gt\\\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01365
consider: goldbook:C01366
consider: goldbook:ET07034
consider: goldbook:H02747
consider: goldbook:M03996
consider: goldbook:P04507

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07014
name: coupled cluster method
def: "A method employed in ab initio quantum mechanical calculations providing for a higher-level treatment of electron correlation beyond MP4."
synonym: "CC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "CC method" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
