consider: goldbook:C01282
consider: goldbook:I03295

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07136
name: crosslinking
def: "Reaction involving sites or groups on existing macromolecules or an interaction between existing macromolecules that results in the formation of a small region in a macromolecule from which at least four chains emanate."
comment: "A reaction of a reactive chain end of a linear macromolecule with an internal reactive site of another linear macromolecule results in the formation of a branch point, but is not regarded as a crosslinking reaction."
comment: "The small region may be an atom, a group of atoms, or a number of branch points connected by bonds, groups of atoms, or oligomeric chains."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779101801
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01409
consider: goldbook:L03554
consider: goldbook:O04286

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07137
name: curing
def: "Chemical process of converting a prepolymer or a polymer into a polymer of higher molar mass and then into a network."
comment: "Curing is achieved by the induction of chemical reactions which might or might not require mixing with a chemical curing agent."
comment: "Physical aging, crystallization, physical crosslinking and post-polymerization reactions are sometimes referred to as 'curing'. Use of the term 'curing' to describe such processes is deprecated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779101801
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01434
