[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07200
name: cationic polymer
def: "Polymer composed of positively charged macromolecules and an equivalent amount of counter-anions."
comment: "If a substantial fraction of constitutional units carries positive charges, then a cationic polymer is a polyelectrolyte."
comment: "The positive charges may be fixed on groups located in main chains as in an ionene or in pendant groups."
comment: "The term cationic polymer should not be used to denote a polymer prepared by cationic polymerization."
