[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07345
name: computational photochemistry
def: "Aspects of research that address the study of photochemical events by means of computer simulations using specialized software tools and strategies in order to get an understanding of the process at a microscopic level. The aim is to uncover the mechanism of known photochemical processes\, design new photochemical systems\, and predict molecular properties that are experimentally inaccessible."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:CT07346
name: concentration depolarization
def: "Loss of emission anisotropy due to transfer of electronic excitation from photo-selected molecules to other molecules with different orientations."
