[Term]
id: goldbook:D01559
name: degenerate rearrangement
def: "A molecular rearrangement in which the principal product is indistinguishable \(in the absence of isotopic labelling\) from the principal reactant. The term includes both 'degenerate intramolecular rearrangements' and reactions that involve intermolecular transfer of atoms or groups \('degenerate intermolecular rearrangements'\)\: both are degenerate isomerizations. The occurrence of degenerate rearrangements may be detectable by isotopic labelling or by dynamic NMR techniques. For example\: thesigmatropic rearrangement of hexa-1\,5-diene \(Cope rearrangement\)\:  Synonymous but less preferable terms are 'automerization'\, 'permutational isomerism'\, 'isodynamic transformation'\, 'topomerization'."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
