[Term]
id: goldbook:D01602
name: deposition velocity
def: "The ratio of flux density \(often given in units of \\\(\\pu\{g cm-2 s-1\}\\\)\) of a substance at a sink surface to its concentration in the atmosphere \(corresponding units of \\\(\\pu\{g cm-3\}\\\)\). While the units of this ratio are clearly those of velocity \(in this case \\\(\\pu\{cm s-1\}\\\)\)\, the ratio is not a flow velocity in the normal sense of the word."
