[Term]
id: goldbook:D01660
name: diabatic photoreaction
def: "Within the Born–Oppenheimer approximation\, a reaction beginning on one excited state 'potential-energy surface' and ending\, as a result of radiationless transition\, on another surface\, usually that of the ground state. Also called non-adiabatic."
