id: goldbook:D01661
name: diacylamines
def: "Compounds having two acyl groups substituted on ammonia or a primary amine acyl-NR-acyl. They are also known as secondary amides and\, especially the cyclic examples derived from diacids\, as imides\, e.g. $\\ce\{\[RC\(=O\)\]2NR\}$\, $\\ce\{RS\(=O\)2NHC\(=O\)R\}$ ."
