[Term]
id: goldbook:D01671
name: diamond
def: "An allotropic form of the element carbon with cubic structure \(space group \\\(O_\{h\}^\{7\}- Fd3m\\\)\) which is thermodynamically stable at pressures above \\\(6\\ \\rm\{GPa\}\\\) at room temperature and metastable at atmospheric pressure. At low pressures diamond converts rapidly to graphite at temperatures above \\\(1900\\ \\rm\{K\}\\\) in an inert atmosphere. The chemical bonding between the carbon atoms is covalent with \\\(\\mathrm\{sp\}^\{3\}\\\) hybridization."
comment: "There is also a hexagonal diamond-like structure of the element carbon (lonsdaleite)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567030473
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
