[Term]
id: goldbook:D01699
name: dienes
def: "Compounds that contain two fixed double bonds \(usually assumed to be between carbon atoms\). Dienes in which the two double-bond units are linked by one single bond are termed conjugated\, e.g. $\\ce\{CH2=CH–CH=CH2\}$ buta-1\,3-diene. Dienes in which the double bonds are adjacent are called cumulative\, e.g. $\\ce\{CH3–CH=C=CH2\}$ buta-1\,2-diene. Those in which one or more of the unsaturated carbon atoms is replaced by a heteroatom may be called heterodienes."
