[Term]
id: goldbook:D01729
name: diffusion potential
def: "For an ideal dilute solution\, \\\(\\Delta \\mathit\{\\Phi \}_\{\\rm\{d\}\}\\\) is the integral of \\\( abla \\mathit\{\\Phi \}\\\) \(given by the following equation\) across the boundary between two regions of different concentrations. \\\[ abla \\mathit\{\\Phi \}=\\frac\{R\\ T\\ \\sum D_\{i\}\\ z_\{i\}\\  abla c_\{i\}\}\{F\\ \\sum s_\{i\}^\{2\}\\ D_\{i\}\\ c_\{i\}\}\\\] where \\\(D_\{i\}\\\) is the diffusion coefficient of species \\\(i\\\)\, \\\(z_\{i\}\\\) is the charge number of species \\\(i\\\)\, \\\(c_\{i\}\\\) is the concentration of species \\\(i\\\)\, \\\(R\\\) is the gas constant\, \\\(T\\\) is the thermodynamic temperature\, and \\\(F\\\) is the Faraday constant."
