[Term]
id: goldbook:D01740
name: dilution rate
def: "The ratio of the ingoing volume flow rate \(\\\(\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}V\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\)\) and the culture volume \(\\\(V\\\)\). In continuous fermentation\, a measure of a rate at which the existing medium is replaced with fresh medium\, \\\(D\\\) is the reciprocal of the hydraulic retention time \(\\\(\\mathrm\{HRT\}\\\)\)."
