[Term]
id: goldbook:D01745
name: di-π-methane rearrangement
def: "Photochemical reaction of a molecular entity comprising two $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}systems\}$\, separated by a saturated carbon atom \(a 1\,4-diene or an allyl-substituted aromatic analogue\)\, to form an ene- \(or aryl-\) substituted cyclopropane."
comment: "The rearrangement formally amounts to a 1,2 shift of one ene group (in the diene) or the aryl group (in the allyl-aromatic analogue) and 'bond formation' between the lateral carbons of the non-migrating moiety."
