[Term]
id: goldbook:D01861
name: droplet
def: "A small liquid particle. The size of droplets encountered in the atmosphere extends over a wide range; e.g. liquid aerosol solutions which make up the fine particle fraction of continental tropospheric aerosol are usually \\\(2\\ \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{m\}\\\) in diameter. Cloud water droplets usually have diameters in the range of \\\(5\{-\}70\\ \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{m\}\\\)\, while rain droplets commonly have diameters ranging from \\\(0.1\{-\}3\\ \\rm\{mm\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00176

[Term]
id: goldbook:D01862
name: drop time
def: "The time that elapses between the instants at which two successive drops of liquid metal are detached from the tip of the capillary."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198557101491
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:D01863
name: drug
def: "Any substance which when absorbed into a living organism may modify one or more of its functions. The term is generally accepted for a substance taken for a therapeutic purpose\, but is also commonly used for abused substances. Synonymous with medicine\, pharmaceutical."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365092003
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:D01864
name: dry bulb temperature
def: "In psychrometry\, the temperature of the gas measured by a dry bulb thermometer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
