[Term]
id: goldbook:D01865
name: drying agent
def: "A substance which removes water \(liquid or gaseous\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:D01866
name: dual substituent-parameter equation
def: "In a general sense\, any equation which expresses substituent effects in terms of two parameters. However\, in practice the term is used more specifically for an equation for summarizing the effects of meta- or para- substituents \(i = m or p\) $\\ce\{\\textbf\{X\}\}$ on chemical reactivity\, spectroscopic properties\, etc. of a probe site $\\ce\{\\textbf\{Y\}\}$ in benzene or other aromatic system. \\\[P^\{\\rm\{i\}\} = \\rho_\{I\}^\{\\rm\{i\}\}\\ \\sigma_\{I\} + \\rho_\{R\}^\{\\rm\{i\}\} \\sigma_\{R\}\\\] \\\(P\\\) is the magnitude of the property $\\ce\{\\textbf\{Y\}\}$ for substituent $\\ce\{\\textbf\{X\}\}$\, expressed relative to the property for $\\ce\{X\} = \\ce\{H\}$; \\\(\\sigma _\{I\}\\\) and \\\(\\sigma _\{R\}\\\) are inductive or polar and resonance substituent constants\, respectively\, there being various scales for \\\(\\sigma _\{R\};\\\,\\rho _\{I\}\\\) and \\\(\\rho _\{R\}\\\) are the corresponding regression coefficients."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02279
consider: goldbook:R05326

[Term]
id: goldbook:D01867
name: dust
def: "Small\, dry\, solid particles projected into the air by natural forces\, such as wind\, volcanic eruption and by mechanical or man-made processes such as crushing\, grinding\, milling\, drilling\, demolition\, shoveling\, conveying\, screening\, bagging and sweeping. Dust particles are usually in the size range from about \\\(1\{-\}100\\ \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{m\}\\\) in diameter and they settle slowly under the influence of gravity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:D01868
name: dust collector
def: "A device for monitoring dust emissions. Also the equipment used to remove and collect dust from process exhaust gases; this may employ simply sedimentation \(dustfall jars\, coated slides\, papers\, etc.\)\, inertial separation \(cyclones\, impactors\, impingers\, etc.\)\, precipitation \(thermal and electrostatic\) or filtration."
