[Term]
id: goldbook:DT06932
name: distribution isotherm
def: "The equilibrium relation between the concentration of a sample component in the stationary phase \\\(c_\{\\rm\{S\}\}\\\)\, and in the mobile phase \\\(c_\{\\rm\{M\}\}\\\)\, expressed as a function \\\(c_\{\\rm\{S\}\}=f\(c_\{\\rm\{M\}\}\)\\\). In some versions of chromatography\, a distribution isotherm can be seen as a partition isotherm\, an adsorption isotherm\, or a combination of these\, depending on the mechanism of separation."
comment: "The relation can be influenced also by concentrations of other sample components. \(c_{\rm{S}}\) and \(c_{\rm{M}}\) are usually expressed per unit volume of the phase; \(c_{\rm{S}}\) may also be expressed per mass of the dry solid phase or per unit surface area."
synonym: "extraction isotherm" []
