[Term]
id: goldbook:DT06960
name: drug design
def: "Drug design includes not only ligand design\, but also pharmacokinetics and toxicity\, which are mostly beyond the possibilities of structure- and/or computer-aided design. Nevertheless\, appropriate chemometric tools\, including experimental design and multivariate statistics\, can be of value in the planning and evaluation of pharmacokinetics and toxicological experiments and results. Drug design is most often used instead of the correct term 'Ligand Design'."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199769051137
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
