[Term]
id: goldbook:DT07362
name: downconversion
def: "Process by which a photon with frequency \\\( u _\{1\}\\\) interacts with a non-linear medium and splits into two simultaneously emitted photons with frequencies \\\( u _\{2\}\\\) and \\\( u _\{3\}\\\) so that the energy is conserved\: \\\[ u _\{1\}= u _\{2\}+ u _\{3\}\\\]"
comment: "Also known as a parametric downconversion."
comment: "The efficiency of the conversion process depends on the parametric gain in the non-linear material. This in turn depends on the power of the incident radiation, the photon frequencies, their indices of refraction in the material, and the non-linear 'hyper-susceptibility' of the material."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:F02525
consider: goldbook:P04627
consider: goldbook:P04792

[Term]
id: goldbook:DT07363
name: driving force
def: "Term widely used to indicate the negative of the standard Gibbs energy change for outer-sphere electron transfer \(\\\(\\Delta _\{\\rm\{ET\}\}G^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\)\)."
comment: "For photo-induced processes, this quantity can often be estimated from independently determined properties of the donor and acceptor species involved using the equation for the calculation of the Gibbs energy of photo-induced electron transfer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:GT07388
consider: goldbook:O04351

[Term]
id: goldbook:DT07364
name: Drude–Nernst equation
def: "Equation describing the contraction \(\\\(\\Delta V_\{\\rm\{el\}\}\\\)\) taking place in a dielectric medium of relative static permittivity \\\(\\varepsilon_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\\\) \(formerly called dielectric constant\) upon introduction of an ion of charge number \\\(z\\\) and radius \\\(r\\\)\: \\\[\\Delta V_\{\\rm\{el\}\} = -\\frac\{\\left \( z\\\,e \\right \)^\{2\}\}\{2\\\,r\\\,\\varepsilon_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\}\\frac\{\\partial\\left \( \\rm\{ln\}\\varepsilon_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\\right\)\}\{\\partial\\\,p\}\\\] with \\\(e\\\) the elementary charge."
comment: "Inasmuch as the derivative of \(\rm{ln}\varepsilon_{\rm{r}}\) with respect to pressure, \(\frac{\partial (\rm{ln}\varepsilon _{\rm{r}})}{\partial p}\), is not known for all media, there are approximations to evaluate this term as a function of \(\varepsilon_{\rm{r}}\) and of the isothermal compressibility of the medium, \(\kappa_{T}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C00993
consider: goldbook:D01697
consider: goldbook:E02032
consider: goldbook:P04507

[Term]
id: goldbook:DT07365
name: dual fluorescence
def: "Systems or molecular species showing two fluorescence bands. Several non-trivial molecular properties may be at the basis of a dual fluorescence\, such as conformational equilibrium in the ground state and a mixture of excited states."
comment: "Trivial reason for dual fluorescence is the coexistence of two independent fluorophores."
