id: goldbook:E01886
name: eclipsing strain
def: "Intramolecular strain present due to nonbonded interactions between two eclipsed atoms or groups. It is\, for example\, one of the interactions responsible for the existence of a rotational barrier and hence restricted rotation about the $\\ce\{C–C\}$ bond in ethane. It has also been called Pitzer strain\, torsional strain and bond opposition strain."
