[Term]
id: goldbook:E01915
name: elastic collision
def: "A particle \(atom or molecule\) can undergo a change in its state of excitation as a result of collisions with other particles. In an elastic collision an exchange only of kinetic energy takes place between the colliding species; in an inelastic collision there is an interchange between the kinetic energy and the internal energy of the particle."
