[Term]
id: goldbook:E01997
name: electronic energy migration
def: "The movement of electronic excitation energy from one molecular entity to another of the same species\, or from one part of a molecular entity to another of the same kind \(e.g. excitation migration between the chromophores of an aromatic polymer\). The migration can happen via radiative or radiationless processes."
