[Term]
id: goldbook:E02007
name: electron probe X-ray microanalysis
def: "Any analytical technique which uses the excitation and evaluation of the characteristic X-ray spectrum of a solid specimen by a focused electron beam \(typically of a diameter of less than \\\(1\\ \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{m\}\\\)\). Qualitative and quantitative X-ray analysis is the main feature of EPXMA. For obtaining supplementary information the secondary\, back scattered and absorbed electrons are also frequently observed. Qualitative and quantitative X-ray analysis is\, however\, the main feature of EPXMA."
synonym: "EPXMA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
