[Term]
id: goldbook:E02010
name: electron stopping power
def: "When a beam of electrons strikes a target or specimen there are three ways in which the electrons may lose energy \(low energy collisions\, X-ray production\, and formation of a spectral continuum\). The average energy loss per unit distance travelled along the electron path is called electron stopping power\, \\\(\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}E\}\{\\rm\{d\}x\}\\\)."
