[Term]
id: goldbook:E02015
name: electron work function
def: "The minimum work needed to extract electrons from the Fermi level of a metal M across a surface carrying no net charge. It is equal to the sum of the potential energy and the kinetic Fermi energy taken with the reverse sign\: \\\[\\mathit\{\\Phi\}^\{M\} = -\(V_\{\\rm\{e\}\} + \\varepsilon_\{\\rm\{e\}\}^\{F\}\)\\\] where \\\(V_\{\\rm\{e\}\}\\\) is the potential energy for electrons in metals and \\\(\\varepsilon_\{\\rm\{e\}\}^\{\\rm\{F\}\}\\\) is the kinetic energy of electrons at the Fermi level."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198658030437
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
