id: goldbook:E02024
name: electrophoretic mobility
def: "The observed rate of migration of a component \(\\\(v\\\)\) divided by electric field strength \(\\\(E\\\)\) in a given medium."
comment: "In a solid support medium, only apparent values can be determined."
comment: "Mobilities are sometimes expressed with a negative sign, because migration of the solutes or particles generally occurs in the direction opposite to the electrophoretic field (which is taken as reference for that direction)."
