[Term]
id: goldbook:E02029
name: electrothermal atomizer
def: "A device which is heated to the temperature required for analyte atomization by the passage of electrical current through its body. In open atomizers the sample vapour\, together with analyte atoms\, leaving the atomizer surface may move freely into the surrounding space. In confined atomizers the sample vapour is restricted by the atomizer wall except for the openings where the optical beam enters and leaves the atomizer and the sample introduction hole."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264020253
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02030
name: electroviscous effects
def: "For dispersions of charged particles\, these are those components of the viscosity connected with the charge of the particles."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197951051213
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:V06627

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02032
name: elementary charge
def: "The elementary charge\, \\\(e\\\)\, is one of seven fixed constants defining the International System of Units\, the SI\, with \\\(e = \\pu\{1.602176634E-19 C\}\\\). The elementary charge \\\(e\\\) corresponds to a coupling strength of the electromagnetic force via the fine-structure constant and is considered as a fundamental constant of nature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1088/1681-7575/aa950a
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02034
name: elementary particle
def: "A particle in which\, at the present\, no structure can be observed at moderate energies."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198254081533
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02035
name: elementary reaction
def: "A reaction for which no reaction intermediates have been detected or need to be postulated in order to describe the chemical reaction on a molecular scale. An elementary reaction is assumed to occur in a single step and to pass through a single transition state."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365102291
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05171
consider: goldbook:S05970
consider: goldbook:T06468

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02036
name: element effect
def: "The ratio of the rate constants of two reactions that differ only in the identity of the element of the atom in the leaving group\, e.g. \\\(\\frac\{k_\{\\rm\{Br\}\}\}\{k_\{\\rm\{Cl\}\}\}\\\). As for isotope effects\, a ratio of unity is regarded as a 'null effect'."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03327
consider: goldbook:L03493

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02038
name: elimination
def: "The reverse of an addition reaction or transformation. In an elimination two groups \(called eliminands\) are lost most often from two different centres \(1/2/elimination or 1/3/elimination\, etc.\) with concomitant formation of an unsaturation in the molecule \(double bond\, triple bond\) or formation of a new ring. If the groups are lost from a single centre \($\\ce\{\\upalpha\\!\\mbox\{-\}elimination\}$\, 1/1/elimination\) the resulting product is a carbene or a 'carbene analogue'."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00007
consider: goldbook:A00133
consider: goldbook:C00806
consider: goldbook:T06446

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02041
name: elute
def: "To chromatograph by elution chromatography. This term is preferred to the term 'develop'\, which has been used in paper chromatography and in thin-layer chromatography. The process of elution may continue until the components have left the chromatographic bed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01075
consider: goldbook:E02042
consider: goldbook:E02046
consider: goldbook:T06346

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02046
name: elution chromatography
def: "A procedure for chromatographic separation in which the mobile phase is passed through the chromatographic bed after the application of the sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:G02670
consider: goldbook:S05554
consider: goldbook:S05969

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02053
name: elutriation
def: "The process of separating the lighter particles of a powder from the heavier ones by means of an upward directed stream of fluid \(gas or liquid\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02054
name: emanation thermal analysis
def: "A thermoanalytical technique in which the release of radioactive emanation from a substance \(and/or its reaction product\(s\)\) is measured as a function of temperature whilst the substance is subjected to a controlled temperature programme."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198557111737
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05077

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02055
name: embryo
def: "An aggregate of a small number of atoms\, molecules or ions. An embryo of such a size that the Gibbs energy at constant pressure and temperature is a maximum is called a critical embryo. An embryo larger than a critical embryo is called a homogeneous nucleus. Colloidal sols may be formed by condensation methods. When a condensation method is applied\, molecules \(or ions\) are deposited on nuclei which may be of the same chemical species as the colloid \(homogeneous nucleation\) or different \(heterogeneous nucleation\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01171
consider: goldbook:C01172
consider: goldbook:H02807
consider: goldbook:H02848

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02056
name: emission
def: "Radiative deactivation of an excited state; transfer of energy from a molecular entity to an electromagnetic field."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:D01528
consider: goldbook:E02257
consider: goldbook:F02453
consider: goldbook:L03641
consider: goldbook:P04569

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02057
name: emission
def: "The total rate at which a solid\, liquid or gaseous pollutant is emitted into the atmosphere from a given source; usually expressed as mass per unit time. Primary emissions are those substances which are emitted directly to the atmosphere \(e.g. $\\ce\{NO\}$\, $\\ce\{SO2\}$\, etc.\)\, while secondary emissions are formed from the primary emissions through thermal or photochemical reactions \(e.g. ozone\, aldehydes\, ketones\, sulfuric acid\, nitric acid\, etc.\). The point or area from which the discharge takes place is called the source; the area in which the emission or its transformed products \(e.g. in the case of aerosols\, acidic deposition\, etc.\) may be deposited is called the receptor area or sink. Emission may be applied to noise\, heat\, etc.\, as well as pollutants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00208
consider: goldbook:K03386
consider: goldbook:N04175
consider: goldbook:RT06841
consider: goldbook:S05703

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02058
name: emission control equipment
def: "Air pollution control equipment which either converts the pollutant chemically to a non-polluting substance or collects the pollutant by some means including gravity settling chambers\, inertial separators\, cyclonic separators\, filters\, electrical precipitators\, scrubbers\, \(spray towers\, jet scrubbers\, Venturi scrubbers\, inertial scrubbers\, mechanical scrubbers and packed scrubbers\). Certain gases and odoriferous compounds are controlled by combustion\, absorption \(spray chambers\, mechanical contactors\, bubble cap or sieve plate contactors and packed towers\) and adsorption units \(packed beds or fluidized beds\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00195

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02059
name: emission flux
def: "The emission per unit area of the appropriate surface of an emitting source."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02060
name: emission spectrum
def: "Plot of the emitted spectral radiant power \(spectral radiant exitance\) or of the emitted spectral photon irradiance \(spectral photon exitance\) against a quantity related to photon energy\, such as frequency\, \\\( u \\\)\, wavenumber\, \\\(\\sigma \\\)\, or wavelength\, \\\(\\lambda \\\). When corrected for wavelength-dependent variations in the equipment response\, it is called a corrected emission spectrum."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01343
consider: goldbook:S05821
consider: goldbook:S05828
consider: goldbook:W06659

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02062
name: emittance
def: "Ratio of radiant exitance of a thermal radiator to that of a full radiator \(black body\) at the same temperature. In ISO this quantity is called emissivity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668040957
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05041

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02063
name: empirical formula
def: "Formed by juxtaposition of the atomic symbols with their appropriate subscripts to give the simplest possible formula expressing the composition of a compound."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1515/pac-2014-0718
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02064
name: emulsifier
def: "A surfactant which when present in small amounts facilitates the formation of an emulsion\, or enhances its colloidal stability by decreasing either or both of the rates of aggregation and coalescence."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01119
consider: goldbook:C01172
