[Term]
id: goldbook:E02065
name: emulsion
def: "A fluid colloidal system in which liquid droplets and/or liquid crystals are dispersed in a liquid. The droplets often exceed the usual limits for colloids in size. An emulsion is denoted by the symbol O/W if the continuous phase is an aqueous solution and by W/O if the continuous phase is an organic liquid \(an 'oil'\). More complicated emulsions such as O/W/O \(i.e. oil droplets contained within aqueous droplets dispersed in a continuous oil phase\) are also possible. Photographic emulsions\, although colloidal systems\, are not emulsions in the sense of this nomenclature."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01171
consider: goldbook:C01172

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02066
name: enamines
def: "Alkenylamines; by usage the term refers specifically to vinylic amines\, which have the structure $\\ce\{R2NCR=CR2\}$ ."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567081307
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:V06622

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02069
name: enantiomer
def: "One of a pair of molecular entities which are mirror images of each other and non-superposable."
synonym: "optical isomer" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
