[Term]
id: goldbook:E02070
name: enantiomeric excess
def: "For a mixture of \\\(\\left\(+\\right\)\\\)- and \\\(\\left\(-\\right\)\\\)-enantiomers\, with composition given as the mole or weight fractions \\\(F_\{\\left\(\\!+\\!\\right\)\}\\\) and \\\(F_\{\\left\(\\!-\\!\\right\)\}\\\) \(where \\\(F_\{\\left\(\\!+\\!\\right\)\}\\\,+\\\,F_\{\\left\(\\!-\\!\\right\)\}=1\\\)\) the enantiomer excess is defined as \\\(|F_\{\\left\(\\!+\\!\\right\)\} - F_\{\\left\(\\!-\\!\\right\)\}|\\\) \(and the percent enantiomer excess by \\\(100\\ |F_\{\\left\(\\!+\\!\\right\)\} - F_\{\\left\(\\!-\\!\\right\)\}|\\\)\). Frequently this term is abbreviated e.e."
synonym: "e.e." RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "enantiomer excess" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
