[Term]
id: goldbook:E02091
name: endergonic reaction
def: "This is usually taken to be a reaction for which the overall standard Gibbs energy change \\\(\\Delta G^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\) is positive. Some workers use this term with respect to a positive value of \\\(\\Delta H^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\) at the absolute zero of temperature."
synonym: "endoergic reaction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02092
name: end-group
def: "A constitutional unit that is an extremity of a macromolecule or oligomer molecule. An end-group is attached to only one constitutional unit of a macromolecule or oligomer molecule."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122287
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01288
consider: goldbook:M03667
consider: goldbook:O04286

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02093
name: endoenzymes
def: "Enzymes that cut internal bonds of a polymer. Endonucleases are able to cleave phosphodiester bonds within a nucleic acid chain by hydrolysis either randomly or at specific base sequences \(cf. restriction enzymes\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02159
consider: goldbook:H02902
consider: goldbook:N04245
consider: goldbook:R05350

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02094
name: <i>endo</i>\, <i>exo</i>\, <i>syn</i>\, <i>anti</i>
def: "Descriptors of the relative orientation of groups attached to non-bridgehead atoms in a bicyclo\[x.y.z\]alkane \(x ≥ y &gt; z &gt; 0\).  If the group is orientated towards the highest numbered bridge \(z bridge\, e.g. C-7 in example below\) it is given the description exo; if it is orientated away from the highest numbered bridge it is given the description endo. If the group is attached to the highest numbered bridge and is orientated towards the lowest numbered bridge \(x bridge\, e.g. C-2 in example below\) it is given the description syn; if the group is orientated away from the lowest numbered bridge it is given the description anti."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00381
consider: goldbook:B00736
consider: goldbook:S06216

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02095
name: endothermic reaction
def: "A reaction for which the overall standard enthalpy change \\\(\\Delta H^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\) is positive."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02141

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02099
name: ene reaction
def: "The addition of a compound with a double bond having an allylic hydrogen \(the 'ene'\) to a compound with a multiple bond \(the 'enophile'\) with transfer of the allylic hydrogen and a concomitant reorganization of the bonding\, as illustrated below for propene \(the 'ene'\) and ethene \(the 'enophile'\). The reverse is a 'retro-ene' reaction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05370

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02100
name: energized species
def: "In an elementary process\, a species having sufficient energy to become an activated complex\, but which does not have the structure of the activated complex. If it is not inactivated by collisions it can become an activated complex and pass at once into products\, after undergoing vibration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00092

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02102
name: energy
def: "Energy of the individual particles or photons of which a radiation consists."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466122513
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05048

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02105
name: energy dispersive X-ray fluorescence analysis
def: "A method of X-ray fluorescence analysis where element specificity is obtained by measuring the energy spectrum of the induced X-radiation."
