id: goldbook:E02219
name: esters
def: "Compounds formally derived from an oxoacid $\\ce\{R_\{k\}E\(=O\)_\{l\}\(OH\)_\{m\}\}$\, \($l  eq 0$\) and an alcohol\, phenol\, heteroarenol\, or enol by linking with formal loss of water from an acidic hydroxy group of the former and a hydroxy group of the latter. By extension acyl derivatives of alcohols\, etc. Acyl derivatives of chalcogen analogues of alcohols \(thiols\, selenols\, tellurols\) etc. are included. E.g. $\\ce\{R'C\(=O\)\(OR\)\}$\, $\\ce\{R'C\(=S\)\(OR\)\}$\, $\\ce\{R'C\(=O\)\(SR\)\}$\, $\\ce\{R'S\(=O\)2\(OR\)\}$\, $\\ce\{\(HO\)2P\(=O\)\(OR\)\}$\, $\\ce\{\(R'S\)2C\(=O\)\}$\, $\\ce\{ROCN\}$ \(but not $\\ce\{R–NCO\}$\) \($\\ce\{R\}  eq \\ce\{H\}$\)."
comment: "O-Alkyl derivatives of other acidic compounds [see amides (1)] may be named as esters but do not belong to the class esters proper. E.g. $\ce{(Ph)2POCH3}$ methyl diphenylphosphinite."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567081307
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
