[Term]
id: goldbook:E02227
name: evaporation
def: "The physical process by which a liquid substance is converted to a gas or vapour. This may occur at or below the normal boiling point of the liquid \(the temperature at which a liquid boils at 1 atmosphere pressure\) and the process is endothermic."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02228
name: even-electron ion
def: "An ion containing no unpaired electrons\, for example $\\ce\{CH3^\{+\}\}$\, in its ground state."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163101541
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:G02704

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02237
name: excess volume
def: "For a pure liquid\, despite its low compressibility\, the variation of density near a solid surface can be detected and measured. The total volume \\\(V\\\) of a system consisting of solid and pure liquid is different from \(usually less than\) that calculated assuming a constant liquid density. If the densities of bulk solid \(\\\(\\rho ^\{\\mathrm\{sol\}\}\\\)\) and liquid \(\\\(\\rho ^\{\\rm\{l\}\}\\\)\) are known then an excess volume \(usually negative\) can be defined as\: \\\[V^\{\\sigma \}=V- V^\{\\mathrm\{sol\}\}- V^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}=V- \\frac\{m^\{\\mathrm\{sol\}\}\}\{\\rho ^\{\\mathrm\{sol\}\}\}- \\frac\{m^\{\\rm\{l\}\}\}\{\\rho ^\{\\rm\{l\}\}\}\\\] where \\\(m^\{\\mathrm\{sol\}\}\\\) is the mass of solid\, \\\(V^\{\\mathrm\{sol\}\}\\\) its volume calculated from the bulk density\, \\\(V^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\) is the initial volume of liquid and \\\(m^\{\\rm\{l\}\}\\\) is the mass of liquid. The excess mass is given by\: \\\[m^\{\\sigma \}=m^\{\\rm\{l\}\}- \(V- V^\{\\mathrm\{sol\}\}\)\\ \\rho ^\{\\rm\{l\}\}\\\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198658070967
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02238
name: exchange current
def: "The common value \\\(I_\{0\}\\\) of the anodic and cathodic partial currents when the reaction is at equilibrium \\\[I_\{0\}=I_\{\\rm\{a\}\}=- I_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\\] For an electrode at equilibrium at which only one reaction is significant \\\(I=0\\\). When more than one reaction is significant at a given electrode\, subscripts to \\\(I_\{0\}\\\) may be used to distinguish exchange currents. \\\(I\\\) is not usually zero when only one of these reactions is at equilibrium."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197437040499
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02239
name: exchange extraction
def: "An extraction operation or process in which a metal from one phase is exchanged with the equivalent amount of a second metal from the other phase."
comment: "This applies also to organic or molecular species."
comment: "This term may be used in connection with any step (e.g. loading, scrubbing or stripping in a process)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365112373
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01420
consider: goldbook:E02301
consider: goldbook:S05511
consider: goldbook:S06054

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02240
name: exchange-inversion transition
def: "A transition between antiferromagnetic and ferromagnetic coupling between two subarrays of magnetic atoms. Example\: Ordered $\\ce\{FeRh\}$ changes from antiferromagnetic to ferromagnetic coupling with the simple cubic $\\ce\{Fe\}$ array in a first-order transition."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466030577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01025
consider: goldbook:F02390

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02241
name: exchange labelling
def: "Labelling of a substance by isotope exchange."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466122513
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03328
consider: goldbook:L03425

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02242
name: excimer
def: "An electronically excited dimer\, 'non-bonding' in the ground state. For example\, a complex formed by the interaction of an excited molecular entity with a ground state partner of the same structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
