[Term]
id: goldbook:E02256
name: excitation transfer
def: "Synonymous with energy transfer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02116

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02257
name: excited state
def: "State of a system with energy higher than that of the ground state. This term is most commonly used to characterize a molecule in one of its electronically excited states\, but can also refer to vibrational and/or rotational excitation in the electronic ground state."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:G02704

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02258
name: exciton
def: "In some applications it is useful to consider electronic excitation as if a quasi-particle\, capable of migrating\, were involved. This is termed an exciton. In organic materials two models are used\: the band or wave model \(low temperature\, high crystalline order\) and the hopping model \(higher temperature\, low crystalline order or amorphous state\). Energy transfer in the hopping limit is identical with energy migration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E01997
consider: goldbook:E02107

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02261
name: exclusion chromatography
def: "Chromatography in which separation is based mainly on exclusion effects\, such as differences in molecular size and/or shape or in charge. The term size-exclusion chromatography may also be used when separation is based on molecular size. The terms gel filtration and gel-permeation chromatography \(GPC\) were used earlier to describe this process when the stationary phase is a swollen gel. The term ion-exclusion chromatography is specifically used for the separation of ions in an aqueous phase."
synonym: "gel-filtration chromatography" []
synonym: "gel-permeation chromatography" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01075
consider: goldbook:F02388
consider: goldbook:G02600
consider: goldbook:P04505

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02262
name: exergonic reaction
def: "This expression is often applied to a reaction for which the overall standard Gibbs energy change \\\(\\Delta G^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\) is negative. Some workers use this term with reference to a negative value of \\\(\\Delta H^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\) at the absolute zero of temperature."
synonym: "exoergic reaction" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02263
name: exfoliated graphite
def: "The product of very rapid heating \(or flash heating\) of graphite intercalation compounds\, such as graphite hydrogensulfate of relatively large particle diameter \(flakes\). The vaporizing intercalated substances force the graphite layers apart. The exfoliated graphite assumes an accordion-like shape with an apparent volume often hundreds of times that of the original graphite flakes."
comment: "Exfoliated graphite is usually prepared from well-crystallized natural flake graphite. It is used for the production of graphite foils. Exfoliated graphite is different from the deflagration product of graphite oxide (graphitic acid)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567030473
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:G02684
consider: goldbook:I03076

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02265
name: exit channel
def: "This expression refers to the region of a potential-energy surface or hypersurface that corresponds to molecular configurations that are closer to those of the products than to those of the reactants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:P04780

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02267
name: exoenzymes
def: "Enzymes that cleave monomers \(sometimes also di- or oligomers\) from one end of a polymer chain. Exonucleases are able to cleave nucleotides\, one by one\, from either the 5- or the 3- \(or both\) ends of nucleic acids."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02159
consider: goldbook:N04245
consider: goldbook:N04255

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02268
name: exon
def: "A section of DNA which carries the coding sequence for a protein or part of it. Exons are separated by intervening\, non-coding sequences \(cf. intron\). In eukaryotes most genes consist of a number of exons."
synonym: "DNA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:D01597
consider: goldbook:G02604
consider: goldbook:I03141
consider: goldbook:ST06775

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02269
name: exothermic reaction
def: "A reaction for which the overall standard enthalpy change \\\(\\Delta H^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\) is negative."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02141

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02273
name: experimental perturbational calculation
def: "To assess the uncertainty of derived final results from a least-squares procedure one can investigate the sensitivity of output data for errors in the input data by means of this calculation. One performs the calculations many times with perturbed input data and studies the relation between the changes \(perturbations\) in the input data and the changes in the output data. The perturbations are preferably generated using random numbers with a distribution function chosen to mimic the distribution of uncertainties in the primary results."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198153091805
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:L03492
consider: goldbook:S05606

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02274
name: explosivity limits
def: "The concentration limits\, usually of a substance in air\, between which combustion will be self-sustaining."
synonym: "explosion limits" []
synonym: "flammable limits" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02275
name: exponential decay
def: "Variation of a quantity \(generally the activity of a quantity of a radionuclide\) according to the law \\\(A=A_\{0\}\\ \\rm\{e\}^\{-\\lambda\\ t\}\\\) where \\\(A\\\) and \\\(A_\{0\}\\\) are the values of the quantity being considered at time \\\(t\\\) and zero respectively\, and \\\(\\lambda\\\) is an appropriate constant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198254081533
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00114
consider: goldbook:R05116

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02277
name: expression
def: "The cellular production of the protein encoded by a particular gene. The process includes transcription of DNA\, processing of the resulting mRNA product and its translation into an active protein.A recombinant gene inserted into a host cell by means of a vector is said to be expressed if the synthesis of the encoded protein can be demonstrated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:D01597
consider: goldbook:G02604
consider: goldbook:M03857
consider: goldbook:T06436
consider: goldbook:T06475
consider: goldbook:V06606

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02279
name: extended Hammett equation
def: "This term applies in a general way to any multiparametric extension of the Hammett equation. It is sometimes used specifically for a form of dual substituent-parameter equation in which the actual value of the correlated property \\\(P\\\) under the influence of the substituent $\\ce\{X\}$ is used\, rather than the value relative to that for $\\ce\{X\}$ = $\\ce\{H\}$. An intercept term \\\(h\\\) corresponding to the value of \\\(P\\\) for $\\ce\{X\}$ = $\\ce\{H\}$ is introduced\, e.g. \\\[P=\\alpha \\ \\sigma _\{I\}+\\beta \\ \\sigma _\{R\}+h\\\] The equation may be applied to systems for which the inclusion of further terms to represent other effects\, e.g. steric\, is appropriate."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:D01866
consider: goldbook:H02732

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02280
name: extended X-ray absorption fine structure
def: "Structure in X-ray absorption spectra remote from the edge and extending to higher energies\, due mainly to the scattering of the expelled electron by neighbouring atoms. Structure closer to the absorption edge is sometimes called near-edge X-ray absorption fine structure \(NEXAFS\)."
synonym: "EXAFS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163050735
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:S05487

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02281
name: extensive quantity
def: "Physical quantity whose magnitude is additive for subsystems."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198658101405
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00134

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02282
name: extent
def: "A quantity measured by its area\, \\\(A\\\) \(or \\\(S\\\)\). For solids\, a real \(true\, actual\) and a geometric surface \(interface\) area\, \\\(A_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\\\) and \\\(A_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\\\)\, respectively\, may be defined if asperities are present whose height is orders of magnitude greater than the atomic or molecular size. The geometric surface is the projection of the real surface on a plane parallel to the macroscopic\, visible phase boundary. If asperities are of the order of the atomic size\, the surface of the solid may be described as stepped. \(High index faces of crystals are stepped surfaces but may be ideally smooth in the sense of the roughness factor.\)"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198658030437
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05419
consider: goldbook:VT07496

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02283
name: extent of reaction
def: "Extensive quantity describing the progress of a chemical reaction equal to the number of chemical transformations\, as indicated by the reaction equation on a molecular scale\, divided by the Avogadro constant \(it is essentially the amount of chemical transformations\). The change in the extent of reaction is given by \\\(\\mathrm\{d\}\\xi =\\frac\{\\mathrm\{d\}n_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\}\{ u _\{\\rm\{B\}\}\}\\\)\, where \\\( u _\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is the stoichiometric number of any reaction entity B \(reactant or product\) and \\\(\\mathrm\{d\}n_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is the corresponding amount."
synonym: "advancement" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264101569
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365102291
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668040957
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00297
consider: goldbook:A00543
consider: goldbook:E02281
consider: goldbook:S06025

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02290
name: external standard
def: "A compound present in a standard sample of known concentration and volume which is analysed separately from the unknown sample under identical conditions. It is used to facilitate the qualitative indentification and/or quantitative determination of the sample components. The volume of the external standard \(standard sample\) need not to be known if it is identical to that of the unknown sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02291
name: external surface
def: "When a porous solid consists of discrete particles it is inconvenient to describe the outer boundary of the particles as the external surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197646010071
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02292
name: exterplex
def: "Termolecular analogue of an exciplex. Use of this term is discouraged."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02246
consider: goldbook:M03989

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02295
name: extra-column volume
def: "The volume between the effective injection point and the effective detection point\, excluding the part of the column containing the stationary phase. It is composed of the volumes of the injector\, connecting lines and detector."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02296
name: extract
def: "The separated phase \(often but not necessarily organic\) that contains the material extracted from the other phase. Where appropriate the term 'loaded solvent' may be used\, but is not recommended."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365112373
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02297
name: extract
def: "To transfer a solute from a liquid phase to another immiscible or partially miscible liquid phase in contact with it. The term is also applied to the dissolution of material from a solid phase with a liquid in which it is not wholly soluble \(i.e. leaching\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365112373
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:D01806
consider: goldbook:S05752

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02298
name: extractability
def: "A property which qualitatively indicates the degree to which a substance is extracted. The term is imprecise and generally used in a qualitative sense. It is not a synonym for fraction extracted."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365112373
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:F02503

[Term]
id: goldbook:E02299
name: extractant
def: "The active component\(s\) primarily responsible for transfer of a solute from one phase to the other."
comment: "Certain extractants that consist of liquids immiscible with water (e.g. tributyl phosphate or certain ketones) might comprise the only component of the initial organic phase but extractant(s) can also be dissolved in diluent."
comment: "The term extracting agent is a synonym but solvent and ligand should not be used in this context."
synonym: "extracting agent" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365112373
