[Term]
id: goldbook:ET07368
name: electrostriction
def: "Contraction of a dielectric in an electric-field gradient."
comment: "For example, the contraction taking place around the charged centres created as a consequence of the sudden formation of separated positive and negative charges in the process of electron transfer."
comment: "The thermodynamic description of electrostriction was given by Drude and Nernst in 1894 to explain the phenomenon of contraction of a continuum medium, such as an alkane, around charges suddenly produced in that medium."
