[Term]
id: goldbook:ET07371
name: entrainment
def: "Term used in photostimulated radical nucleophilic substitution to designate the induction of the reaction of a less reactive \(or non-reactive\) nucleophile with a substrate by the addition of catalytic amounts of another nucleophile\, more reactive at initiation. Often\, the non-reactive nucleophile at initiation is\, however\, quite reactive at propagation."
comment: "Term also used in photobiology in connection with the setting of the circadian clock by biological photosensors such as phytochromes and cryptochromes in plants and cryptochromes in mammals and insects."
