[Term]
id: goldbook:F02390
name: first-order phase transition
def: "A transition in which the molar Gibbs energies or molar Helmholtz energies of the two phases \(or chemical potentials of all components in the two phases\) are equal at the transition temperature\, but their first derivatives with respect to temperature and pressure \(for example\, specific enthalpy of transition and specific volume\) are discontinuous at the transition point\, as for two dissimilar phases that coexist and that can be transformed into one another by a change in a field variable such as pressure\, temperature\, magnetic or electric field. Example\: The transition on heating $\\ce\{CsCl\}$ to \\\(752\\ \\rm\{K\}\\\) at which it changes from the low-temperature\, $\\ce\{CsCl\}$-type structure to the high-temperature $\\ce\{NaCl\}$-type structure. Synonymous with discontinuous phase transition."
synonym: "discontinuous phase transition" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466030577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02141
consider: goldbook:S05807
consider: goldbook:V06600

[Term]
id: goldbook:F02391
name: Fischer projection
def: "A projection formula in which vertically drawn bonds are considered to lie below the projection plane and horizontal bonds to lie above that plane. Thus for the molecule Cabcd\:"
synonym: "Fischer–Tollens projection" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122193
