[Term]
id: goldbook:F02437
name: flow injection enthalpimetry
def: "A term used to describe several related methods in which a transient temperature change in a flowing liquid stream\, caused by a chemical reaction\, is used to quantitatively determine an analyte. The analyte is introduced as a discrete liquid sample \(i.e. test portion\) into the flowing stream. This definition limits the scope to experiments with primarily an analytical emphasis\, performed in a flow injection calorimeter. This maintains a clear distinction from classical flow calorimetric methods where reagents are combined continuously in flowing streams\, or where the heat effect is measured via the flowing of a fluid over a reaction vessel. An acceptable synonym is enthalpimetric flow injection analysis. Other non-recommended terms which have been used in the literature include 'peak enthalpimetry' and 'enzyme thermistor'. Flow enthalpimetry has been used to describe the flow injection technique\, but its use for this purpose is discouraged."
synonym: "enthalpimetric flow injection analysis" []
synonym: "flow enthalpimetry" []
synonym: "peak enthalpimetry" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466122487
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:F02435
consider: goldbook:F02436
consider: goldbook:T06284

[Term]
id: goldbook:F02439
name: flow rate
def: "The volume of mobile phase passing through the column in unit time. The flow rate is usually measured at column outlet\, at ambient pressure \(\\\(p_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\)\) and temperature \(\\\(T_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\)\, in \\\(\\rm\{K\}\\\)\); this value is indicated with the symbol \\\(F\\\). If a water-containing flowmeter was used for the measurement \(e.g. the so-called soap bubble flowmeter\) then \\\(F\\\) must be corrected to dry gas conditions in order to obtain the mobile phase flow rate at ambient temperature \(\\\(F_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\)\)\: \\\[F_\{\\rm\{a\}\}=F\\ \(1- \\frac\{p_\{\\rm\{w\}\}\}\{p_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\}\)\\\] where \\\(p_\{\\rm\{w\}\}\\\) is the partial pressure of water vapour at ambient temperature. In order to specify chromatographic conditions in column chromatography\, the flow-rate \(mobile phase flow rate at column temperature\, \\\(F_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\\)\) must be expressed at \\\(T_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\\) \(kelvin\)\, the column temperature\: \\\[F_\{\\rm\{c\}\}=F_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\ \\frac\{T_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\}\{T_\{\\rm\{a\}\}\}\\\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01182
consider: goldbook:K03374
consider: goldbook:P04420
consider: goldbook:S05721

[Term]
id: goldbook:F02440
name: flow rate
def: "The volume rate of one component\, $\\ce\{\\textbf\{X\}\}$ \(e.g. air\, $\\ce\{O2\}$\)\, of the unburnt gas mixture \(such as $\\ce\{C2H2\}$\, $\\ce\{O2\}$\, etc.\) in the burner tip. Ambient temperature and pressure must be stated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198658121737
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
