[Term]
id: goldbook:F02455
name: fluorescence error
def: "Some samples are excited to fluorescence by the incident radiation beam. When added to the transmitted radiation beam this fluorescence results in an erroneous reading called the fluorescence error. It is particularly noticeable if the photodetector is situated close to the sample."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198860091449
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:F02453
consider: goldbook:R05189

[Term]
id: goldbook:F02457
name: fluorescence yield
def: "For a given transition from an excited state of a specified atom\, the ratio of the number of excited atoms which emit a photon to the total number of excited atoms."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466122513
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02257

[Term]
id: goldbook:F02458
name: fluorimeter
def: "An instrument used to measure the intensity and the wavelength distribution of the light emitted as fluorescence from a molecule excited at a specific wavelength or wavelengths within the absorption band of a particular compound. Characteristic fluorescence bands may be used to identify specific pollutants such as the polynuclear aromatic hydrocarbons. Excitation spectra of impurities can be observed by scanning the wavelength of the excitation light which is incident on the sample over a range of wavelengths and observing the relative intensity of the fluorescence emitted at a given wavelength. These spectra are also characteristic of the impurity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
