[Term]
id: goldbook:F02487
name: Förster cycle
def: "An indirect method of determination of excited state equilibria\, such as \\\(\\rm\{p\}K^\{\\rm\{*\,a\}\}\\\) values\, based on ground state thermodynamics and electronic transition energies. This cycle considers only the difference in molar enthalpy change \(\\\(\\Delta \\Delta H\\\)\) of reaction of ground and excited states\, neglecting the difference in molar entropy change of reaction of those states \(\\\(\\Delta \\Delta S\\\)\)."
