id: goldbook:F02547
name: fullerenes
def: "Compounds composed solely of an even number of carbon atoms\, which form a cage-like fused-ring polycyclic system with twelve five-membered rings and the rest six-membered rings. The archetypal example isfullerene\, where the atoms and bonds delineate a truncated icosahedron. The term has been broadened to include any closed cage structure consisting entirely of three-coordinate carbon atoms."
