id: goldbook:F02554
name: functional class name
def: "A name that expresses the characteristic group as a class term written as a separate word following the name of a parent structure or a name derived from a parent structure. In the latter case\, when the derived name is that for a substituent group \(formerly called a 'radical'\)\, the method has been called 'radicofunctional nomenclature'."
