[Term]
id: goldbook:F02555
name: functional group
def: "Organic compounds are thought of as consisting of a relatively unreactive backbone\, for example a chain of \\\(\\rm\{sp\}^\{3\}\\\) hybridized carbon atoms\, and one or several functional groups. The functional group is an atom\, or a group of atoms that has similar chemical properties whenever it occurs in different compounds. It defines the characteristic physical and chemical properties of families of organic compounds."
