id: goldbook:FT06786
name: Fenton reaction
def: "$\\ce\{Fe^\{2+\} + H2O2 -> Fe^\{3+\} + OH^\{.\} + OH^\{−\}\}$ . This is the iron-salt-dependent decomposition of dihydrogen peroxide\, generating the highly reactive hydroxyl radical\, possibly via an oxoiron\(IV\) intermediate. Addition of a reducing agent\, such as ascorbate\, leads to a cycle which increases the damage to biological molecules."
