id: goldbook:FT07383
name: frequency
def: "The number of waveperiods per time interval. The linear frequency\, \\\( u\\\)\, is the number of cycles per time interval. SI unit \\\(\\rm\{Hz =  s\}^\{-1\}\\\)."
comment: "For the angular frequency the symbol \(\omega\) (\(= 2\pi\nu\)) is used with \(\rm{rad s}^{-1}\) as the SI unit."
