id: goldbook:G02581
name: gas-filled phototube
def: "Similar in construction to a vacuum phototube except that it is filled with a noble gas \(usually $\\ce\{Ar\}$\) at a pressure of about \\\(10\\ \\rm\{Pa\}\\\). Photoelectrons accelerated by the anode electric potential ionize gas atoms. The additional electrons provide a substantial intrinsic gain."
