name: glycosides
def: "Originally mixed acetals resulting from the attachment of a glycosyl group to a non-acyl group $\\ce\{RO– \(which itself may be derived from a saccharide and chalcogen replacements thereof \($\\ce\{RS\\bond\{–\}\}$\, $\\ce\{RSe\\bond\{–\}\}$\).  The bond between the glycosyl group and the $\\ce\{OR\}$ group is called a glycosidic bond. By extension\, the terms N-glycosides and C-glycosides are used as class names for glycosylamines and for compounds having a glycosyl group attached to a hydrocarbyl group respectively.   These terms are misnomers and should not be used. The preferred terms are glycosylamines and C-glycosyl compounds\, respectively."
