consider: goldbook:G02689
consider: goldbook:N04088

[Term]
id: goldbook:G02688
name: graphite whiskers
def: "Thin\, approximately cylindrical filaments in which graphene layers are arranged in a scroll-like manner. There is\, at least in part\, a regular stacking of the layers as in the graphite lattice\, giving rise to h\,k\,l\, X-ray reflections. The physical properties of graphite whiskers approach\, along the cylinder axis\, those of graphite."
comment: "If there is, due to misalignment of the layers caused by their bending, no three-dimensional stacking order as in graphite, the term carbon whiskers should be used. @G02684-1@ whiskers and carbon whiskers should be distinguished from more disordered filamentous carbon."
synonym: "carbon whiskers" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567030473
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
