consider: goldbook:G02684

[Term]
id: goldbook:G02689
name: graphitic carbon
def: "All varieties of substances consisting of the element carbon in the allotropic form of graphite irrespective of the presence of structural defects."
comment: "The use of the term graphitic carbon is justified if three-dimensional hexagonal crystalline long-range order can be detected in the material by diffraction methods, independent of the volume fraction and the homogeneity of distribution of such crystalline domains. Otherwise, the term non-graphitic carbon should be used."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567030473
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
