[Term]
id: goldbook:G02692
name: graphitization heat treatment
def: "A process of heat treatment of a non-graphitic carbon industrially performed at temperatures in the range between \\\(2500\\\) and \\\(3300\\ \\rm\{K\}\\\)\, to achieve transformation into graphitic carbon."
comment: "The term graphitization heat treatment does not include information as to the crystallinity achieved by the heat treatment, that is the extent of transformation into graphitic carbon or the degree of graphitization. Only for such a transformation into graphitic carbon should the term graphitization be used. Consequently: the common use of the term graphitization for the heat treatment process only, regardless of the resultant crystallinity, is incorrect and should be avoided."
