[Term]
id: goldbook:H02722
name: half-wave potential
def: "The potential of a polarographic or voltammetric indicator electrode at the point\, on the rising part of a polarographic or voltammetric wave\, where the difference between the total current and the residual current is equal to one-half of the limiting current. The quarter-wave potential\, the three-quarter-wave potential\, etc.\, may be similarly defined."
