[Term]
id: goldbook:H02744
name: harmonic frequency generation
def: "Production of coherent radiation of frequency \\\(k\\  u \\\) \(\\\(k=2\,3\,...\\\)\) from coherent radiation of frequency. In general\, this effect is obtained through the interaction of laser light with a suitable optical medium with non-linear polarizability. The case \\\(k=2\\\) is referred to as frequency doubling\, \\\(k=3\\\) is frequency tripling and \\\(k=4\\\) is frequency quadrupling. Even higher integer values of \\\(k\\\) are possible."
