[Term]
id: goldbook:H02745
name: harmonic mean
def: "The number of observations\, divided by the sum of reciprocals of the observations. Symbol\: \\\(\\bar\{x\}_\{\\rm\{h\}\}\\\). It can be calculated with the formula\: \\\[\\bar\{x\}_\{\\rm\{h\}\} = \\frac\{n\}\{\\sum x_\{j\}^\{-1\}\}\\\]"
comment: "As in the case of the geometric mean, this quantity is sometimes directly (but inappropriately) calculated, for example, when evaluating kinetic analytical results where the reaction time is inversely proportional to concentration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466030595
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
