[Term]
id: goldbook:H02746
name: harpoon mechanism
def: "Reaction sequence \(thermal or photoinduced\) between neutral molecular or atomic entities in which long-range electron transfer is followed by a considerable reduction of the distance between donor and acceptor sites as a result of the electrostatic attraction in the ion pair created."
