[Term]
id: goldbook:H02748
name: Hartree energy
def: "Atomic fundamental physical constant used as atomic unit of energy\: \\\(E_\{\\rm\{h\}\}=\\frac\{\\mathrm\{\\hslash \}^\{2\}\}\{m_\{\\rm\{e\}\}\\ a_\{0\}^\{2\}\} = 4.359\\ 7482\(26\)\\times 10^\{-18\}\\ \\rm\{J\}\\\)\, where \\\(\\mathrm\{\\hslash\}\\\) is the Planck constant divided by \\\(2\\ \\pi \\\)\, \\\(m_\{\\rm\{e\}\}\\\) the electron rest mass and \\\(a_\{0\}\\\) the Bohr radius."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.6028/jres.092.010
