[Term]
id: goldbook:I02979
name: immunoassay
def: "A ligand-binding assay that uses a specific antigen or antibody\, capable of binding to the analyte\, to identify and quantify substances. The antibody can be linked to a radiosotope \(radioimmunoassay\, RIA\)\, or to an enzyme which catalyses an easily monitored reaction \(enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay\, ELISA\)\, or to a highly fluorescent compound by which the location of an antigen can be visualized \(immunofluorescene\)."
