[Term]
id: goldbook:I02999
name: incoherent radiation
def: "Not having the properties of coherent radiation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01130

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03003
name: increment
def: "An individual portion of material collected by a single operation of a sampling device. Increments may be reduced individually or tested either \(a\) individually or \(b\) combined with other increments with the resulting composite reduced in size and tested as a single unit. Increments are created by the sampling operation and are usually taken from parts of a lot separated in time or space. Increments of a bulk population correspond to units of a packaged population."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062061193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:CT07545

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03004
name: indicated hydrogen
def: "Under certain circumstances it is necessary to indicate in the name of a ring\, or ring system\, containing the maximum number of non-cumulative double bonds\, one or more positions where no multiple bond is attached. This is done by specifying the presence of an 'extra' hydrogen atom at such positions by citation of the appropriate numbered locant followed by an italicized capital H.Example\:  A second type of indicated hydrogen \(sometimes referred to as 'added hydrogen'\) describes hydrogen atoms added to a specific structure as a consequence of the addition of a suffix or a prefix describing a structural modification. This type of indicated hydrogen is normally cited in parentheses after the locant of the additional feature.Example\:"
synonym: "added hydrogen" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971071327
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01437

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03008
name: indifferent absorbing ion
def: "An ion which absorbs through coulomb forces only and which is hence only repelled by surfaces of like sign\, attracted by surfaces of opposite sign\, and is not absorbed on an uncharged surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163060895
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01365
consider: goldbook:S05792

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03009
name: indifferent electrolyte
def: "Synonymous with supporting electrolyte."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198557101491
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:S06149

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03010
name: indirect amplification
def: "A type of amplification reaction where the constituent required is associated with some other constituent which is then amplified and measured."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198254122553
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00307
consider: goldbook:C01281

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03011
name: indirect reaction
def: "A chemical process in which the reactive complex has a lifetime that is longer than its period of rotation is called an indirect reaction \(in contrast to a direct reaction\). In a molecular-beam experiment the products of such reactions are scattered at random with reference to the centre of mass of the system. Indirect reactions are also called complex-mode reactions. \(They are sometimes called complex reactions\, but this usage is not recommended in view of the danger of confusion with composite reactions\, which occur in more than one step\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
