[Term]
id: goldbook:I03058
name: insertion
def: "A chemical reaction or transformation of the general type\: $$\\ce\{X-Z + Y -> X-Y-Z\}$$ in which the connecting atom or group $\\ce\{Y\}$ replaces the bond joining the parts $\\ce\{X\}$ and $\\ce\{Z\}$ of the reactant $\\ce\{XZ\}$. An example is the carbene insertion reaction\:  The reverse of an insertion is called an extrusion."
