[Term]
id: goldbook:I03077
name: intercalation reaction
def: "Reaction\, generally reversible\, that involves the penetration of a host material by guest species without causing a major structural modification of the host."
comment: "Intercalation can refer to the insertion of a guest species into a one-, two- or three-dimensional host structure."
comment: "The guest species is not distributed randomly but occupies positions predetermined by the structure of the host material."
synonym: "insertion reaction" []
