[Term]
id: goldbook:I03097
name: intermediate neutrons
def: "Neutrons of kinetic energy between the energies of slow and fast neutrons. In reactor physics\, the range might be \\\(1\\ \\rm\{eV\}\\\) to \\\(0.1\\ \\rm\{MeV\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198254081533
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:F02329
consider: goldbook:K03402
consider: goldbook:S05712

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03098
name: intermolecular
def: "Descriptive of any process that involves a transfer \(of atoms\, groups\, electrons\, etc.\) or interactions between two or more molecular entities.Relating to a comparison between different molecular entities."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03130
consider: goldbook:M03986

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03102
name: internal conversion
def: "A photophysical process. An isoenenergetic radiationless transition between two electronic states of the same multiplicity. When the transition results in a vibrationally excited molecular entity in the lower electronic state\, this usually undergoes deactivation to its lowest vibrational level\, provided the final state is not unstable to dissociation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:D01528
consider: goldbook:D01801
consider: goldbook:ET07026
consider: goldbook:R05057
consider: goldbook:U06569

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03103
name: internal energy
def: "Quantity the change in which is equal to the sum of heat\, \\\(q\\\)\, brought to the system and work\, \\\(w\\\)\, performed on it\, \\\(\\Delta U=q+w\\\). Also called thermodynamic energy."
synonym: "thermodynamic energy" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668040957
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03105
name: internal filling solution
def: "Aqueous electrolyte solution\, which may be gelled\, containing fixed concentration of hydrogen ions\, e.g. $\\ce\{HCl\}$ or a buffer solution\, and a fixed concentration of the ion to which the internal reference electrode is reversible\, e.g. chloride ion in the case of silver-silver chloride\, or calomel electrodes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198557030531
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03106

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03106
name: internal reference electrode
def: "An 'inner' reference electrode which is contained inside an ion-selective electrode assembly."
comment: "The system frequently consists of a silver/silver chloride electrode in contact with an appropriate solution containing fixed concentrations of chloride and the ion for which the membrane is selective. This 'inner' filling solution is in contact with the ion-selective membrane."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466122527
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03244
consider: goldbook:MT06878
consider: goldbook:R05229

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03108
name: internal standard
def: "A compound added to a sample in known concentration to facilitate the qualitative indentification and/or quantitative determination of the sample components."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03109
name: internal surface
def: "With respect to porous solids\, the surface associated with pores communicating with the outside space. Since the accessibility of pores may depend on the size of the fluid molecules\, the extent of the accessible internal surface may depend on the size of the molecules comprising the fluid\, and may be different for the various components of a fluid mixture \(molecular sieve effect\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197646010071
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:M03998

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03111
name: internal valence force field
def: "A force field expressed in terms of bond-stretching\, angle-bending\, torsional and other displacements directly connected to the structural parameters of the molecule\: \\\[V=\\frac\{1\}\{2\}\\ \\sum k_\{ij\}\\ R_\{i\}\\ R_\{j\}\\\] or \\\[V=\\frac\{1\}\{2\}\\ \\sum K_\{ij\}\\ R_\{i\}\\ R_\{j\}\\\] where \\\(k\\\) \(or \\\(K\\\)\) are the force constants and \\\(R\\\) the internal valence coordinates."
synonym: "IVFF" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197850111707
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00346
consider: goldbook:F02481
consider: goldbook:V06588

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03114
name: international unit
def: "The unit of enzyme activity proposed by the International Union of Biochemistry in 1964. Specifically\, it is the amount of enzyme that catalyses the conversion of one micromole of substrate per minute under the specified conditions of the assay method."
comment: "This unit is no longer recommended because the term does not indicate what physical quantity it refers to, and because the minute is not the SI unit of time."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466122587
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00470
consider: goldbook:E02154

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03115
name: interparticle porosity
def: "The interparticle volume of a packed column per unit column volume\: \\\[\\varepsilon = \\frac\{V_\{0\}\}\{V_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\}\\\] It is also called the interstitial fraction of the column."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03116
name: interparticle volume of the column
def: "The volume occupied by the mobile phase between the particles in the packed section of a column. It is also called the interstitial volume or the void volume of the column. In liquid chromatography\, the interparticle volume is equal to the mobile-phase hold-up volume \(\\\(V_\{\\rm\{M\}\}\\\)\) in the ideal case\, neglecting any extra-column volume. In gas chromatography\, the symbol \\\(V_\{\\rm\{G\}\}\\\) may be used for the interparticle volume of the column. In the ideal case\, neglecting any extra-column volume\, \\\(V_\{\\rm\{G\}\}\\\) is equal to the corrected gas hold-up volume \(\\\(V_\{\\rm\{M\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\}\\\)\). \\\[V_\{\\rm\{G\}\}=V_\{\\rm\{M\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\}=V_\{\\rm\{M\}j\}\\\]"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01075
consider: goldbook:L03578

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03117
name: interpenetrating polymer network
def: "Polymer comprising two or more networks that are at least partially interlaced on a molecular scale but not covalently bonded to each other and cannot be separated unless chemical bonds are broken."
comment: "A mixture of two or more preformed polymer networks is not an IPN."
synonym: "IPN" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779101801
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03119
name: interphase transition
def: "A transition that occurs at boundaries between phases. Example\: The precipitation of second phases or the initiation of new phase growth at an interface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466030577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03042
consider: goldbook:I03082
consider: goldbook:P04795

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03123
name: intersystem crossing
def: "A photophysical process. An isoenergetic radiationless transition between two electronic states having different multiplicities. It often results in a vibrationally excited molecular entity in the lower electronic state\, which then usually deactivates to its lowest vibrational level."
synonym: "state crossing" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
