[Term]
id: goldbook:I03223
name: ion/molecule reaction
def: "An ion/neutral species reaction in which the neutral species is a molecule. The use of ion-molecule reaction is not recommended; the hyphen suggests a reaction of a species that is both an ion and a molecule and is not the intended meaning."
