[Term]
id: goldbook:I03229
name: ionomer
def: "Polymer composed of macromolecules in which a small but significant proportion of the constitutional units has ionic or ionizable groups\, or both."
comment: "Ionic groups are usually present in sufficient amounts (typically less than 10% of constitutional units) to cause micro-phase separation of ionic domains from the continuous polymer phase. The ionic domains act as physical crosslinks."
