consider: goldbook:E02033
consider: goldbook:K03393

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03276
name: isoelectronic
def: "Two or more molecular entities are described as isoelectronic if they have the same number of valence electrons and the same structure\, i.e. number and connectivity of atoms\, but differ in some of the elements involved. Thus\: $\\ce\{CO\}$\, $\\ce\{N2\}$ and $\\ce\{NO^\{+\}\}$ are isoelectronic. $\\ce\{CH2=C=O\}$ and $\\ce\{CH2=N=N\}$ are isoelectronic. $\\ce\{CH3COCH3\}$ and $\\ce\{CH3N=NCH3\}$ have the same number of electrons\, but have different structures\, hence they are not described as isoelectronic."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01274
consider: goldbook:M03986
consider: goldbook:V06588

[Term]
id: goldbook:I03277
name: isoemissive point
def: "Wavelength\, wavenumber or frequency at which the total intensity of emission of light by a sample does not change during a chemical reaction or physical change. The terms isolampsic and isostilbic are sometimes used."
comment: "This term may be misleading because it does not specifically refer to light emission."
