[Term]
id: goldbook:I03280
name: isoequilibrium relationship
def: "A relationship analogous to the isokinetic relationship but applied to equilibrium data. The equation defining the isoequilibrium temperature \\\(\\beta \\\) is\: \\\[\\Delta _\{\\rm\{r\}\}H - \\beta\\ \\Delta _\{\\rm\{r\}\}S = \\rm\{constant\}\\\] where \\\(\\Delta H\\\) and \\\(\\Delta S\\\) are enthalpy and entropy of reaction\, respectively."
