[Term]
id: goldbook:I03282
name: isoionic
def: "A macro-ion of a polyampholyte \(in particular a protein\) is said to be isoionic if besides the polyampholyte and $\\ce\{H^\{+\}\}$ or $\\ce\{OH^\{−\}\}$ ions \(in general ions of the solvent\) no other ions are present in the system."
