[Term]
id: goldbook:I03295
name: isomerization
def: "A chemical reaction\, the principal product of which is isomeric with the principal reactant. An intramolecular isomerization that involves the breaking or making of bonds is a special case of a molecular rearrangement. Isomerization does not necessarily imply molecular rearrangement \(e.g. in the case of the interconversion of conformational isomers\)."
