id: goldbook:I03302
name: isooptoacoustic point
def: "Wavelength\, wavenumber or frequency at which the total energy emitted by a sample as heat does not change upon a chemical reaction in or a physical change of the sample. Its position depends on the experimental conditions."
comment: "The spectral differences between the @I03310@ points and the iso-optoacoustic points are the result of the non-linear relationship between the @M03972@ and the photoacoustic signal."
