[Term]
id: goldbook:I03308
name: isopycnic separation
def: "Chromatographic separations carried out using constant density conditions. The temperature and pressure may be altered during the run \(originally the term 'isoconfertic separation' was used but this term is not recommended\)."
synonym: "isoconfertic separation" []
