[Term]
id: goldbook:I03352
name: isotopomer
def: "Isomers having the same number of each isotopic atom but differing in their positions. The term is a contraction of 'isotopic isomer'. Isotopomers can be either constitutional isomers \(e.g. $\\ce\{CH2DCH=O\}$ and $\\ce\{CH3CD=O\}$\) or isotopic stereoisomers \[e.g. $\\ce\{\(\\textit\{R\}\)-\}$ and $\\ce\{\(\\textit\{S\}\)-CH3CHDOH\}$ or $\\ce\{\(\\textit\{Z\}\)-\}$ and $\\ce\{\(\\textit\{E\}\)-CH3CH=CHD\}$\]."
