consider: goldbook:P04694

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT06944
name: ideal\, non-linear chromatography
def: "Chromatographic process\, where only the curvature of the distribution isotherm determines the shape of the peaks while other peak-broadening processes are neglected."
comment: "The assumption of ideal, non-linear (INL) chromatography is often made in order to facilitate theoretical treatments. It can be justified in cases of efficient columns and distribution isotherms with prominent non-linearity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668081591
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01075
consider: goldbook:DT06932

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07055
name: individual gauge for localized orbitals
def: "A method of calculation of nuclear shieldings\, in which localized molecular orbitals associated with inner shell\, bonding orbitals\, and lone pairs have unique origins for the calculation of diamagnetic and paramagnetic terms. With this method\, satisfactory estimates of NMR chemical shifts for elements in the first and second rows can be achieved in ab initio calculations with basis sets of moderate size provided sufficiently accurate molecular geometries are used."
synonym: "IGLO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:D01668
consider: goldbook:P04404

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07056
name: instability of Hartree–Fock solution
def: "Existence of additional solutions to the equations of the Hartree–Fock method occurring usually in the case when potential energy surfaces of different electronic states are drawn close together. Within the spin-restricted Hartree–Fock method \(RHF\)\, singlet and triplet instabilities are distinguished. The former involves the existence of another solution with lower energy and the electron distribution of lower symmetry. It may be regarded as an indication that the initially assumed molecular shape needs correction. The triplet instability involves rejection of the condition of double occupancy of molecular orbitals and thus transition to the spin-unrestricted Hartree–Fock method \(UHF\). The triplet instability is a necessary\, but insufficient\, condition for the conclusion as to the biradical character of the ground state of a given system."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:B00671
consider: goldbook:G02704
consider: goldbook:H02747
consider: goldbook:MT06972

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07057
name: intrinsic reaction coordinate
def: "A minimum-energy reaction path on a potential energy surface in mass-weighted coordinates\, connecting reactants to products via the transition state."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:M03931
consider: goldbook:T06468

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07058
name: ionic bond
def: "The bond between atoms with sharply different electronegativities. In strict terms\, an ionic bond refers to the electrostatic attraction experienced between the electric charges of a cation and an anion\, in contrast with a purely covalent bond. In practice\, it is preferable to consider the amount of ionic character of a bond rather than referring to purely ionic or purely covalent bonds. The relationship was proposed \(L. Pauling\) for the estimation of ionic character of a bond between atoms A and B\: \\\[\\rm\{Amount of ionic character\} = 1 - e^\{-1/4\}\\ \(\\chi _\{\\rm\{A\}\}\\\,-\\\,\\chi_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\)\\\] where \\\(\\chi _\{\\rm\{A\}\}\\\) and \\\(\\chi _\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) are the Pauling electronegativities of atoms A and B. This type of bonding is realized mostly in solids."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00358
consider: goldbook:C00907
consider: goldbook:C01384
consider: goldbook:E01990

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07059
name: isoconjugate systems
def: "Molecular entities with similar conjugate networks which have the same number of $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}electrons\}$\, e.g. cyclopentadienide anion and pyrrole or benzene and pyridine."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00358

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07060
name: isogyric reaction
def: "A reaction in which the number of electron pairs is conserved\, for example\:  $$\\ce\{CH4\(^\{1\}\\textit\{A\}_\{1\}\) + H\(^\{2\}\\textit\{S\}\) -> CH3\(^\{2\}\\textit\{A\}^\{'\}_\{2\}\) + H2\(^\{1\}\\Sigma^\{+\}_\{\\rm\{g\}\}\)\}$$"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07061
name: isostructural reaction
def: "A ligand exchange reaction\, where the structural type of the metal complex remains the same. $$\\ce\{ML_\{n\} + X -> ML_\{n-1\}X + L + \\Delta\\textit\{E\}\}$$ Although these types of reactions are not necessarily isodesmic reactions\, a substantial degree of error cancellation for the calculated energy\, $\\Delta E$\, is achieved because the coordination sphere of the metal atom $\\ce\{M\}$ is conserved."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01329

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07139
name: interchange reaction
def: "Reaction that results in an exchange of atoms or groups between a polymer and low-molar-mass molecules\, between polymer molecules\, or between sites within the same macromolecule."
comment: "An interchange reaction that occurs with polyesters is called transesterification."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200476040889
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07155
name: ion-exchange polymer
def: "Polymer that is able to exchange ions \(cations or anions\) with ionic components in solution."
comment: "A membrane having ion-exchange groups is called an ion-exchange membrane."
comment: "An ion-exchange polymer in ionized form may also be referred to as a polyanion or a polycation."
comment: "Synthetic ion-exchange organic polymers are often network polyelectrolytes."
comment: "Use of the term 'ion-exchange resin' for 'ion-exchange polymer' is strongly discouraged."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200476040889
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03167
consider: goldbook:MT06878
consider: goldbook:NT07562
consider: goldbook:RT07166

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07175
name: impact-modified polymer
def: "Polymeric material whose impact resistance and toughness have been increased by the incorporation of phase microdomains of a rubbery material."
comment: "An example is the incorporation of soft polybutadiene domains into glassy polystyrene to produce high-impact polystyrene."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200476040889
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:M03667
consider: goldbook:R05315

[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07208
name: intrinsically conducting polymer
def: "Electrically conducting polymer composed of macromolecules having fully conjugated sequences of double bonds along the chains."
comment: "An intrinsically conducting polymer should be distinguished from a conducting polymer composite and from a solid polymer electrolyte."
comment: "Examples of intrinsically conducting polymers are polyacetylene, polythiophene, polypyrrole, or polyaniline. Unlike polymeric electrolytes, in which charge is transported by dissolved ions, charge in intrinsically conducting polymers is transported along and between polymer molecules via generated charge carriers (e.g., holes, electrons)."
comment: "The bulk electrical conductivity of an intrinsically conducting polymer is comparable to that of some metals and results from its macromolecules acquiring positive or negative charges through oxidation or reduction by an electron-acceptor or -donor (charge-transfer agent), termed a dopant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200678112067
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
