[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07233
name: isomorphic polymer blend
def: "Polymer blend of two or more different semi-crystalline polymers that are miscible in the crystalline state as well as in the molten state."
comment: "Such a blend exhibits a single, composition-dependent glass-transition temperature, \(T_{\rm{g}}\), and a single, composition-dependent melting point, \(T_{\rm{m}}\)."
comment: "This behaviour is extremely rare; very few cases are known."
