[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07246
name: impregnation
def: "Penetration of monomeric\, oligomeric\, or polymeric liquids into an assembly of fibres."
comment: "Impregnation is usually carried out on a woven fabric or a yarn."
comment: "The term as defined here is specific to polymer science. An alternative definition of 'impregnation' applies in some other fields of chemistry."
