[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07253
name: interfacial adhesion
def: "Adhesion in which interfaces between phases or components are maintained by intermolecular forces\, chain entanglements\, or both\, across the interfaces."
comment: "Adhesive strength (recommended symbol: \(F_{\rm{a}}\), unit: \(\rm{N m}^{-2}\)) is the force required to separate one condensed phase domain from another at the interface between the two phase domains divided by the area of the interface."
comment: "Interfacial adhesion is also referred to as tack."
comment: "Interfacial tension (recommended symbol: \(\gamma\), unit: \(\rm{N m}^{-1}\), \(\pu{J m-2}\)) is the change in Gibbs energy per unit change in interfacial area for substances in physical contact."
comment: "Use of the term interfacial energy for interfacial tension is not recommended."
