[Term]
id: goldbook:IT07399
name: infrared
def: "Region of the electromagnetic spectrum extending from \\\(780\\ \\rm\{nm\}\\\) to about \\\(20\\\,000\\ \\rm\{nm\}\\\).According to the CIE\, the range between \\\(780\\ \\rm\{nm\}\\\) and \\\(1\\ \\rm\{mm\}\\\) is subdivided into\:IR-A \\\(780\\\)–\\\(1400\\ \\rm\{nm\}\\\)IR-B \\\(1.4\\\)–\\\(3\\ \\unicode\[times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{m\}\\\)IR-C \\\(3\\ \\unicode\[times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{m\}\\\)–\\\(1\\ \\rm\{mm\}\\\)"
comment: "This is the wavelength region in which absorption by a molecular entity causes excitation of its vibrational, rotational, and bending modes."
