[Term]
id: goldbook:L03613
name: logit
def: "In competitive binding assays\, the logit-log dose relationship\, in which the response is defined by\: \\\(R=\\mathrm\{logit\}\\left\(y\\right\)=\\log _\{10\}\(\\frac\{y\}\{1- y\}\)\\\) where \\\(y=\\frac\{b\}\{b_\{0\}\}\\\) with \\\(b\\\) = fraction of tracer bound and \\\(b_\{0\}\\\) = value of \\\(b\\\) with no unlabelled ligand in the system. Logit transformed assay data frequently yield straight-line dose-response curves\, amenable to statistical analysis."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466122513
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00470
consider: goldbook:C01199
consider: goldbook:DT07361
consider: goldbook:L03518
consider: goldbook:T06422

[Term]
id: goldbook:L03614
name: log-normal distribution
def: "A distribution function \\\(F\(y\)\\\)\, in which the logarithm of a quantity is normally distributed\, i.e. \\\(F\(y\)=f_\{\\rm\{gauss\}\}\(\\ln y\)\\\) where \\\(f_\{\\rm\{gauss\}\}\(x\)\\\) is a Gaussian distribution. The size distributions of atmospheric aerosols are often described using this distribution function\, although the term also applies to gaseous pollutants."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

