[Term]
id: goldbook:M03667
name: macromolecule
def: "A molecule of high relative molecular mass\, the structure of which essentially comprises the multiple repetition of units derived\, actually or conceptually\, from molecules of low relative molecular mass."
comment: "If a part or the whole of the molecule has a high relative molecular mass and essentially comprises the multiple repetition of units derived, actually or conceptually, from molecules of low relative molecular mass, it may be described as either macromolecular or polymeric, or by polymer used adjectivally."
comment: "In many cases, especially for synthetic polymers, a molecule can be regarded as having a high relative molecular mass if the addition or removal of one or a few of the units has a negligible effect on the molecular properties. This statement fails in the case of certain macromolecules for which the properties may be critically dependent on fine details of the molecular structure."
synonym: "macromolecular" []
synonym: "polymer molecule" []
synonym: "polymeric" []
