[Term]
id: goldbook:M03680
name: magnetic deflection
def: "The deflection of an ion beam as a result of the motion of the ions in a magnetic field \(magnetic sector\). Generally the direction of motion of the ions is at right angles to the direction of the magnetic field\, and the motion is uniform."
