[Term]
id: goldbook:M03730
name: mass resolving power
def: "Commonly and also acceptably defined in terms of the overlap \(or 'valley'\) between two peaks. Thus for two peaks of equal height\, masses \\\(m_\{1\}\\\) and \\\(m_\{2\}\\\)\, when there is overlap between the two peaks to a stated percentage of either peak height \(10% is recommended\)\, then the resolving power is defined as \\\(\\frac\{m_\{1\}\}\{m_\{1\} - m_\{2\}\}\\\). The percentage overlap \(or 'valley'\) concerned must always be stated."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197850010065
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
