[Term]
id: goldbook:M03732
name: mass spectrometer
def: "An instrument in which beams of ions are separated \(analysed\) according to the quotient mass/charge\, and in which the ions are measured electrically. This term should also be used when a scintillation detector is employed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163101541
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:S05505

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03733
name: mass spectrometer
def: "A mass spectrometer in which the ions to be separated absorb maximum energy through the effect of alternating electric fields which are parallel to the path of the ions. These ions are then separated from other ions with different mass/charge by an additional electric field."
