[Term]
id: goldbook:M03751
name: E/2 mass spectrum
def: "Processes of the charge-stripping type\: \\\[\\rm\{M\}^\{+\}+\\rm\{X\}\\rightarrow \\rm\{M\}^\{2+\}+\\rm\{X\}+\\rm\{e\}\\\] occuring in a collision cell \(containing a gas\, X\) located in a field-free region preceding a magnetic and electric sector combination placed in either order\, may be detected as follows. If the instrument slits are wide and if the electric sector field \\\(E\\\) is set to half the value required to transmit the main ion-beam\, the only ions to be transmitted will be those with a kinetic energy/charge ratio half\, or almost exactly half\, that of the main ion beam. The product ions of the charge-stripping process fulfil this condition. If the magnetic field \\\(B\\\) is scanned\, a mass spectrum of such doubly-charged product ions\, and thus of their singly-charged precursors\, is obtained. Such a spectrum is called an \\\(\\frac\{E\}\{2\}\\\) mass spectrum. Interference from product ions from processes of the type\: \\\[\\rm\{M\}_\{1\}^\{+\}+\\rm\{X\}\\rightarrow \\rm\{M\}_\{2\}^\{+\}+\\rm\{X\}+\\rm\{M\}_\{3\}\\\] where \\\(m_\{1\}\\\)\, \\\(m_\{2\}\\\)\, and \(\\\(m_\{1\}- m_\{2\}\\\)\) are the masses of \\\(\\rm\{M\}_\{1\}^\{+\}\\\)\, \\\(\\rm\{M\}_\{2\}^\{+\}\\\) and \\\(\\rm\{M\}_\{3\}\\\)\, respectively\, and where \\\(m_\{2\}=0.5\\ m_\{1\}\\\)\, can arise in \\\(\\frac\{E\}\{2\}\\\) mass spectra."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163101541
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:K03402
consider: goldbook:S06054

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03752
name: mass-to-charge ratio
def: "The abbreviation \\\(\\frac\{m\}\{z\}\\\) is used to denote the dimensionless quantity formed by dividing the mass number of an ion by its charge number. It has long been called the mass-to-charge ratio although \\\(m\\\) is not the ionic mass nor is \\\(z\\\) a multiple or the elementary \(electronic\) charge\, \\\(e\\\). The abbreviation \\\(\\frac\{m\}\{e\}\\\) is\, therefore\, not recommended. Thus\, for example\, for the ion \($\\ce\{C7H7^\{2+\}\}$\)\, \\\(\\frac\{m\}\{z\}\\\) equals 45.5."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163101541
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C00993
consider: goldbook:M03726

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03753
name: mass transfer
def: "Spontaneous \(irreversible\) process of transfer of mass across non-homogeneous fields. The driving force can be difference in concentration \(in liquids\) or partial pressure \(in gases\) of the component. In fluids\, mass transfer may be enhanced by turbulent flow. In biological systems\, mass transfer through membranes may result from normal diffusion\, facilitated diffusion or active transport."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00112
consider: goldbook:D01716
consider: goldbook:P04420

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03754
name: mass transfer coefficient
def: "The heterogeneous diffusion rate constant defined for the case of the limiting current. A more general definition in terms of the electrode current densities is\: \\\[k_\{\\rm\{d\}\}=\\frac\{j\\  u \}\{n\\ F\\ \(c_\{\\rm\{e\}\}- c_\{0\}\)\}\\\] or \\\[k_\{\\rm\{d\}\} = \\frac\{j\\  u \\ \(1- t_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\ n\\  u ^\{-1\}\\ z_\{\\rm\{B\}\}^\{-1\}\)\}\{n\\ F\\ \(c_\{\\rm\{e\}\}- c_\{0\}\)\}\\\] where \\\(j\\\) is the electrode current density\, \\\( u \\\) is the stoichiometric number\, \\\(n\\\) is the charge number of the electrode reaction\, \\\(F\\\) is the Faraday constant\, \\\(c_\{\\rm\{e\}\}\\\) is the interfacial concentration\, \\\(c_\{0\}\\\) is the bulk concentration\, \\\(t_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is the transport number of species B\, and \\\(z_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is the charge number of species B."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198153101827
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:B00753
consider: goldbook:C00993
consider: goldbook:C00995
consider: goldbook:E01952
consider: goldbook:F02325
consider: goldbook:H02805
consider: goldbook:I03083
consider: goldbook:L03532
consider: goldbook:S06025
consider: goldbook:T06489

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03755
name: mass-transfer-controlled electrolyte rate constant
def: "In controlled-potential coulometry and related techniques\, the empirically evaluated constant of proportionality defined by the equation \\\[s_\{\\rm\{B\}\}=- \\frac\{1\}\{c_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\}\\ \\frac\{\\mathrm\{d\}c_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\}\{\\mathrm\{d\}t\}\\\] where \\\(c_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is the bulk concentration of the substance B\, and \\\(\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}c_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\) is the rate of change of that concentration\, resulting from the consumption of B by reduction or oxidation at the working electrode."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198557101491
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:B00753
consider: goldbook:O04362
consider: goldbook:W06686

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03756
name: matched cells
def: "A pair of cells with closely similar optical properties are called matched cells. One cell is the sample cell while the other\, the reference \(or blank\) cell contains the solvent or a reference solution. In double beam spectrometers\, radiation is passed either simultaneously or alternately through the cells. In single beam instruments the cells are moved sequentially into the radiation beam."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198860091449
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:D01842

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03757
name: material safety data sheet
def: "Compilation of information required under the US OSHA Hazard Communication Standard on the identity of hazardous substances\, health and physical hazards\, exposure limits and precautions."
synonym: "MSDS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365092003
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:HT06827

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03758
name: matrix
def: "The components of the sample other than the analyte."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198961091657
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03759
name: matrix effect
def: "The combined effect of all components of the sample other than the analyte on the measurement of the quantity. If a specific component can be identified as causing an effect then this is referred to as interference."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198961091657
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:M03758

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03760
name: matrix isolation
def: "A term which refers to the isolation of a reactive or unstable species by dilution in an inert matrix \(argon\, nitrogen\, etc.\)\, usually condensed on a window or in an optical cell at low temperature\, to preserve its structure for identification by spectroscopic or other means."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03026
consider: goldbook:U06569

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03761
name: Mattauch–Herzog geometry
def: "An arrangement for a double-focusing mass spectrograph in which a deflection of \\\(\\frac\{\\pi\}\{4\\ \\sqrt\{2\}\}\\\) radians in a radial electrostatic field is followed by a magnetic deflection of \\\(\\frac\{\\pi\}\{2\}\\\) radians."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163101541
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:M03731

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03762
name: maximum allowable concentration
def: "The maximum concentration of a pollutant which is considered harmless to healthy adults during their working hours\, assuming they breathe uncontaminated air at all other times."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03763
name: maximum emission concentration
def: "Standards for maximum concentration of air pollutant emission from stationary or mobile sources."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
