consider: goldbook:A00194

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03765
name: maximum permissible daily dose
def: "Maximum daily dose of substance whose penetration into a human body during a lifetime will not cause diseases or health hazards that can be detected by current investigation methods and will not adversely affect future generations."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365092003
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:DT07361
consider: goldbook:L03515

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03766
name: maximum permissible level
def: "Level\, usually a combination of time and concentration\, beyond which any exposure of humans to a chemical or physical agent in their immediate environment is unsafe."
synonym: "MPL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365092003
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:M03762

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03767
name: maximum storage life
def: "Period during which there is no change in concentration in excess of the value of the uncertainty of the concentration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03768
name: maximum tolerable concentration
def: "Highest concentration of a substance in an environmental medium that does not cause death of test organisms or species \(denoted by \\\(\\rm\{LC\}_\{0\}\\\)\)."
synonym: "MTC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365092003
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03769
name: maximum tolerable dose
def: "Highest amount of a substance that\, when introduced into the body\, does not kill test animals \(denoted by \\\(\\rm\{LD\}_\{0\}\\\)\)."
synonym: "MTD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365092003
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03770
name: maximum tolerable exposure level
def: "Maximum amount or concentration of a substance to which an organism can be exposed without leading to an adverse effect after prolonged exposure time."
synonym: "MTEL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365092003
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:AT06809

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03771
name: maximum tolerated dose
def: "High dose used in chronic toxicity testing that is expected on the basis of an adequate subchronic study to produce limited toxicity when administered for the duration of the test period. It should not induce\: \(a\) overt toxicity\, for example appreciable death of cells or organ dysfunction\, or \(b\) toxic manifestations that are predicted materially to reduce the life span of the animals except as the result of neoplastic development or \(c\) 10% or greater retardation of body weight gain as compared with control animals. In some studies\, toxicity that could interfere with a carcinogenic effect is specifically excluded from consideration."
synonym: "MTD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365092003
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:CT06817
consider: goldbook:DT07361
consider: goldbook:T06414
consider: goldbook:W06668

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03774
name: mean activity of an electrolyte in solution
def: "Defined by the equation\: \\\[a_\{\\pm \}=\\mathrm\{e\}^\{\(\\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}- \\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}^\{\\unicode\{x29B5\}\}\)\\  u \\ R\\ T\}\\\] where \\\(\\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is the chemical potential of the solute $\\ce\{B\}$ in a solution containing B and other species. The nature of $\\ce\{B\}$ must be clearly stated\: it is taken as a group of ions of two kinds carrying an equal number of positive and negative charges\, e.g. $\\ce\{Na^\{+\}\} + \\ce\{NO3^\{−\}\}$ or $\\ce\{Ba^\{2+\}\} + \\ce\{2Cl^\{−\}\}$ or $\\ce\{2Al^\{3+\}\} + \\ce\{3SO4^\{2−\}\}$. \\\(v\\\) is the total number of ions making up the group i.e. 2\, 3 and 5 respectively in the above examples. \\\(\\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}^\{\\unicode\{x29B5\}\}\\\) is the chemical potential of $\\ce\{B\}$ in its standard state\, usually the hypothetical ideal solution of concentration \\\(\\pu\{1 mol kg -1\}\\\) and at the same temperature and pressure as the solution under consideration."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197437040499
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00113
consider: goldbook:C01032
consider: goldbook:S05925

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03775
name: mean catalytic activity rate
def: "The catalytic activity of a specified component in or moved from a system divided by the time during which the component was changed or moved. This kind of quantity should not be confused with rate of reaction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197951122451
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05156

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03776
name: mean current density
def: "Defined as \\\[j=\\frac\{I\}\{A\}\\\] where \\\(I\\\) is the electric current and \\\(A\\\) is usually taken as the geometric area of the electrode. However the nature of the area used in this calculation must be clearly stated. In interpreting the mean current density it is important to know whether the current is uniformly distributed over the electrode interface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197437040499
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01452
consider: goldbook:E01927
consider: goldbook:I03082

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03777
name: mean exchange current density
def: "Defined by \\\[j_\{0\}=\\frac\{I_\{0\}\}\{A\}\\\] where \\\(I_\{0\}\\\) is the exchange current of the electrode reaction and \\\(A\\\) is usually taken as the geometric area of the electrode."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197437040499
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E02238

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03778
name: mean free path
def: "The average distance a molecule travels between collisions. For a molecule\, \\\(\\lambda = \(\\sqrt\{2\}\\ \\pi \\ n\\ d_\{\\rm\{m\}\}^\{2\}\)^\{-1\}\\\)\, where \\\(n\\\) is the number of molecules per unit volume and \\\(d_\{\\rm\{m\}\}\\\) is their mean diameter. For $\\ce\{O2\}$ at one atmosphere and \\\(25\\ ^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\rm\{C\}\\\)\, this distance is only \\\(9.7\\times 10^\{-6\}\\ \\rm\{cm\}\\\); at \\\(10^\{-6\}\\\) atmospheres and \\\(25\\ ^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\rm\{C\}\\\) it is \\\(9.7\\ \\rm\{cm\}\\\). For an aerosol particle\, the mean free path\, \\\(\\lambda _\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) in the Stokes region \(see Stokes law\) is given by\: \\\(\\lambda _\{\\rm\{B\}\} = \\sqrt\{\\frac\{3\\ k\\ T\}\{m\}\}\\ m\\ B\\\) where \\\(m\\\) is the mass of the particle\, \\\(k\\\) is the Boltzmann constant \(\\\(1.381\\times 10^\{-23\}\\ \\rm\{J K\}^\{-1\}\\\)\)\, \\\(T\\\) is the temperature \(\\\(\\rm\{K\}\\\)\) and \\\(B\\\) is the mobility."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00176
consider: goldbook:B00695
consider: goldbook:M03955
consider: goldbook:S06027
consider: goldbook:S06028

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03782
name: mean linear range
def: "In a given material\, for specified charged particles of a specified energy\, the average displacement of the particles before they stop."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198254081533
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03783
