[Term]
id: goldbook:M03788
name: measurable quantity
def: "An attribute of a substance which may be distinguished qualitatively and determined quantitatively. In the context of analytical chemistry\, the attribute may refer to a physical quantity such as X- or $\\upgamma\\!\\mbox\{-\}\\rm\{ray\\ energy\}$\, or it may refer to a measure of amount such as mass or concentration."
