[Term]
id: goldbook:M03815
name: medium effect
def: "The medium effect on ionic species B due to transfer from solvent \\\(\\rm\{S\}_\{1\}\\\) to solvent \\\(\\rm\{S\}_\{2\}\\\) \(number\) is defined by \\\[R\\ T\\ \\ln \\gamma _\{\\rm\{S\}_\{1\}\}^\{\\rm\{S\}_\{2\}\}\\left\(\\rm\{B\}\\right\)=\\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\,\\rm\{S\}_\{2\}\}- \\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\,\\rm\{S\}_\{1\}\}\\\] where \\\(R\\\) is the gas constant\, \\\(T\\\) is the thermodynamic temperature and \\\(\\mu _\{\\rm\{B\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\,\\rm\{S\}_\{i\}\}\\\) is the standard chemical potential of B in solvent \\\(\\rm\{S\}_\{i\}\\\) \(where \\\(i\\\) = 1 or 2\)\, the reference states being the same in both solvents. \\\(\\gamma _\{\\rm\{S\}_\{1\}\}^\{\\rm\{S\}_\{2\}\}\(\\rm\{B\}\)\\\) is not an exactly measurable quantity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197437040499
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01032
consider: goldbook:G02579
consider: goldbook:M03788
consider: goldbook:T06321

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03816
name: medium-pressure mercury lamp
def: "Non-coherent radiation source containing mercury vapour at pressures ranging from \\\(50\\\) to several hundred \\\(\\mathrm\{kPa\}\\\) \(\\\(1\\ \\rm\{atm\} = 101.325\\ \\rm\{kPa\}\\\)\). Emits mostly from \\\(200\\\) to \\\(1000\\ \\rm\{nm\}\\\) with the most intense lines approximately at \\\(218\\\)\, \\\(248\\\)\, \\\(254\\\)\, \\\(266\\\)\, \\\(280\\\)\, \\\(289\\\)\, \\\(297\\\)\, \\\(303\\\)\, \\\(313\\\)\, \\\(334\\\)\, \\\(366\\\)\, \\\(406\\\)\, \\\(408\\\)\, \\\(436\\\)\, \\\(546\\\) and \\\(578\\ \\rm\{nm\}\\\)."
synonym: "medium-pressure mercury arc" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01130

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03818
name: meiosis
def: "The reductive cell division which results in daughter cells containing one copy of each of the chromosome of the parent. The entire meiotic process involves two separate divisions \(meiosis I and meiosis II\). The first division is a true reductive division with the chromosome number being halved\, whereas the second division resembles mitosis in many ways. Thus\, a diploid parental cell will give rise to haploid daughter cells \(cf. ploidy\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01077
consider: goldbook:M03938
consider: goldbook:P04696

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03819
name: Meisenheimer adduct
def: "A cyclohexadienyl derivative formed as Lewis adduct from a nucleophile \(Lewis base\) and an aromatic or heteroaromatic compound\, also called Jackson–Meisenheimer adduct. In earlier usage the term 'Meisenheimer complex' was restricted to the typical Meisenheimer alkoxide adduct of nitro-substituted aromatic ethers\, e.g.  Analogous cationic adducts\, such as\:  considered to be reaction intermediates in electrophilic aromatic substitution reactions\, are called 'Wheland intermediates'\, and sometimes\, inappropriately\, $\\ce\{\\upsigma\\!\\mbox\{-\}complexes\}$."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
