[Term]
id: goldbook:M03821
name: melting
def: "The conversion of a solid to a liquid by the application of heat and/or pressure."
comment: "For a liquid crystal, melting occurs when the three-dimensional periodic structure of a solid collapses to give a liquid-crystal phase in which the molecules have orientational order, but not long range translational order."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466030577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
