[Term]
id: goldbook:M03842
name: mesoionic compounds
def: "Dipolar five- \(possibly six-\) membered heterocyclic compounds in which both the negative and the positive charge are delocalized\, for which a totally covalent structure cannot be written\, and which cannot be represented satisfactorily by any one polar structure. The formal positive charge is associated with the ring atoms\, and the formal negative charge is associated with ring atoms or an exocyclic nitrogen or chalcogen atom. Mesoionic compounds are a subclass of betaines."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567081307
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:B00637
