consider: goldbook:S06207

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03843
name: mesolytic cleavage
def: "Cleavage of a bond in a radical ion whereby a radical and an ion are formed. The term reflects the mechanistic duality of the process\, which can be viewed as homolytic or heterolytic depending on how the electrons are attributed to the fragments."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05066
consider: goldbook:R05073

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03844
name: mesomeric effect
def: "The effect \(on reaction rates\, ionization equilibria\, etc.\) attributed to a substituent due to overlap of its p- or $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}orbitals\}$ with the p- or $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}orbitals\}$ of the rest of the molecular entity. delocalization is thereby introduced or extended\, and electronic charge may flow to or from the substituent. The effect is symbolized by M. Strictly understood\, the mesomeric effect operates in the ground electronic state of the molecule. When the molecule undergoes electronic excitation or its energy is increased on the way to the transition state of a chemical reaction\, the mesomeric effect may be enhanced by the electromeric effect\, but this term is not much used\, and the mesomeric and electromeric effects tend to be subsumed in the term resonance effect of a substituent."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
