consider: goldbook:T06468

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03845
name: mesomerism
def: "Essentially synonymous with resonance. The term is particularly associated with the picture of $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}electrons\}$ as less localized in an actual molecule than in a Lewis formula. The term is intended to imply that the correct representation of a structure is intermediate between two or more Lewis formulae."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
