[Term]
id: goldbook:M03846
name: mesomorphic phase
def: "Often formed by concentrated systems of surfactants. These are states of matter in which anisometric molecules \(or particles\) are regularly arranged in one \(nematic state\) or two \(smectic state\) directions\, but randomly arranged in the remaining direction\(s\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
