[Term]
id: goldbook:M03865
name: metallocenes
def: "Organometallic coordination compounds in which one atom of a transition metal such as iron\, ruthenium or osmium is bonded to and only to the face of two cyclopentadienyl $\\ce\{\[\\upeta\\!^\{5\}\\mbox\{-\}\(C5H5\)\]\}$ ligands which lie in parallel planes. The term should not be used for analogues having rings other than cyclopentadienyl as ligands."
