[Term]
id: goldbook:M03866
name: metallurgical coke
def: "Metallurgical coke is produced by carbonization of coals or coal blends at temperatures up to \\\(1400\\ \\rm\{K\}\\\) to produce a macroporous carbon material of high strength and relatively large lump size."
comment: "Metallurgical cokes must have a high strength to support heavy loads in the blast furnace without disintegration. Metallurgical coke is also used as filler coke for polygranular carbon products."
