[Term]
id: goldbook:M03871
name: metastability
def: "A term that describes the state of a phase in which an energy barrier considerably higher than \\\(k\\ T\\\) must be surmounted before this phase can transform to a phase of lower molar Gibbs energy and molar Helmholtz energy\, where \\\(k\\\) is the Boltzmann constant and \\\(T\\\) the thermodynamic temperature."
comment: "In a thermodynamic sense, the equilibrium state is the state with the lowest molar Gibbs energy; a metastable state corresponds to a relative minimum in the molar Gibbs energy."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466030577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
