[Term]
id: goldbook:M03936
name: mist
def: "A qualitative term applied to a suspension of droplets in a gas. In the atmosphere a mist produces a generally thin\, greyish veil over the landscape. It reduces visibility to a lesser extent than fog but somewhat more than haze \(visibility of less than \\\(2\\ \\rm\{km\}\\\) but greater than \\\(1\\ \\rm\{km\}\\\)\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
