[Term]
id: goldbook:M03941
name: mixed energy release
def: "This is an effect found in a process A + BC when the attacking species A is heavy. Because A is heavy the A–B distance continues to decrease while the repulsive energy of B–C is being released."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03943
name: mixed labelled
def: "A specifically labelled compound is referred to as mixed labelled when the isotopically substituted compound has more than one kind of modified atom e.g. $\\ce\{CH3–CH2–\[^\{18\}O\]\[^\{2\}H\]\}$."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198153101887
