consider: goldbook:R05156
consider: goldbook:S06033

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03947
name: mixing height
def: "The height to which significant mixing of added pollutants occurs within the atmosphere. In reference to stack gases\, it is considered the height at which stack effluent begins mixing with the atmosphere as it leaves the stack."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E01910

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03948
name: mixing ratio
def: "In meteorology\, the dimensionless ratio of the mass of a substance \(such as water vapour\) in an air parcel to the mass of the remaining substances in the air parcel. For trace substances\, this is approximated by the ratio of the mass of the substance to the mass of air. However\, in the case of water vapour the mass of dry air is used. In atmospheric chemistry\, mixing ratios \(molecular\, molar\, by volume\, as well as by weight\) are used to describe relative concentrations of atmospheric trace gases and impurities."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:W06668

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03950
