[Term]
id: goldbook:M03959
name: mode-locked laser
def: "A laser in which many resonant modes are coupled in phase\, to yield a train of very short pulses \(e.g. ps pulses\). The coupling of the modes is obtained by modulation of the gain in the resonator\, and can be active \(electro-optic modulation of the losses or of the pump intensity\)\, or passive \(with a saturable absorber\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
