[Term]
id: goldbook:M03963
name: modified Arrhenius equation
def: "This is an extension of the simple Arrhenius equation in which the pre-exponential factor is proportional to \\\(T^\{n\}\\\) where \\\(T\\\) is the temperature and \\\(n\\\) a constant\: \\\[k = B\\ T^\{n\}\\ \\exp\(-E_\{\\rm\{a\}\}/RT\)\\\] \\\(B\\\) is a temperature-independent constant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00446
consider: goldbook:P04811

[Term]
id: goldbook:M03964
name: modified sample
def: "A sample or a known fraction of the parent population in which the analyte has been isolated or \(usually\) concentrated before being submitted to the laboratory. If the isolation or concentration occurs in the laboratory\, the procedure is usually considered part of the preparation of the test sample from the laboratory sample \(in-laboratory processing\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062061193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
