[Term]
id: goldbook:M04042
name: multi-centre bond
def: "Representation of some molecular entities solely by localized two-electron two-centre bonds appears to be unsatisfactory. Instead\, multi-centre bonds have to be considered in which electron pairs occupy orbitals encompassing three or more atomic centres. Examples include the three-centre bonds in diborane\, the delocalized $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}bonding\}$ of benzene and bridged carbocations."
