[Term]
id: goldbook:MT06928
name: mass distribution ratio
def: "Defined as\: \\\[k_\{\\rm\{MEKC\}\} = \\frac\{n_\{\\rm\{mc\}\}\}\{n_\{\\rm\{aq\}\}\} = K\\cdot \\frac\{V_\{\\rm\{mc\}\}\}\{V_\{\\rm\{aq\}\}\}\\\] where \\\(n_\{\\rm\{mc\}\}\\\) and \\\(n_\{\\rm\{aq\}\}\\\) are the chemical amounts of the analyte in the micellar and aqueous phases\, respectively\, \\\(K\\\) is the distribution constant and \\\(V_\{\\rm\{mc\}\}\\\) and \\\(V_\{\\rm\{aq\}\}\\\) are the corresponding volumes of the phases."
comment: "In the case of an electrically neutral analyte, \(k_{\rm{MEKC}}\) can be calculated directly from the migration times: \[k_{\rm{MEKC}} = \frac{t_{\rm{m}} - t_{\rm{eo}}}{t_{\rm{eo}}(1 - t_{\rm{m}}/t_{\rm{mc}})}\]"
comment: "\(k_{\rm{MEKC}}\) should not be confused with the retention factor (in column chromatography) \(k\). However, \(k_{\rm{MEKC}}\) is analogous to the mass distribution ratio (in chromatography)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200476020443
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
