[Term]
id: goldbook:N04145
name: nitrenes
def: "The neutral compound $\\ce\{HN\{\:\}\}$ having univalent nitrogen\, and its derivatives $\\ce\{RN\}$. Aminylenes is a recognized but less widely used synonym. Other names that have been used include aminediyls\, imidogens\, azenes. They may exist in either a singlet or a triplet electronic state \(four spin-paired electrons\, or two spin-paired and two with parallel spins\, respectively\)\, e.g. $\\ce\{CH3N\{\:\}\}$ methylnitrene.Until the 1960s\, nitrenes had a totally different meaning\: analogues of nitrones in which the double-bonded oxygen is replaced by double-bonded carbon\, thus azomethine ylides."
