id: goldbook:N04205
name: non-uniform corrosion
def: "Corrosion is non-uniform if the time average of the corrosion current through a unit area depends on its position on the surface. Non-uniform corrosion can be due to inhomogeneities of structure or of composition of the corroding material\, or to inhomogeneities of the environment. Special cases of non-uniform corrosion such as pitting or intergranular corrosion are sometimes called localized corrosion."
