[Term]
id: goldbook:NT07428
name: nucleophilic aromatic photosubstitution
def: "Photosubstitution in aromatic compounds with the participation of nucleophiles."
comment: "While electrophilic substitution is the most common reaction on aromatic compounds in the ground state, nucleophilic substitution is typical for the excited states of these compounds. Some electrophilic aromatic photosubstitutions (upon excitation of the aromatic substrate) have been reported."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
