[Term]
id: goldbook:O04315
name: optical yield
def: "In a chemical reaction involving chiral reactants and products\, the ratio of the optical purity of the product to that of the precursor\, reactant or catalyst. This should not be confused with enantiomeric excess. The optical yield is in no way related to the chemical yield of the reaction."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
