[Term]
id: goldbook:O04367
name: oxidative addition
def: "The insertion of a metal complex into a covalent bond involving formally an overall two-electron loss on one metal or a one-electron loss on each of two metals\, i.e. \\\[\\rm\{L\}_\{n\}\\rm\{M\}^\{m\}+\\rm\{XY\}\\rightarrow \\rm\{L\}_\{n\}\\rm\{M\}^\{m+2\}\\left\(\\rm\{X\}\\right\)\\left\(\\rm\{Y\}\\right\)\\\] or \\\[2\\rm\{L\}_\{n\}\\rm\{M\}^\{m\}+\\rm\{XY\}\\rightarrow \\rm\{L\}_\{n\}\\rm\{M\}^\{m+1\}\\left\(\\rm\{X\}\\right\)+\\rm\{L\}_\{n\}\\rm\{M\}^\{m+1\}\\left\(\\rm\{Y\}\\right\)\\\] In radical chemistry\, the term is used to indicate a radical addition to a carbon–carbon double bond\, under oxidative conditions. For example\:"
