property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C00985
consider: goldbook:I03255
consider: goldbook:T06284

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04430
name: particle size
def: "To describe the size of liquid or solid particles \(aerosol\) the average or equivalent diameter is used. For non-spherical particles collected in an impactor\, for example\, the aerodynamic diameter of a particle of arbitrary shape and density refers to the size of a spherical particle of unit density that would deposit on a given impactor surface."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00176
consider: goldbook:E02191

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04431
name: particle size distribution
def: "The size of the liquid or solid particles in the atmosphere usually extends from \\\(>0.01\\\) to \\\(< 100\\ \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{m\}\\\) in diameter. In the earth's atmosphere the distribution function which describes the number of particles as a function of diameter\, mass or surface area of the aerosol can be determined reasonably well with modern instrumentation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00176

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04432
name: particular property
def: "A property of a given object \(phenomenon\, body or substance\). 'Particular property' includes the concept of particular quantity. The adjective 'particular' may be omitted\, if no ambiguity is caused."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567081563
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:P04883

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04433
name: particulate carbon
def: "A carbon material consisting of separated monolithic particles."
comment: "Distinctions should be made between coarse particulate carbon or granular carbon (larger than about \(100\ \unicode[Times]{x3BC}\rm{m}\), but smaller than about \(1\ \rm{cm}\) in average size), fine particulate carbon or powder or flour (between \(1\) and \(100\ \unicode[Times]{x3BC}\rm{m}\) in average size) and colloidal carbon (below approximately \(1\ \unicode[Times]{x3BC}\rm{m}\) in size in at least one direction), e.g. carbon blacks and colloidal carbon."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567030473
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
