[Term]
id: goldbook:P04443
name: passivation
def: "The process of transition from the active to the passive state by formation of the passivating film. Passivation is achieved by an anodic current which at the respective electrode potential must be larger than the maximum current\, or by the presence of an oxidized substance in the neighbouring solution which passivates by being reduced \(passivator\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198961010019
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00111
consider: goldbook:E01956
consider: goldbook:F02366
consider: goldbook:P04447

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04444
name: passivation potential
def: "The most negative electrode potential at which the passivating film is formed. The passivation potential is equal to or more positive than the equilibrium potential of formation of the phase constituting the film. Usually\, the corrosion current goes through a maximum at the passivation potential."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198961010019
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01351
consider: goldbook:C01358
