[Term]
id: goldbook:P04447
name: passive state
def: "The passive state is characterized by a contiguous 'passivating film' of solid corrosion products separating the metallic phase from the adjacent electrolyte. Corrosion in the passive state involves growth of the passivating film and/or transfer of metal ions through the film into the electrolyte."
