id: goldbook:P04468
name: Peierls transition
def: "A metal-insulator transition in quasi one-dimensional solids that occurs as a result of a band gap opening up at the Fermi energy due to a displacive distortion of the regular array increasing the unit cell length\, usually a dimerization; the decrease in electronic energy outweighs the increase in lattice energy. Example\: The transition in methylethylmorpholinium tetracyanoquinodimethanide at \\\(335\\ \\rm\{K\}\\\)."
