[Term]
id: goldbook:P04480
name: peptidoglycan
def: "A glycosaminoglycan formed by alternating residues of ᴅ-glucosamine and either muramic acid \{2-amino-3-O-\[\(S\)-1-carboxyethyl\]-2-deoxy-ᴅ-glucose\} or ʟ-talosaminuronic acid \(2-amino-2-deoxy-ʟ-taluronic acid\)\, which are usually N-acetylated or N-glycoloylated. The carboxyl group of the muramic acid is commonly substituted by a peptide containing residues of both ʟ- and ᴅ-amino acids\, whereas that of ʟ-talosaminuronic acid is substituted by a peptide consisting of ʟ-amino acids only."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198860091389
