[Term]
id: goldbook:P04501
name: peritectoid reaction
def: "An isothermal\, reversible reaction in the solid state\, that\, on cooling of a binary\, ternary\, ... \, \\\(n\\\) system\, results in one\, two\, ... \(\\\(n-1\\\)\) new solid phases. For example\, in a binary system containing two solids \\\(\\alpha'\\\) and \\\(\\alpha''\\\) \\\[\\alpha' + \\alpha'' \\rightarrow \\beta\\\] Synonymous with metatectoid reaction."
