[Term]
id: goldbook:P04605
name: photoelectrochemical cell
def: "An electrochemical cell in which current and a voltage are simultaneously produced upon absorption of light by one or more of the electrodes. Usually at least one of the electrodes is a semiconductor."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163040569
