[Term]
id: goldbook:P04627
name: photon
def: "Particle of zero charge\, zero rest mass\, spin quantum number 1\, energy \\\(h\\  u \\\) and momentum \\\(\\frac\{h\\  u \}\{c\}\\\)\(\\\(h\\\) is the Planck constant\, \\\( u \\\) the frequency of radiation and \\\(c\\\) the speed of light\)\, carrier of electromagnetic force."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C00859
consider: goldbook:M04007
consider: goldbook:P04685

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04629
name: photon counting
def: "Recording of sequential single photons counted by way of recording and counting sequential electron pulses at the anode of the photomultiplier."
comment: "Each electron pulse consists of 105–106 electrons resulting from the multiplication, in the 'dynode' arrangement (or the microchannel plate) of a photomultiplier, of a single photoelectron emitted by a photosensitive layer (the photocathode of the photomultiplier) upon arrival of a single photon."
comment: "Technique used for two purposes: (i) sensitive measurement of low levels of radiation such as those originating from a luminophore and (ii) recording of emission decays."
synonym: "single-photon counting" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00370

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04631
name: photon exitance
def: "Photon flux\, number basis\, \\\(q_\{\\rm\{p\}\}\\\)\, emitted by an element of the surface containing the source point under consideration divided by the area \\\(S\\\) of that element. SI unit is \\\(\\rm\{s\}^\{-1\}\\ \\rm\{m\}^\{-2\}\\\)."
comment: "Formerly called photon emittance."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \(\rm{d}q_{p}/\rm{d}S\). If \(q_{\rm{p}}\) is constant over the surface area considered, \(M_{\rm{p}} = q_{\rm{p}}/S\)."
comment: "This quantity can be expressed on a chemical amount basis by dividing \(M_{\rm{p}}\) by the Avogadro constant. In this case the symbol is \(M_{n\rm{,p}}\), the name 'photon exitance, amount basis', SI unit is \(\pu{mol s-1 m-2}\); common unit is \(\pu{einstein s-1 m-2}\)."
synonym: "photon emittance" []
synonym: "specific photon emission" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00543
consider: goldbook:C01019
consider: goldbook:E02264

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04632
name: photon exposure
def: "Photon irradiance\, \\\(E_\{\\rm\{p\}\}\\\)\, integrated over the time of irradiation for a beam incident from all upward directions. SI unit is \\\(\\rm\{m\}^\{-2\}\\\)."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \(H_{\rm{p}} = \int_{t}E_{\rm{p}}\rm{d}t\). If the photon irradiance is constant over the time interval, \(H_{\rm{p}} = E_{\rm{p}}t\)."
comment: "This quantity can be used on a chemical amount basis by dividing \(H_{\rm{p}}\) by the Avogadro constant, the symbol then being \(H_{n\rm{,p}}\), the name 'photon exposure, amount basis', SI unit is \(\pu{mol m-2}\); common unit is \(\pu{einstein m-2}\)."
comment: "This term refers to a beam not scattered or reflected by the target or its surroundings. For a beam incident from all directions photon fluence (\(H_{\rm{p,o}}\), \(F_{\rm{p,o}}\)) is an equivalent term."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00543
consider: goldbook:C01019
consider: goldbook:I03255
consider: goldbook:P04637

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04633
name: photon flow
def: "The number of photons \(quanta\, \\\(N\\\)\) per unit time. \(\\\(\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}N\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\)\, simplified expression\: \\\(\\mathit\{\\Phi\} _\{\\rm\{p\}\} = \\frac\{N\}\{t\}\\\) when the number of photons is constant over the time considered\). The SI unit is \\\(\\rm\{s\}^\{-1\}\\\). Alternatively\, the term can be used with the amount of photons \(mol or its equivalent einstein\)\, the SI unit then being \\\(\\pu\{mol s-1\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:E01914
consider: goldbook:R05046
consider: goldbook:S05820

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04634
name: photon fluence
def: "Amount of photons \(quanta of radiation\) incident on a small sphere from all directions\, divided by the cross-sectional area of that sphere and integrated over time. Photons per surface area \(\\\(\\rm\{quanta m\}^\{-2\}\\\)\). SI unit is \\\(\\rm\{m\}^\{-2\}\\\)."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \(H_{\rm{p,o}} = F_{\rm{p,o}} = \rm{d}N_{\rm{p}}/\rm{d}S = \int_{t}E_{\rm{p,o}}\rm{d}t\) with \(E_{\rm{p,o}}\) the photon fluence rate, integrated over the duration of the irradiation, \(t\). If \(E_{\rm{p,o}}\) is constant over the time interval, \(H_{\rm{p,o}} = F_{\rm{p,o}} = E_{\rm{p,o}}\,t\)."
comment: "This quantity can be used on a chemical amount basis by dividing \(H_{\rm{p,o}}\) by the Avogadro constant, the symbol then being \(H_{n\rm{,p,o}}\), the name 'photon fluence, amount basis', SI unit is \(\pu{mol m-2}\); common unit is \(\pu{einstein m-2}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00543
consider: goldbook:C01019
consider: goldbook:I03255
consider: goldbook:P04635

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04635
name: photon fluence rate
def: "Rate of photon fluence. Total number of photons \(\\\(N_\{\\rm\{p\}\}\\\)\) incident from all directions on a small sphere divided by the cross-sectional area of the sphere and per time interval. SI unit is \\\(\\rm\{m\}^\{-2\}\\ \\rm\{s\}^\{-1\}\\\). Same as photon fluence rate."
comment: "It reduces to photon irradiance \(E_{\rm{p}}\) for a parallel and normally incident beam not scattered or reflected by the target or its surroundings."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \(E_{\rm{p,o}} = \rm{d}N_{\rm{p}}/\left ( \rm{d}t\, \rm{d}S \right ) = \rm{d}H_{\rm{p,o}}/\rm{d}t\). If \(E_{\rm{p,o}}\) is constant over the time interval and the surface, \(E_{\rm{p,o}} = N_{\rm{p}}/t\, S\). Equivalent definition: \(E_{\rm{p,o}} = \int _{4\pi}L_{\rm{p}}\rm{d}\varOmega\) with \(L_{\rm{p}}\) the photon radiance and \(\varOmega\) the solid angle of the beams passing through the given point on the surface."
comment: "This quantity can be used on a chemical amount basis by dividing \(E_{\rm{p,o}}\) by the Avogadro constant, the symbol then being \(E_{n\rm{,p,o}}\), the name 'photon spherical irradiance, amount basis', SI unit is \(\pu{mol m-2 s-1}\); common unit is \(\pu{einstein m-2 s-1}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00346
consider: goldbook:A00543
consider: goldbook:C01019
consider: goldbook:FT07376
consider: goldbook:P04637
consider: goldbook:P04639

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04636
name: photon flux
def: "Number of photons \(quanta of radiation\, \\\(N_\{\\rm\{p\}\}\\\)\) per time interval. SI unit is \\\(\\rm\{s\}^\{-1\}\\\)."
comment: "Although the symbol recommended by CEI is \(\mathit{\Phi} _{\rm{p}}\), the symbol \(q_{\rm{p}}\) is preferred since \(\mathit{\Phi}\) is reserved for quantum yield."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \(q_{\rm{p}} = \rm{d}N_{\rm{p}}/\rm{d}t\). If the number of photons is constant over the time interval, \(q_{\rm{p}} = N_{\rm{p}}/t\)."
comment: "This quantity can be used on a chemical amount basis by dividing the photon flux, number basis, \(q_{\rm{p}}\), by the Avogadro constant, the symbol then being \(q_{n\rm{,p}}\), the name 'photon flux, amount basis', SI unit is \(\pu{mol s-1}\); common unit is \(\rm{einstein s}^{-1}\)."
synonym: "CEI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
