consider: goldbook:P04641
consider: goldbook:P04650

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04641
name: photooxygenation
def: "The incorporation of molecular oxygen into a molecular entity. There are three common mechanisms\: Type I\: the reaction of triplet molecular oxygen with radicals formed photochemically. Type II\: the reaction of photochemically produced singlet molecular oxygen with molecular entities to give rise to oxygen containing molecular entities. The third mechanism proceeds by electron transfer producing superoxide anion as the reactive species."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00358
consider: goldbook:E02011
consider: goldbook:P04640

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04645
name: photophoresis
def: "In aerosol physics\, the motion of particles due to the influence of light. In many cases\, this amounts to a special form of thermophoresis due to the heating of the particles by the light."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00176

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04646
name: photophosphorylation
def: "The transformation of light \(solar\) energy for the reduction of $\\ce\{CO2\}$ and the generation of adenosine 5'-triphosphate\, ATP."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:T06446

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04647
name: photophysical processes
def: "Photoexcitation and subsequent events which lead from one to another state of a molecular entity through radiation and radiationless transitions. No chemical change results."
