[Term]
id: goldbook:P04650
name: photoreduction
def: "Reduction reactions induced by light. Common processes are\: 1\, addition of one or more electrons to a photoexcited species; 2\, the photochemical hydrogenation of a substance. Reactions in which the substrate is not electronically excited are sometimes called photoinitiated reductions."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
