[Term]
id: goldbook:P04651
name: photoresist
def: "A photoimaging material\, generally applied as a thin film\, whose local solubility properties can be altered photochemically. A subsequent development step produces an image which is useful for the fabrication of microelectronic devices \(e.g. integrated circuits\)."
