[Term]
id: goldbook:P04652
name: photosensitization
def: "The process by which a photochemical or photophysical alteration occurs in one molecular entity as a result of initial absorption of radiation by another molecular entity called a 'photosensitizer'. In mechanistic photochemistry the term is limited to cases in which the photosensitizer is not consumed in the reaction."
synonym: "sensitization" []
