[Term]
id: goldbook:P04657
name: photothermography
def: "A process utilizing both light and heat\, simultaneously or sequentially\, for image recording."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04658
name: phototransistor
def: "A bipolar transistor with its base-collector junction acting as a photodiode\, which\, if irradiated\, controls the response of the device. Due to the inherent current gain \(of the transistor\) the responsivity of the phototransistor is greater than that of photodiodes. A Darlington phototransistor consists of two separate transistors coupled in the high-impedance Darlington configuration with a phototransistor as the input transistor. A field effect phototransistor or photo-FET is a field effect transistor \(FET\) that employs photogeneration of carriers in the channel region \(the neutral region sandwiched between the insulator and the depletion region under the gate of the FET\). It is characterized by high responsivity due to the high current gain of the FET."
synonym: "FET" RELATED OMO:0003012 []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567101745
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
