[Term]
id: goldbook:P04682
name: planar chromatography
def: "A separation technique in which the stationary phase is present as or on a plane. The plane can be a paper\, serving as such or impregnated by a substrate as the stationary bed \(paper chromatography\, PC\) or a layer of solid particles spread on a support e.g. a glass plate \(thin layer chromatography\, TLC\). Sometimes planar chromatography is also termed open-bed chromatography."
