id: goldbook:P04683
name: planar film
def: "A film whose boundaries are represented by ideal parallel planes. The planar film thickness is defined as the distance between these planes. The terms nanometre thick film\, micrometre thick film and millimetre thick film refer specifically to film thickness in the ranges \\\(0.1\{-\}100\\ \\rm\{nm\}\\\)\, \\\(0.1\{-\}100\\ \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{m\}\\\) and \\\(0.1\{-\}100\\ \\rm\{mm\}\\\)\, respectively."
