[Term]
id: goldbook:P04720
name: polyaddition
def: "A polymerization in which the growth of polymer chains proceeds by addition reactions between molecules of all degrees of polymerization."
comment: "The earlier term 'addition polymerization' embraced both the current concepts of 'polyaddition' and 'chain polymerization', but did not include 'condensative chain polymerization'."
comment: "The growth steps are expressed by: \[\rm{P}_{x} + \rm{P}_{y}\rightarrow \rm{P}_{x + y}\hspace{35pt} \{x\}\in \{1,2, \dots \infty\}; \{y\}\in \{1,2, \dots \infty \}\] where \(\rm{P}_{x}\) and \(\rm{P}_{y}\) denote chains of degrees of polymerization \(x\) and \(y\), respectively."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122287
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C00946
consider: goldbook:C00958
consider: goldbook:D01569
consider: goldbook:P04740

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04722
name: polycondensation
def: "A polymerization in which the growth of polymer chains proceeds by condensation reactions between molecules of all degrees of polymerization."
comment: "The earlier term 'polycondensation' was synonymous with 'condensation polymerization'. It should be noted that the current definitions of polycondensation and condensative chain polymerization were both embraced by the earlier term 'polycondensation'."
comment: "The growth steps are expressed by: \[\rm{P}_{x} + \rm{P}_{y}\rightarrow \rm{P}_{x + y} + L\hspace{35pt} \{x\}\in \{1,2, \dots \infty\}; \{y\}\in \{1,2, \dots \infty \}\] where \(\rm{P}_{x}\) and \(\rm{P}_{y}\) denote chains of degree of polymerization \(x\) and \(y\), respectively, and \(\rm{L}\) a low-molar-mass by-product."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122287
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
