id: goldbook:P04736
name: polymer blend
def: "Macroscopically homogeneous mixture of two or more different species of polymer."
comment: "In most cases, blends are homogeneous on scales larger than several times the wavelengths of visible light."
comment: "In principle, the constituents of a blend are separable by physical means."
comment: "No account is taken of the miscibility or immiscibility of the constituent macromolecules, i.e., no assumption is made regarding the number of phase domains present."
comment: "The number of polymeric components which comprise a blend is often designated by an adjective, viz. binary, ternary, quaternary, etc."
comment: "The use of the term polymer alloy for a polymer blend is discouraged, as the former term includes multiphase copolymers but excludes incompatible polymer blends."
