[Term]
id: goldbook:P04771
name: post-column derivatization
def: "A version of reaction chromatography in which the separated components eluting from the column are derivatized prior to entering the detector. The derivatization process is generally carried out 'on-the-fly'\, i.e. during transfer of the sample components from the column to the detector. Derivatization may also be carried out before the sample enters the column or the planar medium; this is pre-column \(preliminary\) derivatization."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05167

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04772
name: post-filter effect
def: "This effect arises when the exciting beam does not fill the cell completely and luminescence is absorbed by the analyte and interfering impurities in the non-illuminated region facing the detector."
