[Term]
id: goldbook:P04804
name: preconcentration coefficient
def: "This is defined as \\\[K = \\frac\{Q_\{\\rm\{T\}\}/Q_\{\\rm\{M\}\}\}\{Q_\{\\rm\{T\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\}/Q_\{\\rm\{M\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\}\}\\\] where \\\(Q_\{\\rm\{T\}\}\\\) and \\\(Q_\{\\rm\{T\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\}\\\) are the quantities of the microcomponent in the concentrate and in the sample\, respectively \(mass units or concentration units\)\, and \\\(Q_\{\\rm\{M\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\}\\\) and \\\(Q_\{\\rm\{M\}\}\\\) and are the quantities of the matrix before and after preconcentration\, respectively. If the recovery is 100%\, \\\(K=\\frac\{Q_\{\\rm\{M\}\}^\{\\rm\{o\}\}\}\{Q_\{\\rm\{M\}\}\}\\\). The terms enrichment coefficient and enrichment factor are not recommended."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197951051195
