id: goldbook:P04822
name: pressure-induced transition
def: "A transition induced by a change of pressure. Example\: The room-temperature transition of $\\ce\{CdS\}$ with a wurtzite-type structure\, at \\\(1.74\\ \\rm\{GPa\}\\\)\, to $\\ce\{CdS\}$ with a $\\ce\{NaCl\}$-type structure."
