[Term]
id: goldbook:P04831
name: primary isotope effect
def: "A kinetic isotope effect attributable to isotopic substitution of an atom to which a bond is made or broken in the rate-controlling step or in a pre-equilibrium step of a specified reaction. The corresponding isotope effect on the equilibrium constant of a reaction in which one or more bonds to isotopic atoms are broken\, is called a 'primary equilibrium isotope effect'."
