id: goldbook:P04838
name: primary pollutant
def: "A pollutant emitted directly into the air from identifiable sources \(e.g. $\\ce\{SO2\}$\, $\\ce\{NO\}$\, hydrocarbons\, etc.\). Secondary pollutants\, such as ozone\, are generated within the atmosphere through chemical changes which occur in primary pollutants."
