[Term]
id: goldbook:P04846
name: principal group
def: "The characteristic group chosen for citation at the end of a name by a suffix or a class name."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971071327
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04847
name: principal ion
def: "A molecular or fragment ion which is made up of the most abundant isotopes of each of its atomic constituents. In the case of compounds that have been artifically isotopically enriched in one or more positions such as $\\ce\{CH3^\{13\}CH3\}$ or $\\ce\{CH2D2\}$ the principal ion may be defined by treating the heavy isotopes as new atomic species. Thus\, in the above two examples\, the principal ions would be of masses 31 and 18\, respectively."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163101541
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03331

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04849
name: principle of least nuclear motion
def: "The hypothesis that\, for given reactants\, the reactions involving the smallest change in nuclear positions will have the lowest energy of activation. \(It is also often simply referred to as principle of least motion.\)"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00102

[Term]
id: goldbook:P04850
name: principle of microscopic reversibility
def: "In a reversible reaction\, the mechanism in one direction is exactly the reverse of the mechanism in the other direction. This does not apply to reactions that begin with a photochemical excitation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
