id: goldbook:P04908
name: protonated molecule
def: "An ion formed by interaction of a molecule with a proton abstracted from an ion\, as often occurs in chemical ionization according to the reaction\: \\\(\\rm\{M\}+\\rm\{XH\}^\{+\}\\rightarrow \\rm\{MH\}^\{+\}+\\rm\{X\}\\\). The symbolism $\\ce\{\[M + H\]^\{+\}\}$ may also be used to represent the protonated molecule. The widely used term 'protonated molecular ion' to describe the $\\ce\{MH^\{+\}\}$ ion is not recommended\, since it suggests an associated product of a proton with a molecular ion."
