comment: "'Pyrographite', a synonym for pyrolytic graphite, was introduced as a trademark and should not be used as a term. Hot working of pyrolytic graphite (by heat treatment under compressive stress at temperatures above \(3000\ \rm{K}\)) results in highly oriented pyrolytic graphite (HOPG)."
