consider: goldbook:T06446

[Term]
id: goldbook:PT07158
name: polymer catalyst
def: "Polymer that exhibits catalytic activity."
comment: "Certain synthetic polymer catalysts can behave like enzymes."
comment: "Poly(4-vinylpyridine) in its basic form, and sulfonated polystyrene in its acid form, are examples of polymers that can act as catalysts in some base- and acid-catalyzed reactions, respectively."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200476040889
