name: polymer support
def: "Polymer to or in which a reagent or catalyst is chemically bound\, immobilized\, dispersed\, or associated."
comment: "A polymer support is usually a network polymer."
comment: "A polymer support is usually prepared in bead form by suspension polymerization."
comment: "The location of active sites introduced into a polymer support depends on the type of polymer support. In a swollen-gel-bead polymer support the active sites are distributed uniformly throughout the beads, whereas in a macroporous-bead polymer support they are predominantly on the internal surfaces of the macropores."
