[Term]
id: goldbook:PT07460
name: photorearrangement
def: "Photoisomerization involving changes in the arrangement of the atoms within the molecular species. It may lead to unstable isomers that react further by\, e.g.\, dehydrogenation\, deprotonation\, or other reactions."
comment: "Examples are photorearrangements of alkenes (other than cis-trans photoisomerization), of cyclohex-2-enones, of endoperoxides, of thioarenes, the di-π-methane rearrangement and others."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
