[Term]
id: goldbook:Q04971
name: quadrupole mass analyser
def: "An arrangement in which ions with a desired quotient mass/charge are made to describe a stable path under the effect of a static and a high-frequency electric quadrupole field\, and are then detected. Ions with a different mass/charge are separated from the detected ions because of their unstable paths."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199163101541
