[Term]
id: goldbook:Q04982
name: quantity
def: "Attribute of a phenomenon\, body or substance that may be distinguished qualitatively and determined quantitatively."
comment: "The term kind-of-quantity refers to the abstract concept of a quantity common to a group of related quantities."
comment: "The term quantity may refer to a quantity in a general sense, for example length, mass, or to a particular quantity, for example length of a particular rod, mass of a specified object."
