id: goldbook:Q04997
name: quasi-enantiomers
def: "Constitutionally different yet closely related chemical species MX and MY having the opposite chirality sense of the large common chiral moiety M. For example \(R\)-2-bromobutane is a quasi-enantiomer of \(S\)-2-chlorobutane."
