[Term]
id: goldbook:R05037
name: radiance
def: "Radiant power\, \\\(P\\\)\, leaving or passing through a small transparent element of surface in a given direction from the source about the solid angle \\\(\\varOmega\\\)\, divided by the solid angle and by the orthogonally projected area of the element in a plane normal to the given beam direction\, \\\(\\rm\{d\}S_\{\\perp \} = \\rm\{d\}S\\\, \\rm\{cos\}\\\,\\theta\\\)"
comment: "Equivalent to \(L = \int_{\lambda}L_{\lambda}\, \rm{d}\lambda\), where \(L_{\lambda}\) is the spectral radiance at wavelength \(\lambda\)."
comment: "For a parallel beam it is the radiant power, \(P\), of all wavelengths leaving or passing through a small element of surface in a given direction from the source divided by the orthogonally projected area of the element in a plane normal to the given direction of the beam, \(\theta\). Mathematical definition in this case: \(\rm{d}P/(\rm{d}S\, \rm{cos}\,\theta)\). If the @R05046-1@ is constant over the surface area considered, \(P/(S\, \rm{cos}\,\theta)\). SI unit is \(\rm{W m}^{-2}\)."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \[L = \frac{\rm{d}^{2}P}{\rm{d}\Omega \, \rm{d}S_{\perp }} = \frac{\rm{d}^{2}P}{\rm{d}\Omega \, \rm{d}S\, \rm{cos}\,\theta}\] for a divergent beam propagating in an elementary cone of the solid angle \(\varOmega\) containing the direction \(\theta\). SI unit is \(\rm{W m}^{-2}\ \rm{sr}^{-1}\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00346
consider: goldbook:R05046
consider: goldbook:S05824
consider: goldbook:W06659

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05039
name: radiant energy
def: "The total energy emitted\, transferred or received as radiation in a defined period of time \(\\\(Q=\\int Q_\{\\lambda \}  \\ \\mathrm\{d\}\\lambda \\\)\). It is the product of radiant power\, \\\(P\\\)\, and time\, \\\(t\\\)\: \\\(Q=P\\ t\\\) when the radiant power is constant over the time considered."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668040957
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05046

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05041
name: radiant exitance
def: "Radiant power\, \\\(P\\\)\, emitted at all wavelengths by an element of surface containing the source point under consideration divided by the area of the source. SI unit is \\\(\\rm\{W m\}^\{-2\}\\\)."
comment: "Equivalent to the integration of the radiant power leaving a source over the solid angle and over the whole wavelength range. Mathematical definition: \(M = \int_{\lambda}M_{\lambda}\, \rm{d}\lambda\), where \(M_{\lambda}\) is the spectral radiant exitance at wavelength \(\lambda\)."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \(M = \rm{d}P/\rm{d}S\). If the radiant power \(P\) is constant over the surface area considered, \(M = P/S\)."
comment: "Same as spherical radiant exitance. Formerly called radiant emittance."
synonym: "exitance" []
synonym: "radiant emittance" []
synonym: "spherical radiant exitance" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00346
consider: goldbook:R05046
consider: goldbook:S05825
consider: goldbook:W06659

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05042
name: radiant exposure
def: "Radiant energy\, \\\(Q\\\)\, incident from all upward directions on a small sphere divided by the cross-sectional area of that sphere. SI unit is \\\(\\pu\{J m-2\}\\\)."
comment: "Equivalent definition: Irradiance, \(E\) integrated over the time of irradiation."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \(H = \rm{d}Q/\rm{d}S = \int _{t} E\, \rm{d}t\). If \(Q\) is constant over the area, \(H = Q/S\). If \(E\) is constant over the time interval, \(H = E\, t\)."
comment: "This term refers to a beam not scattered or reflected by the target or its surroundings. For a beam incident from all directions fluence&nbsp;(\(H_{\rm{o}}\), \(F_{\rm{o}}\)) is an equivalent term."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03255
consider: goldbook:R05039

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05045
name: radiant intensity
def: "Radiant power\, \\\(P\\\)\, at all wavelengths per solid angle\, \\\(\\varOmega\\\). The @R05046-2@ emitted in a given direction by a source or an element of the source in a small cone containing the given direction divided by the solid angle of the cone. SI unit is \\\(\\rm\{W sr\}^\{-1\}\\\)."
comment: "Equivalent to \(I = \int_{\lambda}I_{\lambda}\, \rm{d}\lambda\), where \(I_{\lambda}\) is the spectral radiant intensity at wavelength \(\lambda\)."
comment: "It is not recommended to abbreviate this term to just intensity because it is confusing."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \(I = \rm{d}P/\rm{d}\varOmega\). If the radiant power is constant over the solid angle considered, \(I = P/\varOmega\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00346
consider: goldbook:R05046
consider: goldbook:S05827
consider: goldbook:W06659

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05046
name: radiant power
def: "Power emitted\, transferred or received as radiation. SI unit is \\\(\\pu\{J s-1\} = \\pu\{W\}\\\)."
comment: "In radiometry, flux (\(\varPhi\)) is used with the same units as \(P\). The symbol \(\varPhi\) is reserved for quantum yield in photochemistry. Therefore, the use of flux (\(\varPhi\)) is not recommended."
comment: "Mathematical definition: \(P = \rm{d}Q/\rm{d}t\). If the radiant energy \(Q\) is constant over the time interval, \(P = Q/t\)."
