[Term]
id: goldbook:R05144
name: rate of change of a quantity
def: "The time derivative \\\(\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}Q\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\) of the value of the quantity. The differential quotient may also be called derivative \(or instantaneous\) rate of change. Examples are\: rate of change of mass\, \\\(\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}m\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\); rate of change of amount of substance\, \\\(\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}n\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264101569
