[Term]
id: goldbook:R05147
name: rate of conversion
def: "The rate of conversion for a reaction occurring in a closed system is defined as the time derivative of the extent of reaction\: \\\[\\overset\{\\rm\{.\}\}\{\\xi \}=\\frac\{\\mathrm\{d\}\\xi \}\{\\mathrm\{d\}t\}\\\] In view of the definition of extent of reaction it follows that with reference to any species in a reaction showing time-independent stoichiometry \\\[\\overset\{\\rm\{.\}\}\{\\xi \}=\\frac\{\\mathrm\{d\}\\xi \}\{\\mathrm\{d\}t\}=\\frac\{1\}\{ u _\{i\}\}\\ \\frac\{\\mathrm\{d\}n_\{i\}\}\{\\mathrm\{d\}t\}\\\] where \\\(n_\{i\}\\\) is the amount of the species at any time and \\\( u _\{i\}\\\) is its stoichiometric coefficient."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264101569
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
