[Term]
id: goldbook:R05151
name: rate of fluid consumption
def: "The volume of fluid consumed by the nebulizer divided by time \(in \\\(\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{L\}\\ \\rm\{s\}^\{-1\}\\\)\). Volume rate has also been called volume flow\, flux\, aspiration rate\, aspiration flow or aspiration flux. The fluid consumed is either aspirated or injected. The volume rate of fluid consumption by nebulizers is usually between \\\(10\\\) and \\\(100\\ \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3BC\}\\rm\{L\}\\ \\rm\{s\}^\{-1\}\\\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198658121737
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:CT01101

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05152
name: rate of formation
def: "Like the rate of consumption\, the rate of formation of a specified product may be defined in two ways\:As the time derivative of the amount of a product. Thus for a product $\\ce\{Y\}$\, present at any time in amount \\\(n_\{\\rm\{Y\}\}\\\). the rate of its formation may be given by\: \\\[ u \(n_\{\\rm\{Y\}\}\) = \\frac\{\\rm\{d\}n_\{\\rm\{Y\}\}\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\] This definition is particularly appropriate for open systems.For kinetics in closed systems it is more usual to define a rate of formation per unit volume\, denoted \\\( u \(c_\{\\rm\{Y\}\}\) \\\)\: \\\[ u \(c_\{\\rm\{Y\}\}\) = \\frac\{1\}\{V\}\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}n_\{\\rm\{Y\}\}\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\] When the volume is constant this reduces to\: \\\[ u \(c_\{\\rm\{Y\}\}\) = \\frac\{1\}\{V\}\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}n_\{\\rm\{Y\}\}\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\} = \\frac\{\\rm\{d\[Y\]\}\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\] When the volume is not constant the relationship \\\(n_\{\\rm\{Y\}\} = \[\\rm\{Y\}\]V\\\) may be differentiated to give\: \\\[\{\\rm\{d\}\}n_\{\\rm\{Y\}\} = V\\rm\{d\[Y\]\} + \\rm\{\[Y\]d\}V\\\] and the rate of formation becomes\: \\\[ u \(c_\{\\rm\{Y\}\}\) = \\frac\{\\rm\{d\[Y\]\}\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\} + \\frac\{\\rm\{\[Y\]\}\}\{V\}\\frac\{\\rm\{d\}V\}\{\\rm\{d\}t\}\\\] A rate of formation may be specified even for a reaction of time dependent stoichiometry or of unknown stoichiometry."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05146
consider: goldbook:S06026

