[Term]
id: goldbook:R05169
name: reaction cross-section
def: "A quantity used in collision theories of reactions in order to interpret calculated or experimental rates. In some collision theories the reaction cross-section is considered to be related to \\\(b_\{\\max \}\\\)\, the maximum value of the impact parameter that allows reaction to occur\, by\: \\\[\\sigma _\{\\rm\{r\}\}=P_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\\ \\pi \\ b_\{\\max \}^\{2\}\\\] where \\\(P_\{\\rm\{r\}\}\\\) is the reaction probability."
