[Term]
id: goldbook:R05208
name: recrystallization
def: "\(chemical\)\: The repeated dissolution and precipitation of a solid from a liquid solvent.\(metallurgical\)\: The process in which a crystalline solid with a high degree of disorder develops a new microstructure by the nucleation of relatively imperfection-free regions\, and their propagation throughout the complete solid."
