[Term]
id: goldbook:R05274
name: relative preconcentration
def: "An operation \(process\) as a result of which the ratio of concentration or amounts of microcomponents and main macrocomponents increases. This is a particular example of a separation\, but at greatly differing concentrations of components. The ratio of the masses of the initial and final samples is not of great importance. Frequently\, the main purpose of relative preconcentration is the replacement of a matrix unsuitable for analysis by a suitable medium. In some cases\, it is difficult to trace a boundary between the absolute and the relative preconcentrations as\, for example\, in preconcentration by zone melting."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197951051195
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:M03821
consider: goldbook:P04803

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05276
name: relative retardation
def: "A term which is equivalent to relative retention used in column chromatography\: the ratio of the \\\(R_\{\\rm\{F\}\}\\\) value of a component to the \\\(R_\{\\rm\{F\}\}\\\) value of a standard \(reference\) substance. Since the mobile phase front is common for the two components\, the \\\(R_\{\\rm\{F\}\}\\\) value can be expressed directly as the ratio of the distances travelled by the spot of the compound of interest \(\\\(b_\{i\}\\\)\) and the reference substance \(\\\(b_\{\\rm\{st\}\}\\\)\) respectively\: \\\[R_\{\\rm\{rel\}\}=\\frac\{R_\{\\rm\{F\}\\left\(i\\right\)\}\}\{R_\{\\rm\{F\}\\left\(\\rm\{st\}\\right\)\}\}=\\frac\{b_\{i\}\}\{b_\{\\rm\{st\}\}\}\\\] In former nomenclatures the symbol \\\(R_\{\\rm\{s\}\}\\\) was used to express relative retardation in planar chromatography. Because of its identity with the symbol for peak resolution the symbol \\\(R_\{\\rm\{rel\}\}\\\) is suggested for relative retardation in planar chromatography."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01182
consider: goldbook:P04682

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05277
name: relative retention
def: "The ratio of the adjusted or net retention volume \(time\) or retention factor of a component relative to that of a standard\, obtained under identical conditions\: \\\[r=\\frac\{V_\{\\rm\{R\}i\}^\{'\}\}\{V_\{\\rm\{R\}\\left\(\\rm\{st\}\\right\)\}^\{'\}\}=\\frac\{V_\{\\rm\{N\}i\}\}\{V_\{\\rm\{N\}\\left\(\\rm\{st\}\\right\)\}\}=\\frac\{t_\{\\rm\{R\}i\}^\{'\}\}\{t_\{\\rm\{R\}\\left\(\\rm\{st\}\\right\)\}^\{'\}\}=\\frac\{k_\{i\}\}\{k_\{\\rm\{st\}\}\}\\\] Depending on the relative position of the peak corresponding to the standard compound in the chromatogram\, the value of \\\(r\\\) may be smaller\, larger or identical to unity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365040819
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01071

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05280
name: relative standard deviation
def: "The standard deviation divided by the mean of the series. It can be calculated with the formula\: \\\[s_\{\\rm\{r\}\}=\\frac\{s\}\{\\overline\{x\}\}\\\]"
