[Term]
id: goldbook:R05309
name: residence time
def: "\(instrumentation\)\: The time required for air or reagent parcel to pass from the entrance to the exit of an instrument. Often this is approximated as the ratio of the interior volume of the device to the flow rate.\(atmospheric\)\: The average time a molecule or aerosol spends in the atmosphere after it is released or generated there. For compounds with well defined sources and emission rates\, this is estimated by the ratio of the average global concentration of a substance to its production rate on a global scale. It is a function of not only the emission rates but the loss rates by chemical and physical removal processes."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00176
consider: goldbook:R05190

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05310
name: residence time
def: "The average time a particle or volume element of the culture resides in a bioreactor \(or other device\) through which a liquid medium continously flows. residence time of the liquid is the reciprocal of dilution rate."
synonym: "hydraulic retention time" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:B00662
consider: goldbook:D01740
