[Term]
id: goldbook:R05311
name: residual current
def: "The current that flows\, at any particular value of the applied potential\, in the absence of the substance whose behaviour is being investigated \(i.e. in a blank solution\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198557101491
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00424

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05312
name: residual fuel/oil
def: "The liquid or semi-liquid\, high-boiling fraction of residue from the distillation of petroleum which is used as a fuel. After removal of the lower boiling fraction of crude oil\, sold as petroleum gas\, the somewhat higher boiling fraction becomes gasoline and diesel oil. A portion of the higher boiling fraction is 'cracked' to yield additional gasoline. Still heavier oils become lubricants. paraffin\, asphalt\, etc.\, are also extracted from the crude oil. It is the remaining residual oil\, not economically usable for other industrial purposes\, which is then sold as a relatively low cost fuel for burning."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:P04401

[Term]
id: goldbook:R05313
name: residual liquid junction error
def: "Error arising from breakdown in the assumption that the liquid junction potential remains constant when solution X is substituted for solution S in the operational cell."
synonym: "residual liquid junction potential error" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198557030531
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
