id: goldbook:RT07092
name: relative hardness
def: "The difference between the values of the absolute hardnesses \(\\\(\\eta \\\)\) of a given molecule and the corresponding reference structure \(\\\(\\eta _\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\)\)\: \\\(\\eta _\{\\rm\{r\}\} = \\eta - \\eta _\{\\rm\{a\}\}\\\). The values of relative hardnesses correlate well with the resonance energies of cyclic compounds and may be used as an index of aromaticity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00442
consider: goldbook:R05326

[Term]
id: goldbook:RT07093
name: relativistic effects
def: "Corrections to exact non-relativistic energy from the fact that inner shell electrons in heavy atoms move with velocities comparable in order of magnitude to the velocity of light. The most important relativistic effect is spin–orbit coupling."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:S05870

[Term]
id: goldbook:RT07094
name: resonance hybrid
def: "A localized valence bond representation of a molecule. This describes pictorially an electronic wavefunction that makes some contribution to the state wavefunction of the system. resonance hybrids are needed to describe the state of a system when that system is not adequately described by a single Lewis structure."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:R05326
consider: goldbook:V06588

[Term]
id: goldbook:RT07095
name: ribbon delocalisation
def: "Electron delocalization realized in both acyclic and cyclic $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}conjugated\}$\, 1\, and $\\ce\{\\upsigma\\!\\mbox\{-\}bonded\}$\, 2\, ribbon-like systems.  For cyclic systems\, a variety of linkage fashions between several ribbons \(pericyclic\, spirocyclic\, longicyclic and laticyclic\) is possible."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:D01583

[Term]
id: goldbook:RT07096
name: Rydberg state
def: "An electronic state that arises by the excitation of a valence electron to a diffuse atomic-like orbital. For instance\, the lowest lying Rydberg state \(n\, 3S\) of $\\ce\{NH3\}$ can be described as resulting from the excitation of a non-bonding orbital to a 3S Rydberg orbital."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199971101919
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:ET07026
consider: goldbook:R05431
consider: goldbook:V06588

[Term]
id: goldbook:RT07149
name: radiation reaction
def: "Chemical reaction that is induced by ionizing radiation with $\\upgamma\\!\\mbox\{-\}\\rm\{ray\}$\, X-ray\, electron\, or other high-energy beams."
comment: "A photochemical reaction is sometimes regarded as a type of radiation reaction."
comment: "Radiation reactions involving polymers often lead to chain scission and crosslinking."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200476040889
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
