[Term]
id: goldbook:RT07475
name: rotational relaxation time
def: "Parameter describing the time-dependence of the tumbling of a molecular entity in a medium of viscosity \\\(\\eta\\\) as originally defined by Debye\, and used by Perrin in the original development of the theories of rotational motion of fluorophores."
comment: "Related to the rotational correlation time, \(\tau_{c}\), by \(\rho = 3\tau_{c}\). Thus, in the case of a spherically emitting species reorienting itself in a homogeneous fluid, \(\rho = 1/(6\, D_{r})\), with \(D_{r}\) the rotational diffusion coefficient."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
