[Term]
id: goldbook:S05499
name: Schiller layers
def: "In some systems\, sedimenting particles form layers separated by approximately equal distances of the order of the wavelength of light. This gives rise to strong colours when observed in reflected light and the system is said to form iridescent layers or Schiller layers."
synonym: "iridescent layers" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:W06659

[Term]
id: goldbook:S05501
name: Schulze–Hardy rule
def: "The generalization that the critical coagulation concentration for a typical lyophobic sol is extremely sensitive to the valence of the counter-ions \(high valence gives a low critical coagulation concentration\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
