[Term]
id: goldbook:S05504
name: scintillation counter
def: "A scintillator coupled to a photomultiplier tube. Incident X-ray photons are converted in the scintillator into bursts of visible light photons\, some of which fall on the photocathode and can be measured. For incident photons having energies higher than the absorption edge of the elements contained in the scintillator\, an escape peak can be observed."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567101745
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:P04626
consider: goldbook:VT07496

[Term]
id: goldbook:S05505
name: scintillation detector
def: "A radiation detector using a medium in which a burst of luminescence radiation\, produced along the path of an ionizing particle\, is quantified."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466122513
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:L03641
consider: goldbook:R05048
consider: goldbook:R05054

[Term]
id: goldbook:S05506
name: scintillation spectrometer
def: "A measuring assembly incorporating a scintillation detector and a pulse amplitude analyser used for determining the energy spectrum of certain types of radiation."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198254081533
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
