[Term]
id: goldbook:S05557
name: selective micro-sample
def: "A sample which results where a small portion has been separated from the lot or laboratory sample by selective means such as magnetic-\, density-\, or manual separation\, by micro-drilling\, or by centrifugation\, e.g. the separation of magnetic materials from a geological material\, or the separation of metal particles from a lubricating oil. If individual particles are analysed the term individual particle analysis is applied."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198860091461
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:L03433
consider: goldbook:L03630
consider: goldbook:M03894

[Term]
id: goldbook:S05558
name: selective poisoning
def: "In selective poisoning or selective inhibition\, a poison retards the rate of one catalysed reaction more than that of another or it may retard only one of the reactions."
synonym: "selective inhibition" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197646010071
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03034

[Term]
id: goldbook:S05559
name: selective preconcentration
def: "An operation \(process\) as a result of which microcomponents are selectively isolated from a sample. It is used when the simultaneous presence of several components in the concentrate may distort the results of analysis. Selective preconcentration usually is achieved by isolation of the microcomponent to be determined."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197951051195
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:S05560
name: selective sample
def: "A sample that is deliberately chosen by using a sampling plan that screens out materials with certain characteristics and/or selects only material with other relevant characteristics."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062061193
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:S05563
name: selectivity
def: "It sometimes refers to the discrimination shown by a given reactant A when it reacts with two alternative reactants B and C\, or in two different ways \(e.g. at two different sites\) with a reactant B."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668010149
