[Term]
id: goldbook:S05597
name: semiconductor-metal transition
def: "Any transition from a semiconductor to a metallic state under the influence of a temperature or pressure change or both. Examples\:$\\ce\{Ti2O3\}$\: band-edge crossing in a semiconductor to semimetal transition.SmS\: localized level crossing a band edge. In SmS hydrostatic pressure above the critical pressure \\\(P_\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\approx 0.65\\ \\mathrm\{GPa\}\\\) broadens the Sm-5d band to make the band edge cross the Sm-\\\(4\\rm\{f\}^\{6\}\\\) level.A localized-itinerant transition.A switching transition."
