[Term]
id: goldbook:S05642
name: shear viscosity
def: "For a Newtonian fluid\, the shear viscosity is often termed simply viscosity since in most situations it is the only one considered. It relates the shear components of stress and those of rate of strain at a point in the fluid by\: \\\[\\sigma _\{xy\}=\\sigma _\{yx\}=\\eta \\ \(\\frac\{\\partial  u_\{x\}\}\{\\partial y\}+\\frac\{\\partial  u_\{y\}\}\{\\partial x\}\)=2\\ \\eta \\ \\overset\{\\rm\{.\}\}\{\\gamma \}_\{yx\}\\\] where \\\(\\overset\{\\rm\{.\}\}\{\\gamma \}_\{yx\}\\\)\, the shear component of rate of strain is defined as follows\: \\\[\\overset\{\\rm\{.\}\}\{\\gamma \}_\{yx\}=\\frac\{1\}\{2\}\\ \(\\frac\{\\partial  u_\{x\}\}\{\\partial y\}+\\frac\{\\partial  u_\{y\}\}\{\\partial x\}\)\\\] Corresponding relations hold for \\\(\\sigma _\{xz\}\\\) and \\\(\\sigma _\{yz\}\\\); \\\(\\sigma _\{xy\}\\\) is the component of stress acting in the \\\(y\\\)-direction on a plate normal to the \\\(x\\\)-axis; \\\( u_\{x\}\\\)\, \\\( u_\{y\}\\\)\, \\\( u_\{z\}\\\) are the components of velocity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197951051213
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:N04138
consider: goldbook:S05634
consider: goldbook:S06037
consider: goldbook:V06627

[Term]
id: goldbook:S05644
name: shielding
def: "In the context of NMR spectroscopy shielding is the effect of the electron shells of the observed and the neighbouring nuclei on the external magnetic field. The external field induces circulations in the electron cloud. The resulting magnetic moment is oriented in the opposite direction to the external field\, so that the local field at the central nucleus is weakened\, although it may be strengthened at other nuclei \(deshielding\). The phenomenon is the origin of the structural dependence of the resonance frequencies of the nuclei."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
