[Term]
id: goldbook:S05680
name: simultaneous reactions
def: "Composite reactions\, in which processes like \\\[\\rm\{A\}\\ \\overset\{1\}\{\\rightarrow \}\\ \\rm\{Y\}\\\] and \\\[\\rm\{B\}\\ \\overset\{2\}\{\\rightarrow \}\\ \\rm\{Z\}\\\] occur in parallel\, can be called simultaneous or parallel reactions. Sometimes there is competition involved\, like in the scheme\: \\\[\\rm\{A\}\\\,+\\\,\\rm\{B\}\\ \\overset\{1\}\{\\rightarrow \}\\ \\rm\{Y\}\\\] and \\\[\\rm\{A\}\\\,+\\\,\\rm\{C\}\\ \\overset\{2\}\{\\rightarrow \}\\ \\rm\{Z\}\\\] where B and C compete with one another for A."
