[Term]
id: goldbook:S05749
name: solvatochromism
def: "The \(pronounced\) change in position and sometimes intensity of an electronic absorption or emission band\, accompanying a change in the polarity of the medium. Negative \(positive\) solvatochromism corresponds to a hypsochromic \(bathochromic\) shift with increasing solvent polarity."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
