[Term]
id: goldbook:S05762
name: solvolysis
def: "Generally\, reaction with a solvent\, or with a lyonium ion or lyate ion involving the rupture of one or more bonds in the reacting solute. More specifically the term is used for substitution elimination and fragmentation reactions in which a solvent species is the nucleophile \('alcoholysis' if the solvent is an alcohol\, etc.\)."
