[Term]
id: goldbook:S05763
name: solvophobicity parameter
def: "A solvent parameter defined by\: \\\[Sp = 1 - \\frac\{M\}\{M\\left\(\\rm\{hexadecane\}\\right\)\}\\\] derived from the Gibbs energy of transfer \(\\\(\\Delta _\{\\rm\{t\}\}G^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\)\) of a series of solutes from water to numerous aqueous-organic mixtures and to pure solvents\: \\\[\\Delta _\{\\rm\{t\}\}G^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\left\(\\rm\{to solvent\}\\right\) = M\\ R_\{\\rm\{T\}\}+D\\\] where \\\(R_\{\\rm\{T\}\}\\\) is a solute parameter\, and \\\(M\\\) and \\\(D\\\) characterize the solvent. The \\\(M\\\) values are used to define a solvent solvophobic effect so that \\\(Sp\\\) values are scaled from unity \(water\) to zero \(hexadecane\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
