[Term]
id: goldbook:S05782
name: spatially resolving detector
def: "A detector for the measurement of the spatial distribution of the radiation. Spatially resolving detectors can be divided into two groups\:   the photosensitive area consists of a matrix of discrete photosensitive elements\, the pixels \(picture elements\) forming an array with the facility to separately read out the information\, simultaneously or sequentially.   the photosensitive area consists of a single photosensitive element that must be scanned \(e.g. image dissection tube.\)"
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567101745
