[Term]
id: goldbook:S05789
name: specific acid–base catalysis
def: "Catalysis by acids or bases in solution is said to be specific when the only observable catalytic effects are those due to the ions formed from the solvent itself \(e.g. if when water is the solvent the only observable catalysis is that due to the $\\ce\{H^\{+\}\}$ and $\\ce\{OH^\{−\}\}$ ions\)."
