[Term]
id: goldbook:S05791
name: specific adsorption
def: "Ions become specifically adsorbed when short-range interactions between them and the interphase become important. They are believed then to penetrate into the inner layer and may \(but not necessarily\) come into contact with the surface. They are usually assumed to form a partial or complete monolayer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198658030437
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03118
