[Term]
id: goldbook:S05947
name: static stability
def: "In meteorology\, the stability of the atmosphere in the vertical direction to vertical displacements. If \\\(\\mathit\{\\Gamma\}\\\) is the dry adiabatic lapse rate\, dry air is stable if the lapse rate \\\(-\\frac\{\{\\rm\{d\}\}T\}\{\{\\rm\{d\}\}z\} \\lt \\Gamma\\\)\, unstable if \\\(-\\frac\{\{\\rm\{d\}\}T\}\{\{\\rm\{d\}\}z\} \\gt \\Gamma\\\) and neutral \\\(-\\frac\{\{\\rm\{d\}\}T\}\{\{\\rm\{d\}\}z\} = \\Gamma\\\)."
