[Term]
id: goldbook:S06028
name: Stokes law
def: "\\\(F=6\\ \\pi \\ \\eta \\ r\\  u\\\)\, where \\\(F\\\) is the force exerted on a sphere of radius \\\(r\\\) which is moving through a fluid of viscosity \\\(\\eta \\\) with a relative velocity \\\( u\\\); this equation holds at low velocities which are free from turbulence \(called the stokes region\)."
