[Term]
id: goldbook:S06029
name: Stokes number
def: "Sometimes referred to as the inertial parameter; it is an index of the impactability of an aerosol particle. It is defined by the equation\: \\\(St = 2\\ \\tau \\ \(V_\{\\rm\{t\}\}-  u_\{\\rm\{t\}\}\)\\ D_\{\\rm\{p\}\}\\\) where \\\(D_\{\\rm\{p\}\}\\\) is the diameter of a small drop\, \\\(V_\{\\rm\{t\}\}-  u_\{\\rm\{t\}\}\\\) is the difference in fall velocities of the drop and aerosol particles and \\\(\\tau \\\) is the characteristic relaxation time of a particle."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062112167
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00176
consider: goldbook:R05287

[Term]
id: goldbook:S06030
name: Stokes parameters
def: "Of elliptically polarized incident radiation\, these are given by \\\[s_\{0\}^\{0\}=E_\{1\}^\{0\}+E_\{2\}^\{0\}\\\] \\\[s_\{1\}^\{0\}=E_\{1\}^\{0\}- E_\{2\}^\{0\}\\\] \\\[s_\{2\}^\{0\}=2\\ \\sqrt\{E_\{1\}^\{0\}\\ E_\{2\}^\{0\}\}\\ \\cos   \\delta ^\{0\}\\\] \\\[s_\{3\}^\{0\}=2\\ \\sqrt\{E_\{1\}^\{0\}\\ E_\{2\}^\{0\}\}\\ \\sin   \\delta ^\{0\}\\\] where \\\(E_\{1\}^\{0\}\\\) and \\\(E_\{2\}^\{0\}\\\) specify the irradiances of the incident light polarized with their electric vectors vibrating perpendicular and parallel to the scattering\, respectively and \\\(\\delta ^\{0\}\\\) is the phase difference between these electric vectors."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198355060931
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03254
consider: goldbook:R05048
consider: goldbook:S05492
consider: goldbook:S05493

[Term]
id: goldbook:S06031
name: Stokes shift
def: "The difference \(usually in frequency units\) between the spectral positions of the band maxima \(or the band origin\) of the absorption and luminescence arising from the same electronic transition. Generally\, the luminescence occurring at a longer wavelength than the absorption is stronger than the opposite. The latter may be called an anti-Stokes shift."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:C01130
consider: goldbook:L03641
consider: goldbook:W06659

[Term]
id: goldbook:S06032
name: Stokes type radiation
def: "Fluorescence radiation occurring at wavelengths longer than absorption\, i.e. the normal case\, is said to be of the Stokes type."
