[Term]
id: goldbook:S06037
name: strain
def: "Strain is present in a molecular entity or transition structure if the energy is enhanced because of unfavourable bond lengths\, bond angles or dihedral angles \('torsional strain'\) relative to a standard. It is quantitatively defined as the standard enthalpy of a structure relative to a strainless structure \(real or hypothetical\) made up from the same atoms with the same types of bonding. \(The enthalpy of formation of cyclopropane is \\\(\\pu\{53.6 kJ mol-1\}\\\)\, whereas the enthalpy of formation based on three 'normal' methylene groups\, from acyclic models\, is \\\(\\pu\{-62 kJ mol-1\}\\\). On this basis cyclopropane is destabilized by ca. \\\(\\pu\{115 kJ mol-1\}\\\) of strain energy.\)"
synonym: "steric strain" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466051077
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
