[Term]
id: goldbook:S06049
name: streaming current
def: "The electric current \\\(I\\\) flowing in a streaming cell if the electrodes\, which are supposed to be ideally depolarized\, are short-circuited. \\\(I\\\) is positive if the current in the membrane\, plug\, etc.\, is from high to low pressure side \(and in the outside lead from low to high pressure side\)."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
