id: goldbook:S06069
name: sublimation
def: "The direct transition of a solid to a vapour without passing through a liquid phase. Example\: The transition of solid $\\ce\{CO2\}$ to $\\ce\{CO2\}$ vapour."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199466030577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:S06071
name: subsample
def: "A subsample may be\: \(a\) a portion of the sample obtained by selection or division; \(b\) an individual unit of the lot taken as part of the sample; \(c\) the final unit of multistage sampling. The term 'subsample' is used either in the sense of a 'sample of a sample' or as a synonym for 'unit'. In practice\, the meaning is usually apparent from the context or is defined."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199062061193
