[Term]
id: goldbook:S06132
name: summit current
def: "In ac polarography\, differential pulse polarography\, derivative polarography\, square-wave polarography\, and similar techniques\, the maximum value of the component of the current that is associated with the presence of a substance B. Normally this component of the current is faradaic\, and the maximum arises because the rate of variation \(with applied potential\) of the rate of the charge-transfer process passes through a maximum. Similar maxima arise when this component is non-faradaic \(and when B is surface-active rather than electroactive\). In a case known to be of the latter type\, the term apex current is recommended as being more specific."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198557101491
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:A00412
consider: goldbook:A00424
consider: goldbook:P04716

