[Term]
id: goldbook:S06146
name: supersaturation
def: "In chemistry\, an unstable system which has a greater concentration of a material in solution than would exist at equilibrium is said to be supersaturated.In meteorology\, supersaturation of an air mass with respect to $\\ce\{H2O\}$ vapour is of special interest. It is the saturation ratio minus one\, or the percent supersaturation is the percent relative humidity minus 100."
