consider: goldbook:I03042
consider: goldbook:I03255
consider: goldbook:P04740

[Term]
id: goldbook:ST07194
name: shape-memory polymer
def: "Polymer that\, after heating and being subjected to a plastic deformation\, resumes its original shape when heated above its glass-transition or melting temperature."
comment: "Crystalline trans-polyisoprene is an example of a shape-memory polymer."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200476040889
