name: superabsorbent polymer
def: "Polymer that can absorb and retain extremely large amounts of a liquid relative to its own mass."
comment: "Superabsorbent polymers for water are frequently polyelectrolytes."
comment: "The liquid absorbed can be water or an organic liquid."
comment: "The swelling ratio of a superabsorbent polymer can reach the order of 1000:1."
