id: goldbook:ST07274
name: spinodal
def: "Curve defining the region of composition and temperature for a binary mixture across which a transition occurs from conditions where single-phase mixtures are metastable to conditions where single-phase mixtures are unstable and undergo phase separation by spinodal decomposition."
comment: "In the unstable region bounded by the spinodal curve, phase domain separation is spontaneous, i.e., no nucleation step is required to initiate the separation process."
comment: "The spinodal curve for a binary mixture is defined as the geometrical locus of all states with \[\left ( \frac{\delta^{2}\Delta _{\rm{mix}}G}{\delta\phi ^{2}} \right)_{T,p} = 0\]."
