id: goldbook:ST07417
name: self-localized excitations
def: "Physical and chemical properties of conjugated organic polymers with $\\ce\{\\uppi\\!\\mbox\{-\}electrons\}$ have been interpreted in terms of self-localized excitations\, which are quasi-particles with structural changes over several repeating units. These excitations can be classified into solitons\, polarons\, bipolarons and excitons according to their charge and spin."
