comment: "This factor determines the efficiency of diffusion-controlled reactions, which have an encounter-controlled rate. Typical examples are quenching of fluorescence of aromatic hydrocarbons by $\ce{O2}$, quenching of triplet states by $\ce{O2}$, and triplet–triplet annihilation."
