[Term]
id: goldbook:T06376
name: time constant
def: "If the output of a detector changes exponentially with time\, the time required for it to change from its initial value by the fraction \\\(1 - \\exp\(-t/\\tau _\{\\rm\{c\}\}\)\\\) \(for \\\(t=\\tau _\{\\rm\{c\}\}\\\)\) of the final value\, is called the time constant."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199567101745
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string

[Term]
id: goldbook:T06377
name: time-correlated single photon counting
def: "A technique for the measurement of the time histogram of a sequence of photons with respect to a periodic event\, e.g. a flash from a repetitive nanosecond lamp or a CW operated laser \(mode locked laser\). The essential part is a time-to-amplitude-converter \(TAC\) which transforms the arrival time between a start and a stop pulse into a voltage. Sometimes called single photon timing."
synonym: "single photon timing" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199668122223
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
