[Term]
id: goldbook:T06438
name: transduction
def: "The transfer of genetic information from one bacterium to another by means of a transducing bacteriophage. When the phage is grown on the first host\, a fragment of the host DNA can be incorporated into the phage particles. This foreign DNA can be transferred to the second host upon infection with progeny phage from the first experiment."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199264010143
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
