[Term]
id: goldbook:T06442
name: transfer activity coefficient
def: "A term used to quantify the difference in the free energy of a solute ion in two different standard states often in two different liquid phases. The relationship is \\\(\\Delta _\{\\rm\{t\}\}G^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\} =  u \\ R\\ T\\ \\ln \\mathit\{\\gamma\}_\{\\rm\{t\}\}\\\) where \\\(\\Delta _\{\\rm\{t\}\}G^\{\\\,\\unicode\{x26ac\}\}\\\) is the transfer Gibbs energy and \\\( u \\\) is the number of ions in the solute."
comment: "It does not necessarily imply the physical transfer of a solute between two liquid phases."
comment: "It should not be confused with the mass transfer coefficient which represents the specific rate of transfer of a species from one phase to another."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac199365112373
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
