[Term]
id: goldbook:T06484
name: transmittance
def: "The ratio of the transmitted radiant power \(\\\(P_\{\\lambda \}\\\)\) to that incident on the sample \(\\\(P_\{\\lambda \}^\{0\}\\\)\)\: \\\[T=\\frac\{P_\{\\lambda \}\}\{P_\{\\lambda \}^\{0\}\}\\\] Internal transmittance refers to energy loss by absorption\, whereas the total transmittance is that due to absorption\, reflection\, scatter\, etc."
