[Term]
id: goldbook:U06574
name: upconversion
def: "The process by which two photons with frequencies \\\( u _\{2\}\\\) and \\\( u _\{3\}\\\) combine in a non-linear medium to produce a higher energy photon with frequency \\\( u _\{1\}\\\) such that \\\( u _\{1\}= u _\{2\}+ u _\{3\}\\\)."
comment: "Also known as a parametric upconversion or sum frequency generation. Upconversion is the reverse process of downconversion."
comment: "The efficiency of the conversion process depends on the parametric gain in the non-linear material. This in turn depends on the power of the incident radiation, the photon frequencies, their indices of refraction in the material, and the non-linear 'hyper-susceptibility' of the material."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac200779030293
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:DT07362
consider: goldbook:P04792

