[Term]
id: goldbook:V06608
name: velocity
def: "The flux density \\\(N_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is related to the velocity by the equation \\\[N_\{\\rm\{B\}\}=c_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\ v_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\] The vector \\\(v_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is the macroscopic average velocity at which the species B moves \(which is to be distinguished from the random molecular velocity\); \\\(c_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is the concentration of species B \(\\\(\\pu\{mol m-3\}\\\)\). Note that the velocity is defined with respect to a frame of reference."
