[Term]
id: goldbook:V06612
name: Verwey transition
def: "An electron-ordering transition occurring in a mixed-valent system that results in an ordering of formal valence states in the low-temperature phase. Example\: The prototype system\, first identified by Verwey\, is the ferrospinel magnetite\, $\\ce\{Fe^\{3+\}\[Fe^\{3+\}Fe^\{2+\}\]O4\}$ in which an ordering of $\\ce\{Fe^\{3+\}\}$ and $\\ce\{Fe^\{2+\}\}$ ions within octahedral sites is thought to occur below \\\(T_\{\\rm\{v\}\}\\approx 120\\ \\rm\{K\}\\\)."
