[Term]
id: goldbook:V06639
name: voltammetric constant
def: "In linear-sweep voltammetry and related techniques\, the empirical quantity defined by the equation \\\[\\frac\{i_\{p\}\}\{A\\ \\sqrt\{ u\}\\ c_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\}\\quad \\left\(=\\frac\{j_\{p\}\}\{\\sqrt\{ u\}\\ c_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\}\\right\)\\\] where \\\(i_\{p\}\\\) is the peak current\, A is the area of the electrode-solution interface\, \\\( u\\\) is the rate of change of applied potential\, and \\\(c_\{\\rm\{B\}\}\\\) is the bulk concentration of the substance B whose reduction or oxidation is responsible for the peak in question."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac198557101491
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
