[Term]
id: goldbook:VT07153
name: vulcanization
def: "Chemical crosslinking of high-molar-mass linear or branched polymers to give a polymer network."
comment: "A classic example of vulcanization is the crosslinking of cis-polyisoprene through sulfide bridges in the thermal treatment of natural rubber with sulfur or a sulfur-containing compound."
comment: "The polymer network formed often displays rubber-like elasticity. However, a high concentration of crosslinks can lead to rigid materials."
