id: goldbook:W06687
name: work of adhesion
def: "The work of adhesion per unit area\, \\\(w_\{\\rm\{A\}\}^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}\\\)\, is the work done on the system when two condensed phases $\\ce\{\\upalpha\\!\}$ and $\\ce\{\\upbeta\\!\}$\, forming an interface of unit area are separated reversibly to form unit areas of each of the $\\ce\{\\upalpha\\!\\updelta\\!\\mbox\{-\}\}$ and $\\ce\{\\upbeta\\!\\updelta\\!\\mbox\{-\}\}$ interfaces. \\\[w_\{\\rm\{A\}\}^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}=\\gamma ^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}+\\gamma ^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}- \\gamma ^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \}\\\] where \\\(\\gamma ^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \}\\\)\, \\\(\\gamma ^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}\\\) and \\\(\\gamma ^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B2\} \\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B4\} \}\\\) are the surface tensions between two bulk phases $\\ce\{\\upalpha\\!\}$\, $\\ce\{\\upbeta\\!\}$; $\\ce\{\\upalpha\\!\}$\, $\\ce\{\\updelta\\!\}$ and $\\ce\{\\upbeta\\!\}$\, $\\ce\{\\updelta\\!\}$ respectively. The work of adhesion as defined above\, and traditionally used\, may be called the work of separation."
synonym: "work of separation" []
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:I03082
consider: goldbook:S06192

[Term]
id: goldbook:W06688
name: work of cohesion per unit area
def: "Of a single pure liquid or solid phase $\\ce\{\\upalpha\\!\}$\, \\\(w_\{\\rm\{C\}\}^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \}\\\) is the work done on the system when a column $\\ce\{\\upalpha\\!\}$ of unit area is split\, reversibly\, normal to the axis of the column to form two new surfaces each of unit area in contact with the equilibrium gas phase. \\\[w_\{\\rm\{C\}\}^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \}=2\\ \\gamma ^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \}\\\] where \\\(\\gamma ^\{\\unicode\[Times\]\{x3B1\} \}\\\) is the surface tension between phase and its equilibrium vapour or a dilute gas phase."
property_value: mito:isMentionedBy doi:10.1351/pac197231040577
property_value: hasStatus "current" xsd:string
consider: goldbook:S06192

[Term]
id: goldbook:W06691
name: work softening
def: "The application of a finite shear to a system after a long rest may result in a decrease of the viscosity or the consistency. If the decrease persists when the shear is discontinued\, this behaviour is called work softening \(or shear breakdown\)\, whereas if the original viscosity or consistency is recovered this behaviour is called thixotropy."
synonym: "shear breakdown" []
