id: goldbook:Y06724
name: yield
def: "Ratio expressing the efficiency of a mass conversion process. The yield coefficient is defined as the amount of cell mass \(\\\(\\pu\{kg\}\\\)\) or product formed \(\\\(\\pu\{kg\}\\\)\,\\\(\\pu\{mol\}\\\)\) related to the consumed substrate \(carbon or nitrogen source or oxygen in \\\(\\pu\{kg\}\\\) or \\\(\\pu\{moles\}\\\)\) or to the intracellular ATP production \(\\\(\\pu\{moles\}\\\)\)."
